  <graph edgedefault="directed">
    <node id="&quot;BRAIN TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brain tumor is a broader category that includes gliomas, affecting brain function and requiring various diagnostic and treatment approaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain tumor is a condition that can be frightening and overwhelming, and this book helps make sense of information and treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain tumor is a condition that can cause symptoms like nausea, vomiting, problems with thinking and speech, weakness, and personality changes, and is diagnosed through imaging and biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain tumor is a general term for abnormal growths in the brain, including gliomas, which can be benign or malignant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain tumor is a general term for abnormal growths in the brain, with glioma being a specific type, and diagnosis can be frightening."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain tumor is an abnormal growth of cells in the brain, with gliomas being a specific type. It can cause symptoms and requires various treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COUNSELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Counseling is a support service provided by doctors to help patients quit smoking."&lt;SEP&gt;"Counseling is a supportive service provided by care teams or genetic counselors to help patients quit smoking or make informed genetic testing decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Counseling is a supportive service recommended to help patients quit smoking, especially under stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Counseling is a supportive service that helps cancer patients manage emotional distress and quit smoking or vaping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Counseling is a supportive service that provides emotional and psychological guidance to patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mutations are DNA errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutations are abnormal changes in genes that can increase cancer risk, either inherited or somatic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutations are abnormal changes in genes that can turn normal cells into cancer cells, often occurring spontaneously in bladder cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutations are changes in DNA that can affect gene function and are detected by NGS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutations are changes in the genes of bladder cells that can lead to cancer development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutations are errors in DNA that can lead to cancer or affect treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutations are genetic changes that enable cancer cells to multiply and survive longer than normal cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgical biopsy is a procedure to remove a tumor sample for diagnosis, often used when core needle biopsy is not sufficient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical biopsy is a procedure to remove an entire lump or a portion of tissue for examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical biopsy is an open biopsy procedure that removes a tumor sample through a small incision, performed by a treating surgeon in an operating room."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-CLEAR CELL RCC (NCCRCC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-clear cell RCC is a subtype of RCC that includes several other subtypes, distinct from clear cell RCC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE EXPRESSION PROFILING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of biomarker testing that measures the activity of genes in tumor cells to predict behavior and treatment response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene expression profiling is a biomarker testing method that measures the activity of genes in tumor cells to guide treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene expression profiling is a method to analyze which genes are active in AML cells, helping to understand the cancer's behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene expression profiling is a technique to measure the activity of genes in leukemia cells, used for classification and prognosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene expression profiling is a type of biomarker testing that measures gene activity to guide treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene expression profiling is a type of biomarker testing that measures gene activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene expression profiling is a type of biomarker testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC DISEASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic diseases are conditions caused by mutations in genes, which genetic counselors are trained to assess and manage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AWARENESS MONTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical Cancer Awareness Month is observed in January to educate about prevention and screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Selective estrogen receptor modulators (SERMs) block estrogen from attaching to hormone receptors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSA TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSA test is a blood test measuring prostate-specific antigen levels, used to detect or monitor prostate cancer, but not diagnostic alone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLON CANCER SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Process of detecting polyps or cancer early."&lt;SEP&gt;"Process of detecting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of detecting polyps or cancer early, as discussed in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THICK SALIVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thick saliva is a common side effect of radiation therapy to the neck area, affecting oral comfort."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REIKI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reiki is a complementary energy therapy that promotes relaxation and healing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAPHRAGM USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diaphragm Use is the insertion of a diaphragm for birth control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STOMACH WALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stomach wall is composed of five main layers: mucosa, submucosa, muscle, subserosa, and serosa, and cancer grows outward through these layers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONLINE SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Online support refers to web-based resources for smoking cessation, such as SmokeFree.gov."&lt;SEP&gt;"Online support refers to web-based resources like SmokeFree.gov that provide guidance and community for quitting smoking."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INNER WALL OF THE ABDOMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inner wall of the abdomen is a common area where metastatic bladder cancer can spread, affecting abdominal organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CALCIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A mineral in the blood, assessed in a CMP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Calcium is a mineral in the bloodstream controlled by parathyroid glands."&lt;SEP&gt;"Calcium is a mineral involved in bone formation and remodeling, regulated by osteoclasts and osteoblasts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Calcium is a mineral needed for healthy teeth, bones, and other body tissues; high levels in blood can indicate hypercalcemia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Calcium is a mineral supplement recommended to strengthen bones, especially during thyroid hormone replacement therapy or RAI treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS: BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Bladder Cancer is a resource providing information on bladder cancer, available at NCCN.org/patientguidelines and on the NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer app."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENOMIC TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of biomarker testing that analyzes the entire genome of tumor cells to identify mutations and guide treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic testing examines the entire genome of a tumor to identify mutations and guide therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic testing is a broad term for analyzing DNA and genes in tumors, including biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic testing is a broad term for analyzing DNA or genes in tumors to identify mutations and guide therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic testing is a broad term for analyzing the complete genetic makeup of leukemia cells, including mutations and chromosomal changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic testing is a broad term for analyzing the entire genome of AML cells to identify mutations and guide treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic testing is a type of biomarker testing that analyzes the entire genome for mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic testing is a type of biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genomic testing is another name for biomarker testing, examining genetic mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISTANT PARTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Distant parts refer to areas far from the original cancer site."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant parts refer to areas of the body far from the primary tumor, which imaging tests check for cancer metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER PREVENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer prevention includes HPV vaccination, regular screening, and risk factor reduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Selective estrogen receptor degraders (SERDs) block and destroy estrogen receptors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENERAL HEALTH HISTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"General health history involves collecting patient's past health issues, medications, and physical exam to inform cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER REGISTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Registry is a database that tracks cancer cases for research and public health purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer registry is a database that tracks cancer cases for research and public health purposes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSCLE LAYER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muscle layer is the second or third layer of the rectal wall, where T2 tumors invade, requiring transabdominal surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Muscle layer is the third layer of the stomach wall, which cancer may invade in more advanced locoregional stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"The muscle layer is the third layer of the bladder wall, which is invaded by muscle-invasive bladder cancer stages 2, 3, and 4."&lt;SEP&gt;"The muscular wall of the bladder; invasion of this layer by cancer indicates a more aggressive stage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTHER CANCERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Other cancers are a longer-term side effect of systemic therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Other cancers are a potential long-term side effect of chemotherapy. This refers to the development of new, different cancers years after the original treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Other cancers are additional cancer types that smoking and vaping can increase the risk of developing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Other cancers are additional cancer types that smoking increases the risk of developing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Other cancers are additional malignancies that smoking or inherited mutations may increase the risk of developing, necessitating comprehensive monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"Other cancers refer to additional cancer types linked to smoking and vaping."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICAL TEAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical team is a group of health care professionals who detect blood in urine microscopically and manage patient care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOSPHATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phosphate is a mineral component of bone tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS: SOFT TISSUE SARCOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Soft Tissue Sarcoma is a resource providing information on soft tissue sarcoma, available at NCCN.org/patientguidelines and on the NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer app."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRCA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene associated with hereditary breast cancer; mutations in BRCA can be identified through biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA refers to genes (BRCA1 and BRCA2) that normally help prevent tumor growth; mutations in these genes increase the risk of multiple cancers and can affect treatment response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINE TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urine tests are diagnostic procedures that analyze urine samples to detect blood or other indicators of urinary tract issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urine tests are diagnostic procedures used to detect blood or abnormal cells in urine, aiding in bladder cancer diagnosis and monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urine tests are diagnostic tests used to detect abnormalities in urine, part of the kidney cancer diagnosis process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer treatment includes surgery, radiation, chemotherapy, and newer therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOREMIFENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Toremifene (Fareston) is a SERM used to block estrogen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLACK PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Black people are identified as a group at greater risk for prostate cancer due to genetic and health disparities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COAL SMOKE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coal smoke is a cancer-causing agent that increases lung cancer risk, particularly in smokers. It is produced by burning coal for heating or cooking."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Progesterone receptor is a protein found on some breast cancer cells that binds to progesterone, influencing cancer growth. Testing for progesterone receptor status is part of treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH RECORD SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health record system is a digital platform that stores and manages patient medical information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION (PCR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PCR is a method used in AML mutation testing to amplify and detect specific DNA sequences, identifying mutations unique to AML cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEER VOLUNTEERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peer volunteers are trained individuals who provide empathetic support and practical advice to anal cancer patients and caregivers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUBSEROSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Subserosa is the fourth layer of the stomach wall, which cancer may invade as it progresses outward."&lt;SEP&gt;"The subserosa is a layer of connective tissue supporting the serosa."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NICOTINE WITHDRAWAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nicotine withdrawal is the challenging process of quitting smoking due to nicotine addiction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nicotine withdrawal is the challenging process of quitting smoking or vaping, which can be harder under cancer stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nicotine withdrawal is the set of physical and psychological symptoms experienced when a person stops using nicotine, making quitting challenging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEPHANIE E. WEISS, MD, FASTRO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stephanie E. Weiss, MD, FASTRO is a medical professional, likely an oncologist or radiologist, who provided an image related to lymphoma tumors on scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROXYAPATITE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydroxyapatite is a bone mineral that provides structural integrity to bone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RENAL CELL CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Renal cell carcinoma (RCC) is the most common type of kidney cancer, starting in cells lining the renal tubules, and is the focus of the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Renal cell carcinoma (RCC) is the most common type of kidney cancer, starting in the cells lining the renal tubules, and can appear as multiple tumors in one kidney or involve both kidneys."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMRT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IMRT (Intensity-Modulated Radiation Therapy) is a type of radiation therapy used in cancer treatment, targeting tumors with precision."&lt;SEP&gt;"IMRT (Intensity-Modulated Radiation Therapy) is an advanced form of external beam radiation therapy that uses many small beams of different intensities to target tumors while sparing surrounding tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"IMRT (Intensity-Modulated Radiation Therapy) is an advanced radiation technique that limits exposure to nearby organs, used for anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC COUNSELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic counseling involves discussing inherited cancer risks and testing options with a specialist, often before genetic testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic counseling is a process where a specialist helps assess hereditary cancer risk and discusses genetic testing options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic counseling is a process where individuals discuss inherited cancer risks with a specialist, deciding on germline testing and interpreting results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic counseling is a service provided by genetic counselors to discuss test results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER STAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer staging determines the extent of disease spread, guiding treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FARESTON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fareston is the brand name for toremifene, a SERM."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INHERITED GENETIC MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inherited genetic mutations are specific gene changes that increase prostate cancer risk in individuals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMAGING TEST ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Imaging Test Role Education is understanding how imaging tests detect cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEROSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Serosa (or adventitia) is the outer, fourth layer of the colon wall."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serosa is an outer membrane that covers the gallbladder and bile ducts, also called the serous membrane or visceral peritoneum."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serosa is the outermost layer of the stomach wall, which cancer may reach in advanced locoregional stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Serosa, also known as serous membrane or visceral peritoneum, is a thin membrane covering surfaces in the body, relevant to bile duct anatomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The serosa is the outer membrane covering the stomach, allowing smooth movement against other organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stress is a condition that triggers the body's response, regulated by adrenal hormones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stress is a factor in making decisions about cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stress is a psychological state mentioned as a common experience during medical testing, with support recommended."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stress is a psychological state that can be reduced through supportive care and counseling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stress, such as from having cancer, can make quitting smoking harder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEREOTACTIC BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A precise biopsy technique used when a brain tumor is in a hard-to-reach or vital area."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stereotactic biopsy is a diagnostic procedure involving the insertion of a thin, hollow needle into the brain to remove a sliver of tumor tissue for laboratory analysis, essential for diagnosing primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stereotactic biopsy is a medical procedure used to diagnose a glioma tumor by inserting a thin, hollow needle into the brain to remove a sliver of the tumor for lab testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stereotactic biopsy is a precise biopsy procedure performed by a neurosurgeon, using a frame or markers and a computerized navigation system to remove a tumor sample from the brain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stereotactic biopsy is a precise procedure used when a brain tumor is in a hard-to-reach or vital area, aiming to remove only enough tissue for diagnosis, performed by a neurosurgeon in an operating room."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLLAGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Collagen is a protein that provides flexibility and structure to bone tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Collagen is the most abundant protein in the body, a component of bone tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Collagen is the most abundant protein in the body, a key component of bone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSITIONAL CELL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transitional cell cancer is an older term for urothelial carcinoma, which starts in the cells lining the renal pelvis and ureter."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC ANAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic anal cancer is anal cancer that has spread beyond the pelvis, most commonly to the liver or lungs, and is treated with platinum-based chemotherapy as first-line therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic anal cancer is cancer that has spread beyond the pelvis, mentioned as a separate category from stages I-III."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic anal cancer is stage IV cancer that has spread beyond the pelvis and is treated with systemic therapy such as chemotherapy or immunotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grading is the process of assessing how abnormal cancer cells look and how fast they grow, informing prognosis and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER RECURRENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer recurrence refers to cancer returning after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FASLODEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Faslodex is the brand name for fulvestrant, a SERD."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLOSE FAMILY MEMBER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Close family member refers to a blood relative with prostate cancer, which increases an individual's risk of developing the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE PERIANAL REGION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The perianal region includes the anal opening and surrounding skin, and is another area where anal cancer can start."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ULCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ulcer is a sore that can form in the stomach lining as a result of cancer growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ulcer is a sore or lesion that can form inside the stomach as a result of cancer growth, causing symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSATELLITE INSTABILITY (MSI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MSI is a DNA repair defect."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSI is a biomarker indicating DNA mismatch repair issues, tested in recurrent ovarian cancer to guide treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellite instability (MSI) is a biomarker reflecting high mutation rates due to defective DNA repair, relevant for immunotherapy decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellite instability (MSI) is a condition where DNA repair errors are not fixed, leading to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellite instability is a biomarker test that looks for changes in DNA repeat sequences, used to guide treatment decisions for ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellite instability is a condition of increased mutation frequency in microsatellite regions due to defective DNA repair."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LABORATORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A laboratory is a facility where tissue samples and fluids are analyzed to detect cancer cells, providing critical diagnostic information."&lt;SEP&gt;"A laboratory is a facility where tissue samples from biopsies are sent for analysis by a pathologist."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laboratory is a facility that conducts tests, such as blood work, to monitor patient health during treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laboratory is a facility where biopsy samples are sent for analysis, including histologic and molecular testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laboratory is a facility where blood, tissue, and other samples are analyzed for diagnostic purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laboratory is where tests like PCR, IHC, and NGS are performed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTEOCYTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osteocyte is a mature bone cell that maintains bone tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISTOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Histology is the evaluation of cell structure under a microscope to classify tumors, such as identifying astrocytomas or oligodendrogliomas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Histology is the microscopic examination of tissue, used to determine cancer grade."&lt;SEP&gt;"Histology is the microscopic study of tissue samples, often referred to as histopathology or hematopathology review, used to diagnose AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Histology is the review of tissue samples to diagnose AML, noting cell appearance and type."&lt;SEP&gt;"Histology is the study of tissue under a microscope, used to describe how abnormal tumor cells look and determine grade."&lt;SEP&gt;"Histology is the study of tissues under a microscope, used to classify RCC subtypes and guide treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Histology is the study of tissues under a microscope, used to classify lung cancer subtypes by examining cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Histology is the study of tissues under a microscope, used to determine tumor characteristics and guide treatment planning for renal cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"The study of the anatomy of cells, tissues, and organs under a microscope, used to make treatment decisions in breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DRE (Digital Rectal Exam) is a follow-up exam recommended 8 to 12 weeks after chemoradiation to check treatment results."&lt;SEP&gt;"DRE (Digital Rectal Exam) is a recommended diagnostic test after anal cancer diagnosis to assess the extent of the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOCKAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blockage is an obstruction in the urinary tract, such as a tumor or stone, detected through pyelogram or other imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER METASTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer metastasis is the spread of cancer to other parts of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELACESTRANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Elacestrant (Orserdu) is a SERD used in endocrine therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVERYONE WITH A PROSTATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Everyone with a prostate is at risk for prostate cancer, regardless of other factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIRST-DEGREE RELATIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A close biological relative, such as a parent or sibling, with increased risk of colorectal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Close biological relative with increased risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Relative."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOSS OF VOICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Loss of voice is a symptom that radiation therapy may relieve if caused by cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YOGA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yoga is a physical and mental practice used to improve flexibility, strength, and relaxation in cancer survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mass is a tumor or growth that can form inside the stomach due to cancer, potentially causing symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISMATCH REPAIR (MMR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MMR is a DNA repair system; defects are tested as biomarkers in recurrent ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mismatch repair (MMR) is a biomarker indicating defects in DNA repair mechanisms, tested in cervical cancer to guide treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mismatch repair is a biomarker test that assesses the function of DNA repair mechanisms, relevant for guiding ovarian cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EYE EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An eye exam is a diagnostic procedure using a slit lamp to examine the retina, optic nerve, and other parts of the eye, crucial for detecting vitreoretinal lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"An eye exam is a test to check for effects of nasopharyngeal cancer on the eyes, recommended before treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"An eye exam is a test used to check for lymphoma involvement in the eyes, which can occur in primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"An eye exam is performed to look at the health of the nerves in the back of the eye, as part of the neurological exam for primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eye exam is a test to check the health of the nerves in the back of the eyes, part of a neurological exam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTEOBLAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osteoblast is a bone-forming cell that synthesizes bone matrix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fluids are bodily liquids whose levels are balanced by the kidneys through filtration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liquids recommended by nutritionists to maintain hydration and nutrition before treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTERNAL GENITALIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"External genitalia are nearby organs that IMRT aims to protect from radiation exposure to reduce side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"External genitalia are organs near the cervix that can be affected by radiation, and IMRT aims to reduce radiation to them."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN IN SIDE OR BACK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pain in side or back is a symptom that may lead to urogram or other imaging tests to investigate kidney or urinary tract problems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER PROGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer prognosis is the likely outcome or course of the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORSERDU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Orserdu is the brand name for elacestrant, a SERD."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEST PRACTICES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Best practices are evidence-based methods from top cancer centers that guide treatment teams in providing optimal care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRECANCEROUS CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Precancerous changes are abnormal alterations in the mucosa of the esophagus that can occur before cancer develops."&lt;SEP&gt;"Precancerous changes are abnormal alterations in the stomach mucosa that occur before cancer develops, often without symptoms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Precancerous changes are abnormal cell changes in the stomach mucosa that may develop into cancer over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR MUTATIONAL BURDEN (TMB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TMB is a measure of the number of mutations per million base pairs of tumor DNA; high TMB (TMB-H) indicates potential responsiveness to immune checkpoint inhibitors."&lt;SEP&gt;"TMB measures the number of mutations in tumor DNA, used as a biomarker for immunotherapy response in recurrent ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutational burden (TMB) is a biomarker measuring the number of mutations in a tumor, potentially indicating responsiveness to immunotherapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutational burden is a biomarker test that counts mutations in tumor DNA, helping to predict response to certain therapies in ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITREORETINAL LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vitreoretinal lymphoma is a form of primary CNS lymphoma that involves the eyes, often forming in the retina or vitreous, and is diagnosed through a thorough eye exam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTEOCLAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osteoclast is a bone-resorbing cell that breaks down bone to release calcium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Waste is the undigested or unused material that the body eliminates. The large intestine prepares waste for removal from the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Waste refers to metabolic byproducts carried away by blood from tissues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Waste refers to metabolic byproducts removed from the blood by the kidneys."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIP JOINTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hip joints are nearby structures that IMRT aims to protect from radiation exposure to minimize treatment-related side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hip joints are structures near the cervix that can be affected by radiation, and IMRT aims to reduce radiation to them."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAMILY HISTORY OF CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Family history of cancer is a factor that may prompt genetic testing to assess inherited risk and guide preventive measures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER SURVIVAL RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer survival rate is the percentage of patients who survive a certain time after diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHINYL ESTRADIOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ethinyl estradiol is a hormone used in high doses to treat breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNDERARMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Underarms are body areas where lymph nodes are checked during physical exams for cancer signs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SÉZARY SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sézary syndrome is a type of cutaneous T-cell lymphoma characterized by abnormal T cells in the blood and skin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AXILLARY LYMPH NODE DISSECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Axillary lymph node dissection is a surgical procedure to remove multiple lymph nodes from the armpit to check for cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emergency department is a hospital unit that provides immediate care for urgent medical conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUNX1::RUNX1T1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RUNX1::RUNX1T1 is a gene rearrangement resulting from a chromosome translocation t(8;21)(q22;q1), an example of a genetic change in AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ostomy is a surgical opening created to divert bodily waste, requiring specialized care and support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EARLY-STAGE STOMACH CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Early-stage stomach cancer is a classification where the tumor has not grown beyond the mucosa, is small (2 cm or less), and is not in lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Early-stage stomach cancer is cancer that has not grown beyond the mucosa layer of the stomach wall."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLATE RECEPTOR ALPHA (FRΑ) EXPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FRα is a protein expressed on some cancer cells; testing guides targeted therapy in recurrent ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Folate receptor alpha expression is a biomarker test that detects a protein on tumor cells, potentially relevant for targeted drug delivery in ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PET/CT SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A whole-body imaging test used to detect cancer by taking detailed pictures of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET/CT scan combines a PET scan with CT to create detailed images, useful for finding cancer that has spread outside the bladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET/CT scan is a combined imaging modality that merges PET and CT technologies for more detailed diagnostic information."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET/CT scan is a combined imaging technique that merges PET and CT scans to provide detailed cross-sectional images, useful for detecting cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET/CT scan is a combined imaging technique that merges PET and CT to provide both metabolic and anatomical information."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET/CT scan is a combined imaging test that merges PET and CT technologies for detailed diagnostic information."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET/CT scan is an imaging method combining positron emission tomography and computed tomography to find cancer cells throughout the body, used to check for spread outside the CNS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSEAL SCAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physeal scar is a line visible in bone after skeletal maturity, marking the former growth plate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTIPLE TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Multiple tumors refer to the presence of more than one tumor in a kidney, which can occur in RCC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIMULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Simulation is a planning session before EBRT where the patient is positioned and CT images are taken for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simulation is a planning session in radiation therapy where a patient is positioned and scanned to create a personalized radiation treatment plan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simulation is a planning session required before radiation treatment begins, where imaging and positioning are done to plan the treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGE BELOW 50&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Age below 50 is a criterion that may make germline testing more appropriate for individuals with bladder cancer, due to higher likelihood of inherited mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER RISK ASSESSMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer risk assessment evaluates factors like HPV status and lifestyle to estimate risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUOXYMESTERONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fluoxymesterone is a hormone used in high doses to treat breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTATE-SPECIFIC ANTIGEN (PSA) TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The PSA test is a blood test that measures the amount of prostate-specific antigen in the bloodstream. High levels may indicate prostate cancer, but it is not diagnostic alone and is often paired with other tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE SCAN ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone Scan Role Education is understanding how bone scans detect spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCOREGIONAL STOMACH CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Locoregional stomach cancer is a classification where cancer has invaded deeper layers of the stomach wall and/or spread to nearby lymph nodes or organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NTRK GENE FUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NTRK gene fusion is a genetic alteration involving NTRK genes, tested as a biomarker to guide treatment with specific inhibitors in ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"NTRK gene fusion is a genetic alteration tested as a biomarker in recurrent ovarian cancer for targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"NTRK gene fusion is a rare genetic alteration in cervical sarcoma, tested to determine eligibility for targeted therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"NTRK gene fusion is a specific biomarker that can be present in thyroid cancer cells, making them eligible for targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLETE BLOOD COUNT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood test measuring red and white blood cells and platelets, recommended in initial testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complete blood count (CBC) is a blood test that measures levels of red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets, providing information about oxygen transport, infection fighting, and bleeding control."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complete blood count (CBC) is a blood test that measures the number of blood cells, including in AML diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complete blood count is a common blood test that measures different components of blood, helping to assess overall health and detect abnormalities related to cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARTILAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cartilage is a connective tissue covering bone ends at joints, part of the epiphysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cartilage is a tough, flexible tissue that covers bone ends and provides structure to parts like the nose and ears."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOTH KIDNEYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Both kidneys can be involved in RCC, indicating bilateral disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AQUAPHOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aquaphor is an over-the-counter ointment recommended to soothe skin irritation and promote healing during radiation therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH GRADE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High grade cancer refers to fast-growing tumors, which may warrant germline testing to identify genetic factors influencing treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER GENETIC TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic testing may identify inherited mutations that increase cervical cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEGESTROL ACETATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Megestrol acetate (Megace ES) is a hormone used in high doses to treat breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTATE CANCER SCREENING TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prostate cancer screening tests are initial tests used to detect the possibility of prostate cancer in undiagnosed individuals, including the PSA test and digital rectal exam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE RECTUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The rectum is the last several inches of the large bowel, holding stool until it exits through the anus, and is located in the pelvis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENT ADVOCACY GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patient Advocacy Group is an organization that represents patient interests, providing education and lobbying for better care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient advocacy group is an organization that supports patients' rights and provides resources."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC STOMACH CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic stomach cancer is a classification where cancer has spread to distant parts of the body, such as the liver, peritoneum, or distant lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RETINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The retina is the back part of the eye that converts light into signals, and it can be a site for lymphoma cell invasion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SARCOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sarcoma is a rare type of primary liver cancer that starts in the blood vessel cells of the liver."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sarcoma is a type of cancer of connective tissues, such as muscles, nerves, fat, blood vessels, and fibrous tissue, which sarcomatoid RCC cells resemble."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sarcoma is a type of cancer that arises in connective tissues, including bone, and is treated at specialized centers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADULT'S FIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An adult's fist is a size comparison used to describe the typical size of a kidney."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SILVADENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Silvadene is an over-the-counter ointment used to soothe skin and aid healing during radiation treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER OF UPPER URINARY TRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer of upper urinary tract is a condition that may increase the need for germline testing due to association with inherited mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER BIOMARKER TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biomarker testing looks for specific proteins or genes in cervical cancer to guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEGACE ES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Megace ES is the brand name for megestrol acetate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVAL RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survival rate refers to the percentage of patients who live for a certain period after diagnosis; prostate cancer has one of the highest survival rates when found early."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AVERAGE PERSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A person without increased risk factors for colon cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Person without increased risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Person."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN OR STIFFNESS IN NECK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pain or stiffness in the neck is a symptom that radiation therapy may relieve if caused by cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASSAGE THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Massage therapy is a complementary treatment involving soft tissue manipulation to relieve pain and stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGIONAL LYMPH NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Regional Lymph Nodes are lymph nodes located near the tumor in the breast, such as under the arm, near the collarbone, or near the breastbone, where breast cancer often spreads first."&lt;SEP&gt;"Regional lymph nodes are found near the breast, and their involvement is key in staging breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Regional lymph nodes are lymph nodes near the stomach that may be affected in locoregional stomach cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Regional lymph nodes are those near the tumor, used in N staging for cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRCA GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BRCA genes are inherited genes whose mutations increase the risk of hereditary ovarian cancer; testing for germline mutations is recommended for all diagnosed patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA genes are specific genes that, when mutated, increase the risk of hereditary cancers, including ovarian cancer. Testing for BRCA mutations is crucial for treatment planning and determining homologous recombination deficiency (HRD) status."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITREOUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The vitreous is the clear gel that fills the eye, and lymphoma cells can invade it, requiring a vitrectomy for diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE FORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone formation, or ossification, is the process of creating new bone, starting in the womb and ending in adolescence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPLE SKIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Apple skin is a metaphor used to describe the thin layer of tissue (renal capsule) covering the kidney."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL OPENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The anal opening is the external orifice of the anal canal, part of the perianal region where anal cancer can develop."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYNCH SYNDROME DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lynch syndrome diagnosis is a condition that prompts genetic testing and counseling to manage increased cancer risks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER IMAGING TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Imaging tests like MRI, CT, and PET scans are used to stage cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTOSTERONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Testosterone is a hormone that may be suppressed in endocrine therapy for those assigned male at birth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testosterone is a male hormone that is targeted for reduction in androgen deprivation therapy for prostate cancer. It is produced primarily by the testicles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testosterone is the main androgen hormone produced by the testicles, which can promote prostate cancer growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTATE CANCER DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prostate cancer diagnosis is the process of confirming the presence of prostate cancer through tests and determining its stage, which guides treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISTANT LYMPH NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Distant lymph nodes are lymph nodes far from the stomach that may be affected in metastatic stomach cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant lymph nodes are lymph nodes located far from the primary tumor, which can be a site of breast cancer metastasis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant lymph nodes are lymph nodes located far from the primary tumor, which can be sites of breast cancer metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYNCH SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An inherited condition caused by mutations in MMR genes, increasing risk of colon, endometrial, and ovarian cancers; testing is recommended for dMMR/MSI-H cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"An inherited condition causing high risk of colon, endometrial, and ovarian cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inherited condition causing high risk of cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lynch Syndrome is a hereditary condition that increases the risk of pancreatic cancer, associated with genetic mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lynch syndrome is a hereditary condition associated with increased risk of ovarian and other cancers, often linked to MMR gene mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lynch syndrome is a hereditary condition that can increase the risk of developing adrenal tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lynch syndrome is a hereditary condition that increases the risk of colon, uterine, ovarian, and other cancers, often causing earlier onset of ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lynch syndrome is a rare inherited condition caused by mutations in MMR genes, increasing risk of colorectal, endometrial, and ovarian cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lynch syndrome is an inherited cancer syndrome associated with mismatch repair deficiency (dMMR) or high microsatellite instability (MSI-H) in rectal tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lynch syndrome is an inherited condition that increases the risk of cancer in the urinary tract, including bladder cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lynch syndrome is an inherited condition that increases the risk of colon cancer and is identified through family health history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lynch syndrome is an inherited genetic condition that increases the risk of developing bladder cancer and other cancers, often prompting genetic testing and counseling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPTIC NERVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Optic nerves connect the eyes to the brain, providing a pathway for lymphoma spread from the brain to the eyes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE REMODELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone remodeling is the continuous process of bone breakdown and rebuilding, maintaining calcium levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEARING TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hearing test evaluates hearing loss, its type and severity, using an audiogram, relevant for head and neck tumor patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"A test to detect hearing loss, its type, severity, and cause, often using an audiogram, relevant for head and neck cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hearing test (audiogram) checks for hearing loss that may result from certain cancer treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hearing test is a medical procedure to detect hearing loss, its type, severity, and cause, relevant for head and neck cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNOSUPPRESSANT USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immunosuppressant use is a risk factor for anal cancer, as it weakens the immune system's ability to fight HPV and other infections."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUITTING SMOKING SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Quitting smoking support involves counseling and medicines to help individuals stop smoking, reducing cancer risk and improving treatment outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgery for cervical cancer may involve removing the tumor, cervix, or uterus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POSITRON EMISSION TOMOGRAPHY (PET) SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A scan using a radioactive tracer injected into a vein to highlight cancer cells as bright spots, often combined with CT for a PET/CT scan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTATE CANCER TREATMENT PLANNING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prostate cancer treatment planning is the process where health care providers use test results to develop a personalized treatment strategy for the patient."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CARE OFFICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary care office is a medical practice where patients receive routine health care and referrals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAGET'S DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paget's disease of the nipple is a rare form of breast cancer that affects the skin of the nipple and areola."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYTOGENETICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cytogenetics is a method used in AML mutation testing to analyze chromosomes for abnormalities, often through karyotype."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTOMY SUPPORT GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ostomy support group is a community of individuals with ostomies who share experiences and advice."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood system is a pathway through which cancer cells can spread to distant parts of the body, leading to metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITRECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vitrectomy is a procedure to remove a tiny amount of vitreous from the eye for testing, which can confirm primary CNS lymphoma diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC TESTING FOR INHERITED MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic testing for inherited mutations is a different type of DNA testing than tumor mutation testing, looking at germline mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUDIOGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A graph showing results of a pure-tone hearing test, used to assess hearing loss."&lt;SEP&gt;"An audiogram is a graph showing results of a pure-tone hearing test, used to assess hearing loss."&lt;SEP&gt;"Audiogram is a graph showing the results of a pure-tone hearing test, used to document hearing loss."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONFORMAL RADIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Conformal radiation refers to radiation beams that are shaped to the tumor, a feature of all types of EBRT."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HCC, or hepatocellular carcinoma, is the most common type of primary liver cancer in adults. It is the focus of the patient guideline and is characterized by the uncontrolled growth of liver cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER FOLLOW-UP CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follow-up care after cervical cancer treatment includes regular check-ups and monitoring for recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAZOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A tool similar to a razor used in certain biopsy procedures to remove skin samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTATE CANCER MONITORING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prostate cancer monitoring involves regular tests and check-ups to track the cancer's status, especially during active surveillance or after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREGNANCY TEST ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pregnancy Test Role Education is understanding why pregnancy tests are done before treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHATIC SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymphatic system is a network of tissues and organs that helps the body fight infections and disease, part of the immune system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphatic system is a network of vessels and nodes through which cancer cells can spread, leading to lymph node involvement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphatic system is a network that helps spread cancer cells, involved in metastasis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphatic system is part of the body's immune system, and lymphocytes are an important part of it, as mentioned in the context of CBCL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Part of the immune system, made up of tissues and organs that help the body fight infection and disease, composed mostly of lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lymphatic system is a major part of the body's immune system, including lymph vessels, lymph nodes, tonsils, thymus, spleen, and bone marrow, which helps fight infection and filter foreign materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lymphatic system is a network of organs and vessels that fights infections and circulates lymph fluid, through which cancer cells can spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lymphatic system is a network of tissues and organs, including lymph nodes, spleen, thymus, and bone marrow, that helps fight infection and cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lymphatic system is a network of vessels that carry lymph, a clear fluid that gives cells water and food and contains white blood cells that fight germs. It is involved in the spread of cancer from the liver."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lymphatic system is a network through which esophageal cancer can spread to lymph nodes and other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lymphatic system is part of the immune system, consisting of tissues and organs like lymph nodes, spleen, bone marrow, thymus, and tonsils, that help fight infection and disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lymphatic system is part of the immune system, made up of tissues and organs that help the body fight infection and disease, and is composed mostly of lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lymphatic system is part of the immune system, where lymphoma originates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-GRADE SEROUS CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-grade serous carcinoma is a common and aggressive type of ovarian cancer, typically treated with surgery and chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SLIT LAMP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A slit lamp is a microscope with a bright light used by eye doctors to examine the retina, optic nerve, and other parts of the eye."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEXT-GENERATION SEQUENCING (NGS) METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Next-generation sequencing is a detailed method to determine DNA sequences, identifying mutations that other methods might miss."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPATITIS C&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hepatitis C (HCV) is a liver disease caused by a virus, which can be reactivated by some cancer treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRACTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fractions are small doses of radiation given during treatment, typically administered Monday through Friday for 5-6 weeks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CIRRHOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cirrhosis is a chronic liver disease characterized by scarring of the liver, where liver cells are replaced by scar tissue. It is a major risk factor for liver cancer and can be caused by hepatitis B or C, alcohol use, NAFLD, genetic hemochromatosis, and other conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cirrhosis is a condition of the liver characterized by scarring and impaired function. It is mentioned as a risk factor for developing liver cancer, and individuals with cirrhosis are recommended to enroll in liver cancer screening programs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER SURVIVORSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer survivorship focuses on long-term health and quality of life after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOCTOR'S OFFICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A location where excision biopsies can be performed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTATE CANCER SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prostate cancer screening is the process of testing undiagnosed individuals to detect potential prostate cancer early, using PSA tests and digital rectal exams."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE PELVIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The pelvis is the area between the hip bones, below the abdomen, containing organs such as the bladder, rectum, and reproductive organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVORSHIP CLINIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survivorship Clinic is a specialized clinic that provides follow-up care and monitoring for cancer survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEST RESULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Outcomes of medical tests, such as blood tests or imaging, which are stored in folders and in the binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Test results are findings from blood tests and biopsies used to determine treatment plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Test results are findings from diagnostic tests that determine treatment plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Test results are outcomes from diagnostic tests like biopsy and imaging, used to determine treatment plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Test results are outcomes from imaging and biopsy that determine cancer stage and treatment plan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Test results are outcomes from imaging, biopsy, and other tests that determine the treatment plan for stomach cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Test results are the outcomes of diagnostic tests that inform treatment decisions and are accessible through patient portals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Test results are the outcomes of diagnostic tests, such as imaging and biopsies, used to guide treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Test results from blood tests and biopsies are used to determine treatment plans for CML and NSCLC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Test results from blood tests, imaging, and biopsy are used to determine treatment plans for esophageal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-GRADE ENDOMETRIOID CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-grade endometrioid carcinoma is a common type of epithelial ovarian cancer, with high-grade cancer cells that grow and spread more rapidly than low-grade cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-grade endometrioid carcinoma is a type of ovarian cancer with similar treatment approaches to high-grade serous carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPHTHALMOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ophthalmologist is a doctor who specializes in eye care, relevant for CNS lymphoma that may affect the eyes."&lt;SEP&gt;"An ophthalmologist is a doctor who specializes in eye diseases, relevant for CNS lymphoma that may affect the eyes."&lt;SEP&gt;"An ophthalmologist is an eye specialist who performs thorough eye exams using a slit lamp to detect lymphoma in the eyes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION (PCR) TECHNIQUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymerase chain reaction is a sensitive technique to amplify DNA or RNA, detecting rare abnormal cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNG FUNCTION TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lung function tests (PFTs) measure how well the lungs work, including air capacity, flow, and gas exchange, important for cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT SESSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment sessions are individual radiation therapy appointments, typically 25-30 sessions over 5-6 weeks for anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPATITIS B VIRUS (HBV)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hepatitis B virus (HBV) is a virus that causes hepatitis, a type of liver disease. It is spread by contact with blood and bodily fluids and can lead to chronic hepatitis, cirrhosis, liver failure, and liver cancer. Chronic HBV infection is a significant risk factor for liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer education aims to inform about prevention, symptoms, and treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A needle inserted into a vein to inject the tracer during a PET scan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLEAR CELL RCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clear cell RCC (ccRCC) is the most common subtype of renal cell carcinoma, occurring in about 7 out of 10 people with RCC, characterized by pale or clear cells under a microscope."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNKNOWN REASONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cause of most colon cancers, which are not inherited."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cause of most colon cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cause."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAPILLARY THYROID CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Papillary thyroid cancer is a common type of thyroid cancer, with NIFTP previously known as the encapsulated follicular variant of this cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Papillary thyroid cancer is a differentiated type of thyroid cancer that may respond to RAI therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Papillary thyroid cancer is the most common type of thyroid cancer, often slow-growing, with subtypes like follicular variant, tall-cell, hobnail, and diffuse sclerosing. Treatment may involve surgery or active surveillance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LENGTH OF LIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Length of life refers to survival duration, a factor in treatment decision-making."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENT PORTALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Online systems, such as MyChart or health record accounts, that allow patients to access test results, track appointments, and communicate with their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portals are online platforms that allow patients to access their test results and medical records. They are recommended as a way to stay informed about health status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portals are online systems for accessing test results and health information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portals are online systems for viewing records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portals are online systems that allow patients to access their test results and communicate with care teams."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portals are online systems that allow patients to access their test results and communicate with healthcare providers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portals are online systems that allow patients to access their test results and medical information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portals are online systems that allow patients to access their test results and medical records, facilitating informed decision-making."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portals are online systems that allow patients to access their test results and medical records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portals are online systems to view test results and download records for a medical binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portals are online systems, such as MyChart or health record accounts, that allow patients to access test results, track appointments, and communicate with their care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GYNECOLOGIC ONCOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gynecologic oncologist is a doctor who specializes in surgery and chemotherapy for gynecologic cancers, including ovarian cancer. They should perform the initial surgery when possible."&lt;SEP&gt;"A gynecologic oncologist is a medical expert specializing in surgery and chemotherapy for female reproductive cancers, including cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A gynecologic oncologist is a specialist in cancers of the female reproductive system, including cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A gynecologic oncologist is a surgeon specializing in cancers of the female reproductive organs, essential for performing ovarian cancer surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOACTIVE DRUG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A radioactive drug is injected into a vein during PET imaging to make cancer cells appear as bright spots on scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radioactive drug is injected into a vein during a PET scan to highlight cancer cells as bright spots."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radioactive drug, also known as a tracer, is used in PET scans to detect cancer cells by showing areas of high metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radioactive drug, or tracer, is injected for PET scans to detect cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer diagnosis is the process of confirming cancer presence via biopsy and testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIETICIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dietician is a professional who provides dietary advice to ensure adequate nutrition for cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FROG-LEGGED POSITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The frog-legged position is a body positioning technique used during simulation and treatment for IMRT, with knees out to the side."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPATITIS C VIRUS (HCV)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hepatitis C virus (HCV) is a virus that causes hepatitis, a type of liver disease. It is spread by contact with blood and bodily fluids and can lead to chronic hepatitis, cirrhosis, liver failure, and liver cancer. Chronic HCV infection is a significant risk factor for liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER RESEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer research seeks to improve prevention, detection, and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHATIC FLUID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A fluid that travels through lymph nodes and filters substances, potentially carrying cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clear fluid that gives cells water and food and helps fight germs, draining from breast tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1A is a specific stage of ovarian cancer where cancer is confined to one ovary with an intact capsule and no cancer cells in ascites or washings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREGNANCY PLANNING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pregnancy Planning is the process of deciding when to conceive after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSURANCE FORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Documents related to health insurance coverage, which are organized in folders within a medical binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are administrative documents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are documents organized in a medical binder for administrative purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are documents related to health coverage that patients need to organize for managing cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are documents related to health coverage that patients need to organize."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are documents related to health coverage, which patients need to organize for managing medical costs and claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are documents related to health coverage, which patients need to organize for treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are documents related to health insurance claims and coverage. The text suggests organizing these forms as part of managing medical records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are documents related to health insurance coverage that patients need to organize for medical billing and claims."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are documents related to health insurance coverage that patients need to organize for medical care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are documents related to health insurance coverage, which patients need to organize for treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are medical documents that patients should organize as part of their care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are paperwork related to health coverage for medical services and treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are paperwork related to healthcare coverage, which patients need to organize for treatment access."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are part of medical documents that need to be organized for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance forms are part of medical documents that patients should keep organized."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYSTERECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hysterectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the uterus, which affects the approach to brachytherapy applicator placement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hysterectomy is a surgical procedure that removes the uterus and cervix, potentially causing surgical menopause if ovaries are removed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hysterectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the uterus, and considerations about keeping ovaries are discussed in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hysterectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the uterus, often used for early-stage cervical cancer when fertility preservation is not desired. It eliminates the possibility of future pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hysterectomy is surgery to remove the uterus, often combined with BSO for ovarian cancer treatment, making pregnancy impossible."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hysterectomy is surgical removal of the uterus, sometimes used to treat cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgery to remove the uterus (including the cervix), with types including extrafascial, modified radical, and radical hysterectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSMA (prostate-specific membrane antigen) is a protein found on the surface of prostate cancer cells, used as a target for tracers in imaging and therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer treatment involves various therapies and may affect fertility, requiring specialist consultation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANNABIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cannabis is a substance that may affect the amount of anesthesia used during surgery, as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cannabis is a substance that might affect anesthesia amounts during surgery, relevant for cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cannabis use might affect the amount of anesthesia needed during surgery, indicating a potential impact on medical procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPUTER SOFTWARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Computer software is used in treatment planning to calculate the best radiation dose and number of treatments based on CT images."&lt;SEP&gt;"Computer software is used with CT images to create a treatment plan for radiation therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALCOHOL USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alcohol use is a risk factor for head and neck cancer and can limit treatment effectiveness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alcohol use refers to the consumption of alcoholic beverages. High alcohol use can cause damage to the liver, leading to cirrhosis and increasing the risk of developing liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER STATISTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer statistics include incidence, mortality, and survival data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NODAL DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition where cancer has spread to the lymph nodes, also referred to as regional squamous cell skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nodal disease is cancer present in lymph nodes, rare in bone cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAPILLARY RCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Papillary RCC (PRCC) is the most common subtype of non-clear cell RCC, occurring in about 1 out of 10 people with RCC, characterized by finger-like growths under a microscope."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECIALIST OFFICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Specialist office is a medical practice where patients see doctors with expertise in specific conditions like cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYLLODES TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phyllodes tumor is a rare breast tumor that grows in the connective tissue, which can be benign or malignant."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEREDITARY CANCER SYNDROMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hereditary cancer syndromes are conditions passed from parent to child that increase cancer risk, including leukemia predisposition syndromes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACTIVE LIFESTYLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An active lifestyle refers to maintaining physical activity and engagement, possible for ostomy patients with proper guidance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL RECORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Comprehensive documents of a patient's health history, including tests and treatments, stored in folders in a binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documents including blood tests, imaging results, and cancer reports organized in a medical binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical Records are documents compiled in a binder for organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are comprehensive documents containing a patient's health history, test results, and treatment details. The text advises keeping copies and organizing them for reference."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are comprehensive documents containing a patient's health history, test results, and treatment details."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are comprehensive documents of a patient's health history, test results, and treatments, essential for coordinated care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are documents containing a patient's health history, test results, and treatment details, important for care coordination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are documents containing a patient's health history, test results, and treatment information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are documents containing a patient's health information, including test results and treatment history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are documents containing a patient's health information, test results, and treatment history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are documents containing patient health information and treatment history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are documents containing patient health information, including test results and treatment history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are documents that patients should organize, including test results and treatment history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are organized documents containing patient health information, test results, and treatment history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are part of medical documents that patients should keep organized."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records are part of the documents that patients should keep organized for their cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical records include blood tests, imaging results, and reports organized in a medical binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BILATERAL SALPINGO-OOPHORECTOMY (BSO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy is surgery to remove both ovaries and fallopian tubes, commonly performed with hysterectomy for ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSMA-PET SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSMA-PET scan is a diagnostic imaging technique that uses tracers targeting PSMA to detect prostate cancer recurrence or determine suitability for targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER PROGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer prognosis is the predicted outcome based on cancer type and stage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EASTERN COOPERATIVE ONCOLOGY GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) is an organization that developed a scale to rate performance status in cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INK MARKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ink marks (tattoos) on the skin help position the body accurately for daily radiation treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ink marks on the skin are used to position the body accurately for daily radiation treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-ALCOHOLIC FATTY LIVER DISEASE (NAFLD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD) is a condition where fat builds up in the liver in people who drink little or no alcohol. It can lead to cirrhosis and is a risk factor for liver cancer, often associated with high weight, diabetes, and high cholesterol."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER DISPARITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer disparities refer to differences in incidence and outcomes among populations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUNBURNS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A common cause of squamous cell skin cancer, resulting from overexposure to the sun."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHROMOPHOBE RCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chromophobe RCC is a subtype of non-clear cell RCC with pale but larger cells than clear cells, having distinct microscopic appearance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIRTH CONTROL ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Birth Control Role Education is understanding the role of contraception in treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bone scan is a nuclear imaging test used to detect bone abnormalities, including cancer spread to bone. It may not be needed if FDG-PET/CT clearly shows bone cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bone scan is an imaging test to detect cancer spread to bones, using a radioactive tracer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone Scan is an imaging test that uses a radiotracer to detect cancer spread to bones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone scan is a diagnostic imaging procedure using a radioactive tracer to detect cancer spread to bones, often used for monitoring or when bone metastasis is suspected."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone scan is a diagnostic imaging test performed when symptoms suggest cancer may have spread to the bones, helping to detect metastatic disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone scan is a diagnostic imaging test that uses a radiotracer to detect areas of bone damage, which may be caused by cancer, cancer treatment, previous injuries, or other health issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone scan is a diagnostic imaging test used to detect whether cancer has spread to the bones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone scan is an imaging test that detects cancer spread to bones by injecting a radioactive tracer and imaging the skeleton."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone scan is an imaging test that may not be needed if FDG-PET/CT clearly shows cancer in the bone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone scan is an imaging test that uses a radiotracer to detect areas of bone damage, which show up as bright spots, and takes about 30 minutes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone scan is an imaging test to detect cancer in bones, potentially unnecessary if FDG-PET/CT clearly shows bone involvement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone scan is an imaging test used to detect cancer spread to bones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone scan is an imaging test using a radioactive tracer to detect cancer spread to bones, often used when bone pain or high risk of bone metastases is present."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTACT INFORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contact information includes details such as phone numbers and emails for the care team, which patients should keep organized."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contact information includes names and details of team members, kept for easy communication."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contact information is a list of care team details that patients should maintain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contact information is a list of care team members' details that patients should keep updated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contact information is a list of details for care team members, important for emergencies and coordination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contact information is a list of details for care team members, kept accessible for emergencies and coordination of care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contact information is a list of details for care team members, kept for emergencies and coordination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contact information is a list of names and details for each care team member, helping patients know whom to reach with questions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contact information refers to details of care team members, kept accessible for emergencies and coordination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY-SPARING SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility-sparing surgery is a type of procedure, like trachelectomy, that preserves the ability to have children."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility-sparing surgery is an option for early ovarian cancer, removing one or both ovaries and fallopian tubes while preserving the uterus for potential pregnancy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER STAGING OVERVIEW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer staging overview is a general description of how staging is done for bone cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone cancer staging overview is a general explanation of staging for bone cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANESTHESIOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A physician who administers anesthesia to prevent pain during surgery or procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesiologist gives anesthesia to prevent pain during surgery or procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesiologist is a medical professional who performs pre-anesthesia assessments and administers anesthesia during surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN IRRITATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skin irritation is a common side effect of radiation therapy at the treatment site, including tenderness, redness, and sores."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin irritation is a side effect of brachytherapy and EBRT, occurring near the treatment area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC HEMOCHROMATOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic hemochromatosis is an inherited condition that causes the liver to store too much iron from food. This can lead to liver damage and cirrhosis, increasing the risk of liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER IN PREGNANCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer in pregnancy requires special management to protect both mother and fetus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LESION EXAMINATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An inspection of suspicious skin areas, part of testing for CSCC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSLOCATION RCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Translocation RCC is a subtype of renal cell carcinoma found at all ages but more common in children or younger adults, characterized by unique gene fusions that promote cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE BLADDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The bladder is an organ in the pelvis that stores urine, and is the site of bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALDOSTERONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aldosterone is a hormone produced by the adrenal cortex that helps regulate blood pressure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aldosterone is a hormone that regulates blood pressure, produced by the adrenal cortex."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LATE EFFECTS CLINIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Late Effects Clinic is a clinic that focuses on managing long-term side effects of cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSRECTAL ULTRASOUND (TRUS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transrectal ultrasound (TRUS) is a specific ultrasound procedure where a probe is inserted into the rectum to visualize the prostate, often used to guide biopsies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HERBALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Herbals are plant-based products used for medicinal purposes. The text warns that some herbals can interact with medicines prescribed by the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Herbals are plant-based supplements a patient takes, listed in medical history for bladder cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Herbals are plant-based supplements a patient takes, listed in medical history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Herbals are plant-based supplements that may interact with cancer treatments and should be reported to the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Herbals are plant-based supplements that may interact with prescribed medicines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Herbals are plant-based supplements that patients may use, which can interact with cancer treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Herbals are plant-based supplements that patients may use, which can interact with prescribed cancer treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Herbals are plant-based supplements that patients should disclose, as they may interact with prescribed medicines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEBULKING SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Debulking or cytoreductive surgery aims to remove as much cancer as possible when it has spread beyond the ovaries, potentially involving nearby organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KEY POINTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Key points are important summary statements about bone cancer testing, treatment, and fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Key points are important summary statements about primary CNS lymphoma, including its nature, symptoms, and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Key points are important summary statements that highlight essential information about bladder cancer diagnosis, treatment, and patient decision-making."&lt;SEP&gt;"Key points are summaries of important information presented in each chapter of the NCCN Guidelines for Patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Key points are the main takeaways from the text, emphasizing that lung cancer starts in lung cells and that regular screening can help find it early."&lt;SEP&gt;"Summary of main topics discussed in the guide, including testing, treatment, and survivorship."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SLEEP ISSUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sleep issues are disturbances in sleep patterns that can occur in cancer patients due to distress or treatment side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sleep issues refer to problems with sleeping, such as insomnia, which can be part of distress in cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN WHILE URINATING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pain while urinating is a short-term side effect of radiation therapy for anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 4 PRIMARY BILIARY CHOLANGITIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 4 primary biliary cholangitis is an advanced stage of a chronic liver disease that affects the bile ducts, leading to liver damage and cirrhosis. It is a risk factor for developing liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER IN YOUNG WOMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer in young women may have different treatment considerations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAD-TO-TOE SKIN EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A complete skin examination to look for other lesions after a CSCC diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNCLASSIFIED RCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unclassified RCC describes cancer cells that do not match any known subtype or contain more than one subtype, making classification difficult."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INHERITED CANCER SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A disorder increasing cancer risk, such as Lynch syndrome or FAP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Disorder increasing cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Disorder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR THYROID CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follicular thyroid cancer is a differentiated type of thyroid cancer that may respond to RAI therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELIGIOUS BELIEFS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Religious beliefs are personal values that may influence treatment choices."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRI-TRUS FUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MRI-TRUS fusion is a technique that combines MRI images with real-time ultrasound to improve biopsy precision by providing a more detailed view of the prostate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD RELATIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood relatives are family members related by birth whose health history is relevant for genetic risk assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood relatives are family members related by birth, whose health history informs family history for cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood relatives are family members related by birth, whose health history is important for assessing cancer risk and other diseases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood relatives are family members related by birth, whose health history is important for genetic risk assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood relatives are family members related by birth, whose health history is relevant for assessing genetic risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood relatives are family members related by genes, whose health history is important for risk assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood relatives are family members who may carry the same germline mutations, relevant for genetic testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood relatives are family members who share genetic material, and having close relatives with certain cancers increases pancreatic cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood relatives are family members whose blood or tissue samples are tested for HLA matching."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood relatives of someone with CLL can have a higher chance of developing CLL themselves, indicating a genetic or familial risk factor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood relatives of someone with CLL have a higher chance of developing the disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Family members related by blood whose health history is considered in family history assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNILATERAL SALPINGO-OOPHORECTOMY (USO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unilateral salpingo-oophorectomy is surgery to remove one ovary and its fallopian tube, an option for cancer confined to one ovary."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SARCOMA CANCER CENTER NEARBY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sarcoma cancer center nearby is a specialized facility that patients may seek for bone cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEARING LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition detected by hearing tests, characterized by reduced ability to hear."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hearing loss is a condition where a person's ability to hear is reduced, which can be caused by head and neck tumors or their treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hearing loss is a potential side effect of cisplatin, affecting auditory function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEXUAL HEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sexual health concerns are addressed during cancer treatment to manage side effects and maintain quality of life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sexual health is a long-term aspect affected by radiation therapy for cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sexual health is a long-term aspect of health that can be affected by radiation therapy for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sexual health refers to the management of sexual side effects after anal cancer treatment, including erectile dysfunction, vaginal dryness, and pain during sex."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALPHA-1-ANTITRYPSIN DEFICIENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alpha-1-antitrypsin deficiency is a genetic condition that can cause liver disease, including cirrhosis, and is a risk factor for liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER IN OLDER WOMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer in older women may be diagnosed at later stages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSA TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSA testing refers to the measurement of prostate-specific antigen levels in the blood to screen for potential prostate issues, including cancer. It is a warning sign that may prompt further testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1B&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1B is a specific stage of ovarian cancer where cancer is present in both ovaries with intact capsules and no cancer cells in ascites or washings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREASTFEEDING CONSIDERATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breastfeeding Consideration is the need to avoid certain treatments if breastfeeding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTATE BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical procedure using a hollow needle to remove tissue cores from the prostate or a metastasis for laboratory analysis to detect cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostate biopsy is a specific biopsy procedure where core samples are taken from the prostate gland, typically guided by ultrasound, to evaluate for cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEART DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chronic disease that may run in families, relevant to family health history."&lt;SEP&gt;"A disease that can run in families, relevant to family history assessment for health risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart disease is a condition affecting the heart and blood vessels. It is mentioned as a health issue to inquire about in family history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart disease is a condition that may run in families and is relevant to family history assessments for overall health risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart disease is a health condition that may be present in family history, relevant for overall health assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart disease is a health condition that may run in families and is asked about as part of family history assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart disease is a health condition that may run in families and is part of family history assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart disease is a health condition that may run in families and is relevant to family history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart disease is a health condition that may run in families, asked about in family history assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart disease is a health condition that may run in families, part of family health history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart disease is a health condition that may run in families, relevant to family history assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart disease is a health issue in family history that may indicate genetic risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart disease is a longer-term side effect of systemic therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart disease is a potential long-term side effect of chemotherapy. It can develop years after treatment and requires ongoing cardiac monitoring."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IN VITRO FERTILIZATION (IVF)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"In vitro fertilization is an assisted reproductive technique where eggs are fertilized with sperm in a lab, enabling pregnancy after BSO using own or donor eggs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERIENCED SURGEON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An experienced surgeon is a medical professional with expertise in performing specific cancer surgeries, sought for better outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Experienced surgeon is a medical professional recommended to perform biopsies at the treatment center."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIVER DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liver disease is a broad term encompassing conditions that impair liver function, including cirrhosis and hepatitis. The text notes that living with liver disease is challenging but possible to manage, as illustrated by a personal anecdote."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liver disease is a condition affecting liver function, which can be caused by hepatitis B or C viruses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOWEL FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bowel function is a long-term aspect affected by radiation therapy for cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bowel function is a long-term aspect of health that can be affected by radiation therapy for anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALPHA-FETOPROTEIN (AFP) TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The alpha-fetoprotein (AFP) test is a blood test that checks for the protein AFP. An elevated or rising AFP level may be a sign of primary liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER IN IMMUNOCOMPROMISED PATIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immunocompromised patients have higher risk of cervical cancer due to weakened immune systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYMPTOMS AND QUALITY OF LIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Symptoms and quality of life assessments involve evaluating urinary, bowel, and sexual issues and their impact on daily activities, providing a holistic view of patient well-being."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RENAL MEDULLARY CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Renal medullary carcinoma (RMC) is a rare subtype of non-clear cell RCC found in young people of African descent who carry sickle cell trait or disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOVERNMENT HEALTH AGENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Government health agency is a public organization that provides guidelines and resources for cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANGIOSARCOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Angiosarcoma is a rare cancer that arises in the lining of blood or lymph vessels, sometimes occurring in the breast."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THOSE WITH OVARIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Those with ovaries are individuals who may become pregnant, requiring pregnancy tests and birth control during cancer treatment to prevent harm."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIABETES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chronic disease that may run in families, relevant to family health history."&lt;SEP&gt;"A disease that can run in families, relevant to family history assessment for health risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes is a chronic condition that may be hereditary and is considered in family history evaluations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes is a condition where the body has problems processing sugar, which can increase the risk of developing NAFLD and liver cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes is a health condition that increases the risk of developing pancreatic cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes is a health condition that may be present in family history, relevant for overall health assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes is a health condition that may run in families and is asked about as part of family history assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes is a health condition that may run in families and is part of family history assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes is a health condition that may run in families, asked about in family history assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes is a health condition that may run in families, part of family health history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes is a health condition that may run in families, relevant to family history assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes is a health issue in family history that may indicate genetic risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes is a metabolic disease characterized by high blood sugar. It is listed as a health issue to ask about in family history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes is a metabolic disease that may be hereditary and is part of family health history."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAPAROTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical approach using a traditional large incision through the abdomen for procedures like hysterectomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laparotomy is a surgical method involving a long abdominal incision, commonly used for ovarian cancer staging and cytoreductive surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTASIS BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastasis biopsy is a procedure to sample tissue from areas where cancer has spread, such as lymph nodes or bones, to assess the extent of disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIRTH PARENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Birth parents are the biological parents from whom germline mutations may be inherited."&lt;SEP&gt;"Birth parents are the biological parents from whom inherited mutations may come, distinct from tumor mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIRUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Virus is a microscopic infectious agent, such as HBV or HCV, that can cause disease and be reactivated by cancer treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLADDER FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bladder function is a long-term aspect affected by radiation therapy for cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bladder function is a long-term aspect of health that can be affected by radiation therapy for anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENT GUIDELINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A patient guideline is a document or resource designed to educate patients about a specific disease, its risk factors, screening, and treatment options, such as the one on liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND FERTILITY PRESERVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility preservation options may be considered for cervical cancer patients of reproductive age."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD AND URINE TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood and urine tests are laboratory analyses that detect biomarkers, such as PSA, to screen for prostate issues. Additional tests like 4Kscore, PHI, and ExoDx may be used for further evaluation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLEAR CELL PAPILLARY RENAL CELL TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clear cell papillary renal cell tumor is a recently defined type of renal cell carcinoma with distinct characteristics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY PRESERVATION ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility Preservation Role Education is understanding the importance of preserving fertility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAPAROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Laparoscopy is a minimally invasive surgical method using small incisions, used in select ovarian cancer cases, requiring an experienced gynecologic oncologist."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF CHICAGO MEDICINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Chicago Medicine is a medical institution that provided images illustrating PSMA-PET scan findings in prostate cancer cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH CARE TEAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health care team includes doctors, nurses, and other professionals who provide medical care and support during cancer diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care team includes providers who discuss next steps and treatment with the patient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care team is the group of medical professionals who interact with patients, answer questions, and guide care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALLERGIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Allergies are adverse reactions to drugs or medicines that are assessed during pre-anesthesia evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Allergies are health conditions that may prevent some people from having a contrast agent in a CT scan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTI-CANCER MEDICINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anti-cancer medicines are drugs used in chemotherapy to kill cancer cells, often given intravenously."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY LIVER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary liver cancer is cancer that starts in the liver, as opposed to secondary liver cancer which spreads from other parts of the body. HCC is the most common type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND SEXUAL HEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer and its treatment can affect sexual health, requiring supportive care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;4KSCORE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"4Kscore is a blood biomarker test that measures four prostate-specific markers to assess the risk of aggressive prostate cancer, used as an adjunct to PSA testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUMARATE HYDRATASE-DEFICIENT RCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fumarate hydratase-deficient RCC is a recently defined type of renal cell carcinoma associated with genetic mutations in the fumarate hydratase gene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL ADENOCARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anal adenocarcinoma is a rare type of anal cancer that starts in glandular cells, distinct from squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC COUNSELING SERVICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic Counseling Service is a service that provides risk assessment and counseling for hereditary cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLIOMA DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glioma diagnosis is the process of identifying a glioma brain tumor, which can be frightening and overwhelming."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL STAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A procedure to surgically remove and test lymph nodes before treatment to determine the extent of cancer spread, often using minimally invasive methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical staging is the most accurate way to stage ovarian cancer, involving tissue sampling during surgery to detect microscopic metastases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical staging, also called pathologic staging, is the process of determining cancer stage based on examination of removed tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOACTIVE TRACER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A radioactive tracer is a substance injected into the bloodstream that accumulates in areas of bone damage or cancer, enabling imaging via special cameras."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radioactive tracer is a substance used in PET and bone scans to highlight cancerous cells or areas of bone damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer center is a facility specializing in bone cancer treatment, where biopsies should be performed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPRODUCTIVE SPECIALISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reproductive specialists are medical professionals who help cancer patients with fertility preservation and reproductive health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAVENOUS ADMINISTRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intravenous administration is a method of delivering chemotherapy drugs directly into a vein, commonly used for mitomycin and cisplatin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intravenous administration is a method of delivering chemotherapy medicines slowly into the body through a vein."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECONDARY LIVER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Secondary liver cancer is when cancer from other parts of the body spreads to the liver, making it a metastatic condition rather than originating in the liver."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND MENTAL HEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer diagnosis and treatment can impact mental health, needing psychological support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PHI (Prostate Health Index) is a blood test that combines PSA isoforms to improve prostate cancer risk prediction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELOC-MUTATED RCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ELOC (formerly TCEB1)-mutated RCC is a recently defined type of renal cell carcinoma characterized by mutations in the ELOC gene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATHOLOGIST&quot;&lt;|(&quot;ENTITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HYPERPLASTIC POLYPS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"category"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW-IODINE DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A low-iodine diet is required for 1-2 weeks before RAI therapy to enhance iodine uptake by thyroid cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIRITUAL BELIEFS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spiritual beliefs are personal values that may influence treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLIOMA CURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glioma cure refers to the possibility of treating and eliminating a glioma, a question addressed in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OMENTUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The omentum is a fatty layer of tissue covering abdominal organs, which may be removed during ovarian cancer surgery to check for spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"The omentum is a fatty tissue layer covering abdominal organs, often removed during surgical staging for ovarian cancer due to spread risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIQUID BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood sample test to look for cancer cells in the blood, used as an alternative to traditional tissue biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A liquid biopsy is a blood test that looks for cancer cells in the bloodstream, offering a less invasive alternative to tissue biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liquid biopsy is a blood test that detects cancer DNA or cells, offering a less invasive way to monitor cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liquid biopsy is a method of biomarker testing using blood samples to detect tumor DNA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABNORMAL CELL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal cell is a cancer cell that PCR can detect among many normal cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Abnormal cell is a cancer cell that PCR can detect with high sensitivity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TNM STAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TNM staging is a system used to describe the extent of cancer spread, including tumor size (T), lymph node involvement (N), and metastasis (M). It is applied to squamous cell carcinoma of the nasopharynx."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORAL ADMINISTRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oral administration is a method of delivering chemotherapy medicines by mouth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oral administration is a method of taking chemotherapy drugs by mouth, such as capecitabine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CIRRHOSIS (WITHOUT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cirrhosis (without) refers to individuals who do not have cirrhosis but may still have risk factors for liver cancer, such as chronic hepatitis B infection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND NUTRITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutrition plays a role in supporting cervical cancer patients during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOPSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IsoPSA is a blood test that analyzes structural variants of PSA to enhance prostate cancer detection accuracy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SARCOMATOID RCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sarcomatoid RCC (sRCC) is a form of renal cell carcinoma where cells resemble sarcoma, occurring in less than a fraction of RCC tumors, growing quickly and spreading more easily."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1C&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1C is a specific stage of ovarian cancer where cancer is in one or both ovaries with additional factors such as surgical spill, capsule rupture, or cancer cells in ascites or washings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT AVOIDANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment Avoidance is the decision to skip certain therapies during pregnancy or breastfeeding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CBC (COMPLETE BLOOD COUNT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CBC is a blood test that measures different components of blood, such as red and white blood cells and platelets, used in the evaluation of ovarian cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE (PELVIS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph nodes in the pelvis are common sites of prostate cancer spread, as shown in PET/CT and PSMA-PET scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gene mutation is a change in DNA sequence that can be targeted by therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARAPHARYNGEAL SPACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The parapharyngeal space is a triangular area near the pharynx, between the base of the skull and the hyoid bone. It contains fat, blood vessels, nerves, lymph nodes, and parts of the salivary gland."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW ANTERIOR RESECTION (LAR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low anterior resection (LAR) is a type of transabdominal surgery for tumors in the mid to upper rectum, removing part of the colon and possibly creating a colostomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRONIC HEPATITIS B&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chronic hepatitis B is a long-term infection with the hepatitis B virus that can lead to cirrhosis, liver failure, and liver cancer, and is a key risk factor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chronic hepatitis B is a long-term viral infection of the liver. It is identified as a risk factor for liver cancer, and those with this condition are advised to participate in liver cancer screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND PHYSICAL ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physical activity can improve outcomes and quality of life for cervical cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXODX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ExoDx is a urine test that examines exosomal RNA to assess the risk of high-grade prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL SPREAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local spread refers to cancer invasion into nearby tissues such as fat, blood vessels, lymph nodes, adrenal glands, or Gerota's fascia in locally advanced disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLEURAL MEMBRANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The pleural membrane is a thin layer of tissue that surrounds the lungs, protecting them and facilitating breathing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOME HEALTH AGENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Home health agency is a service that provides medical care and support in a patient's home."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALE BREAST CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Male breast cancer is a rare form of breast cancer that occurs in individuals assigned male at birth, with similar treatment approaches."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPEECH OR SWALLOWING THERAPIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A speech or swallowing therapist tests and helps improve a patient's ability to speak and swallow before and after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UROLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical specialist who performs procedures like TURBT to diagnose and treat bladder cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specialist in the urinary system and male reproductive organs, involved in diagnosing and treating urinary tract cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"A urologist is a doctor specializing in diseases of the urinary system and male reproductive organs, who typically performs prostate biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A urologist is a medical doctor specializing in the urinary tract and male reproductive system, who may diagnose and treat bladder cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A urologist is a medical doctor who specializes in treating diseases of the urinary system and male reproductive organs, including performing prostate biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urologist is a medical doctor specializing in the urinary tract, who performs cystoscopy and can remove small tumors or take biopsy samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urologist is a medical professional specializing in the urinary tract and male reproductive system, who discusses risks, benefits, and side effects of procedures like radical cystectomy with patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMISTRY PROFILE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood test measuring various chemicals in the blood, recommended in initial testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemistry profile (comprehensive metabolic panel) is a group of blood tests providing information about kidney, liver, and other organ function."&lt;SEP&gt;"A group of blood tests, also known as a comprehensive metabolic panel (CMP), providing information about kidney, liver, and organ function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemistry profile is a blood test that measures various chemicals and enzymes in the blood, helping to assess organ function in ovarian cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE PAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone pain is a symptom that may indicate bone metastasis, prompting the use of bone scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone pain is a symptom that may indicate cancer spread to bones, prompting a bone scan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNA SEQUENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DNA sequence is the order of nucleotides determined by NGS."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA sequence is the order of nucleotides in DNA, determined by NGS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The ovaries are organs that make eggs for sexual reproduction and produce hormones affecting breast growth, body shape, and the menstrual cycle. They are part of the female reproductive system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLORECTAL ANASTOMOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colorectal anastomosis is a surgical reconnection of the colon to the remaining rectum after tumor removal, allowing for near-normal bowel movements."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRONIC HEPATITIS C&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chronic hepatitis C is a long-term infection with the hepatitis C virus that can lead to cirrhosis, liver failure, and liver cancer, and is a key risk factor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND COMPLEMENTARY THERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Complementary therapies like acupuncture may help manage cervical cancer symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIR SENTINEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"miR Sentinel is a urine test that measures microRNA biomarkers to help determine the need for prostate biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SICKLE CELL TRAIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sickle cell trait is a genetic condition that can be associated with renal medullary carcinoma, a rare kidney cancer subtype."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD PRESSURE SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood pressure screening is a preventive health measure recommended for anal cancer survivors to monitor cardiovascular health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT PLANNING ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment Planning Role Education is understanding how planning considers fertility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR MARKER TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor marker tests are blood tests that detect substances produced by cancer cells, such as CA-125, used to monitor ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE METASTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone metastasis is the spread of breast cancer to bones, commonly the spine, causing pain and fractures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone metastasis is the spread of cancer to bones, detected via bone scans and a risk factor for further testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC INFORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic information is the DNA content that PCR amplifies for analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic information is the DNA or RNA content that PCR amplifies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FALLOPIAN TUBE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fallopian tube is part of the female reproductive system where ovarian cancer can also start, close to where the tube meets the ovary."&lt;SEP&gt;"The fallopian tubes connect the ovaries to the top part of the uterus and are the passage through which eggs travel from the ovary to the uterus. They are part of the female reproductive system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T3 CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T3 cancer is a larger tumor that hasn't spread to lymph nodes, potentially treated with transabdominal surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HBV CARRIER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An HBV carrier is a person who has the hepatitis B virus in their body and may not show symptoms but can transmit the virus. Carriers with a family history of liver cancer are at increased risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND PALLIATIVE CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Palliative care is important for managing symptoms in advanced cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MPS (MyProstateScore) is a urine test that evaluates genetic markers to improve prostate cancer risk assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SICKLE CELL DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sickle cell disease is a genetic disorder that can cause sickling of red blood cells, associated with renal medullary carcinoma risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL MELANOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anal melanoma is a rare type of anal cancer that starts in pigment-producing cells, not covered in the main guide."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL CANCER SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anal Cancer Screening is a medical examination to detect anal cancer early, especially in high-risk populations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genetic test identifies abnormal changes (mutations) in genes, which can indicate inherited or somatic risks for cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A test to identify harmful changes in genes, including hereditary and somatic mutations, to assess cancer risk and guide treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic tests are medical procedures used to identify abnormal changes in genes that may increase the risk of prostate cancer. They include germline testing and molecular biomarker testing, which analyze DNA for mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GERMLINE BRCA MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Germline BRCA mutations are inherited genetic changes in BRCA genes, detected through blood testing, increasing ovarian cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Germline BRCA mutations are inherited genetic changes, distinct from somatic tumor mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-RISK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-risk refers to patients with increased likelihood of cancer spread, who may require bone scans or other imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR SAMPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor sample is a tissue sample taken from a tumor during endoscopy or biopsy for analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor sample is obtained via biopsy and used for mutation testing and biomarker analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEMALE REPRODUCTIVE SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The female reproductive system includes the ovaries, fallopian tubes, uterus, cervix, and vagina. It is responsible for sexual reproduction, hormone production, and menstruation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The female reproductive system is a group of organs including the uterus, cervix, ovaries, fallopian tubes, and vagina, working together for sexual reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXALIPLATIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxaliplatin is a chemotherapy drug that can cause neuropathy, with symptoms like numbness and tingling in fingers and toes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxaliplatin is a chemotherapy drug used in combination with 5-FU and leucovorin in the FOLFOX regimen for metastatic anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxaliplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug that can cause nerve damage to fingers and toes with extended use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxaliplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in ovarian cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASIAN MALE ASSIGNED SEX AT BIRTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Asian male assigned sex at birth refers to individuals of Asian descent assigned male at birth who are 40 years of age or over, which is a risk factor for liver cancer in those with hepatitis B."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND END-OF-LIFE CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"End-of-life care focuses on comfort and dignity for terminal cervical cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PCA3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PCA3 is a urine test that detects prostate cancer gene 3 expression, aiding in biopsy decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRENAL GLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adrenal glands are organs located near the kidneys that can be invaded by kidney cancer in locally advanced disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adrenal glands are small, triangle-shaped glands located on top of each kidney, producing hormones that regulate metabolism, stress response, and other bodily functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adrenal glands are small, yellow glands that are part of the body's endocrine system, located on top of each kidney. They produce hormones that regulate various bodily functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYNCH SYNDROME TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genetic test recommended for cancers with dMMR/MSI-H to identify inherited mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONE INJECTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormone injections, such as thyrotropin alfa, are used to increase TSH levels for RAI therapy when hormone replacement is stopped."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COST OF TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cost of treatment refers to financial expenses associated with cancer care, affecting decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GERMLINE TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Germline testing is a genetic test to identify inherited mutations that increase cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Germline testing is a type of genetic test that looks for inherited mutations in genes like BRCA1, BRCA2, ATM, CHEK2, MLH1, MSH2, MSH6, PALB2, PMS2, and others, using blood, urine, or saliva samples. It is recommended for individuals with prostate cancer and certain family histories or risk factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Germline testing is a type of genetic test that looks for inherited mutations in genes like BRCA1, BRCA2, ATM, CHEK2, MLH1, MSH2, MSH6, PALB2, and PMS2, which can increase cancer risk. It is done using blood, urine, or saliva samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Germline testing is a type of genetic testing that looks for inherited mutations present in every cell of the body, often recommended for individuals with certain cancer histories or family risk factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATIC BRCA MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somatic BRCA mutations are genetic changes in BRCA genes that occur in tumor tissue, not inherited, tested to guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOLLOW NEEDLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hollow needle is used in biopsies to extract core samples of tissue from the prostate or metastasis sites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hollow needle is a medical instrument used in core needle biopsies to extract tissue samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPSY PLACEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biopsy placement is critical for accurate diagnosis, requiring experienced surgeons."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOCERVIX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The endocervix is the canal between the vagina and the body of the uterus, lined with glandular cells that produce mucus."&lt;SEP&gt;"The endocervix is the inner part of the cervix forming a canal between the vagina and the uterus. It is lined with columnar cells that produce mucus and contains the internal os."&lt;SEP&gt;"The inner part of the cervix, which is included in tissue samples during a cone biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC FLOOR MUSCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic floor muscle, specifically the levator ani, may be involved in lower rectal tumors and removed during APR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASIAN FEMALE ASSIGNED SEX AT BIRTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Asian female assigned sex at birth refers to individuals of Asian descent assigned female at birth who are 50 years of age or over, which is a risk factor for liver cancer in those with hepatitis B."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND CLINICAL GUIDELINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical guidelines provide evidence-based recommendations for cervical cancer management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SELECTMDX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SelectMDx is a urine test that measures gene expression to assess prostate cancer risk and reduce unnecessary biopsies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONNECTIVE TISSUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Connective tissues include muscles, nerves, fat, blood vessels, and fibrous tissue, which are the origin of sarcomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD DRAW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood Draw is the procedure of collecting a blood sample via needle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3A1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3A1 is a specific stage of ovarian cancer where cancer has spread to retroperitoneal lymph nodes, with substages based on lymph node size."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prostate is a gland in the male body where prostate cancer originates, and its size and features are examined in imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostate is a gland in the male reproductive system that makes semen and is important for sexual reproduction. It produces prostate-specific antigen (PSA) and contains muscles that help propel semen during ejaculation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostate is a gland in the male reproductive system that may be removed during radical cystectomy if cancer has spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostate is a gland located deep inside the pelvis, just below the bladder, about the size of a ping-pong ball, and is part of the male reproductive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostate is a gland located deep inside the pelvis, just below the bladder, and is an important part of the male reproductive system; it makes fluid that nourishes and helps transmit sperm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostate is a male reproductive gland where cancer originates. Imaging tests provide detailed views of this organ to assess cancer presence and extent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostate is a male reproductive gland whose size and health affect PSA production and cancer risk. Its size is measured via transrectal ultrasound or MRI to calculate PSA density."&lt;SEP&gt;"The prostate is a gland in the male reproductive system that surrounds the urethra just beneath the bladder, and it is the site where prostate cancer develops."&lt;SEP&gt;"The prostate is a male reproductive organ located near the bladder and rectum. It is the site where prostate cancer develops and where biopsies are performed to diagnose the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNA REPAIR GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DNA repair genes are genes involved in fixing DNA damage, such as BRCA and others, whose mutations are tested in ovarian cancer tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIDEO DISPLAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A video display shows real-time ultrasound images to guide the urologist during a biopsy procedure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A treatment center with experience in treating brain lymphomas is recommended for optimal care of primary CNS lymphoma patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment Center is a specialized facility offering cancer treatments like radiation therapy or chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment center is a facility with experience in treating bone cancer, where patients can receive specialized care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment center is a facility with experience in treating brain tumors, recommended for seeking care for gliomas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment center is where the patient receives care, and biopsy should be performed there."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SQUAMO-COLUMNAR JUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The squamo-columnar junction, or transformation zone, is the area where the endocervix and ectocervix meet. Most cervical cancers and pre-cancers start in the ectocervix portion of this zone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEVATOR ANI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Levator ani is a pelvic floor muscle that may be removed in APR when tumors have grown into it."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AFRICAN/NORTH AMERICAN BLACK PERSONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"African/North American Black persons refers to individuals of African or North American Black descent with hepatitis B, who are at increased risk for liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND HEALTH POLICY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health policy affects cervical cancer screening and vaccination programs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SAW PALMETTO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Saw palmetto is an herbal supplement that can affect PSA levels, requiring disclosure to care teams."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saw palmetto is an herbal supplement that can affect PSA levels, requiring disclosure to the care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIBROUS TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fibrous tissue is a type of connective tissue that can be involved in sarcomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CUTANEOUS T-CELL LYMPHOPROLIFERATIVE DISORDERS (PCLPDS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary cutaneous T-cell lymphoproliferative disorders are a group of conditions involving abnormal T-cell growth in the skin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOSPICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hospice is a service that provides palliative care for patients with advanced cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A noninvasive, stage 0 cancer found in the cells lining the milk ducts of the breast; treated to prevent invasive breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS) is a non-invasive breast cancer where abnormal cells are confined to the ducts, considered a precursor to invasive cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS) is a noninvasive breast cancer found only in the ducts, with no spread to surrounding tissue, lymph nodes, or distant sites."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPPORT AND COUNSELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Support and counseling are services available to help patients deal with strong feelings and distress related to cancer diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC LYMPH NODE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pelvic lymph node is a small gland in the pelvic area that can be affected by prostate cancer when the disease spreads. It is identified through imaging techniques like special cameras that detect tracers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pelvic lymph node is a lymph node in the pelvic area that may be affected by cancer spread, visible in PET/CT scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FALLOPIAN TUBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fallopian tubes are female reproductive structures that may be removed during radical cystectomy if cancer has spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fallopian tubes are long, thin tubes that connect the ovaries to the uterus. They catch eggs released by the ovaries and transport them to the uterus, where fertilization and fetal development can occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fallopian tubes are part of the female reproductive system, often removed during ovarian cancer surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fallopian tubes are part of the female reproductive system, visualized during ultrasound to assess for cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fallopian tubes are part of the female reproductive system, which can be moved during ovarian transposition to protect from radiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fallopian tubes are reproductive organs that can be affected by ovarian cancer spread, particularly in Stage 2A."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fallopian tubes are structures that transport eggs from ovaries to uterus, removed during BSO for ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The fallopian tubes are female reproductive organs that may be removed during pelvic exenteration for cervical cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRI SCANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MRI scans are imaging studies that can be combined with ultrasound for more precise biopsy guidance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER SPREAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Spread refers to metastasis, which can be detected through tests like ALP and bone scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer spread refers to metastasis to lymph nodes or other body parts, assessed in staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer spread refers to the process where cancer cells break through the bladder and invade other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer spread, or metastasis, is the process by which cancer cells move to other parts of the body, detected through imaging tests like bone scans or chest imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL STROMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The cervical stroma is the thick layer of muscular tissue beneath the cervical lining. Cancer becomes invasive when abnormal cells invade this tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLOANAL ANASTOMOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coloanal anastomosis is a surgical reconnection where the colon is attached directly to the anus, used when the rectum is removed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH WEIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High weight, or obesity, is a condition that can lead to NAFLD and increase the risk of liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND GLOBAL HEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer is a global health issue, with higher burden in low-resource settings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ST. JOHN'S WORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"St. John's wort is an herbal supplement that can interfere with PSA levels and cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"St. John's wort is an herbal supplement that may influence PSA levels, necessitating communication with healthcare providers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic tumor is a new tumor formed outside the kidney through metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPATITIS C SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hepatitis C screening is a test recommended for anal cancer survivors to detect potential infections."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENT PORTAL ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patient Portal Role Education is understanding how portals provide access to records."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENT ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patient Role Education is understanding the patient's responsibilities in managing care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSA LEVEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSA (Prostate-Specific Antigen) level is a blood test marker used to screen for prostate cancer. High PSA levels can indicate the presence of cancer, prompting further diagnostic tests like biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSA level is a measure of prostate-specific antigen in the bloodstream, used as a screening tool for prostate cancer risk. It is influenced by age, race, prostate size, sexual activity, exercise, medications, and biopsy procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSA level refers to the amount of prostate-specific antigen in the bloodstream, which can be an indicator of prostate cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVARIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Female reproductive organs that produce eggs and hormones, which may be removed during hysterectomy, leading to surgical menopause."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovaries are female reproductive organs that can be affected by cancer and cancer treatment, impacting fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovaries are female reproductive organs that can be affected by cancer treatment, impacting fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovaries are female reproductive organs that can be damaged by radiation therapy, affecting fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovaries are female reproductive organs that can be damaged by radiation, leading to infertility, and are targeted in fertility preservation methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovaries are female reproductive organs that may be removed during radical cystectomy if cancer has spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovaries are female reproductive organs that produce eggs and hormones, the primary site of ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovaries are female reproductive organs that produce eggs and hormones. Fertility-sparing treatment preserves the ovaries, allowing for natural pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovaries are organs that produce estrogen; they may be kept during hysterectomy or moved via transposition to avoid radiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovaries are reproductive organs that can be affected by cancer treatment, impacting fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovaries are the female reproductive organs that are the main source of estrogen and progesterone during premenopause."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovaries are the female reproductive organs where ovarian cancer originates, examined via physical and imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reproductive organs that can be affected by cancer treatment, impacting fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ovaries are female reproductive organs that may be removed during pelvic exenteration for cervical cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ovaries are part of the female reproductive system, making eggs for sexual reproduction. They are the primary site where ovarian cancer can develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ovaries are part of the female reproductive system, responsible for producing eggs for sexual reproduction and releasing hormones that affect breast growth, body shape, and the menstrual cycle. Each ovary is about the size and shape of a grape, located on either side of the uterus."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ovaries are reproductive organs that may be removed during hysterectomy, causing surgical menopause."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDUCTION PHASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Induction phase is the first step in treating primary CNS lymphoma, aiming to eliminate as many lymphoma cells as possible. It typically lasts several months and involves multiple courses of chemotherapy, often with high-dose methotrexate and rituximab."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR LOCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor location indicates where the cancer is situated in the body, influencing treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor location is a factor in risk assessment; tumors on the head, neck, hands, feet, shins, or sex organs are considered high risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor location is where the tumor is in the body, used in staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL DYSPLASIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical dysplasia refers to areas of abnormal cells on the lining of the cervix, classified as low-grade (LSIL/CIN 1) or high-grade (HSIL/CIN 2 and 3), with HSIL considered a pre-cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical dysplasia, or cervical intraepithelial neoplasia (CIN), refers to abnormal microscopic cells on the surface of the cervix. It is graded from 1 to 3 and can progress to cancer if untreated."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROPATHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neuropathy is nerve damage caused by oxaliplatin, with symptoms like numbness, cramping, tingling, or pain in fingers and toes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neuropathy is nerve damage causing tingling or numbness in hands and feet, a side effect of some chemotherapy drugs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neuropathy is nerve damage, a potential side effect of chemotherapy, causing symptoms like pain or numbness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NODULES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nodules are small, round areas of tissue that can be found in the liver during an ultrasound. Not all nodules are cancerous, but larger ones may require further testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND LOW-RESOURCE SETTINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer prevention and treatment face challenges in low-resource settings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEEING FREQUENTLY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peeing frequently is a symptom of prostate cancer that is assessed to understand its impact on the patient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peeing frequently is a urinary symptom that may indicate prostate issues and is assessed in symptom evaluations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastases are multiple metastatic tumors that have spread from the primary site."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastases are secondary tumors that have spread from the primary thyroid cancer to other parts of the body, such as the lungs, liver, or bones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGESTIVE HEALTH EXPERTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Digestive health experts are specialists in the digestive system, including the anus and rectum, who form part of the treatment team for anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLOSTOMY CARE TRAINING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colostomy Care Training is an educational session for patients and caregivers on managing a colostomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A digital rectal exam (DRE) is a procedure where a doctor inserts a finger into the rectum to feel the prostate for irregularities or hardening that could indicate a tumor. It is a direct method to assess prostate size and texture."&lt;SEP&gt;"A digital rectal exam is a physical examination where a doctor feels the prostate through the rectum to detect abnormalities that may indicate prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A digital rectal exam is the simplest way to check the size and texture of the prostate, and is used in prostate cancer detection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Digital rectal exam (DRE) is a diagnostic procedure where a doctor inserts a gloved, lubricated finger into the anus and rectum to detect growths or abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Digital rectal exam is a physical examination of the prostate to detect abnormalities, such as hardening or irregularity, which may indicate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Digital rectal exam is a physical examination where a doctor presses on the surface of the skin to check for enlarged lymph nodes or abnormalities in the anal area. It is repeated after diagnosis to assess the extent of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Digital rectal exam is a physical test where a doctor feels the prostate for irregularities, often paired with PSA test for further evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digital rectal exam is a physical examination used to detect abnormalities in the prostate gland, often paired with the PSA test to decide if a biopsy is needed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSCOPIC METASTASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microscopic metastases are cancer cells that have spread beyond the ovaries or pelvis but are only visible under a microscope, detected during surgical staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microscopic metastases are cancer cells that have spread outside the ovaries or pelvis and can only be seen with a microscope."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSOLIDATION PHASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Consolidation phase is the second step in treating primary CNS lymphoma, aimed at destroying any remaining cancer cells and preventing relapse. It follows the induction phase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone tissue is a living tissue made up of specialized bone cells, collagen, blood vessels, nerves, proteins, vitamins, and minerals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone tissue is living tissue made of cells, minerals, and collagen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL INTRAEPITHELIAL NEOPLASIA (CIN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CIN is a term for cervical dysplasia, graded as CIN 1, 2, or 3, representing abnormal cell growth on the cervix."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical intraepithelial neoplasia (CIN) is a grading system for cervical dysplasia based on the depth of abnormal cells. Grades range from 1 (mild) to 3 (severe)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCALLY ADVANCED CANCERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Locally advanced cancers are those that have spread to nearby tissues, typically treated with chemoradiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;10 MILLIMETERS (MM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"10 millimeters (mm) is a size threshold for nodules found on an ultrasound, where nodules of this size or larger may trigger additional tests for liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND SCREENING PROGRAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Screening programs aim to detect cervical cancer early in populations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFICULTY PEEING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Difficulty peeing is a symptom of prostate cancer that is assessed to understand its impact on the patient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Difficulty peeing is a urinary symptom that can signal prostate problems and is part of symptom assessments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE FUSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gene fusions are unique genetic alterations that promote cancer in translocation RCC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAMILIAL ADENOMATOUS POLYPOSIS (FAP) TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic testing for FAP when an inherited syndrome is suspected."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REMNANT ABLATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Remnant ablation is the use of low-dose iodine-131 shortly after thyroidectomy to destroy remaining thyroid tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRAVEL TO TREATMENT CENTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Travel to treatment centers is a logistical factor in accessing cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANESTHESIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medicine administered by an anesthesiologist to prevent pain during surgery or procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesia is a drug-induced loss of feeling or awareness used during surgery to prevent pain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesia is a medical intervention used to numb pain or induce sleep during invasive procedures like prostate biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesia is a medical intervention used to prevent pain during procedures like cystoscopy and pyelogram, ensuring patient comfort."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesia is a medical substance or procedure used to induce sleep or loss of sensation during surgical procedures like biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesia is a medical substance used to induce loss of sensation during surgery. Cannabis use may affect the amount needed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesia is a medical substance used to numb pain or induce sleep during procedures like prostate biopsies, ensuring patient comfort."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesia is a medical treatment that induces sleep or loss of sensation, used during stereotactic biopsy procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesia is a method to make patients comfortable during bone marrow procedures, sometimes provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesia is administered to a patient to go to sleep during a stereotactic biopsy procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesia is the use of medication to induce a lack of sensation or consciousness, sometimes provided during bone marrow procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anesthesia is used to make patients comfortable during procedures like direct laryngoscopy and panendoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medication given to put a patient to sleep during TURBT."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DONOR EGGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Donor eggs are eggs from women who undergo hormone treatment to stimulate egg production, used in IVF for ovarian cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RITUXIMAB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rituximab (Rituxan) is a monoclonal antibody used in immunotherapy for primary CNS lymphoma. It attaches to CD20 proteins on cancer cells, helping the immune system destroy them. It is given via IV infusion and can cause various side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rituximab is a drug that binds to CD20 on B cells, used in the treatment of certain cancers, as illustrated in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rituximab is a drug that may be added to chemotherapy for MGZL when tumor cells express certain markers, forming chemoimmunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rituximab is an immunotherapy drug that targets CD20 on B-cells, used to treat primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rituximab is an immunotherapy drug used in treating primary CNS lymphoma, often combined with chemotherapy like methotrexate. It can be given alone but works better with chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rituximab is the main immunotherapy drug used to treat primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKELETAL MATURITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skeletal maturity is when bone growth is complete, leaving a physeal scar."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW-GRADE SQUAMOUS INTRAEPITHELIAL LESION (LSIL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LSIL refers to mild dysplasia (CIN 1) of the cervix, indicating early abnormal cell changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (LSIL) refers to mild dysplasia, classified as CIN 1. It is a low-risk cervical change."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSABDOMINAL RESECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transabdominal resection is recommended if cancer signs appear after chemoradiation, and may be followed by chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;3 TO 6 MONTHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"3 to 6 months is a time interval for repeating ultrasound and AFP tests if smaller nodules are found, to monitor for changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND VACCINATION COVERAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vaccination coverage rates affect cervical cancer prevention effectiveness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFICULTY POOPING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Difficulty pooping is a bowel symptom that may be related to prostate enlargement or cancer, evaluated in symptom checks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Difficulty pooping is a symptom of prostate cancer that is assessed to understand its impact on the patient."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUMARATE HYDRATASE GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fumarate hydratase gene is a gene that, when mutated, leads to fumarate hydratase-deficient RCC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALP TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALP Test is a blood test measuring alkaline phosphatase levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3A2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3A2 is a specific stage of ovarian cancer where cancer has spread to the abdominal lining, visible only under a microscope."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD-BRAIN BARRIER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The blood-brain barrier is a protective layer around the brain that blocks toxins and germs but also prevents some chemotherapy drugs from reaching the brain, necessitating high doses of drugs like methotrexate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ULTRASOUND PROBE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ultrasound probe is a device inserted into the rectum to create images of the prostate using sound waves."&lt;SEP&gt;"An ultrasound probe is a medical device inserted into the rectum to provide visual images of the prostate, guiding the needle during a biopsy procedure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMBRYOS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Embryos are fertilized eggs created during IVF, which can be implanted into the uterus or frozen for future use."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADOLESCENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adolescence is the period between 10 and 19 years when ossification ends."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-GRADE SQUAMOUS INTRAEPITHELIAL LESION (HSIL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HSIL refers to moderate or severe dysplasia (CIN 2 and 3) and is considered a pre-cancerous condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (HSIL) refers to moderate or severe dysplasia, classified as CIN 2 and 3. It is considered a pre-cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABDOMINAL SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abdominal surgery is a broader term for transabdominal surgery, involving cutting into the abdomen to remove tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;6 MONTHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"6 months is the recommended interval for repeating ultrasound and AFP tests in liver cancer screening for at-risk individuals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND HEALTH EQUITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health equity aims to reduce cervical cancer disparities across populations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEXUAL PROBLEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sexual problems are symptoms of prostate cancer that are assessed to understand their impact on the patient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sexual problems, such as erectile dysfunction, can be symptoms of prostate issues and are assessed for quality of life impact."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELOC GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ELOC gene (formerly TCEB1) is a gene that, when mutated, leads to ELOC-mutated RCC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REHABILITATION CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rehabilitation center is a facility that helps patients recover physical function after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (LCIS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lobular carcinoma in situ (LCIS) is a condition where abnormal cells grow in the lobules, increasing the risk of developing invasive breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEELINGS OF SADNESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Feelings of sadness are emotional responses that can be part of distress in cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLONOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical procedure used to examine the colon and remove polyps, often used for screening and diagnosis of colon cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonoscopy is a medical procedure recommended at intervals for monitoring rectal cancer, with the next one scheduled in 3 years and then every 5 years."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonoscopy is a medical procedure used to examine and remove polyps from the colon, often involving a polypectomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonoscopy is a medical procedure used to examine the colon and rectum, during which polyps can be removed to prevent cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonoscopy is a procedure used to view the colon and rectum, often used to detect and remove polyps."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonoscopy is a procedure used to view the colon and remove polyps, often via a polypectomy, to prevent cancer development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonoscopy is a procedure using a scope to examine the large bowel (rectum and colon). It is mentioned as a diagnostic tool for GI tract evaluation in the context of ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonoscopy is a surveillance procedure recommended after treatment for colon cancer to detect new growths or recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonoscopy is a surveillance testing procedure recommended after treatment for colon cancer. For stage 1, it is recommended 1 year after surgery, with follow-ups based on results; for stages 2 and 3, it is part of a broader surveillance schedule."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRI SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scan is a diagnostic procedure using radio waves and powerful magnets to produce detailed images of internal structures without x-rays. It may be closed or open, and contrast is often used. It requires patients to hold their breath during image collection."&lt;SEP&gt;"A magnetic resonance imaging scan that uses radio waves and powerful magnets to take pictures of the inside of the body, without x-rays, and may use contrast."&lt;SEP&gt;"An MRI scan is an imaging technique that can be combined with ultrasound to provide a highly accurate picture of prostate cancer, aiding in biopsy guidance."&lt;SEP&gt;"An MRI scan is an imaging test used to detect adrenal tumors and other conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"An MRI scan uses radio waves and magnets to produce detailed images without radiation, with closed and open types."&lt;SEP&gt;"MRI scan (magnetic resonance imaging) uses magnets and radio waves to produce images without radiation, useful for detecting leukemic meningitis."&lt;SEP&gt;"MRI scan (magnetic resonance imaging) uses radio waves and powerful magnets to take pictures of the inside of the body without radiation, often with contrast, and can be closed or open."&lt;SEP&gt;"MRI scan is a diagnostic imaging method using radio waves and magnets to get detailed views of the prostate and check for spread to lymph nodes or bones."&lt;SEP&gt;"MRI scan is a diagnostic imaging test using radio waves and magnets to produce detailed images of the body's interior, without using x-rays."&lt;SEP&gt;"MRI scan is an imaging method used to measure prostate size, contributing to PSA density calculations and cancer assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"MRI scan is an imaging test using radio waves and magnets to produce detailed images of the prostate, lymph nodes, and pelvic bones. It helps in diagnosis, staging, treatment planning, and recurrence detection."&lt;SEP&gt;"MRI scan is an imaging test using radio waves and magnets to produce detailed images without x-rays, often with contrast, and includes closed and open types."&lt;SEP&gt;"MRI scan is an imaging test using radio waves and magnets, without radiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPERM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reproductive cells that can be damaged by cancer treatment, affecting fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sperm are male reproductive cells that can be damaged by cancer and cancer treatment, impacting fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sperm are male reproductive cells that can be damaged by cancer treatment, affecting fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sperm are male reproductive cells that can be damaged by cancer treatment, necessitating contraception."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sperm are male reproductive cells used to fertilize eggs during IVF."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sperm are reproductive cells from the testicles that are part of semen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sperm are reproductive cells produced by the testicles, carried in semen, and nourished by prostate fluid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sperm are reproductive cells produced with the help of testosterone; testosterone reduction affects sperm production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sperm are reproductive cells transported by semen, with PSA aiding in their transport."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sperm can be damaged by cancer treatment, affecting fertility in those with testicles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WOMB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Womb is where bone formation starts during fetal development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAP SMEAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Pap smear is a procedure to collect cells from the cervix to detect abnormal changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pap smear is a screening test used to detect abnormal cervical cells. Its widespread use has significantly reduced cervical cancer rates in the United States."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECTAL WALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rectal wall is the tissue layer of the rectum, with tumor invasion depth determining cancer stage and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE MARROW ASPIRATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone marrow aspirate is a medical procedure where a hollow needle is used to draw liquid bone marrow from the hip bone for diagnostic testing, often performed alongside a biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow aspirate is a procedure that draws liquid bone marrow from the hip bone using a hollow needle."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow aspirate is a procedure to collect a sample of bone marrow for testing, used in AML diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow aspirate is a procedure to remove a sample of bone marrow tissue for testing, used to confirm AML diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow aspirate is a procedure using a hollow needle to draw liquid bone marrow from the pelvis for testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND PATIENT ADVOCACY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patient advocacy groups work to improve cervical cancer care and awareness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINE TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A urine test analyzes urine samples for biomarkers like PCA3 or exosomal RNA to assess prostate cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SICKLE CELL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sickle cell refers to abnormal red blood cells that can cause sickling, associated with renal medullary carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNIZATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immunizations are vaccines recommended for cancer survivors to prevent infections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immunizations, such as the flu shot, are recommended for anal cancer survivors to prevent infections."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECOND OPINION ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Second Opinion Role Education is understanding the value of getting a second opinion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYPECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A minor surgical procedure used to remove polyps during a colonoscopy, which can prevent cancer from developing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polypectomy is a minor surgical procedure performed during a colonoscopy to remove polyps from the colon or rectum."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polypectomy is a minor surgical procedure performed during a colonoscopy to remove polyps from the rectal or colon wall."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polypectomy is a minor surgical procedure performed during colonoscopy to remove polyps, preventing potential cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polypectomy is a minor surgical procedure to remove polyps during a colonoscopy, often sufficient for treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORE SAMPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A core sample is a small cylindrical piece of prostate tissue, typically 1-2 mm wide and 12-20 mm long, removed during a biopsy for analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"A core sample is a small piece of prostate tissue, typically 1-2 millimeters wide and 12-20 millimeters long, removed during a biopsy for testing. Multiple samples are taken from different parts of the prostate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer affecting the bladder, requiring multidisciplinary care and various diagnostic tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of cancer that starts in the urothelial cells lining the bladder, with various stages and grades that determine treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bladder cancer is a disease characterized by abnormal cell growth in the bladder lining, with diagnosis and management involving various imaging tests, biopsies, and genetic assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bladder cancer is a disease characterized by abnormal cell growth in the bladder, with types including urothelial carcinoma, squamous cell carcinoma, adenocarcinoma, and small cell carcinoma. It can be non-muscle-invasive, muscle-invasive, or metastatic, and is often found due to symptoms like hematuria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bladder cancer is a disease characterized by the abnormal growth of cells in the bladder, with treatment options depending on stage, grade, overall health, and patient preferences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bladder cancer is a disease characterized by the growth of abnormal cells in the bladder wall, with stages ranging from 0 to 4 and grades of low or high aggressiveness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bladder cancer is a disease characterized by the growth of malignant cells in the bladder, treated with various methods including surgery, intravesical therapy, and systemic therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bladder cancer is a disease characterized by the growth of tumors in the bladder, treated with procedures like TURBT, cystectomy, and intravesical therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bladder cancer is a disease where abnormal cells grow out of control in the bladder's inner lining, often affecting adults aged 55 and over, and can recur after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bladder cancer is a disease where abnormal cells in the inner layer of the bladder grow out of control. It has phases and stages, and can be non-invasive, muscle-invasive, or metastatic. It is commonly recurring and treatable, with various treatment options available."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bladder cancer is a type of cancer affecting the bladder, with treatments including surgery, intravesical therapy, chemotherapy, and immunotherapy, each causing specific side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bladder cancer is the disease being diagnosed and monitored through procedures like cystoscopy and imaging tests, with potential to spread to other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bladder cancer is the disease being treated, with various therapies including chemotherapy, immunotherapy, targeted therapy, and radiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOINT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Joint is where bones meet, covered by cartilage at the epiphysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASE OF SKULL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The base of the skull is an anatomical landmark that forms the upper boundary of the parapharyngeal space."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIDNEY FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kidney function involves filtering blood, removing waste, and making hormones, as described in the kidney cancer section."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kidney function is a factor that determines whether contrast material can be used, as poor function may preclude its use."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNOPHENOTYPING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immunophenotyping is a laboratory test that identifies cell types based on surface markers, used in CBCL diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immunophenotyping is a process that uses antibodies to detect the presence or absence of white blood cell antigens called biomarkers, which are proteins on the surface or inside white blood cells, and is used in AML treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immunophenotyping is a process using antibodies to detect white blood cell antigens (biomarkers) on or inside cells, crucial for identifying cell types and guiding AML treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immunophenotyping is a process using flow cytometry to identify markers on cells, particularly in the immune system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immunophenotyping is a test used to characterize cells in FL diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND SURVIVOR STORIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survivor stories provide inspiration and education for cervical cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTASIZED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastasized indicates that cancer has spread from the prostate to other parts of the body, detected via imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastasized refers to cancer that has spread from the primary site to other parts of the body, detected by imaging tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AFRICAN DESCENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"African descent is a demographic factor associated with higher risk of renal medullary carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE COLON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The colon is the first and longest section of the large bowel, part of the digestive system, and is distinct from the rectum and anus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN MANAGEMENT CONSULTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pain Management Consultation is a medical appointment to address pain related to cancer or treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CECUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The cecum is a pouch at the start of the colon, from which the appendix protrudes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A complication is an unwanted and unplanned result from a medical procedure, such as infection, bleeding, or blood in urine, stool, or semen, which can occur after a prostate biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1 bladder cancer has grown through the inner lining into the connective tissue layer but has not invaded the muscle layer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 1 colon cancer has grown into the second or third layer of the colon wall without spreading to lymph nodes or distant sites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 1 is an invasive breast cancer stage where cancer has grown outside ducts or lobules but is localized, possibly involving axillary lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 1 is early NSCLC, where cancer has grown from the airway into lung tissue but has not spread to other organs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 1 rectal cancer indicates tumor growth into the second or third layer of the rectal wall, with no further treatment needed after surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROWTH PLATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Growth plate, or physis, is cartilage that allows bone growth, leaving a scar after maturity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYOID BONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The hyoid bone is a bone under the tongue that forms the lower boundary of the parapharyngeal space."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hyoid bone is located in the middle of the neck and serves as an attachment point for tongue muscles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RCC SUBTYPES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RCC subtypes refer to different types of renal cell carcinoma, a form of kidney cancer, though details are not provided in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BPDCN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BPDCN (Blastic Plasmacytoid Dendritic Cell Neoplasm) is a subtype of AML that may require additional biopsies, such as lymph node or skin lesion biopsies, for diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"BPDCN (Blastic Plasmacytoid Dendritic Cell Neoplasm) is an aggressive subtype of AML that can be found in blood, bone marrow, lymph nodes, and/or skin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND CAREGIVER SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Caregiver support is essential for those caring for cervical cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANDROGEN DEPRIVATION THERAPY (ADT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ADT is a hormone therapy that reduces testosterone levels to slow or shrink prostate cancer growth, using medications or surgical castration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Androgen deprivation therapy (ADT) is a treatment that reduces testosterone levels to a very low level, used primarily for prostate cancer. It includes various methods such as LHRH agonists, LHRH antagonists, anti-androgens, and surgical castration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YOUNGER ADULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Younger adults are an age group where translocation RCC tends to be diagnosed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLETE BLOOD COUNT (CBC) TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood test measuring white blood cells, red blood cells, and platelets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHOLE-BODY SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A whole-body scan is an imaging procedure done before or after RAI therapy to detect thyroid tissue or cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIME AWAY FROM WORK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Time away from work is a practical consideration for cancer patients undergoing treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPENDIX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The appendix is a skinny, finger-sized tube attached to the cecum, closed at one end."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene is a segment of DNA that can have mutations affecting its function, analyzed by NGS."&lt;SEP&gt;"A gene on chromosome 9 produces the p16 protein, which slows cell division."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene is a segment of DNA that can have mutations affecting function, such as IDH1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene is a segment of DNA that codes for specific proteins, and mutations in genes can contribute to cancer development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are coded instructions for proteins, and mutations in genes can lead to cancer and are tested in biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are coded instructions for proteins, and mutations in genes like FLT3 are important in AML, with testing identifying specific changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are coded instructions for proteins; mutations in genes can lead to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are segments of DNA inside cells that provide instructions for making proteins. Abnormal changes or mutations in genes can lead to diseases like prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are segments of DNA that code for proteins; mutations in genes like FLT3 are important in AML for targeted treatment and prognosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 2 bladder cancer has grown into the muscle layer but has not reached the fatty layer or spread elsewhere."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 2 colon cancer has grown into or beyond the fourth layer of the colon wall without lymph node involvement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 2 is an invasive breast cancer stage with more extensive growth or lymph node involvement than stage 1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 2 is considered locally advanced NSCLC, with cancer grown into lung tissue and possibly spread to lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 2 rectal cancer indicates tumor growth through the rectal wall, possibly into nearby tissues, requiring more treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIDDLE REGION OF BONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Middle region of bone is the diaphysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JUGULAR VEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The jugular vein is a major blood vessel located in the parapharyngeal space, which can be affected by tumor spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIBEROPTIC LARYNGOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fiberoptic laryngoscopy (nasolaryngoscopy) is a diagnostic procedure using a small flexible scope passed through the nose into the throat, typically taking less than 1 minute, with numbing medicine sprayed in the nose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fiberoptic laryngoscopy (nasolaryngoscopy) is a method using a small flexible scope passed through the nose into the throat, typically taking less than a minute, with numbing spray."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS SCALE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS scale (Performance Status scale) is a measure used to rate a patient's general health and functional ability, often used in oncology to guide treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND TELEMEDICINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Telemedicine can improve access to cervical cancer care in remote areas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONE THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormone Therapy is a cancer treatment that blocks hormones that fuel certain cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormone therapy is a systemic treatment that adds, blocks, or removes hormones, particularly androgens like testosterone, to manage prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormone therapy is a treatment approach for prostate cancer that aims to block or reduce testosterone levels, including ADT and other medications. It has been a main treatment for advanced prostate cancer for decades."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormone therapy is a treatment for advanced-stage prostate cancer that aims to slow down cancer growth by reducing or blocking hormones that fuel cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormone therapy is a treatment for prostate cancer that reduces or blocks hormones that fuel cancer growth, used in both early and advanced stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormone therapy is a treatment that blocks or lowers hormones like estrogen and progesterone to slow or stop hormone-receptor-positive breast cancer growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YOUNG PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Young people of African descent are at risk for renal medullary carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CBC TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CBC Test is a blood test measuring red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3C&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3C is a specific stage of ovarian cancer where visible cancer on the abdominal lining is larger than 2 centimeters, possibly spreading to the liver or spleen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-DOSE CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-dose chemotherapy is a treatment that destroys cancer cells but also kills stem cells in the bone marrow, necessitating stem cell rescue."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-dose chemotherapy is an intensive treatment that destroys cancer cells but also kills bone marrow stem cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-dose chemotherapy is an intensive treatment used in stem cell rescue to kill lymphoma cells. It also destroys bone marrow stem cells, leaving the body vulnerable to infection and fatigue until new stem cells are transplanted."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-dose chemotherapy is an intensive treatment using large amounts of drugs like methotrexate to kill cancer cells, particularly needed to cross the blood-brain barrier for CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A change in a gene's DNA sequence that can damage its function and lead to diseases like cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A change in genes, such as those in MMR genes, that can cause cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mutation is a change in the genetic code, such as deletion, insertion, or point mutation, which can be found in AML cells and influence treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mutation is an abnormal change in DNA that can disrupt cell behavior and lead to diseases like cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mutation is an abnormal change in a gene that can cause it to produce incorrect proteins or no protein, potentially leading to cancer. Mutations can be inherited (germline) or acquired (somatic)."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mutation is an error in the genetic code that can lead to cancer and is identified through biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mutation is an error in the genetic code that can lead to cancer or affect treatment response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Change in genes, such as in MMR genes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Change."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene change."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutation is a genetic abnormality that can cause lymphocytes to grow out of control, leading to lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutation is an abnormality in cells that causes them to grow out of control, leading to cancer, and it is not typically hereditary in gliomas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutation is an error or change in the genetic code, which can lead to cancer and may be targeted by specific therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutation refers to an abnormality in glial cells that causes them to grow out of control, leading to glioma formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutation refers to changes in the genetic code, such as deletion, insertion, inversion, amplification, translocation, or point mutation, which are unique to AML cells and guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage of cervical cancer where the tumor extends to the pelvic wall or involves the lower vagina, treated as locally advanced."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 3 bladder cancer has grown through the bladder wall into the fatty layer, with subgroups 3A and 3B, potentially spreading to nearby lymph nodes or organs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 3 colon cancer has spread to nearby lymph nodes or has tumor deposits in the fat around the colon."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 3 is an invasive breast cancer stage with significant lymph node involvement or chest wall invasion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 3 is considered locally advanced NSCLC, with cancer grown into lung tissue and possibly spread to lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 3 rectal cancer indicates cancer spread to nearby lymph nodes, requiring more treatment such as chemoradiation or chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;END OF BONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"End of bone is the epiphysis, covered with cartilage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SALIVARY GLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The salivary gland, specifically parts of it, is located in the parapharyngeal space and can be involved in tumor spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIRECT LARYNGOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Direct laryngoscopy is a detailed exam performed under general anesthesia in an operating room using a laryngoscope to view deeper throat areas and take tissue samples for biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Direct laryngoscopy is a detailed exam performed under general anesthesia in an operating room, using a laryngoscope to see deeper in the throat and take tissue samples for biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISTOPATHOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Histopathology is the examination of diseased tissue under a microscope, synonymous with histology in the context of AML diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Histopathology is the microscopic examination of tissue to diagnose AML, performed by a pathologist."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Artificial intelligence is being explored for cervical cancer screening and diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LHRH AGONIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LHRH agonists are a type of hormone therapy that includes drugs like goserelin, leuprolide, and triptorelin. They work by causing the testicles to stop making testosterone, and are typically administered as injections."&lt;SEP&gt;"LHRH agonists, such as goserelin, leuprolide, or triptorelin, are medications used in ADT to reduce testosterone production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONE RECEPTORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormone receptors, including estrogen and progesterone receptors, are tested on biopsy samples to guide treatment decisions for breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormone receptors, such as estrogen and progesterone receptors, are proteins on cancer cells that can bind to hormones and influence cancer growth. Testing for these receptors is part of treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICAL TRIAL SITE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical trial site is a location where experimental cancer treatments are tested."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRIPLE-NEGATIVE BREAST CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Triple-negative breast cancer is a subtype that lacks estrogen, progesterone, and HER2 receptors, making it more aggressive and harder to treat."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HELPLESSNESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Helplessness is an emotional response that can be part of distress in cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMOZOLOMIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Temozolomide is a chemotherapy drug used as an alternative or addition to methotrexate in treating primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRCA1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of prostate, breast, ovarian, pancreatic, and skin cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA1 is a gene associated with inherited mutations that increase risk for prostate, breast, ovarian, pancreatic, and skin cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA1 is a gene mutation that increases risk of breast cancer and is required for PARP inhibitor eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA1 is a gene that, when mutated, can increase the risk of prostate cancer. It is one of the genes tested in germline testing for inherited cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA1 is a gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of breast and ovarian cancer. Genetic testing can identify these mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA1 is a gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of ovarian, breast, and other cancers; it is a common cause of hereditary ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA1 is a gene whose mutations increase risk for breast, ovarian, and other cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 4 bladder cancer has grown through the bladder wall and may have spread to lymph nodes or distant organs, with subgroups 4A and 4B."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 4 colon cancer has metastasized to distant organs, most commonly the liver and/or lungs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 4 is an advanced numbered stage of mouth cancer, which may or may not be metastatic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 4 is metastatic breast cancer where cancer has spread to distant sites, possibly developing from earlier stages or as de novo."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 4 is metastatic cancer at the time of diagnosis, indicating spread to other organs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 4 is the most advanced stage of ovarian cancer, where cancer has spread to distant parts of the body, including fluid around the lungs or internal organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGION BETWEEN PHYSIS AND DIAPHYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Region between physis and diaphysis is the metaphysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDIAL PTERYGOID MUSCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The medial pterygoid muscle is a muscle of mastication located near the parapharyngeal space, and tumor invasion into it is considered in T2 staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESOPHAGOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Esophagoscopy is a procedure where a device is guided down the throat into the esophagus under anesthesia to examine the swallowing tube for abnormal growths."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOPATHOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hematopathology is a subspecialty of pathology focusing on diseases of the blood and bone marrow, including AML diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND LIQUID BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liquid biopsy is a blood test that may detect cervical cancer DNA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTI-ANDROGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anti-androgens are medications that block the action of androgens (male hormones) on prostate cancer cells. Examples include nilutamide, flutamide, and bicalutamide, which are taken as pills."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anti-androgens, such as nilutamide, flutamide, or bicalutamide, block cancer cells from using testosterone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2 RECEPTORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HER2 (human epidermal growth factor receptor 2) receptors are proteins on cancer cells that can promote cancer growth. Testing for HER2 status is part of treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"HER2 receptors are proteins on cancer cells that are tested to determine if targeted therapy is appropriate for breast cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTHY BODY WEIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maintaining a healthy body weight is part of a healthy lifestyle for anal cancer survivors to improve outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD KEEPING ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Record Keeping Role Education is understanding the importance of organizing records."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRCA2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of prostate, breast, ovarian, pancreatic, and skin cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA2 is a gene associated with inherited mutations that increase risk for prostate, breast, ovarian, pancreatic, and skin cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA2 is a gene mutation that increases risk of breast cancer and is required for PARP inhibitor eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA2 is a gene that, when mutated, can increase the risk of prostate cancer. It is one of the genes tested in germline testing for inherited cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA2 is a gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of breast and other cancers. Genetic testing can identify these mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA2 is a gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of ovarian, breast, and other cancers; it is a common cause of hereditary ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA2 is a gene whose mutations increase risk for breast, ovarian, and other cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW GRADE (LG)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A classification indicating that cancer cells are slow-growing, as determined by their similarity to normal cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low grade (LG) refers to bladder cancer cells that are slow growing and less aggressive."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VINCRISTINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vincristine is a chemotherapy medicine sometimes included with methotrexate and rituximab for induction therapy of primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE MINERAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone mineral, such as hydroxyapatite, provides hardness to bone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LATERAL PTERYGOID MUSCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The lateral pterygoid muscle is a muscle of mastication located near the parapharyngeal space, and tumor invasion into it is considered in T2 staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRONCHOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bronchoscopy is a procedure using a device inserted through the nose or mouth to examine the airway, including trachea and bronchi, under anesthesia, used to detect cancer or perform treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sedation is a medical state induced to relax patients during procedures like bone marrow tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sedation is a method to make patients comfortable during bone marrow procedures, sometimes provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sedation is the use of medication to relax a patient during procedures like bone marrow aspirate and biopsy, improving comfort."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND MOLECULAR PROFILING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular profiling analyzes genetic changes in cervical cancer to guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LHRH ANTAGONIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LHRH antagonists are a type of hormone therapy that includes drugs like degarelix and relugolix. They block the effects of luteinizing hormone-releasing hormone, reducing testosterone production. They can be given as injections or, in the case of relugolix, as a daily tablet."&lt;SEP&gt;"LHRH antagonists, such as degarelix or relugolix, are medications that lower testosterone levels in ADT."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICAL BREAST EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical breast exam is a physical exam by a healthcare provider to check for lumps or changes in the breast."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE LARGE INTESTINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The large intestine, also called the bowel, includes the colon, rectum, and anus, and is part of the digestive system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL MARIJUANA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medical marijuana is a cannabis-based product used to manage symptoms like pain or nausea in cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENIGN ADRENAL TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benign adrenal tumors are non-cancerous growths that do not spread to other parts of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITION COUNSELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutrition Counseling is a session with a nutritionist to optimize diet during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene involved in DNA repair; mutations increase the risk of prostate cancer and other cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"ATM is a gene associated with inherited mutations that increase risk for prostate cancer and other cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"ATM is a gene that, when mutated, can increase the risk of prostate cancer. It is one of the genes tested in germline testing for inherited cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH GRADE (HG)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A classification indicating that cancer cells are fast-growing, as determined by their dissimilarity to normal cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"High grade (HG) refers to bladder cancer cells that are fast growing and more aggressive."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROCARBAZINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Procarbazine is a chemotherapy drug that may be added to methotrexate and rituximab for treating primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cells are specialized cells that make up bone tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone cells include osteocytes, osteoblasts, and osteoclasts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREVERTEBRAL MUSCLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The prevertebral muscles are muscles located in front of the spine, and tumor invasion into them is considered in T2 staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PANENDOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Panendoscopy is a comprehensive procedure using different endoscopes to examine the mouth, oropharynx, larynx, esophagus, trachea, and bronchi under anesthesia, often to locate primary tumors or assess abnormal lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN LESION BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skin lesion biopsy is a procedure to diagnose BPDCN subtype of AML, involving removal of skin tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin lesion biopsy is a procedure to sample a skin lesion, used when BPDCN subtype of AML is suspected."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND IMMUNOTHERAPY BIOMARKERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immunotherapy biomarkers help predict response to immune-based treatments in cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL CASTRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgical castration is a procedure that removes the testicles to reduce testosterone production, serving as an effective method of androgen deprivation therapy for prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical castration, or orchiectomy, is a permanent procedure that removes the testicles to reduce testosterone, considered a form of hormone therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT OR MRI OF ABDOMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CT or MRI of the abdomen is an imaging test used to check for cancer spread to abdominal organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEA LEVEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The level of carcinoembryonic antigen in blood, used for monitoring colon cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAMMA RAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gamma rays are a form of high-energy radiation used in radiation therapy to kill cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PORTAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Portal is an online system where patients can access test results and medical records."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CMP TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CMP Test is a blood test measuring 14 substances in plasma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEK2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene involved in DNA repair; mutations increase the risk of prostate cancer and other cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"CHEK2 is a gene associated with inherited mutations that increase risk for prostate cancer and other cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"CHEK2 is a gene that, when mutated, can increase the risk of prostate cancer. It is one of the genes tested in germline testing for inherited cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UROTHELIAL LAYER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The urothelial layer is the inner lining of the bladder where most bladder cancers originate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IBRUTINIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ibrutinib (Imbruvica) is a targeted therapy used as an alternative induction option for primary CNS lymphoma when methotrexate is not suitable."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTEOCYTE FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osteocyte function is to maintain bone tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTERNAL OS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The external os is a narrow opening in the center of the ectocervix that allows blood to pass into the vagina during menstruation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINE-NEEDLE BIOPSY (FNB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fine-needle biopsy (FNB) is a biopsy procedure that may be guided by ultrasound or CT to sample small areas of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine-needle biopsy (FNB) is a biopsy technique using a needle to remove a sample of tissue from a tumor or lymph node for pathological examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine-needle biopsy (FNB) is a biopsy technique using a needle to remove a sample of tumor or lymph node, similar to FNA but with a slightly larger needle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERIPHERAL BLOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peripheral blood is circulating blood that can be used for flow cytometry and other tests to detect AML cells and biomarkers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peripheral blood is circulating blood that can be used in flow cytometry to detect specific cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peripheral blood is the circulating blood in the body, which can be used for flow cytometry to detect AML cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND COMBINATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Combination therapy uses multiple treatments together for cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NODE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Node refers to lymph nodes; the N component in the TNM system indicates whether cancer has spread to these nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERIPHERAL NEUROPATHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peripheral neuropathy is a common side effect of paclitaxel, causing pain, tingling, and numbness in hands and feet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD BANK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood bank is a facility that collects and stores blood for transfusions during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MLH1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene involved in DNA repair; mutations increase the risk of colorectal, uterine, and prostate cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"MLH1 is a gene associated with inherited mutations that increase risk for colorectal, uterine, and prostate cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"MLH1 is a gene that, when mutated, can increase the risk of prostate cancer. It is one of the genes tested in germline testing for inherited cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONNECTIVE TISSUE LAYER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The connective tissue layer is the second layer of the bladder wall, which stage 1 cancer has grown into."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LENALIDOMIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lenalidomide is an immunomodulatory drug used with or without rituximab as an alternative induction therapy for primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTEOBLAST FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osteoblast function is to create bone from calcium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNAL OS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The internal os is the upper part of the endocervix that serves as an opening between the uterus and the cervix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPSY OF METASTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biopsy of metastasis is a procedure to confirm cancer spread to areas like lymph nodes or lungs, with each suspected site potentially biopsied depending on location."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBODIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibodies are proteins made by B cells to fight infections, and are part of the immune response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibodies are proteins made by B lymphocytes (B cells) that help fight infections. They are a key product of B cells, which are affected in B-cell ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibodies are proteins produced by B cells that fight infections by latching onto and destroying invading viruses or bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibodies are proteins used in immunophenotyping to detect specific antigens on white blood cells, aiding in AML classification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibodies are proteins used in immunophenotyping to detect specific white blood cell antigens or biomarkers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND NEOADJUVANT THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neoadjuvant therapy is given before surgery to shrink cervical tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LHRH AGONIST (GOSERELIN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Goserelin is a specific LHRH agonist medication used in ADT to reduce testosterone production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL PHOTOGRAPHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medical photographs are images taken of the breast to document the appearance of inflammatory breast cancer for diagnosis and monitoring."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONE-RECEPTOR-POSITIVE BREAST CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormone-receptor-positive breast cancer is a subtype that expresses estrogen or progesterone receptors, treated with hormone therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANGER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anger is an emotional response that can be part of distress in cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MODERATE INTENSITY EXERCISE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moderate intensity exercise, such as 150 minutes per week, is recommended for anal cancer survivors to improve health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MSH2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene involved in DNA repair; mutations increase the risk of colorectal, uterine, and prostate cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSH2 is a gene associated with inherited mutations that increase risk for colorectal, uterine, and prostate cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSH2 is a gene that, when mutated, can increase the risk of prostate cancer. It is one of the genes tested in germline testing for inherited cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OUTER FATTY LAYER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The outer fatty layer is the fourth layer of the bladder wall, which stage 3 cancer has grown into."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEMETREXED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pemetrexed is a chemotherapy drug listed as an alternative induction therapy for primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTEOCLAST FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osteoclast function is to break down bone, releasing calcium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLUMNAR CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Columnar (glandular) cells line the endocervix and produce mucus. They are one of the two main cell types in the cervix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PD-L1 TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PD-L1 testing checks for the programmed death ligand 1 protein on cancer cells, which can suppress immune response and guide immunotherapy treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"PD-L1 testing measures programmed death-ligand 1 expression on cancer cells using a combined positive score (CPS) to determine eligibility for immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"PD-L1 testing measures the expression of programmed death ligand 1 protein on cancer cells, using a combined positive score (CPS), to determine if immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy may be effective."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIGENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antigens are proteins on cell surfaces that can be detected by antibodies, serving as biomarkers in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antigens are proteins on the surface or inside white blood cells that serve as biomarkers, detected by antibodies in immunophenotyping."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND ADJUVANT THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adjuvant therapy is given after surgery to reduce recurrence risk in cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LHRH AGONIST (LEUPROLIDE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leuprolide is a specific LHRH agonist medication used in ADT to lower testosterone levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIRTH CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Birth Control includes methods like condoms, IUDs, and barrier methods used to prevent pregnancy during and after cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Birth control refers to methods to prevent pregnancy during cancer treatment, as some treatments may harm a developing fetus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE ANAL SPHINCTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The anal sphincters are muscles surrounding the anal canal that relax to allow stool to exit the body through the anus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MSH6&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene involved in DNA repair; mutations increase the risk of colorectal, uterine, and prostate cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSH6 is a gene associated with inherited mutations that increase risk for colorectal, uterine, and prostate cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSH6 is a gene that, when mutated, can increase the risk of prostate cancer. It is one of the genes tested in germline testing for inherited cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARCINOMA IN SITU (CIS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carcinoma in situ (CIS) is a flat patch of high-grade, aggressive cancer cells on the surface of the bladder lining, classified as stage 0is."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POMALIDOMIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pomalidomide is a drug listed as an alternative induction therapy option for primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CALCIUM REGULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Calcium regulation is the maintenance of calcium levels in the body, involving bone remodeling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CIN 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CIN 1 is mild cervical dysplasia, also known as low-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (LSIL)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR P16 (HPV) TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor p16 (HPV) testing is recommended for throat cancer patients to detect human papillomavirus presence, which influences prognosis and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHROMOSOME TRANSLOCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chromosome translocation is a genetic change involving the switching of part of one chromosome with another within lymphoma cells, common in FL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosome translocation is a genetic change where parts of chromosomes are swapped, such as t(8;21), which is important in AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND BRACHYTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brachytherapy is a type of radiation therapy where radioactive material is placed inside the cervix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LHRH AGONIST (TRIPTORELIN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Triptorelin is a specific LHRH agonist medication used in ADT to suppress testosterone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERYTHEMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Erythema is reddening of the skin, usually in patches, a possible sign of inflammatory breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erythema is redness of the skin, a symptom of inflammatory breast cancer caused by lymph vessel blockage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL REHABILITATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physical Rehabilitation is a program to restore physical function after surgery or treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CIRCULATING TUMOR DNA (CTDNA) TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A test for tumor DNA in blood, of growing interest for monitoring or treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALB2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene involved in DNA repair; mutations increase the risk of prostate cancer and other cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"PALB2 is a gene associated with inherited mutations that increase risk for prostate cancer and other cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"PALB2 is a gene that, when mutated, can increase the risk of prostate cancer. It is one of the genes tested in germline testing for inherited cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 0A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 0a is a subgroup of stage 0 bladder cancer where cancer cells grow from the inner lining toward the hollow center of the bladder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Folate is a form of vitamin B that methotrexate blocks to prevent lymphoma cells from multiplying."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER INTERRUPTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer interruption refers to how some cancers disrupt bone formation or remodeling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CIN 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CIN 2 is moderate cervical dysplasia, which is part of high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (HSIL)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL BINDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical binder is a notebook used to organize medical records, including blood tests, imaging results, and reports, helpful for second opinions and appointments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical binder is a notebook used to organize medical records, test results, and contact information for the care team, helping patients manage their health information."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical binder is an organizational tool for keeping copies of test results and medical records, useful for second opinions and treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical binder or notebook is a tool used by patients to organize medical information, test results, and treatment plans, helping manage their health condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"A notebook or binder to organize medical records, including blood tests, imaging results, and cancer reports, useful for second opinions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A notebook or binder used to organize medical records, including blood tests, imaging results, and reports, for easy access and second opinions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A notebook or binder used to organize medical records, including blood tests, imaging results, and reports, with sections for insurance forms, test types, treatments, and questions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical Binder is a physical or digital organizer used to compile and manage medical records, test results, and treatment information for cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical binder is a notebook for organizing records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical binder is a physical or digital organizational tool used to compile and store medical records, test results, and notes for cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE REARRANGEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gene rearrangement is a genetic change at the gene level, such as RUNX1::RUNX1T, resulting from chromosome translocations in AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"External beam radiation delivers radiation from outside the body to treat cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTI-ANDROGEN (NILUTAMIDE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nilutamide is a specific anti-androgen medication that blocks testosterone from fueling cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRENOCORTICAL CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adrenocortical carcinoma (ACC) is a rare adrenal cancer that starts in the adrenal cortex. It can occur at any age but is most common in children under 5 and adults in their 40s and 50s. It may be functioning or nonfunctioning, and if caught early, it can be cured."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adrenocortical carcinoma is a rare cancer of the adrenal cortex."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adrenocortical carcinoma is a rare type of adrenal gland cancer that begins in the adrenal cortex and can be functioning or nonfunctioning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIDNEY DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kidney disease is a condition that may require dose adjustment of RAI therapy in patients on dialysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Record refers to medical documentation of a patient's health history and test results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LFT TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LFT Test is a blood test assessing liver health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PMS2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene involved in DNA repair; mutations increase the risk of colorectal, uterine, and prostate cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"PMS2 is a gene associated with inherited mutations that increase risk for colorectal, uterine, and prostate cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"PMS2 is a gene that, when mutated, can increase the risk of prostate cancer. It is one of the genes tested in germline testing for inherited cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 0IS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 0is is a subgroup of stage 0 bladder cancer, also known as carcinoma in situ, a flat patch of aggressive cancer cells on the bladder lining."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spine is a part of the bone that is a common site for breast cancer metastasis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spine is the spinal or vertebral column, a flexible column of bones including vertebrae, sacrum, and coccyx, with 24 flexible bones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spine is the vertebral column located behind the esophagus, providing structural support."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spine is a less frequent site where throat cancer cells can spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spine is part of the central nervous system; cancer found in the spine or spinal fluid may require different treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER TREATMENT EFFECT ON FERTILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer treatment can affect fertility, requiring referral to a specialist."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CIN 3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CIN 3 is severe cervical dysplasia, which is part of high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (HSIL) and is considered a pre-cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ULTRASOUND (US)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ultrasound (US) is a test that uses sound waves to create pictures of the inside of the body. It is used in liver cancer screening to detect nodules or abnormalities in the liver."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ultrasound (US) is an imaging technique used to guide lymph node biopsies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DELETION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Deletion is a type of genetic change where part of a chromosome or gene is missing, such as del(5q), seen in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deletion is a type of genetic mutation where part of a chromosome or gene is missing, such as del(5q), seen in AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND CHEMORADIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemoradiation combines chemotherapy and radiation for cervical cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTI-ANDROGEN (FLUTAMIDE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flutamide is a specific anti-androgen medication used to block testosterone effects in prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADJUVANT CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adjuvant chemotherapy is chemotherapy given after surgery to eliminate remaining cancer cells, as described in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOTE TAKING ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Note Taking Role Education is understanding the benefit of writing questions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPSY CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biopsy center is a medical facility where tissue samples are collected for analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3A bladder cancer may be in the fatty tissue surrounding the bladder or spread to a single nearby lymph node, possibly invading nearby reproductive organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPINAL FLUID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spinal fluid is the fluid surrounding the spine and brain, which may contain leukemia cells requiring lumbar puncture for testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spinal fluid surrounds the brain and spine; lymphoma in this fluid may alter treatment choices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spinal fluid, also known as cerebrospinal fluid, surrounds the spine and brain. Leukemia can travel to this fluid, and a lumbar puncture is used to test for leukemia cells there."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER BIOMARKER TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer biomarker testing looks for proteins in tumor samples to guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNA MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Changes in the DNA sequence of tumor cells that may be identified through biomarker testing to guide treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA Mutations are specific genetic changes in tumors that may be tested to identify targeted therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA mutations are changes in genetic material that can be inherited or acquired, affecting cancer risk and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA mutations are changes in the genetic material of cancer cells that may be targeted with specific therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA mutations are changes in the genetic material of cervical cells that cause them to become abnormal, leading to dysplasia and potentially cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGRAMMED DEATH-LIGAND 1 (PD-L1)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PD-L1 is a protein targeted by immune checkpoint inhibitors, often used in treating metastatic or unresectable TMB-H cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"PD-L1 is an immune protein on cancer cells that suppresses immune response; testing measures its expression to guide therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Programmed death-ligand 1 (PD-L1) is an immune protein that, when expressed on cancer cells, can suppress immune response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSERTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insertion is a genetic change where a new part of a chromosome or gene is included, seen in AML cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insertion is a genetic mutation where a new part of a chromosome or gene is added, which can occur in AML cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND HORMONE THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormone therapy is rarely used for cervical cancer but may be considered in certain cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTI-ANDROGEN (BICALUTAMIDE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bicalutamide is a specific anti-androgen medication that inhibits testosterone action on cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUSHING SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cushing syndrome is a condition caused by an adenoma producing too much cortisol, leading to various health issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cushing syndrome is a condition caused by excess cortisol production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIVER METASTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liver metastasis is the spread of breast cancer to the liver, affecting liver function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUILT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Guilt is an emotional response that can be part of distress in cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLANTBASED FOODS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plantbased foods are part of a healthy diet recommended for anal cancer survivors to reduce cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERINEUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The area between the anus and genitals, involved in abdominoperineal resection surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"The perineum is the area between the anus and genitals, which is affected by radiation therapy and surgery for anal cancer, and is a focus for healing after APR."&lt;SEP&gt;"The perineum is the area of skin between the anus and scrotum, a site through which a biopsy needle may be inserted during a transperineal biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The perineum is the skin between the anus and scrotum, through which a biopsy needle can be inserted to reach the prostate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3B&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3B bladder cancer has the same traits as stage 3A but has spread to multiple lymph nodes in the pelvis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 3B is a specific stage of ovarian cancer where visible cancer is present on the abdominal lining, smaller than 2 centimeters."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASCENDING COLON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The ascending colon is the first main section of the colon after the cecum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER GENETIC TESTING REFERRAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer genetic testing referral is when a health care provider suggests genetic testing for inherited mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MENSTRUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Menstruation is the monthly period that may stop during cancer treatment but often returns within 2 years in those under 35."&lt;SEP&gt;"Menstruation is the monthly process where the external os opens slightly to allow blood to pass into the vagina."&lt;SEP&gt;"Menstruation, or period, may stop during treatment but often returns within 2 years in those 35 and under, though pregnancy is still possible."&lt;SEP&gt;"Menstruation, or the menstrual period, may stop during cancer treatment but often returns within 2 years in younger patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"The menstrual period that may stop during treatment but often returns within 2 years in those under 35."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMBINED POSITIVE SCORE (CPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CPS is a scoring system used to measure the expression of immune proteins like PDL1 in a tumor and the immune system, guiding treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Combined positive score (CPS) measures PD-L1 expression in tumor and immune cells, used to determine eligibility for immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Combined positive score (CPS) measures PD-L1 expression in tumors and immune cells to determine eligibility for immunotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVERSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inversion is a genetic change where parts within one chromosome are switched, such as inv(16) and inv(3), seen in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inversion is a genetic mutation where parts within a chromosome are switched, such as inv(16) and inv(3), found in AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND WATCHFUL WAITING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Watchful waiting involves monitoring cervical cancer without immediate treatment in certain cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LHRH ANTAGONIST (DEGARELIX)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Degarelix is a specific LHRH antagonist medication used in ADT to rapidly lower testosterone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALDOSTERONOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aldosteronoma is an adenoma that produces too much aldosterone, a hormone that regulates blood pressure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aldosteronoma is an adenoma that produces too much aldosterone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE PROSTATE GLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The prostate gland is an organ in the pelvis, part of the male reproductive system, located near the bladder and rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anus is the opening at the end of the digestive tract through which waste is expelled."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anus is the opening at the end of the digestive tract, sometimes removed in APR or involved in colostomy procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anus is the opening at the end of the large bowel through which stool exits the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"The anus is an organ in the pelvis that may be removed during pelvic exenteration, always requiring a permanent colostomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The anus is an organ where HPV can infect and cause cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The anus is the opening at the end of the digestive tract, near the perineum, and is involved in the insertion of biopsy instruments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The anus is the opening through which stool exits the body, located at the end of the rectum."&lt;SEP&gt;"The anus is the opening through which stool exits the body, located in the pelvis at the end of the large bowel."&lt;SEP&gt;"The anus is the opening through which stool leaves the body after being held in the rectum."&lt;SEP&gt;"The anus is the opening through which stool leaves the body, located at the end of the rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 4A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage of cervical cancer where the tumor invades the bladder or rectum, treated as locally advanced."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 4A bladder cancer has invaded the wall of the pelvis or abdomen, or spread to lymph nodes far from the bladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 4A is a substage of Stage 4 ovarian cancer where there are cancer cells in the fluid around the lungs, called malignant pleural effusion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSVERSE COLON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The transverse colon is the second main section of the colon, running across the abdomen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER STAGING SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer staging system includes TNM scores and numbered stages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEXUAL REPRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sexual reproduction is the biological process by which organisms produce offspring, involving the female reproductive system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEOXYRIBONUCLEIC ACID (DNA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DNA molecules are tightly packaged into chromosomes, containing genetic information and genes that code for proteins."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMPLIFICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amplification is a genetic change where a part of a chromosome or gene is duplicated, potentially affecting AML behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amplification is a genetic change where a part or whole chromosome or gene is increased or duplicated, seen in AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND SECOND OPINION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Seeking a second opinion can help cervical cancer patients confirm diagnosis and treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LHRH ANTAGONIST (RELUGOLIX)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Relugolix is a specific LHRH antagonist medication used in ADT to reduce testosterone levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRENAL CORTEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adrenal cortex is the outer part of the adrenal gland, producing hormones like cortisol and aldosterone."&lt;SEP&gt;"The adrenal cortex is the outer layer of the adrenal gland, where adrenocortical carcinoma begins. It is involved in producing hormones such as cortisol and aldosterone."&lt;SEP&gt;"The adrenal cortex is the outer part of the adrenal gland, producing hormones like cortisol, aldosterone, and DHEA that control metabolism, blood pressure, and body features."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSYCHOLOGICAL SUPPORT SESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Psychological Support Session is a counseling session to help patients cope with emotional challenges."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DESCENDING COLON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The descending colon is the third main section of the colon, moving downward on the left side."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCROTUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The scrotum is the pouch of skin containing the testicles, located near the perineum, and is a reference point for biopsy procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 4B&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 4B bladder cancer has spread to far away lymph nodes and organs like the bones, liver, or lungs, and is metastatic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 4B is a stage of cervical cancer where the cancer has metastasized to distant organs at the time of diagnosis, indicating advanced disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 4B is a substage of Stage 4 ovarian cancer where cancer has spread to the inside of the liver or spleen, distant lymph nodes, or other organs outside the abdomen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER STAGING INFORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer staging information includes tumor location, size, spread, and grade."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UTERINE SARCOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Uterine sarcoma is a rare type of uterine cancer that arises in the muscle or supporting tissues of the uterus, distinct from cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHROMOSOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chromosome is a tightly packaged structure of DNA, with normal human cells containing 23 pairs, and it carries genetic information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosomes are structures containing DNA and genes; normal human cells have 23 pairs, and changes in chromosomes are key in AML diagnosis and prognosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosomes are structures containing DNA, with normal human cells having 23 pairs (46 total), each containing thousands of genes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosomes are structures containing DNA, with normal human cells having 23 pairs; changes like translocations or deletions are key in AML diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosomes are structures containing DNA; normal human cells have 23 pairs, each with thousands of genes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POINT MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Point mutation is a genetic change where a single part of a gene is altered, which can be found in AML cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Point mutation is a genetic change where part of a gene is altered, seen in AML cells and detected by mutation testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND PATIENT EDUCATION MATERIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patient education materials provide information about cervical cancer for patients and families."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORCHIECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Orchiectomy is a surgical procedure to remove one or both testicles, permanently reducing testosterone as a form of hormone therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRENAL MEDULLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adrenal medulla is the inner part of the adrenal gland, producing stress-response hormones."&lt;SEP&gt;"The adrenal medulla is the inner part of the adrenal gland, producing hormones like epinephrine, norepinephrine, and dopamine that control the body's response to stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"The adrenal medulla is the inner part of the adrenal gland, where pheochromocytoma begins. It produces catecholamines like adrenaline and noradrenaline."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dialysis is a treatment for kidney failure that may affect RAI therapy dosing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DCIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DCIS (Ductal Carcinoma In Situ) is a type of breast cancer that starts in the cells lining the milk ducts, and is a focus of testing and treatment planning in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREGNANCY TEST ADMINISTRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pregnancy Test Administration is giving a pregnancy test before treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIGMOID COLON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sigmoid colon is the last section of the colon, removed in LAR procedures for rectal tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The sigmoid colon is the final section of the colon, connecting to the rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINARY SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The urinary system includes organs like the bladder and urethra, which are relevant to urologist specialization and biopsy complications."&lt;SEP&gt;"The urinary system includes organs like the kidneys, bladder, and urethra, which are involved in urine production and excretion. Diseases of this system are treated by urologists."&lt;SEP&gt;"The urinary system is a group of organs including the kidneys, ureters, bladder, and urethra that remove waste from the body in the form of urine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic bladder cancer is a type that has spread outside the bladder to other areas such as lymph nodes, bones, lungs, liver, and the inner wall of the abdomen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic bladder cancer is an advanced form of bladder cancer that has spread, often treated with a combination of targeted therapy and immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic bladder cancer is cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, typically not curable but treatable."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic bladder cancer refers to cancer that has spread to distant parts of the body, such as in stage 4B."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER KEY POINTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer key points are important facts about testing, treatment, and fertility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHOVASCULAR SPACE INVASION (LVSI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LVSI is a risk factor in cervical cancer indicating the presence of tumor cells in blood or lymph vessels within the tumor. It increases the likelihood of spread to nearby lymph nodes and guides treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNE CHECKPOINT INHIBITOR THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy is a treatment that activates the immune system to fight cancer cells, used when PD-L1 expression is high."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy is a treatment that activates the immune system to fight cancer, often used when PD-L1 is expressed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy is a treatment that targets proteins like PD-1 and PD-L1 to activate the immune system against cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy is a treatment that targets proteins like PD-1 and PD-L1 to help the immune system fight cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE FUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gene fusion is a genetic event where parts of chromosomes break and recombine, leading to abnormal gene combinations, common in Ewing sarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND SUPPORTIVE CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Supportive care addresses side effects and quality of life in cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANDROGENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Androgens are male hormones, primarily testosterone, that can promote prostate cancer growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1C1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1C1 is a substage of Stage 1C ovarian cancer where the capsule of the ovary broke open during surgery, known as surgical spill."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPOINTMENT ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Appointment Role Education is understanding the importance of bringing records to visits."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC TESTING LAB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic testing lab is a facility that analyzes DNA for mutations related to cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER STAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer staging is a process used to describe the extent of cancer in the body, including tumor size, lymph node involvement, and metastasis, to guide treatment and prognosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer staging is the process of describing tumor size, location, spread, and grade to guide treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer staging is the process of determining the extent of cancer at diagnosis, using TNM scores and biomarker testing to guide prognosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer staging is the process of determining the extent of cancer in the body, divided into clinical and pathologic stages, and used to guide treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALE REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Male reproductive organs include the prostate and seminal vesicles, which are the focus of urologist expertise."&lt;SEP&gt;"Male reproductive organs include the prostate, testicles, and seminal vesicles, which are involved in reproduction and are treated by urologists."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-MUSCLE-INVASIVE BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer includes stages 0 and 1, where the cancer has not grown into the muscle layer of the bladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer is a type of bladder cancer that hasn't spread into the muscle layer, often treated with intravesical therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer is a type that has grown on or in the bladder's inner urothelial layer but not into the muscle layer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER QUESTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer questions are patient queries about diagnosis, treatment, and support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADICAL TRACHELECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of trachelectomy where about 2 centimeters of vaginal tissue is removed in addition to the cervix."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radical trachelectomy is a fertility-sparing surgery that removes the cervix and part of the vagina while preserving the uterus, allowing for future pregnancy. It is used for certain stage 1 cervical cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARYNGOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Laryngoscopy is a general term for examining the larynx (voice box) using a scope, encompassing both fiberoptic and direct methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laryngoscopy is an exam of the back of the throat, including the larynx and hypopharynx, using a laryngoscope; it can be performed indirectly, with a flexible scope, or directly under anesthesia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISMATCH REPAIR PROTEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mismatch repair proteins are cellular components that fix DNA errors; defects in them lead to microsatellite instability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND SYMPTOM MANAGEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Symptom management helps control pain, fatigue, and other cervical cancer symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gland is an organ that produces hormones; the testicles are glands that make testosterone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 4: TREATMENT BY RISK AND RECURRENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 4 is a section of the NCCN Guidelines for Patients that provides treatment recommendations based on risk and recurrence of cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNG METASTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lung metastasis is the spread of breast cancer to the lungs, causing breathing difficulties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T (TUMOR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T (Tumor) refers to the size and depth of the primary tumor, measured in centimeters, with specific staging criteria for different locations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE DENSITY MONITORING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone density monitoring is a test to assess bone strength, recommended for anal cancer survivors due to radiation effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICAL STAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical Stage is the cancer stage given before treatment, based on physical exam, biopsy, and imaging tests, such as cN1 or cM."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clinical stage (c) is the rating given before any treatment, based on physical exam, biopsy, and imaging tests, such as cN2 or cM."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clinical stage (c) is the rating given before any treatment, based on physical exam, biopsy, and imaging tests, used in initial diagnosis of nasopharyngeal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clinical stage (c) is the rating given before any treatment, based on physical exam, biopsy, and imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clinical stage is the cancer rating given before treatment, based on physical exam, biopsy, and other tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVASIVE TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An invasive test is a medical procedure that goes into the body, such as a biopsy, and carries risks like infection, bleeding, and pain."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSCLE-INVASIVE BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muscle-invasive bladder cancer includes stages 2, 3, and 4, where the cancer has grown into the muscle layer and requires more intense treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Muscle-invasive bladder cancer is a more advanced stage where cancer has spread into the bladder muscle, requiring complex treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Muscle-invasive bladder cancer is a type of bladder cancer that has grown through the inner urothelial layer into the muscle layer of the bladder wall."&lt;SEP&gt;"Muscle-invasive bladder cancer is a type of bladder cancer that has spread into the muscle layer, often treated with radical cystectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER INSURANCE COVERAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer insurance coverage is a concern about payment for tests and treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic lymph node evaluation is a procedure to assess lymph nodes in the pelvis for cancer spread. It is often performed alongside cone biopsy or trachelectomy for early-stage cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHARYNGOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pharyngoscopy is a procedure to examine the pharynx (throat) using an endoscope, often part of panendoscopy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUORIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fluoride is a chemical element used in the production of FDG, a radiotracer for PET scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fluoride is a chemical element used in the synthesis of FDG for PET imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fluoride is a component of FDG, a radiotracer used in PET scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND PSYCHOSOCIAL SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Psychosocial support addresses emotional and social needs of cervical cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INHERITED GENETIC MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An inherited genetic mutation is present in every cell of the body, increasing cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 2: TESTING FOR BASAL CELL SKIN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 2 is a section of the NCCN Guidelines for Patients that covers testing procedures for diagnosing basal cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE UTERUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The uterus is a female reproductive organ located in the pelvis, near the bladder and rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATHOLOGIC STAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pathologic Stage is the cancer stage determined after surgery by examining removed tissue, such as pN, providing more accurate details."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathologic stage (p) or surgical stage is determined by examining tissue removed during surgery, providing a more accurate picture of cancer spread, such as pN."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathologic stage (p) or surgical stage is determined by examining tissue removed during surgery, providing more specific details about cancer size and lymph node status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathologic stage is a prognostic stage determined after surgery, providing more specific details about cancer size and lymph node status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathologic stage is the post-surgery stage determined from surgical findings, guiding treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathologic stage, or surgical stage, is determined by examining tissue removed during surgery, including features like size, shape, and cell type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLEEDING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bleeding can be detected by imaging tests and may impact care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bleeding is a complication that can occur after a prostate biopsy, either from the rectum or internally, and usually resolves within a few days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bleeding is a potential complication of biopsies, which may occur from the rectum or other biopsy sites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bleeding is a side effect of bladder removal surgery, requiring medical attention to manage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bleeding is the loss of blood, which is controlled by platelets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bleeding is the loss of blood, which the body stops by forming clots; impaired clotting can cause excessive bleeding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTATE GLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prostate gland is a gland in the male reproductive system, located just below the bladder, where prostate cancer develops."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostate gland is a male reproductive organ that produces PSA, where cancer originates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The prostate gland is a male reproductive organ that can develop cancer and is the target of biopsies and imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"The prostate gland is a male reproductive organ that produces PSA, a protein that helps semen transport sperm. It is the site where prostate cancer develops."&lt;SEP&gt;"The prostate gland is a male reproductive organ that produces PSA. Abnormalities in the prostate can lead to increased PSA production."&lt;SEP&gt;"The prostate gland is a male reproductive organ where prostate cancer originates; tumor growth beyond it indicates advanced disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"The prostate gland is a reproductive organ in males that stage 3A bladder cancer may invade."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER HELP PAYING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer help paying refers to financial assistance for tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAGINAL BRACHYTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vaginal brachytherapy is a type of internal radiation therapy where a radioactive source is placed inside the vagina to target cancer cells. It may be added to EBRT and chemotherapy for certain cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR HISTOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor histology is the cancer subtype determined by a pathologist examining biopsy samples under a microscope."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor histology is the microscopic classification of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor histology refers to the microscopic classification of cancer subtype determined by a pathologist."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor histology refers to the microscopic examination of tumor tissue to determine its subtype and characteristics, performed by a pathologist."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INCISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Incision is a small cut made during surgical biopsies to access and remove tumor samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND FINANCIAL TOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Financial toxicity refers to the economic burden of cervical cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRONIC MYELOID LEUKEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chronic myeloid leukemia (CML) is a type of blood cancer caused by a specific abnormal gene (BCR::ABL1) and the Philadelphia chromosome, leading to an overproduction of white blood cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A skin exam is a focused examination of the skin."&lt;SEP&gt;"A skin exam is a physical examination of the skin to identify concerning lesions that may indicate basal cell skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A skin exam is a test for CBCL that involves examining the skin for lesions or nodules."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINANCIAL AID PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Financial Aid Program is an initiative to help patients cover treatment costs and related expenses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P16-NEGATIVE (HPV-) CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"p16-negative throat cancer starts in the oropharynx and is not caused by human papillomavirus (HPV), with specific TNM staging for squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pain is a common symptom of cancer and treatment, requiring management strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pain is a physical symptom that may persist after cancer treatment, addressed in survivorship care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pain is a potential complication of a prostate biopsy, managed with anesthesia during the procedure and typically subsiding afterward."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pain is a symptom that can be managed by pain specialists and supportive care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pain is a symptom that may indicate breast cancer or bone issues, leading to diagnostic imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pain is a symptom that may indicate nerve invasion by cancer, including burning, stinging, or loss of feeling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pain is not expected during a biopsy after local anesthetic is administered, ensuring patient comfort."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAGINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The female reproductive organ near which the urethra opens, examined during cystoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The muscular canal leading from the cervix to the outside of the body, which may be involved in cancer spread and treated with brachytherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The muscular canal leading from the cervix to the outside of the body, which may be partially removed in certain surgeries."&lt;SEP&gt;"The vagina is a female reproductive organ that may be removed during pelvic exenteration and reconstructed afterward."&lt;SEP&gt;"The vagina is a nearby organ that anal cancer can invade in stage IIIB or IIIC."&lt;SEP&gt;"The vagina is a part of the female reproductive system, partially removed in some cervical cancer surgeries."&lt;SEP&gt;"The vagina is a reproductive organ in females that stage 3A bladder cancer may invade."&lt;SEP&gt;"The vagina is an organ where HPV can infect and cause cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The vagina is part of the female reproductive system, serving as the canal that connects the cervix to the outside of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"The vagina is the canal leading from the cervix to the external body, and cervical cancer can spread into its upper or lower portions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The vagina is the canal leading from the cervix to the outside of the body. Cervical cancer can spread to the upper vagina (stage 2A)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The vagina is the canal through which the applicator is inserted for brachytherapy treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The vagina, or birth canal, is the muscular passage through which babies are born. It connects to the cervix and is part of the female reproductive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vagina is a female reproductive organ, part of which may be removed during radical cystectomy if cancer has spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vagina is a part of the female reproductive tract that can be imaged via MRI to assess cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vagina is part of the female reproductive system, included in the context of ovarian cancer anatomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vagina is the anatomical site affected by atrophy, where the lining becomes thin, dry, and inflamed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vagina is the canal leading to the cervix, examined during pelvic exam and used for transvaginal ultrasound."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER NEXT STEPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer next steps are discussions with health care providers about treatment plans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 2A is a specific stage of ovarian cancer where cancer has grown into or spread to the uterus and/or fallopian tubes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 2A is a stage of cervical cancer where the tumor has spread to the upper vagina but not to the pelvic wall. Treatment typically involves surgery or radiation therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNE CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immune cells are found in lymph nodes and help the body fight infection and disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune cells are part of the body's defense system that may be affected by PD-L1 expression on cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune cells are part of the body's defense system, and PD-L1 on cancer cells can cause them to ignore cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune cells are part of the body's defense system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune cells are part of the body's defense system; cancer can suppress them via PD-1/PD-L1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune cells, such as granulocytes, help prevent and control infection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYRINGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Syringe is a medical device used to draw liquid bone marrow during an aspirate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND INSURANCE COVERAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insurance coverage affects access to cervical cancer screening and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutrients are substances carried by blood to cells throughout the body for energy and function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutrients are substances in food that the body needs for energy, growth, and repair. The digestive system absorbs nutrients in the small intestine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORTISOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cortisol is a hormone produced by the adrenal cortex that controls metabolism and stress response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cortisol is a hormone that controls metabolism and stress response, produced by the adrenal cortex."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREGNANT PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pregnant people are a group requiring special safety measures around radiation exposure after RAI therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH CARE PROVIDERS (HCPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health Care Providers (HCPs) include professionals such as breast specialists, breast diagnostic radiologists, gynecologists, and lactation consultants, who are involved in breast health and cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE SCAN IMAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone Scan Imaging is the process of taking pictures of bones using a radiotracer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACUTE LYMPHOBLASTIC LEUKEMIA (ALL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) is a fast-growing blood cancer that starts in disease-fighting white blood cells called lymphocytes. It involves the bone marrow producing too many immature lymphocytes called lymphoblasts, which crowd out normal bone marrow and reduce blood production. ALL has two main types: B-cell ALL (B-ALL) and T-cell ALL (T-ALL)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) is a fast-growing blood cancer starting in lymphocytes, common in children, with subtypes B-ALL and T-ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) is a fast-growing blood cancer that starts in lymphocytes, most common in children, with types including B-ALL and T-ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) is a fast-growing blood cancer where bone marrow produces too many immature lymphocytes called lymphoblasts, making it hard for bone marrow or blood to function. Diagnosis requires 20% or more lymphoblasts in the bone marrow."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) is a fast-growing cancer that starts in lymphocytes, a type of white blood cell. It is characterized by the overproduction of immature lymphocytes called lymphoblasts in the bone marrow, which can crowd out other blood cells and impair blood function. Treatment depends on the type of ALL, age at diagnosis, and other factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD IN URINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A symptom that may prompt urine cytology testing to check for cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood in urine is a possible complication after a prostate biopsy, where red blood cells appear in the urine, usually resolving within a few days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood in urine is a possible complication following a prostate biopsy, indicating bleeding in the urinary tract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood in urine is a symptom that can occur in prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood in urine is a symptom that may indicate urinary tract issues, prompting tests like urogram or pyelogram to identify causes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood in urine is a symptom that may occur in prostate cancer, indicating potential issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UROTHELIAL CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cells that make up the inner lining of the bladder; most bladder cancers originate from these cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urothelial cells are stretchy cells that line the inside of the bladder and the rest of the urinary tract, where most bladder cancers originate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urothelial cells are the cells that make up the inner lining of the bladder, where most bladder cancers start."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER PROGNOSIS AND TREATMENT OPTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer prognosis and treatment options are determined by cancer type and stage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1A1 CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1A1 cancer is a very early-stage cervical cancer where the tumor is microscopic and confined to the cervix. Treatment may involve cone biopsy or radical trachelectomy, with or without pelvic lymph node evaluation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTI-TUMOR IMMUNE RESPONSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anti-tumor immune response is the body's ability to fight cancer cells, which can be suppressed by PD-L1 expression."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anti-tumor immune response is the body's immune reaction against cancer, which PD-L1 can suppress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anti-tumor immune response is the body's reaction against cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anti-tumor immune response is the immune system's attack on cancer, which can be suppressed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEEK SWAB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cheek swab is a method of collecting saliva or cells for genetic testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cheek swab is a method to collect saliva for genetic testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
