    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESECTABLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Resectable describes a tumor that can be completely removed with surgery, indicating a favorable treatment outlook."&lt;SEP&gt;"Resectable refers to a tumor that can be completely removed with surgery, as a term used in cancer staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD IN STOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood in stool is a possible complication after a prostate biopsy, where red blood cells appear in the stool, usually resolving within a few days."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood in stool is a possible complication following a prostate biopsy, indicating bleeding in the digestive tract."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESOPHAGUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Esophagus (swallowing tube) is examined during esophagoscopy and panendoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Esophagus is a body part examined in esophagoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Esophagus is a body part."&lt;SEP&gt;"Esophagus is a muscular tube in the digestive system that transports food from the throat to the stomach, and is the site of esophageal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The esophagus is a hollow muscular tube that carries food and liquid to the stomach. It is part of the throat anatomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The esophagus is a muscular tube connecting the throat to the stomach, composed of layers including mucosa, submucosa, muscularis propria, and tunica adventitia, with upper, middle, and lower parts having different muscle types."&lt;SEP&gt;"The esophagus is a muscular tube connecting the throat to the stomach. It is part of the digestive tract and transports food and drink."&lt;SEP&gt;"The esophagus is a part of the digestive system that connects the mouth to the stomach, allowing food and drink to pass through."&lt;SEP&gt;"The esophagus is a tube that connects the throat to the stomach, allowing food and drink to pass through. It is part of the digestive tract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The esophagus is part of the upper GI tract, examined during upper endoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The esophagus is the tube that goes to the stomach, connected to the pharynx and a potential site for cancer, such as esophageal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER SARCOMA CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
