    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNRESECTABLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unresectable describes a tumor that cannot be completely removed with surgery due to involvement of vital structures, making removal unsafe."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unresectable refers to a tumor that cannot be completely removed with surgery due to involvement of nearby structures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD IN SEMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood in semen is a possible complication after a prostate biopsy, where red blood cells appear in the semen, usually resolving within a few weeks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood in semen is a possible complication following a prostate biopsy, indicating bleeding in the reproductive tract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood in semen is a symptom that can occur in prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood in semen is a symptom that may occur in prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL INTESTINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Small intestine is a part of the digestive system used in the construction of the Indiana pouch to connect the pouch to a stoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Small intestine is a part of the digestive system, sections of which are used in urinary diversions like ileal conduit and neobladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Small intestine is part of the digestive system where food is broken down into liquid after leaving the stomach."&lt;SEP&gt;"The small intestine is a long, coiled tube where most nutrient absorption occurs. It receives chyme from the stomach."&lt;SEP&gt;"The small intestine is a part of the digestive system where nutrients from chyme are absorbed into the bloodstream."&lt;SEP&gt;"The small intestine is part of the digestive system where bile and pancreatic juices aid in digestion and nutrient absorption."&lt;SEP&gt;"The small intestine is part of the digestive tract where nutrients are absorbed into the bloodstream. It is connected to the stomach and is involved in the digestion process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The small intestine is where bile and pancreatic juices aid in digestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER BIOPSY RECOMMENDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer biopsy recommendation is to have biopsy at an experienced center."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1B1 CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1B1 cancer is an early-stage cervical cancer with a tumor larger than 1A2 but still confined to the cervix. Treatment may include cone biopsy for very low-risk cases or radical trachelectomy with lymph node evaluation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUMBING MEDICINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Numbing medicine is sprayed in the nose during fiberoptic laryngoscopy to reduce discomfort."&lt;SEP&gt;"Numbing medicine is used to reduce discomfort during procedures like laryngoscopy and endoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Numbing medicine, or local anesthetic, is injected into the skin before a biopsy to prevent pain during the procedure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EWS GENE (EWSR1)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EWS gene (EWSR1) is a gene on chromosome 22 that fuses with ETS family members in Ewing sarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND CULTURAL COMPETENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cultural competence in healthcare improves cervical cancer care for diverse populations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATURE BLOOD CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mature blood cells are fully developed red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets that function normally."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPINEPHRINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Epinephrine is a hormone produced by the adrenal medulla that controls the body's response to stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epinephrine is a hormone that controls stress response, produced by the adrenal medulla."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE OVARIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The ovaries are female reproductive organs located in the pelvis, near the bladder and rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCOREGIONAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Locoregional or locally advanced refers to a tumor that has spread to tissue, organs, or lymph nodes in the head and neck region."&lt;SEP&gt;"Locoregional or locally advanced refers to a tumor that has spread to tissue, organs, or lymph nodes in the head and neck."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACTIVE SURVEILLANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A management strategy for some very-low-risk thyroid cancers, involving close monitoring instead of immediate surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Active surveillance is a management strategy for early-stage prostate cancer where patients undergo regular tests to monitor the cancer without immediate treatment, aiming to avoid side effects unless the cancer progresses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Active surveillance is a management strategy for low-risk prostate cancer where treatment is deferred and the cancer is closely monitored with regular tests and imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Active surveillance is a management strategy for prostate cancer where patients undergo regular monitoring, including repeated biopsies, to track disease progression without immediate treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Active surveillance is a monitoring approach for very small, low-risk thyroid tumors, using ultrasound to track size without immediate surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GALLBLADDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gallbladder is a small organ that stores bile produced by the liver, releasing it to aid in fat digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gallbladder is a small organ that stores bile, which aids in digestion. It is listed as part of the digestive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gallbladder is a small, pear-shaped organ under the liver that stores bile produced by the liver."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gallbladder is an organ associated with bile ducts, covered by serosa and containing layers like epithelium and muscle."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gallbladder is an organ in the digestive system that stores bile produced by the liver."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gallbladder is an organ that stores bile produced by the liver, and is part of the hepatobiliary system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER BIOPSY PLACEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer biopsy placement is critical for accurate diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1B2 CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1B2 cancer is an early-stage cervical cancer with a larger tumor confined to the cervix. Fertility-sparing surgery is less common, and abdominal surgery is generally preferred."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARYNGOSCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Laryngoscope is a scope used in direct laryngoscopy to view the throat."&lt;SEP&gt;"Laryngoscope is a thin, long tube with a fiberoptic light used in laryngoscopy to examine the throat and voice box."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETS GENE FAMILY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ETS gene family includes genes like FLI1, ERG, ETV1, ETV4, and FEV that fuse with EWSR1 in Ewing sarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND LANGUAGE BARRIERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Language barriers can hinder cervical cancer education and care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIVER ISSUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liver issues are potential side effects of certain drugs like gemtuzumab ozogamicin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOREPINEPHRINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Norepinephrine is a hormone produced by the adrenal medulla that helps control stress response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Norepinephrine is a hormone that helps control stress response, produced by the adrenal medulla."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICAL TRIAL ENROLLMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical Trial Enrollment is the process of joining a clinical trial, involving consent and eligibility checks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic refers to cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, including lung and distant lymph nodes, and is considered very advanced disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic refers to cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, including the lung and distant lymph nodes, often called very advanced disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONFIRMATORY BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A confirmatory biopsy is a second biopsy performed within a year of the initial diagnosis to verify the presence of cancer and assess any changes over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PANCREAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pancreas is an organ in the digestive system that produces enzymes and hormones for digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pancreas is a gland that helps digest food and control blood sugar, and is the organ where pancreatic cancer develops."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pancreas is a large gland in the digestive system, located deep inside the body below the liver and behind the stomach. It makes enzymes and hormones."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pancreas is an organ in the digestive system that produces enzymes and hormones, including insulin."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pancreas is an organ in the digestive system that produces enzymes and hormones. It is mentioned as part of the digestive system's components."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pancreas is an organ near the esophagus that can be invaded by esophageal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pancreas is an organ near the liver that produces digestive enzymes and hormones, sometimes considered part of the hepatobiliary system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pancreas is an organ near the liver that produces digestive enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pancreas is an organ that produces digestive enzymes and hormones like insulin. It is part of the digestive system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER EXPERIENCED SURGEON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer experienced surgeon is a specialist who performs biopsies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2A CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 2A cancer is a cervical cancer that has spread to the upper vagina but not to the pelvic wall. Treatment typically involves surgery or radiation therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A scope is a thin, tube-shaped tool inserted into the mouth or nose to examine the throat (pharynx)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scope is a general term for instruments used to examine internal body parts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scope is a thin, tube-shaped tool with a light and camera used in scoping procedures to examine internal areas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLI1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FLI1 is a gene in the ETS family that most commonly fuses with EWSR1 in Ewing sarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND HEALTH LITERACY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health literacy affects understanding of cervical cancer prevention and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD COUNT RECOVERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood count recovery refers to the return of normal levels of blood cells after treatment, which may be delayed by certain therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOPAMINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dopamine is a hormone involved in stress response, produced by the adrenal medulla."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dopamine is a hormone produced by the adrenal medulla that is involved in stress response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE 1 GLIOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade 1 gliomas are slow-growing, usually benign brain tumors that can often be treated with surgery alone, more common in children than adults."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST DIAGNOSTIC RADIOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breast diagnostic radiologist interprets results of mammograms, MRIs, and other imaging tests, and performs needle biopsies as needed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOTRACER INJECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiotracer Injection is the administration of a tracer into the vein for bone scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPIGLOTTIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The epiglottis is a flap that closes the airway to the trachea, and tumor growth into it indicates a T3 stage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR BIOMARKER TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular biomarker testing is a type of genetic test that analyzes tumor tissue or blood for specific biomarkers to guide prostate cancer treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular biomarker testing is a type of test that examines molecular components of a biopsy sample to assess the risk of prostate cancer spreading. It is also called genomic testing, tumor profiling, or molecular tumor testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The cardia is the opening where the esophagus connects to the stomach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER TREATMENT CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer treatment center is where the patient receives care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONE BIOPSY MARGINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cone biopsy margins refer to the edges of tissue removed during a cone biopsy. If cancer or pre-cancer is found at the margins, further treatment may be needed, such as another cone biopsy, hysterectomy, or brachytherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMAGING RESULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Imaging Results are reports from imaging tests like bone scans, included in a medical binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging results are from tests like CT or ultrasound."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging results are outputs from imaging tests, such as CT or MRI scans, used to document cancer findings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging results are outputs from tests like CT, MRI, or ultrasound, used to visualize internal structures and guide treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging results are reports from scans like MRI, CT, or PET that help determine the extent of NPC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging results are reports from tests like mammograms or MRIs, used to guide diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging results from tests like CT scans or ultrasounds are part of medical records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical images such as scans that are part of records organized in a medical binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Results from imaging tests like CT, MRI, or PET scans, which are copied and stored in a medical binder for reference and second opinions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ERG is a gene in the ETS family that can fuse with EWSR1 in Ewing sarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND DIGITAL HEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Digital health tools can support cervical cancer screening and patient engagement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONE RECEPTOR STATUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormone receptor status is a test result indicating whether breast cancer cells have receptors for hormones like estrogen or progesterone, guiding treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormone receptor status refers to the presence of estrogen or progesterone receptors on cancer cells, which is a key biomarker for treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1C3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1C3 is a substage of Stage 1C ovarian cancer where cancer cells are found in ascites or washings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUTANEOUS B-CELL LYMPHOMA (CBCL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cutaneous B-cell lymphoma (CBCL) is a type of primary cutaneous lymphoma that develops from abnormal B cells, appearing as nodules under the skin that may look like small pimples called papules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cutaneous B-cell lymphoma (CBCL) starts in B cells, a type of lymphocyte, and appears as a condition related to the lymphatic system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cutaneous B-cell lymphoma is a type of cancer that affects the skin, requiring accurate testing for diagnosis and treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONLINE FORUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Online forum is a digital community where patients share experiences and advice."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARYNX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larynx (voice box) is a part of the body examined during laryngoscopy and fiberoptic nasopharyngolaryngoscopy to look for tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larynx (voice box) is a structure examined during laryngoscopy and panendoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larynx is a body part examined in laryngoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larynx is a body part."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larynx is a part of the body where cartilage provides structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larynx is a part of the throat that can be affected by advanced nasopharyngeal cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larynx is part of the throat, and tumor invasion into it indicates a T4a stage of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larynx, also known as the voice box, is a specific part of the throat. Tumors from throat cancer can grow into nearby tissue and organs, such as the larynx."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larynx, or voice box, is a site where head and neck cancer can occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larynx, or voice box, is part of the throat anatomy, connected to the pharynx and a potential site for head and neck cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INHERITED MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene change passed from parents, causing syndromes like Lynch syndrome."&lt;SEP&gt;"An inherited mutation, also called a germline mutation, is a genetic change present in every cell of the body, passed down from parents, which can increase cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Change."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene change from parents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene change passed from parents."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNDUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The fundus is the upper part of the stomach, storing undigested food and gases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER HEALTH CARE PROVIDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer health care provider is a medical professional who guides treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRE-CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pre-cancer refers to abnormal cells that have the potential to become cancerous. It may be found in cone biopsy margins and influences treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATHOLOGY REPORTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pathology Reports are documents detailing tissue analysis, included in a medical binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathology reports are documents detailing the analysis of biopsy or tissue samples, providing critical information for cancer diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathology reports are documents from biopsy analysis included in medical records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathology reports are from biopsy analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathology reports contain detailed information about cancer, including abbreviations like pN0(mol+), ypT2, or cN, which need explanation by care teams."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETV1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ETV1 is a gene in the ETS family that can fuse with EWSR1 in Ewing sarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND MOBILE HEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mobile health apps can provide cervical cancer education and reminders."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PD-1 AND PD-L1 TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PD-1 and PD-L1 testing checks for immune proteins on cancer cells that suppress immune response; expression may guide checkpoint inhibitor therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNCTIONAL ADRENAL TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Functional adrenal tumors are usually benign but can produce hormones and may be found during tests for hormone-related symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHARMACIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pharmacist dispenses medications and provides information about drug interactions and side effects for breast cancer treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A professional who prepares chemotherapy and other medicines and offers treatment advice."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M (METASTASIS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M (Metastasis) describes whether cancer has spread to distant parts of the body, with M0 and M1 categories including lung or other sites."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APR SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"APR (Abdominoperineal Resection) surgery removes the anus and creates a permanent colostomy, used for anal cancer that does not respond to treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INHERITED MUTATIONS OF MMR GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mutations passed from parents that cause Lynch syndrome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAROTID ARTERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The carotid artery is a major blood vessel in the neck that can be involved in advanced nasopharyngeal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The carotid artery is a major blood vessel in the neck, and tumor encasement of it indicates a T4b stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"The carotid artery is a major blood vessel located in the parapharyngeal space, which can be affected by tumor spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACQUIRED MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene change occurring spontaneously in some cells due to environmental factors or chance."&lt;SEP&gt;"An acquired mutation, also called a somatic mutation, is a genetic change that occurs spontaneously in some cells later in life, potentially leading to cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BODY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Body refers to the physical structure where symptoms like weakness, sensory disturbances, and blood clots can occur in brain tumor patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"The body is the main part of the stomach where digestion continues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER FERTILITY SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer fertility specialist is a doctor who helps preserve fertility before treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WELL DIFFERENTIATED (LOW GRADE) G1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A grade of perianal cancer indicating low-grade differentiation, relevant for determining eligibility for local excision."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOLOGY REPORTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiology Reports are documents from imaging tests, included in a medical binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiology reports are documents from imaging tests included in medical records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiology reports are from imaging tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETV4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ETV4 is a gene in the ETS family that can fuse with EWSR1 in Ewing sarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND WEARABLE TECHNOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wearable technology may monitor cervical cancer patients' health during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immunohistochemistry (IHC) is a staining technique to visualize proteins on cancer or immune cells under a microscope."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immunohistochemistry is a lab technique used to detect specific proteins like hormone receptors and HER2 on cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALIGNANT ADRENAL TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Malignant adrenal tumors are cancerous and rare, with about 300 to 500 people diagnosed each year."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HERBAL TEAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Herbal teas are plant-based beverages used as complementary therapy for relaxation and symptom relief."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE VAGINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The vagina is a female reproductive organ located in the pelvis, near the bladder and rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) is the genetic material in cells that may contain mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) is the genetic material in cells, containing instructions for protein production, and mutations in DNA can lead to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) is the molecule that carries genetic information, packaged into chromosomes within cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) molecules are tightly packaged into chromosomes, containing genetic information, and are the basis for genetic testing in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) molecules are tightly packaged into chromosomes, which contain genes that code for proteins; mutations in DNA can lead to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA contains genetic information; mutations in cancer cells are analyzed in biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA controls how cells grow and function. Damage to DNA inside basal skin cells from UV radiation can cause cells to become abnormal and grow out of control, leading to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA is genetic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA is the body's genetic instructions, and mutations in it can lead to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA is the genetic material analyzed by next-generation sequencing to identify mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA is the genetic material analyzed in tests like NGS and PCR to identify mutations associated with leukemia."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA is the genetic material in cells that can contain mutations leading to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA is the genetic material in cells where mutations can occur, leading to cancer development and providing targets for biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA is the genetic material that can be damaged and repaired by MMR genes, and mutations can lead to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA is the genetic material that can undergo mutations, translocations, and other changes relevant to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"DNA is the molecule inside cells that contains genetic information, organized into genes, which can undergo mutations leading to diseases like cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The molecule containing genetic instructions, composed of segments called genes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTRUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The antrum is the lower portion of the stomach where food mixes with enzymes and acid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN PAPILLOMAVIRUS (HPV)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV is a common sexually transmitted infection with over 100 strains; long-term infection with high-risk types like HPV16 and HPV18 causes almost all cervical cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV is a group of viruses that can cause warts and some cancers, including throat cancer, and may be tested in nasopharyngeal cancer cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV is a sexually transmitted virus strongly linked to anal cancer and other cancers, with high-risk strains like HPV16 increasing cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human papillomavirus (HPV) is a group of viruses that can cause warts and cancers, including throat cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human papillomavirus (HPV) is a virus associated with some throat cancers. The text mentions p16 (HPV) testing as part of the diagnostic process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human papillomavirus (HPV) is a virus causing abnormal tissue growth and is almost always the cause of anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human papillomavirus (HPV) is a virus linked to throat cancer; p16 testing detects its presence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human papillomavirus (HPV) is a virus that can cause throat cancer, with p16-positive cancers being HPV-related."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human papillomavirus (HPV) is the most common sexually transmitted infection and is the primary cause of most cervical cancers. Long-term infection with HPV leads to cervical changes and cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER GENETIC TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer genetic testing is a referral for inherited mutation analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED (INTERMEDIATE GRADE) G2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A grade of perianal cancer indicating intermediate differentiation, relevant for treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETICS REPORTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetics Reports are documents on genetic testing, included in a medical binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetics reports are documents from biomarker testing included in medical records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetics reports are from biomarker testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FEV is a gene in the ETS family that can fuse with EWSR1 in Ewing sarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND BIG DATA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Big data analytics can improve cervical cancer research and outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRCA TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BRCA tests detect mutations in BRCA1 or BRCA2 genes, which increase risk for breast, ovarian, and other cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISTANT PARTS OF THE BODY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Distant parts of the body refer to areas far from the original cancer site where metastasis can occur."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic conditions are hereditary mutations passed from parent to child that can increase the risk of developing adrenal tumors. Examples include Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome, Li-Fraumeni syndrome, and Lynch syndrome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic conditions are inherited factors that may increase the risk of developing malignant adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVOR SUPPORT GROUP MEETING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survivor Support Group Meeting is a gathering of cancer survivors to share experiences and provide mutual support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecules produced by cells based on gene instructions, essential for bodily functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are molecules made by cells based on instructions from genes, and abnormal proteins due to mutations can contribute to cancer development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins like Nectin-4 and Trop-2 are found on cancer cells and serve as targets for certain targeted therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PYLORUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The pylorus is a valve connecting the stomach to the duodenum, regulating the passage of chyme."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Infants are a patient group covered in the ALL treatment guidelines, as ALL can occur in this age group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infants are the most common age group for neuroblastoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infants are young children who may be diagnosed with ALL, and treatment depends on age at diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NASOPHARYNGEAL CARCINOMA (NPC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nasopharyngeal carcinoma (NPC) is a type of cancer that affects the nasopharynx, a small tube-shaped structure connecting the nasal cavity to the oropharynx. It is a rare cancer most common in people from parts of Asia, Native America, and North Africa, and typically starts in squamous cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nasopharyngeal carcinoma (NPC) is a type of cancer that starts in the nasopharynx, the upper part of the throat behind the nose. It is classified using TNM staging for squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nasopharyngeal carcinoma (NPC) is a type of cancer that starts in the nasopharynx, with staging based on TNM scores and other factors like Epstein-Barr virus levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POORLY DIFFERENTIATED (HIGH GRADE) G3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A grade of perianal cancer indicating high-grade differentiation, associated with more aggressive disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT REPORTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment reports are documents about therapies included in medical records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment reports document therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHROMOSOME 11&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chromosome 11 is a chromosome involved in translocations with chromosome 22, common in Ewing sarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND PRECISION MEDICINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Precision medicine tailors cervical cancer treatment based on individual characteristics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CA 15-3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CA 15-3 is a tumor marker protein tested in blood or tissue, elevated levels may suggest cancer growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVOCATE FOR YOURSELF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Advocating for yourself involves actively participating in your care by asking questions and making informed decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE 2 GLIOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade 2 gliomas are slow-growing tumors with somewhat abnormal cells that can invade normal tissue and may recur as higher-grade gliomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SORAFENIB (NEXAVAR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sorafenib (Nexavar) is a targeted therapy drug recommended as an alternative for treating thyroid cancer that cannot be removed with surgery and is progressing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTATION CONSULTANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lactation consultant specializes in breastfeeding support and guidance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactation consultant specializes in breastfeeding, providing support and guidance to those who are lactating."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAMERA IMAGING&quot;">
