      <data key="d1">"Camera Imaging is the use of a special camera to capture tracer distribution in bones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD SAMPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood sample is a specimen of blood taken from a patient, used for germline testing to detect inherited mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"A blood sample is used for various tests, including CBC, chemistry profile, CEA, and ctDNA testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood Sample is the specimen taken for blood tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood sample is a sample of blood used in biomarker testing to detect genetic mutations or features of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood sample is used in tumor mutation testing to detect cancer DNA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUODENUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The duodenum is the first part of the small intestine, receiving chyme from the stomach."&lt;SEP&gt;"The duodenum is the first part of the small intestine, where bile and pancreatic secretions enter."&lt;SEP&gt;"The duodenum is the first part of the small intestine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHILDREN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Children are an age group where translocation RCC tends to be diagnosed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children are individuals who may inherit germline mutations from their parents, affecting cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children are the most common age group for ALL diagnosis, and treatment guidelines cover this population."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children are the most common group diagnosed with ALL, and treatment is tailored to their specific needs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children can inherit gene mutations from parents, making family history important."&lt;SEP&gt;"Children with thyroid cancer may require adjusted doses of RAI therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPSTEIN-BARR VIRUS (EBV)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) is a virus whose levels in the blood are used as a prognostic factor in staging nasopharyngeal carcinoma, and it is also associated with lymph node positivity in T0 cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNDIFFERENTIATED (HIGH GRADE) G4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A grade of perianal cancer indicating undifferentiated high-grade disease, associated with aggressive behavior."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROCEDURE REPORTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Procedure reports are documents about surgical or diagnostic procedures included in medical records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Procedure reports document diagnostic or surgical procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSLOCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Translocation is a genetic change where parts are switched between two chromosomes, such as t(8;21)(q22;q1), seen in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Translocation is a genetic event where parts of chromosomes break and switch, leading to gene fusions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND GENOMICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genomics studies genetic changes in cervical cancer to develop targeted therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CA is a tumor marker protein (likely CA 27.29) tested in breast cancer, but not reliable alone for detection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3A1 (I)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3A1 (i) is a substage of Stage 3A1 where cancer in the lymph nodes is 10 millimeters or smaller."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CUTANEOUS LYMPHOMAS (PCL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary cutaneous lymphomas (PCL) are a rare group of non-Hodgkin lymphomas that develop in the skin from abnormal B or T lymphocytes, not from skin cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLON TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A tumor in the colon, analyzed for biomarkers like dMMR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINE SAMPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A urine sample is a specimen of urine taken from a patient, used for germline testing to detect inherited mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESOPHAGOGASTRIC JUNCTION (EGJ)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The esophagogastric junction is where the esophagus joins the stomach, just below the diaphragm."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YOUNG ADULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Young Adults are patients for whom fertility preservation resources are provided by NCCN."&lt;SEP&gt;"Young adults are a demographic for whom the HPV vaccine is routinely recommended, as they are likely unexposed to HPV."&lt;SEP&gt;"Young adults are a patient group covered in the ALL treatment guidelines, as ALL can occur in this age group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Young adults are another group that can be diagnosed with ALL, and treatment approaches may differ based on age."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NASOPHARYNX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The nasopharynx is a small, tube-shaped structure above the soft palate that connects the nasal cavity to the oropharynx. It is part of the pharynx and is the site where nasopharyngeal carcinoma develops."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nasopharynx is one of the three parts of the pharynx, located behind the nose."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nasopharynx is the anatomical location where nasopharyngeal carcinoma starts, and it is part of the pharynx, with cancer potentially spreading to nearby areas like the nasal cavity and base of the skull."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nasopharynx is the anatomical region that connects the nasal cavity to the pharynx, and it is the site where NPC develops."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nasopharynx is the upper part of the pharynx, located behind the nasal cavity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nasopharynx is the upper part of the throat behind the nose, where nasopharyngeal carcinoma originates. It is a specific anatomical location in the head and neck region."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nasopharynx is the upper part of the throat near the nasal cavity, a site for head and neck cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL EXCISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure for removing perianal cancer, considered only for low-grade (G1) and intermediate-grade (G2) cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local excision is a surgical option for some slow-growing stage I and II perianal cancers, as an alternative to chemoradiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local excision is a surgical procedure that removes only the tumor and a small area of surrounding tissue, recommended for some early-stage, low-risk perianal cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local excision is a surgical procedure to remove rectal tumors, with outcomes sometimes requiring additional treatment based on high-risk features or tumor invasion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECOND OPINION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A consultation with another medical professional, facilitated by organized medical records."&lt;SEP&gt;"A process where a patient seeks an additional medical opinion from another doctor, facilitated by having organized medical records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Getting a second opinion on treatment may help patients decide which treatment to receive for pancreatic cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Opinion is a consultation with another doctor to confirm a diagnosis or treatment plan, facilitated by a medical binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Opinion is a consultation with another doctor to confirm a diagnosis or treatment plan, often sought by patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second opinion is a consultation with another doctor to confirm or refine a cancer diagnosis or treatment plan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second opinion is a medical consultation that may be facilitated by having a medical binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second opinion is a medical consultation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second opinion is a process where a patient consults another doctor to confirm a diagnosis or treatment plan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second opinion is a process where another doctor reviews test results and suggests a treatment plan, a normal part of cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL DIVISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell division is the process where cells replicate, and errors can lead to somatic mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND PROTEOMICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proteomics studies proteins in cervical cancer to identify biomarkers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MELANOMA SKIN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Melanoma skin cancer is a type of cancer that can be associated with BRCA mutations, increasing risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BODY FEATURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Body features, such as hair growth and body shape, are influenced by hormones like DHEA from the adrenal cortex."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUSAN G. KOMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Susan G. Komen is an organization dedicated to fighting breast cancer through research, advocacy, and patient support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VERTEBRA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vertebra are the bones of the spine, with specific staging for tumors based on the number of affected vertebrae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOWEL AND BLADDER CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bowel and bladder changes are common late side effects of anal cancer treatment, including incontinence and urgency, managed with diet and medication."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLON AND RECTUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The parts of the body where polyps form in FAP and where colorectal cancer can occur."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SALIVA SAMPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A saliva sample is a specimen of saliva taken from a patient, used for germline testing to detect inherited mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAPHRAGM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The diaphragm is a muscle located just above the esophagogastric junction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The diaphragm is a thin muscle below the lungs and heart that separates the chest from the abdomen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BCR::ABL1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BCR::ABL1 is a fused abnormal gene created by the translocation of chromosome 9 and chromosome 22, leading to uncontrolled blood cell growth and chronic myeloid leukemia (CML). It is not found in normal blood cells and is not inherited."&lt;SEP&gt;"BCR::ABL1 is a fused abnormal gene formed from parts of chromosomes 9 and 22, which produces a protein causing uncontrolled blood cell growth in CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"BCR::ABL1 is a fused gene created when pieces of chromosome 9 and chromosome 22 trade places, resulting in the Philadelphia chromosome and causing chronic myeloid leukemia."&lt;SEP&gt;"BCR::ABL1 is a fused gene created when pieces of chromosomes 9 and 22 trade places, causing CML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN.ORG/PATIENTS/FEEDBACK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN.org/patients/feedback is a survey link for patients to provide feedback on cancer information provided by NCCN."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patients/feedback is a web resource where patients can provide feedback on cancer information provided by NCCN."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patients/feedback is a website for patient feedback on cancer information, aiming to improve educational materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patients/feedback is a website where patients can provide feedback on cancer information, indicating it is part of the National Comprehensive Cancer Network's patient resources."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL MARGIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgical margin is the normal tissue surrounding a removed lesion; a margin of at least 1 cm without cancer cells is required for successful local excision."&lt;SEP&gt;"The normal tissue surrounding a lesion removed during surgery; a margin of at least 1 cm without cancer cells indicates no further treatment needed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PD-L1 EXPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PD-L1 expression is protein presence on cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"PD-L1 expression refers to the presence of PD-L1 protein on cancer cells, measured by CPS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) is an organization that provides guidelines for cancer care, including the NCCN Guidelines for Patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"National Comprehensive Cancer Network provides clinical guidelines for cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND METABOLOMICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolomics studies metabolic changes in cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR DNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor DNA is the genetic material in cancer cells, analyzed in tumor mutation testing and NGS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRESS RESPONSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stress response is the body's reaction to stress, controlled by hormones from the adrenal medulla."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UROLOGIC ONCOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgeon who diagnoses and treats cancers of the urinary tract and male reproductive organs using surgery and intravesical therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHILADELPHIA (PH) CHROMOSOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Philadelphia (Ph) chromosome is a shortened chromosome 22 that results from the translocation of genetic material between chromosomes 9 and 22, leading to the BCR::ABL1 gene and CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Philadelphia chromosome is a shortened chromosome 22 resulting from the translocation with chromosome 9, containing the BCR::ABL1 fusion gene. It is the hallmark of CML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A diagnostic procedure where samples of cervical tissue are removed and tested for dysplasia and cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical biopsy is a medical procedure involving the removal of small tissue samples from the cervix to diagnose cervical cancer, commonly used and examined by a pathologist."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical biopsy is a procedure to remove small tissue samples from the cervix to diagnose cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The muscle layer (muscularis propria) is soft tissue that helps move food through the stomach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NASOPHARYNGEAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nasopharyngeal cancer is a type of head and neck cancer that can affect the eyes and hearing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nasopharyngeal cancer is a type of head and neck cancer, often EBV-related, and is the focus of the text's staging and treatment discussions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nasopharyngeal cancer is another term for nasopharyngeal carcinoma, a type of cancer that starts in the nasopharynx, with staging described in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MITOMYCIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemotherapy drug used in combination with other agents for perianal cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mitomycin is a chemotherapy drug used in combination with other agents (capecitabine or 5-FU) for treating anal cancer, administered intravenously."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mitomycin is a chemotherapy drug used in combination with radiation to treat anal cancer, often paired with capecitabine or 5-FU."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mitomycin is a chemotherapy drug used in regimens like mitomycin and capecitabine or 5-FU and mitomycin for recurrent anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CPS (combined positive score) is a metric used to quantify PD-L1 expression."&lt;SEP&gt;"CPS is a score for PD-L1."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTING FOR AML&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Testing for AML involves various tests such as blood tests, bone marrow tests, and biomarker testing to diagnose and treat AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND MICROBIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The microbiome may influence cervical cancer risk and progression."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INHERITED MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inherited mutations are gene changes passed from biological parents, increasing cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIGHT OR FLIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fight or flight is a physiological response to stress, triggered by adrenaline from the adrenal medulla."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT PLANNING SESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment Planning Session is a meeting where doctors discuss and decide the best treatment approach for the patient."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHROMOSOME 9&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chromosome 9 is a human chromosome where the gene for p16 is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosome 9 is a normal human chromosome that, when broken and exchanged with chromosome 22, contributes to the formation of the BCR::ABL1 gene and Philadelphia chromosome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosome 9 is a part of the genetic material that breaks off and switches with chromosome 22, contributing to the formation of the Philadelphia chromosome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosome 9 is a piece of genetic material that can break off and trade places with chromosome 22, leading to CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosome 9 is a piece of genetic material that, when broken and traded with chromosome 22, contributes to the formation of the BCR::ABL1 gene and Philadelphia chromosome in CML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONE BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A diagnostic procedure to remove a cone-shaped piece of tissue from the cervix to examine for cancer or pre-cancer, used to determine staging and treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"A procedure that removes a cone-shaped portion of the cervix, used for gathering more information after a cervical biopsy or treating early cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cone biopsy is a surgical procedure to remove a cone-shaped piece of tissue from the cervix for diagnosis or treatment of early-stage cervical cancer. It can be used for stage 1A1 and select 1A2/1B1 cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cone biopsy, also known as cervical conization, is a procedure that removes a cone-shaped portion of the cervix, used both as a diagnostic test and a treatment for early cervical cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL TYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intestinal type adenocarcinoma is a subtype where cells stick together and form tube- and gland-shaped structures, more likely to have targetable mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR (T)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor (T) is a component of TNM staging that describes the size and extent of the primary cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor (T) is a component of the TNM staging system for breast cancer, describing the size and extent of the primary tumor, measured in centimeters or millimeters, with categories from T1 to T4 and special designations like T1mi and T4d."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor (T) is a component of the TNM system that describes the size and extent of the primary tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;5-FU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"5-FU (fluorouracil) is a chemotherapy agent used in chemoradiation for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"5-FU (fluorouracil) is a chemotherapy drug given by continuous intravenous infusion over several days, used in regimens with mitomycin or cisplatin for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"5-FU (fluorouracil) is a chemotherapy drug used in various regimens for anal cancer, including with cisplatin, mitomycin, leucovorin, or capecitabine."&lt;SEP&gt;"5-FU (fluorouracil) is a chemotherapy drug used with radiation for anal cancer, often combined with mitomycin or cisplatin."&lt;SEP&gt;"5-FU is an abbreviation for 5-fluorouracil, a chemotherapy cream applied directly to the skin for treating early CSCC and actinic keratoses."&lt;SEP&gt;"A chemotherapy drug used in combination with Mitomycin or cisplatin for perianal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P16&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"p16 is a protein marker used in HPV testing for throat cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"p16 is a protein marker used in HPV testing to determine the presence of HPV in throat cancer, influencing staging and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"p16 is a protein marker."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT FOR AML&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment for AML includes various types of therapies, discussed in the book, including treatment for subtypes like APL and BPDCN."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND EPIGENETICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Epigenetics studies gene expression changes in cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HALF-SIBLINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Half-siblings are blood relatives who share one biological parent, relevant for family health history."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRENALINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adrenaline is another name for epinephrine, a hormone produced by the adrenal medulla."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE 3 GLIOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade 3 gliomas are high-grade tumors with abnormal cells that grow quickly and invade nearby tissue, requiring additional therapy like radiation and chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIPPLE-AREOLA COMPLEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nipple-areola complex refers to the combined anatomical parts of the nipple and areola."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPORT GENERATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Report Generation is the creation of diagnostic reports by radiologists."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHROMOSOME 22&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chromosome 22 is a chromosome that contains the EWSR1 gene, involved in translocations with chromosome 11."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosome 22 is a normal human chromosome that, when broken and exchanged with chromosome 9, results in the Philadelphia chromosome and BCR::ABL1 gene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosome 22 is a part of the genetic material that breaks off and switches with chromosome 9, resulting in the abnormal Philadelphia chromosome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosome 22 is a piece of genetic material that can break off and trade places with chromosome 9, leading to CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosome 22 is a piece of genetic material that, when broken and traded with chromosome 9, contributes to the formation of the BCR::ABL1 gene and Philadelphia chromosome in CML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLD KNIFE CONIZATION (CKC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cold knife conization is a technique used in cone biopsy where a surgical scalpel removes cervical tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFUSE TYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diffuse type adenocarcinoma is a subtype where cells don't stick together and appear scattered, less common."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NODE (N)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Node (N) is a component of the TNM system that describes whether cancer has spread to nearby lymph nodes and how many are affected."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL CANAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer affecting the anal canal, with treatment similar to perianal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal canal cancer refers to cancer that starts in the anal canal, with stages I-III being non-metastatic and treated primarily with chemoradiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHROMOSOMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chromosomes are structures carrying genetic information; abnormalities can be present in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosomes are structures containing DNA, and abnormalities in them are detected through karyotype and FISH testing in leukemia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosomes are structures containing DNA, with 23 pairs in normal human cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosomes are structures in cells that carry DNA, and translocations between them can lead to gene fusions in cancers like Ewing sarcoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosomes are structures in cells that contain genetic material, and defects in them are detected via karyotype or FISH tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosomes are structures in human cells that carry genetic information, including the p16 gene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosomes are structures within human cells that carry genetic information; a karyotype visualizes them to detect abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chromosomes contain DNA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"APL (Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia) is a rare subtype of AML characterized by the abnormal fusion gene PML::RARA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER AND TUMOR MICROENVIRONMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The tumor microenvironment affects cervical cancer growth and treatment response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUNTS AND UNCLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aunts and uncles are blood relatives whose health history can inform cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3A1 (II)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3A1 (ii) is a substage of Stage 3A1 where cancer in the lymph nodes is larger than 10 millimeters."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T cells, or T lymphocytes, are a type of lymphocyte that help kill tumor cells and control immune responses, and abnormal T cells can lead to cutaneous T-cell lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLAST PHASE CML (BP-CML)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blast phase CML (BP-CML) is an advanced form of chronic myeloid leukemia characterized by an increased amount of immature blood cells (blasts)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blast phase CML is an advanced form of CML that can cause increased lymphoid or myeloid progenitor cells, affecting treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blast phase CML is an advanced form of chronic myeloid leukemia where there is an increased amount of lymphoid or myeloid progenitor cells, affecting treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOOP ELECTROSURGICAL EXCISION PROCEDURE (LEEP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LEEP is a procedure that uses a wire loop heated by electric current to remove abnormal tissue from the cervix."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loop electrosurgical excision procedure is an alternative technique in cone biopsy using a thin loop of electrified wire to cut out cervical tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESOPHAGEAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Esophageal cancer is a disease where abnormal cells grow out of control in the layers of the esophagus inner lining."&lt;SEP&gt;"Esophageal cancer is a disease where cells in the epithelium of the esophagus grow out of control, with types including squamous cell carcinoma and adenocarcinoma, and can spread to other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Esophageal cancer is a type of cancer affecting the esophagus, which should not be confused with nasopharyngeal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Esophageal cancer is a type of cancer that can arise from tumors starting in the cardia of the stomach and crossing into the esophagogastric junction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Esophageal cancer is a type of cancer where p16 can be found."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTASIS (M)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastasis (M) is a component of the TNM staging system, indicating whether cancer has spread to distant parts of the body, with categories M0 (no distant metastasis) and M1 (distant metastasis present&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastasis (M) is a component of the TNM system that describes whether cancer has spread to distant organs or parts of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLOW-UP AND SURVEILLANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follow-up and surveillance is the next step after treatment, involving monitoring for cancer recurrence, referenced on page 23."&lt;SEP&gt;"Post-treatment monitoring to detect early signs of cancer recurrence, including physical exams and imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDORECTAL ULTRASOUND (EUS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endorectal ultrasound is an imaging test using sound waves to assess the extent of rectal cancer in the pelvis and may guide biopsies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERYTHROCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Erythrocytes (red blood cells) carry oxygen throughout the body. They are produced from blood stem cells and are often reduced in ALL due to crowding by lymphoblasts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erythrocytes are another name for red blood cells, which carry oxygen throughout the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erythrocytes, also known as red blood cells, are a type of blood cell that carry oxygen throughout the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A polyp is an overgrowth of cells on the inner lining of the colon wall, with types including adenomas, pedunculated, and sessile polyps, which can become cancerous."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIECES AND NEPHEWS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nieces and nephews are blood relatives whose health history can inform cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INCIDENTAL FINDING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Incidental finding refers to discovering adrenal tumors through imaging tests done for unrelated reasons."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST CANCER RESEARCH FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Breast Cancer Research Foundation is an organization that funds research to prevent and cure breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPENDICULAR SKELETON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Appendicular skeleton is composed of 126 bones of the upper limbs, lower limbs, shoulder girdle, and pelvic girdle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROIN DISSECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Groin dissection is a surgical procedure recommended if cancer returns to lymph nodes in the groin after initial radiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Groin dissection is a surgical procedure to remove lymph nodes in the groin area that contain cancer, often performed during APR or as a standalone surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOMETRIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer associated with Lynch syndrome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CML&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CML (Chronic Myeloid Leukemia) is a type of cancer characterized by the presence of the Philadelphia chromosome and the BCR::ABL1 gene, leading to uncontrolled blood cell growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chronic myeloid leukemia (CML) is a type of cancer caused by the BCR::ABL1 gene, leading to uncontrolled blood cell growth. It is diagnosed by the presence of the Philadelphia chromosome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOCERVICAL CURETTAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endocervical curettage is a procedure where a curette scrapes a tissue sample from the cervical canal, often performed after cone biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICAL STAGE (C)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical Stage (c) is the rating given before any treatment, based on physical exam, biopsy, and imaging tests, such as cN2 or cM."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clinical stage (c) is the rating given before any treatment, based on physical exam, biopsy, and imaging tests, with examples like cN2 or cM."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clinical stage (c) is the rating given before any treatment, written as cTNM, based on initial assessments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION (DRE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A physical exam procedure recommended 8 to 12 weeks after chemoradiation and periodically thereafter to check for cancer recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPERM BANKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sperm banking is a fertility preservation method that stores semen by freezing it in liquid nitrogen for later use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sperm banking is a method of preserving fertility by freezing semen in liquid nitrogen for later use."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEUKOCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leukocytes are another name for white blood cells, which fight infections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leukocytes, also known as white blood cells, are a type of blood cell that fight infections."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEDUNCULATED POLYP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pedunculated polyps are mushroom-shaped polyps that stick out from the colon wall, having a stalk and round top."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRANDCHILDREN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grandchildren are blood relatives whose health history can inform cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIGNS AND SYMPTOMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Signs and symptoms are indicators of a disease, such as those associated with adrenocortical carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVANCED PRACTICE PROVIDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Registered nurse practitioners and physician assistants who monitor health and provide care as part of the team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BURKITT LEUKEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Burkitt leukemia is a rare subtype of mature B-cell ALL, essentially the same as Burkitt lymphoma (a type of non-Hodgkin lymphoma), but treated differently from B-ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Burkitt leukemia is a rare subtype of mature B-cell ALL, essentially the same as Burkitt lymphoma but treated differently from B-ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Burkitt leukemia is a rare subtype of mature B-cell ALL, essentially the same as Burkitt lymphoma but treated differently."&lt;SEP&gt;"Burkitt leukemia, also known as mature B-cell ALL, is a rare subtype of B-ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH HISTORY AND PHYSICAL EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health history and physical exam are part of testing and staging for cervical cancer to create a treatment plan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health history and physical exam involve a doctor asking about past and current health, lifestyle, and performing a physical examination, including pelvic exams, to plan treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MY DAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"My dad is a person who was diagnosed with stomach cancer in 2013, given 6 months to live, but is now clinically cured after seeking expert help."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATHOLOGIC STAGE (P)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pathologic Stage (p) or surgical stage is determined by examining tissue removed during surgery, providing more specific and accurate details about the cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathologic stage (p) or surgical stage is determined by examining tissue removed during surgery, with examples like pN."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathologic stage (p) or surgical stage is determined by examining tissue removed during surgery, written as pTNM."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A procedure to examine the anal canal, recommended every 6 to 12 months for 3 years after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anoscopy is a diagnostic procedure recommended after anal cancer diagnosis to examine the anal canal and surrounding tissues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anoscopy is a procedure to examine the anus and lower rectum using a scope, recommended after treatment for lymph node recurrence to monitor for recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anoscopy is a surveillance procedure recommended every 6 to 12 months for 3 years after anal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVARIAN TISSUE BANKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ovarian tissue banking is a fertility preservation method involving the removal and freezing of ovarian tissue containing eggs for later use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovarian tissue banking is a fertility preservation method that removes and freezes part of an ovary containing eggs for later transplantation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovarian tissue banking is a fertility preservation method that removes and freezes part or all of an ovary containing eggs for later transplantation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THROMBOCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thrombocytes (platelets) help control bleeding. They are produced from blood stem cells and can be reduced in ALL due to crowding by lymphoblasts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thrombocytes are another name for platelets, which help control bleeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thrombocytes, also known as platelets, are a type of blood cell that help control bleeding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SESSILE POLYP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sessile polyps are flatter polyps without a stalk, located on the colon wall."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHECKPOINT INHIBITOR THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Checkpoint inhibitor therapy is a treatment that activates the immune system against cancer, used when PD-1/PD-L1 is expressed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHAT'S NEXT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"What's next is a section that guides patients on the next steps after testing and diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIATION THERAPY SESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiation Therapy Session is a scheduled appointment where the patient receives radiation treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CARE PHYSICIAN (PCP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A primary care physician (PCP) is a doctor who provides general healthcare and coordinates with specialists. They are encouraged to be kept informed of a patient's cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary care physician is a doctor who provides general health care and should be kept informed of changes in the care team and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary care physician is a doctor who provides general healthcare and coordinates with specialists. The text emphasizes keeping the PCP informed of treatment changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary care physician is a general practitioner who can be part of the cancer care team, helping manage overall health and communication."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary care physician is a healthcare provider who manages overall patient care. The text advises keeping the PCP informed of changes in the care team and treatment details."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Care Physician (PCP) is a health care provider who coordinates overall care, is kept informed of changes in the care team, and provides guidance on screening for transgender individuals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary care physician (PCP) is a doctor who should be updated regarding changes in a patient's cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary care physician (PCP) is a healthcare provider who should be updated on cancer treatment details and contacted for general care coordination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary care physician is a doctor who coordinates a patient's overall care and should be updated about cancer treatment changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary care physician is a healthcare provider who coordinates overall patient care and is kept informed of changes in the patient's health status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary care physicians are partners in patient care, kept informed of changes in the care team and involved in overall health management."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary care physician (PCP) is a healthcare provider who coordinates overall care and is kept informed of the patient's cancer treatment and changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary care physician is a doctor who coordinates overall health care and should be kept informed of changes in the patient's cancer care team and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary care physician is a doctor who provides general healthcare and should be updated on cancer treatment changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary care physician is a healthcare provider who coordinates overall patient care and is kept informed of changes in the patient's health status."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD CHEMISTRY PROFILE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood chemistry profile measures levels of chemicals affected by organs like kidneys and bones. Abnormal levels may signal organ dysfunction or cancer spread, and it provides nutrient information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood chemistry profile measures chemical levels in blood, indicating organ health, with abnormal levels possibly signaling organ dysfunction or cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPPORT COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A support community is a group of people providing emotional and practical help to those diagnosed with cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER DRUG THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Drug Therapy is a treatment that may be given before surgery, affecting staging notation with a 'y' prefix."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer drug therapy is a treatment given before surgery in some cases, which may affect the staging notation with a 'y' prefix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERSISTENT DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A state where cancer remains in the body but has not grown or spread after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREMATURE OVARIAN INSUFFICIENCY (POI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Premature ovarian insufficiency is a condition caused by radiation damage to ovaries, leading to early menopause and reduced fertility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic mutations are changes in DNA that can promote cancer, such as gene fusions in translocation RCC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic mutations are changes in genes or chromosomes that can be present in leukemia cells, used to classify ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic mutations are changes in genes that can indicate how aggressive AML might be."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOWEL BLOCKAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bowel blockage is a condition where a tumor grows large enough to block the flow of stool, requiring various treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPSY TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biopsy tissue is a sample used for tumor marker testing and biomarker analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRACTICES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Practices are the standard procedures used in cancer care, based on expert recommendations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE 4 GLIOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade 4 gliomas are high-grade tumors with very abnormal cells that grow and spread quickly, including glioblastomas, the most common type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST EXAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breast exams are clinical or self-examinations to check for lumps or changes in breast tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESULT REVIEW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Result Review is the process of discussing test results with the doctor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Testing encompasses various diagnostic procedures like blood tests, imaging, and biopsies, used to detect and characterize cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testing includes various medical procedures used to diagnose and stage cancer, such as biopsies and imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testing is a topic covered in Chapter 2, including biomarker and tumor mutation testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testing is the process of conducting medical examinations, including physical exams, imaging tests, and biopsies, to diagnose and plan treatment for breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testing is the process of diagnosing and treating CML and ALL, including blood tests, bone marrow tests, and genetic testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testing is the process used to diagnose and plan treatment for adrenal tumors, including general health tests, imaging tests, blood tests, genetic tests, and biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIVER FUNCTION TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liver function tests are blood tests assessing liver health, ordered during surveillance for recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liver function tests are blood tests that evaluate the health of the liver by measuring enzymes and proteins, relevant in ovarian cancer management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liver function tests measure chemicals made or processed by the liver. Abnormal levels may indicate liver damage or cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liver function tests measure enzymes processed by the liver to detect liver damage or cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHYME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chyme is the liquid mixture of food and digestive juices produced in the stomach. It is released into the small intestine for nutrient absorption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chyme is the semi-fluid mass of partly digested food that passes from the stomach to the small intestine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chyme is the semi-liquid mixture of partially digested food and gastric juices that moves from the stomach to the small intestine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NASAL CAVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The nasal cavity is an area near the nasopharynx where nasopharyngeal cancer can spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nasal cavity is the space behind the nose, and it is a location where head and neck cancers can occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nasal cavity is the space inside the nose, and tumor growth into this area is considered in T1 staging of nasopharyngeal carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nasal cavity is the space inside the nose, lying above the hard palate and curving down at the back to join the throat. It connects to the nasopharynx."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGRESSIVE DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A state where cancer has grown or spread after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVORSHIP CHAPTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Survivorship chapter is a section of a guide that provides information on managing side effects like fertility issues after cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH ORGANIZATION CLASSIFICATION (WHO5)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health Organization classification (WHO5) is a classification system used to categorize follicular lymphoma subtypes, including classic FL and follicular large B cell lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stent is a mesh metal tube placed to keep the colon open, allowing gas and stool to pass, used in rare cases of bowel blockage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Probes are special dyes used in FISH that attach to pieces of DNA to detect known genetic changes in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Probes are special dyes used in FISH to attach to DNA pieces."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASHINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Washings are fluid samples taken from the abdominal cavity during surgery to check for cancer cells in ovarian cancer staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CUTANEOUS MARGINAL ZONE LYMPHOMA (PCMZL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary cutaneous marginal zone lymphoma (PCMZL) is a type of cutaneous B-cell lymphoma that is indolent or slow-growing, also called PCMZ lymphoproliferative disorder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TELEHEALTH VISITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Telehealth visits are remote medical appointments that can be used for consultations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Telehealth visits are remote medical consultations conducted over the phone or video, allowing patients to receive care without being physically present."&lt;SEP&gt;"Telehealth visits are remote medical consultations via phone or video, used for cancer care appointments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIV TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HIV test is a blood test recommended to detect human immunodeficiency virus, with positive results leading to referral to an HIV specialist."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOODSTREAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bloodstream is the circulatory system through which chemotherapy drugs travel to treat cancer throughout the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bloodstream is the circulatory system through which systemic therapy medicines travel to reach cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bloodstream is the system of blood vessels through which blood cells are released from the bone marrow into circulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bloodstream is the system through which contrast agents and tracers are injected to circulate throughout the body for imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bloodstream is where calcium is released during bone breakdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bloodstream is the system of blood vessels that carries nutrients and oxygen throughout the body. Nutrients are absorbed into the bloodstream in the small intestine."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bloodstream is the system of blood vessels that carries oxygen, nutrients, and cancer cells throughout the body. Cancer cells can spread via the bloodstream."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bloodstream is the system of blood vessels through which nutrients absorbed from the small intestine are transported."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bloodstream is the system that carries hormones from their production site to target organs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bloodstream is the system through which chemotherapy medicines travel to reach cancer cells throughout the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPOPHARYNX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hypopharynx is the area behind the voice box, examined during laryngoscopy to look for tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hypopharynx is a part of the throat near the nasopharynx where nasopharyngeal cancer can spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hypopharynx is one of the three parts of the pharynx, located in the lower part of the throat behind the larynx."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hypopharynx is the lower part of the pharynx near the larynx. It is one of the three parts of the pharynx and can be a site for head and neck cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hypopharynx is the lower part of the pharynx, located behind the larynx."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hypopharynx is the lower part of the throat near the voice box, a site for head and neck cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JANET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An anal cancer survivor who provides a supportive quote about the condition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENADRYL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benadryl is an antihistamine medication advised to reduce the risk of allergic reactions to contrast agents used in imaging tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL CONSENSUS CLASSIFICATION (ICC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"International Consensus classification (ICC) is a classification system that groups follicular lymphoma grades 1 and 2 as classic FL, and is the system followed in this text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN JOINT COMMITTEE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"American Joint Committee is an organization referenced in the text, likely involved in cancer staging guidelines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMICAL MARKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical marker is added in IHC to stain cells for microscopic study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRIANGLE-SHAPED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Triangle-shaped describes the physical form of the adrenal glands."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION (WHO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The WHO is an international organization that provides global health guidance, including cancer prevention and control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAITH-BASED ORGANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Faith-based organization is a religious group that offers spiritual and practical support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHOULDER GIRDLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shoulder girdle is a set of bones connecting the arm to the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FECAL URGENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fecal urgency is the urgent need to pass stool, a common bowel change after anal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVARIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer associated with Lynch syndrome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MYELOBLASTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Myeloblasts are immature blood cells formed from myeloid progenitor cells, often referred to as blasts in CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloblasts are immature cells formed from myeloid progenitor cells that mature into non-lymphoid blood cells such as granulocytes and monocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloblasts are immature cells formed from myeloid progenitor cells, which develop into non-lymphoid blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloblasts are immature cells that can develop into granulocytes or other non-lymphoid blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloblasts are immature myeloid cells that form from myeloid progenitor cells and are referred to as blasts in CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloblasts are immature white blood cells that accumulate in AML, with 20% or more presence indicating diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloblasts are immature white blood cells that can be overproduced in CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloblasts are immature white blood cells that mature into granulocytes (neutrophils). In AML, abnormal myeloblasts crowd out other blood cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymes are biological molecules that speed up chemical reactions, such as breaking down food in the stomach and small intestine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymes are proteins that speed up chemical reactions. The stomach secretes enzymes to aid in digestion, as described in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASE OF THE SKULL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Base of the skull is a location where chordomas are usually found."&lt;SEP&gt;"The base of the skull is an anatomical area near the nasopharynx where nasopharyngeal cancer can spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERIANAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer occurring in the perianal area, with treatment guidelines similar to anal canal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Perianal cancer is a type of cancer occurring in the perianal area, with stages I-III being nonmetastatic, often treated with chemoradiation or local excision for early-stage cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Perianal cancer starts in the perianal region, which includes the anal opening and surrounding skin, and is treated similarly to anal canal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEROID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Steroid is a medication that may be given before imaging scans to lower the risk of allergic reactions to contrast."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR LYMPHOMA (FL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follicular lymphoma (FL) is a slow-growing (indolent) lymphoma that typically forms tumors in lymph nodes, with excess abnormal B lymphocytes forming clusters in germinal centers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUCUS GLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mucus glands are found in the submucosa layer of the colon wall, producing mucus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PCR PRODUCT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PCR product is the amplified DNA copies made by PCR, used for NGS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YELLOW GLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yellow glands is a descriptive term for the adrenal glands' appearance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BURKITT LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Burkitt lymphoma (BL) is a type of non-Hodgkin lymphoma with germinal centers that differ from those in follicular lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Burkitt lymphoma is a type of non-Hodgkin lymphoma that is essentially the same as Burkitt leukemia but treated differently."&lt;SEP&gt;"Burkitt lymphoma is a type of non-Hodgkin lymphoma that is essentially the same as Burkitt leukemia, a rare subtype of mature B-cell ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Burkitt lymphoma is a type of non-Hodgkin lymphoma that is essentially the same as mature B-cell ALL (Burkitt leukemia) but treated differently."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPUTED TOMOGRAPHY (CT) SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A procedure using a computer linked to an x-ray machine to create detailed 3-D pictures of tissues and organs from different angles, often with contrast dye."&lt;SEP&gt;"Computed tomography (CT) scan is an imaging test recommended to assess lymph node involvement in regional CSCC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Computed tomography scan is a detailed x-ray that creates 3-D images of the chest, abdomen, or pelvis, often using contrast for clarity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acid, specifically gastric acid, is secreted by the stomach to help break down food. It is part of the digestive process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acid, such as gastric acid, is produced in the stomach to help break down food."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jaw is a part of the body imaged in panoramic dental x-rays, including upper and lower jaw."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jaw is part of the head and neck area that can be affected by cancer treatment, requiring dental care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jaw is part of the head and neck area that can be affected by cancer treatment, requiring dental monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"Part of the head and neck that can be affected by cancer treatment, requiring dental monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"The jaw is an anatomical area near the nasopharynx where nasopharyngeal cancer can spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE I CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage of perianal cancer that is high-grade and fast-growing, requiring chemoradiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EGGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eggs are female reproductive cells that are frozen and stored during egg freezing for fertility preservation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLASSIC FL (CFL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Classic FL (cFL) is a subtype of follicular lymphoma, defined as grade 1 or 2 according to ICC, and is the most common form of FL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOWEL HABITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bowel habits refer to the pattern of stool elimination, which may change after colectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gene changes are mutations or alterations in DNA that NGS can identify."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Small is a descriptive term for the size of the adrenal glands."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMOTHERAPY SESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemotherapy Session is a scheduled appointment where the patient receives chemotherapy drugs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-HODGKIN LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL) is a cancer of lymphocytes that begins in the lymphatic system, encompassing various subtypes including follicular lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-Hodgkin lymphoma is a broad category of lymphoma that includes PMBL, which MGZL overlaps with."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-Hodgkin lymphoma is a group of blood cancers that includes Burkitt lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-Hodgkin lymphoma is a group of blood cancers that includes primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-Hodgkin lymphoma is a type of cancer that affects the lymphatic system. Burkitt lymphoma is a subtype of non-Hodgkin lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-Hodgkin lymphoma is a type of cancer that includes Burkitt lymphoma, which is related to Burkitt leukemia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-Hodgkin lymphoma is a type of cancer that includes Burkitt lymphoma, which is related to mature B-cell ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PET/CT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PET/CT combines CT with positron emission tomography, using radiotracers to highlight cancer cells that use sugar more quickly."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET/CT is an advanced imaging test that may be used to detect CSCC spread beyond lymph nodes or to plan treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mucus is a sticky, thick liquid produced by the stomach epithelium that protects the stomach lining."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROOF OF THE MOUTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The roof of the mouth is an anatomical area near the nasopharynx where nasopharyngeal cancer can spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE II CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage of perianal cancer that may have invaded the sphincter, requiring chemoradiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVARIAN TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ovarian tissue contains eggs and is frozen during ovarian tissue banking for later transplantation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR LYMPHOMA GRADE 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follicular lymphoma grade 1 is a subtype of FL classified as classic FL under both WHO5 and ICC systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONE-STAGE COLECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"One-stage colectomy is a surgical option for bowel blockage that removes the cancer and unblocks the bowel in one procedure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-THROUGHPUT METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-throughput method is a technique like NGS that analyzes many DNA sequences quickly."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOP OF EACH KIDNEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Top of each kidney is the anatomical location of the adrenal glands."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TARGETED TREATMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Targeted treatments are therapies designed for specific genetic mutations in gliomas, currently limited but under research."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSGENDER INDIVIDUALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transgender individuals are people whose gender identity differs from sex assigned at birth, for whom screening guidance is not provided due to lack of evidence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PORTAL ACCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Portal Access is logging into online patient portals to view records."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAREGIVERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Caregivers are individuals who provide care to cancer patients, and advance care planning can lower their stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caregivers are individuals who provide support to anal cancer patients, often benefiting from peer-to-peer programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caregivers are individuals who provide support to patients and should ask questions during appointments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caregivers are individuals who provide support to patients, and they should also ask questions during appointments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caregivers are individuals who provide support to patients, including asking questions and assisting with medical care coordination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caregivers provide physical, mental, and emotional support to glioma patients, assisting with appointments and treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Individuals who provide care to cancer patients and may also experience distress, depression, and anxiety."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVIX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervix is part of the female reproductive system, included in the context of ovarian cancer anatomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervix is the lower part of the uterus, examined during a pelvic exam and sampled in a Pap test."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervix is the lower part of the uterus, where cervical cancer originates and where dye is injected for sentinel node biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervix is the lower part of the uterus, where cervical cancer originates, and is the focus of biopsy procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervix is the lower part of the uterus, which is the primary site of cervical cancer and is examined through imaging tests like MRI and ultrasound."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cervix is an organ where HPV can infect and cause cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cervix is the lower part of the uterus connecting to the vagina, consisting of the ectocervix (outer part) and endocervix (canal)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cervix is the lower part of the uterus that connects to the vagina, playing a role in the female reproductive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cervix is the lower part of the uterus that connects to the vagina. Cervical cancer originates in this area."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cervix is the lower part of the uterus, removed in hysterectomy or trachelectomy for cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cervix is the lower part of the uterus, sometimes removed during a total hysterectomy for ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cervix is the lower part of the uterus, where cervical cancer originates and where brachytherapy instruments are placed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cervix is the lower part of the uterus, which is the site where cervical cancer originates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cervix is the lower part of the uterus. Cervical cancer screening involves scraping cells from the cervix to test for HPV and cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cervix is the narrow, lower end of the uterus that opens into the vagina. It is the site where cervical cancer develops and is composed of the ectocervix and endocervix."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lower part of the uterus that connects to the vagina, where cervical cancer originates and where surgical procedures are focused."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormones are chemical messengers produced by stomach glands that regulate digestive processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormones are chemical messengers produced by the kidneys to control blood pressure and stimulate red blood cell production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormones are chemical substances produced by the endocrine system that travel through the bloodstream to regulate bodily functions, such as metabolism, growth, and reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormones are chemical substances produced in one part of the body and carried through the bloodstream to help control how organs or cells work."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormones are produced by bones, among other functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormones are substances made by the kidneys, contributing to bodily functions, as mentioned in kidney function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONES AND MUSCLES BEHIND THE NASAL CAVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bones and muscles behind the nasal cavity are areas that can be involved in advanced nasopharyngeal cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE III CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage of perianal cancer that has spread to lymph nodes or nearby structures, requiring chemoradiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISMATCH REPAIR DEFICIENCY (DMMR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker indicating that the cancer has defects in DNA repair genes, guiding treatment and Lynch syndrome testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mismatch repair deficiency (dMMR) is a biomarker indicating a defect in DNA repair mechanisms, making the cancer eligible for immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mismatch repair deficiency is a biomarker in rectal tumors indicating a higher likelihood of Lynch syndrome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR LYMPHOMA GRADE 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follicular lymphoma grade 2 is a subtype of FL classified as classic FL under both WHO5 and ICC systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLECTOMY WITH COLOSTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colectomy with colostomy is a surgical option for bowel blockage where the colon is removed and a colostomy is created, often temporary."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAB PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lab process refers to procedures like PCR or IHC used in testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RETROPERITONEAL LYMPH NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Retroperitoneal lymph nodes are lymph nodes in the back of the abdomen, which are checked for cancer spread in ovarian cancer staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CUTANEOUS FOLLICLE CENTER LYMPHOMA (PCFCL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary cutaneous follicle center lymphoma (PCFCL) is a type of cutaneous B-cell lymphoma that is indolent or slow-growing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRIENDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Friends are individuals who can provide emotional support, transportation, and other assistance during cancer diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Friends are individuals who can provide support such as transportation, meals, and emotional support during FL treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Friends are individuals who can provide support, such as transportation or meals, during cancer diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Friends are individuals who may provide support and advice when considering clinical trial enrollment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Friends are individuals who provide social support, contributing to the patient's quality of life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Friends are part of a support system that can provide transportation, meals, and emotional support during diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Friends are part of a support system, providing transportation, meals, and emotional support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECTOCERVIX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ectocervix is the rounded, bottom part of the cervix from which tissue samples may be taken during a cervical biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ectocervix is the outer part of the cervix extending into the vagina, lined with squamous cells where most cervical cancers start."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ectocervix is the outer part of the cervix that extends into the vagina and is lined with squamous cells. It contains the external os and is visible during a speculum examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"The outer part of the cervix, which is included in tissue samples during a cone biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LESSER CURVATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The lesser curvature is the inner curve of the stomach where lymph nodes are found."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MODERATELY OR VERY ADVANCED DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moderately or Very Advanced Disease includes cancer spread to neck structures like bones, muscles, sinuses, or skin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moderately or very advanced disease includes cancer that has spread to parts of the neck such as the base of the skull, larynx, oropharynx, bones and muscles behind the nasal cavity, jaw, and roof of the mouth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPHINCTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The muscular structure around the anus that may be invaded by stage II perianal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH MICROSATELLITE INSTABILITY (MSI-H)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High microsatellite instability is a biomarker in rectal tumors associated with Lynch syndrome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR LYMPHOMA GRADE 3A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follicular lymphoma grade 3A is a subtype of FL that may be treated as classic FL or DLBCL depending on the cancer center and cell types found."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLOSTOMY FIRST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colostomy first is a surgical approach for bowel blockage where a colostomy is done initially, followed by a second surgery to remove the cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECIAL STAINING PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Special staining process is IHC, which uses chemical markers to visualize proteins."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONE OR BOTH ADRENAL GLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"One or both adrenal glands indicates that adrenal tumors can affect either one or both glands."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPSY NEEDLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biopsy needle is a tool used to extract tissue samples from the breast for diagnostic testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMPLOYER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Employer is an entity that may provide health insurance and workplace accommodations for patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC GIRDLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic girdle is a set of bones connecting the leg to the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLATULENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flatulence is increased gas, a common bowel change reported by anal cancer survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UPPER ENDOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Upper endoscopy is a procedure where a scope is guided down the throat to examine the esophagus, stomach, and small bowel. It is used to assess the upper GI tract."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peers are individuals in similar situations who can provide understanding and support based on shared experiences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peers are individuals who can offer support and understanding during cancer diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peers are individuals who can provide support during FL diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peers are individuals who can provide support during cancer diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peers are part of a support system, providing transportation, meals, and emotional support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOCERVICAL CANAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endocervical canal is the passage within the cervix from which tissue samples may be taken during a cervical biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREATER CURVATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The greater curvature is the outer curve of the stomach where lymph nodes are found."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTIMETERS (CM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Centimeters (cm) are units of measurement used to describe tumor size, with examples like a baseball (7 cm), golf ball (4 cm), and pea (1 cm)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INGUINAL LYMPH NODE EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surveillance procedure recommended every 3 to 6 months for 5 years after treatment to check for cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISMATCH REPAIR PROFICIENT (PMMR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker indicating that the cancer has functional DNA repair, opposite of dMMR."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mismatch repair proficient is a biomarker status in rectal tumors indicating no deficiency in mismatch repair."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR LYMPHOMA GRADE 3B (FL3B)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follicular lymphoma grade 3B (FL3B) is a rare subtype of FL, also called follicular large B cell lymphoma in WHO5, and is treated as DLBCL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STENT PLACEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stent placement is a procedure where a mesh metal tube is inserted to keep the colon open, used in rare cases of bowel blockage before cancer removal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUORESCENT PROBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fluorescent probes are dyes used in FISH to bind DNA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;300 TO 500 PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"300 to 500 people is the annual number of diagnoses for malignant adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOCTOR VISITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Doctor visits are appointments where patients discuss care, and bringing someone can be beneficial."&lt;SEP&gt;"Doctor visits are appointments where patients discuss diagnosis and treatment, often with support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Doctor visits are appointments with health care providers where patients discuss symptoms, test results, and treatment plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Doctor visits are appointments with healthcare providers where patients can discuss their condition, receive tests, and get treatment recommendations. It is suggested to bring someone along or have someone on the phone for support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Doctor visits are appointments with healthcare providers where patients discuss symptoms, test results, and treatment plans, often involving note-taking and questions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSFORMATION ZONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The transformation zone is the area on the cervix where most cervical cancers and pre-cancers originate."&lt;SEP&gt;"The transformation zone, also known as the squamo-columnar junction, is the area where the endocervix and ectocervix meet, and is the most common site for cervical cancer origin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transformation zone is the area where the ectocervix and endocervix meet, where most cervical cancers start, and is removed during cone biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURFACE EPITHELIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The surface epithelium is a thin, moist layer of cells forming the interior stomach lining and producing mucus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T0 is a TNM score indicating no tumor is found, but neck lymph nodes test positive for Epstein-Barr virus."&lt;SEP&gt;"T0 is a TNM staging category indicating no tumor is found in the nasopharynx, but neck lymph nodes test positive for Epstein-Barr virus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT OF THE CHEST, ABDOMEN, AND PELVIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An imaging test recommended annually for 3 years for stage II and III anal cancers in complete remission."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COIL DEVICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coil device is a light equipment placed on the patient during MRI to send and receive radio waves."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR LARGE B CELL LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follicular large B cell lymphoma is an alternative name for FL3B in WHO5, treated as DLBCL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPEN METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Open method is a surgical technique for colectomy involving a large cut in the abdomen to remove tumor tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC MATERIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic material is DNA in cells, analyzed in FISH and other tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic material refers to DNA and chromosomes, and changes in it are detected via biomarker tests like FISH and DNA sequencing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1 TO 2 PEOPLE OUT OF EVERY 1 MILLION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1 to 2 people out of every 1 million is the incidence rate for adrenocortical carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FELLOW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A doctor who has completed residency and is undergoing further specialized training."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGERY APPOINTMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgery Appointment is a scheduled time for the patient to undergo a surgical procedure like APR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPOINTMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Appointments are medical visits where a medical binder may be brought for reference."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appointments are medical visits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appointments are scheduled meetings with health care providers for consultations, tests, or treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appointments are scheduled meetings with healthcare providers where patients can ask questions and take notes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appointments are scheduled meetings with healthcare providers, which may be coordinated together for convenience."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appointments are scheduled visits with healthcare providers, where a medical binder is brought for reference."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appointments are scheduled visits with healthcare providers, where medical binders are brought for discussion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scheduled meetings with healthcare providers, during which the medical binder should be brought for reference."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAMINA PROPRIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lamina propria is a thin layer of connective tissue under the epithelium in the esophagus mucosa."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lamina propria is a type of connective tissue found under the epithelium in the bile ducts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lamina propria is a connective tissue layer under the epithelium, containing stomach glands."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lamina propria is the bottom layer of connective tissue in the oral mucosa, through which tumors can grow."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS: COLORECTAL CANCER SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A set of patient guidelines for colorectal cancer screening, available at NCCN.org and on the NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer app, providing information on prevention and diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Colorectal Cancer Screening is a resource providing information on finding polyps early, available at NCCN.org and on the NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer app."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRI OF THE ABDOMEN AND PELVIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An imaging test alternative to CT for surveillance of stage II and III anal cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Treatment encompasses all therapies, including chemotherapy, that can affect fertility and require monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer Treatment encompasses various modalities, including surgery, radiation, chemotherapy, and targeted therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer treatment encompasses various medical procedures and therapies aimed at combating cancer, including imaging tests, surgeries, and other interventions, and can have side effects impacting fertility and overall health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer treatment includes therapies guided by biomarker testing, such as checkpoint inhibitors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer treatment includes therapies like chemotherapy and radiation that can impair fertility and affect pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer treatment includes therapies that can affect ovaries, damage sperm, and cause bone damage, requiring careful planning regarding pregnancy and monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer treatment is based on the tumor location and involves planning based on test results, including imaging, biopsy, and biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer treatment refers to the medical interventions used to manage cancer, based on tumor location and cancer stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer treatment refers to therapies such as chemotherapy or radiation that may cause bone damage, which can be detected through imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical interventions, including surgery, chemotherapy, and imaging, used to manage colon cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNCOMMON FL (UFL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Uncommon FL (uFL) is a subtype of FL with uncommon pathologic features or t(14;18)-negative status, treated as classic FL in this book."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINIMALLY INVASIVE METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Minimally invasive method is a surgical technique for colectomy involving a few small cuts and tools to see and remove part of the colon."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNE RESPONSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immune response is the body's defense against cancer, suppressed by PD-1/PD-L1."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHILDREN AGES 5 AND UNDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Children ages 5 and under are the population affected by neuroblastoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THOSE ASSIGNED MALE AT BIRTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Those assigned male at birth are individuals who do not undergo regular mammogram screening but should seek care if symptoms arise."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD DOWNLOAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Record Download is saving records from the portal to a device."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMERGENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An emergency is a situation requiring immediate medical attention, and it is important to know how to communicate with the care team in such cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency is a situation where patients need to know how to communicate with their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency refers to urgent medical situations where immediate communication with the care team is necessary, and patients should know the proper channels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency refers to urgent situations where access to contact information for the care team is critical for immediate medical assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency refers to urgent situations where patients need to know how to communicate with their care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSCULARIS MUCOSAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The muscularis mucosae is a thin strip of muscle separating the mucosa from the submucosa."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISMATCH REPAIR (MMR) GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genes that fix damaged DNA; mutations in these genes are tested in colon cancer to determine mismatch repair status, which guides treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mismatch repair (MMR) genes are genes that fix damaged DNA; mutations in these genes can lead to rectal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition where cancer has spread to areas far from the pelvis, requiring different treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic Disease is cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, including lung and distant lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BARRIER METHODS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Barrier Methods include condoms, diaphragms, cervical caps, and contraceptive sponges used to prevent pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Barrier methods are types of birth control that include condoms, diaphragms, cervical caps, and the contraceptive sponge, used to prevent pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Barrier methods include condoms, diaphragms, cervical caps, and contraceptive sponges, used to prevent pregnancy during treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Barrier methods include condoms, diaphragms, cervical caps, and contraceptive sponges, used to prevent pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contraceptive methods such as condoms, diaphragms, cervical caps, and contraceptive sponges used to prevent pregnancy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEDIATRIC-TYPE FL (PTFL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pediatric-type FL (PTFL) is a subtype of FL that usually occurs in children but can occur in adults, often with only one enlarged lymph node in the head and neck region."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gas is a substance that passes through the colon, which can be blocked by tumors and relieved by stents."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEREDITARY CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hereditary cancer is cancer caused by inherited mutations, about 1 in 10 breast cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hereditary cancer refers to cancers caused by inherited genetic mutations, such as those in BRCA genes. The text discusses testing for these mutations to guide treatment and risk assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALIGNANT PLEURAL EFFUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Malignant pleural effusion is the presence of cancer cells in the fluid around the lungs, a characteristic of Stage 4A ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CUTANEOUS DIFFUSE LARGE B-CELL LYMPHOMA, LEG TYPE (PC-DLBCL, LEG TYPE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary cutaneous diffuse large B-cell lymphoma, leg type (PC-DLBCL, leg type) is a type of cutaneous B-cell lymphoma, with treatment options found in NCCN Guidelines for Patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT RECORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment Records are documents detailing therapies received, included in a medical binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEGAL AID SERVICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Legal aid service is an organization that helps patients with insurance or employment legal issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINE NEEDLE ASPIRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fine needle aspiration is a biopsy technique using a thin needle to extract cells from a suspicious area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TECHNICIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A professional who operates imaging equipment and communicates with patients during scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"A technician is a healthcare professional who operates imaging equipment during CT or MRI scans. They are present outside the room during the scan to ensure patient safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technician is a healthcare professional who operates imaging equipment and communicates with patients during scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technician is a professional who operates imaging machines like CT scans, communicating with the patient during the procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technician operates the radiation machine from an adjacent room and communicates with the patient during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSCULARIS PROPRIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muscularis propria is a layer of the esophagus wall, part of the four main layers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Muscularis propria is a thick muscle layer in the esophagus that contracts to push food down via peristalsis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Muscularis propria is the third layer of the colon wall, consisting of muscle tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"The muscularis propria is the muscle layer of the stomach wall that helps move food."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CML SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A CML specialist is a doctor with expertise in chronic myeloid leukemia, whose opinion is recommended for best care."&lt;SEP&gt;"A CML specialist is a healthcare professional with expertise in treating chronic myeloid leukemia, whose opinion is recommended for best care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DMMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker indicating mismatch repair deficiency in colon cancer, guiding treatment and Lynch syndrome testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"dMMR (mismatch repair deficient) is an abnormal result in MMR testing, indicating a lack of DNA repair function in the tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCALLY PROGRESSIVE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition where cancer is limited to the anal area but has progressed, treated similarly to recurrent non-metastatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONDOMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A barrier method of contraception recommended to prevent pregnancy during and after cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condoms are a barrier method of birth control used to prevent pregnancy and protect against infections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condoms are a barrier method of contraception recommended to prevent pregnancy during and after cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condoms are a type of barrier method used to prevent pregnancy and may be recommended during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condoms are a type of barrier method used to prevent pregnancy during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSFORMED FL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transformed FL is a subtype of FL that has transformed into a more aggressive lymphoma, typically DLBCL, and can occur before, during, or after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bag is a medical device attached to the skin around a stoma to collect stool."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GERMLINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Germline refers to inherited mutations present in all cells, tested via blood or saliva."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNCTIONAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Functional describes tumors that produce hormones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATERY STOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Watery stool is a common bowel change after anal cancer treatment, managed with anti-diarrheal medication."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CA-125 TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CA-125 is a tumor marker test measuring protein levels in blood. High levels may suggest ovarian cancer, but it cannot diagnose alone due to other conditions affecting levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHANGE IN TASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Change in taste is a possible side effect of RAI therapy, altering sensory perception."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYMPTOMS OF CLL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Symptoms of CLL include swollen glands, fatigue, night sweats, fever, infections, loss of appetite, and weight loss."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIV SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HIV specialist is a doctor who manages HIV care, to whom patients with HIV are referred."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEROUS MEMBRANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The serous membrane, also called serosa, is the outer membrane covering the stomach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Guide is a reference document for possible tests and procedures in kidney cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guide is a reference document that provides information about possible tests and procedures for cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guide is a reference for other systemic therapies available."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guide refers to a document or resource that provides information on follow-up exam schedules for skin cancer and CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guide refers to the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, which is organized into chapters on testing and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guide refers to the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, which serves as a resource for understanding cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Guide is a reference document that provides information about possible tests and procedures related to ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MSI-H&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker indicating microsatellite instability-high in colon cancer, similar to dMMR."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSI-H (microsatellite instability-high) is a specific type of MSI with more microsatellites than normal."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSI-H (microsatellite instability-high) is an abnormal result in MMR testing, indicating high instability in microsatellite regions of DNA."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSI-H is high microsatellite instability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECURRENT NON-METASTATIC ANAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer that returns but has not spread to distant areas, treated with surgery or other options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAPHRAGMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A barrier contraceptive device used to prevent pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diaphragms are a barrier method of birth control inserted into the vagina to prevent pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diaphragms are a barrier method of contraception mentioned as an option."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diaphragms are a type of barrier method used to prevent pregnancy and may be recommended during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diaphragms are a type of barrier method used to prevent pregnancy during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BCL2 PROTEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BCL2 protein is a protein that is often present in excess levels in FL tumors, associated with chromosome translocations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REVERSAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reversal is an operation to reconnect the colon after a colostomy, often possible for colon cancer surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAMILY CANCER HEALTH HISTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Family cancer health history is a record of cancer in blood relatives, used for risk assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NONFUNCTIONING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nonfunctioning describes tumors that do not produce hormones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSYCHIATRIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical doctor specializing in mental health, able to prescribe medication for conditions like depression and anxiety."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HERBAL PREPARATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Herbal preparations are plant-based remedies used in complementary therapy for cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONE-RELATED SYMPTOMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormone-related symptoms are signs caused by excess hormone production from functional adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRE-TREATMENT CONSULTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pre-treatment Consultation is a meeting with healthcare providers to prepare for treatment, including discussing risks and logistics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CONIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical conization is another name for cone biopsy, involving removal of a cone-shaped portion of the cervix for diagnosis and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GASTROESOPHAGEAL JUNCTION (GEJ)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gastroesophageal junction is another name for the esophagogastric junction where the esophagus meets the stomach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chapter is a section of a book; the text references chapters on treatment options for prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chapter is a section of the book, such as Chapter 2, 3, or 4."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chapter refers to a section of a document explaining bladder cancer phases, stages, and treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chapter refers to sections of the NCCN Guidelines book, each ending with 'Questions to ask'."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker indicating microsatellite stability in colon cancer, meaning no dMMR or MSI-H."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSS (microsatellite stable) is a normal result in MMR testing, indicating stable microsatellite regions in the tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC EXENTERATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic exenteration is a radical surgical procedure that removes multiple organs from the pelvis, including the uterus, fallopian tubes, ovaries, vagina, and potentially the bladder, rectum, and/or anus, with the goal of curing cancer by removing all organs to which cancer has or may spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pelvic exenteration is a surgical procedure for local or regional recurrence of cervical cancer in the pelvis, involving removal of pelvic organs, often combined with radiation and systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CAPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A barrier contraceptive device placed over the cervix to prevent pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical Caps are a barrier method of birth control placed over the cervix to prevent pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical caps are a barrier method of contraception mentioned as an option."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical caps are a type of barrier method used to prevent pregnancy and may be recommended during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical caps are a type of barrier method used to prevent pregnancy during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T(14;18)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"t(14;18) is a specific chromosome translocation often found in FL; its absence may lead to classification as uncommon FL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMAGING (MRI OR CT SCAN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Imaging tests such as MRI or CT scans are used to detect tumors and confirm the presence of primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGE OF DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Age of diagnosis is the age at which a relative was diagnosed with cancer, important for risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAGNOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diagnose is the process of identifying a disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITION EVALUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutrition evaluation assesses dietary needs and swallowing function during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CURETTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Curette is a spoon-shaped tool used to scrape tissue samples from the cervical canal during endocervical curettage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRAFASCIAL (SIMPLE) HYSTERECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure for cervical cancer treatment involving removal of the uterus and cervix, typically recommended for early-stage cancers with low risk factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extrafascial (simple) hysterectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the uterus, typically recommended for stage 1A1 cervical cancer when fertility preservation is not desired."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOOK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Book is a guide for patients to find information for making decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Book refers to the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, organized into chapters on testing and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PMMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker indicating mismatch repair proficiency in colon cancer, meaning no dMMR."&lt;SEP&gt;"pMMR (mismatch repair proficient) is a normal result in MMR testing, indicating functional DNA repair in the tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAGINAL RECONSTRUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vaginal reconstruction is a surgical procedure to create an artificial vagina using muscle from another area of the body, often performed after pelvic exenteration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTRACEPTIVE SPONGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A barrier contraceptive device inserted into the vagina to prevent pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contraceptive Sponge is a barrier method of birth control inserted into the vagina to prevent pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contraceptive sponge is a type of barrier method used to prevent pregnancy and may be recommended during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The contraceptive sponge is a barrier method of contraception mentioned as an option."&lt;SEP&gt;"The contraceptive sponge is a type of barrier method used to prevent pregnancy during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-HODGKIN LYMPHOMA (NHL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL) is a cancer of lymphocytes, a type of white blood cell, that can develop when lymphocytes grow without proper regulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL) is a cancer that develops from lymphocytes, a type of white blood cell, and includes follicular lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NERVE CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nerve changes are specific neurological symptoms caused by a lymphoma located in the brain, including leg or arm weakness and coordination or movement problems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TYPE OF CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Type of cancer is the specific cancer a relative had, important for family history."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treat is the process of managing a disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD PRINTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Record Printing is creating physical copies of records for the binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THOSE ASSIGNED FEMALE AT BIRTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Those assigned female at birth are the primary population for breast cancer screening recommendations in this text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-GRADE SEROUS TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-grade serous tumors are a type of ovarian cancer tumor that require six cycles of chemotherapy, as specified in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUTANEOUS T-CELL LYMPHOMA (CTCL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cutaneous T-cell lymphoma (CTCL) is a type of primary cutaneous lymphoma that develops from abnormal T cells, with types including mycosis fungoides and Sézary syndrome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bones are a common area where metastatic bladder cancer can spread, causing pain and other complications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bones are a common site for distant metastasis of kidney cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bones are a common site for metastasis in advanced prostate cancer, where cancer cells can spread and cause symptoms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bones are a common site for metastatic prostate cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bones are a common site for metastatic thyroid cancer spread, requiring monitoring and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bones are distant organs that stage 4B bladder cancer may spread to."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bones are part of the body that affect blood chemistry levels, as mentioned in the context of blood chemistry profile."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bones are potential sites for cancer metastasis, and are evaluated using bone scans when symptoms suggest spread from bladder cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bones are the target of bone scans to detect cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bones are tissues that affect blood chemistry levels, assessed in a blood chemistry profile."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bones in the pelvis may be checked for cancer spread using MRI."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hard tissue that can be a site of prostate cancer metastasis, often causing pain or fractures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Structures that are potential sites of distant metastasis, but locally advanced cervical cancer has not spread to these structures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRACHYTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of internal radiation therapy where radioactive material is placed inside or near the tumor, used for cervical cancer treatment, often in combination with other therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of radiation therapy where a radiation source is placed close to or in direct contact with the tumor for a short period."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of radiation therapy where radioactive material is placed inside or near the tumor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brachytherapy is a form of internal radiation therapy where radioactive material is placed near the tumor, used for local recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brachytherapy is a radiation therapy method involving radioactive material placed inside the body to deliver a high dose directly to the tumor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brachytherapy is a type of internal radiation therapy where radioactive sources are placed inside or near the tumor, used as a treatment option for recurrent cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brachytherapy, also known as internal radiation therapy, involves placing radioactive material inside the body to target tumors, used for cervical cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT PLANNING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The process of creating a plan for colon cancer treatment based on testing results, including MMR status."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of determining the best course of medical action based on test results and cancer stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment Planning is the process of deciding on cancer therapies and considering fertility impacts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment planning is the process of deciding the best approach for bladder cancer based on stage and health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment planning is the process of determining the appropriate treatment approach based on diagnosis and testing results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment planning is the process of determining the appropriate treatment approach based on test results and diagnosis of adrenal tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment planning is the process of developing a personalized care strategy based on test results and cancer characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment planning is the process of using test results to guide cancer therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment planning is the process that starts with testing and uses results to determine the care approach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAMILIAL ADENOMATOUS POLYPOSIS (FAP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An inherited syndrome causing hundreds to thousands of polyps in the colon and rectum, which can become invasive cancer, often by age 50 in classic cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"An inherited syndrome causing many polyps."&lt;SEP&gt;"Familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP) is a rare inherited syndrome causing hundreds to thousands of polyps in the colon and rectum, which can become invasive cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Familial adenomatous polyposis is a hereditary syndrome associated with increased risk of thyroid cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inherited syndrome causing many polyps."&lt;SEP&gt;"Syndrome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ILEAL CONDUIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ileal conduit is a type of urinary diversion where a new tube is created from a piece of intestine to allow urine to exit the body through a stoma into an ostomy bag."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ileal conduit is a type of urinary diversion where a section of the small intestine is used as a tube, connected to a stoma on the abdominal wall, requiring an ostomy bag to collect urine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV-RELATED CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV-related cancer is a cancer caused by human papillomavirus, with throat cancer being most often related to HPV."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV-related cancer is cancer caused by HPV, such as squamous cell carcinomas of the throat."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B LYMPHOCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B lymphocytes (B cells) are a type of lymphocyte that make antibodies, which are proteins that help fight infection."&lt;SEP&gt;"B lymphocytes are a type of lymphocyte that, in FL, form abnormal clusters (follicles) in germinal centers of lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"B lymphocytes, or B cells, are a type of lymphocyte that produce antibodies to target infections or cancer cells and are involved in follicular lymphoma development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONFUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Confusion is a neurological symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, impacting cognitive function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAUSE OF DEATH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cause of death may be cancer, relevant for family history if relative died from it."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORIGINAL AREA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Original area is the site where cancer first appeared."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINANCIAL ASSISTANCE PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Financial assistance program is a service that helps patients cover medical costs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FISH is a lab test used to detect HER2 gene amplification in breast cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"FISH is a method using special dyes called probes that attach to DNA pieces to detect known changes too small for other methods, performed on bone marrow or blood samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) is a lab test that can show missing parts and extra copies of chromosomes, detecting biomarkers like 17p deletion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EBRT (EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of radiation therapy that delivers high-energy beams from outside the body to target cancer cells, used for cervical cancer treatment, often combined with chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONLINE PATIENT PORTALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Digital platforms where patients can view test results and other medical records, which can be downloaded or printed for a binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Online Patient Portals are digital systems to access records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Online patient portals are digital platforms for accessing test results and health information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Online patient portals are digital platforms where patients can access their test results and medical information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Online patient portals are secure websites that allow patients to view their medical records, including test results. They are recommended as a convenient way to access health information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Online patient portals are systems that allow patients to access test results and medical information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEA BLOOD TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A test measuring carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) levels in blood, which can be higher in people with colon cancer, especially if it has spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"CEA blood test measures carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) protein levels in blood, which can be elevated in colorectal cancer and may indicate spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTINENT URINARY DIVERSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Continent urinary diversion, also known as an artificial bladder or Indiana pouch, uses a segment of intestine to create a pouch to hold urine, drained via catheter without an external bag."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV TYPE 16&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV type 16 is a specific strain of HPV responsible for 9 out of 10 throat cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAD AND NECK REGION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Head and neck region is a location where PTFL often presents with an enlarged lymph node."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEMORY PROBLEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Memory problems are a long-term side effect of whole-brain radiation therapy, affecting cognition months or years after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Memory problems are a symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, affecting the ability to recall information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRONG FEELINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Strong feelings are normal emotional responses to a cancer diagnosis, addressed by distress screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONCERNING LESION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A concerning lesion is an abnormal skin area that may indicate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOMOGRAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nomograms are tools used in risk assessment for prostate cancer to predict outcomes based on clinical characteristics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTI-DIARRHEAL MEDICINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anti-diarrheal medicine helps control frequent and watery bowel movements by thickening stool."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABDOMINAL PAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abdominal pain is a symptom of ovarian cancer, impacting eating and overall health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWOLLEN GLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Swollen glands are a symptom of CLL, often in the neck or stomach area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MODIFIED RADICAL HYSTERECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure for cervical cancer that removes the uterus, cervix, and surrounding tissues, including part of the vagina and lymph nodes, used for certain stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of hysterectomy that removes the uterus, a portion of connective tissue, and about a half inch or less of the vagina."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV16&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV16 is a high-risk strain of HPV strongly linked to cervical cancer and other HPV-related cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV16 is a high-risk strain of HPV that is more likely to lead to anal cancer and other related cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV16 is a high-risk strain of human papillomavirus that is strongly linked to anal cancer and other related cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARCINOEMBRYONIC ANTIGEN (CEA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A protein in blood, often higher in colon cancer patients, used for monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"CEA is a tumor marker found in higher amounts in LCOCs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) is a protein found in blood, often elevated in people with colorectal cancer, used for monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) is a tumor marker protein that may be elevated in breast cancer, indicating possible progression."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOUBLE-BARRELED WET COLOSTOMY (DBWC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Double-barreled wet colostomy (DBWC) is a surgical technique that creates one stoma for both urine and stool, keeping them separate until exit, with benefits like fewer leaks compared to separate diversions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV33&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV33 is a strain of HPV that can cause throat cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROIN AREA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Groin area is a common location for swollen lymph nodes in FL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOSS OF BLADDER CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Loss of bladder control (incontinence) is a symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, affecting bodily functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMOTIONAL DISTRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emotional distress is a psychological response to cancer, screened for in distress screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL AND FAMILY HISTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medical and family history is information about a patient's health and relatives' health, used in diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIVER FUNCTION TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A test measuring enzymes like alkaline phosphatase and bilirubin to assess liver health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POST-TREATMENT CHECK-UP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Post-treatment Check-up is a follow-up visit to monitor recovery and detect any issues after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A body region included in imaging for surveillance of anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chest is a body part that may be scanned in CT or MRI to detect cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chest is a body region scanned via CT or MRI to check for ovarian cancer spread to the lungs or other areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chest is a body region scanned via CT to check for cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chest is a location where swollen lymph nodes can be found on imaging scans in FL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chest is the anatomical region containing the mediastinum, where mediastinal lymphomas develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chest is the body region scanned via CT to detect cancer spread to the lungs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chest is the part of the body containing the lungs, which is imaged by thoracic radiologists."&lt;SEP&gt;"The chest is a body area that may be scanned via CT to check for lymphoma spread outside the central nervous system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The chest is a part of the body imaged via CT scan during surveillance after recurrence treatment to detect cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"The chest is the part of the body containing the heart and lungs. CT scans of the chest are used to check for cancer spread to the lungs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADICAL HYSTERECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A more extensive surgical procedure for cervical cancer that removes the uterus, cervix, upper vagina, and surrounding tissues, including pelvic lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of hysterectomy that removes the uterus, much of the connective tissue, and the top quarter or third of the vagina."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radical hysterectomy is a surgical procedure that removes the uterus and surrounding tissues, typically considered in carefully selected patients for recurrent cervical cancer in the pelvis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNOSUPPRESSANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immunosuppressants are anti-rejection medicines taken after organ transplants that weaken the immune system, increasing the risk of anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immunosuppressants are drugs taken after organ transplantation to prevent rejection, but they also reduce the body's ability to fight infections and diseases, increasing the risk of skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CTDNA TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ctDNA testing (liquid biopsy) looks for small pieces of tumor DNA in blood to detect microscopic cancer cells, still under study in clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"ctDNA testing, also known as liquid biopsy, is a test that detects circulating tumor DNA in the blood to identify microscopic disease after colectomy, currently recommended only in clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic cervical cancer is a type of cancer that has spread to distant organs such as the liver, lungs, or bone, and is typically treated with systemic therapies like platinum-based chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cervical cancer is cervical cancer that has spread to distant organs such as the liver, lungs, or bone, and is very hard to cure, typically treated with systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P16 PROTEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"p16 protein is a biomarker that slows cell division and is overexpressed in HPV-positive throat cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility tests are assessments to evaluate reproductive health, important for AYAs with ALL before treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility tests are general health tests that may be part of FL evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility tests are part of CBCL testing, assessing reproductive health in all genders before treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFICULTY SPEAKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Difficulty speaking is a symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, affecting communication abilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSYCHOLOGICAL SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Psychological support is provided through distress screening to help patients cope."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESOURCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A resource is a source of information or support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UTERUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The female reproductive organ that may be removed during hysterectomy, with preservation of ovaries being an option."&lt;SEP&gt;"The uterus is a female reproductive organ that may be removed during pelvic exenteration or radical hysterectomy for cervical cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The uterus is a female reproductive organ where the applicator is inserted during brachytherapy for cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The uterus is a part of the female reproductive system where a fetus grows and develops during pregnancy. It is connected to the fallopian tubes and cervix."&lt;SEP&gt;"The uterus is a reproductive organ in females that stage 3A bladder cancer may invade."&lt;SEP&gt;"The uterus is a reproductive organ that can be affected by ovarian cancer spread, particularly in Stage 2A."&lt;SEP&gt;"The uterus is part of the female reproductive system, often removed during ovarian cancer surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"The uterus is the female reproductive organ where a fetus develops. It is removed during a hysterectomy, eliminating the possibility of pregnancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The uterus is the female reproductive organ where fetal development occurs, removed during hysterectomy for ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The uterus is the female reproductive organ where the cervix is located, and cervical cancer can spread to surrounding tissues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The uterus is the organ removed in hysterectomy, part of the female reproductive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The uterus is the organ where a baby grows and develops before birth. The cervix is part of the uterus, but uterine cancer is diagnosed and treated differently from cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Uterus is a female reproductive organ that can be imaged via MRI to show tissues in detail for cancer assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Uterus is a female reproductive organ that may be removed during radical cystectomy if cancer has spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Uterus is an organ whose size, position, and appearance are checked during a pelvic examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Uterus is part of the female reproductive system, included in the context of ovarian cancer anatomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Uterus is the female reproductive organ where the lining can be biopsied to rule out uterine cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Uterus is the organ that may be removed in a hysterectomy, and the cervix is part of it."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE EVALUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A procedure to examine lymph nodes for cancer spread, often performed during hysterectomy for cervical cancer staging and treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VULVAR CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vulvar cancer is a type of cancer caused by HPV, and a history of it increases the risk of anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vulvar cancer is a type of cancer where p16 can be found."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSATELLITE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microsatellite is a short, repeated string of DNA, and instability in these regions can indicate cancer-related DNA repair issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellites are short repeated DNA sequences that can become unstable (MSI-H) in certain cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABLATIVE THERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ablative therapies are treatments that destroy cancerous lesions with minimal harm to nearby tissue, often delivered via a needle probe or electrode placed directly into or next to the tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTRAST MATERIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contrast material is a substance used in imaging tests to enhance image clarity, not a dye, and is excreted via urine after tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast material is a substance used in imaging tests to enhance picture clarity, administered orally or intravenously, with considerations for allergies and kidney function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast material is a substance used to enhance and improve the clarity of images of internal body structures during imaging tests like CT and MRI scans. It is not a dye, is temporary, and is excreted in urine. Its use may be limited in patients with allergies or kidney issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast material is a substance used to enhance images of internal organs and structures during imaging tests, not a dye, and is excreted in urine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast material is a substance used to enhance imaging pictures, not a dye, and is eliminated from the body via urine after tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast material is a substance used to enhance imaging test images, not a dye."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast material is a substance used to improve the quality of images of the inside of the body, enhancing pictures of organs and structures, and is used in CT and MRI scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast material is a substance used to improve the quality of imaging pictures, taken orally or intravenously, and may be avoided in cases of serious allergy or poor kidney function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast material refers to substances used in imaging tests like CT and MRI to enhance and improve the clarity of images of internal organs and structures; it is not a dye and is excreted via urine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAREGIVER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A caregiver provides physical, mental, emotional, and hands-on support to a person with primary CNS lymphoma, helping with appointments and treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caregiver is a person who assists the patient with daily activities and home care during and after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caregiver is a person who provides support to a patient, asking questions and assisting with care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caregiver is a person who supports the patient, may be involved in discussions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFICULTY SWALLOWING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Difficulty swallowing is a symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, affecting the ability to eat and drink."&lt;SEP&gt;"Difficulty swallowing is a symptom that radiation therapy may relieve if caused by cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medical testing includes biomarker testing, genetic testing, and tumor marker analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRACAVITARY BRACHYTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intracavitary brachytherapy is a method where instruments are placed in the cervix, uterus, and vagina to deliver radiation, most often used for cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREGNANT OR LACTATING INDIVIDUALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pregnant or lactating individuals are those who require special consideration for breast cancer screening and testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BINDER PURCHASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Binder Purchase is selecting and buying a binder that meets patient needs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW-GRADE TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A low-grade tumor is a less aggressive type of ovarian cancer, where observation may be an option for Stage 1A or 1B."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTING FOR CBCL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Testing for CBCL includes general health tests, skin exams, fertility tests, blood tests, imaging tests, biopsy, immunophenotyping, and biomarker/genetic testing to diagnose and treat the condition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STOMACH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stomach is a digestive organ that receives food from the esophagus and continues the digestion process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stomach is an organ felt and listened to during a physical exam of the abdomen."&lt;SEP&gt;"The stomach is a digestive organ that breaks down food using contractions, enzymes, and acid. It has parts including the cardia, fundus, body, antrum, and pylorus."&lt;SEP&gt;"The stomach is a muscular, hollow organ located between the esophagus and small intestine. It secretes enzymes and acid to break down food into chyme, playing a key role in digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The stomach is an organ near the liver involved in digestion, mentioned as part of nearby organs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The stomach is an organ near the liver involved in digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The stomach is an organ that meets the esophagus at the esophagogastric junction, and tumors starting there can be treated as esophageal cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The stomach is part of the GI tract, involved in digestion and examined during upper endoscopy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC LYMPH NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph nodes located in the pelvic region that may be removed during trachelectomy or lymph node dissection to check for cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph nodes located in the pelvic region that may be removed or evaluated during cervical cancer surgery to check for cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pelvic lymph nodes are lymph nodes near the cervix, and their involvement is a criterion for stage 3C cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAGINAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vaginal cancer is a type of cancer caused by HPV, and a history of it increases the risk of anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SALIVA TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A saliva test is used to detect inherited gene mutations, such as those causing Lynch syndrome or FAP."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEREOTACTIC BODY RADIATION THERAPY (SBRT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SBRT is a special type of radiation therapy used for limited small metastases in anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stereotactic body radiation therapy (SBRT) is a highly specialized type of EBRT used to treat tumors in the liver, lungs, or bone, requiring only a few treatment sessions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TECHNOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A technologist is a healthcare professional who operates imaging equipment and ensures patient safety, such as checking for metal before an MRI."&lt;SEP&gt;"A technologist is a healthcare professional who operates imaging equipment such as MRI machines and collects images during scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"A technologist operates imaging equipment like MRI machines and collects images during tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technologist is a healthcare professional who operates imaging equipment, such as MRI machines, and collects images during tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technologist is a healthcare professional who operates imaging equipment, such as MRI machines, and instructs patients during tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Technologist is a professional who operates imaging equipment, such as MRI machines, and guides patients during scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDIANA UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indiana University is the institution where surgeons developed the Indiana pouch, a type of urinary diversion procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Indiana University is the institution where surgeons developed the continent cutaneous pouch, also known as the Indiana pouch."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EYESIGHT CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eyesight changes, such as blurry or double vision, are symptoms of primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGNOSTIC MARKERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prognostic markers are biomarkers that indicate cancer progression, like tumor markers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERSTITIAL BRACHYTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Interstitial brachytherapy is a specialized technique using catheters placed in or near the tumor, used for more advanced cervical cancers involving the parametrium."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC EXAMINATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic examination is a physical exam to check the size, position, and appearance of the cervix and uterus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARA-AORTIC LYMPH NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph nodes located in the abdomen near the aorta that may be removed or evaluated in cervical cancer cases to check for cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Para-aortic lymph nodes are lymph nodes in the abdomen, and their involvement is a criterion for stage 3C cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Para-aortic lymph nodes are lymph nodes located in the abdomen. They may be removed during surgery for certain stages of cervical cancer to check for spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL DYSPLASIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anal dysplasia is a precancerous condition characterized by abnormal cells on the anal surface, which may progress to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal dysplasia refers to pre-cancerous lesions in or near the anus, also known as anal intraepithelial neoplasia (AIN), which can be low-grade (LSIL) or high-grade (HSIL). Identifying and treating it may prevent anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INHERITED GENE MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An inherited gene mutation is a genetic change passed from parents, increasing cancer risk, such as in Lynch syndrome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL RECURRENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local recurrence is the return of cancer to the same place as the original tumor, a risk associated with high-risk CSCC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local recurrence is the return of cervical cancer in the pelvis, also known as regional recurrence, requiring specific treatment approaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local recurrence refers to the return of cervical cancer in the same area where it originally occurred, often treated with surgery, radiation, and systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENT ACCESS SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A patient access system is a digital platform for patients to view their health information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient access system is a system where test reports might be available, but patients are advised to wait to discuss results with their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient access system is an online platform for patients to view medical records and test results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDIANA POUCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indiana pouch is a type of urinary diversion that uses a section of the small intestine to create a pouch and a one-way valve, eliminating the need for an ostomy bag."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRESSURE ON THE CNS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pressure on the CNS is caused by the growth of a lymphoma tumor, leading to neurological symptoms and difficulties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREDICTIVE MARKERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Predictive markers are biomarkers that predict treatment response, like TMB-H for immunotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH DOSE-RATE (HDR) BRACHYTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High dose-rate brachytherapy delivers radiation in short bursts, commonly used in current treatment centers for cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METAMUCIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metamucil is a psyllium-based fiber supplement that may help with bowel changes after anal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL BOWEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The small bowel is part of the GI tract, involved in nutrient absorption and examined via upper endoscopy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EARLY SATIETY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Early satiety is a symptom of CLL, where patients feel full too quickly."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATERY VAGINAL DISCHARGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Watery vaginal discharge is a possible symptom of cervical cancer that the doctor asks about during health history."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMORADIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A treatment combining chemotherapy and radiation therapy for cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A treatment combining chemotherapy and radiation therapy, used for locally advanced cervical cancer to improve outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A treatment combining chemotherapy and radiation, recommended for nonmetastatic perianal cancers that do not meet criteria for local excision."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation combines chemotherapy and radiation therapy, used for certain stages of cervical cancer, requiring post-treatment imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a combination of chemotherapy and radiation therapy used together to treat bladder cancer, working better than either alone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment approach combining chemotherapy and radiation therapy, commonly used for anal and perianal cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment approach combining chemotherapy and radiation therapy, generally not considered after chemotherapy with the modified DCF regimen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment combining chemotherapy and radiation therapy concurrently, commonly used for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment combining chemotherapy and radiation therapy for certain cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment combining chemotherapy and radiation therapy, commonly used for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment combining chemotherapy and radiation therapy, recommended as the primary treatment for most non-metastatic anal cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment combining chemotherapy and radiation therapy, used after certain chemotherapy regimens for metastatic anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment combining chemotherapy and radiation, recommended for most non-metastatic anal cancers to cure the disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment combining chemotherapy and radiation, recommended for most non-metastatic anal cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment combining chemotherapy and radiation, used for locally advanced rectal cancers, with potential follow-up chemotherapy or watch-and-wait strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment combining external beam radiation therapy (EBRT) with platinum chemotherapy. It is recommended for locally advanced cervical cancer or when cancer is found in lymph nodes or tissues beyond the cervix."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment strategy combining EBRT and chemotherapy concurrently for locally advanced cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment strategy combining EBRT and chemotherapy concurrently, recommended for most locally advanced cervical cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemoradiation is a treatment strategy combining EBRT and platinum-based chemotherapy given concurrently for cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LSIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LSIL (Low-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion) is a mild form of anal dysplasia, a pre-cancerous condition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOMETRIAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer associated with Lynch syndrome, increasing risk in affected individuals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endometrial cancer is a type of cancer associated with Lynch syndrome, affecting the uterus lining."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endometrial cancer is a type of cancer; a personal or family history may be relevant to thyroid cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endometrial cancer is a type of uterine cancer that arises in the lining of the uterus, distinct from cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGIONAL RECURRENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Regional recurrence is the return of cervical cancer in the pelvic region, treated with surgery, radiation, or systemic therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Regional recurrence refers to the return of cervical cancer in nearby lymph nodes or tissues, treated similarly to local recurrence with surgery, radiation, and systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASE OF THE TONGUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Base of the tongue is a lymphoid tissue area that may appear bright on PET scans normally."&lt;SEP&gt;"The base of the tongue is a site where HPV-related throat cancers can occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"The base of the tongue is part of the oropharynx and is included in the area where throat cancer can form."&lt;SEP&gt;"The base of the tongue is part of the oropharynx, found in the throat."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS CALMETTE-GUÉRIN (BCG)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillus Calmette-Guérin (BCG) is a type of intravesical therapy that uses a weak bacterium to trigger the immune system to attack bladder cancer cells, commonly used for high-grade non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary CNS lymphoma diagnosis involves several tests to confirm the presence of the disease and rule out other conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREVENTIVE MEASURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Preventive measures may be recommended based on genetic risk, such as increased screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW DOSE-RATE (LDR) BRACHYTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low dose-rate brachytherapy delivers radiation in long bursts, less commonly used compared to HDR brachytherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIDNEY FUNCTION TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A test measuring waste products like creatinine and blood urea nitrogen to check kidney function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medicines are drugs a patient takes, including prescription and over-the-counter, listed in medical history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medicines are drugs given to prevent allergic reactions to contrast material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medicines are drugs used in treatment, including over-the-counter and prescription, which may interact with each other."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medicines are pharmaceutical aids that can help patients quit smoking."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medicines are pharmaceutical treatments that can help cancer patients quit smoking or vaping and manage side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medicines are pharmacological aids recommended to help patients quit smoking and manage nicotine addiction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medicines are pharmacological aids used to help quit smoking or treat cancer, improving treatment outcomes and reducing side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medicines are prescription or over-the-counter drugs that the doctor asks about during health history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medicines include prescription drugs, over-the-counter drugs, herbals, and supplements that patients take and should list for their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prescription and over-the-counter drugs, herbals, or supplements that a patient takes, to be listed for the doctor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prescription and over-the-counter drugs, herbals, or supplements that a patient takes, which may interact with treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of chemotherapy using platinum-based drugs, such as cisplatin, often used in combination with radiation for cervical cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platinum chemotherapy is a type of chemotherapy drug (e.g., cisplatin) used in combination with radiation therapy (chemoradiation) for cervical cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HSIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HSIL (High-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion) is a moderate or severe form of anal dysplasia, a pre-cancerous condition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENIGN GROWTHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benign growths are non-cancerous polyps that can become invasive cancer over time, as in FAP."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISTANT RECURRENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Distant recurrence is the return of cervical cancer in areas far from the original site, managed similarly to metastatic disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant recurrence refers to the return of cervical cancer in distant organs such as the liver, lungs, or bone, after treatment, and is considered metastatic disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VULVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The vulva is an organ where HPV can infect and cause cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAVESICAL CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intravesical chemotherapy is a treatment that only affects the inside of the bladder, distinct from systemic chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intravesical chemotherapy is a type of intravesical therapy that delivers chemotherapy drugs directly into the bladder to treat cancer and reduce recurrence risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTHER DISEASES WITH SIMILAR SYMPTOMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Other diseases with similar symptoms to primary CNS lymphoma include neurological illnesses and other types of brain cancer, requiring tests for confirmation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Screening involves regular tests like mammograms to detect breast cancer early in asymptomatic individuals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Screening is the process of testing for breast cancer in asymptomatic individuals to detect disease early."&lt;SEP&gt;"Screening is the process of testing for cancer in at-risk individuals, guided by family history."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPLICATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An applicator is a device inserted into the uterus through the vagina for brachytherapy, with types like tandem and ring or tandem and ovoid, used to guide radiation delivery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE STATUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph Node Status refers to whether cancer has spread to nearby lymph nodes, a key component of staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIFESTYLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lifestyle factors such as smoking, obesity, exercise, and maintaining a healthy weight influence prostate cancer risk and outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lifestyle includes diet, activity level, smoking, and alcohol consumption, which are discussed during health history."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN.ORG/PATIENTS/RESPONSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An online platform for patients to provide feedback on the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, used to improve patient resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patients/response is a website where patients can complete an online survey about the NCCN Guidelines for Patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patients/response is an online survey link for patients to provide feedback on the NCCN Guidelines for Patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AIN (Anal intraepithelial neoplasia) is another name for anal dysplasia, a pre-cancerous condition in the anus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSMA/PET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSMA/PET is a specialized PET imaging technique that targets the prostate-specific membrane antigen on prostate cancer cells, useful for detecting spread and recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECTUS ABDOMINUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The rectus abdominus is a muscle in the lower abdomen often used for vaginal reconstruction after pelvic exenteration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLAUSTROPHOBIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Claustrophobia is a dread or fear of enclosed spaces, which is relevant when choosing between open and closed MRI machines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claustrophobia is a dread or fear of enclosed spaces, which may affect a patient's choice between closed and open MRI."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claustrophobia is a dread or fear of enclosed spaces, which may affect patients undergoing closed MRI scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claustrophobia is a fear of enclosed spaces, relevant for closed MRI scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claustrophobia is a fear of enclosed spaces, relevant to closed MRI scans, requiring discussion with the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claustrophobia is a fear of enclosed spaces, which is a consideration for patients undergoing MRI scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claustrophobia is a fear of enclosed spaces, which may affect a patient's ability to undergo a closed MRI, and should be discussed with the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Claustrophobia is a fear of enclosed spaces, which may affect patients undergoing closed MRI scans. Patients are advised to discuss this with their care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TURBT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TURBT (Transurethral Resection of Bladder Tumor) is a surgical procedure to remove visible bladder cancer, often followed by intravesical therapy to destroy remaining cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"TURBT (transurethral resection of bladder tumor) is a surgical procedure used to examine and remove tumors on the bladder wall, often performed in combination with intravesical therapy and sometimes repeated to ensure complete tumor removal."&lt;SEP&gt;"TURBT is a procedure to remove all visible cancer from the bladder, used as part of trimodal therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROLOGICAL ILLNESSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neurological illnesses are diseases that affect the nervous system and may have symptoms similar to primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EARLY DETECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Early detection is the goal of screening and biomarker testing to catch cancer early."&lt;SEP&gt;"Early detection refers to identifying lung cancer at its earliest, most treatable stages through regular screening in at-risk populations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TANDEM AND RING APPLICATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A tandem and ring applicator is a common device for HDR brachytherapy, consisting of a long thin tube (tandem) and a hollow circle (ring) placed in the vagina."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST PAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breast pain is a symptom that may require further testing to rule out cancer or other conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLDER CREATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Folder Creation is making categories within the binder for different record types."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MGZL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MGZL (mediastinal gray zone lymphoma) is a type of cancer with features of both classical Hodgkin lymphoma and non-Hodgkin PMBL, often involving the mediastinum and presenting with extranodal disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 5&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 5 is a section of the NCCN guidelines that discusses treatment with surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chapter 5 is a specific section of the text that describes Richter transformation, providing detailed information for patients with this condition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ILLNESSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Illnesses are past and current diseases that the doctor asks about during health history."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1A1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specific stage of cervical cancer characterized by microscopic invasion of cancer cells into cervical tissue, with specific treatment recommendations based on risk factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 1A1 is a very early stage of cervical cancer where the tumor is microscopic and confined to the cervix. Treatment may involve cone biopsy or radical trachelectomy, with or without pelvic lymph node evaluation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV VACCINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV vaccine protects against 9 strains of HPV, including high-risk types; available in the US for adults up to age 45, and works best in younger people."&lt;SEP&gt;"The HPV vaccine protects against 9 different strains of HPV, including high-risk strains, and is recommended for routine use in adolescents and young adults, with options for adults up to age 45."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSA (prostate-specific antigen) is a blood marker; high levels may indicate prostate cancer, and PSA density is a measurement used in risk assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSA (prostate-specific antigen) is a blood test used to screen for prostate cancer. High levels may indicate cancer, prompting further tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ILEUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ileum is the final section of the small intestine, removed and used as a tube in the ileal conduit urinary diversion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ileum is a piece of the intestine used to create a new tube for an ileal conduit or a pouch for a continent urinary diversion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT DOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The amount of treatment given, which influences fertility changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment Dose is the amount of therapy given, which affects fertility outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment dose refers to the amount of cancer therapy given, which affects the degree of fertility impairment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BCG SHORTAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BCG shortage is a global supply issue affecting the availability of BCG therapy for bladder cancer, leading to alternative treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTHER TYPES OF BRAIN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Other types of brain cancer are diseases that may have symptoms similar to primary CNS lymphoma, requiring differential diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENT EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patient Education is learning about cancer treatment effects and fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient education involves informing patients about testing and family history importance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient education involves providing information to help patients understand their condition and make informed decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TANDEM AND OVOID APPLICATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A tandem and ovoid applicator uses hollow, rounded capsules instead of a ring, used in brachytherapy for cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGERIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgeries are past procedures that the doctor asks about during health history."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1A2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage of cervical cancer with deeper invasion into cervical tissue, requiring more aggressive treatment such as hysterectomy with lymph node evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 1A2 is an early stage of cervical cancer where the tumor is slightly larger than 1A1 but still confined to the cervix. Treatment may include cone biopsy or radical trachelectomy with pelvic lymph node evaluation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECTAL BLEEDING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rectal bleeding is the most common symptom of anal cancer, where blood may appear in stool, on toilet paper, or in toilet water."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRACER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A radioactive drug injected into a vein during a PET scan to highlight cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"A radioactive substance injected into a vein for PET scans to help see cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"A tracer is a radioactive substance injected into a vein during a PET scan to visualize cancer cells and their metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracer is a radioactive drug injected into a vein for PET scans to see cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracer is a radioactive drug injected into a vein to visualize cancer cell activity in PET scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracer is a radioactive drug used in PET scans, injected into a vein to see where cancer cells are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracer is a radioactive substance injected into a vein for PET scans to detect cancer cells and their sugar uptake."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracer is a radioactive substance injected into the body for PET scans to visualize cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracer is a radioactive substance used in PET and bone scans to highlight cancerous cells or bone damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracer is a radioactive substance used in PET scans that targets cancer cells, showing up as bright spots on the scan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracer is a radioactive sugar-based substance used in PET scans, injected into a vein to identify cancer cells in the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tracer is another term for radiotracer, injected into the vein for bone scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stoma is a small opening created on the abdomen for urine or stool to exit the body, used in various diversions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A stoma is an opening created on the surface of the abdomen during a colostomy, through which stool exits the body into a bag."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stoma is a small hole created in the abdominal wall for urine to exit the body in urinary diversions like ileal conduit and continent cutaneous pouch."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stoma is an opening in the abdomen created during urinary diversion surgery, through which a catheter is inserted to drain urine from the pouch."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stoma is an opening on the abdomen created by a colostomy, through which stool exits the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stoma is an opening on the surface of the abdomen created during a colostomy, through which stool exits the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT LENGTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The duration of treatment, which affects fertility and other side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment Length is the duration of therapy, which impacts fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment length is the duration of cancer therapy, influencing the likelihood and permanence of fertility loss."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGEONS AT INDIANA UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgeons at Indiana University are the medical professionals who developed the Indiana pouch, a specific urinary diversion technique."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SAMPLE OF FLUID OR TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A sample of fluid or tissue is taken during a biopsy to look for cancer cells and confirm a diagnosis of primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIVACY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Privacy is a consideration in genetic testing, as results are sensitive."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEEP SEDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Deep sedation is often required for brachytherapy applicator placement, especially the first time, to ensure patient comfort and immobility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTHESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A prosthesis is an artificial breast form used after mastectomy to restore shape."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHITE BLOOD CELL (WBC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"White blood cells are immune cells whose normal formation requires B12 and folic acid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOMETRIOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endometriosis is a non-cancerous condition that can raise CA-125 levels, complicating diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNINTENTIONAL WEIGHT LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unintentional weight loss is a symptom of CLL, occurring without deliberate dieting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTRAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A substance used in imaging tests to make pictures clearer, which may cause allergic reactions in some patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"A substance used in imaging to make pictures clearer, often used in CT or MRI scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast is a substance injected or ingested to make CT pictures clearer, possibly causing flushing or hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast is a substance used in imaging tests to enhance picture clarity, injected or ingested, and may require premedication to reduce allergic reactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast is a substance used in imaging tests to make pictures clearer, injected into a vein or mixed with a drink."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast is a substance used in imaging tests to make pictures clearer. It can be ingested orally or injected intravenously, and may cause side effects like flushing or hives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Substances used to enhance and improve images of organs and structures in the body during imaging tests, taken orally or intravenously, and not permanent."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1B1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage of cervical cancer where the tumor is larger than 5 mm in depth but less than 4 cm, with treatment options depending on risk factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 1B1 is an early stage of cervical cancer where the tumor is larger than 1A2 but still confined to the cervix. Treatment may include cone biopsy for very low-risk cases or radical trachelectomy with lymph node evaluation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMORRHOIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hemorrhoids are swollen veins in the anus or lower rectum, which can cause symptoms similar to anal cancer, such as bleeding and itching."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTATE-SPECIFIC MEMBRANE ANTIGEN (PSMA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSMA is a protein found on the surface of prostate cancer cells, targeted by specific tracers in PSMA/PET imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"PSMA is a protein on the surface of prostate cancer cells that is targeted by specific tracers in PSMA-PET scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTOMY BAG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ostomy bag, also called an ostomy pouch, is a disposable bag attached to the skin to collect urine or stool from a stoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ostomy bag (or ostomy pouch) is a disposable bag attached to the abdomen to collect urine from a stoma in ileal conduit."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ostomy bag is an external collection device not needed with the Indiana pouch, which is a benefit for some patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT TYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The specific cancer treatment used, which affects fertility and other outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment type includes various cancer therapies like chemotherapy and radiation, each with different impacts on fertility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONE-WAY VALVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"One-way valve is a component made from part of the intestine in the Indiana pouch, preventing urine from flowing out of the stoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SLOWING GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Slowing growth refers to the effect of treatment on primary CNS lymphoma, reducing its progression and symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cost is a factor in genetic testing and biomarker testing, affecting access."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIATION SOURCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A radiation source travels from a brachytherapy machine through hollow tubes into the applicator to deliver treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMARKER TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A test identifying specific tumor cells or biomarkers, providing clues about bladder cancer but not yet reliable for diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOTRACERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiotracers are small amounts of radioactive materials used in PET scans to highlight cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiotracers are small amounts of radioactive materials used in PET scans, injected into the body to emit energy detectable by imaging machines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1B2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage of cervical cancer with a tumor larger than 4 cm but confined to the cervix, requiring radical hysterectomy with lymph node evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 1B2 is an early stage of cervical cancer with a larger tumor confined to the cervix. Fertility-sparing surgery is less common, and abdominal surgery is generally preferred."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GYNECOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gynecologist is a doctor specializing in female reproductive health, who can be part of the cervical cancer care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"A gynecologist is a health care professional that people with anal cancer symptoms may reach out to for evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gynecologist diagnoses and treats diseases of the female reproductive organs, and may be involved in breast cancer screening and care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gynecologist diagnoses and treats diseases of the female reproductive organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTRAST DYE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A liquid injected into a vein during CT or MRI scans to make tissues and organs show up more clearly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast dye is another term for contrast agent, injected into the bloodstream to enhance imaging clarity in MRI scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAFER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A wafer is an adhesive part that sticks to the skin and acts as a watertight barrier to hold an ostomy bag in place."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREGNANCY TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pregnancy test is performed before starting treatment for those who can become pregnant to ensure safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"A pregnancy test is performed on those with ovaries before starting cancer treatment to ensure safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"A test conducted before starting treatment for those who can become pregnant to ensure safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy Test is a diagnostic test given to those who can become pregnant before starting cancer treatment to ensure safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy test is a test given to patients with potential to become pregnant before cancer treatment to ensure safety of the unborn baby."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy test is a test given to those who can become pregnant before treatment begins to avoid pregnancy during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BELLY BUTTON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Belly button is an alternative location for the stoma in some Indiana pouch procedures, making it less noticeable."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REDUCING SYMPTOMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reducing symptoms is a goal of treatment for primary CNS lymphoma, improving quality of life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACCESS TO CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Access to care is important for biomarker testing and genetic counseling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRACHYTHERAPY MACHINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A brachytherapy machine is connected to the applicator and delivers the radiation source for treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NODULAR LYMPHOCYTE-PREDOMINANT HODGKIN LYMPHOMA (NLPHL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NLPHL is a rare form of Hodgkin lymphoma characterized by popcorn-shaped cells, usually slow-growing but can transform into aggressive cancers like DLBCL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLORECTAL SURGEON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A colorectal surgeon is a specialist best qualified to evaluate anal cancer, as they are trained in procedures like high-resolution anoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colorectal Surgeon is a specialist in surgeries of the colon, rectum, and anus, including APR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUGAR RADIOTRACER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sugar radiotracer is a substance injected into the body through a vein, emitting energy detected by PET scan machines to show cell activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sugar radiotracer is a type of radiotracer injected before a PET scan, taken up more quickly by cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1B3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage of cervical cancer with a tumor larger than 4 cm that does not extend beyond the cervix, often treated as locally advanced."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMAGING ROOM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Imaging room is the location where MRI, CT, PET, or bone scans are performed, with safety precautions regarding metal objects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TARGETED THERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Targeted therapies are treatments aimed at specific genetic abnormalities, monitored using RT-PCR."&lt;SEP&gt;"Targeted therapies are treatments that specifically target cancer cells based on biomarkers, potentially used for metastatic cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREASTFEEDING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition that requires avoiding certain cancer treatments to protect the baby."&lt;SEP&gt;"Breastfeeding is a condition that may require avoiding certain cancer treatments during diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Breastfeeding is a condition that may require avoiding certain cancer treatments if present at diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Breastfeeding is a condition that may require avoiding certain cancer treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSTILLATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Instillation is the process of delivering medicine into the bladder through a catheter during intravesical therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROLONGING LIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prolonging life is a goal of treatment for primary CNS lymphoma, extending survival time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH DISPARITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health disparities may affect access to testing and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNAL RADIATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Internal radiation therapy, also known as brachytherapy, involves placing radioactive material inside the body to treat cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skin changes on the breast, such as redness or dimpling, are symptoms that warrant further testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DATE ORGANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Date Organization is arranging records chronologically within folders."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-HODGKIN PMBL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-Hodgkin PMBL (primary mediastinal B-cell lymphoma) is a type of lymphoma with features overlapping with MGZL, affecting treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MYCOSIS FUNGOIDES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mycosis fungoides is a type of cutaneous T-cell lymphoma, a rare form of lymphoma affecting the skin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-RESOLUTION ANOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-resolution anoscopy (HRA) is a procedure using a colposcope to examine the anal canal with magnification, often after a DRE, to identify abnormal cells or lesions."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-resolution anoscopy is a specialized examination to detect anal cancer or precancerous changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAGNETIC RESONANCE IMAGING (MRI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scan is a diagnostic procedure using radio waves and powerful magnets to produce detailed images of internal structures without x-rays. It may be closed or open, and contrast is often used."&lt;SEP&gt;"MRI is an imaging test that uses strong magnetic fields and radio waves to create detailed pictures of soft tissues without radiation, useful for examining the uterus, cervix, and vagina."&lt;SEP&gt;"Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) uses radio waves and magnets to produce detailed images without radiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Magnetic resonance imaging is an imaging test that may be performed with PET in some cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Magnetic resonance imaging is an imaging test that uses a magnetic field and radio waves to create detailed pictures of soft tissues. It is recommended to determine the extent of anal cancer in the pelvis and does not use radiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2A1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage of cervical cancer where the tumor extends into the upper vagina but is less than 4 cm, treated with radical hysterectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRI SCANNER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MRI scanner is a large machine with a tunnel that uses magnets and radio waves to create detailed images of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNOTHERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immunotherapies are treatments that boost the immune system to fight cancer, potentially used for metastatic cervical cancer based on biomarker testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERIOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Menstrual flow that may stop during treatment but often returns within 2 years in those under 35."&lt;SEP&gt;"Period, or menstruation, may stop during treatment but often returns within 2 years in patients 35 and under."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLADDER MUSCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bladder muscle is the layer of the bladder that cancer may invade, and BCG therapy aims to prevent this progression."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMBINATION OF TREATMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A combination of treatments for primary CNS lymphoma may include chemotherapy, radiation therapy, and stem cell transplant."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Research is ongoing to improve biomarker testing and targeted therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Research refers to the latest scientific studies that inform cancer care recommendations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATHETERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Catheters are thin hollow tubes that may be placed in the tumor or nearby tissue for interstitial brachytherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL SEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A history of anal sex is a risk factor for anal cancer, often associated with increased HPV transmission."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal sex is a lifestyle-related risk factor for anal cancer, as it can increase the likelihood of HPV infection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HIV (Human Immunodeficiency Virus) infection is a risk factor for anal cancer, often associated with immunosuppression."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIV (Human Immunodeficiency Virus) is a risk factor for anal cancer, often associated with immunosuppression and increased vulnerability to HPV-related cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIV (Human Immunodeficiency Virus) is a virus that increases the risk of developing anal cancer. Testing for HIV is important for patients with anal cancer, as managing HIV can improve cancer treatment outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIV (Human Immunodeficiency Virus) is an infection that weakens the immune system, increasing the risk of anal cancer by making it harder for the body to clear HPV infection."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIV (human immunodeficiency virus) is a condition that weakens the immune system, increasing risk of CSCC."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIV is an immunodeficiency virus that causes AIDS and is frequently linked to primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIV is human immunodeficiency virus, which can be detected through a blood test and does not affect cancer treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2A2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage of cervical cancer where the tumor extends into the upper vagina and is larger than 4 cm, often treated with chemoradiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PET SCANNER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PET scanner is a large machine with a tunnel that detects radioactive tracers to create images of cancerous cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 2: TESTING FOR BONE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 2 provides an overview of tests for bone cancer, including general health tests, fertility considerations, biomarker testing, and tumor mutation testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chapter 2: Testing for bone cancer is a section of the book that provides an overview of tests, fertility impact, and biomarker testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTRACEPTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contraception includes methods like condoms to prevent pregnancy during and after cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contraception refers to birth control methods, such as condoms, used to prevent pregnancy during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-GRADE BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-grade bladder cancer is an aggressive form of bladder cancer that hasn't invaded the muscle layer, commonly treated with BCG therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POTENTIAL NEW THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A potential new therapy is a treatment being studied in clinical trials for primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUIDELINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Guidelines are recommendations for best practices in cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guidelines from organizations recommend when to use biomarker testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORMAL TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Normal tissue refers to healthy cells surrounding the tumor, which brachytherapy aims to spare from radiation damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHEDEMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymphedema is swelling in the arm or chest caused by lymph node removal or radiation, a common side effect of breast cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMOGLOBIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hemoglobin is the molecule in blood that carries oxygen, and its production depends on iron."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPINAL CANAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spinal canal is the space within the vertebrae that houses the spinal cord, relevant for T4 staging in spine tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIVERTICULITIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diverticulitis is a non-cancerous condition that can raise CA-125 levels, complicating diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKALINE PHOSPHATASE (ALP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alkaline Phosphatase (ALP) is an enzyme in the blood; high levels may indicate cancer spread to bone or liver."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEXUALLY TRANSMITTED INFECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A history of sexually transmitted infections is a risk factor for anal cancer, indicating higher exposure to HPV and other pathogens."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sexually transmitted infections (STIs) are infections spread through sexual contact, and a history of them increases the risk of anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIV-POSITIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HIV-positive refers to a patient with HIV, who may be referred to an HIV specialist but still receives the same cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2B&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage of cervical cancer where the tumor extends into the parametrium (tissue beside the cervix), treated as locally advanced."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 2B is a specific stage of ovarian cancer where cancer has spread to other pelvic organs such as the bladder, colon, or rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT SCANNER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CT scanner is a machine that takes multiple x-rays from different angles to create detailed cross-sectional images."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 3: BONE CANCER STAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 3 explains how bone cancer is staged and where bone tumors might be found in the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chapter 3: Bone cancer staging explains how bone cancer is staged and where tumors might be found."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEVELOPING BABY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A developing baby can be harmed by cancer treatment if pregnancy occurs during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTHY CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Healthy cells are normal body cells that can be damaged by systemic therapy, causing side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Healthy cells are normal body cells that can be harmed by chemotherapy, leading to side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Healthy cells are normal body cells that may be harmed by chemotherapy, leading to side effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELAPSE IN THE BRAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Relapse in the brain is the return of primary CNS lymphoma in the brain after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGULATORY APPROVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Regulatory approval is needed for new tests and therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAVENOUS INFUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intravenous infusion is a method of delivering systemic therapies slowly into the bloodstream through a vein."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINE CYTOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A lab test analyzing urine for cancer or precancerous cells, often used when blood is present in urine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CROHN'S DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crohn's disease is an autoimmune disorder that increases the risk of anal cancer due to its effects on the immune system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIV-NEGATIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HIV-negative refers to a patient without HIV, who receives the same cancer treatment as HIV-positive patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL CELL NEUROENDOCRINE CARCINOMA OF THE CERVIX (NECC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rare and aggressive type of cervical cancer that requires specific surveillance and treatment approaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"NECC is a rare type of cervical cancer for which MRI of the brain is recommended as part of initial testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Small cell neuroendocrine carcinoma of the cervix (NECC) is a rare and aggressive subtype of cervical cancer, requiring specialized surveillance and treatment approaches."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE METASTASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone metastases are areas where prostate cancer has spread to bones, detected through bone scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 4: TYPES OF TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 4 gives an overview of different treatment types and who might be on a treatment team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chapter 4: Types of treatment gives an overview of treatment options for bone cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPSY SAMPLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biopsy samples are tissue specimens tested for p16 protein to detect HPV in throat cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATHOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pathology is a medical specialty involving the examination of tissues and cells to diagnose diseases like cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathology is the study of disease, including analysis of biopsy tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELAPSE IN THE SPINAL CORD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Relapse in the spinal cord is the return of primary CNS lymphoma in the spinal cord after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONCOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oncology is the medical field focused on cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT CYCLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment cycles are periods of treatment days followed by rest days, allowing the body to recover between systemic therapy sessions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV Test is a screening test to detect HPV infection, which is a risk factor for anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTING FOR HODGKIN LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Testing for Hodgkin lymphoma includes biopsy, lab testing, health history, physical exam, blood tests, imaging tests, and heart and lung tests to diagnose the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Modified radical mastectomy is a surgical procedure that removes the entire breast and underarm lymph nodes, often used for inflammatory breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Modified radical mastectomy is a surgical procedure that removes the entire breast, some lymph nodes, and possibly part of the chest wall muscle, used in breast cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LVSI (LYMPHOVASCULAR SPACE INVASION)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pathological finding indicating the presence of cancer cells in the small blood or lymphatic vessels, which influences treatment decisions for cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRONIC LYMPHOCYTIC LEUKEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia (CLL) is a type of cancer that affects white blood cells, specifically B cells, and is the central topic of the text, with various tests and biomarkers discussed for diagnosis and prognosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chronic lymphocytic leukemia is a cancer of white blood cells in the bone marrow that can weaken the immune system, increasing the risk of squamous cell skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chronic lymphocytic leukemia is a type of blood cancer that increases the risk of anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTATE HEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prostate health refers to the overall condition of the prostate, assessed through PSA tests, exams, and imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 5: CHONDROSARCOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 5 discusses chondrosarcoma treatment, which is usually surgery to remove the tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT RESULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment results refer to expected outcomes, which are better for HPV-linked cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiology is a medical field using imaging techniques like x-rays and scans for diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELAPSE IN THE EYE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Relapse in the eye is the return of primary CNS lymphoma in the eye after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL ONCOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medical oncology is a specialty that uses biomarker testing to guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECURRENT CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Recurrent cancer is cancer that returns after initial treatment, for which targeted therapy and immunotherapy may be options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUMPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lumps are abnormal masses in the breast that require diagnostic evaluation to determine if cancerous."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUESTION DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Question Documentation is writing down questions in the binder for appointments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVOLVED-SITE RADIATION THERAPY (ISRT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Involved-site radiation therapy is a treatment option that may be added for localized MGZL disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer treatment using external radiation beams to target cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"External Beam Radiation Therapy (EBRT) is a type of radiation therapy that uses a machine to direct high-energy beams at the tumor from outside the body, typically given in 5 sessions per week for 5-6 weeks."&lt;SEP&gt;"External beam radiation therapy (EBRT) is a type of radiation treatment that uses a machine called a linear accelerator to aim radiation at the whole breast and lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"External beam radiation therapy (EBRT) uses high-energy waves to kill cancer cells, delivered in small doses called fractions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EARLY-STAGE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer that is confined to the cervix or has minimal spread, often treated with surgery alone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Early-stage cancer refers to cervical cancer that has not spread far, often treated with surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Early-stage cervical cancer refers to cancers confined to the cervix (stage 1) or spread to the upper vagina (stage 2A). Treatment often involves surgery, such as hysterectomy or fertility-sparing procedures, with possible adjuvant radiation or chemoradiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Early-stage esophageal cancer is contained within the esophagus, with a small tumor (2 cm or less) and no lymph node involvement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTIPLE MYELOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Multiple myeloma is a type of blood cancer that increases the risk of anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Multiple myeloma is a type of cancer that is excluded from the most common bone cancers list, but is referenced in NCCN guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Multiple myeloma is a type of cancer that is excluded from the most common bone cancers list."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTHY BONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Healthy bone absorbs less tracer than damaged bone, helping to differentiate normal from abnormal areas in bone scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 6: CHORDOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 6 discusses chordoma treatment, with options including surgery or radiation therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT DECISIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment decisions are influenced by p16 testing results and HPV status."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetics is the study of genes and heredity, relevant to cancer risk and treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FATAL OUTCOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatal outcome refers to the possibility that primary CNS lymphoma is fatal for some patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL ONCOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgical oncology may involve biopsy for testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAST-GROWING CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fast-growing cells, such as those in the intestines, mouth, and blood, are particularly affected by chemotherapy, leading to side effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGIONAL NODAL IRRADIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Regional nodal irradiation (RNI) is a type of radiation therapy targeting lymph nodes in the chest wall, infraclavicular, supraclavicular, or axillary regions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCALLY ADVANCED CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer that has grown beyond the cervix but has not spread to distant organs, typically treated with chemoradiation and brachytherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Locally advanced cancer refers to cervical cancer that has spread locally, often treated with chemoradiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Locally advanced cancer refers to rectal cancer that has grown deeply into surrounding tissues but has not spread to distant organs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Locally advanced cervical cancer typically refers to cancers that have spread beyond the cervix to nearby tissues or lymph nodes. Treatment usually involves chemoradiation, combining external beam radiation therapy (EBRT) with platinum chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV18&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV18 is a high-risk strain of HPV associated with cervical cancer and included in some vaccines."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV18 is a high-risk strain of HPV that can cause anal cancer and other related cancers, similar to HPV16."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV18 is a strain of HPV that can cause throat cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bodily fluid used for hereditary gene testing and where blood may appear as a biopsy complication."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urine is a bodily fluid that can contain blood or other indicators of urinary tract issues, and is used in diagnostic tests and genetic testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urine is bodily fluid through which contrast material is excreted after imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urine is the bodily fluid through which contrast agents and tracers are flushed out after imaging procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urine is the bodily fluid through which contrast material is excreted after imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urine is the liquid waste produced by the kidneys and stored in the bladder before being excreted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urine is the waste product formed by the kidneys from filtered blood, containing excess water and waste substances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 7: EWING SARCOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 7 discusses Ewing sarcoma treatment options, which begin with systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURROGATE MARKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surrogate marker is a substitute indicator, like p16 for HPV infection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatments refer to medical interventions for cancer, including surgery, chemotherapy, and radiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hope is a positive outlook for patients with primary CNS lymphoma, supported by improved detection methods and new therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIATION ONCOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiation oncology is a cancer treatment modality, not directly related to biomarker testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC SORENESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic soreness is a side effect of brachytherapy, affecting the pelvic area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARDIOTOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cardiotoxicity is heart damage that can occur from certain breast cancer treatments, such as HER2-targeted therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRON DEFICIENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iron deficiency is a condition of low iron levels in the body, monitored and treated with supplements."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREAT VESSELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Great vessels are large blood vessels, such as the aorta, that can be involved in tumor spread (T4 in spine, T4b in pelvis)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INHIBIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inhibin is a tumor marker (typically inhibin A and B) found in higher amounts in LCOCs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAUTERINE DEVICE (IUD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intrauterine Device (IUD) is a form of birth control that may be recommended or not, depending on the patient's situation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RISK FACTORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Characteristics such as tumor size, LVSI, and margin status that influence whether additional treatment like EBRT is recommended after surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk Factors are conditions or behaviors that increase the likelihood of developing cancer, such as HPV infection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk factors are conditions or behaviors that increase the likelihood of developing a disease, such as adrenal tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk factors for basal cell skin cancer include UV light exposure, fair skin, red or blond hair, light eye color, age, history of skin cancer, radiation therapy, and immune suppression. These factors increase the chance of developing the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL INTRAEPITHELIAL NEOPLASIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anal intraepithelial neoplasia (AIN) is a pre-cancerous condition in the anus, synonymous with anal dysplasia, and can be graded as low or high grade."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRONIC LYMPHOCYTIC LEUKEMIA (CLL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia (CLL) is a type of cancer that affects blood and bone marrow, characterized by changes in bone marrow and abnormal B cells. It is not currently curable but can be managed with treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) is a type of blood cancer that grows slowly, affecting lymphocytes, and may not require treatment for years."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 8: GIANT CELL TUMOR OF BONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 8 discusses GCTB treatment options, noting that GCTB is usually not cancer but requires aggressive treatment to prevent bone damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABNORMAL TISSUE GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal tissue growth, or warts, can result from HPV infection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROCEDURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Procedures are medical actions like biopsies or surgeries performed for cancer diagnosis or treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMPROVED DETECTION METHODS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Improved detection methods have shortened the time to diagnosis and led to better outcomes for primary CNS lymphoma patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVOCACY ORGANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Advocacy organization may provide resources for genetic testing and support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFICULTY URINATING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Difficulty urinating is a side effect of brachytherapy, causing pain or discomfort during urination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRECANCEROUS CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal cells that may become cancerous, detected in urine cytology tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOMEOPATHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Homeopathy is a complementary therapy using highly diluted substances to stimulate healing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEOADJUVANT THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neoadjuvant therapy is chemotherapy given before surgery to shrink tumors, as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neoadjuvant therapy is systemic drug treatment given before surgery to shrink the tumor or reduce cancer burden."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neoadjuvant therapy is treatment given before surgery to shrink tumors, making them easier to remove."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 0 ANAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 0 anal cancer refers to the earliest stage where abnormal cells are present but have not spread, often synonymous with high-grade anal dysplasia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL LYMPHOCYTIC LYMPHOMA (SLL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Small Lymphocytic Lymphoma (SLL) is the same cancer as CLL, but the abnormal cells are primarily found in lymph nodes and spleen rather than blood and bone marrow. It is treated the same as CLL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 9: OSTEOSARCOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 9 discusses osteosarcoma treatment options, noting that osteosarcoma is the more common type of bone cancer and treatment is a combination of therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR FEATURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor features are specific characteristics of HPV-positive throat cancer that can be targeted in treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZIPPER POCKET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zipper Pocket is a feature of a binder to hold small items like pens and cards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zipper pocket is a feature of a medical binder for storing small items like pens and insurance cards."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEAKENED IMMUNE SYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weakened immune systems are a condition in patients that may affect the prognosis and treatment of primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Food and Drug Administration regulates tests and therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OUTCOMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Outcomes are the results of cancer care, which can be improved by following expert recommendations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPEECH AND SWALLOWING EVALUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Speech and swallowing evaluation assesses functional impact of cancer and treatment on these abilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL PAP SMEAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anal Pap Smear is a screening test to detect abnormal cells in the anus, often used for high-risk individuals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARMPITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The armpits are parts of the body where high numbers of lymph nodes are found."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADJUVANT THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adjuvant therapy is systemic drug treatment given after surgery to eliminate remaining cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjuvant therapy is treatment given after primary surgery to reduce the risk of cancer recurrence, such as chemotherapy or hormone therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Therapy given after primary treatment to lower the risk of cancer recurrence, often using radiation after surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSVAGINAL ULTRASOUND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transvaginal ultrasound is a type of ultrasound where a probe is inserted into the vagina to get clearer images of the ovaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transvaginal ultrasound is an imaging test using sound waves to create pictures of the cervix and nearby areas, performed by inserting a probe into the vagina."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENITAL WARTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genital warts are abnormal skin growths caused by certain HPV strains, which can appear on the anus or genitals and may be mistaken for other growths."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The lymph (or lymphatic) system is a network that plays a key role in fighting infections, containing many B cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lymph system includes tonsils, thymus, spleen, lymph vessels, and lymph nodes. It plays a key role in fighting infections and is involved in CLL and SLL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 10: OTHER RESOURCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 10 provides information on patient advocacy groups and where to get help."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Human cells have 23 pairs of chromosomes, totaling 46, where genes like p16 are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human cells normally contain 23 pairs of chromosomes for a total of 46 chromosomes, which are analyzed in a karyotype."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CALENDAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Calendar is a tool for scheduling appointments and tracking treatment dates, often kept in a medical binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Calendar is a tool used to track appointments and treatment schedules, often kept in a medical binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERAPIES SPECIFICALLY DESIGNED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Therapies specifically designed to treat primary CNS lymphoma are being studied in clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTERS FOR DISEASE CONTROL AND PREVENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Centers for Disease Control and Prevention provides public health information on cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INCREASED VAGINAL DISCHARGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Increased vaginal discharge is a side effect of brachytherapy, affecting vaginal secretions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENTIATED HIGH-GRADE CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Differentiated high-grade carcinoma is a specific type of thyroid cancer characterized by aggressive features, requiring intensive monitoring and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Differentiated high-grade carcinoma is a type of thyroid tumor that, if present, indicates RAI therapy is usually recommended."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH CHECKUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health checkups are routine medical examinations that may include breast cancer screening."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health checkups are routine medical visits where breast cancer screening may be discussed or performed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOTE SECTION ADDITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Note Section Addition is adding a dedicated area for notes in the binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROID NODULES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thyroid nodules are small, often round areas of abnormal growth within the thyroid gland, most of which are benign and asymptomatic."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2-TARGETED THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HER2-targeted therapy includes antibodies, inhibitors, and conjugates like trastuzumab and pertuzumab, used to treat cancers with HER2 expression."&lt;SEP&gt;"HER2-targeted therapy is a treatment that targets HER2-positive cancer cells, mentioned in treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"HER2-targeted therapy is a treatment that targets HER2-positive cancer cells, part of treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"HER2-targeted therapy is drug therapy that treats HER2-positive breast cancer by targeting the HER2 protein, often used with chemotherapy or endocrine therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREGNANCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition that must be considered during cancer treatment to avoid harm to a developing baby."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy is a biological state that may be affected by cancer treatment, requiring careful planning with a doctor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy is a condition that cancer patients may plan for, requiring discussion with care team about fertility and treatment impacts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy is a condition that may be planned by patients, and its planning should be discussed with the care team before treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy is a condition that requires careful management during cancer treatment to avoid harm to the developing baby."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy is a condition that requires careful planning during cancer treatment to avoid harm to the developing baby."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy is a condition that should be avoided during cancer treatment due to potential harm to the fetus and mother."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy is a condition where ultrasound is commonly used, as mentioned in the text for comparison."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy is a special consideration in CLL testing and treatment, as it may affect the approach to care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy is a state of carrying a developing baby, and the text discusses precautions and planning during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy is the state of carrying a developing fetus, which may be impacted by cancer treatments and fertility preservation options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL SKIN TAGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anal skin tags are benign growths near the anus that can be mistaken for cancerous lesions, sometimes found during examinations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RICHTER TRANSFORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Richter transformation is a condition described in Chapter 5, which may occur in CLL patients and requires reading that chapter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Richter transformation is a medical condition described in Chapter 5 of the text, indicating a progression or complication of lymphoma that requires specific attention."&lt;SEP&gt;"Richter transformation is a rare complication of CLL that can lead to more aggressive cancers such as diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) or Hodgkin lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC CANCER RISK TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic cancer risk testing assesses inherited genetic mutations that may increase the risk of developing breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic cancer risk testing assesses inherited mutations that increase the risk of developing breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic cancer risk testing is a method using blood or saliva to identify inherited germline mutations that may increase cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic cancer risk testing is a test to identify inherited mutations that increase cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testing for inherited genetic mutations that increase the risk of developing cancer, often based on family history."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Expression refers to the presence of p16 protein, detected through biomarker testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSURANCE CARDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insurance Cards are documents used for billing and coverage, often kept in a medical binder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance Cards are kept in a binder for reference."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance cards are identification for health coverage, stored in medical binders for access."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
