      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHARMACEUTICAL COMPANY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pharmaceutical Company is an entity that develops and tests new cancer drugs, often sponsoring clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pharmaceutical company develops targeted therapies and checkpoint inhibitors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PULMONOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pulmonologist is a board-certified doctor who specializes in lung diseases, including the diagnosis and treatment of conditions such as lung nodules and lung cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pulmonologist is a doctor who is an expert in lung diseases and part of the care team for lung nodules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pulmonologist is a specialist in lung diseases who may be involved in diagnosing and treating SCLC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CDK4/6 INHIBITORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CDK4/6 inhibitors are drugs that block cyclin-dependent kinases to slow cancer cell growth, used with endocrine therapy for hormone receptor-positive, HER2-negative breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY-SPARING TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility-sparing treatment includes procedures like trachelectomy, aimed at preserving fertility in early-stage cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility-sparing treatment is a cancer treatment approach that aims to preserve the ability to become pregnant, typically an option for small, early-stage cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility-sparing treatment is a surgical approach for early-stage cervical cancer that preserves the uterus, requiring MRI follow-up."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility-sparing treatment refers to surgical approaches for early-stage cervical cancer that preserve the uterus and ovaries, allowing for future natural pregnancy. It is an option for certain stage 1 cancers without high-risk features."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment options for cervical cancer that preserve fertility, applicable when cancer is only in the cervix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACETIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acetic acid is a liquid applied to anal canal tissue during high-resolution anoscopy to make abnormal cells appear differently under magnification."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFUSE LARGE B-CELL LYMPHOMA (DLBCL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DLBCL is a fast-growing type of cancer that NLPHL can transform into in rare cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) is a more aggressive cancer that can develop as a result of Richter transformation in CLL patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) is an aggressive lymphoma that FL can transform into, with tumors commonly found in lymph nodes, spleen, liver, bone marrow, or other tissues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHORDOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chordoma is a bone cancer that starts in notochordal cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chordoma is a type of bone cancer that can be treated with surgery or radiation therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chordoma starts in notochordal cells that form the spine and vertebrae, usually found in the lower spinal column or base of the skull."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
