      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bright spots on PET scans indicate areas of high activity, potentially cancer or other conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEXT CHAPTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Next chapters in the book explain tests needed to diagnose the disease, treatment options, and what happens after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSURANCE COMPANY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insurance Company is an entity that provides coverage for medical treatments, influencing patient decisions on cost and care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance company is an entity that provides health coverage and may have rules about second opinions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance company is an entity that provides health coverage and processes claims for medical expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance company may cover or deny genetic testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THORACIC SURGEON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A thoracic surgeon is a board-certified doctor who specializes in operations within the chest, including surgical procedures for lung cancer and other thoracic conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thoracic surgeon is a doctor who is an expert in operations within the chest, involved in surgical treatment of lung cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thoracic surgeon is a specialist who performs surgical procedures on the chest, including lung cancer removal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BETA-2 MICROGLOBULIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beta-2 microglobulin is a small protein found on most cells, released into the blood by B cells, and high levels may suggest CLL is growing or harder to treat."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MYELOID GROWTH FACTORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Myeloid growth factors (MGFs) are treatments that increase white blood cell counts to prevent infections during chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid growth factors are supportive agents that help boost white blood cell counts during chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid growth factors are supportive care agents that help boost white blood cell counts during chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVARIAN TRANSPOSITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ovarian transposition is a procedure that moves ovaries and fallopian tubes out of the radiation beam range to protect fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovarian transposition is a surgery to move ovaries out of the radiation field, potentially preserving ovarian function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovarian transposition is a surgical procedure (oophoropexy) that moves one or both ovaries out of the range of radiation therapy to preserve fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovarian transposition is a surgical procedure that moves ovaries out of the radiation field to protect them during rectal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANOSCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An anoscope is a short, hollow tool inserted into the anus during high-resolution anoscopy to allow viewing of the anal canal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEF1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LEF1 is a protein found on CLL cells, used to distinguish CLL from other types of lymphoma like mantle cell lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GIANT CELL TUMOR OF BONE (GCTB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Giant cell tumor of bone (GCTB) is usually not cancer but requires aggressive treatment to prevent bone damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Giant cell tumor of bone is an overgrowth of cells in the metaphysis, extending into the epiphysis area of the bone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPUTER TECHNOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Computer technology combines x-ray images in CT scans to form detailed pictures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Computer technology is used in CT scans to combine multiple x-ray images into detailed pictures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TONSIL LYMPHOID TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tonsil lymphoid tissue is part of the immune system that can appear bright on PET scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTS NEEDED TO DIAGNOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tests needed to diagnose primary CNS lymphoma include neurological exams, imaging, biopsies, blood tests, and eye exams."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESEARCH INSTITUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Research Institution is an organization that conducts studies to advance cancer treatment and understanding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Research institution conducts studies on biomarkers and treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Research institution is an organization that conducts studies to improve cancer diagnosis and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNG NODULE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A lung nodule is a small mass of tissue in the lung. Many people have lung nodules, and most are not cancer. Imaging is used to assess whether a nodule is cancerous."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung nodule is a small mass of tissue in the lungs that may be benign or cancerous, requiring expert evaluation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER RECURRENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Recurrence is the return of cancer after treatment, which patients need to monitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UPPER CHEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The upper chest is the location of the thymus, a small organ where lymphocytes develop into T cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERIMUSCULAR FIBROUS TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Perimuscular fibrous tissue is a type of connective tissue that surrounds muscle in the bile ducts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOXORUBICIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Doxorubicin (Adriamycin) is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by interfering with DNA replication."&lt;SEP&gt;"Doxorubicin is a chemotherapy drug included in the ddMVAC combination for bladder cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Doxorubicin is an anthracycline chemotherapy drug used to treat breast cancer, often given as an infusion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTERNAL BEAM RADIATION THERAPY (EBRT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of radiation therapy where a beam is directed at the tumor from a machine, using electrons for superficial tumors and photons for deeper ones."&lt;SEP&gt;"EBRT is a type of radiation therapy that damages ovaries, potentially affecting fertility, and is used in cervical cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"EBRT is a type of radiation therapy that delivers high-energy beams from outside the body to target cancer cells. It is used alone or with chemotherapy (chemoradiation) for cervical cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"EBRT is a type of radiation therapy where a large machine aims radiation at the tumor area, commonly used for bladder cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"EBRT is a type of radiation therapy where radiation is delivered from outside the body using a large machine, with IMRT being a preferred form."&lt;SEP&gt;"External beam radiation therapy (EBRT) uses high-energy x-rays or particles from a machine outside the body to destroy cancer cells, used for certain thyroid cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"External beam radiation therapy is a treatment for aggressive, recurrent, or metastatic thyroid cancers that cannot be surgically removed."&lt;SEP&gt;"External beam radiation therapy is a type of radiation treatment for rectal cancer that can affect nearby organs like the ovaries."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUMBING GEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Numbing gel is applied to the anal area before high-resolution anoscopy to minimize discomfort during the procedure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANTLE CELL LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mantle cell lymphoma is a type of lymphoma that does not have CD200 and LEF1 proteins, helping to differentiate it from CLL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTEOSARCOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osteosarcoma is a type of bone cancer that starts in cells commonly found in rapidly growing areas of bone near growth plates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Osteosarcoma is the more common type of bone cancer, treated with a combination of therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAGNETS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Magnets are powerful components of MRI machines that help create detailed images of the body's internal structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Magnets are powerful components of MRI machines that help create images."&lt;SEP&gt;"Magnets are powerful components of MRI machines used to generate images."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-ENERGY SOUND WAVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-energy sound waves are used in ultrasound to create images of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENT TREATMENT OPTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Different treatment options for primary CNS lymphoma include chemotherapy, radiation therapy, stem cell transplant, and clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University may be involved in research and education on cancer genetics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radon is a cancer-causing agent that increases the risk of lung cancer, especially in people who smoke. It is a radioactive gas that can accumulate in buildings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIFTP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NIFTP (noninvasive follicular thyroid neoplasm with papillary-like nuclear features) is a low-risk, noninvasive thyroid tumor, previously known as encapsulated follicular variant of papillary thyroid cancer, requiring no further treatment after surgical removal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BINDER BRINGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Binder Bringing is taking the medical binder to appointments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOCETAXEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Docetaxel (Taxotere) is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by inhibiting cell division."&lt;SEP&gt;"Docetaxel is a chemotherapy drug used as part of the modified DCF regimen for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Docetaxel is a chemotherapy drug used in the modified DCF regimen for metastatic anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Docetaxel is a taxane chemotherapy drug used in breast cancer treatment, often given as an infusion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Docetaxel is a taxane chemotherapy drug used in ovarian cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EGG FREEZING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Egg freezing is a fertility preservation method involving the removal, freezing, and storage of unfertilized eggs for future use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Egg freezing is a fertility preservation method that involves removing, freezing, and storing unfertilized eggs for later use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Egg freezing, also known as oocyte preservation, is a process where unfertilized eggs are removed, frozen, and stored for later use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Egg freezing, or oocyte cryopreservation, is a method of preserving fertility by removing, freezing, and storing unfertilized eggs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUTOIMMUNE DISORDERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Autoimmune disorders are risk factors for anal cancer, potentially due to chronic inflammation or immune dysregulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Autoimmune disorders, such as Crohn's disease, can weaken the immune system and increase the risk of anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATCH AND WAIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Watch and wait is a period of monitoring for CLL patients where treatment is not immediately started but the condition is closely observed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Watch and wait is a stage where patients don’t start treatment aside from those that make them feel better, as discussed in Chapter 3."&lt;SEP&gt;"Watch and wait is a strategy after chemoradiation where no immediate treatment is given, but monitoring continues for signs of cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNCTIONAL ASSESSMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Functional assessment is an evaluation of a patient's ability to manage tasks and activities used in daily life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIATION EXPOSURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiation exposure is avoided in MRI scans, unlike CT scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation exposure, such as from past head or neck treatment or environmental catastrophic events, is a risk factor for thyroid cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SONOGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sonogram is an image produced by ultrasound, similar to those used in pregnancy, referenced in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sonogram is an imaging technique similar to ultrasound, used in pregnancy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHAT TREATMENT OPTIONS DO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"What treatment options do refers to the effects of treatments on primary CNS lymphoma, such as slowing growth and reducing symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOVERNMENT AGENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Government agency funds research and sets health policies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROID-STIMULATING HORMONE (TSH)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) is a hormone produced by the pituitary gland that regulates thyroid function. Its levels are measured in blood tests to monitor thyroid cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) is a hormone produced by the pituitary gland that regulates thyroid hormone production; its level is monitored to adjust thyroid hormone replacement therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) is a hormone that regulates thyroid function; levothyroxine therapy keeps TSH levels low or normal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thyroid-stimulating hormone is a hormone produced by the pituitary gland that controls thyroid hormone production, used in blood tests to assess thyroid function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMARKER AND GENETIC CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biomarker and genetic changes are tests that identify specific molecular alterations in CBCL cells, guiding treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAPECITABINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemotherapy drug used in combination with Mitomycin for perianal cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Capecitabine is a chemotherapy drug used in regimens like mitomycin and capecitabine, or as an alternative to 5-FU in chemoradiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Capecitabine is an antimetabolite chemotherapy drug used for breast cancer, available as an oral pill."&lt;SEP&gt;"Capecitabine is an oral chemotherapy agent used as an alternative to 5-FU in chemoradiation for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Capecitabine is an oral chemotherapy drug taken twice daily on radiation days for 5.5 to 6 weeks, used in combination with mitomycin for anal cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Capecitabine is an oral chemotherapy drug used in regimens for colon cancer, often after colectomy for certain stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Capecitabine is an oral chemotherapy drug used with radiation for anal cancer, often combined with mitomycin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURROGACY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surrogacy involves a surrogate volunteer carrying a pregnancy for individuals with frozen embryos or eggs, often a relative or friend."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADOLESCENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adolescents are a demographic for whom the HPV vaccine is routinely recommended, as they are likely unexposed to HPV."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adolescents are young patients for whom fertility preservation information is available via NCCN."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINIMAL RESIDUAL DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Minimal residual disease is a condition where treatment results in mostly healthy blood cells, allowing a full life, though it is not a cure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKELETAL SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skeletal system is the framework of bones in the body, examined during a physical exam for bone cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metal in the body can interfere with MRI scans, requiring disclosure to technologists."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metal in the body must be reported before an MRI due to strong magnets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAND-LIKE PROBE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wand-like probe, or transducer, is a device used in ultrasound to emit sound waves."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHICH TREATMENT OPTIONS ARE RIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Which treatment options are right refers to the personalized selection of treatments for individual patients with primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NONPROFIT ORGANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nonprofit organization is a charitable group that offers support, education, and advocacy for cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nonprofit organization provides support and education for cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BERYLLIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beryllium is a cancer-causing agent that increases lung cancer risk, particularly in occupational settings. It is a metal used in aerospace and electronics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHEOCHROMOCYTOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pheochromocytoma is a tumor that begins in the adrenal medulla, characterized by symptoms such as high blood pressure, headache, rapid heartbeat, and sweating. Most are benign, but some can be cancerous."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T3 TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T3 tumor indicates more than 1 tumor in the primary bone site in appendicular skeleton, torso, skull, or face."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAVENOUS (IV) IRON SUPPLEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IV iron supplement is a treatment given when iron levels are low, administered intravenously."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALPHA-FETOPROTEIN (AFP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AFP is a tumor marker found in higher amounts in LCOCs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD TEST RESULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood Test Results are lab reports from tests like CBC, CMP, and LFTs, included in a medical binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRASTUZUMAB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trastuzumab (Herceptin) is a HER2-targeted therapy used in systemic therapy to treat HER2-positive cancers, with biosimilars like Kanjinti and Ogivri."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trastuzumab is a HER2-targeted therapy antibody that blocks HER2 growth signals and is used to treat HER2-positive breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trastuzumab is a targeted therapy used to treat HER2-positive breast cancer by blocking HER2 receptors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADULTS AGED 45 AND UNDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adults aged 45 and under are now eligible for the HPV vaccine, though it is most effective in younger people."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLDER ADULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Older adults are more prone to developing mutations that can cause CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Older adults tend to develop changes or mutations over time that could cause cancer like CLL to form, making age a risk factor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormonal Birth Control is a method that may or may not be recommended, depending on cancer type."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormonal birth control includes methods like IUDs that may be recommended to prevent pregnancy during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormonal birth control is a method of contraception that may or may not be recommended during cancer treatment, requiring doctor consultation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormonal birth control is a method of contraception that may or may not be recommended during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLOSED MRI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A closed MRI has a capsule-like design with the magnet surrounding the patient."&lt;SEP&gt;"A closed MRI is a type of MRI machine with a capsule-like design where the magnet surrounds the patient, providing high-resolution images."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closed MRI is a more common type of imaging device that fully encloses the patient, which may cause discomfort for those with claustrophobia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closed MRI is a more common type of magnetic resonance imaging machine, typically enclosed, which may cause discomfort for patients with claustrophobia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closed MRI is a type of MRI machine with a capsule-like design where the magnet surrounds the patient, creating a small, enclosed space."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closed MRI is a type of MRI machine with a capsule-like design where the magnet surrounds the patient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closed MRI is a type of MRI with a capsule-like design where the magnet surrounds the patient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closed MRI is a type of MRI with a capsule-like design, more common but may cause claustrophobia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DENTAL X-RAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dental x-ray is an imaging test capturing the mouth, including teeth and jaws."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHAT HAPPENS AFTER TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"What happens after treatment refers to the follow-up care and monitoring for patients with primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROFESSIONAL SOCIETY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Professional society like ASCO develops guidelines for biomarker testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CADMIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cadmium is a cancer-causing agent linked to lung cancer, especially in smokers. It is a heavy metal used in batteries and pigments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFUSE SCLEROSING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diffuse sclerosing is a subtype of papillary thyroid cancer characterized by diffuse involvement and a higher risk of spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;17P DELETION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"17p deletion is a biomarker detected by FISH, indicating a missing part of chromosome 17, which is relevant in CLL treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH CARE PROFESSIONAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health care professionals are individuals who diagnose and treat conditions like CLL and gliomas, providing care and guidance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care professionals include doctors and specialists who evaluate and treat patients with anal cancer symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVEROLIMUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Everolimus (Afinitor) is an mTOR inhibitor used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by blocking cell growth signals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Everolimus (Afinitor) is an mTOR inhibitor used to restore effectiveness of endocrine therapy, often with exemestane."&lt;SEP&gt;"Everolimus is an mTOR inhibitor used in breast cancer treatment, often taken with exemestane or other endocrine therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOWEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bowel is an organ near the cervix that can be affected by radiation, and IMRT aims to reduce radiation to it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bowel is an organ that may be examined for signs of cancer spread, using procedures like proctoscopy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B cells are a type of lymphocyte that make antibodies to fight infections and are central to CLL and CBCL."&lt;SEP&gt;"B cells are a type of white blood cell that are part of the immune system. Many B cells are found in the lymph system, and abnormal B cells are characteristic of CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"B cells, or B lymphocytes, are a type of lymphocyte that produce antibodies to fight infections, and abnormal B cells can lead to cutaneous B-cell lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"B cells, or B lymphocytes, are a type of white blood cell made in bone marrow that help fight infections; in CLL, abnormal B cells grow out of control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAUTERINE DEVICES (IUDS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A form of hormonal birth control that may be recommended to prevent pregnancy during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intrauterine devices (IUDs) are a form of birth control mentioned as an option during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intrauterine devices (IUDs) are a form of contraception that may be an option during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intrauterine devices (IUDs) are a type of birth control that may be an option during cancer treatment, as discussed with a doctor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intrauterine devices (IUDs) are hormonal birth control options that may be recommended during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPEN MRI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An open MRI has a magnetic top and bottom, allowing openings on each end."&lt;SEP&gt;"An open MRI is a type of MRI machine with magnets above and below, offering a more open space for patients who may feel claustrophobic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Open MRI is a type of MRI machine with a magnetic top and bottom, allowing for an opening on each end."&lt;SEP&gt;"Open MRI is a type of MRI machine with a magnetic top and bottom, allowing openings on each end for patients with claustrophobia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Open MRI is a type of MRI with a magnetic top and bottom, allowing openings on each end."&lt;SEP&gt;"Open MRI is a type of MRI with a magnetic top and bottom, offering more space for patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Open MRI is a type of imaging device with a magnetic top and bottom, allowing openings on each end, designed to accommodate patients with claustrophobia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Open MRI is a type of magnetic resonance imaging machine with a magnetic top and bottom, allowing openings on each end, designed to accommodate patients with claustrophobia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEETH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Structures in the mouth that may be impacted by head and neck cancer treatment, requiring dental care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Teeth are oral structures that can be affected by head and neck cancer treatment, requiring dental checkups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Teeth are part of the oral cavity that can be affected by head and neck cancer treatment, requiring dental care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Teeth are structures in the mouth imaged by panoramic dental x-rays."&lt;SEP&gt;"Teeth are structures in the mouth imaged in panoramic dental x-rays."&lt;SEP&gt;"Teeth are structures in the mouth that aid in chewing and are held in place by gums and alveolar ridges."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THOUGHTS ON NEXT STEPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thoughts on next steps are recommendations for patients and caregivers after a primary CNS lymphoma diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN SOCIETY OF CLINICAL ONCOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"American Society of Clinical Oncology is a professional society that issues guidelines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHROMIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chromium is a cancer-causing agent that increases lung cancer risk, particularly in industrial workers. It is a metal used in stainless steel and plating."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LATE EFFECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Late Effects are long-term side effects of cancer treatment that may appear months or years later."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACK OF THE THROAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The back of the throat is where the tonsils, small masses of lymph tissue, are located."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diet refers to eating habits, with high-fat foods like meat and dairy linked to increased prostate cancer risk, while fruits and vegetables may lower risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STANDARD ANOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Standard anoscopy is a procedure similar to high-resolution anoscopy but without the use of a colposcope, and may be less effective at identifying abnormalities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABEMACICLIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abemaciclib (Verzenio) is a CDK4/6 inhibitor used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by blocking cell cycle progression."&lt;SEP&gt;"Abemaciclib is a CDK4/6 inhibitor used with endocrine therapy for hormone receptor-positive, HER2-negative breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
