    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTING FOR ALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Testing for ALL is a chapter that provides an overview of diagnostic tests for ALL, including blood tests, bone marrow tests, imaging, and genetic testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALBOCICLIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Palbociclib (Ibrance) is a CDK4/6 inhibitor used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by blocking cell cycle progression."&lt;SEP&gt;"Palbociclib is a CDK4/6 inhibitor used with endocrine therapy for hormone receptor-positive, HER2-negative breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYSTOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A procedure under anesthesia to look for signs of cancer in the bladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"A procedure using a cystoscope to look inside the urethra and bladder for signs of cancer, potentially including biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cystoscopy is a medical procedure to examine the inside of the urethra and bladder for signs of cancer, using a cystoscope to view and potentially biopsy suspicious areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cystoscopy is a procedure that uses a scope to examine the inside of the bladder, essential for diagnosing and staging bladder cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cystoscopy is a procedure that uses a viewing device inserted through the urethra to examine the inside of the bladder for cancer or other abnormalities, often combined with a pyelogram for detailed imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cystoscopy is a procedure using a cystoscope to see inside the bladder and urinary tract, potentially with tissue sampling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cystoscopy is a test that looks inside the bladder to diagnose bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anemia is a condition of low red blood cells, which can occur in CLL patients and may indicate a need for treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
