      <data key="d1">"Muscle (muscularis) is a type of soft tissue found in the bile duct walls."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BECKWITH-WIEDEMANN SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome is a hereditary condition that can increase the risk of developing adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-ALL TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This chapter discusses treatment options for T-ALL, including clinical trials and chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREEN TEA EXTRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Green tea extract is an herbal supplement that may interact with systemic therapies, potentially affecting drug efficacy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARAMETRIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Parametrium is the tissue next to the cervix that may be checked for cancer spread via MRI."&lt;SEP&gt;"The parametrium is the fat and connective tissue surrounding the cervix and uterus, and its involvement defines stage 2B cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The parametrium is the fat and connective tissue that surrounds the uterus and cervix, connecting them to the pelvis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The parametrium is the tissue around the cervix, involvement of which indicates more advanced cervical cancer requiring specialized brachytherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PILLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pills are a treatment option for CLL, taken daily or in combination with IV infusions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNDERARM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Area of the body examined for enlarged lymph nodes during a physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underarm is a body area where lymph nodes are felt for enlargement during a physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underarm is a body part where lymph nodes are felt for enlargement during a physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underarm is a location where lymph nodes are checked for enlargement during physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underarm is a part of the body where lymph nodes can be felt for enlargement, as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underarm is an area checked for enlarged lymph nodes during physical exam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EARLY-STAGE PROSTATE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Early-stage prostate cancer has not spread beyond the prostate and is also called localized prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Early-stage prostate cancer refers to cancer confined to the prostate, with treatment options differing from advanced stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Early-stage prostate cancer, also called localized prostate cancer, has not spread beyond the prostate and usually grows slowly."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRACTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Extractions are dental procedures for removing teeth, planned with panoramic x-rays."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extractions are dental procedures to remove teeth, which may be planned using panoramic dental x-rays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RARE AND AGGRESSIVE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rare and aggressive cancer describes primary CNS lymphoma, which most often affects the brain."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESEARCH LABORATORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Research laboratory develops new testing methods."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AIR POLLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Air pollution, including fine particulates, ozone, nitrogen oxides, and sulfur dioxide, is a cancer-causing agent that increases lung cancer risk, especially in smokers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATHOLOGIC EXAMINATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pathologic examination involves testing removed tissue or biopsies to determine cancer type, invasiveness, and presence of high-risk features, guiding further treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY PRESERVATION ACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility Preservation Action is taking steps like egg or sperm freezing before treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFANT ALL TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This chapter discusses treatment for infant ALL, which is different from other age groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ST. JOHN’S WORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"St. John’s Wort is an herbal supplement that may interact with systemic therapies, potentially affecting drug efficacy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTRAST AGENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A contrast agent is injected into the bloodstream before a CT scan to make areas of cancer easier to see."&lt;SEP&gt;"A contrast agent, also called contrast dye, is a substance injected into the bloodstream to highlight areas in organs, blood vessels, or tissues during imaging tests like MRI."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast agent is a chemical that highlights body tissues for a CT scanner, given through a needle, and may not be safe for people with allergies or chronic kidney disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast agent is a substance injected into the bloodstream to make blood vessels, organs, and tissues stand out in imaging tests like MRI."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast agent is a substance used in imaging tests like CT and MRI to make pictures clearer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast agent is a substance used in imaging tests like CT or MRI to make pictures clearer, which may cause side effects like flushing or hives."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cure for primary CNS lymphoma is rare but possible if diagnosed early and treated immediately, especially in younger, healthier patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cure refers to the complete elimination of CLL, which is currently not possible, but effective treatment can manage the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ears are examined during a physical exam to check for abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ears are examined during physical exam to check for hearing issues or infections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ears are parts of the body where cartilage provides structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organs examined during a physical exam to assess hearing and overall health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVANCED-STAGE PROSTATE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Advanced-stage prostate cancer has spread beyond the prostate, requiring more aggressive treatments like hormone therapy and chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advanced-stage prostate cancer has spread outside the prostate to other areas, including lymph nodes, bones, liver, lungs, and other organs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advanced-stage prostate cancer is a life-long disease where cancer has spread outside the prostate, requiring ongoing management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advanced-stage prostate cancer, also called metastatic prostate cancer, has spread beyond the prostate to other areas such as lymph nodes, bones, liver, or lungs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMPLANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Implants are dental devices placed in the jaw, planned with panoramic x-rays."&lt;SEP&gt;"Implants are dental prosthetics placed in the jaw, which may be planned using panoramic dental x-rays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPREAD TO OTHER AREAS IN THE NERVOUS SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spread to other areas in the nervous system is a characteristic of primary CNS lymphoma, though it rarely spreads to other body areas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACADEMIC MEDICAL CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Academic Medical Center is a hospital affiliated with a university, often offering cutting-edge treatments and clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Academic medical center combines research and patient care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COWDEN SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cowden syndrome, also known as PTEN hamartoma tumor syndrome, is an inherited condition that can cause follicular thyroid cancer and other health issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC BREAST CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic breast cancer is stage 4 cancer that has spread to distant sites, requiring advanced treatment approaches."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTHER RESOURCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This chapter provides information on patient advocacy groups and where to get help for ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIOXIDANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antioxidants are supplements that may interact with systemic therapies, potentially affecting drug efficacy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Probe is an instrument used in transvaginal ultrasound, inserted into the vagina to create images of the cervix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood test involves drawing blood to analyze components like PSA and other biomarkers for disease detection."&lt;SEP&gt;"A blood test is used to confirm CLL by providing a small sample of blood for laboratory analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood Test is a laboratory test to monitor health markers during and after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nose is a body part through which scopes are passed in some procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nose is a body part."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nose is a part of the body where cartilage provides structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nose is an anatomical site where a scope may be inserted for throat examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nose is an entry point for scopes in fiberoptic laryngoscopy and nasopharyngolaryngoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nose is examined during a physical exam to check for abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nose is examined during physical exam to check for nasal issues related to NPC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organ examined during a physical exam to assess respiratory and olfactory health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC PROSTATE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic prostate cancer is an advanced-stage form of prostate cancer that has spread outside the prostate to other areas such as lymph nodes, bones, or organs like the liver or lungs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic prostate cancer is cancer that has spread beyond the prostate to distant parts of the body, such as bones, liver, or lungs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic prostate cancer is cancer that spreads outside the prostate to other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic prostate cancer is prostate cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, and may be treated with targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGIONAL SQUAMOUS CELL SKIN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Regional squamous cell skin cancer is a form of the disease that has spread to nearby lymph nodes, often treated with surgery and radiation therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell skin cancer that has spread to lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPREAD TO OTHER AREAS OF THE BODY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spread to other areas of the body is rare for primary CNS lymphoma, which typically remains within the nervous system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE (N)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph Node (N) is a component of the TNM staging system, indicating whether cancer has spread to regional lymph nodes, with categories from N0 to N3, including N1mi for micrometastases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNG CANCER SCREENING BASICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lung cancer screening basics refer to the fundamental principles and procedures for detecting lung cancer early in high-risk individuals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T0 TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T0 tumor indicates no tumor can be found."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRUISES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bruises are discolorations from bleeding under the skin, a symptom of coagulopathy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HE4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HE4 is a tumor marker found in higher amounts in LCOCs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROCEDURES RECORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Procedures Records are documents on medical procedures performed, included in a medical binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiation is a cancer treatment using high-energy rays to destroy cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation is a form of energy used in imaging tests like panoramic dental x-rays and CT scans, with small doses used for diagnostic purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation is a treatment modality using high-energy particles or waves to destroy cancer cells, often given in multiple sessions over days to weeks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation is a type of therapy used to treat high-grade gliomas (grades 3 and 4) after surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation is emitted by radiotracers in bone scans, used for imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation is energy emitted in the form of waves or particles. CT scans use radiation, while MRI does not."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation is energy used in imaging and treatment, with small doses in x-rays, but can damage cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation is high-energy radiation from x-rays, gamma rays, protons, and other sources used in radiation therapy to kill cancer cells and shrink tumors. It is also used to treat pain caused by cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation is high-energy waves used in therapy to kill cancer cells, delivered via machines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOUND WAVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sound waves are high-energy waves used in ultrasound to create images of the inside of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sound waves are used in ultrasound imaging to create pictures of areas inside the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN PATIENT GUIDES FOR CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer is a resource providing patient-friendly cancer information."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer is an app that provides patient guidelines for various cancers, including pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURFACE PROTEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surface proteins are molecules on the surface of cells, such as CD20, CD200, and LEF1, that help identify the type of cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THROAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Area examined during a physical exam to assess respiratory and digestive health."&lt;SEP&gt;"The throat is a site where HPV can infect and cause cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat is a body part examined in laryngoscopy and panendoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat is a body part."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat is an area examined during laryngoscopy and endoscopy procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat is examined during a physical exam to check for abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat is examined during physical exam to check for abnormalities in the oropharynx or nasopharynx."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat is the passage connecting the mouth to the esophagus, part of both respiratory and digestive systems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGIONAL PROSTATE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Regional prostate cancer grows from the prostate to nearby lymph nodes but no farther, also called locally advanced prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Regional prostate cancer, also called locally advanced prostate cancer, has spread to nearby areas like lymph nodes but not farther."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL SQUAMOUS CELL SKIN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local squamous cell skin cancer is a form of the disease that has not spread to lymph nodes, with monitoring schedules based on risk level."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell skin cancer that has not spread to nearby lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMPAIRED IMMUNE SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An impaired immune system is a risk factor for developing primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN EPIDERMAL GROWTH FACTOR RECEPTOR 2 (HER2)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Human Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor 2 (HER2) is a biomarker status that indicates whether the cancer makes too much of the HER2 protein, which is important for prognosis and targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lobes are sections of the lungs; the left lung has 2 lobes and the right lung has 3 lobes, which are part of the lung's anatomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TP53&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TP53 is a gene that controls cell death, and mutations in it are looked for via DNA sequencing in CLL patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSURANCE COVERAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insurance Coverage is the extent to which health insurance pays for medical treatments and services."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE RADIATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph node radiation therapy, also called regional nodal irradiation, targets lymph nodes in the chest wall, infraclavicular, supraclavicular, or axillary regions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAGNETIC FIELDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Magnetic fields are used in MRI to create detailed images of internal body structures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PANCREATIC DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA (PDAC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PDAC is the most common type of pancreatic cancer, forming from exocrine cells that line the ducts of the pancreas. It is the focus of the pancreatic cancer section."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIAID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NIAID (National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases) is the source of a derivative work image showing Rituximab binding to CD20 on a B cell surface, used for illustrative purposes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMPERATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Temperature is a vital sign checked during a physical exam to assess health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature is a vital sign checked during physical exam to assess for fever or infection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISPANIC MALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hispanic males are a demographic group with lower risk of prostate cancer compared to white and Black males."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hispanic males are less likely than white and Black males to be diagnosed with prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEREOTACTIC BODY RADIOTHERAPY (SBRT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stereotactic body radiotherapy (SBRT) is a special radiation technique that delivers high doses to small areas to kill cancer cells, used for distant tumors causing symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL PART OF THE BRAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The central part of the brain is a location where a lymphoma can cause leg or arm weakness, coordination difficulties, and other symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE (G)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade (G) describes how abnormal the tumor cells look under a microscope, with categories from G1 (low grade) to G3 (high grade), indicating the risk of recurrence and growth rate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAT CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flat cells line the inside of the bronchi and are the origin of squamous cell carcinoma, a subtype of NSCLC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEREDITARY PARAGANGLIOMA-PHEOCHROMOCYTOMA SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hereditary paraganglioma-pheochromocytoma (PGL/PCC) syndrome is a genetic condition that raises the risk of adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROGLOBULIN (TG) LEVEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thyroglobulin level is a blood test marker used after surgery to assess remaining thyroid tissue or cancer, with high levels indicating need for RAI therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHOLE BREAST RADIATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Whole breast radiation therapy (WBRT) is a type of external beam radiation that targets the entire breast."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OOPHOROPEXY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oophoropexy is the medical name for ovarian transposition, a surgery to move ovaries out of radiation range."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oophoropexy is the medical term for ovarian transposition, a procedure to move ovaries out of the radiation field."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROENDOCRINE TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A neuroendocrine tumor is a less common type of pancreatic cancer that forms from endocrine cells, which make hormones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B CELL SURFACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B cell surface refers to the outer membrane of B cells where proteins like CD20 are located, relevant to cancer identification and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PULSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pulse is a vital sign checked during a physical exam to assess heart rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pulse is a vital sign checked during physical exam to assess heart rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pulse is the heart rate, checked during a physical exam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASIAN MALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Asian males are a demographic group with lower risk of prostate cancer compared to white and Black males."&lt;SEP&gt;"Asian males are less likely than white and Black males to be diagnosed with prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER DOCTORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer doctors are specialists who discuss treatment options for patients, especially when surgery is not possible or when systemic therapy is planned."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MESSAGE TO CAREGIVERS AND LOVED ONES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A message to caregivers and loved ones is a section of the book addressing the challenges of supporting a person with primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC BREAST CANCER (MBC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic Breast Cancer (MBC) is breast cancer that has spread to distant parts of the body, such as bone and lung, and is indicated by M1 in the TNM system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic breast cancer (MBC) is breast cancer that has spread outside the breast and lymph nodes to other parts of the body. It can occur even when axillary lymph nodes are negative for cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic breast cancer (MBC) is breast cancer that has spread to distant organs, such as bone, liver, lungs, or brain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic breast cancer is breast cancer that has spread beyond the breast and nearby lymph nodes to distant parts of the body, such as bones, lungs, liver, or brain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic breast cancer is breast cancer that has spread outside the breast and lymph nodes under the arm (axilla) to other parts of the body, also known as advanced breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARGE CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Large cells can grow anywhere in the lungs and are the origin of large cell carcinoma, a subtype of NSCLC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY OPTION DISCUSSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility Option Discussion is talking with specialists about preservation methods."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTIPLE ENDOCRINE NEOPLASIA (MEN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Multiple endocrine neoplasia is a hereditary syndrome that increases the risk of thyroid cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECONSTRUCTIVE (PLASTIC) SURGEON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reconstructive (plastic) surgeon performs breast reconstruction for those who undergo mastectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LINEAR ACCELERATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A linear accelerator is a large machine used in external beam radiation therapy to deliver radiation from outside the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Linear accelerator (linac) is a machine used in external beam radiation therapy to deliver precise radiation doses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OOCYTE PRESERVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oocyte preservation is the medical term for egg freezing, a fertility preservation method."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXOCRINE CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Exocrine cells are cells in the pancreas that make and move digestive enzymes. They are the origin of pancreatic adenocarcinomas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exocrine cells are cells in the pancreas that produce and secrete digestive enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exocrine cells line the ducts of the pancreas and are the cells from which pancreatic adenocarcinomas form."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL RESCUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell rescue is a medical procedure involving the harvesting, freezing, and reinfusion of a patient's own stem cells to restore bone marrow after high-dose chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Height is a body measurement taken during a physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Height is a physical measurement taken during a physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Height is a physical measurement taken during physical exam to assess growth and body mass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROSTATE-SPECIFIC ANTIGEN (PSA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSA is a protein made by the prostate that nourishes and helps transmit semen, used as a biomarker for prostate health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostate-specific antigen (PSA) is a protein produced by the prostate gland. Elevated levels in the blood may indicate prostate cancer or other prostate conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prostate-specific antigen is a protein made by prostate cells, measured in blood tests to indicate potential cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREVENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prevention refers to steps patients can take to reduce the risk of getting squamous cell skin cancer again, as they are at higher risk after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEMS WITH BRAIN FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Problems with brain function are common in people with lymphoma in the central nervous system, including slower thinking and memory loss."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS (ITCS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isolated Tumor Cells (ITCs) are malignant cell clusters no larger than a certain size, which may be present in lymph nodes and are noted in N0 staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMOPREVENTIVE AGENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemopreventive agents are treatments being researched to prevent lung cancer caused by smoking, potentially used in clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T1 SPINE TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T1 spine tumor is confined to 1 vertebra or 2 adjacent vertebrae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMBRYO FREEZING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Embryo freezing is a fertility preservation option where embryos are frozen for later use."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOCRINE CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endocrine cells are cells in the pancreas that make hormones like insulin and glucagon. They are the origin of neuroendocrine tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endocrine cells are cells in the pancreas that produce hormones like insulin and glucagon."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTIDISCIPLINARY CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Multidisciplinary care involves a team of doctors, specialists, and allied health providers working together to coordinate a patient's treatment and care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A physical measurement checked during a physical exam to assess overall health and nutritional status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight is a body function influenced by thyroid hormones and metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight is a body measurement taken during a physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight is a physical measurement taken during a physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight is a physical measurement taken during physical exam to assess nutritional status and body mass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRCA2 GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BRCA2 is a gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA2 is a gene where inherited genetic changes (mutations) increase the risk of developing prostate cancer and other cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTHY ORGANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Healthy organs are critical structures that may be damaged by radiation therapy, influencing the decision to use systemic therapy alone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SLOWER THINKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Slower thinking is a problem with brain function in primary CNS lymphoma patients, affecting cognitive speed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROMETASTASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Micrometastases are very small collections of cancerous cells, approximately 200 cells, larger than a certain size but not larger than another, found in lymph nodes and noted as N1mi."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;U.S. FDA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The U.S. FDA (Food and Drug Administration) is the agency that approves investigational treatments after clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. FDA (Food and Drug Administration) is the regulatory agency that approves drugs, devices, or treatment approaches after they are found safe and effective in clinical trials. It plays a key role in the approval of cancer treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. FDA is the Food and Drug Administration, which approves investigational treatments after clinical trials show efficacy and safety."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD CLOTS (THROMBOSIS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood clots can form abnormally in coagulopathy, leading to complications like thrombosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE THERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maintenance therapies are treatments guided by biomarker status, such as BRCA and HRD."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUESTIONS SECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Questions Section is a part of a medical binder for noting questions and taking notes during appointments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRUG INTERACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Drug interaction occurs when supplements or medicines affect the ability of a drug to work properly, potentially reducing efficacy or increasing toxicity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURROGATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surrogate is a volunteer, often a relative or friend, who carries a pregnancy for individuals with frozen embryos or eggs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTIAGENT CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Multiagent chemotherapy is a treatment approach for ALL that uses multiple chemotherapy drugs together."&lt;SEP&gt;"Multiagent chemotherapy is a treatment for ALL that involves multiple drugs, as mentioned in Chapter 3."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUALITY OF LIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Quality of Life is a measure of overall well-being, including physical, emotional, and social aspects, during and after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quality of life refers to a person's overall well-being and ability to participate in usual activities, considered a main priority in guiding treatment and care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quality of life refers to overall satisfaction with well-being and ability to participate in regular activities, affected by symptoms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quality of life refers to overall well-being, including physical, emotional, and social aspects, considered in treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quality of life refers to the overall well-being of bladder cancer patients, which treatments aim to improve."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ILLNESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A disease or period of sickness that is part of a patient's medical history, to be listed with dates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illness refers to any disease or health condition a patient has had, recorded in medical history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illness refers to past health conditions listed in medical history, relevant for bladder cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illness refers to past health conditions that are part of a patient's medical history, relevant for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Illness refers to past health conditions that inform a patient's overall health history for cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OBESITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Obesity is a lifestyle factor that increases the risk of developing and dying from prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYSTEMIC THERAPY ALONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Systemic therapy alone is a treatment approach where drugs are used without surgery or radiation, recommended when radiation is not expected to be effective or may harm healthy organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFICULTY MOVING OR WALKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Difficulty moving or walking is a problem with brain function in primary CNS lymphoma patients, affecting mobility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T4 is a tumor size category in the TNM system, indicating the tumor is of any size and has invaded nearby structures such as the chest wall or skin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KINASE INHIBITORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kinase inhibitors are targeted therapies currently used for thyroid cancer. They are mostly capsules that are swallowed and work by targeting specific cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hypnosis is a complementary therapy using guided relaxation to manage pain or anxiety."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TWO ADRENAL GLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Two adrenal glands refers to the pair of glands in the human body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICAL TRIAL ELIGIBILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical Trial Eligibility refers to the criteria that determine whether a patient can participate in a trial."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTHRACYCLINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anthracyclines are a class of chemotherapy drugs, including doxorubicin, doxorubicin liposomal injection, and epirubicin, used to treat breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anthracyclines are a type of chemotherapy that damage and disrupt DNA synthesis, causing cell death. They can cause heart issues and have a lifetime dose limit. Examples include daunorubicin, idarubicin, and mitoxantrone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anthracyclines damage and disrupt DNA making, causing cell death, with examples including daunorubicin, idarubicin, and mitoxantrone, and may cause heart issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENERAL ANESTHESIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A state of deep sleep induced for surgical procedures, used during extensive surgeries and sentinel lymph node biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"General anesthesia is a deep sleep induced for extensive surgeries like lymph node dissection."&lt;SEP&gt;"General anesthesia is a medical state induced for surgery, potentially needed when closing wounds involving deeper tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"General anesthesia is a state of controlled unconsciousness used during direct laryngoscopy for detailed examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"General anesthesia is a state of full sedation used during examinations under anesthesia (EUAs) for bladder and bowel checks."&lt;SEP&gt;"General anesthesia is medicine that puts a patient into a deep sleep during surgery to prevent pain."&lt;SEP&gt;"General anesthesia is often required for brachytherapy applicator placement, especially the first time, to ensure patient comfort and immobility."&lt;SEP&gt;"General anesthesia is sometimes used during high-resolution anoscopy when the procedure is performed in an operating room."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHILDREN’S (PEDIATRIC) LEUKEMIA CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A children's (pediatric) leukemia center is a specialized facility for treating childhood leukemia, recommended for ALL care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHOLE-BRAIN RADIATION THERAPY (WBRT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Whole-brain radiation therapy (WBRT) is a radiation technique that treats the entire brain to address primary CNS lymphoma, which can occur in multiple spots, and can also reach the upper spine and eyeballs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Whole-brain radiation therapy (WBRT) is a type of radiation therapy that treats the entire brain. It can be expanded to include the eyes for primary CNS lymphoma, but may cause long-term cognitive problems and vision issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Whole-brain radiation therapy is the most commonly used radiation technique for primary CNS lymphoma, targeting cancer cells in the brain."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INJURY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Injury is a past physical trauma that is part of a patient's health history, relevant to treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Injury refers to past physical trauma that is part of a patient's medical history, relevant for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Injury refers to past physical traumas listed in medical history, relevant for overall health assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Injury refers to physical harm a patient has experienced, recorded in medical history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Physical harm or damage to the body that is part of a patient's medical history, to be listed with dates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRUITS AND VEGETABLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eating more fruits and vegetables is associated with a lower risk of developing advanced prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fruits and vegetables are dietary components that may reduce the risk of prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIATION THERAPY WITH SYSTEMIC THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiation therapy with systemic therapy is a combined treatment approach used when surgery is not possible, often involving chemotherapy or immunotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TROUBLE SPEAKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trouble speaking is a long-term side effect of whole-brain radiation therapy, affecting communication."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trouble speaking is a problem with brain function in primary CNS lymphoma patients, affecting communication."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T4D&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T4d is a specific subtype of T4, indicating inflammatory carcinoma (inflammatory breast cancer)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICAL TRIAL PHASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical trial phases are stages of testing for cancer treatments. Phase 1 trials study safety and side effects, Phase 2 trials study effectiveness against specific cancers, Phase 3 trials test against standard treatments, and Phase 4 trials study long-term safety and benefit of FDA-approved treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTIPLE ENDOCRINE NEOPLASIA TYPE 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Multiple endocrine neoplasia type 1 (MEN 1) is a hereditary condition associated with a higher risk of adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CD20 PROTEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CD20 is a protein found on the surface of cancerous blood cells and some healthy blood cells. Rituximab targets this protein to help the immune system locate and destroy cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHOLE-BODY RAI IMAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Whole-body RAI imaging is a diagnostic procedure using radioactive iodine to detect cancer cells throughout the body after RAI therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Whole-body RAI imaging is a scan performed after RAI therapy to look for remaining thyroid cancer cells in the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HÜRTHLE CELL CARCINOMA (HCC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hürthle cell carcinoma is the former name for oncocytic carcinoma, an uncommon thyroid cancer type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TAXANES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Taxanes are a class of chemotherapy drugs, including docetaxel, paclitaxel, and albumin-bound paclitaxel, used in breast cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYSTOSCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A tube with a camera and light used during cystoscopy to examine the urethra and bladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cystoscope is a hollow tool with a magnifying lens used in cystoscopy to see inside the bladder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PANCREATIC CANCER BASICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pancreatic cancer basics is a chapter that provides an overview of pancreatic cancer, including causes, stages, and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORTICOSTEROIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of steroid treatment option for primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corticosteroids are a type of drug used to reduce inflammation and treat certain cancers, including primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corticosteroids are a type of steroid used to reduce inflammation and swelling in the brain, often referred to simply as steroids in the context of lymphoma treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corticosteroids are anti-inflammatory drugs used to reduce swelling and treat lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corticosteroids are medications that can be used in hormone therapy for prostate cancer, taken as pills, to help manage symptoms and reduce inflammation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVER-THE-COUNTER (OTC) MEDICINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"OTC medicines are non-prescription drugs that patients should list for their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Over-the-counter (OTC) medicines are drugs available without prescription, listed in medical history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Over-the-counter (OTC) medicines are non-prescription drugs that patients may take, which can interact with prescribed treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Over-the-counter medicines are drugs available without a prescription that patients should list in their medical history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Over-the-counter medicines are drugs available without a prescription. The text advises listing these, along with herbals and supplements, as they may interact with prescribed treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Over-the-counter medicines are medications available without a prescription that patients may take and should disclose to their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Over-the-counter medicines, herbals, and supplements are non-prescription items that can interact with prescribed medicines and should be reported to the care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEAT AND DAIRY PRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High consumption of meat and dairy products, which are high in fat, is linked to an increased risk of prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Meat and dairy products are high-fat foods linked to an increased risk of prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGERY AND RADIATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgery and radiation therapy are local treatments that may be used together to treat squamous cell skin cancer, especially for regional disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INABILITY TO DO EVERYDAY ACTIVITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inability to do everyday activities is a problem with brain function in primary CNS lymphoma patients, affecting daily life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T1MI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T1mi is a tumor size category indicating a micrometastasis, a very small collection of cancerous cells smaller than 1 mm."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTERNAL RADIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"External radiation is a type of radiation therapy where high-energy beams are directed from outside the body to the tumor. It is commonly used for cancer treatment, with sessions lasting 30 to 60 minutes, typically 5 times per week. Side effects can include skin rash, problems swallowing, dry mouth, thick saliva, changes in taste, and tiredness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT IMPACT DISCUSSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment Impact Discussion is talking with the care team about how treatment affects fertility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROXINE (T4)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thyroxine is a hormone produced by the thyroid, essential for regulating metabolism and other body functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESIDENTS AND FELLOWS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Residents and fellows are doctors in training, some specializing in fields like oncology."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIMETABOLITES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antimetabolites are a class of chemotherapy drugs, including capecitabine, fluorouracil, gemcitabine, and methotrexate, used in breast cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antimetabolites are a type of chemotherapy that prevent the building blocks of DNA from being used, thereby inhibiting cancer cell growth. Examples include Cladribine, Clofarabine, Cytarabine, Fludarabine, and Methotrexate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antimetabolites prevent the building blocks of DNA from being used, with examples including Cladribine, Clofarabine, Cytarabine, Fludarabine, and Methotrexate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROCTOSCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proctoscope is a thin, tube-like instrument with a light and magnifying lens used in proctoscopy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSULIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insulin is a hormone made by the pancreas that controls blood sugar levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEURO-ONCOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A neuro-oncologist is a physician specializing in the treatment of cancers of the nervous system, including primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"A neuro-oncologist is a specialist who treats cancers of the nervous system, including primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEM CELL TRANSPLANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stem cell transplant is a treatment for AML that requires HLA typing to match donors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stem cell transplant is a treatment option for primary CNS lymphoma, often used in combination with other therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER RESEARCHERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer researchers are scientists who study the causes and risk factors of prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer researchers are scientists who study the causes of cancer, including prostate cancer, but don't know exactly what causes cells to grow out of control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISTANT TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Distant tumors are cancer growths that have spread to other parts of the body, which may be treated with radiation or surgery to relieve symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHANGES IN BEHAVIOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Changes in behavior are a problem with brain function in primary CNS lymphoma patients, affecting personality and actions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N0 is a lymph node category indicating no cancer is found in regional lymph nodes, though isolated tumor cells may be present."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAI THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RAI (Radioactive Iodine) therapy is a treatment for thyroid cancer that uses radioactive iodine to destroy remaining thyroid tissue or cancer cells. It is used after total thyroidectomy and for metastatic cancers that take up iodine."&lt;SEP&gt;"RAI (Radioactive Iodine) therapy is a treatment for thyroid cancer that uses radioactive iodine to destroy thyroid cancer cells. It is mentioned as a treatment option that may not be suitable for certain thyroid cancers that have returned or metastasized."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IGHV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IGHV is a gene that controls cell death, and mutations in it are looked for via DNA sequencing in CLL patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T2 SPINE TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T2 spine tumor is confined to 3 adjacent vertebrae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUCAGON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glucagon is a hormone made by the pancreas that controls blood sugar levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HER2 (human epidermal growth factor receptor 2) is a protein that can promote cancer cell growth. HER2 status is tested to determine if targeted therapies like trastuzumab are appropriate."&lt;SEP&gt;"HER2 (human epidermal growth factor receptor 2) is a protein that can promote cancer cell growth; its status is tested to guide targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"HER2 is a protein biomarker that may be overexpressed in some cancers, tested to guide targeted therapy options."&lt;SEP&gt;"HER2 is a protein involved in normal cell growth; higher amounts in breast cancer make it HER2-positive, which can be targeted by specific therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"HER2 is a protein that can be overexpressed in breast cancer cells; its status is part of biomarker testing to guide targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human epidermal growth factor receptor 2, a protein involved in normal cell growth. When overexpressed, it can cause cells to grow and divide rapidly in breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TISSUE SAMPLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tissue samples are removed and tested (biopsied) if abnormal areas are seen during cystoscopy or proctoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissue samples are small pieces of tissue removed during biopsy and sent to a pathologist for microscopic examination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROSURGEON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A neurosurgeon is a surgeon who operates on the brain and nervous system, involved in diagnosing and treating CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"A neurosurgeon is a surgeon who operates on the brain and spinal cord, involved in biopsy or surgical treatment of CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"A neurosurgeon is a surgeon who performs stereotactic biopsies, making an opening in the skull and inserting a needle to remove a tumor sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neurosurgeon is a medical specialist who performs biopsies, including stereotactic and open biopsies, to diagnose brain tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neurosurgeon is a surgeon who performs procedures like resection and stereotactic biopsy to remove or sample brain tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRAMEDULLARY LEUKEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Extramedullary leukemia is leukemia outside the blood and bone marrow, detected with FDG-PET/CT."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECIALISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Specialists are medical professionals researching areas like racial disparities in prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLOW-UP CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follow-up Care is the ongoing medical monitoring after treatment to detect recurrence and manage late effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Follow-up care encompasses the monitoring and surveillance procedures after thyroid cancer treatment, including physical exams, blood tests, and imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Follow-up care refers to monitoring and check-ups after treatment to detect any recurrence of squamous cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOSING ONE'S SENSE OF SELF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Losing one's sense of self is a problem with brain function in primary CNS lymphoma patients, affecting identity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N1MI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N1mi is a lymph node category indicating micrometastases (approximately 200 cells, larger than 0.2 mm but not larger than 2 mm) are found in lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BODY ACHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Body aches are a side effect more often seen with targeted therapy. They can cause discomfort and may require pain management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOPATHOLOGY REVIEW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hematopathology review is a specialized examination of blood and bone marrow samples for AML diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRECISION ONCOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Precision oncology is an approach using biomarker testing to tailor cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-hormonal Birth Control includes barrier methods and IUDs, preferred after breast cancer diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIFESTYLE FACTORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lifestyle factors are behaviors such as smoking, heavy alcohol use, and diet that can increase the risk of pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2 ANTIBODIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HER2 antibodies are a type of HER2-targeted therapy that prevent growth signals from HER2 from outside the cell and increase immune cell attack."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPSIED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biopsied refers to the process of removing tissue samples for testing to determine if cancer is present."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NURSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nurses are healthcare professionals who provide direct care, symptom management, and support to cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nurses are healthcare professionals who provide direct patient care, including administering treatments and monitoring side effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CNS BLEED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CNS bleed is bleeding in the central nervous system, suspected and diagnosed with brain CT."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCREENING TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Screening tests are early detection methods for prostate cancer, which may be recommended earlier or more often for Black males."&lt;SEP&gt;"Screening tests are medical procedures used for early detection of prostate cancer, especially recommended for Black males."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-RISK PATIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-risk patients are those with a greater chance of cancer recurrence, requiring more frequent skin exams and monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-risk patients are those with thyroid cancer who have a higher likelihood of recurrence or metastasis, requiring more intensive monitoring."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physical support is a type of help provided by caregivers to patients with primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N1 is a lymph node category indicating regional lymph node metastases are found, with a higher number indicating more lymph nodes involved."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RASH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rash is a side effect more often seen with targeted therapy. It can cause skin irritation and may require dermatological care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rash is a side effect of chemotherapy, appearing on the skin and requiring management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT SIDE EFFECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment Side Effects are adverse reactions to cancer treatments, which can be managed with medical support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER-CAUSING CHEMICALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer-causing chemicals are substances like pesticides that can increase the risk of pancreatic cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer-causing chemicals, such as pesticides, are environmental risk factors that increase the chance of developing pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2 INHIBITORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HER2 inhibitors are a type of HER2-targeted therapy that stop growth signals from HER2 from within the cell."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNG PROBLEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lung problems are potential complications during chemotherapy, increased by smoking and vaping."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CARE DOCTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A physician who manages non-cancer-related medical care and helps patients communicate with their cancer care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary care doctor is a general physician who coordinates overall health care and may be part of the multidisciplinary team."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary care doctor is a general physician who manages overall health and coordinates care with specialists."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary care doctor is a healthcare provider who recommends cancer screenings and other preventive health measures based on a patient's sex, age, and risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary care doctors (PCPs) play a key role in post-treatment care, coordinating with oncologists for follow-up and overall health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS: DISTRESS DURING CANCER CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A patient guide providing information on managing distress during cancer care, available at NCCN.org."&lt;SEP&gt;"A patient guideline document from the National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) that provides information on managing distress during cancer care, accessible at NCCN.org/patientguidelines and via the NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer app."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Distress During Cancer Care is a resource providing information on managing anxiety, depression, and distress in cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"The NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Distress During Cancer Care is a resource providing information on managing distress and mental health issues for cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCALIZED PROSTATE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Localized prostate cancer is an early-stage form of prostate cancer that remains within the prostate gland and has not spread to other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Localized prostate cancer is cancer contained entirely within the prostate, synonymous with early-stage prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW-RISK PATIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low-risk patients are those with a lower chance of cancer recurrence, requiring less frequent skin exams after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MENTAL SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mental support is a type of help provided by caregivers to patients with primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N2 is a lymph node category indicating regional lymph node metastases are found, with more lymph nodes involved than in N1."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHILDCARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Childcare is an indirect cost that may arise due to extra appointments during a clinical trial."&lt;SEP&gt;"Childcare is an indirect cost that participants may incur during a clinical trial due to extra appointments. It is not covered by the study sponsor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EYE RADIATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eye radiation therapy is a focused radiation treatment for primary CNS lymphoma in the eyes, often applied to both eyes simultaneously at a lower dose. Side effects include temporary or permanent vision problems and cataracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTIPLE ENDOCRINE NEOPLASIA TYPE 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2 (MEN 2) is a hereditary condition that can increase the risk of adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR SUBTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor subtype refers to the specific type of thyroid cancer, such as follicular or oncocytic, which influences treatment decisions including RAI therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health conditions are various medical issues that can lead to the formation of lung nodules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health conditions like heart disease and diabetes are part of family health history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health conditions such as diabetes and chronic inflammation of the pancreas are risk factors for pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2 CONJUGATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HER2 conjugates or antibody drug conjugates (ADCs) deliver cell-specific chemotherapy by attaching to HER2 and releasing chemotherapy inside the cell."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADOLESCENT AND YOUNG ADULT CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specific patient population addressed in NCCN guidelines, relevant for fertility and family planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adolescent and Young Adult Cancer is a category of cancer affecting individuals aged 18-33, where thyroid cancer is most common."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adolescent and Young Adult Cancer is a category of cancer patients for whom NCCN guidelines provide fertility information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adolescent and Young Adult Cancer is a specific patient group addressed in NCCN guidelines, relevant to fertility preservation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adolescent and Young Adult Cancer is a specific patient population addressed in NCCN guidelines, with fertility preservation considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adolescent and Young Adult Cancer is a topic covered in NCCN Guidelines for Patients®, which includes fertility preservation information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adolescent and Young Adult Cancer refers to cancer that occurs in adolescents and young adults. The NCCN provides specific guidelines for this population, including information on fertility and family planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adolescent and young adult cancer is a patient group for which NCCN guidelines provide fertility preservation information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NURSE PRACTITIONERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nurse practitioners are advanced practice nurses who can diagnose and treat conditions, often part of the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nurse practitioners are advanced practice nurses who provide patient care, including diagnosis and treatment management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIGO SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The International Federation of Gynecology and Obstetrics system used to stage cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCALLY ADVANCED PROSTATE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Locally advanced prostate cancer is another term for regional prostate cancer, which has spread to nearby lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLETE SKIN CHECK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A complete skin check is a full-body examination performed by a doctor during follow-up visits to detect any new or recurring skin cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMOTIONAL SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emotional support is a component of supportive care, helping patients cope with cancer-related stress and depression."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emotional support is a type of help provided by caregivers to patients with primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N3 is a lymph node category indicating regional lymph node metastases are found, with the most lymph nodes involved among N1, N2, and N3."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIBEROPTIC NASOPHARYNGOLARYNGOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fiberoptic nasopharyngolaryngoscopy is a scoping procedure used to examine the larynx and nearby structures, performed while the patient is awake with a topical spray for comfort."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTRACEPTION USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contraception Use is employing birth control methods to prevent pregnancy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRIIODOTHYRONINE (T3)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Triiodothyronine is a hormone produced by the thyroid, working with T4 to regulate metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NURSE PRACTITIONERS (NPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nurse practitioners (NPs) are health care providers who may conduct clinic visits and manage patient care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEREDITARY PANCREATIC CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hereditary pancreatic cancer is a form of pancreatic cancer where a higher risk is passed down through genes, accounting for about 1 in 10 cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hereditary pancreatic cancer is a type of pancreatic cancer that is passed down through families, accounting for about 1 in 10 cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYCLIN-DEPENDENT KINASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cyclin-dependent kinase (CDK) is a cell protein that helps cells grow and divide; CDK4/6 inhibitors target this protein."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AML&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AML (Acute Myeloid Leukemia) is a type of blood cancer characterized by abnormal growth of myeloid cells in the bone marrow, with various genetic changes and biomarkers that guide treatment and prognosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"AML (Acute Myeloid Leukemia) is a type of cancer that affects blood and bone marrow, characterized by genetic mutations and chromosomal abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"AML (Acute Myeloid Leukemia) is a type of cancer that affects the blood and bone marrow, characterized by the presence of myeloid blasts. It is the central topic of the text, with testing and treatment discussed in detail."&lt;SEP&gt;"AML (Acute Myeloid Leukemia) is a type of cancer that affects the blood and bone marrow, characterized by the rapid growth of abnormal white blood cells. It is the primary disease context for the treatment options discussed in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"AML (Acute Myeloid Leukemia) is a type of cancer that affects the blood and bone marrow, characterized by the rapid growth of abnormal white blood cells. The text discusses various tests and procedures for diagnosing and monitoring this condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"AML (Acute Myeloid Leukemia) is a type of cancer that starts in the blood stem cells and makes abnormal myeloblasts, affecting the bone marrow and blood."&lt;SEP&gt;"AML (Acute Myeloid Leukemia) is a type of cancer that starts in the bone marrow, characterized by abnormal cell growth, and is the focus of the diagnostic and testing procedures described."&lt;SEP&gt;"AML (Acute Myeloid Leukemia) is a type of leukemia that is diagnosed through bone marrow tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute myeloid leukemia (AML) is a type of blood cancer that can be treated with various targeted therapies and chemotherapy combinations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICIAN ASSISTANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physician assistants are healthcare professionals who work under the supervision of doctors to provide patient care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Physician assistants are healthcare providers who practice medicine under a doctor's supervision, contributing to patient care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUITTING SMOKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Quitting smoking is a behavioral change that reduces bladder cancer risk and improves treatment effectiveness, often supported by counseling and medicines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quitting smoking is a preventive measure and lifestyle change that reduces the risk of bladder cancer and improves treatment outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The act of stopping smoking, which can lead to better cancer treatment outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UROTHELIAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The most common type of bladder cancer, arising from urothelial cells, with rare subtypes that have different features."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urothelial cancer is a type of cancer that starts in urothelial cells, which can occur in the bladder or other parts of the urinary tract."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAPER GOWN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A paper gown is a disposable garment worn by patients during skin exams to allow the doctor to examine different areas of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HANDS-ON SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hands-on support is a type of help provided by caregivers to patients with primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M0 is a metastasis category indicating no evidence of distant metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDIRECT LARYNGOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indirect laryngoscopy is a method of laryngoscopy using a small mirror held at the back of the throat to view the area, possibly with numbing medicine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLEX KARYOTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Complex karyotype is a condition of 3 or more unrelated changes or deletions in chromosomes, detected via karyotype testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T3 SPINE TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T3 spine tumor is confined to 4 or more adjacent vertebrae, or any nonadjacent vertebrae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MELANOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of skin cancer associated with inherited mutations in BRCA1 and BRCA2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Melanoma is a less common but more aggressive type of skin cancer that originates in melanocytes, the cells producing melanin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Melanoma is a type of cancer that, when present in close blood relatives, increases the risk of pancreatic cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Melanoma is a type of cancer where p16 can be found."&lt;SEP&gt;"Melanoma is a type of skin cancer that arises from melanocytes. It is mentioned in the text as a separate condition from basal cell skin cancer, with information available in NCCN Guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Melanoma is a type of skin cancer that is a risk factor for pancreatic cancer when present in close blood relatives."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"mTOR is a cell protein that helps cells grow and divide; when overactive, it can make endocrine therapy stop working."&lt;SEP&gt;"mTOR is a cell protein that regulates cell growth and division; its overactivity can cause endocrine therapy resistance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AML SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An AML specialist is a healthcare provider with expertise in treating acute myeloid leukemia, whose opinion is recommended for optimal care."&lt;SEP&gt;"An AML specialist is a medical professional with expertise in acute myeloid leukemia, whose opinion is recommended for patients seeking care."&lt;SEP&gt;"An AML specialist is a medical professional with expertise in treating AML, whose opinion is recommended for optimal care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALLIATIVE CARE SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A palliative care specialist focuses on relieving symptoms and improving quality of life for patients with serious illnesses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVARY PRESERVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The option to keep ovaries during hysterectomy to avoid surgical menopause and its associated risks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLANDULAR SUBTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rare subtype of urothelial cancer with features resembling glandular cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNDERGARMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Undergarments are clothing items that can be worn during skin exams, as mentioned in the text regarding patient comfort."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TAKING THE PATIENT TO APPOINTMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Taking the patient to appointments is a task performed by caregivers for primary CNS lymphoma patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M1 is a metastasis category indicating distant metastasis is found, which is metastatic breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOCAL CORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vocal cords are located in the larynx and allow speech; they are examined during laryngoscopy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONLINE SURVEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An online survey is a questionnaire about the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, available at NCCN.org/patients/response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIGHT-SENSITIVE DYE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Light-sensitive dye is used in flow cytometry to stain cells for detection and counting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor mutations are somatic changes in cancer cells, analyzed for treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENZYME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzyme is a protein like ALP that is measured in blood tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLASSIC TYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Classic type is the most common subtype of papillary thyroid cancer, typically slow-growing with good outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN EXPERTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN experts are a group of medical professionals from the National Comprehensive Cancer Network who provide guidelines and recommendations for cancer care, including follow-up exam schedules for skin cancer and chronic myeloid leukemia."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN experts are specialists from the National Comprehensive Cancer Network who provide recommendations for follow-up care and monitoring after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVARIAN ABLATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ovarian ablation or suppression is a treatment to stop ovarian function, required for premenopausal women on CDK4/6 inhibitor regimens."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ovarian ablation uses radiation to permanently stop ovaries from making hormones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN LEUKOCYTE ANTIGEN (HLA) TYPING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HLA typing is a test to match tissue types for potential stem cell transplantation, which is a treatment option for AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human leukocyte antigen (HLA) typing is a test to match donors for stem cell transplants, important in AML treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pain specialist is a doctor who manages pain, often part of supportive care for cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE DISSECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph node dissection is a surgical procedure to remove lymph nodes containing cancer, performed in the groin area for anal cancer that has spread to lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph node dissection is an extensive surgery to remove lymph nodes when cancer has spread, performed under general anesthesia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph node dissection, or lymphadenectomy, is a surgical procedure to remove lymph nodes to test for cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical removal of lymph nodes to check for cancer spread, as cancer cells can travel through lymph."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SQUAMOUS CELL SUBTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rare subtype of urothelial cancer with features resembling squamous cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECONDARY INTENTION HEALING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A wound healing process where a wound is left open to heal naturally by filling in and closing up, requiring regular dressings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HELPING TO LESSEN SIDE EFFECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Helping to lessen side effects is a task performed by caregivers for primary CNS lymphoma patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AXILLARY NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Axillary Nodes are lymph nodes under the arm, which are common sites for breast cancer spread and are assessed in clinical staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAMERA LENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Camera lens is a component of a scope that captures images of internal body areas during scoping procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLOSTOMY CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colostomy Care involves managing a colostomy, including cleaning, changing bags, and monitoring for complications."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRONIC MYELOID LEUKEMIA (CML)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chronic myeloid leukemia (CML) is a type of blood cancer caused by a specific abnormal gene (BCR::ABL1) and the Philadelphia chromosome, leading to an overproduction of white blood cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPIRUBICIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Epirubicin (Ellence) is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by damaging DNA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epirubicin is an anthracycline chemotherapy drug used in breast cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHITE BLOOD CELLS (WBCS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"White Blood Cells (WBCs) fight infection and are measured in a CBC."&lt;SEP&gt;"White blood cells (WBCs or leukocytes) are a type of blood cell that fight infections. They include granulocytes, monocytes, and lymphocytes. In ALL, there are too many abnormal white blood cells (lymphoblasts)."&lt;SEP&gt;"White blood cells (WBCs) are blood cells that fight infection, measured in a complete blood count."&lt;SEP&gt;"White blood cells (WBCs) are blood cells that fight infections and include granulocytes, monocytes, and lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"White blood cells (WBCs) are cells that fight infection; abnormal or high counts can indicate leukemia, as in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"White blood cells (leukocytes) are a type of blood cell that fight infections, including granulocytes (neutrophils), monocytes, and lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"White blood cells (leukocytes) are a type of blood cell that fight infections. They include granulocytes, monocytes, lymphocytes, and others. They are produced in the bone marrow from blood stem cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"White blood cells are immune cells that fight infection. In AML, abnormal malignant white blood cells may be elevated, and their counts are measured in a CBC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSYCHOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A mental health expert who helps manage issues like depression and anxiety affecting patient well-being."&lt;SEP&gt;"A psychologist offers mental health support to breast cancer patients dealing with emotional challenges."&lt;SEP&gt;"A psychologist provides mental health support, helping patients cope with emotional and psychological aspects of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A psychologist provides mental health support, helping patients cope with the emotional aspects of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Psychologist is a mental health professional who provides counseling to help patients cope with cancer-related stress and anxiety."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAUSEA AND VOMITING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Common side effects of cancer treatment that can be managed with various options, with more information available on NCCN resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea and vomiting are common side effects of chemotherapy and radiation therapy, which can be managed with medications, as detailed in NCCN Guidelines for Patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea and vomiting are common side effects of chemotherapy, manageable with medications and care team support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea and vomiting are common side effects of systemic therapy, including chemotherapy and targeted therapy. They can be managed with medications and supportive care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea and vomiting are symptoms that can be caused by a brain tumor putting increased pressure on the brain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea and vomiting can be caused by increased pressure on the brain from a glioma tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROPAPILLARY SUBTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rare subtype of urothelial cancer with micropapillary features."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LINEAR CLOSURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A wound healing method where the surgeon reshapes the wound into an oval and stitches it together in a line."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASSISTING WITH TREATMENT DECISIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Assisting with treatment decisions is a task performed by caregivers for primary CNS lymphoma patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNAL MAMMARY NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Internal Mammary Nodes are lymph nodes near the breastbone, which can be sites for breast cancer spread and are assessed in clinical staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Light is a component of a scope that illuminates internal areas during scoping procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELATIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Relative is a type of support person who can help a patient during stressful medical times."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROFIBROMATOSIS TYPE 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neurofibromatosis type 1 (NF1) is a hereditary condition that may increase the risk of adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONOCLONAL ANTIBODY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A monoclonal antibody is a type of immunotherapy drug that hunts for specific proteins on the surface of cancer cells. Rituximab is an example used for primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRANULOCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Granulocytes (or neutrophils) are a type of white blood cell that help prevent and control infection. They are derived from myeloid blasts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Granulocytes (or neutrophils) are a type of white blood cell that help prevent and control infection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Granulocytes are a type of white blood cell that fight infections, included in the white blood cell category."&lt;SEP&gt;"Granulocytes are a type of white blood cell that fight infections. They are part of the white blood cell family, which also includes monocytes and lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Granulocytes are a type of white blood cell that includes neutrophils, eosinophils, and basophils, and are often overproduced in CML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOXORUBICIN LIPOSOMAL INJECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Doxorubicin liposomal injection (Doxil) is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy, with a liposomal formulation to reduce side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Doxorubicin liposomal injection is a formulation of doxorubicin, an anthracycline chemotherapy drug."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATELETS (PLTS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Platelets (PLTs) are blood cells that control bleeding, measured in a complete blood count."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets (PLTs) are blood cells that help control bleeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets (PLTs) are cells that help blood clot, preventing or stopping bleeding; their levels are measured in a CBC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets (PLTs) control bleeding and are measured in a CBC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets (thrombocytes) are a type of blood cell that help control bleeding. They are produced in the bone marrow from blood stem cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets are cells that help blood clot. Low platelet counts are common in AML and can lead to bleeding, making their measurement important in a CBC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets are cells that make the clot, thus preventing or stopping bleeding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOCIAL WORKERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Social workers are healthcare professionals who provide emotional and practical support to cancer patients and their families."&lt;SEP&gt;"Social workers are healthcare professionals who provide emotional support, counseling, and help with practical concerns like insurance and finances for cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Social workers are part of the care team, helping with everyday problems and financial/insurance stresses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Social workers are professionals who help people solve and cope with everyday problems, with clinical social workers diagnosing and treating mental, behavioral, and emotional issues, including managing anxiety related to cancer diagnoses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Social workers assist patients with practical and emotional needs, such as navigating healthcare systems and providing counseling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Social workers at treatment sites are professionals who help connect cancer survivors with mental health and financial resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Social workers help people solve and cope with everyday problems, including financial and insurance stresses related to cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DYSPLASIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal cell changes in cervical tissue that can be detected through biopsy and may indicate precancerous conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASMACYTOID SUBTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rare subtype of urothelial cancer with plasmacytoid features."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN GRAFT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure where a patch of skin is removed from one area and transplanted to another to aid healing and reduce scarring."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTS FOR DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tests for diagnosis are procedures used to identify primary CNS lymphoma, including neurological exams, imaging, and biopsies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFRACLAVICULAR NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Infraclavicular Nodes are lymph nodes below the collarbone, which can be sites for breast cancer spread and are assessed in clinical staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infraclavicular nodes are lymph nodes located below the collarbone, where cancer may be present in breast cancer cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TELEVISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Television is a display device used to view images captured by scopes during procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOCTOR CONSULTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Doctor Consultation is seeking advice on birth control and pregnancy planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARATHYROID GLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Parathyroid glands are four pea-sized glands on the back of the thyroid that control calcium levels in the bloodstream."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICIAN ASSISTANTS (PAS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physician assistants (PAs) are health care providers who may conduct clinic visits and assist in patient care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOCIAL MEDIA GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Social media group is an online community that offers peer support for cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGIONAL CSCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Regional CSCC refers to squamous cell carcinoma that has spread to nearby lymph nodes, requiring specific testing and treatment approaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"Regional CSCC refers to squamous cell skin cancer that has spread to nearby lymph nodes, requiring more frequent physical exams and CT scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PACLITAXEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paclitaxel (Taxol, Abraxane) is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by stabilizing microtubules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paclitaxel is a chemotherapy drug used in combination with other agents for treating metastatic cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paclitaxel is a chemotherapy drug used in preferred regimens for ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paclitaxel is a chemotherapy drug used in the carboplatin and paclitaxel regimen for recurrent or metastatic anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paclitaxel is a taxane chemotherapy drug commonly used in combination with platinum-based drugs for ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Paclitaxel is a taxane chemotherapy drug used in breast cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMOGLOBIN (HGB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hemoglobin (Hgb) is a protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen; its measurement indicates oxygen-carrying capacity and need for transfusion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hemoglobin is a measurement of how much oxygen can move through blood and if a red blood cell transfusion might be needed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hemoglobin is a protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen. Its measurement indicates oxygen-carrying capacity and helps determine if a transfusion is needed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITIONIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nutrition expert who advises on appropriate foods and fluids to ensure adequate nutrition before treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nutritionist advises on diet and nutrition to support health during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nutritionist or dietician is a professional who advises on food and fluids to ensure adequate nutrition before treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"An expert who provides guidance on diet and food suitable for a patient's condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutritionist is a professional who advises on diet and nutrition to support patients during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutritionist is a professional who suggests best foods and fluids for cancer patients to maintain nutrition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAPAROSCOPIC SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A minimally invasive surgical approach using small cuts, associated with less pain, scarring, and shorter recovery time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SARCOMATOID SUBTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rare subtype of urothelial cancer with sarcomatoid features."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASAL CELL NEVUS SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genetic condition that increases the risk of skin cancer caused by radiation, making radiation therapy inappropriate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTS AFTER DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tests after diagnosis are procedures used to determine how far primary CNS lymphoma extends within the central nervous system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPRACLAVICULAR NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Supraclavicular Nodes are lymph nodes above the collarbone, which can be sites for breast cancer spread and are assessed in clinical staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supraclavicular nodes are lymph nodes located above the collarbone, where cancer may be present in breast cancer cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPUTER MONITOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Computer monitor is a display device used to view images captured by scopes during procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAGNOSTIC CT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diagnostic CT (Computed Tomography) is an imaging test like an x-ray but shows body tissue more clearly, using more radiation and a contrast agent, and may be needed to look for big lymph nodes or assess cancer extent."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T4 SPINE TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T4 spine tumor has grown into the spinal canal or great vessels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN EXAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skin exams are regular check-ups by a doctor to monitor for the return of squamous cell skin cancer, including a full-body skin check and lymph node examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin exams are regular check-ups performed by a doctor to monitor for recurrence or new skin cancers after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALBUMIN-BOUND PACLITAXEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Albumin-bound paclitaxel is a taxane chemotherapy drug used in breast cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL (CMP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A comprehensive metabolic panel is a blood test that measures organ function, including liver and kidney health, which is important during AML treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A comprehensive metabolic panel measures substances in your blood, providing information about how well your kidneys and liver are working."&lt;SEP&gt;"A group of 14 blood tests providing information about blood sugar, calcium, electrolyte levels, and liver and kidney health."&lt;SEP&gt;"A group of blood tests providing information about kidney, liver, and organ function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comprehensive Metabolic Panel (CMP) measures 14 substances in blood plasma to evaluate kidney and liver function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comprehensive metabolic panel (CMP) is a blood test that measures substances like creatinine, BUN, electrolytes, and LDH to assess kidney and liver function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comprehensive metabolic panel is a blood test measuring chemicals and proteins, used to check organ function like kidneys and liver in bladder cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comprehensive metabolic panel is a blood test that measures glucose, electrolytes, and liver and kidney function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REHABILITATION SPECIALISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rehabilitation specialists, including physical, occupational, and speech therapists, help patients recover function and quality of life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIMPLE TRACHELECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of trachelectomy where only the cervix is removed, preserving fertility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NESTED SUBTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rare subtype of urothelial cancer with nested features."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XERODERMA PIGMENTOSUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genetic condition that increases sensitivity to radiation and skin cancer risk, making radiation therapy inappropriate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KEY TO CONFIRMING THE DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The key to confirming the diagnosis of primary CNS lymphoma is removing a small sample of the tumor tissue and testing it."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN OF THE BREAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skin of the Breast is a nearby structure that can be invaded by a T4 tumor, indicating advanced local spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOPICAL SPRAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Topical spray is a numbing medicine applied to the throat or nose to make scoping procedures more comfortable."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MACHINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Machine in flow cytometry passes dyed cells through a beam of light to measure cell properties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECURRENT OVARIAN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Recurrent ovarian cancer is cancer that returns after treatment, requiring additional biomarker testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAMERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Camera is a device used in bone scans to capture images of tracer distribution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGE AT DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Age at diagnosis is a factor considered in RAI therapy decisions, as it may affect risk assessment and treatment approach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT SCANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CT scans are imaging tests that can detect lung cancer, though SCLC is often found later due to rapid growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"CT scans are imaging tests used to monitor patients with regional CSCC for signs of cancer in lymph nodes or other parts of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUOROURACIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fluorouracil is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by interfering with DNA synthesis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fluorouracil is a chemotherapy drug used in the modified DCF regimen and as 5-FU in chemoradiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fluorouracil is an antimetabolite chemotherapy drug used in breast cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Uric acid is a substance measured in blood tests, relevant in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Uric acid is a waste product in the blood. Elevated levels can occur in AML due to rapid cell turnover and may require monitoring."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL THERAPIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A physical therapist helps breast cancer patients recover mobility and strength after surgery or during treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A physical therapist helps patients improve mobility and physical function during and after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A physical therapist is a healthcare professional who provides hands-on techniques and exercises for pelvic floor rehabilitation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Physical Therapist is a professional who helps patients recover physical function after surgery or treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRAFASCIAL HYSTERECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of hysterectomy that removes only the uterus (including the cervix), commonly used for stage IA1 cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHOEPITHELIOMA-LIKE SUBTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rare subtype of urothelial cancer with lymphoepithelioma-like features."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCLERODERMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A connective tissue disease that may make radiation therapy inappropriate for some patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL SAMPLE OF TUMOR TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A small sample of tumor tissue is removed during a biopsy to confirm the diagnosis of primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRUG THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Drug Therapy is a treatment given before surgery in some cases, which can affect staging, as indicated by the ypT notation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY SITES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary sites are the original locations where cancer begins, which can be identified via FDG-PET/CT."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTENSITY-MODULATED RADIATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intensity-Modulated Radiation Therapy (IMRT) is a precise form of radiation therapy that shapes radiation beams to conform to tumor shape."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intensity-modulated radiation therapy (IMRT) is an advanced EBRT using many small beams of different strengths to deliver high radiation doses while sparing normal tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUTROPHILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neutrophils are a type of granulocyte (white blood cell) that help prevent and control infection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neutrophils are a type of granulocyte involved in fighting infections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neutrophils are a type of granulocyte, a white blood cell that fights infections."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEMCITABINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gemcitabine is an antimetabolite chemotherapy drug used in breast cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTATE DEHYDROGENASE (LDH)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enzyme test that measures levels of LDH; high levels can indicate cell damage from cancer or other conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDH is a tumor marker found in higher amounts in LCOCs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactate dehydrogenase (LDH) is an enzyme released by dying or fast-growing cells, such as tumor cells, and is measured in blood tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactate dehydrogenase is an enzyme found in most cells; dying cells and fast-growing cells release LDH into blood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactate dehydrogenase is an enzyme that can be elevated in AML, indicating cell damage or rapid cell turnover, and is used as a marker of disease activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OCCUPATIONAL THERAPIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An occupational therapist assists patients in performing daily activities and maintaining independence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC SQUAMOUS CELL SKIN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic squamous cell skin cancer is a form of the disease that has spread to other parts of the body, requiring systemic therapy when surgery and radiation are not options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic squamous cell skin cancer is a type of CSCC that has spread beyond lymph nodes, requiring advanced treatment considerations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROCYSTIC AND TUBULAR SUBTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rare subtype of urothelial cancer with microcystic and tubular features."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOACTIVE SUBSTANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blue-colored substance injected near a tumor to help locate sentinel lymph nodes during biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radioactive substance is injected into the cervix during sentinel lymph node biopsy to identify sentinel nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radioactive substance, also called a tracer, is injected into the bloodstream during a PET scan to highlight cancerous cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOW FAR THE CANCER EXTENDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"How far the cancer extends refers to the extent of primary CNS lymphoma within the central nervous system, determined by tests after diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-CELL ALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-cell ALL (B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia) is a subtype of ALL that affects B-cell lymphocytes, with a rare mature B-cell form called Burkitt leukemia, which is treated differently from B-ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARYNX (VOICE BOX)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larynx (voice box) is a part of the body examined during laryngoscopy and fiberoptic nasopharyngolaryngoscopy to look for tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood cells include red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets, which are produced by hematopoietic stem cells in the bone marrow. Cancer treatment can reduce their numbers, leading to various side effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VON HIPPEL-LINDAU SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome (VHL) is a hereditary condition linked to an increased risk of adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METHOTREXATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Methotrexate is a chemotherapy drug effective against primary CNS lymphoma. It works by blocking folate use, preventing lymphoma cells from multiplying. High doses are needed to cross the blood-brain barrier."&lt;SEP&gt;"Methotrexate is a chemotherapy drug included in the ddMVAC combination for bladder cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Methotrexate is a chemotherapy drug that is the main treatment for primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Methotrexate is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by inhibiting folic acid metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Methotrexate is a chemotherapy drug, specifically high-dose methotrexate, used to treat primary CNS lymphoma, but can cause damage to kidneys, liver, and other organs, requiring hospital stay and fluids during treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Methotrexate is an antimetabolite chemotherapy drug used in breast cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Methotrexate is an antimetabolite chemotherapy drug used to treat AML, including intrathecal administration for AML in the spinal fluid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Methotrexate is an antimetabolite chemotherapy drug used to treat AML, including intrathecal administration for spinal fluid involvement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Methotrexate is the main chemotherapy drug used to treat primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B12&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B12 is a vitamin measured in blood tests, relevant in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamin B12 is a nutrient measured in blood tests to assess overall health and rule out other causes of blood abnormalities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EOSINOPHILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eosinophils are a type of granulocyte involved in allergic responses and fighting parasites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eosinophils are a type of granulocyte, a white blood cell involved in fighting infections and allergic reactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPEECH THERAPIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specialist who tests and helps improve speech and swallowing abilities before and after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A speech therapist helps patients with speech and swallowing difficulties that may arise from treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEMIPLIMAB-RWLC (LIBTAYO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cemiplimab-rwlc (Libtayo) is an immunotherapy drug suggested before surgery for regional CSCC to shrink tumors and reduce surgical risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 0 BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage where abnormal cells are present on the inner lining of the bladder but have not invaded the muscle layer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WOUND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An injury to the skin or tissue that requires healing, often after surgical procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-CELL ALL (B-ALL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-cell ALL (B-ALL) is a subtype of Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia that starts in B-cell lymphocytes. It is more common than T-ALL. A rare subtype is mature B-cell ALL (Burkitt leukemia), which is similar to Burkitt lymphoma but treated differently. In some cases, B-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in lymph nodes, leading to B-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma (B-LL or B-LBL)."&lt;SEP&gt;"B-cell ALL or B-ALL is a subtype of ALL that starts in B-cell lymphocytes. It is more common than T-ALL. A rare subtype is mature B-cell ALL (Burkitt leukemia), which is similar to Burkitt lymphoma but treated differently."&lt;SEP&gt;"B-cell ALL or B-ALL is a type of Acute lymphoblastic leukemia that starts in B-cell lymphocytes. It is more common than T-ALL. A rare subtype is mature B-cell ALL, also called Burkitt leukemia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-CELL LYMPHOBLASTIC LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma (B-LL or B-LBL) occurs when B-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in lymph nodes instead of bone marrow."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALLERGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Allergy is a condition where the body reacts adversely to substances like contrast material, affecting test choices."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARE TEAM COMMUNICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Care Team Communication is discussing concerns with healthcare providers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLDER PERSONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Older persons are a demographic group mentioned as having a higher rate of bone marrow involvement and more advanced-stage disease in the context of MGZL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONCOLOGY PHARMACISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oncology pharmacists are experts in using medicines to treat cancer and manage symptoms and side effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXEMESTANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Exemestane is a steroidal aromatase inhibitor used in endocrine therapy for breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exemestane is an endocrine therapy drug used in breast cancer treatment, often taken with everolimus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Folic acid (folate) helps the body make new proteins and is needed for normal red blood cell and white blood cell formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Folic acid (folate) is a nutrient that helps the body make new proteins and is needed for normal blood cell formation, with levels monitored."&lt;SEP&gt;"Folic acid is a vitamin measured in blood tests to evaluate nutritional status and rule out deficiencies that can affect blood cell production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Folic acid is a vitamin measured in blood tests, relevant in AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASOPHILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Basophils are a type of granulocyte involved in inflammatory responses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Basophils are a type of granulocyte, a white blood cell involved in inflammatory responses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAUSEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nausea and vomiting are possible side effects of RAI therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea and vomiting are symptoms of gliomas, often due to increased pressure in the brain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a common side effect during EBRT."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a common side effect of cancer therapy, such as chemotherapy, which can be managed to prevent interference with treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a common side effect of cancer treatment, such as chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a common side effect of chemotherapy and radiation therapy, which can be managed with medications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a common side effect of chemotherapy regimens discussed in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a common side effect of chemotherapy regimens for anal cancer, manageable with supportive care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a common side effect of chemotherapy, caused by damage to fast-growing cells in the digestive tract."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a common side effect of chemotherapy, managed with anti-nausea medications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a common side effect of high-dose chemotherapy, often managed with medications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a short-term side effect of radiation therapy for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a side effect of chemotherapy and radiation, often managed with medications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, often caused by increased pressure in the brain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nausea is a symptom that can occur in adrenal cancer, especially if the tumor presses on nearby organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAD AND NECK TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Head and neck tumors refer to CSCC located in the head or neck region, requiring specific surgical considerations for lymph node removal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1 BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A stage where a tumor has formed and invaded the connective tissue layer of the bladder wall but not the muscle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAD AND NECK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Areas of the body where radiation therapy can be very effective for treating small tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-CELL ALL (T-ALL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-cell ALL (T-ALL) is a subtype of Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia that starts in T-cell lymphocytes. It can cause an enlarged thymus, leading to breathing problems due to pressure on the windpipe and blood vessels. In some cases, T-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the thymus, leading to T-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma (T-LL or T-LBL)."&lt;SEP&gt;"T-cell ALL or T-ALL is a subtype of ALL that starts in T-cell lymphocytes. It can cause an enlarged thymus, leading to breathing problems. In some cases, T-cell lymphoblasts grow in the thymus instead of bone marrow, called T-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"T-cell ALL or T-ALL is a type of Acute lymphoblastic leukemia that starts in T-cell lymphocytes. It is less common than B-ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-CELL LYMPHOBLASTIC LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma (T-LL or T-LBL) occurs when T-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the thymus instead of bone marrow."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-CLEAR CELL RCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-clear cell RCC (nccRCC) is a category of renal cell carcinoma subtypes other than clear cell, including papillary, chromophobe, translocation, and unclassified types."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLL SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CLL specialist is a doctor who provides consultation and advice on CLL, as mentioned in a patient testimonial."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T1 PELVIC TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T1 pelvic tumor is confined to 1 pelvic segment without growth outside the bone, with subcategories T1a (≤8 cm) and T1b (&gt;8 cm)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FULVESTRANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fulvestrant (Faslodex) is a SERD used in endocrine therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fulvestrant (Faslodex) is a selective estrogen receptor degrader (SERD) used in endocrine therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fulvestrant is an endocrine therapy drug used in breast cancer treatment, sometimes taken with everolimus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD CLOTTING TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood clotting tests assess the ability of blood to clot, which is important in AML because low platelets or other factors can increase bleeding risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood clotting tests assess the blood's ability to clot, part of AML testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood clotting tests assess the body's ability to stop bleeding by forming clots, involving coagulation factors produced by the liver."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood clotting tests assess the process of turning blood into a gel-like form to form a blood clot, involving coagulation factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONOCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Monocytes are a type of white blood cell that fight infections and are part of the immune system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Monocytes are a type of white blood cell that fight infections, included in the white blood cell category."&lt;SEP&gt;"Monocytes are a type of white blood cell that fight infections. They are part of the white blood cell family, which also includes granulocytes and lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Monocytes are a type of white blood cell that fight infections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Monocytes are a type of white blood cell that helps fight infections by engulfing pathogens."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOMITING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vomiting is a common side effect of chemotherapy and radiation therapy, which can be managed with medications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vomiting is a common side effect of chemotherapy regimens discussed in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vomiting is a common side effect of chemotherapy, often managed with antiemetic medications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vomiting is a common side effect of chemotherapy, resulting from damage to fast-growing cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vomiting is a possible side effect of RAI therapy, often accompanied by nausea."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vomiting is a side effect of cancer therapy, often occurring with nausea, and requires management to maintain treatment continuity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vomiting is a side effect of cancer treatment that can affect quality of life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vomiting is a side effect of high-dose chemotherapy, which can be reduced with antiemetic medicines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vomiting is a symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, often caused by increased pressure in the brain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vomiting is a symptom that can occur in adrenal cancer, especially if the tumor presses on nearby organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Extracapsular extension (or extranodal extension) is a condition where cancer grows through the protective outer layer of lymph nodes, influencing treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extracapsular or extranodal extension refers to cancer growing through the protective outer layer of lymph nodes, which is a factor in determining the need for systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2 BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A muscle-invasive stage where the tumor has invaded the muscle layer of the bladder wall."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCALP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An area of the body where CSCC may not heal well after radiation due to weakened tissues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scalp is the area where a small portion of hair is trimmed before making an opening in the skull during a stereotactic biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-CELL LYMPHOBLASTIC LYMPHOMA (B-LL OR B-LBL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma (B-LL or B-LBL) occurs when B-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the lymph nodes instead of in the bone marrow, as a variant of B-cell ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"B-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma is a condition where B-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in lymph nodes instead of bone marrow, related to B-ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEDIATRIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pediatric refers to ALL found in infants, children, and young adults, including anyone 18 years or under and certain adolescents and young adults (AYAs)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEIGHBOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neighbor is a type of support person who can help a patient during stressful medical times."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTING FOR MOUTH CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Testing for mouth cancer involves various procedures such as imaging tests, biopsies, and biomarker testing to determine the cancer stage and treatment plan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INITIAL SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Initial surgery is when a biopsy is usually performed to diagnose ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOCTOR'S DISCUSSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Doctor's Discussion is the process of reviewing test results with the patient."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINIMALLY INVASIVE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Minimally invasive cancer is less aggressive thyroid cancer that may be treated with lobectomy or watch-and-wait approach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TAMOXIFEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tamoxifen is a selective estrogen receptor modulator (SERM) used to block estrogen in breast cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tamoxifen is an endocrine therapy drug used in breast cancer treatment, sometimes taken with everolimus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE MARROW ASPIRATE AND BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone marrow aspirate and biopsy are diagnostic procedures used to analyze bone marrow cells for AML diagnosis and treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow aspirate and biopsy are diagnostic procedures used to assess FL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow aspirate and biopsy are procedures involving the removal of a sample of tissue or group of cells for testing. They are used to confirm a diagnosis of AML by examining the bone marrow for the presence of myeloblasts and other abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow aspirate and biopsy are procedures where samples of bone and liquid bone marrow are removed for testing, often used in diagnosing and monitoring AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow aspirate and biopsy is a procedure to collect bone marrow samples for analysis, including AML biomarker and genetic testing, to confirm diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow aspirate and biopsy is a procedure to collect bone marrow samples for biomarker and genetic testing, crucial for AML diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLASTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blasts are immature white blood cells committed to becoming a type of blood cell; in AML, abnormal myeloblasts are found."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blasts are immature white blood cells; high numbers in blood or bone marrow are indicative of leukemia, such as AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blasts are very immature blood cells, including myeloblasts and lymphoblasts, that are often increased in advanced CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blasts is a general term for very immature cells like myeloblasts or lymphoblasts in CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blasts or leukemia cells can sometimes be detected in the blood and usually are reported as a percentage of cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIARRHEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diarrhea is a common side effect during EBRT."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diarrhea is a common side effect of chemotherapy regimens discussed in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diarrhea is a common side effect of chemotherapy, requiring hydration and management strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diarrhea is a common side effect of systemic therapy, including chemotherapy and targeted therapy. It can lead to dehydration and requires management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diarrhea is a possible side effect of chemotherapy, which can be managed with medications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diarrhea is a short-term side effect of radiation therapy for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diarrhea is a side effect of brachytherapy, causing loose or watery stools."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diarrhea is a side effect of chemotherapy and immunotherapy, causing digestive issues that need treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diarrhea is a side effect of high-dose chemotherapy, affecting the digestive system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NERVE INVASION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nerve invasion, where the tumor has grown into a nerve or group of nerves, indicates a high-risk or very high-risk cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3 BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A muscle-invasive stage where the tumor has grown into the fat layer around the bladder, possibly affecting nearby lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EYE AREA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A region where CSCC radiation can lead to cataracts as a long-term side effect."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-CELL LYMPHOBLASTIC LYMPHOMA (T-LL OR T-LBL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma (T-LL or T-LBL) occurs when T-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the thymus instead of in the bone marrow, as a variant of T-cell ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"T-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma is a condition where T-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the thymus instead of bone marrow, related to T-ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AYAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AYAs (adolescents and young adults) are those 15 to 39 years of age at the time of initial cancer diagnosis, who may be treated in pediatric or adult centers depending on the type of cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COWORKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coworker is a type of support person who can help a patient during stressful medical times."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAOCULAR CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intraocular chemotherapy is a type of chemotherapy where drugs are infused directly into the eye to treat primary CNS lymphoma occurring in the eye, with possible side effects including eye irritation, infection, inflammation, and cataracts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABDOMINOPERINEAL RESECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abdominoperineal Resection (APR) is a surgical procedure removing the anus, rectum, and part of the colon, often resulting in a colostomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEFT VENTRICULAR EJECTION FRACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) is a measure of heart function, monitored before and during trastuzumab treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAIN CT WITHOUT CONTRAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A brain CT without contrast is an imaging test used if central nervous system bleeding is suspected in AML patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain CT without contrast is an imaging test used if central nervous system bleeding is suspected in AML patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGENITOR CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Progenitor cells (or precursor cells) are intermediaries that develop from blood stem cells and become specific blood cell types. They include lymphoid progenitor cells and myeloid progenitor cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Progenitor cells are intermediaries that become red blood cells, white blood cells, or platelets, including lymphoid and myeloid progenitor cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Progenitor cells are intermediary cells that develop from blood stem cells and mature into specific blood cell types."&lt;SEP&gt;"Progenitor cells, also called precursor cells, are intermediaries that develop from blood stem cells into specific blood cell types."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALLIATIVE CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Palliative Care is specialized medical care focused on relieving symptoms and improving quality of life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Palliative care focuses on relieving symptoms and improving quality of life for breast cancer patients, regardless of stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Palliative care focuses on relieving symptoms and improving quality of life for cervical cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Palliative care is a form of supportive care for advanced cancers, focusing on symptom relief and improving quality of life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Palliative care, also called supportive care, focuses on relieving symptoms and improving quality of life for patients with serious illnesses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR DEPTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor depth refers to how deep the tumor has invaded into the skin, with deeper invasion increasing the risk of recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 4 BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic bladder cancer that has spread outside the bladder to distant sites in the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTRONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Type of radiation beam used to treat superficial tumors in external beam radiation therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADOLESCENT AND YOUNG ADULT (AYA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An adolescent and young adult (AYA) is someone 15 to 39 years of age at the time of initial cancer diagnosis. AYAs are a unique group that can be treated by pediatric or adult oncologists."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACUTE LYMPHOBLASTIC LEUKEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) is a type of blood cancer that affects lymphocytes, most often B cells or T cells, and is characterized by too many abnormal white blood cells (lymphoblasts)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRI MACHINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MRI machine is the equipment used in magnetic resonance imaging, with open and closed types."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEM CELL REMOVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stem cell removal is the first step in stem cell rescue, where healthy stem cells are collected from the patient's blood or bone marrow, then frozen and stored for later use."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRENAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adrenal cancer, also called adrenocortical cancer (ACC), is a rare cancer that starts in one or both of the adrenal glands. It can occur at any age but is most likely to affect children under 5 and adults in their 40s and 50s. If caught early, it can be cured, but if it spreads, cure becomes less likely."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRECURSOR CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Precursor cells are another name for progenitor cells, which develop into mature blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Precursor cells are another term for progenitor cells, which are early cells that differentiate into mature blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Precursor cells are cells that develop into specialized cells like astrocytes and oligodendrocytes, and they are the origin of glioblastomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSA DENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSA density is a calculated value that adjusts PSA level for prostate size, providing a more accurate risk assessment for prostate cancer. It is derived by dividing PSA level by prostate volume, measured via ultrasound or MRI."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAIN MRI WITH CONTRAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A brain MRI with contrast is an imaging test used if leukemic meningitis is suspected, helping detect leukemia in the central nervous system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain MRI with contrast is an imaging test used if leukemic meningitis is suspected."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALLIED HEALTH PROVIDERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Allied health providers are trained professionals who support patient care, such as therapists, nutritionists, and social workers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL EVALUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgical evaluation is the process of determining if a patient is a candidate for surgery to remove cancerous lesions and nearby lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAVESICAL THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A treatment for bladder cancer where medication is placed directly into the bladder through a catheter."&lt;SEP&gt;"A treatment that involves filling the bladder with liquid medication to destroy cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intravesical therapy involves placing cancer medicine directly into the bladder via a catheter, using a process called instillation, to treat bladder cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intravesical therapy is a treatment for bladder cancer involving medication directly into the bladder, causing side effects like inflammation, frequent urination, and pain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intravesical therapy is a treatment method where medicine is placed directly into the bladder via a catheter to destroy cancer cells that are not visible or hard to reach."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intravesical therapy is a treatment often done in combination with TURBT, involving the administration of medication directly into the bladder to treat bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAVENOUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method of administering systemic therapy through the veins."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intravenous refers to the method of delivering chemotherapy directly into the bloodstream through a vein."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADULT CANCER CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adult cancer center is a treatment facility for AYAs or others with ALL, as opposed to pediatric centers, with guidelines available from NCCN."&lt;SEP&gt;"An adult cancer center is a medical facility that provides treatment and care for adults with cancer, and this book is intended for those being treated at such a center."&lt;SEP&gt;"An adult cancer center is a medical facility where AYAs and adults are treated for ALL, as referenced in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATURAL KILLER (NK) CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Natural killer (NK) cells are a type of lymphocyte that can kill tumor cells or virus-infected cells. They are not typically affected in ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Natural killer (NK) cells are a type of lymphocyte that can kill tumor cells or virus-infected cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Natural killer (NK) cells are a type of lymphocyte with granules containing enzymes that can kill tumor cells or cells infected with a virus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FDG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FDG (F-18 fluorodeoxyglucose) is a specific radiotracer used in PET/CT scans, made of fluoride and glucose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN RESOURCE ACCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN Resource Access is using NCCN guidelines and app for fertility information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE MARROW INVOLVEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone marrow involvement refers to the spread of cancer cells to the bone marrow, which is more common in older persons with MGZL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALLIATIVE CARE NURSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Palliative care nurses are part of the care team, providing extra support for symptom management and quality of life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Palliative care nurses provide extra support with cancer-related care, focusing on symptom management and quality of life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENTIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Differentiation is the process by which blood stem cells gradually develop into mature blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Differentiation is the process by which blood stem cells gradually develop into specific types of blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Differentiation is the process by which blood stem cells mature into specific types of blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Differentiation is the process by which blood stem cells mature through various stages to become red blood cells, white blood cells, or platelets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Differentiation is the process by which blood stem cells mature through various stages to become specific blood cell types, such as red blood cells, white blood cells, or platelets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade Group is a classification based on biopsy results that helps determine the risk group of prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grade Group is a classification system that groups prostate cancer based on Gleason scores to predict prognosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grade Group is a classification system that interprets Gleason scores into five groups (1-5) to estimate prostate cancer aggressiveness. Higher groups indicate more aggressive cancer, with Group 1 corresponding to Gleason 6 and Group 5 to Gleason 9-10."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grade Group is a system used to classify prostate cancer based on Gleason scores, ranging from Grade Group 1 (lowest risk) to Grade Group 5 (highest risk), with Grade Groups 2 and 3 indicating intermediate risk and Grade Groups 4 and 5 predicting high and very high risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FDG-PET/CT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FDG-PET/CT is a combined imaging test that detects metabolic activity of cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"FDG-PET/CT is a combined imaging test using fluorodeoxyglucose radiotracer to detect cancer in lymph nodes and distant sites, requiring fasting before the scan."&lt;SEP&gt;"FDG-PET/CT is a specialized imaging test that combines PET and CT to detect cancer spread and metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"FDG-PET/CT is a specific PET/CT scan using fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG) as a radiotracer to detect cancer cell activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"FDG-PET/CT is a specific PET/CT scan using fluorodeoxyglucose as a radiotracer to detect cancer metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"FDG-PET/CT is a specific type of PET/CT scan using fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG) as a radiotracer, requiring fasting before the procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"FDG-PET/CT is a specific type of PET/CT scan using fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG) as a radiotracer. It is used when other imaging results are unclear, helping to find cancer in lymph nodes and distant sites. Patients must fast for at least 4 hours before the scan."&lt;SEP&gt;"FDG-PET/CT is a specific type of PET/CT scan using the radiotracer F-18 fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG), helpful when other imaging results are unclear, and can identify cancer in primary sites, lymph nodes, and distant sites."&lt;SEP&gt;"FDG-PET/CT is an imaging test used if leukemia outside the blood and bone marrow (extramedullary) is suspected."&lt;SEP&gt;"FDG-PET/CT is an imaging test used to detect distant metastases in NPC patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"FDG-PET/CT is an imaging test used to detect leukemia outside the blood and bone marrow, such as extramedullary disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NURSE PRACTITIONER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nurse practitioner can provide cervical cancer screening and patient education."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nurse practitioner is an advanced practice nurse who can diagnose and treat conditions, often part of the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nurse practitioner is an advanced practice provider who can help prevent, evaluate, examine, and diagnose diseases including breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEMIPLIMAB-RWLC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cemiplimab-rwlc is an immunotherapy drug used to shrink tumors before surgery in regional CSCC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSURETHRAL RESECTION OF BLADDER TUMOR (TURBT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure that removes bladder tumors through the urethra without abdominal incision, used for diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"TURBT is a surgical procedure used to examine and remove tumors on the bladder wall, often used for diagnosis and treatment of early-stage bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PILL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An oral form of systemic therapy taken by mouth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEDIATRIC CANCER CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pediatric cancer center is a medical facility where AYAs may seek ALL treatment, with more information available at NCCN.org."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pediatric cancer center is a treatment facility for children and AYAs with ALL, as referenced in the book."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 2: TESTING FOR ALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 2: Testing for ALL provides an overview of tests a child might receive, how fertility might be impacted by treatment, and the role of genetic and biomarker mutation testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINE-NEEDLE BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fine-needle biopsy is a procedure to sample small areas of cancer, often guided by ultrasound or CT."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY COUNSELOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility counselor is a professional who helps patients learn about fertility preservation options before starting treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T2 PELVIC TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T2 pelvic tumor is confined to 1 pelvic segment with growth outside the bone, or 2 segments without growth outside, with subcategories T2a and T2b."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOPOIETIC STEM CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hematopoietic stem cells (blood stem cells) are early cells in bone marrow that develop into all types of blood cells. They are the origin of all blood cell types, including those affected in ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hematopoietic stem cells are blood stem cells in bone marrow that create all types of blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hematopoietic stem cells are blood-forming cells made in the bone marrow. They can develop into any type of blood cell and are used in stem cell rescue to regrow healthy bone marrow after cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hematopoietic stem cells are blood-forming stem cells in bone marrow that give rise to all blood cell types."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hematopoietic stem cells are early blood-forming cells in bone marrow that give rise to all blood cell types."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hematopoietic stem cells are early blood-forming cells in bone marrow that multiply and differentiate into blood cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLEASON SCORE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gleason score is a grading system that assesses the aggressiveness of prostate cancer based on biopsy samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gleason score is a numerical system used to grade prostate cancer aggressiveness, with scores from 6 to 10, where higher scores indicate more aggressive cancer; it is used to assign Grade Groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gleason score is a numerical value (6-10) derived from the two most common Gleason patterns in a biopsy sample, indicating how much the cancer resembles normal prostate tissue and its potential aggressiveness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEUKEMIC MENINGITIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leukemic meningitis is a condition where leukemia cells spread to the membranes covering the brain and spinal cord, requiring MRI or lumbar puncture for diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leukemic meningitis is a condition where leukemia spreads to the meninges, suspected and diagnosed with brain MRI or lumbar puncture."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICIAN ASSISTANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A physician assistant is a healthcare provider who practices medicine under a doctor's supervision, contributing to patient care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Physician assistant is an advanced practice provider who can help prevent, evaluate, examine, and diagnose diseases including breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIBTAYO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Libtayo is the brand name for cemiplimab-rwlc, an immunotherapy drug used in CSCC treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAT LAYER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The layer of fat around the bladder that stage 3 cancer has grown into."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATINUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A metal used in chemotherapy drugs like cisplatin and carboplatin to treat cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platinum is a metal contained in cisplatin, a chemotherapy drug used for bladder cancer, which can be effective but may damage kidneys."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHOCYTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymphocyte is a type of white blood cell found in blood and lymph tissue, helping fight and prevent infection, with three main types: B lymphocytes, T lymphocytes, and natural killer (NK) cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphocyte is a type of white blood cell, with B cells and T cells being the main types involved in ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 3: TYPES OF TREATMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 3: Types of treatments gives a general overview of treatment, including steroids and multiagent chemotherapy for everyone with ALL, and other systemic therapy options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIBEROPTIC LIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fiberoptic light is a component of a laryngoscope that illuminates the throat area during examination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUCOSAL LIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The mucosal lip is the inner part of the lip where mouth cancer can develop."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The tumor is a differentiated high-grade carcinoma, indicating a specific type of thyroid cancer with aggressive features."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENT PORTAL ACCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patient Portal Access is the ability to view records online, which can be printed for the binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYSTECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cystectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the bladder, with radical cystectomy removing the entire bladder, nearby lymph nodes, and other organs, and partial cystectomy removing only part of the bladder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER CENTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer centers are leading medical institutions where experts develop and practice current cancer care recommendations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer centers are medical facilities that provide comprehensive cancer care, including social work services to manage anxiety and navigate financial and insurance complexities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer centers are specialized medical facilities with experience in performing interstitial brachytherapy for advanced cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer centers are specialized medical facilities with experience in treating gray zone lymphomas, recommended for MGZL patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLEASON PATTERNS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gleason patterns are numbers (1-5) assigned by a pathologist based on the appearance of cancer cells under a microscope, with lower numbers indicating more normal-looking cells and higher numbers indicating more abnormal cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRAMEDULLARY DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Extramedullary disease refers to leukemia that has spread outside the blood and bone marrow, such as to organs or tissues, detected via imaging tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOCIAL WORKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A professional who provides counseling and support to cancer patients and their families dealing with emotional distress."&lt;SEP&gt;"A social worker assists patients with practical and emotional needs, such as navigating healthcare systems and providing counseling."&lt;SEP&gt;"A social worker provides emotional and practical support to breast cancer patients, helping with resources and coping strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A social worker provides emotional and practical support to cervical cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Social Worker is a professional who helps patients navigate emotional, financial, and logistical challenges related to cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1A CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1A cervical cancer is an early stage where the tumor is 5 millimeters or smaller, with sub-stages 1A1 (≤3 mm) and 1A2 (3-5 mm)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIDE EFFECTS OF TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unwanted effects that may occur as a result of cancer treatments, such as pain or blood in urine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN REDNESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A short-term side effect of radiation therapy, along with itching and mild discomfort."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin redness and irritation are common side effects during EBRT."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-CELL LYMPHOCYTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-cell lymphocytes are a type of lymphocyte that can become cancerous in B-ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 4: SUPPORTIVE CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 4: Supportive care discusses what supportive care is and possible side effects of treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLEXIBLE SCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flexible scope is a type of scope used in fiberoptic laryngoscopy, passed through the nose into the throat."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DHEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DHEA is a hormone that influences body features, produced by the adrenal cortex."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMORADIATION REGIMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemoradiation Regimen is a specific combination of chemotherapy drugs and radiation therapy used for anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASAL CELL SKIN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Basal cell skin cancer is a type of skin cancer that can recur or metastasize, and its treatment is discussed in the text, including testing and management options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Basal cell skin cancer, also known as basal cell carcinoma (BCC), is the most common type of skin cancer, with about 3 million cases diagnosed annually in the United States. It is highly treatable and curable, especially when caught early, and rarely metastasizes. It develops in the basal cells of the epidermis, often in sun-exposed areas like the face, head, neck, arms, legs, and trunk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RISK GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Risk group is a classification that combines PSA level, Grade Group, tumor stage, and biopsy results to determine the likely course and outcome of prostate cancer, guiding treatment intensity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNG CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lung cancer is a broad category of cancers originating in the lungs, including NSCLC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung cancer is a disease characterized by uncontrolled cell growth in the lungs, with subtypes including non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) and small cell lung cancer (SCLC). It is a major health concern, with risk factors including smoking and secondhand smoke exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung cancer is a disease that starts in the cells of the lungs. It includes subtypes such as non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) and small cell lung cancer (SCLC), and is often linked to risk factors like smoking."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung cancer is a disease where lung cells grow out of control, forming tumors and potentially spreading, with NSCLC being a major subtype."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung cancer is a type of cancer associated with smoking and vaping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the lungs, mentioned as a contrast to AML because it has stages, unlike AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REHABILITATION SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rehabilitation specialist, including physical, occupational, or speech therapists, helps patients recover function and quality of life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1B1 CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1B1 cervical cancer is a stage where the tumor is larger than 5 mm but smaller than 2 cm, confined to the cervix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical facility where TURBT may be performed."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical facility where cystoscopy may be performed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clinic is a healthcare facility offering testing and counseling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clinic is a medical facility where patients receive outpatient care, including tests and consultations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATARACTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A serious long-term side effect of radiation therapy for CSCC in the eye area."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cataracts are a possible side effect of intraocular chemotherapy, treatable with routine surgery by an eye surgeon."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cataracts are a potential side effect of radiation therapy to the eyes, causing clouding of the lens. They can be treated with a routine operation by an eye surgeon."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-CELL LYMPHOCYTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-cell lymphocytes are a type of lymphocyte that can become cancerous in T-ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-LL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-LL (B-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma) is a condition where B-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in lymph nodes instead of bone marrow, also called B-LBL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MODIFIED DCF REGIMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Modified DCF regimen is a chemotherapy protocol involving docetaxel, cisplatin, and fluorouracil, used in the treatment of anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEM CELL REPLACEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stem cell replacement is the final step in stem cell rescue, where thawed healthy stem cells are returned to the patient's body to regrow bone marrow and restore blood cell production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRENAL TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adrenal tumors are tumors found in one or both adrenal glands. Most are benign (not cancer), but some can be cancerous. They can be functioning (producing hormones) or nonfunctioning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPIDERMIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Epidermis is the outermost layer of skin, providing a waterproof barrier and containing squamous cells, basal cells, and melanocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The epidermis is the top layer of skin that is removed during superficial shave biopsies, and is where squamous cell carcinoma originates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The epidermis is the top layer of the skin, providing a waterproof barrier and creating skin color through melanin. It contains squamous cells, basal cells, and melanocytes, and is the layer where most skin cancers form."&lt;SEP&gt;"The outermost layer of skin, part of the area involved in certain biopsy procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSRECTAL ULTRASOUND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transrectal ultrasound is an imaging technique used to measure prostate size, which is essential for calculating PSA density."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Induction is a phase of treatment for primary CNS lymphoma, likely involving initial intensive therapy to achieve remission."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1B2 CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1B2 cervical cancer is a stage where the tumor is between 2 and 4 cm, confined to the cervix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPSY SAMPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A tissue sample taken for examination by a pathologist, often during a second TURBT."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIDER VEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A long-term side effect of radiation therapy, involving visible blood vessels on the skin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-CELL LYMPHOBLASTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-cell lymphoblasts are immature B-cell lymphocytes that can grow in lymph nodes instead of bone marrow, leading to B-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-LBL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-LBL (B-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma) is another name for B-LL, where B-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALLIATIVE RADIATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Palliative radiation therapy is used to limit tumor size and alleviate symptoms in metastatic anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH MONITORING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health Monitoring is tracking organ function and disease signs through tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRA-MEDIASTINAL DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Extra-mediastinal disease refers to cancer found outside the mediastinum, which leads to a diagnosis of DLBCL-NOS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVANCED PRACTICE PROVIDERS (APPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Advanced practice providers (APPs) are health care professionals who help with cancer-related care and support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advanced practice providers are part of the care team, offering additional clinical support in cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DERMIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dermis is the middle layer of skin containing connective tissue, hair follicles, and sweat glands."&lt;SEP&gt;"The dermis is the layer of skin beneath the epidermis, which may be partially removed during shave biopsies and is involved in skin cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"The dermis is the middle layer of the skin, involving connective tissue, blood vessels, oil and sweat glands, nerves, and hair follicles. Skin cancers less commonly occur in this layer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The layer of skin beneath the epidermis, also involved in certain biopsy procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A factor influencing fertility changes related to cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Age is a demographic factor that influences PSA levels, with PSA tending to increase as individuals get older, affecting cancer risk interpretation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Age is a factor affecting fertility loss during cancer treatment, as noted in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Age is a factor in eligibility criteria for clinical trials, determining who can enroll."&lt;SEP&gt;"Age is a factor that can influence cancer risk and treatment outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Age is a risk factor for basal cell skin cancer, as sun exposure builds up over time, increasing the risk. However, skin cancer is becoming more common in younger people."&lt;SEP&gt;"Age is a risk factor for bladder cancer, with risk increasing as a person gets older."&lt;SEP&gt;"Age is the biggest risk factor for prostate cancer, with diagnosis most often in those aged 65 years and above."&lt;SEP&gt;"Age is the biggest risk factor for prostate cancer, with the chances of developing the disease increasing as a person ages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Age is the leading risk factor for prostate cancer, with risk increasing as individuals grow older."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Heart is an organ listened to during a physical exam and assessed through heart tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart is an organ listened to during a physical exam to check for cardiac issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart is an organ listened to during physical exam to check for cardiovascular issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart is an organ that may be bright on PET scans normally."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart is an organ that normally appears bright on PET scans and is the focus of cardiac tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart is an organ that normally appears bright on PET scans due to high metabolic activity, and is not necessarily indicative of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart is an organ that normally appears bright on PET scans due to high metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart is an organ that normally appears bright on PET scans, which is a normal finding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart is an organ that normally appears bright on PET scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart is an organ whose function is assessed by heart tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart is an organ whose function is considered when determining the best systemic therapy for bladder cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organ listened to during a physical exam to assess cardiovascular health."&lt;SEP&gt;"The heart is an organ that may appear bright on PET scans due to normal metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The heart is an organ whose function is assessed through heart tests before certain AML treatments to ensure safety."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSOLIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Consolidation is a phase of treatment following induction, aimed at eliminating any remaining cancer cells and preventing relapse."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1B3 CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1B3 cervical cancer is a specific substage of stage 1, characterized by larger tumor size, requiring FDG-PET/CT scans after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 1B3 cervical cancer is a stage where the tumor is larger than 4 cm, confined to the cervix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLADDER WALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The tissue layers of the bladder, including the lining, connective tissue, muscle, and fat layers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-HEALING ULCERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A serious long-term side effect of radiation therapy, where wounds do not heal properly."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-CELL LYMPHOBLASTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-cell lymphoblasts are immature T-cell lymphocytes that can grow in the thymus instead of bone marrow, leading to T-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-LL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-LL (T-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma) is a condition where T-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the thymus instead of bone marrow, also called T-LBL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHASE I TRIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phase I trials study the safety and side effects of an investigational drug or treatment approach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMOIMMUNOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemoimmunotherapy is a type of treatment that may be targeted based on certain biomarkers in CLL patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T3 PELVIC TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T3 pelvic tumor spans 2 pelvic segments with growth outside the bone, with subcategories T3a and T3b."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPODERMIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hypodermis (subcutis) is the deepest layer of skin, composed of fat and connective tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hypodermis is the deepest tissue layer of the skin, made up of fat and connective tissue. It is not typically a site for skin cancer development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Race is a demographic factor affecting normal PSA levels, with Black males typically having higher PSA levels than white males of the same age, though the reason is under investigation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Race is a demographic factor that can influence cancer risk and access to care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Race is a risk factor, with Black males more likely to develop prostate cancer, at an earlier age, and with more aggressive disease compared to white males."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EYES, EARS, NOSE, AND THROAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eyes, ears, nose, and throat are examined during physical exam to check for signs of disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"These are parts of the body examined during a physical exam to check for signs of disease or infection in AML patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT FOR THE SPINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment for the spine is a specific phase addressing lymphoma involvement in the spinal cord or cerebrospinal fluid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2 CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 2 cervical cancer indicates cancer has spread beyond the cervix to nearby tissues, requiring imaging 3-6 months after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 2 cervical cancer is a stage where the cancer has grown beyond the cervix, with sub-stages 2A (upper vagina involvement) and 2B (parametrium involvement)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT OR PET/MRI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CT or PET/MRI is a combined imaging test used to determine the location of cancer cells, considered more accurate than either scan alone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECOND CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rare long-term risk of radiation therapy, more common in young patients decades later."&lt;SEP&gt;"A second cancer is a new, unrelated cancer that may develop due to genetic risk or treatment side effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MYELOID STEM CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Myeloid stem cells are a type of stem cell that can develop into various blood cells, and AML originates from them."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-LBL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-LBL (T-cell lymphoblastic lymphoma) is another name for T-LL, where T-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the thymus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHASE II TRIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phase II trials study how well a drug or approach works against a specific type of cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUCCAL MUCOSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Buccal (oral) mucosa is the lining inside the cheeks and lips, a site for mouth cancer development."&lt;SEP&gt;"The buccal mucosa is the lining inside the cheeks and lips, a site where mouth cancer can occur."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NECK ULTRASOUND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neck ultrasound is a follow-up imaging test recommended 6 to 12 months after total thyroidectomy to monitor for recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck ultrasound is an imaging procedure used to monitor for the return of thyroid cancer in the neck area, recommended 6 to 12 months after surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIGNS OF DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Signs of Disease are indicators detected through blood tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARTIAL CYSTECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Partial cystectomy is a surgical procedure to remove part of the bladder, rarely used for bladder cancer, and only eligible for fewer than 1 out of 20 people with the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASAL CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Basal cells are found in the lower part of the epidermis and constantly divide to form new cells that replace squamous cells on the skin's surface. Abnormal growth of these cells leads to basal cell skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Basal cells are found in the lower part of the epidermis and constantly divide to form new cells, eventually becoming squamous cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENLARGED PROSTATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enlarged prostate is a condition where the prostate gland increases in size, leading to higher PSA production and potentially affecting cancer risk assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enlarged prostate is a non-cancerous condition that can cause high PSA levels, complicating diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enlarged prostate, also called benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH), is a condition that can push against the bladder and compress the urethra, causing urinary symptoms; it is much more common than prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enlarged prostate, also called benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH), is a non-cancerous condition that can cause urinary symptoms similar to prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD TRANSFUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood transfusion is a procedure to replace red blood cells or platelets, which may be needed in AML if counts are dangerously low."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT FOR THE EYES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment for the eyes is a specific phase addressing lymphoma involvement in the eyes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2A1 CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 2A1 cervical cancer is a sub-stage where the cancer has grown into the upper vagina and is 4 cm or smaller."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FDG-PET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FDG-PET is a type of PET scan that uses a radioactive sugar tracer (18-fluorodeoxyglucose) to detect active cancer cells, which appear brighter in images. It is used to assess the aggressiveness of neuroendocrine tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONNECTIVE TISSUE DISEASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Conditions like lupus or scleroderma that may make radiation therapy inappropriate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WINDPIPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The windpipe is the trachea, near which the thymus is located; an enlarged thymus in T-ALL can cause breathing problems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph tissue includes lymph vessels and lymph nodes, and is where lymphocytes are found."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph tissue includes lymph vessels and lymph nodes, and it is where lymphocytes are found along with blood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph tissue includes lymph vessels and lymph nodes, where lymphocytes are found. It is part of the immune system and is involved in the development and function of lymphocytes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHASE III TRIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phase III trials test a drug or approach against a standard treatment, potentially leading to FDA approval."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER SUBTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Subtype refers to the specific type of cancer based on cell characteristics, which influences treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MELANOCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Melanocytes are cells in the top layer of skin that produce melanin, responsible for skin, hair, and eye color, and protect against UV rays."&lt;SEP&gt;"Melanocytes are cells located in the lower part of the epidermis that produce melanin, which is responsible for hair, skin, and eye color and protects the skin from harmful ultraviolet (UV) rays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sex is an activity that can temporarily increase PSA levels after ejaculation, requiring patients to avoid it before PSA tests for accurate results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PANCREATIC CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer associated with inherited mutations in genes like BRCA1 and BRCA2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pancreatic cancer is a disease characterized by the uncontrolled growth of cells in the pancreas, requiring a series of tests for diagnosis and treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pancreatic cancer is a disease characterized by the uncontrolled growth of cells in the pancreas, with stages ranging from 0 to 4, and is the focus of the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pancreatic cancer is a type of cancer that can be associated with BRCA mutations, increasing risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pancreatic cancer is a type of cancer that can be related to germline mutations in genes like BRCA1 and BRCA2, and is mentioned as a family history factor for germline testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pancreatic cancer is a type of cancer that starts in the pancreas, a gland involved in digestion and blood sugar regulation. It includes subtypes like pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) and neuroendocrine tumors, with a focus on PDAC in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pancreatic cancer is a type of cancer that, when present in family history, may increase prostate cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORTICOSTEROID THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Corticosteroid therapy is a treatment using steroids to reduce inflammation and shrink tumors in primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2A2 CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 2A2 cervical cancer is a sub-stage where the cancer has grown into the upper vagina and is larger than 4 cm."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SSTR-PET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SSTR-PET is a type of PET scan that uses a tracer binding to somatostatin receptors (SSTRs) on cell surfaces, helping to locate adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-RISK TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumors with a higher chance of recurrence, for which adjuvant radiation therapy is recommended."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SQUAMOUS CELL SKIN CANCER (CSCC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Squamous cell skin cancer (CSCC) is a type of skin cancer that can be local, high-risk, or very high-risk, and is treated with surgery, radiation, or systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHILDREN'S CANCER CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Children's cancer center is a treatment facility for pediatric patients with ALL, as referenced in the book."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHASE IV TRIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phase IV trials study the long-term safety and benefits of an FDA-approved treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IV INFUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IV infusion is a method of administering drugs like rituximab directly into the bloodstream through a vein."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNCTIONING TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A functioning tumor is an adrenal tumor that produces excess hormones, leading to symptoms such as weight gain, muscle weakness, and hormonal changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MELANIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Melanin is a pigment produced by melanocytes that gives color to hair, skin, and eyes and filters out harmful UV rays from the sun, reducing the risk of skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Melanin is a pigment produced by melanocytes that gives color to hair, skin, and eyes and protects against UV rays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXERCISE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Exercise is a lifestyle activity that may decrease the aggressiveness of prostate cancer and the likelihood of dying from it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exercise is a lifestyle factor that may decrease the aggressiveness of prostate cancer and likelihood of dying from it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exercise is a physical activity that can help cancer patients manage stress and improve overall well-being."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exercise is a physical activity that can temporarily raise PSA levels, and patients are advised to avoid vigorous exercise before PSA testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTIDISCIPLINARY CONSULT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A multidisciplinary consult is a meeting of experts from different fields to discuss and plan pancreatic cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Multidisciplinary consult is a meeting where a care team reviews health records, performs physical exams, and discusses diagnosis and treatment options for pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEM CELL RESCUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A procedure that restores blood-forming stem cells after high-dose chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stem cell rescue is a procedure that uses the patient's own stem cells to restore bone marrow after high-dose chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stem cell rescue is a treatment procedure that is an essential part of chemotherapy for primary CNS lymphoma, involving the use of stem cells to help the body recover after high-dose chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stem cell rescue, also known as hematopoietic stem cell transplant, is a procedure to regrow bone marrow after high-dose chemotherapy. It involves removing, freezing, and re-infusing healthy stem cells to restore blood cell production. It is used after other treatments or in cases of relapse."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2B CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 2B cervical cancer is a sub-stage where the cancer has grown into the parametrium, the fat and connective tissue around the cervix and uterus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOCHEMICAL TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biochemical tests measure hormones in blood, urine, or saliva that may be produced by adrenal tumors, helping to diagnose related syndromes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTROCARDIOGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Electrocardiogram (ECG or EKG) is a heart test that records electrical activity to assess heart rate, rhythm, and potential abnormalities like prolonged QTc interval."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOTODYNAMIC THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Photodynamic therapy (PDT) is a superficial treatment where a light-sensitive drug is applied to the skin and activated by light to kill cancer cells, with side effects including itching and pain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Photodynamic therapy is a treatment option for actinic keratoses, using a photosensitizing agent and light to destroy abnormal cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Photodynamic therapy is a treatment option for actinic keratoses, using light to activate a photosensitizing agent to destroy abnormal cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMARKER MUTATION TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biomarker mutation testing is a type of testing for ALL that looks at biomarkers, as mentioned in Chapter 2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THOM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thom is an anal cancer survivor who shares a personal quote about staying focused on recovery, illustrating the emotional journey of treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thom is an anal cancer survivor who shares advice about staying calm, being organized, and advocating for oneself during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISEASE DETECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Disease Detection is identifying cancer through blood and imaging tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDIASTINUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The mediastinum is the area in the chest between the lungs, where MGZL typically occurs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIATION THERAPISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiation therapists are part of the care team, delivering radiotherapy treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation therapists provide hands-on delivery of radiotherapy treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UV RADIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"UV radiation, from the sun or tanning beds, is a primary cause of basal cell skin cancer. It can damage DNA inside basal skin cells, leading to abnormal cell growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRUGS AND SUPPLEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A list of all prescription drugs, over-the-counter medicines, supplements, vitamins, and herbs that the patient takes, which can interfere with cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Drugs and supplements are substances that can affect PSA levels, potentially altering test results and cancer risk interpretation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOSCOPIC TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endoscopic tests are diagnostic procedures used to examine the pancreas and surrounding areas for signs of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endoscopic tests are part of the series of tests needed to identify pancreatic cancer and make a treatment plan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHOLE-BRAIN RADIATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Whole-brain radiation therapy is a radiation technique that treats the entire brain, commonly used for primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3A CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3A cervical cancer is a stage where the cancer has grown into the lower third of the vagina."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUNLIGHT/OUTDOOR TANNING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sunlight/outdoor tanning is a major risk factor for squamous cell skin cancer, caused by prolonged sun exposure over many years."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECHOCARDIOGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An echocardiogram (or echo) is a diagnostic test that uses sound waves (ultrasound) to create pictures of the heart. It shows the structure (valves and muscle thickness) and function (ejection fraction) of the heart, helping to assess heart function, particularly in relation to treatments that may affect the heart, such as certain chemotherapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"An echocardiogram uses sound waves to create pictures of the heart, tracking heartbeat and assessing heart function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Echocardiogram (echo) is an ultrasound-based heart test that visualizes heart structure and function, including ejection fraction, to evaluate cardiac performance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECURRENT TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Recurrent tumors are cancers that have returned after treatment, considered high-risk squamous cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVASIVE BREAST CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breast cancer that has spread from the milk ducts or lobules into surrounding breast tissue or nearby lymph nodes, potentially spreading further via lymph or blood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Invasive breast cancer is breast cancer that has spread from the milk ducts or lobules into surrounding breast tissue or nearby lymph nodes, potentially leading to metastasis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Invasive breast cancer is breast cancer that has spread from the milk ducts or lobules into surrounding breast tissue or nearby lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Invasive breast cancer is cancer that has grown outside the ducts or lobules into surrounding tissue, and can spread through lymph or blood to other parts of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SORES IN THE MOUTH AND LINING OF THE ANUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sores in the mouth and lining of the anus are common side effects of chemotherapy regimens discussed in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CUTANEOUS LYMPHOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary cutaneous lymphomas are a group of lymphomas that start in the skin, and Cutaneous B-cell lymphoma (CBCL) is one type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN LESIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skin lesions are abnormal growths or sores on the skin that can be signs of basal cell skin cancer. They can appear as flat pale areas, red patches, shiny bumps, or open sores that don't heal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR STAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor stage is a classification of how far cancer has spread, used in determining the risk group of prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor stage is a measure of cancer extent and spread, used alongside PSA level and Grade Group to determine risk group and guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC TESTS FOR INHERITED MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic tests for inherited mutations are used to identify genetic changes that may increase the risk of pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL NERVOUS SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Central nervous system includes the brain and spinal cord, where glial cells and gliomas are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central nervous system is the part of the body including the brain and spinal cord, where gliomas originate."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central nervous system (CNS) includes the brain and spinal cord, and is the primary site where primary CNS lymphoma occurs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central nervous system includes the brain and spinal cord, and ALL can be found in organs such as the testicles or the central nervous system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central nervous system includes the brain and spinal cord, where gliomas develop and cause functional problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central nervous system includes the brain and spinal cord, where primary CNS lymphoma occurs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3B CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3B cervical cancer is a stage where the cancer has grown into the pelvic wall and/or has caused kidney swelling or dysfunction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDOOR TANNING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indoor tanning using machines like booths or beds is a major risk factor for developing any type of skin cancer, including squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACUTE MYELOID LEUKEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acute myeloid leukemia (AML) is a cancer of immature white blood cells (myeloid blasts) characterized by buildup in bone marrow and blood, diagnosed via bone marrow aspirate and biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERINEURAL INVASION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Perineural invasion is when a tumor has grown into a nerve, indicating high-risk or very high-risk cancer, with symptoms like pain or vision changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2 STATUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HER2 status is a test result indicating whether breast cancer cells have excess HER2 protein, which affects treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IV HYDRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IV hydration is routinely given to individuals receiving platinum-based chemotherapy to reduce effects on the kidneys."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GINGIVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gingiva, or gums, are the upper and lower soft tissues surrounding the teeth, where mouth cancer can develop."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROGLOBULIN (TG)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thyroglobulin (Tg) is a protein produced only by thyroid tissue. Its levels in the blood are used as a marker to monitor for cancer recurrence after total thyroidectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGAN FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organ Function is assessed through tests like CMP and LFTs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEOBLADDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neobladder is a type of urinary diversion where the bladder is replaced with a segment of small intestine, allowing urine to exit through the urethra without needing a stoma or ostomy bag."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASAL CELL CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Basal cell carcinoma (BCC) is another name for basal cell skin cancer, the most common type of skin cancer. It is characterized by abnormal growth of basal cells in the epidermis and is highly treatable when detected early."&lt;SEP&gt;"Basal cell carcinoma is the most common type of skin cancer, arising from basal cells in the epidermis, and is less aggressive than melanoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prognosis is the likely course and outcome of a disease based on tests, used to predict how cancer will turn out."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis is the likely course and outcome of a disease, predicting how it will turn out."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis is the likely course and outcome of a disease, predicting how the illness will turn out."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis is the likely course and outcome of cancer, influenced by staging and other factors, and is used to guide treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis is the likely course of cancer, determined through genetic and biomarker tests in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis is the likely course of cancer, predicted through staging, which helps in treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis is the likely course of cancer, used to guide treatment decisions and reflect staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis is the likely course of the cancer, determined through genetic and biomarker tests, and influences treatment decisions for AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis is the likely outcome of cancer, influenced by cancer type and stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis is the likely outcome of cancer, which is reflected in staging and guides treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis is the predicted likely course and outcome of prostate cancer, based on risk group, which guides treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis predicts the likely course and outcome of prostate cancer, guiding treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis refers to the likely course and outcome of CLL, which can be discussed with the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis refers to the likely course and outcome of a disease, discussed in advance care planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prognosis refers to the likely course and outcome of cancer, which is predicted based on staging information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMARKER TESTS FOR PROFILING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biomarker tests for profiling are used to identify unique features of the cancer that may guide specific treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT GOALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment goals are the objectives of cancer therapy, discussed regularly with the care team to align with patient needs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment goals include controlling cancer, improving well-being, and maintaining quality of life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3C CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3C cervical cancer is a stage where there is cancer in pelvic or para-aortic lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL TOXINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental toxins, such as tobacco smoke, vehicle exhaust, and arsenic, can cause skin damage leading to squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental toxins, such as tobacco smoke, vehicle exhaust, and arsenic, can cause skin damage that may lead to squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOPOIETIC CELL TRANSPLANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hematopoietic cell transplant is a procedure to replace diseased bone marrow with healthy stem cells, used in AML treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hematopoietic cell transplant is a treatment option for AML that involves replacing diseased bone marrow with healthy stem cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CURETTAGE AND ELECTRODESICCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Curettage and electrodesiccation is a type of surgery for squamous cell skin cancer, involving scraping and burning the tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUCTAL CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ductal carcinoma is a common type of breast cancer that originates in the milk ducts of the breast."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ductal carcinoma is a type of breast cancer starting in the cells lining milk ducts, the most common form."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ductal carcinoma is a type of breast cancer that arises in the cells lining the milk ducts. It is one of the most common types of breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ductal carcinoma is a type of breast cancer that starts in the cells lining the milk ducts, the most common type of breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ductal carcinoma is a type of breast cancer that starts in the cells lining the milk ducts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSMA-PET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PSMA-PET is a specialized PET scan that targets prostate-specific membrane antigen on prostate cancer cells, used for monitoring recurrence and determining targeted therapy eligibility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gender is a demographic factor that may affect cancer incidence and treatment response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The face is a common area where basal cell skin cancer develops due to sun exposure, and it is often the site of skin lesions associated with the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAGNOSTIC RADIOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specialist who reads results of x-rays and other imaging tests to aid in diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnostic radiologist interprets imaging tests like mammograms and ultrasounds to aid in cancer diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnostic radiologist is a specialist who interprets imaging tests to help diagnose and stage pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DAY-TO-DAY ACTIVITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Day-to-day activities refer to routine tasks that patients aim to maintain during treatment, a key aspect of quality of life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 4A CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 4A cervical cancer indicates spread to adjacent organs like the bladder or rectum, requiring imaging surveillance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 4A cervical cancer is a stage where the cancer has spread to nearby organs such as the bladder or rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCARS AND CHRONIC WOUNDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scars and chronic wounds, such as ulcers and burns, can be sites where squamous cell carcinoma develops, known as Marjolin’s ulcer, and are often more difficult to treat."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scars and chronic wounds, such as ulcers and burns, can develop into squamous cell carcinoma, known as Marjolin ulcer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARDIOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A cardiologist is a heart specialist who may be consulted to monitor heart function or treatment side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cardiologist is a heart specialist who may be consulted to monitor heart function during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PDEMA/MOHS SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PDEMA/Mohs surgery is a type of surgery for squamous cell skin cancer, involving precise removal of layers of skin to ensure complete tumor removal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOBULAR CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lobular carcinoma is a common type of breast cancer that originates in the milk glands (lobules) of the breast."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lobular carcinoma is a type of breast cancer starting in the lobules (milk glands) of the breast."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lobular carcinoma is a type of breast cancer that arises in the cells lining the lobules (milk glands). It is another common type of breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lobular carcinoma is a type of breast cancer that starts in the cells lining the lobules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lobular carcinoma is a type of breast cancer that starts in the lobules (milk glands) of the breast, the second most common type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VISION PROBLEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vision problems are a possible side effect of radiation therapy to the eyes, which may be temporary or permanent, and can include cataracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vision problems include blurred vision, double vision, or loss of peripheral vision, which can be caused by gliomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC AND BIOMARKER TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic and biomarker tests are used to learn more about the subtype of AML, to target treatment, and to determine the likely course of the cancer (prognosis). They can identify specific gene mutations or abnormal chromosomes that influence diagnosis and treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC ABNORMALITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic abnormalities are changes in genes that may not be inherited but can increase prostate cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NONFUNCTIONING TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nonfunctioning tumor is an adrenal tumor that does not produce excess hormones and may not cause symptoms unless it grows large enough to press on nearby organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The arms are common areas where basal cell skin cancer develops due to sun exposure, and they can be sites of skin lesions associated with the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORMAL PROSTATE TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Normal prostate tissue is healthy prostate cells, used as a reference for comparing cancer cell patterns in Gleason scoring."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERVENTIONAL RADIOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Interventional radiologist is a medical professional who performs core needle biopsies under light sedation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interventional radiologist is a specialist who performs minimally invasive procedures, such as biopsies, guided by imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interventional radiologist is a specialist who uses imaging guidance to perform minimally invasive procedures, such as biopsies, for cancer diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interventional radiologist performs needle biopsies and places intravenous ports for treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANXIETY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A common psychological condition in cancer patients, involving excessive worry and fear."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anxiety is a common psychological condition in cancer patients, which can be managed with support groups, therapy, or medication."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anxiety is a common side effect of an incorrect levothyroxine dose, affecting the patient's mental state."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anxiety is a feeling of worry that can be managed with psychological support and medications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anxiety is a mental health condition involving excessive worry or fear, which can be part of distress in cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anxiety is a mental health condition that can affect anal cancer survivors, often due to fear of judgment or treatment effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anxiety is a mental health condition that can occur as part of distress in cancer patients, causing excessive worry and fear."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anxiety is a psychological condition that may affect cancer survivors, addressed in survivorship care resources."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 4B CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 4B cervical cancer is a metastatic stage where the cancer has spread to distant organs like the liver, lungs, abdomen, bone, or other lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 4B cervical cancer is metastatic cancer that has spread to distant organs, with imaging used to monitor response to systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARJOLIN ULCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marjolin ulcer is a type of squamous cell carcinoma that forms in chronic wounds or scars."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUORODEOXYGLUCOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG) is a specific radiotracer used in FDG-PET/CT scans to detect cancer activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR BORDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor border refers to the clinical extent of the tumor; a well-defined border is low risk, while an uneven border is high risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERMINAL DUCT LOBULAR UNITS (TDLUS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Terminal duct lobular units (TDLUs) are the functional units of the breast where breast cancer typically originates. They consist of lobules and ducts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Terminal duct lobular units are the functional units of the breast where most breast cancers arise, specifically in the epithelial cells lining these structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Terminal duct lobular units are the functional units of the breast where most breast cancers arise."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SENSORY DISTURBANCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sensory disturbances include numbness, tingling, or burning sensations, often on one side of the body, which can be symptoms of gliomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT SIDE EFFECT MANAGEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment Side Effect Management is addressing fertility and other impacts of therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolism is the process by which the body converts food into energy, regulated by thyroid hormones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism refers to the body's chemical processes, which are controlled by hormones from the adrenal cortex."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITIONISTS AND DIETITIANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutritionists and dietitians are part of the care team, providing dietary guidance for cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutritionists and dietitians provide guidance on suitable foods for patients' conditions during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOLUNTEER NETWORK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volunteer network is a group of individuals who provide unpaid assistance to patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Legs are part of the body where blood clots can occur in high-grade glioma patients, causing swelling."&lt;SEP&gt;"The legs are common areas where basal cell skin cancer develops due to sun exposure, and they can be sites of skin lesions associated with the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLACK MALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Black males are a demographic group at higher risk for prostate cancer, with earlier onset, more aggressive disease, and higher mortality rates compared to white males."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black males are a demographic group with typically higher normal PSA levels compared to white males, affecting cancer risk assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black males in the United States are more likely to develop prostate cancer, often at an earlier age, with more aggressive and advanced disease, and are twice as likely to die from it compared to white males."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GASTROENTEROLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gastroenterologist is a health care professional that people with anal cancer symptoms may reach out to for evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gastroenterologist is a specialist in digestive system disorders, involved in endoscopic tests for pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutrition refers to dietary intake, which is important for maintaining health during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER NAVIGATORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer navigators are healthcare professionals who help patients navigate the cancer care system, providing support and resources."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;18-FLUORODEOXYGLUCOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"18-fluorodeoxyglucose is a radioactive type of sugar used as a tracer in FDG-PET scans to detect active cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"A radioactive type of sugar used as a tracer in FDG-PET scans, taken up by active cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic tests are medical tests to identify inherited mutations that may increase cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic tests are used to identify gene mutations or chromosomal abnormalities in AML, guiding treatment and prognosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic tests are used to identify hereditary conditions that may increase the risk of adrenal tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic tests detect genes linked to hereditary conditions that increase the risk of pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR SHAPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor shape is a factor in risk assessment; uneven shapes are considered high risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIPPLE-AREOLA COMPLEX (NAC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nipple-areola complex (NAC) refers to the nipple and the ring of darker breast skin called the areola."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nipple-areola complex refers to the nipple and the darker skin around it (areola), part of breast anatomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nipple-areola complex refers to the nipple and the surrounding darker skin (areola) on the breast, which are involved in milk delivery."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term referring to both the nipple and the areola, the darker skin ring around the nipple."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARIETAL LOBE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Parietal lobe is an area of the brain associated with intelligence, language, reading, sensation, and sensory perception."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS®&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN Guidelines for Patients® is an organization that provides patient guidelines, including information on fertility preservation, available at NCCN.org/patientguidelines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRUNK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The trunk is a common area where basal cell skin cancer develops due to sun exposure, and it can be a site of skin lesions associated with the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHITE MALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"White males are a demographic group with lower average normal PSA levels compared to Black males, influencing risk interpretation."&lt;SEP&gt;"White males are a demographic group with lower risk of prostate cancer compared to Black males."&lt;SEP&gt;"White males in the United States have a lower risk of developing prostate cancer compared to Black males but a higher risk than Hispanic and Asian males."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical oncologist is a doctor who specializes in treating cancer with chemotherapy and other medicines. They are part of the care team for ovarian cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical oncologist is a doctor who treats cancer using chemotherapy, immunotherapy, and other systemic therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical oncologist is a doctor who treats cancer using systemic (drug) therapy, such as chemotherapy or targeted therapy. They are part of the care team for AML patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical oncologist is a medical expert specializing in treating cancer with chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical oncologist is a physician who treats cancer with chemotherapy, immunotherapy, and other systemic therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical oncologist is a specialist who manages cancer treatment using systemic therapies, such as chemotherapy or hormone therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical oncologist is a specialist who manages cancer treatment with systemic therapies, including targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical oncologist treats cancer using systemic (drug) therapy, including chemotherapy, targeted therapy, and immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specialist who treats cancer with systemic therapies like chemotherapy and immunotherapy, often coordinating patient care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical Oncologist is a specialist who manages chemotherapy and other systemic treatments for cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical oncologist is a specialist who treats cancer using chemotherapy, immunotherapy, and other systemic therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical oncologist is a specialist who treats cancer using medications such as chemotherapy or targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical oncologist treats cancer in adults using systemic therapies like chemotherapy or hormone therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDITATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Meditation is a mind-body practice that can help reduce stress and improve well-being."&lt;SEP&gt;"Meditation is a mind-body practice used to reduce stress and improve well-being in cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPPORT GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Support groups are gatherings of individuals facing similar challenges, providing emotional support for cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support groups are gatherings of people at different stages of cancer treatment, providing emotional and practical help."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support groups are groups of individuals who provide emotional and social support to patients during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATOSTATIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somatostatin is a hormone that helps control other hormones in the body and binds to somatostatin receptors on cell surfaces."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMARKER TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biomarker tests are advanced blood or urine tests that measure specific biological indicators to help determine the need for further prostate cancer testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarker tests are lab tests that identify unique features of CLL cells, called biomarkers, to plan treatment specifically for a patient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarker tests are used for profiling cancer markers to guide treatment decisions for pancreatic cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarker tests are used to learn about AML subtype, target treatment, and determine prognosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DAMAGED SKIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Damaged skin, such as from radiation therapy, wounds, scars, or inflammation, is a risk factor for high-risk squamous cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AXILLARY LYMPH NODES (ALNS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Axillary lymph nodes (ALNs) are lymph nodes near the armpit that drain lymph from breast tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Axillary lymph nodes (ALNs) are nodes near the armpit that receive lymph fluid from breast tissue, playing a role in immune response and cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Axillary lymph nodes are lymph nodes located near the armpit, which drain lymph fluid from the breast tissue. They are important in the spread of breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Axillary lymph nodes are lymph nodes located under the arm, which are common sites for breast cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph nodes near the armpit that receive lymph fluid from breast tissue; important in cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OCCIPITAL LOBE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Occipital lobe is an area of the brain associated with vision and color perception."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLOOR OF THE MOUTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The floor of the mouth is the area under the tongue, a site for mouth cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The floor of the mouth is the area under the tongue, a site where mouth cancer can develop."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTI-THYROGLOBULIN ANTIBODIES (TG AB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anti-thyroglobulin antibodies (Tg ab) are antibodies produced by some people with thyroid cancer that can interfere with Tg level measurements. Their levels are monitored to assess treatment effectiveness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTHER PARTS OF BODY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Other Parts of Body are areas where cancer may spread, detected via imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTINENT CUTANEOUS POUCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Continent cutaneous pouch (Indiana pouch) is a type of urinary diversion using a portion of the large intestine to create a pouch, connected to a stoma, with a one-way valve to prevent urine leakage, requiring catheterization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESEARCHERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Researchers are individuals working on clinical trials to find more targeted treatments for gliomas and other cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Researchers are scientists investigating the reasons for racial differences in PSA levels, contributing to understanding of prostate cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL ONCOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgical oncologist is a specialist who performs surgery to remove pancreatic cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical oncologist performs operations to remove cancer, such as lumpectomy or mastectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEEK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The cheek is a specific location on the face where a basal cell lesion can be pictured, as mentioned in the text, indicating it as a common site for such lesions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physical therapy is a rehabilitation service that helps improve physical function and mobility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TALK THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Talk therapy is a form of counseling that helps cancer patients manage emotional distress and improve mental health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATOSTATIN RECEPTOR (SSTR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somatostatin receptor (SSTR) is a protein on cell surfaces that binds to somatostatin, found on many cell types, and is targeted by SSTR-PET tracers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARDIAC TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cardiac tests are synonymous with heart tests, used to assess heart health and function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NERVE DAMAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nerve damage to fingers and toes can occur with extended treatment with oxaliplatin, causing numbness, cramping, tingling, or pain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nerve damage, or perineural invasion, is a risk factor for high-risk or very high-risk squamous cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOBULES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lobules are milk-producing glands in the breast that look like tiny clusters of grapes, where breast cancer can originate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lobules are milk-producing glands in the breast, and are a common site where breast cancer originates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lobules are milk-producing glands in the breast, where lobular carcinoma originates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lobules are milk-producing glands in the breast, which look like tiny clusters of grapes. They are connected to the nipple by ducts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lobules are structures in the breast that make breast milk, resembling tiny clusters of grapes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lobules are structures in the breast that make breast milk. They are part of the terminal duct lobular units (TDLUs) where breast cancer arises."&lt;SEP&gt;"Milk-producing glands in the breast that look like tiny clusters of grapes; connected to the nipple by ducts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THIN, HOLLOW NEEDLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thin, hollow needle is inserted into the brain during a stereotactic biopsy to remove a tissue sample."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMORBIDITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Comorbidity is the presence of other health conditions that may affect cancer treatment and outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QTC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"QTc is a measure of the heart's electrical activity, specifically the time for the heart to recharge between beats. Certain treatments can cause a prolonged QTc, which may lead to dangerous heart rhythms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAXILLARY SINUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maxillary sinus is a structure that can be involved in T4a stage of mouth cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A broader term encompassing both anal canal and perianal cancers, with surveillance and treatment protocols."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal Cancer is a disease in which malignant cells form in the tissues of the anus, often linked to HPV infection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal cancer is a disease characterized by abnormal cell growth in the anal canal or perianal area, with stages I-III being nonmetastatic and treated with chemoradiation or surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal cancer is a disease characterized by abnormal cell growth in the anal canal or perianal region, often caused by HPV infection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal cancer is a disease characterized by malignant cells in the anus, which can metastasize to lymph nodes, liver, or lungs, and requires various treatments including surgery, radiation, and chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal cancer is a disease characterized by the abnormal growth of cells in the anal canal or perianal region. The text focuses on invasive anal squamous cell carcinoma, which is more advanced than SISCCA, and discusses diagnosis, testing, staging, and treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal cancer is a disease characterized by the growth of abnormal cells in or near the anus, often caused by high-risk HPV strains, with symptoms including rectal bleeding and anal itching."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal cancer is a disease that starts in the anal canal or perianal region, with squamous cell carcinoma being the most common type. It is strongly linked to HPV infection and has various risk factors including HIV, immunosuppression, and smoking."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal cancer is a disease that starts in the anal canal or perianal region, with stages ranging from precancerous lesions to metastatic disease, and is most commonly squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal cancer is a rare type of cancer affecting the anus, treated with chemotherapy, radiation, and surgery, with specific follow-up protocols."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal cancer is a type of cancer affecting the anal canal, with treatment often leading to side effects such as bowel, bladder, and sexual dysfunction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal cancer is a type of cancer affecting the anal region, with specific survivorship care guidelines and treatment considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal cancer is an uncommon cancer of the digestive system, most often starting in squamous cells of the anal canal or perianal region, and is treated by a multidisciplinary team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIATION ONCOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A doctor who is an expert in radiation treatment and should administer radiation therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A radiation oncologist is a doctor who specializes in using radiation therapy to treat cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A radiation oncologist is a doctor who uses radiation therapy to treat cancer, including CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"A radiation oncologist is a medical expert specializing in the use of radiation therapy to treat cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A radiation oncologist is a medical professional who devises treatment plans to aim radiation beams at tumors and lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A radiation oncologist is a specialist who administers radiation therapy, such as EBRT, for cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A radiation oncologist is a specialist who prescribes and oversees radiation therapy for cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specialist who prescribes and plans radiation therapy to treat cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation Oncologist is a specialist who administers radiation therapy, such as IMRT, for cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation oncologist is a doctor who makes the treatment plan using CT images and software, specifying doses and sessions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation oncologist is a medical professional who discusses possible side effects of radiation therapy with patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation oncologist is a specialist who uses radiation therapy to treat cancer, including SCLC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation oncologist is a specialist who uses radiation therapy to treat pancreatic cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation oncologist prescribes and delivers radiation therapy to treat cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TANNING BEDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tanning beds are a source of UV radiation that increases the risk of developing basal cell skin cancer, as they emit harmful UV rays that can damage skin DNA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTEGRATIVE MEDICINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Integrative medicine combines conventional and complementary therapies to support patient well-being."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medication can be used to manage anxiety, depression, or other symptoms in cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRENAL TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adrenal tumors are growths on the adrenal glands that may secrete hormones, detected through imaging and biochemical tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adrenal tumors can be benign or malignant, occurring in one or both adrenal glands, and may be functional (producing hormones) or nonfunctional."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumors of the adrenal glands, which are the focus of the NCCN guidelines and may be detected and monitored using imaging tests like CT, MRI, and PET scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QTC INTERVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"QTc interval is a measure of heart electrical recharging time; prolonged QTc can lead to dangerous heart rhythms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSPORTATION COSTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transportation costs are indirect costs that participants may incur due to extra appointments in a clinical trial."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transportation costs are indirect expenses patients may incur due to extra appointments during a clinical trial."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ducts are small tubes in the breast that carry milk from the lobules to the nipple. They are part of the breast's glandular structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ducts are small tubes in the breast that connect lobules to the nipple, and are a common site for breast cancer development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ducts are structures in the breast that carry breast milk from the lobules to the nipple. They are part of the terminal duct lobular units (TDLUs) where breast cancer arises."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ducts are structures within the breast that carry breast milk from the lobules to the nipple, and are a common site where breast cancer starts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ducts are thin tubes that carry milk from the lobules to the nipple."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thin tubes in the breast that carry milk from the lobules to the nipple; where DCIS originates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENIGN TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A benign tumor is a noncancerous growth that does not spread to other parts of the body. Most adrenal tumors are benign."&lt;SEP&gt;"Benign tumors are non-cancerous growths that may be found after surgery, requiring no further cancer treatment but possibly needing hormone replacement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN OF THE FACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skin of the face is a structure that can be involved in T4a stage of mouth cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SISCCA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SISCCA (Superficially Invasive Squamous Cell Carcinoma) is a less advanced form of anal cancer. The guide does not apply to SISCCA, as it focuses on more invasive forms of anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"SISCCA (Superficially invasive squamous cell carcinoma) is the earliest form of anal cancer, with tiny lesions less than 7 mm wide, often found accidentally during biopsies or removal of non-cancerous growths."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GERIATRICIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Geriatrician is a specialist who focuses on the health care of older adults, potentially involved in pancreatic cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The sun is a primary source of UV radiation, which is a major cause of basal cell skin cancer. Exposure to sunlight over time increases the risk of developing the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOSPITAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hospital is a healthcare facility that provides medical services, including cancer treatment and supportive care."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hospital is a medical center where diagnostic procedures like biopsies and imaging tests are performed, and where patients receive care."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hospital is a medical facility where AML patients may receive treatment, including specialized care for their subtype."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location where excision biopsies can be performed."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical facility where TURBT may be performed."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical facility where cystoscopy and other procedures may be performed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital is a healthcare institution that may offer cancer treatment and support services."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital is a medical facility that may provide treatment for bone cancer, especially if it has experience with such tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital is a medical facility where cancer treatments, surgeries, and follow-up care are provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital is a medical facility where patients receive diagnostic tests, treatments, and follow-up care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospital is where testing and treatment are provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hospitals are medical institutions that provide surgical and cancer care, with those performing many surgeries often having better outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH INSURANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health insurance is a financial resource that can help cover cancer treatment costs, and lack of it may be a concern for patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONE SECRETION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormone secretion refers to the production and release of hormones by adrenal tumors, which can cause symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EJECTION FRACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ejection fraction is the amount of blood pumped out of the left side of the heart per beat, indicating heart function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ejection fraction is the amount of blood pumped out of the left side of the heart with each beat. It is measured via an echocardiogram to assess heart function, and a lower-than-normal value indicates decreased heart function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHILD CARE COSTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Child care costs are indirect costs that participants may incur due to extra appointments in a clinical trial."&lt;SEP&gt;"Child care costs are indirect expenses patients may incur due to extra appointments during a clinical trial."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AREOLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Areola is the ring of darker breast skin surrounding the nipple, part of the nipple-areola complex."&lt;SEP&gt;"Areola is the ring of darker breast skin surrounding the nipple."&lt;SEP&gt;"Areola is the ring of darker skin surrounding the nipple, part of the nipple-areola complex."&lt;SEP&gt;"The areola is the ring of darker skin surrounding the nipple on the breast. It is part of the nipple-areola complex."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ring of darker skin around the nipple, part of the nipple-areola complex."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IODIZED SALT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iodized salt is a dietary source of iodine, used by the thyroid to produce hormones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSYCHOLOGISTS AND PSYCHIATRISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Psychologists and psychiatrists are mental health experts who manage issues like depression, anxiety, or other mental health conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Psychologists and psychiatrists are part of the care team, managing mental health issues like depression and anxiety."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THORACIC VERTEBRAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thoracic vertebrae are the 12 bones in the upper back region of the spine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLLECTING DUCT RCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Collecting duct RCC (cdRCC) is a rare subtype of non-clear cell RCC that forms in the cells of the collecting ducts or tubules in the kidney."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRONIC KIDNEY DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chronic kidney disease is a health condition that may prevent some people from having a contrast agent in a CT scan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASTICATOR SPACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Masticator space is a region that can be invaded by tumor in T4b stage of mouth cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INGUINAL LYMPH NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inguinal lymph nodes are lymph nodes in the groin area, which are examined and may be removed if they contain cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inguinal lymph nodes are lymph nodes in the groin, often affected by anal cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inguinal lymph nodes are lymph nodes located in the groin area. They are a common site for anal cancer to spread if left untreated, and are examined through palpation or imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGISTERED DIETITIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A registered dietitian is a healthcare professional who provides nutritional guidance. The text recommends consulting one for help planning healthy meals during ovarian cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Registered dietitian is a specialist who provides nutritional support and advice to patients with pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAIR SKIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fair skin is a risk factor for basal cell skin cancer, as people with lighter skin have less melanin to filter out harmful UV rays, making them more susceptible to DNA damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVOCATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An advocate is a person who supports the patient, helping them communicate needs and make decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNEMPLOYMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unemployment is a potential financial issue for cancer patients who may miss work during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUTANEOUS SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA (CSCC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A very common type of skin cancer occurring more often in lighter-skinned people, commonly found on sun-exposed areas like the head and neck, rarely spreading but can cause severe damage if untreated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma (CSCC) is another term for squamous cell skin cancer, originating in squamous cells of the skin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPINAL TAP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spinal tap is another name for lumbar puncture, a procedure to collect spinal fluid for analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW DRUG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A new drug is an experimental treatment tested in clinical trials, often combined with standard treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIPPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nipple is the raised tip within the areola through which breast milk is released."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nipple is the raised tip within the areola through which milk ducts connect, part of breast anatomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nipple is the raised tip within the areola through which milk is delivered."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nipple is the part of the breast where ducts carry milk, and it can show changes such as discharge or bleeding during breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nipple is the raised tip within the areola on the breast, through which milk is delivered. It is part of the nipple-areola complex."&lt;SEP&gt;"The raised tip within the areola through which milk is delivered."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N0 NODE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N0 node indicates no cancer in nearby lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RETROMOLAR TRIGONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The retromolar trigone is the small area behind the wisdom teeth, a site for mouth cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALK GENE FUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALK gene fusion is a specific biomarker that can be present in thyroid cancer cells, making them eligible for targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PTERYGOID PLATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pterygoid plates are structures that can be invaded by tumor in T4b stage of mouth cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINE-NEEDLE ASPIRATION (FNA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biopsy method using a thin needle to take small samples of suspicious thyroid nodules, often guided by ultrasound."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine-needle aspiration (FNA) is a biopsy technique using a thin needle to remove a sample of fluid or tissue from a tumor or lymph node for examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine-needle aspiration (FNA) is a biopsy technique using a thin needle to remove a sample of tumor or lymph node, often guided by ultrasound or CT scan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine-needle aspiration (FNA) is a type of biopsy that uses a thin needle to remove a sample of fluid or tissue from a tumor or lymph node for cancer diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine-needle aspiration (FNA) is a type of biopsy that uses a thin needle to remove a sample of tissue or fluid from the breast or lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine-needle aspiration (FNA) is a type of biopsy used to test lymph nodes for CSCC spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine-needle aspiration is a biopsy technique that can suggest follicular or oncocytic cancer but cannot definitively diagnose these types, requiring pathologic examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine-needle aspiration is a procedure where a thin needle is used to remove a sample of tissue from a lymph node for testing. It is used when lymph nodes feel enlarged or look suspicious on imaging tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC COUNSELOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genetic counselor is a healthcare professional who provides counseling to individuals with genetic risks of cancer, helping them understand their risk and manage their health throughout treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genetic counselor is a healthcare professional with special training in genetic diseases who helps patients decide about germline testing and interpret results."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genetic counselor is a specialist who provides guidance on genetic testing and inherited cancer risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genetic counselor is an expert who talks with patients and families about inherited syndromes and can order blood or saliva tests for gene mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"A genetic counselor specializes in assessing inherited cancer risks and guiding patients through genetic testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A healthcare professional who provides guidance and testing for inherited syndromes related to colon cancer, such as Lynch syndrome and FAP."&lt;SEP&gt;"A healthcare professional with specialized training in genetic diseases who helps patients decide about genetic testing and interpret results."&lt;SEP&gt;"A professional who advises on genetic testing and inherited syndromes."&lt;SEP&gt;"An expert who interprets how family history may impact treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic counselor is a health expert with special training to help patients understand gene changes related to disease, providing guidance on hereditary cancer risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic counselor is a specialist who helps patients understand genetic test results and inherited cancer risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic counselor is a specialist who helps patients understand hereditary cancer risks and the implications of genetic testing results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic counselor is a specialized expert trained in genetic diseases who helps patients decide whether to undergo germline testing and interprets results to guide medical decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic counselor is a trained professional who discusses hereditary genetic testing results with patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Professional for genetic testing guidance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Professional who provides guidance on genetic testing for inherited syndromes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Professional."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RED HAIR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Red hair is a risk factor for basal cell skin cancer, often associated with fair skin and lighter eye color, which increase susceptibility to UV radiation damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLDER PATIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Older patients are elderly individuals who may have other health conditions and may not tolerate aggressive treatments well."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COSTS OF CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Costs of care refer to the financial expenses associated with cancer treatment, which can be managed with help from the treatment team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KERATINOCYTE CARCINOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Keratinocyte carcinomas is a term used for basal cell and squamous cell skin cancers, which do not behave like melanoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTIDISCIPLINARY TEAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A multidisciplinary team is a group of experts from different fields who work together to treat pancreatic cancer, as recommended in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Multidisciplinary team includes oncologists, genetic counselors, and pathologists for comprehensive care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Multidisciplinary team is a group of healthcare professionals from various specialties involved in AML treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELIGIBILITY REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eligibility requirements are criteria that determine if a patient can join a clinical trial, including treatment history and cancer stage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PECTORAL MUSCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chest muscle located behind the breast that provides support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pectoral muscle is the chest muscle located behind the breast, providing structural support."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pectoral muscle is the chest muscle located behind the breast. It provides support and structure to the breast area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Copies are duplicates of records made for the binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAS DEFERENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vas deferens is a tube that carries sperm away from the testicles, part of which may be removed during radical cystectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY PRESERVATION EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility Preservation Education is learning about options from specialists and NCCN."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKULL BASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skull base is a structure that can be invaded by tumor in T4b stage of mouth cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skull base is an anatomical region imaged with MRI to assess NPC extension."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPUTED TOMOGRAPHY (CT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A computed tomography (CT) scan is a diagnostic imaging procedure that uses x-rays and computer technology to create detailed cross-sectional images of the body. It is used to detect cancer and other abnormalities, often with contrast material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Computed tomography (CT) is an imaging technique that combines multiple x-rays to create cross-sectional images of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Computed tomography (CT) is an imaging technique that uses x-rays to create cross-sectional images, often used with contrast material and combined with PET scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Computed tomography is an imaging test that uses x-rays to take detailed pictures of areas inside the body. It is recommended to determine the extent of anal cancer in the pelvis and to look for spread to areas beyond the pelvis, such as the chest and abdomen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALLIATIVE CARE PROVIDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Palliative care provider is a specialist who focuses on relieving symptoms and improving quality of life for cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOND HAIR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blond hair is a risk factor for basal cell skin cancer, often associated with fair skin and lighter eye color, which increase susceptibility to UV radiation damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRAIL PATIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Frail patients are those with reduced physical capacity, for whom supportive care alone may be a reasonable option."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVESTIGATIONAL TREATMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Investigational treatments are experimental therapies being studied in clinical trials for safety and effectiveness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NONMELANOMA SKIN CANCERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nonmelanoma skin cancers include basal cell and squamous cell carcinomas, which are less aggressive than melanoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY AND FAMILY PLANNING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A topic in the text related to testing and care, possibly impacted by cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Considerations for patients regarding reproductive health during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility and family planning refers to considerations and options for preserving fertility before cancer treatment, including sperm banking, egg freezing, and ovarian tissue banking."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER INFORMATION SERVICE (CIS) PHONE NUMBER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Cancer Information Service (CIS) phone number is 1-800-4-CANCER (6237), a resource for help finding clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RIBS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bones behind the breast that provide structural support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ribs are bones behind the breast that provide structural support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ribs are bones of the chest that lie behind the breast and pectoral muscle."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ribs are the bones behind the breast and pectoral muscle, part of the chest anatomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ribs are the bones that form the chest cavity, located behind the breast and pectoral muscle. They provide structural support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EYE SURGEON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eye surgeon is a medical professional who performs routine operations to treat cataracts, a possible side effect of intraocular chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER STAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer stages describe the extent of cancer spread in the body, influencing treatment decisions and prognosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Classification of cancer extent, such as stage 0 for DCIS, used in treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOLOGIC ONCOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hematologic oncologist is a medical expert in blood diseases and blood cancers, such as AML, and treats these conditions. They are part of the care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNAL CAROTID ARTERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Internal carotid artery is a vessel that can be encased by tumor in T4b stage of mouth cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POSITRON EMISSION TOMOGRAPHY (PET)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A positron emission tomography (PET) scan is a diagnostic imaging test that uses a radioactive tracer to detect cancer cells by showing metabolic activity. Cancer cells appear as bright spots, but not all bright spots are cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is an imaging test that uses radioactive materials called radiotracers to detect cancer, which appears brighter due to higher sugar consumption by cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Positron emission tomography (PET) is an imaging technique that uses radioactive tracers to detect metabolic activity, such as cancer cell growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Positron emission tomography (PET) is an imaging test using a radioactive drug to see where cancer cells are in the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Positron emission tomography is an imaging test that involves injecting radioactive glucose into the body to detect cancer cells, which appear brighter because they use sugar more quickly. It may be combined with CT or MRI."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MENTAL HEALTH PROVIDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mental health provider is a specialist who supports patients' emotional and psychological well-being during cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIGHT EYE COLOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Light eye color is a risk factor for basal cell skin cancer, often associated with fair skin and lighter hair, which increase susceptibility to UV radiation damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTHER DISEASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Other diseases refer to comorbidities that can affect treatment decisions and overall health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT OUTCOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment outcome refers to the expected result of cancer treatment, which is noted in the treatment plan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ULTRAVIOLET (UV) RAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ultraviolet (UV) rays are harmful radiation from the sun that can damage skin and increase the risk of skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISMATCH REPAIR TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mismatch repair testing is a lab analysis of colon tumors to detect deficiency (dMMR) or high microsatellite instability (MSI-H), which are biomarkers for certain cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCI WEBSITE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The NCI website at cancer.gov provides resources for finding clinical trials and cancer information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIGAMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Connective tissue in the breast that helps hold the breast in place."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ligaments are connective tissue in the breast that help hold it in place."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ligaments are fibrous tissues in the breast that help hold the breast in place."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCEROUS TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A cancerous tumor is a malignant growth that can spread to other parts of the body. Some adrenal tumors, such as adrenocortical carcinoma and neuroblastoma, are cancerous."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORTICAL BONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cortical bone is a type of bone that can be invaded by tumor in T4a stage of mouth cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV (Human Papillomavirus) is a group of more than 100 strains of viruses, some of which are high-risk and can cause anal cancer and other related cancers, as well as abnormal skin growths or warts."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV (Human Papillomavirus) is a virus that can cause anal cancer and other cancers, often transmitted sexually."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV (Human Papillomavirus) is a virus that causes almost all cervical cancers and is also linked to anal cancer. It is a key factor in the development of these cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV (Human Papillomavirus) is an extremely common sexually transmitted virus and the risk factor most strongly linked with anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV (Human Papillomavirus) is an extremely common sexually transmitted virus and the strongest risk factor for anal cancer, with long-term infection being particularly dangerous."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV (human papillomavirus) is a factor in throat cancer, as indicated by p16 (HPV) testing mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV (human papillomavirus) is a virus linked to throat cancer, detected via p16 testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV is a virus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALE REPRODUCTIVE SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Male reproductive system includes the prostate, penis, seminal vesicles, and testicles, and is important for sexual reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Male reproductive system includes the prostate, penis, seminal vesicles, and testicles, and is responsible for sexual reproduction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISTORY OF SKIN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A history of skin cancer, either personal or familial, is a risk factor for developing basal cell skin cancer, indicating a genetic or environmental predisposition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Conditions are health issues that may coexist with cancer, influencing treatment choices."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIDE EFFECTS MANAGEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Side effects management is the process of addressing adverse effects of cancer treatment, involving the patient and care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOBACCO SMOKE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tobacco smoke is an environmental pollutant that can cause skin damage and increase the risk of developing squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tobacco smoke is an environmental pollutant that can cause skin damage leading to squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tobacco smoke is the biggest risk factor for lung cancer, containing over 50 cancer-causing compounds. Both direct smoking and secondhand smoke increase risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYPS WITH CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyps with cancer are abnormal growths on the colon lining that can become invasive, with types including adenomas and adenocarcinomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NLM WEBSITE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The NLM website at clinicaltrials.gov provides a worldwide database of clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPITHELIAL CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Epithelial cells are cells lining the inner or outer surfaces of the body, where most breast carcinomas arise."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epithelial cells are cells that line the inner or outer surfaces of the body, and are the origin of most breast cancers in the terminal duct lobular units."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epithelial cells are cells that make up the lining of the breast ducts and lobules. Breast cancer arises from these cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHILDHOOD CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Childhood cancer is a type of cancer that, when treated with radiation to the head or neck, increases risk of thyroid cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE-STRENGTHENING THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone-strengthening therapy is a treatment to support bone health, possibly used in metastatic breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone-strengthening therapy is a treatment to support bone health, possibly used in metastatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOLOGY DEPARTMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiology department is a hospital department where CT scans are performed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiology department is a hospital unit that performs imaging studies such as CT scans and MRIs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPITHELIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Epithelium is a thin, moist layer of cells that covers the inside of the gallbladder and bile ducts, mentioned in the context of bile duct cancer stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epithelium is the innermost lining of the mucosa in the esophagus, normally made up of flat, thin squamous cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epithelium is the surface layer lining the inside of the mouth, where squamous cell carcinoma starts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epithelium is the surface layer of tissue surrounding the ovaries where most ovarian cancers are found."&lt;SEP&gt;"The epithelium is the inner lining of the esophagus where cancer cells begin to grow out of control."&lt;SEP&gt;"The epithelium is the surface layer of the oral mucosa containing stratified squamous cells, which can be keratinized or nonkeratinized depending on the region."&lt;SEP&gt;"The epithelium is the surface layer of tissue surrounding the ovaries, where most ovarian cancers are found. It is the site of origin for various types of epithelial ovarian cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GYNECOLOGIC EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gynecologic exam is a medical examination of the female reproductive system, including screening for cervical cancer. It is recommended for patients with anal cancer to check for HPV-related cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gynecologic exam is a medical examination of the female reproductive system, including screening for cervical cancer. It is recommended for patients with anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BPH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BPH (benign prostatic hyperplasia) is a common non-cancerous condition where the prostate enlarges, causing urinary symptoms."&lt;SEP&gt;"BPH (benign prostatic hyperplasia) is a condition of an enlarged prostate that causes urinary symptoms, often confused with prostate cancer based on symptoms alone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNE SUPPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immune suppression, resulting from organ transplants or autoimmune diseases, is a risk factor for basal cell skin cancer, as a weakened immune system is less able to fight abnormal cell growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD-FORMING STEM CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood-forming stem cells are cells in the bone marrow that produce all blood cells; they are harvested for cell rescue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLIAL CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glial cells are support cells in the central nervous system that help nerve cells function. They are the origin of gliomas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glial cells are supportive cells in the brain and spinal cord that can develop into gliomas when mutations cause them to grow out of control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARSENIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arsenic is a cancer-causing agent that increases lung cancer risk, especially in smokers. It is a toxic element found in some water and industrial processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arsenic is a toxic substance found in soil, water, and air that can cause skin damage and lead to squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arsenic is an environmental toxin found in soil, water, and air that can cause skin damage and lead to squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVASIVE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Invasive cancer refers to colon cancer that has spread beyond the polyp into the colon wall, requiring specific treatment approaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"Invasive cancer refers to thyroid cancer that has grown beyond the thyroid or into surrounding tissues, requiring more aggressive treatment like total thyroidectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DENTISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dentists are healthcare professionals who commonly perform panoramic dental x-rays and may use them for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dentists are medical professionals who commonly perform procedures involving teeth, jaws, and surrounding structures, and are involved in planning treatments for dentures, braces, extractions, and implants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERFORMANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Performance refers to a patient's functional ability, assessed as performance status to guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N1 NODE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N1 node indicates cancer is found in regional lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPSY RESULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biopsy results provide tissue analysis to confirm cancer diagnosis and type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAF GENE MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BRAF gene mutations are specific biomarkers that can be present in thyroid cancer cells, making them eligible for targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SQUAMOUS CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Squamous cells are cells found in the tissues that form the surface of the skin and other areas, where anal cancer typically originates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cells are cells that make up the epithelial layer of the mouth, from which SCC originates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cells are flat cells found in the tissues forming the surface of the skin and other body areas, where squamous cell carcinoma originates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cells are flat cells found in the upper part of the epidermis. They are one of the main cell types in the epidermis and can be involved in other types of skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cells are flat, thin cells that normally line the epithelium of the esophagus, and their abnormal growth can lead to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cells are thin, flat cells found in the inner lining of the esophagus, which can change in Barrett esophagus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cells are thin, flat cells found throughout the body, including the skin, and are the origin of squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cells are thin, flat cells in the epidermis that look like fish scales and can develop into squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cells line the ectocervix and are the cell type from which most cervical cancers arise."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAP TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pap test is a procedure where cells are removed from the cervix for testing, used to detect cervical cancer or pre-cancer, not ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pap test is a screening method that tests cervical cells for cancer and cell changes, but not HPV."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pap test is a screening procedure that involves scraping cells from the cervix to test for cancer and cell changes. It is part of cervical cancer screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic changes (mutations) are alterations in DNA that allow cancer cells to multiply and survive longer than normal cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic changes (mutations) are alterations in cells that allow cancer cells to multiply and grow out of control."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic changes refer to alterations in DNA, such as chromosome translocations, tested in FL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic changes refer to alterations in genes, such as BCR::ABL1, that are tested for in cancer diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic changes, such as the BCR::ABL1 fusion, are biomarkers tested in CML to guide diagnosis and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGAN TRANSPLANTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organ transplants are medical procedures that can lead to immune suppression, which is a risk factor for developing basal cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTHY BLOOD CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Healthy blood cells are produced by new stem cells after rescue, restoring normal blood function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASTROCYTOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Astrocytomas are a common type of glioma tumor that arises from astrocytes, a type of glial cell."&lt;SEP&gt;"Astrocytomas are a type of glioma that look like star-shaped glial cells called astrocytes, which maintain the chemical environment for nerve cell communication."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VEHICLE EXHAUST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vehicle exhaust is an environmental pollutant that can cause skin damage and increase the risk of developing squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vehicle exhaust is an environmental pollutant that can cause skin damage and increase the risk of squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMOTHERAPY AFTER SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemotherapy after surgery is a treatment approach for non-metastatic colon cancer to eliminate remaining cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORAL SURGEONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oral surgeons are healthcare professionals who commonly perform panoramic dental x-rays and may use them for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oral surgeons are medical professionals who perform procedures on the mouth, teeth, and jaws, often in everyday practice, and are involved in treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adults are the population where gliomas occur more often, and this book specifically discusses gliomas in adults."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL CALENDAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Small Calendar is an item kept in a binder for scheduling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROXIMAL URETHRA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proximal urethra is the part of the urethra that goes through the prostate, sometimes removed during radical cystectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREGNANCY PREVENTION EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pregnancy Prevention Education is understanding birth control methods during treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pregnancy Prevention Education is understanding how to avoid pregnancy during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEM CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stem cells are cells in bone marrow that can develop into blood cells, and AML starts in these cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stem cells are cells in bone marrow that can develop into blood cells; AML starts in these cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stem cells are immature cells that can develop into various blood cells; they are harvested from the patient's blood or bone marrow for cell rescue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stem cells are undifferentiated cells that can develop into various cell types, including blood stem cells that give rise to all blood cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV/PAP CO-TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV/Pap co-test is a screening method that tests cervical cells for both HPV and cancer, providing more comprehensive results."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV/Pap co-test is a screening procedure where cervical cells are tested for both HPV and cancer. It is a more comprehensive test than a Pap test alone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN MALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"American males are the population group most affected by prostate cancer, which is the second most common cancer in this group after skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUTOIMMUNE DISEASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Autoimmune diseases are conditions that weaken the immune system, increasing the risk of cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Autoimmune diseases are conditions where the immune system attacks the body, and they can lead to immune suppression, increasing the risk of basal cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMOTHERAPY DRUGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemotherapy drugs are medications that kill rapidly dividing cells, including cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Drugs used in chemotherapy whose levels can be affected by supplements or herbs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLIGODENDROGLIOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oligodendrogliomas are a common type of glioma tumor that arises from oligodendrocytes, a type of glial cell."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oligodendrogliomas are a type of glioma that resemble oligodendrocytes, which protect electrical signaling in nerve cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ULCERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ulcers are chronic sores that can be sites for the development of squamous cell carcinoma, particularly in the form of Marjolin’s ulcer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ulcers are chronic sores that can develop into squamous cell carcinoma, known as Marjolin ulcer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAMILIAL ADENOMATOUS POLYPOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP) is a hereditary condition that can increase the risk of developing adrenal tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Familial adenomatous polyposis is an inherited syndrome that causes numerous polyps in the colon, increasing cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENT DOCTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ear, nose, and throat (ENT) doctor is a specialist who should be consulted if abnormalities are felt around the neck, glands, tongue, or mouth area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR CHARACTERISTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular characteristics refer to the unique genetic and biological features of each glioma, making each person's tumor unique."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESTROGEN RECEPTOR STATUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A test to determine if breast cancer cells have receptors for estrogen, which influences treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Estrogen receptor status is a test that determines whether breast cancer cells have receptors for estrogen, guiding treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATHETER PLACEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Catheter placement is a procedure where a thin, long tube is inserted into a large vein, often in the upper arm, to deliver systemic therapy, fluids, and blood products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Changes in genes, such as those in MMR genes, that can cause cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene mutations are changes in DNA that can be inherited or somatic, affecting cancer risk and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene mutations are changes in DNA that can be present in AML, influencing diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene mutations are changes in DNA that can cause cancer, with targeted therapies like Balversa designed for specific mutations such as FGFR3."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene mutations are changes in DNA that can drive AML development and aggressiveness, identified through genetic testing to guide treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gene mutations are changes in genes that can influence the subtype and treatment of AML, as mentioned in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN JOINT COMMITTEE ON CANCER (AJCC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The AJCC created a staging system used to determine the extent of cancer, including tumor size, lymph node spread, and metastasis, to guide prognosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) developed one of the staging systems for ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) is a medical organization that develops and maintains the tumor, node, metastasis (TNM) staging system for cancer, including colon cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) is an organization that created a staging system to determine the extent of cancer in the body, including tumor size, location, and subtype, used for prognosis and treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) is an organization that created a staging system to determine the extent of cancer in the body, including tumor size, lymph node involvement, and metastasis, used for prognosis and treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The American Joint Committee on Cancer is an organization that developed the TNM staging system used to stage anal cancer. It provides a standardized framework for assessing cancer extent."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAUNDICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jaundice is a symptom characterized by yellowed skin or eyes, which may indicate pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FULL SKIN EXAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Full skin exams are recommended at least once a year following treatment for basal cell skin cancer, to monitor for recurrence or new skin cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIATION TECHNIQUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A radiation technique is a method of delivering radiation therapy, such as whole-brain radiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLIOBLASTOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glioblastomas are a common and aggressive type of glioma tumor, known for rapid growth and difficulty in treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glioblastomas are the most common grade 4 gliomas, characterized by rapid growth and spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glioblastomas are the most destructive and dangerous type of glioma, originating from precursor cells that develop into cells like astrocytes and oligodendrocytes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BURNS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Burns are chronic wounds that can develop into squamous cell carcinoma, known as Marjolin ulcer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Burns are injuries to the skin that can lead to chronic wounds and scarring, increasing the risk of squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The narrator or patient who shares a personal journey of being dismissed for over a year, emphasizing perseverance, self-care, and mental health before diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINE NEEDLE BIOPSY (FNB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fine needle biopsy (FNB) is a biopsy procedure using a needle to remove a tissue sample for examination to confirm cancer presence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAIN FUNCTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brain functions are activities controlled by the brain, which can be disrupted by gliomas occurring in the upper part of the brain."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONAL CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormonal changes are symptoms caused by excess hormone production from functioning adrenal tumors, including excess facial hair, hair loss, irregular periods, enlarged breast tissue, and shrinking testicles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CAP USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical Cap Use is the placement of a cervical cap for birth control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABNORMAL CHROMOSOMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal chromosomes are changes in chromosomes that can influence the subtype and treatment of AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Abnormal chromosomes are structural changes in chromosomes that can be present in AML and affect diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Abnormal chromosomes are structural changes in chromosomes that can occur in AML, detected through genetic testing and influencing prognosis and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TNM SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A standardized cancer staging system describing tumor size (T), lymph node involvement (N), and metastasis (M)."&lt;SEP&gt;"TNM System is a staging system for breast cancer that combines scores for Tumor (T), Node (N), and Metastasis (M) to assign a cancer stage, such as T3N2M0."&lt;SEP&gt;"TNM System is a staging system using tumor (T), node (N), and metastasis (M) scores to describe cancer extent, with higher numbers indicating larger tumors or more spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"TNM system (tumor, node, metastasis) is used to stage bone cancers, describing tumor size, lymph node involvement, and metastasis."&lt;SEP&gt;"TNM system is a staging system for bone cancers, using T (tumor), N (node), and M (metastasis) to describe cancer growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"TNM system is a staging system that assesses the extent of cancer based on three key pieces: T (tumor size and invasion), N (lymph node involvement), and M (metastasis). It is used to stage anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The TNM system is a staging method using tumor (T), node (N), and metastasis (M) scores to describe cancer growth and spread, with higher numbers indicating more advanced disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"The TNM system is a standardized method for describing cancer, using letters T (tumor), N (node), and M (metastasis) to categorize the size, spread, and location of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tumor, node, metastasis (TNM) system is used to stage throat cancer, with scores assigned to T, N, and M to describe cancer growth and spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PANCREATIC DUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pancreatic ducts are tubes in the pancreas that can appear wider than normal on x-rays, indicating potential cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRACHELECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgery to remove the cervix, potentially including upper vagina and pelvic lymph nodes, preserving fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trachelectomy is a fertility-sparing surgery that removes the cervix, possibly including the upper part of the vagina."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAPIDLY DIVIDING CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rapidly dividing cells are cells that multiply quickly, such as cancer cells, which chemotherapy targets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDEMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Edema is swelling caused by excess fluid in body tissue, a possible sign of inflammatory breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Edema is swelling caused by fluid accumulation, a symptom of inflammatory breast cancer due to lymph vessel blockage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Edema is swelling in brain tissue around a tumor, often caused by glioma growth, contributing to symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAIR-SKINNED PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fair-skinned people are individuals with light skin, hair, and eyes who are at higher risk for squamous cell skin cancer due to sun exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENEMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A procedure involving liquid inserted into the rectum, sometimes needed before an MRI for rectal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGRAMMED DEATH PROTEIN 1 (PD-1)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Programmed death protein 1 (PD-1) is a protein targeted by immune checkpoint inhibitors in treating cancers with high tumor mutational burden."&lt;SEP&gt;"Programmed death protein 1 (PD-1) is an immune protein that, when expressed on cancer cells, can suppress immune response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NERVE CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nerve cells, or neurons, are cells in the central nervous system that transmit signals, and their function is supported by glial cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATASTROPHIC EVENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A catastrophic event, such as a nuclear accident, can expose people to large amounts of radiation, increasing thyroid cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B LYMPHOCYTES (B CELLS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B lymphocytes (B cells) are a type of lymphocyte that make antibodies, which are proteins that help fight infections. They are the cells affected in B-cell ALL (B-ALL)."&lt;SEP&gt;"B lymphocytes or B cells are a type of lymphocyte that make antibodies, which are proteins. ALL most often affects B cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER CARE TEAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer care team is a group of healthcare professionals who work together to plan and provide cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer care team is a group of medical professionals, including oncologists and specialists, who provide care for cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNE SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immune system is a function of blood, playing a role in fighting infection, as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune system is the body's defense mechanism that BCG therapy triggers to attack cancer cells in the bladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune system is the body's defense mechanism, and lymphocytes are an important part of it."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is a complex network of cells and proteins that defends the body against infection, involving white blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense against disease, which immunotherapy harnesses to fight cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense mechanism against abnormal cells, activated by certain topical treatments like imiquimod."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense mechanism against infection and disease, of which the lymphatic system is a part."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense mechanism against infections and diseases, involving cells like lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense mechanism against infections and diseases. It includes lymphocytes, which are affected in ALL, and plays a role in fighting infections and tumor cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense mechanism against infections, and blood plays an important role in it."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense mechanism against infections, involving white blood cells and other components."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense mechanism that can clear HPV infections in most people, but in some, the virus persists and leads to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense mechanism that immunotherapy stimulates to find and destroy cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense mechanism, which can be activated by calcipotriene to treat actinic keratosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense mechanism, which immunotherapy aims to enhance to destroy cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense mechanism, which is regulated by hormones from the adrenal glands."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense mechanism. An impaired immune system is a risk factor for developing primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's defense network, including the lymphatic system, that fights infection and cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's natural defense against infection and disease, which immunotherapy leverages to find and destroy cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune system is the body's natural defense against infection and disease. An impaired immune system may increase the risk of developing primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFLAMED PANCREAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inflamed pancreas is a condition that can be a sign of pancreatic cancer on x-rays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EBRT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EBRT (External Beam Radiation Therapy) is a type of radiation therapy delivered from outside the body, used for pelvic recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"EBRT (External Beam Radiation Therapy) is a type of radiation therapy that delivers radiation from outside the body to the tumor site, recommended after surgery and for treating metastatic lesions."&lt;SEP&gt;"EBRT (External Beam Radiation Therapy) is a type of radiation therapy used to treat cervical cancer, typically administered in 5 sessions per week for 5 to 6 weeks, often combined with chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"EBRT (External Beam Radiation Therapy) is a type of radiation therapy where a large machine aims radiation at the cancer site."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAIR FOLLICLE CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hair follicle cells are rapidly dividing cells that are damaged by chemotherapy, causing hair loss."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW-GRADE GLIOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low-grade glioma is a type of glioma that usually grows slowly, indicating a less aggressive tumor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low-grade gliomas are slow-growing tumors that may not cause symptoms for years, often diagnosed incidentally."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OUTDOOR WORKERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Outdoor workers are individuals who spend significant time in the sun, increasing their risk of squamous cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISMATCH REPAIR DEFICIENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker (dMMR) indicating a deficiency in DNA repair, tested in colon cancer tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DENTAL CLEANINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dental cleanings are regular checkups recommended for head and neck cancer patients to maintain oral health during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSCLE WEAKNESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muscle weakness is a symptom of adrenal cancer, often related to hormonal imbalances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Muscle weakness is a symptom of gliomas, affecting physical strength and coordination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT WITH CONTRAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CT with contrast is an imaging test that uses dye to enhance tumor visualization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LENVATINIB (LENVIMA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lenvatinib (Lenvima) is a targeted therapy drug recommended for treating thyroid cancer that cannot be removed with surgery and is progressing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer care encompasses all aspects of treatment, including biomarker testing and distress screening."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer care encompasses the comprehensive medical and supportive services provided to patients, including screening, treatment, and psychological support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer care involves making decisions about treatment, guided by expert recommendations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer care involves making decisions about treatment, which can be stressful and complex, and is guided by expert recommendations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer care involves making decisions about treatment, with recommendations from experts like NCCN Guidelines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRECANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Precancer refers to abnormal cells on the surface of the anal canal or perianal region that may develop into cancer if left untreated. It is a precursor to invasive anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Precancer refers to abnormal cells on the surface of the anal canal or perianal region that may develop into cancer, including conditions like anal dysplasia and high-grade anal intraepithelial neoplasia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH CARE PROVIDERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health care providers are medical professionals who monitor bladder cancer patients for recurrence and manage ongoing care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care providers are medical professionals who use various tests to diagnose prostate cancer, plan treatment, and monitor patients' health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care providers are professionals who can recommend screening tests and discuss prostate cancer risk with patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care providers are professionals who should be informed of symptoms for special testing and diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care providers are professionals who suspect and diagnose pancreatic cancer based on symptoms and tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care providers are professionals who work with patients to determine appropriate screening and treatment for prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care providers include doctors, specialists, and allied health professionals who deliver medical care to patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL CANCER INSTITUTE (NCI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"National Cancer Institute (NCI) is a U.S. government agency providing comprehensive cancer information and research resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"The NCI is a U.S. government agency that provides resources for finding clinical trials and offers a Cancer Information Service (CIS) for patient support."&lt;SEP&gt;"The NCI is a U.S. organization providing resources for finding clinical trials and cancer information, including its Cancer Information Service (CIS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Cancer Institute (NCI) is a U.S. government agency that conducts and supports cancer research and provides resources for finding clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Cancer Institute (NCI) is a U.S. government agency that provides information and resources for cancer treatment and clinical trial searches via cancer.gov."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Cancer Institute (NCI) is a U.S. government agency that provides information and resources on cancer treatment and clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Cancer Institute (NCI) is a U.S. government agency that provides resources for finding clinical trials and cancer information, including a Cancer Information Service."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIEMETIC MEDICINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antiemetic medicines are drugs used to reduce nausea and vomiting during chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-GRADE GLIOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-grade glioma is a type of glioma that often grows rapidly, indicating a more aggressive tumor."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-grade gliomas are fast-growing tumors that develop quickly, causing severe symptoms and requiring aggressive treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS® ADRENAL TUMORS, 2022&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A set of guidelines for patients with adrenal tumors, published in 2022, providing information on medical history, imaging tests, and other relevant topics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSATELLITE STABLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker (MSS) indicating stable microsatellites, meaning no dMMR or MSI-H."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PDL1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PDL1 is a protein whose expression is measured using a combined positive score (CPS) to determine if a cancer patient may benefit from immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WALKING DIFFICULTIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Walking, balance, or coordination difficulties are symptoms of gliomas, impacting motor functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLDERS FOR INSURANCE FORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Folders for Insurance Forms are organizational tools in a binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADHESIVE RING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adhesive ring is a watertight barrier that sticks to the skin and holds the ostomy bag in place."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEST RESULT INTERPRETATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Test Result Interpretation is understanding what blood and imaging results mean."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL CANAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anal canal is the small section of the large intestine connecting the rectum to the anal opening."&lt;SEP&gt;"The anal canal is the small section of bowel between the rectum and the anus, where anal cancer typically starts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The anal canal is the terminal part of the large intestine through which stool passes. It is the primary site where anal cancer develops, and the text discusses tumors in this area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT OPTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment options are discussed by the care team with the patient, including whether surgery is an option."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment options are the various medical approaches available for bone cancer, including surgery, immunotherapy, and targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment options are various therapies available for primary CNS lymphoma, including chemotherapy, radiation, and stem cell rescue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment options for glioma include surgery, radiation, chemotherapy, and clinical trials, often combined for effectiveness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment options for primary CNS lymphoma include chemotherapy, radiation therapy, stem cell transplant, or clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE (NLM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The NLM is a U.S. library that hosts clinicaltrials.gov, a worldwide database for finding clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The NLM is a U.S. organization that hosts clinicaltrials.gov, a database for finding clinical trials worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM) is a U.S. government agency that maintains clinicaltrials.gov, a database of clinical trials worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM) is a federal library that hosts clinicaltrials.gov, a worldwide database for clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM) is a federal library that maintains clinicaltrials.gov, a global database for clinical trial information."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM) is a federal library that maintains clinicaltrials.gov, a worldwide database of clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN MEDICATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pain medications are drugs used to manage pain, often prescribed by pain specialists."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAGNOSTIC TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diagnostic tests are procedures used to confirm a prostate cancer diagnosis and determine its stage, such as biopsies or imaging, following screening tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnostic tests are used to confirm cancer, determine if it is localized or advanced, plan treatment, and detect recurrence or spread after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnostic tests are used to identify cancer characteristics, such as biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnostic tests include imaging, biopsy, and lab testing used to identify and characterize gliomas for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnostic tests, including biopsy and imaging, are used to confirm or rule out prostate cancer when initial screenings suggest abnormalities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FDG-PET/CT SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of PET scan using radioactive sugar as a tracer to detect active cancer cells, which use sugar faster than normal cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"FDG-PET/CT scan is a specific imaging test combining positron emission tomography and computed tomography to detect cancer activity, often used 3-6 months after treatment for certain stages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISMATCH REPAIR PROFICIENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker (pMMR) indicating normal DNA repair function, opposite of dMMR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL-FREE DNA TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell-free or circulating tumor DNA (ctDNA) testing uses a blood sample to detect cancer cells or tumor DNA fragments, used by some providers to monitor treatment response and recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPEECH DIFFICULTIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Difficulty speaking or swallowing are symptoms of gliomas, affecting communication and basic functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Another term for ductal carcinoma in situ, referring to cancer within the ducts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PORT PLACEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Port placement is a procedure where a small, round disc is inserted under the skin, usually in the chest, to deliver systemic therapy, fluids, and blood products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERIANAL REGION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Perianal region is the anal opening and surrounding skin, relevant to anal cancer location."&lt;SEP&gt;"The perianal region includes the anal opening and the skin directly surrounding it, where anal cancer can also start."&lt;SEP&gt;"The perianal region includes the anal opening and the skin directly surrounding it, where perianal cancer can originate."&lt;SEP&gt;"The perianal region is the area surrounding the anus. Abnormal cells can develop on the surface of this region, leading to precancerous lesions or cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARE PLAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Care plan is a personalized plan developed by the care team for the patient's specific needs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN CANCER CENTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN Cancer Centers are U.S. institutions that provide cancer care and can be found via NCCN.org/cancercenters."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Cancer Centers are a network of cancer treatment centers in the United States that provide clinical trial information and care for cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Cancer Centers are a network of cancer treatment centers in the United States, providing resources for finding clinical trials via NCCN.org/cancercenters."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Cancer Centers are institutions listed on NCCN.org that provide cancer treatment and are resources for finding clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Cancer Centers are part of the National Comprehensive Cancer Network, providing cancer care and patient guidelines, accessible via NCCN.org."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Cancer Centers is a network of cancer treatment centers in the United States, providing resources for finding clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITIONAL ADVICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutritional advice is guidance on diet provided by nutritionists to support health during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEADACHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Headaches are a common side effect of radiation therapy, which can be controlled with medications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Headaches are a common symptom of glioma, often worse in the morning or waking patients at night, and can occur with nausea."&lt;SEP&gt;"Headaches are a neurological symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, caused by pressure on the central nervous system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Headaches, especially unusual or frequent ones, are common symptoms of gliomas caused by pressure on the brain."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPORTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Written documents from healthcare providers about a patient's specific type of cancer, which are included in the medical binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARCINOEMBRYONIC ANTIGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood test (CEA) measuring a protein that may indicate cancer presence, recommended in initial testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THROAT (PHARYNX)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The throat (pharynx) is the anatomical location where throat cancer occurs, and examinations may involve a scope inserted through the mouth or nose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICAL TRIAL PARTICIPATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical trial participation is an event where patients with gliomas may enroll to test potential new treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PINK OR PURPLE STRETCH MARKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pink or purple stretch marks on the skin are a symptom of adrenal cancer, often associated with excess cortisol production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M0 METASTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M0 metastasis indicates no distant metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMAGING SCANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Imaging scans are diagnostic tools used to determine if cancer has spread deep within the skin or to other parts of the body, aiding in staging and treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging scans are tests used to visualize the size and location of tumors and detect cancer spread beyond the prostate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging scans are used to determine if cancer has spread deeper into the skin or to other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging scans, such as MRI, are used to calculate DOI and assess tumor characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical tests such as CT, MRI, or bone scans used to visualize tumors and metastases for staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PENIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Penis is part of the male reproductive system, involved in sexual reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Penis is part of the male reproductive system, through which semen is released during ejaculation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Penis is the organ through which semen and urine are released from the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"The male reproductive organ through which the urethra passes, examined during cystoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The penis is an organ where HPV can infect and cause cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER INFORMATION SERVICE (CIS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CIS is a service of the NCI that helps people find clinical trials, reachable via phone or cancer.gov/contact."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CIS is a service provided by the NCI that offers help finding clinical trials and cancer-related information via phone or website."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Cancer Information Service (CIS) is a service of the NCI that provides assistance and information about cancer and clinical trials via phone and online."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Cancer Information Service (CIS) is a service of the NCI that provides assistance in finding clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Cancer Information Service (CIS) is a service of the NCI that provides help finding clinical trials via phone (1-800-4-CANCER) and cancer.gov/contact."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Cancer Information Service (CIS) is a service provided by the NCI to help patients find clinical trials and answer cancer-related questions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physical function refers to the ability to perform physical activities, which rehabilitation aims to improve."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEIZURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Seizures are a neurological symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, caused by abnormal brain activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seizures are common symptoms of gliomas, resulting from abnormal electrical activity in the brain due to tumor invasion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seizures are frequent in brain tumor patients and are often an early sign of glioma, especially in low-grade types."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUESTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A section in the medical binder for noting questions to ask healthcare providers during appointments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EBV-RELATED CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EBV-related cancer is a type of cancer caused by the Epstein-Barr virus, with most nasopharyngeal cancers being EBV-related."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGNOSTIC STAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prognostic stage includes anatomic TNM plus tumor grade and assumes standard-of-care treatment, divided into clinical and pathologic stages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE X-RAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone x-ray is a diagnostic imaging test using low-dose radiation to take pictures of bones, useful for detecting tumors and bone issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INHERITED GENE MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inherited gene mutations are changes in DNA passed down that can increase risk of hereditary thyroid cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T LYMPHOCYTES (T CELLS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T lymphocytes (T cells) are a type of lymphocyte that help fight infections, kill tumor cells, and control immune responses. They are the cells affected in T-cell ALL (T-ALL)."&lt;SEP&gt;"T lymphocytes are a type of lymphocyte that develop in the thymus and are crucial for immune response."&lt;SEP&gt;"T lymphocytes or T cells are a type of lymphocyte that help fight infections, kill tumor cells, and control immune responses. ALL can affect T cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 3: WATCH AND WAIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 3: Watch and wait is a section of a guide that discusses the watch and wait stage for CLL patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISTANT METASTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Distant Metastasis refers to cancer spread to distant organs, such as lungs or liver, indicating advanced disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant metastasis is cancer spread to parts of the body far from the primary tumor, classified as M1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant metastasis is cancer that has spread to parts of the body outside the neck, as opposed to regional lymph node metastasis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant metastasis is the spread of cancer to distant parts of the body, such as lungs, lymph nodes, bones, liver, or brain, far from the primary site."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant metastasis refers to cancer that has spread to areas far from the primary tumor, such as the lung or bone in the case of liver cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant metastasis refers to cancer that has spread to body parts far from the primary tumor, such as bone, lungs, liver, brain, or distant lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant metastasis refers to cancer that has spread to body parts far from the primary tumor, such as bones, lungs, liver, or brain."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOACTIVE GLUCOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radioactive glucose is a sugar substance injected into the body during a PET scan. Cancer cells absorb it more quickly, making them appear brighter on the scan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEMINAL VESICLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Seminal vesicles are glands that help make semen, sometimes removed during radical cystectomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seminal vesicles are part of the male reproductive system, contributing to semen production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seminal vesicles are two glands located above the prostate and behind the bladder that produce and store fluid that becomes part of semen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seminal vesicles are two glands that make and store part of the fluid that becomes semen, located above the prostate and behind the bladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Seminal vesicles are two glands that make part of the fluid that becomes semen, located above the prostate and behind the bladder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FATIGUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatigue is a common general side effect of anal cancer treatment, affecting quality of life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a common side effect during EBRT, developing gradually over treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a common side effect of both radiation therapy and chemotherapy, affecting patient energy levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a common side effect of cancer treatment, addressed in survivorship care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a common side effect of cancer treatment, affecting energy levels and daily activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a common side effect of chemotherapy and radiation therapy, which can last for weeks after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a common side effect of chemotherapy, impacting daily activities and quality of life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a common side effect of cisplatin chemotherapy, characterized by extreme tiredness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a common side effect of various cancer treatments, including targeted therapy, immunotherapy, and high-dose chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a debilitating symptom of glioma, not related to sleep or activity, but may be helped by physical exercise."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a feeling of tiredness and weakness that occurs after stem cell rescue and during recovery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a short-term side effect of radiation therapy for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a symptom described as more than just being tired, encompassing physical, cognitive, or emotional exhaustion, potentially caused by external sources like noise or internal sources like medication, poor diet, or lack of exercise."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is a symptom of CLL, characterized by tiredness or excessive tiredness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is extreme tiredness that can result from cancer treatment, affecting daily activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue is extreme tiredness, a common side effect of chemotherapy and immunotherapy in cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatigue, or tiredness, is a common side effect of both radiation therapy and systemic therapy for cancer. It can occur during treatment and may persist for a period after treatment ends."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPEECH FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Speech function is the ability to speak, which speech therapists help restore if affected by treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEMS WITH THINKING AND SPEECH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cognitive issues such as confusion, memory loss, and speech difficulties are symptoms of glioma affecting brain function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Problems with thinking and speech include confusion, memory loss, and speech difficulties, which are symptoms of a brain tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A section in the medical binder for taking notes during medical appointments or about health information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Notes are written records of questions or information, kept in a medical binder for reference."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGRAMMED DEATH LIGAND 1 (PD-L1)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PD-L1 is an immune protein expressed on cancer cells that can cause immune cells to ignore the cancer, and its presence may indicate benefit from checkpoint inhibitor therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Programmed death ligand 1 (PD-L1) is an immune protein expressed on cancer cells that suppresses immune response; its testing guides immunotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE STATUS (N)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph node status (N) is a component of TNM staging that indicates whether cancer has spread to nearby lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST MRI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breast MRI is a magnetic resonance imaging test used to get detailed images of the breast, often when other tests are inconclusive."&lt;SEP&gt;"Breast MRI is a specific type of MRI used to image the breast, often in addition to a mammogram, with the patient positioned face down."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endoscopy is a procedure using a scope to examine internal areas, often with examination under anesthesia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INCREASED RISK OF INFECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Increased risk of infection is a common side effect of chemotherapy due to lowered white blood cell counts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Increased risk of infection is a side effect of chemotherapy due to damage to fast-growing blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Increased risk of infection is a side effect of cisplatin, due to lowered immune function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE METASTASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph node metastases are cancer cells found in regional lymph nodes, with risk increasing with DOI."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHATICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymphatics are vessels that carry lymph fluid and can transport cancer cells. They are a route for anal cancer to spread to lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The network of vessels in the breast through which dye and radioactive material travel to reach lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URETHRA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The tube through which urine exits the body, examined during cystoscopy for cancer signs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tube through which urine passes and through which TURBT instruments are guided."&lt;SEP&gt;"The urethra is a nearby organ that anal cancer can invade in stage IIIB or IIIC."&lt;SEP&gt;"The urethra is a tube that takes urine from the bladder to outside the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urethra is a anatomical structure through which a cystoscopy device is inserted to view the bladder, playing a role in diagnostic procedures for urinary tract conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urethra is a part of the urinary tract that is examined during cystoscopy, where bleeding may occur after the procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urethra is a tube that can be compressed by an enlarged prostate, affecting urine flow."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urethra is a tube that carries urine from the bladder and out of the body, surrounded by the prostate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urethra is a tube that carries urine from the bladder and out of the body; the prostate surrounds it just beneath the bladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urethra is a tube that carries urine out of the body during urination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urethra is the canal through which a catheter is inserted for intravesical therapy to deliver medicine into the bladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urethra is the tube that carries urine from the bladder out of the body, part of the urinary tract's inner layer where cancer can start."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urethra is the tube through which urine exits the body, sometimes removed in radical cystectomy or used in neobladder construction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urethra is the tube through which urine is expelled from the body during urination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWALLOWING FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Swallowing function is the ability to swallow, which speech therapists address if impaired."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEAKNESS OR PROBLEMS MOVING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muscle weakness on one side of the body, difficulty walking, or balance issues are symptoms of glioma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weakness or problems moving refers to muscle weakness on one side of the body or difficulty with walking or balance, which can occur in people with a brain tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH CHOLESTEROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A health condition that may run in families, relevant to family health history."&lt;SEP&gt;"High cholesterol is a condition that can contribute to NAFLD and increase the risk of liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR HPV TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor HPV testing detects human papillomavirus in tumor samples, which is relevant for certain head and neck cancers, including some nasopharyngeal cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISTANT METASTASIS (M)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Distant metastasis (M) is a component of TNM staging that indicates whether cancer has spread to distant organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPINE AND BRAIN MRI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spine and brain MRI is a type of MRI used to detect breast cancer that has spread to the spine or brain, with specific positioning and contrast use."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLDERS FOR TEST TYPES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Folders for Test Types categorize records by test kind."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EARLY NSCLC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Early NSCLC refers to stage 1 cancer that has grown from the airway into lung tissue but has not spread to other organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOLOGY REPORT REVIEW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiology Report Review is reading radiologist reports on imaging tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLEEDING OR BRUISING EASILY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bleeding or bruising easily is a common side effect of chemotherapy due to lowered platelet counts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bleeding or bruising easily is a side effect of chemotherapy, caused by damage to blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bleeding or bruising easily is a side effect of cisplatin, related to reduced platelet counts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARCINOMA IN SITU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carcinoma in situ (Tis) is a very early form of cancer where abnormal cells are present but have not invaded surrounding tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carcinoma in situ is a precancerous condition where abnormal cells are present but have not invaded deeper tissues, also known as stage 0 anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carcinoma in situ is a stage where cancerous cells are found only in the squamous cell layer, as in Tis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cancer screening involves scraping cells from the cervix and testing them for HPV, cancer, and cell changes. It is recommended for anal cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical cancer screening is a procedure to detect HPV and cancer in cervical cells, recommended for anal cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical cancer screening is recommended for patients with anal cancer due to the shared link with HPV infection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer, including melanoma, associated with inherited mutations in BRCA1 and BRCA2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin cancer is a broad category of cancer that occurs in the skin, with basal cell carcinoma being the most common type. It can also include squamous cell carcinoma and melanoma, which are mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin cancer is a type of cancer that can be screened for during regular checkups, as mentioned in the context of cancer prevention."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin cancer is a type of cancer that develops from skin cells, distinct from primary cutaneous lymphomas which develop from lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin cancer is a type of cancer that develops in skin cells, including squamous cell carcinoma (CSCC)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin cancer is the most common cancer in American males, with prostate cancer being the second most common."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COGNITIVE PROBLEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cognitive problems are issues with thinking or memory that may occur from cancer or treatment, a goal to minimize."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cognitive problems, such as memory issues, slowed thinking, and trouble speaking, are potential long-term side effects of radiation therapy, particularly WBRT."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHANGES IN PERSONALITY OR MOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Behavioral changes, including personality shifts and mood alterations, can occur due to glioma affecting brain areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Changes in personality or mood refer to alterations in behavior, mood, and personality that can occur in people whose tumors are located in parts of the brain that control these functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STROKE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A disease that may run in families, relevant to family health history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stroke is a health condition that may run in families and is asked about as part of family history assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TMB-H&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TMB-H (tumor mutational burden-high) is a biomarker indicating a high number of mutations in cancer cells, making them more likely to respond to immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"TMB-H (tumor mutational burden-high) is defined as 10 or more mutations per million base pairs of tumor DNA, often treated with immunotherapy drugs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR GRADE (G)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor grade (G) describes how much cancer cells resemble normal cells, providing prognostic information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BILATERAL MAMMOGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bilateral mammogram is a type of mammogram that includes pictures of both breasts, used for comprehensive breast imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREINVASIVE DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition like DCIS where cancerous cells are in place and have not spread, but may progress if untreated."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN GUIDELINE FOR PATIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The NCCN Guideline for Patients provides information about early-stage prostate cancer and is available at NCCN.org/patientguidelines and on the NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer app."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NERVE DAMAGE (NEUROPATHY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nerve damage, or neuropathy, is a common side effect of chemotherapy, causing pain, numbness, or tingling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nerve damage, or neuropathy, is a side effect of cisplatin, causing pain, numbness, or tingling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local disease refers to cancer that is confined to the original site, with stages like T4a and T4b indicating advanced local disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local disease refers to squamous cell skin cancer that has not spread to nearby lymph nodes, usually treated with surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV testing detects the presence of high-risk HPV strains in cervical cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV testing is a laboratory test to detect the presence of HPV in cervical cells, often combined with a Pap test."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV testing is a laboratory test to detect the presence of HPV in cervical cells. It is part of cervical cancer screening."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV testing, specifically p16 testing, is recommended for all patients diagnosed with throat (oropharyngeal) cancer to gather prognostic and treatment information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERECTILE DYSFUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Erectile dysfunction (difficulty getting an erection) or painful ejaculation is a symptom that may indicate prostate issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erectile dysfunction is a sexual side effect of anal cancer treatment, characterized by difficulty achieving or maintaining an erection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erectile dysfunction is a symptom of prostate cancer, involving difficulty getting an erection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WELL-BEING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Well-being is a state of physical and mental health, central to quality of life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAB TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lab testing analyzes tissue or fluid samples to identify genetic markers and characteristics of glioma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANCESTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ancestry refers to the countries of origin of a family, which may influence genetic risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"The countries of origin of a family's ancestors, which is part of family health history."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NASOPHARYNGEAL CANCER STAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nasopharyngeal cancer staging is a process to describe the size and spread of cancer, guiding prognosis and treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANATOMIC STAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anatomic stage is based on the extent of cancer as defined by tumor size (T), lymph node status (N), and distant metastasis (M)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOMOSYNTHESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tomosynthesis is a 3-dimensional (3D) mammogram technique that provides more detailed images of the breast compared to standard 2D mammography."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tomosynthesis is a 3D mammogram technique that provides detailed images of the breast, used for screening and diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABDOMINAL BLOATING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abdominal bloating is a symptom of adrenal cancer, often due to tumor growth pressing on abdominal organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M1 METASTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M1 metastasis indicates distant metastasis is found, with M1a (lung) and M1b (bone or other distant sites)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIDNEY DAMAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kidney damage is a more severe side effect of intraperitoneal chemotherapy, affecting renal function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kidney damage is a potential side effect of cisplatin, which may limit its use in patients with poor kidney function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kidney damage is a potential side effect of cisplatin, which may prevent its use in patients with poor kidney function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kidney damage is a side effect of platinum-based chemotherapy medicines, including carboplatin, cisplatin, and oxaliplatin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVANCED DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Advanced disease refers to cancer that has spread or is very advanced, such as metastatic or T4b stages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell changes are abnormal alterations in cervical cells that may indicate precancerous or cancerous conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cell changes refer to abnormal alterations in cervical cells that may lead to cancer. They are detected during cervical cancer screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAINFUL EJACULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Painful ejaculation is a symptom of prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Painful ejaculation is a symptom that may indicate prostate issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENJOYMENT OF LIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enjoyment of life is a component of quality of life, reflecting overall satisfaction and happiness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH AND SYMPTOMS EVALUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health and symptoms evaluation is the initial step in glioma diagnosis, involving review of medical history and symptom assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOLOGIST'S REPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A written report by a radiologist interpreting imaging test results, sent to the patient's doctor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NPC STAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NPC stages refer to the classification of nasopharyngeal cancer based on TNM scores, reflecting prognosis and treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAW, TEETH, AND GUMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jaw, teeth, and gums are oral health areas that can be affected by head and neck cancer treatment, requiring dental care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2D DIGITAL MAMMOGRAPHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2D digital mammography is a standard mammogram technique that uses low-dose x-rays to create two-dimensional images of the breast."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPORADIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sporadic refers to cancers with no clear cause or risk factor, as most thyroid cancers are."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK® (NCCN®)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"National Comprehensive Cancer Network® (NCCN®) is an organization that holds the copyright for the text provided, indicating it is a source of cancer-related guidelines and information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 4: TREATMENT FOR CLL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 4: Treatment for CLL is a section of a guide that discusses treatment options for CLL, including biomarkers used to select treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood cancer includes types like lymphoma, chronic lymphocytic leukemia, and multiple myeloma, which increase the risk of anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood cancer is a broad category that includes ALL and AML, characterized by abnormal blood cell production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood cancer is a type of cancer affecting blood cells, including AML, as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood cancer is a type of cancer affecting blood cells, including CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood cancer is a type of cancer affecting blood cells, including lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood cancer is a type of cancer that affects blood cells, such as chronic myeloid leukemia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BURNING OR PAIN WHILE URINATING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Burning or pain while urinating is a symptom of prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Burning or pain while urinating is a symptom that may occur in prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TINNITUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tinnitus is a ringing in the ears, a side effect of cisplatin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tinnitus is ringing in the ears, a potential side effect of cisplatin chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;USUAL ACTIVITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Usual activities are routine tasks that patients aim to maintain, part of quality of life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOVED ONES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Loved ones are family and friends who support and understand the challenges of primary CNS lymphoma, as addressed in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loved ones of glioma patients offer support and help understand the disease and its challenges."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTRAST MATERIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Substances used to enhance imaging, which may cause allergic reactions and are not permanent."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SAMPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A sample is a piece of tissue removed during biopsy and sent to a lab for microscopic examination to diagnose skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sample refers to a portion of tumor tissue or blood taken for diagnostic testing, including biopsy and biomarker analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PD-L1 BIOMARKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PD-L1 biomarker is a protein that can be present on cancer cells, and its presence influences the choice of first-line systemic therapy regimens for metastatic cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;3D MAMMOGRAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"3D mammograms, also known as tomosynthesis, are an advanced imaging technique that creates three-dimensional images of the breast."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RED BLOOD CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cells in the blood that carry oxygen; their count is measured in a CBC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cells that carry oxygen throughout the body, measured in a CBC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red Blood Cells are blood cells that may be low in CLL; their counts are measured in blood tests to assess disease impact."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells (RBCs or erythrocytes) are a type of blood cell that carry oxygen throughout the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells (RBCs or erythrocytes) carry oxygen throughout the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells are a type of blood cell that carries oxygen, formed from blood stem cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells are a type of blood cell that carry oxygen, and their numbers are reduced in AML("entity"&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells are a type of blood cell that carry oxygen, and their numbers are reduced in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells are a type of blood cell that may be low in CLL patients, as mentioned in the context of blood counts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells are blood cells that can sickle in certain genetic conditions, related to renal medullary carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells are blood components that carry oxygen throughout the body, measured in a complete blood count."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells are produced from blood stem cells in red marrow."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells are produced in response to hormones from the kidneys, which help maintain healthy oxygen transport."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells carry oxygen throughout the body and are measured in a CBC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells carry oxygen throughout the body, measured in a CBC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells carry oxygen throughout the body, measured in complete blood count for bladder cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER STAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer stage describes how far the cancer has spread, influencing treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer stage describes the extent of cancer spread, guiding treatment decisions for bladder cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer stage describes the extent of cancer spread, used to guide treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer stage describes the extent of lung cancer in the body, with stages 1, 2, 3, and 4 indicating progression from early to metastatic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer stage describes where the cancer has or hasn't spread from the ovary. Surgery is needed to know exactly how much cancer is in the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer stage is a factor in eligibility criteria for clinical trials, indicating the extent of disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer stage is a measure of how far cancer has spread, determined by the TNM system, and guides treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer stage is an assessment of the extent of cancer in the body, determined by the TNM system. It helps guide treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer stage is an assessment of the extent of cancer in the body, with stages I-III being non-metastatic and stage IV being metastatic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer stage refers to the extent of cancer spread in the body, which determines treatment approach."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer stage refers to the extent of cancer spread in the body, which determines treatment options for bladder and anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNEXPLAINED WEIGHT LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unexplained weight loss is a symptom of advanced prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unexplained weight loss is a symptom that may occur in prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEARING PROBLEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hearing problems are a potential side effect of cisplatin, including hearing loss."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hearing problems or hearing loss can occur with extended treatment with cisplatin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hearing problems or loss are side effects of cisplatin, affecting auditory function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARE GOALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Care goals are objectives set by the patient and team, including cancer control and quality of life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVAL STATISTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survival statistics are historical data on glioma outcomes, which may not reflect current treatment improvements."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIPHENHYDRAMINE (BENADRYL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medicine given to prevent allergic reactions to contrast materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFECTIOUS MONONUCLEOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Infectious mononucleosis is an illness caused by Epstein-Barr virus, which can lead to EBV-related cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEVACIZUMAB (AVASTIN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bevacizumab (Avastin) is a targeted therapy, a biologic designed to work with chemotherapy, and may be added to certain first-line regimens for metastatic cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"bevacizumab (Avastin) is a medication that stops the growth of new blood vessels feeding tumors, used in chemotherapy for ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHELLFISH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shellfish, such as shrimp, are a potential allergen that may be related to contrast allergies, and patients should inform doctors of any such allergies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLDERS FOR TREATMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Folders for Treatments organize records by therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCALLY ADVANCED NSCLC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Locally advanced NSCLC refers to stage 2 and 3 cancers that have grown into lung tissue and may have spread to lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATHOLOGY REPORT REVIEW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pathology Report Review is examining tissue analysis reports."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN GUIDELINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Guidelines for cancer care, including colorectal cancer screening, developed by NCCN."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guidelines for cancer care, including colorectal cancer screening."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guidelines for cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines are clinical practice guidelines provided by the National Comprehensive Cancer Network, offering recommendations for cancer treatment, including kidney cancer and related conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines are evidence-based recommendations for cancer care, including breast cancer treatment and management."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines are patient guidelines for breast cancer types, including DCIS, invasive, and metastatic, available at NCCN.org/patientguidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines are recommendations for cancer care, trusted by patients and providers, based on expert research."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines are trusted resources for patients and providers, explaining current cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines provide evidence-based recommendations for cancer care, including patient guidelines for prostate cancer, accessible via NCCN.org."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines provide evidence-based recommendations for cancer care, including patient guides for colon and rectal cancer, accessible at NCCN.org."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines provide patient information on cancer care, including fertility and family planning resources for young adults."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines provide patient information, including for adolescents and young adults with cancer, available at NCCN.org/patientguidelines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T CATEGORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T category is a component of the TNM system that describes the size and extent of the primary tumor."&lt;SEP&gt;"T category is a component of the TNM system that measures the size and extent of invasion of the anal tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE, HIP, OR BACK PAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone, hip, or back pain is a symptom of advanced prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone, hip, or back pain is a symptom that may occur in prostate cancer, potentially indicating spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER TYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer type is a factor in eligibility criteria for clinical trials, specifying which cancers are studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer type refers to the specific kind of cancer, such as cervical cancer, which determines treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIST OF NAMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A list of names is a record of the multidisciplinary team members for reference."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLOW-UP VISITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follow-up visits are periodic appointments recommended after glioma treatment to monitor for tumor regrowth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Follow-up visits are periodic check-ups recommended after glioma treatment to monitor for recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREDNISONE (STEROIDS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A steroid medicine given to prevent allergic reactions to contrast materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGRAMMED CELL DEATH PROTEIN 1 (PD-1)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PD-1 is a protein targeted by immune checkpoint inhibitors, often used in treating metastatic or unresectable TMB-H cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"PD-1 is a protein targeted by immunotherapy drugs in TMB-H cancers, helping activate immune response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TISOTUMAB VEDOTIN-TFTV (TIVDAK)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tisotumab vedotin-tftv (Tivdak) is a targeted therapy option for metastatic cervical cancer without specific biomarkers, used in second-line or beyond treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUMP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lump is a symptom that may indicate breast cancer, prompting the use of diagnostic mammograms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2D DIGITAL MAMMOGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A standard two-dimensional mammogram using low-dose x-rays to examine the breast."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOPHARMACEUTICALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiopharmaceuticals are a treatment for advanced-stage prostate cancer that deliver radiation directly to cancer cells, often used for bone metastases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patients are individuals diagnosed with glioma who undergo testing, treatment, and follow-up care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patients are individuals receiving cancer care, whose preferences about treatment are important and should be communicated to their care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N CATEGORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N category is a component of the TNM system that indicates whether lymph nodes are involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"N category is a component of the TNM system that indicates whether lymph nodes near the anus have cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINATING FREQUENTLY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urinating frequently, especially at night, is a symptom of prostate issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urinating frequently, especially at night, is a symptom that may require special testing for prostate issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT HISTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment history is a factor in eligibility criteria for clinical trials, affecting which patients can participate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatment history is a record of prior cancer treatments, used in eligibility criteria for clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COORDINATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A coordinator is a person who manages and schedules care, ensuring communication among team members."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADDITIONAL ROUNDS OF TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Additional rounds of treatment are often needed because gliomas tend to grow back after initial therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SSTRPET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of PET scan that may be helpful for those with adrenal tumors, using somatostatin receptor targeting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNOTHERAPY DRUGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immunotherapy drugs target proteins like PD-1 or PD-L1 to activate the immune system against cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVANCE CARE PLANNING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Advance care planning involves discussions with doctors about prognosis and creating end-of-life care plans, offering benefits like knowing what to expect and reducing caregiver stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIPPLE THICKENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nipple thickening is a symptom that may indicate breast cancer, prompting diagnostic mammograms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEVER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fever is a symptom of CLL, indicating possible infection or disease activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fever is a symptom that can occur in adrenal cancer, possibly due to tumor-related inflammation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCLC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SCLC (Small Cell Lung Cancer) is a type of lung cancer characterized by rapid growth, primarily caused by smoking, and is difficult to detect early."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROVIDERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Providers are healthcare professionals who use NCCN Guidelines to recommend care for patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Providers are healthcare professionals who use the NCCN Guidelines to inform patient care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M CATEGORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"M category is a component of the TNM system that indicates whether cancer has metastasized to distant areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"M category is a component of the TNM system that indicates whether cancer has metastasized."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEAK OR INTERMITTENT URINE STREAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weak or intermittent urine stream is a symptom of prostate issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weak or intermittent urine stream is a symptom that may indicate prostate problems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENERAL HEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"General health is a factor in clinical trial eligibility, ensuring participant safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health is a factor in eligibility criteria for clinical trials, determining patient suitability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHASES OF TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phases of treatment include induction, consolidation, and specific treatments for spine and eyes, outlining the treatment journey."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONLINE RESOURCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Online resources are listed in the back of the book to help caregivers and patients gather support for primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Online resources provide information and support for glioma patients and caregivers, as listed in the book."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PANORAMIC DENTAL X-RAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A panoramic dental x-ray (Panorex) is a dental imaging procedure using a small dose of radiation to capture the entire mouth, including teeth, jaws, and surrounding structures. It is used by dentists and oral surgeons for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Panoramic dental x-ray (Panorex) is an imaging test using a small dose of radiation to capture the entire mouth, including teeth, jaws, and surrounding structures, commonly used by dentists for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Panoramic dental x-ray is an imaging test capturing the entire mouth in one image, used by dentists for treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOLOGICAL PARENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biological parents are the genetic parents from whom germline mutations are inherited."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biological parents are the source of inherited genetic mutations, which are not tested in tumor mutation testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDIASTINAL GRAY ZONE LYMPHOMA (MGZL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mediastinal gray zone lymphoma (MGZL) is a type of lymphoma with overlapping features of primary mediastinal B-cell lymphoma (PMBL) and Hodgkin lymphoma (HL), typically treated with chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIPPLE DISCHARGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nipple discharge is a symptom that may indicate breast cancer, prompting diagnostic mammograms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nipple discharge is a symptom that may indicate breast issues requiring medical evaluation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEREDITARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hereditary refers to cancers caused by inherited gene mutations, a small number of thyroid cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTS AND PROCEDURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tests and procedures are medical examinations or interventions used to diagnose or treat conditions like ALL, as referenced in the guide."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 5: RICHTER TRANSFORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 5: Richter transformation is a section of a guide that describes Richter transformation, a condition that may occur in CLL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Experts are medical professionals who predict improvements in bladder cancer treatment and outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Experts are respected professionals in the field of cancer care who contribute to the NCCN Guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Experts are respected professionals in the field who contribute to NCCN Guidelines recommendations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTIMETER (CM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Centimeter is a metric unit of length used to measure tumor size, with approximately 2.5 cm in an inch."&lt;SEP&gt;"Centimeter is a unit of measurement used to describe tumor size. Approximately 2.5 cm make up one inch."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TROUBLE URINATING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trouble urinating is a common side effect of ovarian cancer surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trouble urinating or straining to urinate is a symptom of prostate issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trouble urinating or straining to urinate is a symptom that may indicate prostate issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAMILY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Family is the group of blood relatives whose history is important for risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Family refers to relatives who may be consulted when making decisions about clinical trial participation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Family refers to relatives who provide support and are involved in the patient's care and quality of life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDIVIDUAL TREATMENT PLAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An individual treatment plan is a personalized approach developed by the team based on the patient's specific needs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 2 of the book explains the tests needed to diagnose and monitor glioma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUORODEOXYGLUCOSE (FDG)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG) is a radiotracer made of fluoride and glucose, used in FDG-PET/CT scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG) is a radiotracer used in FDG-PET/CT scans, made of fluoride and glucose, to detect cancer cells that use sugar for growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG) is a radiotracer used in PET scans, composed of fluoride and glucose, to detect cancer cell activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fluorodeoxyglucose is a radiotracer used in FDG-PET/CT scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gums are oral tissues that can be affected by head and neck cancer treatment, requiring dental care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gums are part of the oral cavity that can be affected by head and neck cancer treatment, requiring dental care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soft tissue in the mouth that can be affected by cancer treatment, requiring dental checkups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY MEDIASTINAL B-CELL LYMPHOMA (PMBL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary mediastinal B-cell lymphoma (PMBL) is a type of non-Hodgkin lymphoma that shares features with MGZL but is treated differently."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST SHAPE CHANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breast shape change is a symptom that may indicate breast cancer, prompting diagnostic mammograms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TNM SCORES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TNM scores are a staging system component that describes tumor size (T), lymph node spread (N), and distant metastasis (M)."&lt;SEP&gt;"TNM scores are a staging system used to describe the extent of cancer spread, including tumor, node, and metastasis categories."&lt;SEP&gt;"TNM scores are a system used in cancer staging to describe tumor size, lymph node involvement, and metastasis."&lt;SEP&gt;"TNM scores are a system used to determine numbered stages of cancer, as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"TNM scores are part of the tumor, node, metastasis system used to stage breast cancer, based on tumor size, lymph node involvement, and metastasis."&lt;SEP&gt;"TNM scores are specific values for tumor (T), node (N), and metastasis (M) used in staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inch is a unit of measurement. Approximately 2.5 cm make up one inch, used to describe tumor size."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inch is an imperial unit of length, with approximately 2.5 cm in an inch, used to describe tumor size."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TROUBLE HOLDING IN URINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trouble holding in urine is a symptom of prostate issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trouble holding in urine is a symptom that may indicate prostate problems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSURANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insurance affects where a patient can be treated, and patients are advised to find out where their insurance allows treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance concerns involve coverage and costs related to cancer treatment and follow-up care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance is a financial mechanism that covers standard cancer care costs during clinical trials, with copays and uncovered costs being the patient's responsibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance is a financial mechanism that covers standard cancer care costs during clinical trials, with patients responsible for copays and uncovered costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance is a financial mechanism that may cover cancer tests and treatments, as mentioned in questions to ask."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance is a system that covers standard cancer care costs during a clinical trial, with patients responsible for copays and uncovered costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance is a system that covers the cost of standard cancer care during a clinical trial. Participants are responsible for copays and other costs not covered by insurance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance is a system that often covers standard cancer care costs during a clinical trial, but patients are responsible for copays and uncovered expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance is a system that often covers standard treatment costs in clinical trials, with patients responsible for copays and uncovered costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance may cover genetic testing, but patients should check coverage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insurance refers to health insurance that may cover the costs of tests and treatments for AML, as mentioned in questions to ask."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHILADELPHIA CHROMOSOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Philadelphia (Ph) chromosome is a shortened chromosome 22 resulting from the translocation that creates the BCR::ABL1 gene, a hallmark of CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Philadelphia chromosome is an abnormal chromosome 22 created by a translocation with chromosome 9, serving as the hallmark of CML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 3 of the book discusses treatment options for those already diagnosed with glioma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SODIUM FLUORIDE PET/CT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sodium fluoride PET/CT is a specialized imaging test for bone cancer detection, possibly not needed if FDG-PET/CT is conclusive."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sodium fluoride PET/CT is a type of PET/CT scan that may be used to detect cancer in bone, but may not be needed if FDG-PET/CT clearly shows cancer in bone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sodium fluoride PET/CT is an imaging test that may not be needed if FDG-PET/CT clearly shows cancer in the bone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survey is a tool used by NCCN to gather patient feedback on cancer information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HODGKIN LYMPHOMA (HL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hodgkin lymphoma (HL) is a type of lymphoma characterized by Reed-Sternberg cells, and MGZL has overlapping features with it."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST SIZE CHANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breast size change is a symptom that may indicate breast cancer, prompting diagnostic mammograms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLDERS FOR PROCEDURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Folders for Procedures organize records by medical procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EARLY AND LOCALLY ADVANCED NON-SMALL CELL LUNG CANCER 2024&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Early and Locally Advanced Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer 2024 is a specific edition of NCCN guidelines focusing on early and locally advanced NSCLC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETICS REPORT REVIEW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetics Report Review is examining genetic testing reports."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 0 colon cancer, also called carcinoma in situ, involves abnormal cells on the innermost layer of the colon wall that may become cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 0 is noninvasive breast cancer, such as ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS), confined to the ducts without spread to surrounding tissue or lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 0 is the earliest numbered cancer stage, indicating carcinoma in situ with no invasion into deeper tissues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 0 is the earliest numbered stage of cancer, as part of the staging system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 0 is the earliest numbered stage of cancer, indicating no invasion or spread, as part of the numbered staging system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 0 is the earliest numbered stage of mouth cancer, indicating no invasion into deeper tissues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 0 is the earliest stage of bladder cancer, affecting only the inner lining of the bladder, with subgroups 0a and 0is (carcinoma in situ)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEELING LIKE BLADDER HASN'T FULLY EMPTIED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Feeling like the bladder hasn't fully emptied is a symptom of prostate issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Feeling like the bladder hasn't fully emptied is a symptom that may indicate prostate issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSPORTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transportation is an indirect cost associated with clinical trial participation, due to extra appointments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transportation is an indirect cost associated with clinical trial participation, such as travel to extra appointments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transportation is an indirect cost that participants may incur during a clinical trial due to extra appointments. It is not covered by the study sponsor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NSCLC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NSCLC (Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer) is a type of lung cancer that originates from lung cells, with subtypes including adenocarcinoma, large cell carcinoma, and squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"NSCLC (Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer) is another type of lung cancer, mentioned as a reference point in the context of patient guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"NSCLC (Non-small cell lung cancer) is the most common type of lung cancer, characterized by uncontrolled growth of lung cells that can spread to form tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROLOGICAL EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A neurological exam is a series of tests to assess alertness, balance, coordination, reflexes, hearing, and other senses, used as part of the diagnostic process for primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"A neurological exam is a test used to assess brain and nervous system function, important for diagnosing primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neurological exam involves simple tests to check alertness, thinking, balance, coordination, reflexes, strength, hearing, and senses of touch and smell, as well as an eye exam to check nerve health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A substance that may be inserted into the rectum before an MRI to improve imaging of rectal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gel is a substance applied to the skin during an ultrasound to facilitate the transmission of sound waves from the transducer to the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gel is a substance applied to the skin during ultrasound to facilitate the transmission of sound waves."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gel is applied to the skin during ultrasound to facilitate sound wave transmission."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY BONE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary bone cancer is cancer that starts in the bone, as opposed to metastatic cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary bone cancer refers to cancers that originate in the bone, including sarcomas like osteosarcoma, Ewing sarcoma, and chondrosarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-MEDIASTINAL GRAY ZONE LYMPHOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-mediastinal gray zone lymphomas occur in older persons, have higher rates of bone marrow involvement and extranodal disease, and are more advanced-stage than MGZL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRIPTORELIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Triptorelin is an LHRH agonist used in androgen deprivation therapy for prostate cancer, administered as an injection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;3D MAMMOGRAM (TOMOSYNTHESIS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A three-dimensional mammogram that provides more detailed images of the breast."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage I anal cancer is a non-metastatic stage where the cancer is localized and has not spread beyond the pelvis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage I is a numbered stage of cancer, indicating early-stage disease with less advanced tumor growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage I is an early cancer stage, typically indicating a small tumor without lymph node involvement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage I is an early numbered stage of cancer, indicating limited tumor growth without significant spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage I is an early stage of cancer, as part of the numbered staging system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVASIVE ANAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Invasive anal cancer is a form of anal cancer that has invaded deeper tissues, as opposed to SISCCA, and is the focus of the guide."&lt;SEP&gt;"Invasive anal cancer is a form of anal cancer that has penetrated deeper tissues, as opposed to SISCCA. It is the focus of the guide."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DULL PAIN IN GROIN OR PELVIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dull pain in the groin or pelvis is a symptom of prostate issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dull pain in the groin or pelvis is a symptom that may indicate prostate problems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHILD CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Child care is an indirect cost associated with clinical trial participation, due to extra appointments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tests include blood tests, bone marrow tests, and other diagnostic procedures used to diagnose and treat CML and NSCLC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GADOLINIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gadolinium is a contrast agent used in MRI scans for primary CNS lymphoma, injected into the bloodstream to highlight areas in organs and tissues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORAL SURGEON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An oral surgeon is a healthcare professional who performs panoramic dental x-rays and may use them to plan surgical treatments for oral conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oral surgeon is a healthcare professional who commonly performs panoramic dental x-rays and may use them for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oral surgeon is a specialist who may perform panoramic x-rays and surgical procedures for oral conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECONDARY BONE MALIGNANCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Secondary bone malignancy, or metastatic cancer to bone, originates from other body parts like breast, lungs, or kidney and behaves differently from primary bone cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDIASTINAL LYMPHOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mediastinal lymphomas are growths found behind the breastbone in the chest area that separates the lungs and holds the heart."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NILUTAMIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nilutamide is an anti-androgen medication used in hormone therapy for prostate cancer, taken as a pill."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOSS OF WEIGHT WITHOUT TRYING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Loss of weight without trying is a symptom of adrenal cancer, often related to metabolic changes from the tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARCINOGENS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carcinogens are cancer-causing chemicals, such as radon and asbestos, that increase the risk of developing SCLC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESIDENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A doctor in training who continues education, potentially specializing in a field of medicine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE II&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage II anal cancer is a non-metastatic stage where the cancer is larger but still confined to the pelvis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage II is a cancer stage indicating a larger tumor or limited spread to nearby lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage II is a numbered stage of cancer indicating more extensive tumor growth or lymph node involvement than stage I."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage II is a numbered stage of cancer, indicating more advanced disease than stage I."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage II is a stage of cancer, as part of the numbered staging system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL CANCER CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anal cancer cells are abnormal cells originating in the anal canal that can spread to lymph nodes and distant organs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal cancer cells are abnormal cells originating in the anal canal. They can spread to lymph nodes and distant organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A non-profit organization that funds and distributes NCCN Guidelines for Patients and supports cancer research and patient care."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Foundation is a non-profit organization that funds and distributes NCCN Guidelines for Patients, supports patients and families affected by cancer, and funds promising doctors in cancer research."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STUDY SPONSOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The study sponsor is an entity that pays for research-related costs in a clinical trial, including the study drug, but not indirect costs like transportation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The study sponsor is an entity that pays for research-related costs in a clinical trial, including the study drug, with no fee for enrollment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The study sponsor is an entity that pays for research-related costs in a clinical trial, including the study drug."&lt;SEP&gt;"The study sponsor is the entity that funds and manages a clinical trial, covering research-related costs including the study drug."&lt;SEP&gt;"The study sponsor is the entity that pays for research-related costs in a clinical trial, including the study drug. There is no fee to enroll in a clinical trial, but participants may have indirect costs like transportation or childcare."&lt;SEP&gt;"The study sponsor is the entity that pays for research-related costs in a clinical trial, including the study drug."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BCR::ABL1 PROTEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BCR::ABL1 protein is the product of the BCR::ABL1 gene, leading to uncontrolled blood cell growth in CML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAIN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brain cancer is a type of cancer that occurs in the brain, and other types of brain cancer can have symptoms similar to primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WOUND HEALING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wound healing is the body's repair process, which can be impaired by smoking or vaping during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wound healing is the process of recovery after surgery or injury. Smoking and vaping can prevent proper wound healing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SARCOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sarcomas are a rare group of cancers, with two main types: soft tissue sarcomas and bone sarcomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOPOTECAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Topotecan is a chemotherapy drug that may be used in combination with other agents for treating metastatic cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUTAMIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flutamide is an anti-androgen medication used in hormone therapy for prostate cancer, taken as a pill."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIRUS-INFECTED CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Virus-infected cells are cells that have been infected by a virus and can be killed by natural killer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-CELL LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-cell lymphoma is a type of cancer that starts in B cells, and CBCL is a cutaneous form."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE III&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage III anal cancer is a non-metastatic stage where the cancer has spread to nearby lymph nodes but not beyond the pelvis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage III is a cancer stage indicating more extensive local or regional spread of the tumor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage III is a numbered stage of cancer indicating further spread to nearby tissues or lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage III is a numbered stage of cancer, indicating further progression of the disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage III is a stage of cancer, as part of the numbered staging system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An examination of lymph nodes to check for enlargement, indicating possible cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph node exam is a procedure where a doctor examines lymph nodes by palpation to check for enlargement, which may indicate cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph node exams are recommended every 3 to 6 months for 5 years during remission to monitor for cancer recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PFIZER INC.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A corporate supporter that provides funding to help make NCCN Guidelines for Patients available, but does not participate in their development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pfizer Inc. is a corporate supporter that provides funding to help make NCCN Guidelines for Patients available, but does not participate in their development or content."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER.GOV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer.gov is a website of the National Cancer Institute providing information on clinical trials and cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"cancer.gov is the website of the National Cancer Institute, providing resources for finding clinical trials and contacting the Cancer Information Service."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORMAL BLOOD CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Normal blood cells do not contain the BCR::ABL1 gene, distinguishing them from CML cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL EXAMINATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A physical examination is a general assessment of a patient's health, conducted before specific diagnostic tests for primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINE-NEEDLE BIOPSY (FNB) GUIDANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fine-needle biopsy (FNB) may be guided by ultrasound or CT scan to accurately sample tissue from lymph nodes or tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOFT TISSUE SARCOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soft tissue sarcomas are more common than bone sarcomas and arise in fat, muscles, nerves, tendons, blood and lymph vessels, and other supportive tissues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MSI-H/DMMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MSI-H/dMMR (microsatellite instability-high or mismatch repair deficient) are biomarkers indicating defects in DNA repair, making cancers more responsive to immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSI-H/dMMR refers to microsatellite instability-high or deficient mismatch repair, indicating DNA repair defects that can be targeted with certain treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BICALUTAMIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bicalutamide is an anti-androgen medication used in hormone therapy for prostate cancer, taken as a pill."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE IV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage IV anal cancer is metastatic, meaning the cancer has spread to distant parts of the body beyond the pelvis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage IV is the most advanced cancer stage, indicating significant spread to lymph nodes or distant organs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage IV is the most advanced numbered stage of cancer, as part of the staging system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage IV is the most advanced numbered stage of cancer, indicating significant spread, including metastatic disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage IV is the most advanced numbered stage of cancer, indicating widespread disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PALPATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Palpation is a physical examination technique where a doctor presses on the skin to feel for enlarged lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HODGKIN LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A highly curable cancer that begins in lymphocytes, characterized by Reed-Sternberg cells, typically starting in lymph nodes in the upper body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hodgkin lymphoma is a highly curable cancer that begins in lymphocytes, characterized by Reed-Sternberg cells, and typically starts in lymph nodes in the upper body, most commonly diagnosed in people aged 15-30 or after age 55."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hodgkin lymphoma is a type of cancer that affects the lymphatic system, with two main types: classic Hodgkin lymphoma (CHL) and nodular lymphocyte-predominant Hodgkin lymphoma (NLPHL). It is characterized by abnormal lymphocytes and is diagnosed through biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hodgkin lymphoma is another type of cancer that can develop as a result of Richter transformation in CLL patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICALTRIALS.GOV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinicaltrials.gov is a database hosted by the U.S. National Library of Medicine for finding clinical trials worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"clinicaltrials.gov is a database hosted by the U.S. National Library of Medicine for finding clinical trials worldwide."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL DOCUMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medical documents include insurance forms, medical records, and test results that patients should organize."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical documents include insurance forms, medical records, and test results that should be organized for cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAVENOUS (IV) LINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An intravenous (IV) line is a method of delivering contrast agent or medication directly into the bloodstream, used during imaging tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph node biopsy is a procedure to diagnose BPDCN subtype of AML, involving removal of lymph node tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph node biopsy is a procedure to remove a sample of lymph node tissue, sometimes performed if BPDCN subtype of AML is suspected."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph node biopsy is a procedure to remove a sample of tissue from a lymph node to check for cancer, often guided by ultrasound or CT."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph node biopsy is a procedure to test for cancer spread to lymph nodes, performed if spread is suspected."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE SARCOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone sarcomas, such as osteosarcomas, start in the cells that form bone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOLOGIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biologic is a type of targeted therapy derived from living organisms, designed to work with chemotherapy, such as bevacizumab."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEGARELIX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Degarelix, also known as Firmagon, is a commonly used LHRH antagonist for prostate cancer, administered as an injection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMOKING CESSATION HELP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Smoking cessation help provides support to quit smoking, which can improve treatment outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGANIZE BY DATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organize by Date is a method to arrange records chronologically."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 8&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 8 is a section of the NCCN guidelines that discusses chemoradiation treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT RECORD REVIEW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment Record Review is checking records of therapies received."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER (6237)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CANCER (6237) is a phone number for the NCI's Cancer Information Service to get help finding clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR SIZE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The measurement of the cancer's dimensions, which is a critical factor in staging and determining appropriate treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor size is a factor considered in deciding whether RAI therapy is helpful, with larger tumors more likely to require treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor size is a factor in risk assessment; tumors over 4 cm are very high risk, and certain sizes on specific locations are high risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor size is a measure of the tumor's dimensions, used in staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor size is measured in centimeters or millimeters, with examples like a golf ball (4 cm) and a pea (1 cm)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT SCAN OF CHEST AND ABDOMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CT scan of the chest and abdomen is a specific imaging test recommended to look for areas of cancer beyond the pelvis, such as the liver or lungs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REED-STERNBERG CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormally large lymphocytes with more than one nucleus that are characteristic of Hodgkin lymphoma when viewed under a microscope."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reed-Sternberg cells are abnormally large lymphocytes with more than one nucleus that are characteristic of Hodgkin lymphoma when viewed under a microscope."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reed-Sternberg cells are large abnormal lymphocytes that are a hallmark of classic Hodgkin lymphoma, used for diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reed-Sternberg cells are large, abnormal lymphocytes that may contain more than one nucleus, characteristic of Hodgkin lymphoma and seen in gray zone lymphomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL CELL LUNG CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Small cell lung cancer is a different type of lung cancer from NSCLC, covered in another book."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical center is a healthcare facility that provides diagnostic and treatment services, including those for primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Medical center is a healthcare facility, ideally specializing in prostate cancer, where patients may seek care or second opinions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUNX1::RUNX1T&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RUNX1::RUNX1T is a gene rearrangement resulting from a translocation, used as a marker in AML diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"RUNX1::RUNX1T is a specific genetic rearrangement associated with leukemia, particularly acute myeloid leukemia (AML), and is a focus of genetic testing and predisposition syndromes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPACT BONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Compact bone, or cortical bone, is the hard, dense outer layer of bone covered by the periosteum."&lt;SEP&gt;"Compact bone, or cortical bone, is the hard, dense outer layer of bone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOSPICE CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hospice care is a component of supportive care focused on comfort and quality of life for patients with terminal illness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELUGOLIX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Relugolix, also known as Orgovyx, is an LHRH antagonist for prostate cancer that comes as a tablet taken once daily."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TELEHEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Telehealth is a method of receiving medical consultations remotely via phone or video, allowing patients to include others in visits."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR THICKNESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor thickness is different from DOI, as DOI measures depth of invasion into tissue layers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT SCAN OF PELVIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CT scan of the pelvis is an imaging test used to determine the extent of anal cancer in the pelvis and nearby lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN CLINICAL PRACTICE GUIDELINES IN ONCOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Evidence-based, frequently updated recommendations for cancer care developed by NCCN and used by healthcare providers worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology are evidence-based recommendations for cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology are frequently updated, evidence-based recommendations for cancer care developed by NCCN and used by health care providers worldwide."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL MENOPAUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Menopause caused by removal of both ovaries during surgery, leading to sudden drop in estrogen and various symptoms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical menopause is menopause caused by surgical removal of ovaries, with symptoms similar to radiation-induced menopause."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical menopause is premature menopause caused by removal of the ovaries during hysterectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNG CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lung carcinoma is a type of cancer that forms from cells lining the airways, with NSCLC being the most common form."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUTURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sutures are medical materials used to close openings in the scalp after biopsy procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sutures are stitches used to close the opening in the scalp after a stereotactic biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEUKEMIA PREDISPOSITION SYNDROMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leukemia predisposition syndromes are hereditary cancer syndromes passed from parent to child that increase risk of leukemia, affecting treatment and requiring testing of non-leukemic cells like skin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leukemia predisposition syndromes are hereditary conditions that can increase risk of leukemia, affecting treatment decisions and requiring additional testing like skin punch biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leukemia predisposition syndromes are hereditary conditions that increase an individual's risk of developing leukemia, often detected through genetic testing of non-leukemic cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPONGY BONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spongy bone, or cancellous bone, is the spongy, porous inner layer of bone containing red marrow."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spongy bone, or cancellous bone, is the spongy, porous inner layer of bone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN SPECIALISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pain specialists are healthcare professionals who manage pain as part of supportive care for cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANDROGEN SYNTHESIS INHIBITORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Androgen synthesis inhibitors are medications that block the production of androgens, used in hormone therapy for prostate cancer, taken as pills."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEREDITARY CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hereditary conditions are genetic mutations inherited from biological parents that can increase the risk of developing adrenal tumors. They account for a small portion of adrenal tumor cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTRACEPTIVE SPONGE USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contraceptive Sponge Use is the insertion of a sponge for birth control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NICOTINE ADDICTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nicotine addiction is a dependency on nicotine found in tobacco, making it difficult to quit smoking, especially under stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-ENERGY X-RAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-energy x-rays are a form of radiation used in EBRT to destroy cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-energy x-rays are used in radiation therapy to kill cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH VESSELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph vessels are channels that carry lymph fluid from breast tissue to lymph nodes, involved in cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are channels that carry lymph fluid from breast tissue to lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are part of lymph tissue and transport lymph fluid, which contains lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are part of lymph tissue that transport lymph fluid and lymphocytes throughout the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are part of lymph tissue, which contains lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are part of soft tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are part of the lymphatic system in the breast skin; when blocked by cancer cells, they cause the symptoms of inflammatory breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are part of the lymphatic system that carry lymph fluid from tissues to lymph nodes. They are involved in the spread of breast cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are part of the lymphatic system that drain lymph fluid from breast tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are part of the lymphatic system that transport lymph fluid and can serve as pathways for cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are part of the lymphatic system. Tumor cells in lymph vessels within a tumor are a sign of LVSI, increasing the risk of cancer spread to lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are part of the network in the head and neck, along with lymph nodes, muscles, nerves, and blood vessels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are part of the submucosa layer, involved in transporting lymph and potentially cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph vessels are structures that can contain cancer cells, indicating lymphovascular invasion and higher spread risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vessels that carry lymph fluid from breast tissue to lymph nodes, part of the breast's anatomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRI OF PELVIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MRI of the pelvis is an imaging test used to determine the extent of anal cancer in the pelvis, providing detailed images of soft tissues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HODGKIN LYMPHOMA IN ADULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hodgkin Lymphoma in Adults is a specific resource focusing on the diagnosis, testing, staging, and treatment of Hodgkin lymphoma in adult patients, as covered in the NCCN Guidelines for Patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROENDOCRINE TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neuroendocrine tumors are other lung carcinomas, distinct from NSCLC, with information available at NCCN.org."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neuroendocrine tumors are tumors that can be assessed for aggressiveness using FDG-PET scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPUTERIZED NAVIGATION SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A computerized navigation system is a technology connected to MRI or CT imaging that allows surgeons to precisely target and remove tissue samples during a biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN PUNCH BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical procedure where a small piece of skin and connective tissue are removed using a hand-held tool, often requiring stitches to close the opening."&lt;SEP&gt;"A skin punch biopsy is a medical procedure that removes a small piece of skin and connective tissue to obtain DNA unaffected by leukemia, used to test for inherited predisposition syndromes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A skin punch biopsy is a procedure that removes a small piece of skin and connective tissue using a hand-held tool, often requiring stitches to close the wound."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin punch biopsy is a procedure to remove a small piece of skin and connective tissue to obtain DNA not altered by AML, used to detect inherited leukemia predisposition syndromes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin punch biopsy is a procedure to remove a small skin sample to test for genetic changes present at birth, distinguishing inherited predispositions from acquired leukemia mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RED MARROW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Red marrow contains blood stem cells that can become red blood cells, white blood cells, or platelets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMOTIONAL AND SPIRITUAL SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emotional and spiritual support are components of supportive care addressing psychological and spiritual needs of cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL METASTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local metastasis refers to cancer that has spread to nearby body parts, such as axillary lymph nodes, and may be called local/regional disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local metastasis refers to cancer that has spread to nearby body parts, such as axillary lymph nodes, and may be called locoregional disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE OR CHROMOSOME CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gene or chromosome changes are specific genetic alterations in leukemia cells that are used to classify subtypes of ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NURSE ASSISTANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nurse Assistant is a healthcare worker who may be present during exams to support the provider."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOACTIVE MATERIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A substance injected into the area of a breast tumor to help locate sentinel lymph nodes during a biopsy procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radioactive material is used in brachytherapy, placed inside the body to treat tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD VESSELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood vessels are a type of connective tissue that can be involved in sarcomas and can be invaded by kidney cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are channels in the breast that carry blood, through which cancer can spread to other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are part of bone tissue and other body structures, involved in circulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are part of the breast anatomy, supplying blood to breast tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are part of the circulatory system that carry blood throughout the body. They are involved in the spread of cancer cells through the bloodstream."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are part of the circulatory system within the liver, through which cancer can spread to other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are part of the circulatory system. Tumor cells in blood vessels within a tumor are a sign of LVSI, increasing the risk of cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are part of the network in the head and neck, along with lymph nodes and other structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are part of the submucosa layer, involved in transporting blood and potentially cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are pathways through which esophageal cancer can spread to distant sites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are present in the submucosa of the esophagus, supplying nutrients and oxygen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are structures in the kidney where renal sarcoma can originate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are structures near the bile duct that cancer can grow into or spread to, affecting staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels are structures that can contain cancer cells, indicating lymphovascular invasion and higher spread risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood vessels in and around the thyroid can be invaded by follicular and oncocytic cancers, with invasion confirmed through pathologic examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vessels in the breast that carry blood, which can be pathways for cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLASSIC HODGKIN LYMPHOMA (CHL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A subtype of Hodgkin lymphoma with specific treatment recommendations, as discussed in the NCCN Guidelines for Patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Classic Hodgkin lymphoma (CHL) is a subtype of Hodgkin lymphoma that is discussed in the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, with specific treatment recommendations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Classic Hodgkin lymphoma is the most common type of Hodgkin lymphoma, recognized by large lymphocytes called Reed-Sternberg cells, with several subtypes but similar care recommendations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRONCHI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bronchi are body parts examined in bronchoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronchi are body parts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronchi are breathing passages in the lungs examined during bronchoscopy and panendoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronchi are large breathing tubes that connect the windpipe (trachea) to the lungs. Each lung has one bronchus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronchi are the two main airways branching from the trachea into the lungs, further dividing into bronchioli."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronchi are the two main airways in the lungs that split from the trachea, where lung carcinomas can form."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronchi are the two main airways that split from the trachea and further divide into bronchioli within the lungs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRAME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A frame is a device fitted around the head to aid in precise targeting during a stereotactic biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Frame or tiny markers are fitted around the head to aid surgery during a stereotactic biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AML MUTATION TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AML mutation testing is a diagnostic process that uses methods like karyotype, FISH, NGS, and PCR to identify genetic changes unique to AML cells, guiding treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YELLOW MARROW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yellow marrow is made mostly of fat and often replaces red marrow as we age."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREASTBONE (STERNUM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breastbone (sternum) is the bone behind which mediastinal lymphomas are located in the chest."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUTEINIZING HORMONE-RELEASING HORMONE (LHRH)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Luteinizing hormone-releasing hormone is a hormone that stimulates the testicles to produce testosterone. LHRH agonists and antagonists target this pathway in prostate cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TISSUE LINING AROUND THE LUNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tissue lining around the lung is the pleura, which can be affected by cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMARKERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biomarkers are biological indicators used to determine eligibility for targeted therapy or immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarkers are biological signs found in the body that indicate a condition or disease; in cancer care, they include changes in genes, proteins, and other markers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarkers are proteins or other molecules in tumor samples that can indicate cancer characteristics and guide treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarkers are specific features of cancers that targeted therapy and immunotherapy are most effective against."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSCLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muscles are a common site for metastatic thyroid cancer spread, requiring monitoring and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Muscles are a type of connective tissue that can be involved in sarcomas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Muscles are part of soft tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Muscles are part of the network in the head and neck, binding lymph nodes together."&lt;SEP&gt;"Muscles are tissues that produce creatinine as a waste product, measured in blood."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIV STATUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HIV status refers to whether a person is infected with HIV. Knowing HIV status is important for managing anal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NLPHL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NLPHL (Nodular Lymphocyte-Predominant Hodgkin Lymphoma) is a subtype of Hodgkin lymphoma that has its own treatment section in the NCCN Guidelines for Patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nodular Lymphocyte-Predominant Hodgkin Lymphoma, a subtype of Hodgkin lymphoma with its own treatment section in the guidelines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRONCHIOLI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bronchioli are smaller airways in the lungs that branch from the bronchi and lead to alveoli."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronchioli are smaller airways in the lungs that divide from the bronchi, where lung cancer cells can originate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronchioli are smaller airways in the lungs that lead to alveoli, where oxygen exchange occurs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARKERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Markers are proteins on cells identified by flow cytometry, particularly in immunophenotyping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Markers are tiny devices placed around the head to aid in precise targeting during a stereotactic biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FISH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FISH (Fluorescence in situ hybridization) is a laboratory technique using fluorescent probes to detect chromosomal abnormalities that are too small for other methods, applicable to blood or bone marrow samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"FISH (Fluorescence in situ hybridization) is a testing method using fluorescent probes to detect specific DNA sequences in cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS®: SOFT TISSUE SARCOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN Guidelines for Patients®: Soft Tissue Sarcoma is a specific guideline document for soft tissue sarcoma, referenced for more information."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines for Patients®: Soft Tissue Sarcoma is a specific guideline document for soft tissue sarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPRACLAVICULAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Supraclavicular refers to the area above the collar bone, where lymph nodes may be involved in MGZL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUPRON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lupron is the brand name for leuprolide, a commonly used LHRH agonist in prostate cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIRROR AND FIBEROPTIC EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mirror and fiberoptic exam is a procedure to visualize hard-to-see areas of the mouth and throat."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOWNLOAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Download is the action of saving records from portals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABNORMAL BLOOD RESULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal blood results refer to test outcomes that indicate potential cancer recurrence or other issues, prompting further investigation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 9&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 9 is a section of the NCCN guidelines that provides suggested questions to ask the care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROCEDURE RECORD REVIEW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Procedure Record Review is checking records of medical procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONCURRENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Concurrent refers to treatments given during the same time period, as in chemoradiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NERVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nerve tissue in the breast that provides sensation and is part of the breast's anatomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nerves are a type of connective tissue that can be involved in sarcomas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nerves are found in the submucosa of the esophagus, transmitting signals for muscle control and sensation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nerves are part of bone tissue and soft tissue, involved in signaling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nerves are part of the body that require electrolytes to function properly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nerves are part of the network in the head and neck, binding lymph nodes together."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nerves are part of the submucosa layer, providing sensation and function to the colon."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIV CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HIV care refers to medical treatment and management for people with HIV, which can improve cancer treatment outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNITED STATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The United States is a country where NCCN Cancer Centers and the NCI are located, and where clinical trials are conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States is a country where NCCN Cancer Centers and the NCI operate, and where clinical trial resources are available."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States is a country where NCCN Cancer Centers and the NCI provide clinical trial resources, and where the FDA approves treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States is a country where NCCN Cancer Centers and the National Cancer Institute are located, and where clinical trials are conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States is a country where Pap smear screening has led to lower rates of cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States is a country where about 3 million cases of basal cell skin cancer are diagnosed every year, indicating a significant prevalence of the disease in this geographic region."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States is a country where the 9-valent HPV vaccine is available for adults up to age 45."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States is the country where NCCN Cancer Centers and the National Cancer Institute operate, providing clinical trial resources and cancer care standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States is the geographic context where racial differences in prostate cancer incidence and outcomes are discussed, particularly among Black and white males."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United States is the geographic location where top cancer centers are part of the NCCN alliance, and where the NCCN Guidelines for Patients are developed and distributed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The geographic location where top cancer centers are part of the NCCN alliance and where the guidelines are developed."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States is a country where BCG has been in short supply, impacting the treatment of non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"United States is a country where prostate cancer statistics show Black males are more likely to develop the disease than white males."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRACHEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The trachea is the windpipe located near the thyroid; a tumor in a high-risk location such as the back of the thyroid butting against the trachea may preclude active surveillance."&lt;SEP&gt;"The trachea, or windpipe, is the airway that connects the throat to the bronchi, allowing air to travel into the lungs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The trachea, or windpipe, leads to the lungs and is part of the throat anatomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trachea (windpipe) is a part of the airway examined during bronchoscopy and panendoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trachea is a body part examined in bronchoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trachea is a body part."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trachea is the windpipe that splits into bronchi, part of the airway system in the lungs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trachea is the windpipe that splits into bronchi, part of the airway system where lung cancer can develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trachea, or windpipe, is a part of the respiratory system that splits into bronchi, leading to the lungs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"New growth refers to the appearance of new tumors, which follow-up MRIs are used to detect in patients with primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KARYOTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A karyotype is a picture of chromosomes used to detect extra, missing, rearranged, or abnormal pieces of chromosomes in human cells, requiring a sample of bone marrow or blood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Karyotype is a picture of chromosomes showing extra, missing, rearranged, or abnormal pieces, requiring growing cells from bone marrow or blood, used in AML mutation testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Karyotype is a test that can show defects in chromosomes, and a complex karyotype is 3 or more unrelated changes or deletions in more than one cell."&lt;SEP&gt;"Karyotype is a test that produces a picture of chromosomes to identify extra, missing, or rearranged chromosomes, requiring growing cells from bone marrow or blood."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS®: MULTIPLE MYELOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN Guidelines for Patients®: Multiple Myeloma is a specific guideline document for multiple myeloma, referenced for more information."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN Guidelines for Patients®: Multiple Myeloma is a specific guideline document for multiple myeloma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DLBCL-NOS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DLBCL-NOS (diffuse large B-cell lymphoma, not otherwise specified) is a diagnosis for cancers found outside the mediastinum in gray zone lymphoma cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"DLBCL-NOS (diffuse large B-cell lymphoma, not otherwise specified) is a type of lymphoma diagnosed when cancer is found outside the mediastinum, with distinct characteristics from MGZL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIRMAGON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Firmagon is the brand name for degarelix, a commonly used LHRH antagonist in prostate cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLADDER CANCER TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bladder cancer treatment refers to the various medical interventions and procedures used to manage and treat bladder cancer, which may include surgery, chemotherapy, radiation, or immunotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYSTEMIC THERAPY FOR CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Systemic therapy for cervical cancer includes chemotherapy, targeted therapy, and immunotherapy, used based on cancer stage and biomarkers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A potential complication of biopsy, involving harmful microorganisms entering the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection can show up as a bright spot on PET scans, potentially mimicking cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection can show up as bright spots on PET scans and may impact care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a bodily condition that can appear as a bright spot on PET scans, potentially mimicking cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a complication that can occur after a prostate biopsy, involving the invasion of harmful microorganisms into the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a condition caused by pathogens that can cause inflammation and appear as bright spots on PET scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a condition caused by pathogens; patients with CLL may have increased susceptibility to infections."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a condition that can appear as bright spots on PET scans, potentially mimicking cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a condition that can cause bright spots on PET scans, complicating cancer detection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a condition that can cause bright spots on PET scans, complicating cancer diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a condition that can show up as bright spots on PET scans, potentially mimicking cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a condition that can show up as bright spots on PET scans, requiring differentiation from cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a possible side effect of intraocular chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a potential complication of invasive procedures like biopsies, involving the invasion of harmful microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a potential complication of low white blood cell counts caused by chemotherapy, requiring prompt medical attention."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a potential side effect of various cancer treatments, including surgery, chemotherapy, and immunotherapy, requiring monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is a stressor that triggers germinal center formation in lymph nodes, and can lead to lymphoma if B cells grow unregulated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infection is something that lymph nodes help fight, as part of the immune system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV INFECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV infection is the presence of the human papillomavirus, which is a cause of anal and cervical cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MYCHART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An example of an online patient portal that helps patients track appointments and communicate with their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"MyChart is a health record account system that helps patients track appointments and communicate with their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"MyChart is a patient portal system that allows patients to access their health records, track appointments, and communicate with their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"MyChart is an example of an online patient portal that can help patients track appointments and communicate with their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"MyChart is an online health record system that allows patients to track appointments and communicate with their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"MyChart is an online patient portal system that allows patients to access test results and communicate with their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"MyChart is an online patient portal used to access test results and communicate with care teams."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal growths in the head and neck that can affect hearing and other functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumors are abnormal growths that can form in other parts of the body when cancer cells spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumors are masses of cancer cells that form from uncontrolled growth, as seen in NSCLC and other cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACTINIC KERATOSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Actinic keratoses are pre-cancerous lesions that can be treated with photodynamic therapy, cryotherapy, or topical therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Actinic keratoses are pre-cancerous lesions that can be treated with superficial treatments, often in the same area as Bowen’s disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Actinic keratoses are precancerous skin growths caused by sun damage, characterized by thick, rough, scaly patches on the skin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEXT-GENERATION SEQUENCING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Next-generation sequencing (NGS) is a high-throughput method to determine DNA sequences or gene changes in tumor tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing (NGS) is a method that determines DNA sequences in detail, identifying gene mutations that affect function, often more sensitive than other techniques."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing is a genetic test that analyzes multiple genes to identify mutations that may guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC THYROID CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic thyroid cancer is a condition where thyroid cancer has spread, requiring consideration of various treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLASSICAL HODGKIN LYMPHOMA (CHL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Classical Hodgkin lymphoma (CHL) is a type of Hodgkin lymphoma with features that MGZL overlaps with."&lt;SEP&gt;"Classical Hodgkin lymphoma is a type of lymphoma that shares features with MGZL, influencing treatment approaches."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGOVYX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Orgovyx is the brand name for relugolix, an LHRH antagonist that is taken as a daily tablet for prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIDNEY TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kidney tumors are growths in the kidney that can be associated with some hereditary conditions that also increase the risk of adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARANEOPLASTIC SYNDROMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paraneoplastic syndromes are abnormal body responses to lung cancer, causing additional symptoms in some SCLC patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABSOLUTE NEUTROPHIL COUNT (ANC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Absolute neutrophil count (ANC) measures neutrophils, a type of white blood cell that fights bacteria and protects against infections."&lt;SEP&gt;"An absolute neutrophil count measures cells that fight bacteria and protect us from infections."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HARMFUL THINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Harmful things are removed by lymph nodes from the body, as part of their filtering function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cells are cells from the cervix that are scraped during screening to test for HPV and cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPPORT SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A support system includes friends, family members, or peers who provide transportation, meals, and emotional support during diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support system includes friends, family, or peers who help during diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support system includes friends, family, or peers who provide transportation, meals, and emotional support during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A support system refers to friends, family members, or peers who can provide transportation, meals, and emotional support during diagnosis and treatment of a disease like ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Friends, family members, or peers who provide transportation, meals, and emotional support during diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support system includes friends, family, or peers who provide transportation, meals, and emotional support during diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support system refers to friends, family, or peers who provide transportation, meals, and emotional support during diagnosis and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICAL SOCIAL WORKERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical social workers are part of the care team, diagnosing and treating mental, behavioral, and emotional issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clinical social workers are specialized social workers who diagnose and treat mental, behavioral, and emotional issues, often working in cancer centers to support patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clinical social workers diagnose and treat mental, behavioral, and emotional issues, often helping with cancer-related anxiety."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;5-FLUOROURACIL (5-FU)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"5-Fluorouracil (5-FU) is a chemotherapy drug used in combination with leucovorin for colon cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"5-Fluorouracil is a topical chemotherapy agent applied directly to the skin to treat actinic keratoses by destroying abnormal cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAIN CT SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A CT scan of the brain uses x-rays and computer technology to take detailed pictures, primarily used to look for bleeding, and is a quick test."&lt;SEP&gt;"A brain CT scan is a quick imaging test using x-rays to detect bleeding in the brain, potentially relevant in leukemia cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RAI (Radioactive Iodine) is a treatment option for thyroid cancer, but may not be suitable if cancer doesn't take up iodine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REAL-TIME OR REVERSE TRANSCRIPTASE (RT) PCR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of PCR used to look for gene rearrangements such as PML::RARA, aiding in diagnosis and monitoring response to targeted therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MILK DUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Milk ducts are small tubes in the breast that carry milk from the lobules to the nipple. They are part of the breast's glandular structure and can be the site of breast cancer origin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Milk ducts are small tubes that carry breast milk from lobules to the nipple, where ductal carcinoma originates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARCINOEMBRYONIC ANTIGEN (CEA) BLOOD TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) blood test is a surveillance test used for stages 2 and 3 colon cancer to monitor for recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CREATININE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A waste product measured in kidney function tests to evaluate kidney function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Creatinine is a blood test measuring kidney function, often checked alongside BUN."&lt;SEP&gt;"Creatinine is a waste produced in the muscles, filtered out of the blood by the kidneys; its level indicates kidney function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Creatinine is a waste product filtered by the kidneys; high levels indicate poor kidney function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH ISSUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Health issues are other medical conditions that can cause bone damage, which may be detected through imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health issues are serious problems caused by AML due to lack of healthy blood cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABNORMAL CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal cells are cells that have changed and may be precancerous or cancerous. They can be found on the anal surface or cervix."&lt;SEP&gt;"Abnormal cells are cells that have undergone genetic mutations, leading to uncontrolled growth and cancer development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Abnormal cells are cells that have undergone mutations and grow uncontrollably, forming tumors in the bladder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Diagnosis is the point at which a patient learns they have cancer, triggering treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer diagnosis is the event that triggers the need for support systems, care team coordination, and understanding of test results, as discussed in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer diagnosis refers to the identification of cancer, with age and type important for family history."&lt;SEP&gt;"The event that triggers the need for support systems, care team coordination, and understanding of test results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFLAMMATORY BREAST CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of breast cancer characterized by inflamed skin on the breast, which requires a skin biopsy for diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammatory breast cancer (IBC) is a treatable form of breast cancer that requires a combination of local and systemic therapies, including surgery, radiation, and systemic treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammatory breast cancer is a rare and aggressive form of breast cancer that can be difficult to diagnose, often requiring referral to a breast specialist."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammatory breast cancer is a rare, aggressive type of breast cancer that causes redness and swelling, often without a distinct lump."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CALCIPOTRIENE (SORILUX, DOVONEX)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Calcipotriene is a vitamin D analog cream used in combination with 5-FU to treat actinic keratoses by activating the skin's immune system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAIN MRI SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A brain MRI scan uses magnetic fields to detect swelling of the brain's outer layer (leukemic meningitis), without radiation exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"An MRI scan uses radio waves and magnets to take pictures of the brain, can show leukemic meningitis, and does not use radiation; it may be closed or open design."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TSH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TSH (Thyroid Stimulating Hormone) is a hormone that is kept down using levothyroxine in thyroid cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTROCARDIOGRAM (ECG OR EKG)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An electrocardiogram shows electrical changes in the heart, revealing heart rate and rhythm, and can detect prolonged QTc intervals that may lead to dangerous rhythms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MILK GLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Milk glands, also known as lobules, are structures in the breast that produce milk. They are involved in breast cancer development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD UREA NITROGEN (BUN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A waste product measured in kidney function tests to assess how well the kidneys are working."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood urea nitrogen (BUN) is a waste product filtered by the kidneys; high levels can signal kidney issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood urea nitrogen is a waste product filtered out of the blood by the kidneys; a high level can indicate kidney problems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FATAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatal refers to AML being life-threatening if left untreated, as stated in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LESIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal tissue growths on the colon that can be cancerous, alongside polyps."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lesions are abnormal areas of tissue, such as precancerous lesions on the anal canal or perianal region."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lesions are abnormal growths on the rectal wall that can be cancerous."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EGFR INHIBITORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EGFR inhibitors are targeted therapies that block the epidermal growth factor receptor, preventing cancer cells from dividing, used to treat squamous cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASTECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure to remove the breast, often performed in breast cancer treatment, during which a sentinel lymph node biopsy may be done."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mastectomy is a surgical procedure to remove all or part of the breast, often a modified radical mastectomy for inflammatory breast cancer, which also removes underarm lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mastectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the breast, a treatment for breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mastectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the breast, often performed to treat breast cancer, and may be accompanied by sentinel lymph node biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mastectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the breast, often used in breast cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mastectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the entire breast, often used for larger tumors or when cancer is widespread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMIQUIMOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Imiquimod is a prescription cream used to treat early CSCC and actinic keratoses, belonging to topical therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imiquimod is an immune response modifier cream that treats abnormal skin growths by activating the immune system to damage abnormal cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOLOGICAL PARENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biological parent is an individual who passes down hereditary traits, including cancer predisposition syndromes, to a child."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERIOSTEUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Periosteum is a membrane of strong connective tissue covering compact bone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT RESPONSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment response refers to how well a patient responds to therapy, monitored using PCR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breast tissue is the tissue that makes up the breast, including milk ducts, fat, nerves, lymph and blood vessels, ligaments, and connective tissue. It is the site where breast cancer develops."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABNORMAL ULTRASOUND RESULTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal ultrasound results refer to imaging findings that suggest potential cancer recurrence, requiring additional testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRINT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Print is the action of creating physical copies of records."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNG TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lung tissue is the functional tissue of the lungs where cancer can grow and spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSURANCE FORM ORGANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insurance Form Organization is filing insurance documents in the binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTROLYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Electrolytes are ions or particles with electrical charges that help nerves, muscles, heart, and brain work properly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Electrolytes are ions with electrical charges that help nerves, muscles, heart, and brain function; they are measured in a CMP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minerals in the blood that help regulate bodily functions, assessed in a CMP."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUBTYPES OF AML&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Subtypes of AML are grouped based on gene mutations, abnormal chromosomes, and other factors, affecting treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tissue is a collection of cells that is sampled during biopsies for diagnostic testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissue is a group of cells that perform a specific function. Lung tissue can be invaded by cancer cells growing from the airways."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissue is a group of cells that perform a specific function. Samples of tissue may be removed for biopsy to diagnose cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissue is a group of cells, such as bone tissue or soft tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissue refers to groups of cells; biopsy removes tissue samples for cancer testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CETUXIMAB (ERBITUX)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cetuximab (Erbitux) is an EGFR inhibitor used to treat squamous cell skin cancer and other cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INHIBITORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inhibitors are drugs that block specific pathways in cancer cells, part of targeted therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inhibitors are drugs that block specific pathways in cancer cells, part of treatment options like HER2-targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inhibitors, including CDK4/6, mTOR, and PARP inhibitors, are systemic therapies that block specific pathways to slow cancer growth, with examples like abemaciclib and olaparib."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIRBANIBULIN (KLISYRI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tirbanibulin is a topical microtubule inhibitor used to treat actinic keratoses by killing fast-growing abnormal cells, applied once daily for 5 consecutive days."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOPOIETIC CELL DONORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hematopoietic cell donors are biological family members who may be tested for leukemia predisposition syndromes before donating cells for transplantation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hematopoietic cell donors are biological family members who might be tested for leukemia predisposition syndrome before donating cells for transplant."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOTOCHORDAL CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Notochordal cells are cells that form the spine and vertebrae, from which chordomas start."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IV CONTRAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IV contrast is a type of contrast material given through a vein, leaving the body in urine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECONDARY TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Secondary tumors are tumors that form when cancer cells spread from the primary tumor to other parts of the body through metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLADDER CANCER BASICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bladder cancer basics is an introductory section that provides foundational information about bladder cancer, its causes, and its impact on patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CD20&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CD20 is a protein found on the surface of B cells, used as a marker in diagnosing and classifying certain types of cancer, including CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"CD20 is a protein on B-cells that rituximab targets in immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"CD20 is a surface protein found on CLL cells, used as an example to identify the correct type of cancer. It is also a target for certain treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEEDLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Needle is a medical instrument used to draw blood samples for bladder cancer testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Needle is a thin instrument used in fine-needle aspiration to remove tissue samples from lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Needle is the instrument used to draw blood for tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PD-1 INHIBITORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PD-1 inhibitors are immune checkpoint inhibitors that block programmed death ligand 1, enhancing immune response against cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIVER FUNCTION TESTS (LFTS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liver Function Tests (LFTs) assess liver health by measuring chemicals produced or processed by the liver."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liver function tests (LFTs) measure chemicals made or processed by the liver to assess liver health and detect blockages in bile ducts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liver function tests are blood tests that measure enzymes and proteins to assess liver health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liver function tests look at the health of the liver by measuring chemicals made or processed by the liver."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST RECONSTRUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breast reconstruction is a surgical option after mastectomy to rebuild the breast, often done in stages after cancer treatment, requiring consultation with a plastic surgeon."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPERKERATOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hyperkeratosis is the thickening of the outer skin layer, often present in actinic keratoses, requiring softening before treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PML::RARA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PML::RARA is a gene rearrangement detected by RT-PCR, used in diagnosis and monitoring of targeted therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"PML::RARA is a specific gene rearrangement associated with acute promyelocytic leukemia, detected by PCR for diagnosis and monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"PML::RARA is an abnormal fusion gene found in APL, a rare subtype of AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"PML::RARA is an abnormal fusion gene found in APL, a subtype of AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone tumor is an abnormal growth of cells within a bone, which may be malignant or benign."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QT INTERVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"QT interval is a measure of heart muscle recharge time; prolonged QTc can cause dangerous rhythms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEREDITARY BREAST-OVARIAN CANCER SYNDROME (HBOC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HBOC is a hereditary health condition that increases the risk of pancreatic cancer, linked to genetic mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FECAL INCONTINENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fecal incontinence is the inability to control bowel movements, a common side effect of anal cancer radiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"fecal incontinence is a condition characterized by the inability to control bowel movements, often a side effect of anal cancer treatment, managed through dietary changes and fiber supplements."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEDIATRIC ALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pediatric ALL refers to Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia found in infants, children, and young adults. It includes anyone 18 years of age or under, and certain adolescents and young adults (AYAs) aged 15 to 39 at diagnosis. This book applies to AYAs treated at pediatric or children's cancer centers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERISTALSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peristalsis is the coordinated contraction of muscles in the esophagus that pushes food down to the stomach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL HOSPITAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local hospital is a healthcare facility where patients can seek support groups and medical care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B CELL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B Cell is a type of white blood cell that produces antibodies; its surface contains proteins like CD20, which are relevant in diagnosing CLL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skin is a site where leukemia can spread, detected by imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin is a surface where HPV can infect cells, potentially leading to warts or cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin is a tissue where leukemia can spread, and it is also the site for punch biopsies to obtain unaffected DNA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin is the largest organ of the body, protecting against invaders, regulating temperature, and providing sensation. It has three layers: epidermis, dermis, and hypodermis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin is the organ where primary cutaneous lymphomas, including CBCL, appear."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin is the outer body layer where ultrasound can detect small superficial cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin is the outer covering of the body. In excisional biopsy, the skin is cut to remove lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The outer tissue layer of the body, which is the site of CSCC and various surgical procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEMIPLIMAB (LIBTAYO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cemiplimab (Libtayo) is a PD-1 inhibitor used to treat squamous cell skin cancer and other cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cemiplimab (Libtayo) is an immunotherapy option for metastatic cervical cancer without specific biomarkers, used in second-line or beyond treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITAMIN B12&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vitamin B12 helps the body make new proteins and is needed for normal red blood cell and white blood cell formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamin B12 is a nutrient essential for protein synthesis and normal red and white blood cell formation, with levels monitored in patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC SURGEON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A plastic surgeon is a medical professional who performs breast reconstruction surgery, often consulted for post-mastectomy reconstruction options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRYOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cryotherapy is a treatment option for actinic keratoses, involving freezing abnormal cells to destroy them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cryotherapy is a treatment that freezes abnormal cervical cells to destroy them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cryotherapy is a treatment that freezes and destroys cancer cells using a very cold liquid or tool, used for actinic keratoses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cryotherapy, also called cryosurgery, is a superficial treatment that freezes and destroys precancerous and cancerous cells using liquid nitrogen, causing a blister and scab that heals over 2-3 weeks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URETEROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ureteroscopy is a similar exam to cystoscopy but goes further to examine the ureters and inner kidneys, used when abnormalities are suspected in those areas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOFT TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soft tissue includes fat, muscles, nerves, tendons, blood and lymph vessels, and other supportive tissues of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAND-FOOT SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hand-foot syndrome is a side effect of capecitabine, characterized by redness, swelling, and pain on palms and soles, sometimes with blisters, requiring dose adjustment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEUTZ-JEGHERS SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peutz-Jeghers Syndrome is a hereditary condition that increases the risk of pancreatic cancer, characterized by specific genetic markers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1 COLON CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1 colon cancer is an early stage of colon cancer where surveillance includes a colonoscopy 1 year after surgery, with follow-ups based on results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIRTH DEFECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Birth defects are potential risks of chemotherapy treatment, leading to advice to avoid pregnancy during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOPATHOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hematopathologist is a specialist who analyzes cells and tissues removed during a biopsy, providing cancer diagnosis, staging, and biomarker information for AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hematopathologist is a specialist who diagnoses cancers of blood and immune cells by examining blood, bone marrow, and lymph node samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"An expert hematopathologist is a specialist who reviews tissue samples to confirm the diagnosis of mediastinal gray zone lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hematopathologist is a medical specialist who examines blood, bone marrow, and lymph node samples under a microscope to diagnose blood diseases like CLL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;X-RAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"X-rays are a form of electromagnetic radiation used in CT scans and panoramic dental x-rays to create images of internal structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"X-rays are a form of high-energy radiation used in radiation therapy to kill cancer cells and shrink tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"X-rays are a form of radiation used in CT scans to create pictures of the inside of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"X-rays are a form of radiation used in imaging tests like panoramic dental x-rays and CT scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"X-rays are high-energy waves used in radiation therapy to kill cancer cells and shrink tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"X-rays are imaging tests that can detect lung abnormalities, sometimes before symptoms of SCLC appear."&lt;SEP&gt;"X-rays are radiation used in CT scans and panoramic dental x-rays to create images."&lt;SEP&gt;"X-rays are used in CT scans to create detailed images of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEMBROLIZUMAB (KEYTRUDA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pembrolizumab (Keytruda) is a PD-1 inhibitor used to treat squamous cell skin cancer and other cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pembrolizumab (Keytruda) is a checkpoint inhibitor used in immunotherapy for dMMR/MSI-H colon cancers, often before colectomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pembrolizumab (Keytruda) is an immune checkpoint inhibitor, a type of immunotherapy, used in first-line and second-line treatments for metastatic cervical cancer, particularly for cancers with specific biomarkers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pembrolizumab is an immune checkpoint inhibitor used to treat metastatic anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pembrolizumab, also known as Keytruda, is an immunotherapy drug used to treat MSI-H/dMMR tumors and sometimes TMB-H tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iron is a mineral important for producing hemoglobin, which carries oxygen in the blood; levels are monitored for deficiency or overload."&lt;SEP&gt;"Iron is important in maintaining body functions such as producing hemoglobin, the molecule in blood that carries oxygen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A cancer center is a hospital or facility that specializes in cancer treatment, potentially offering expertise in specific subtypes of AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"A cancer center is a specialized medical facility with expertise in cancer prevention and treatment, recommended by NCCN for individuals with genetic syndromes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical facility that provides diagnostic imaging services, including PET/CT scans, for cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer center is a facility where PET-CT scans may be performed, potentially using one or two machines depending on the center's equipment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer center is a facility where PET/CT scans may be performed, potentially using one or two machines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer center is a medical facility specializing in cancer diagnosis, treatment, and supportive care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer center is a medical facility where PET-CT scans may be performed using one or two machines, depending on available equipment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer center is a medical facility where biopsies and treatments are recommended to be performed by experienced professionals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer center is a specialized facility that offers comprehensive cancer diagnosis, treatment, and support services."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer centers are specialized facilities that offer comprehensive cancer treatment, including surgery, radiation, and systemic therapies, with experienced teams."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TAZAROTENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tazarotene is a topical retinoid related to vitamin A, used to treat hyperkeratotic actinic keratoses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLUE LIGHT CYSTOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blue light cystoscopy is a newer technique using blue light and a special dye to identify tumors more distinctly than standard white light cystoscopy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINERALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Minerals are components of bone tissue, contributing to strength."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL VENOUS CATHETER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Central venous catheter is a thin, flexible tube inserted into a large vein in the chest or arm, used for delivering chemotherapy drugs like 5-FU over extended periods."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LI-FRAUMENI SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Li-Fraumeni Syndrome is a hereditary condition that increases the risk of pancreatic cancer, linked to genetic mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Li-Fraumeni syndrome is a hereditary condition linked to an increased risk of adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NO EVIDENCE OF DISEASE (NED)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"No evidence of disease (NED) is a status indicating that follow-up test results are normal and there are no signs of cancer recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONCOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A doctor specializing in cancer treatment who receives imaging results and coordinates care."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical professional specializing in cancer treatment who performs physical exams and guides surveillance after cervical cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"An oncologist is a cancer doctor who leads the care team and coordinates treatment for patients with cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"An oncologist is a doctor specializing in cancer treatment, including cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"An oncologist is a doctor who receives imaging results and plans cancer treatment based on them."&lt;SEP&gt;"An oncologist is a doctor who receives imaging results from the radiologist and is part of the care team managing cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"An oncologist is a doctor who specializes in cancer treatment, including breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"An oncologist is a doctor who specializes in treating cancer, including ALL and rectal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"An oncologist is a doctor who works with hematopathologists to examine blood samples and plan treatment for CLL patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"An oncologist is a medical professional specializing in cancer diagnosis and treatment, who performs physical exams and orders follow-up tests during surveillance."&lt;SEP&gt;"An oncologist is a medical professional who provides surveillance and treatment for cancer patients, including regular exams and monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"An oncologist is a physician specializing in cancer diagnosis and treatment, who may be involved in managing squamous cell carcinoma and providing genetic counseling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oncologist is a medical professional who receives CT scan results from a radiologist and is part of the cancer care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oncologist is a physician specializing in cancer treatment; they review lab results and plan treatment for patients with CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oncologist is a specialist in cancer treatment, often consulted for anal cancer care, including chemotherapy and radiation therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oncologists are cancer doctors who develop survivorship care plans and coordinate treatment with primary care physicians."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAGNETIC FIELD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Magnetic field is used in MRI to create detailed images of soft tissues in the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;U.S. FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION (FDA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The FDA approves drugs, devices, or treatments that are found safe and effective in clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The FDA is a U.S. regulatory agency that approves drugs, devices, and treatment approaches after they are found safe and effective in clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The FDA is a U.S. regulatory agency that approves drugs, devices, and treatment approaches after they are proven safe and effective in clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The FDA is the U.S. regulatory agency that approves drugs, devices, and treatment approaches after clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) is the regulatory agency that approves investigational treatments after clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COAGULATION PANEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coagulation panel is a set of tests known together as a coagulation or DIC panel, used to screen for clotting problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Coagulation panel is a set of tests known together to screen for clotting problems, also called disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC) panel."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XELODA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Xeloda (capecitabine) is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by interfering with cell division."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOPICAL KERATOLYTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Topical keratolytics, including urea, lactic acid, or salicylic acid, are used to soften and break down thick skin layers before treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHITE LIGHT CYSTOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"White light cystoscopy is the standard method using white light to view inside the bladder, which may be less effective at detecting certain tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;206 BONES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The human body has 206 bones, providing structure and support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PICC LINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PICC line is a type of deep IV inserted into the arm, used for delivering chemotherapy drugs over the duration of treatment, as an alternative to a central venous catheter."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAMILIAL MALIGNANT MELANOMA SYNDROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Familial Malignant Melanoma Syndrome, also known as FAMMM, is a hereditary condition that increases the risk of pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEST TYPE ORGANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Test Type Organization is categorizing records by test kind."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD SMEAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood smear is a method where a drop of blood is examined under a microscope to look for abnormal cells, aiding in cancer diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood Smear is a laboratory test where a drop of blood is examined under a microscope to look for abnormal cells, aiding in cancer diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIO WAVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radio waves are a type of electromagnetic radiation used in MRI scans to create detailed images of internal structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radio waves are used in MRI scans to create images of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radio waves are used in MRI scans to produce images without radiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radio waves are used in MRI to generate images of soft tissues in the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radio waves are used in MRI to generate images of the body's internal structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radio waves are used in MRI to record images of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHASE 1 TRIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phase 1 trials study the dose, safety, and side effects of an investigational drug or treatment approach, looking for early signs of effectiveness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phase 1 trials study the dose, safety, and side effects of an investigational drug or treatment approach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COAGULOPATHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coagulopathy is an impaired clotting process common in leukemia, leading to bleeding, bruises, or blood clots."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYCLOPHOSPHAMIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cyclophosphamide is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by damaging DNA in cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOPICAL DICLOFENAC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Topical diclofenac is an alternative therapy for actinic keratoses, applied to the skin to reduce abnormal growths."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NARROW-BAND IMAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Narrow-band imaging is a technology that helps detect tumors more clearly during cystoscopy without requiring a dye, though it is still in testing phase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECONDARY BONE MALIGNANCIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Secondary bone malignancies are cancers that start elsewhere and spread to bone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPHINCTER MUSCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sphincter muscle is a muscular structure in the anal region; its invasion by cancer determines whether local excision is a viable treatment option."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEREDITARY PANCREATITIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hereditary Pancreatitis is a hereditary condition that increases the risk of pancreatic cancer, involving chronic inflammation of the pancreas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLOW-UP TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follow-up testing refers to regular medical examinations and tests conducted after initial treatment to monitor for cancer recurrence or progression."&lt;SEP&gt;"Follow-up testing refers to the diagnostic procedures used to monitor for cancer recurrence after treatment, including blood tests and imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADOLESCENTS AND YOUNG ADULTS (AYAS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adolescents and Young Adults (AYAs) are individuals aged 15 to 39 at the time of initial cancer diagnosis. They can be treated in pediatric or adult centers depending on the type of cancer. This book applies to AYAs treated at pediatric or children's cancer centers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSYLLIUM-BASED PRODUCTS (METAMUCIL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Psyllium-based products, such as Metamucil, are fiber supplements that may help slow and thicken stool, aiding in managing bowel changes after anal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPHINCTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sphincters are circular muscles in the esophagus that normally remain closed except during swallowing, controlling food passage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLOW CYTOMETRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flow Cytometry is a laboratory method that detects patterns of proteins on cell surfaces, used to identify immunophenotypes and diagnose CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flow cytometry is a laboratory method used to detect, identify, and count specific cells by passing dyed cells through a beam of light, useful for distinguishing subtle differences in blood cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flow cytometry is a laboratory method using light-sensitive dye to detect, identify, and count specific cells, including subtle differences in blood cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flow cytometry is a laboratory technique used to identify markers on cells, particularly in the immune system, and can detect subtle differences between different types of blood cancers by analyzing cells from blood or bone marrow aspirate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flow cytometry is a method used to test blood samples for CLL, helping to identify the type of cancer based on surface proteins."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALLERGIC REACTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Allergic reactions are a common side effect of targeted therapy, which may include symptoms like fever, chills, and rashes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Allergic reactions are adverse responses to contrast agents used in imaging tests, which can range from mild hives to serious reactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Allergic reactions are adverse responses to contrast material that patients should report to their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Allergic reactions are adverse responses to substances like contrast material, which must be reported to the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Allergic reactions to contrast material are important to report to the care team, as they may affect test choices."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHASE 2 TRIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phase 2 trials study how well a drug or approach works against a specific type of cancer, providing preliminary efficacy data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phase 2 trials study how well a drug or approach works against a specific type of cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HLA TYPING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HLA typing is a blood test that detects a person's HLA type, important for matching donors in hematopoietic cell transplant."&lt;SEP&gt;"HLA typing is a blood test that detects a person's HLA type, used before allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplant to find a donor match."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERIBULIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eribulin (Halaven) is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by inhibiting microtubule dynamics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMICAL PEELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical peels, such as trichloroacetic acid, are used to treat actinic keratoses by removing damaged skin layers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urogram is a diagnostic imaging test that uses contrast and CT or MRI to visualize the lining of the kidneys, ureters, and bladder, helping to detect abnormalities such as tumors or blockages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urogram is an imaging test using contrast solution with CT or MRI to evaluate the entire urinary tract, including kidneys, ureters, and bladder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SACRUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sacrum is a part of the spine, located at the base, connecting to the coccyx."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sacrum is the lower spinal column where chordomas are usually found."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE IIA PERIANAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage IIA perianal cancer is a specific substage where local excision may be an option if the cancer has not invaded the sphincter muscle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 0 PANCREATIC CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 0 pancreatic cancer is the earliest stage, where cancer is only in the innermost layer of the duct wall."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOCIAL MEDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Social media platforms can be used to find support groups and connect with others."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNOPHENOTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immunophenotype is the identifiable pattern of proteins on the surface of cells, used to distinguish normal from abnormal cells in CLL diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immunophenotype refers to the pattern of surface proteins on CLL cells, such as CD20, CD200, and LEF1, used to identify the cancer type."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immunophenotype refers to the type of lymphocyte (most often B cell or T cell) within the leukemia cells and how mature the cells are, used for classification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immunophenotype refers to the type of lymphocyte and maturity of cells in leukemia, used to classify ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hives are a skin reaction that can occur as a side effect of contrast agents used in CT scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHASE 3 TRIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phase 3 trials test a drug or approach against a standard treatment to compare effectiveness, often leading to FDA approval if results are positive."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phase 3 trials test a drug or approach against a standard treatment, potentially leading to FDA approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phase 3 trials test a drug or approach against a standard treatment; if results are good, it may be approved by the FDA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN LEUKOCYTE ANTIGEN (HLA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HLA is a protein on cell surfaces that plays a role in immune response, unique to each person, marking cells as self."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human leukocyte antigen is a protein found on the surface of most cells, playing a role in the body's immune response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VINORELBINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vinorelbine (Navelbine) is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by inhibiting cell division."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LASER RESURFACING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Laser resurfacing is a technique used to treat actinic keratoses by removing sun-damaged skin layers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RENAL ULTRASOUND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Renal ultrasound is a painless imaging test using sound waves to produce real-time black and white images of the kidneys, ureters, and bladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Renal ultrasound is a painless, non-surgical imaging test that uses sound waves to produce real-time black and white images of the kidneys, ureters, and bladder, often used to assess organ structure and function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCAPULA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scapula, or shoulder blade, is a flat bone where Ewing sarcoma can occur."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NONMETASTATIC CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nonmetastatic cancer refers to cancer that has not spread beyond its original site, such as stages I-III anal and perianal cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1 PANCREATIC CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1 pancreatic cancer consists of a tumor that is 4 centimeters or smaller and has not spread outside the pancreas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGES 2 AND 3 COLON CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stages 2 and 3 colon cancer are more advanced stages of colon cancer requiring surveillance including physical exams, CEA blood tests, CT scans, and colonoscopy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SLOWED THINKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Slowed thinking is a long-term side effect of whole-brain radiation therapy, affecting cognition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CLL (Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia) is a type of cancer characterized by the accumulation of abnormal B lymphocytes in the blood, bone marrow, and lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLL (Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia) is a type of cancer that affects white blood cells, specifically B cells, and is the central topic of the text, with various tests and biomarkers discussed for diagnosis and prognosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUSHED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flushed refers to a feeling of warmth or redness in the skin, which can be a side effect of contrast injection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHASE 4 TRIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phase 4 trials study the long-term safety and benefit of an FDA-approved treatment, monitoring real-world outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phase 4 trials study the long-term safety and benefit of an FDA-approved treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOPOIETIC CELL TRANSPLANT (HCT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HCT is a transplant procedure requiring HLA typing to ensure donor match, with allogeneic (donor) transplants being a treatment option."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hematopoietic cell transplant is a procedure where donor cells are transplanted, requiring a good HLA match."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALPELISIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alpelisib (Piqray) is a PI3K inhibitor used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by targeting specific mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alpelisib (Piqray) is a PIK3CA inhibitor used for breast cancer with PIK3CA mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DERMABRASION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dermabrasion is a mechanical resurfacing technique that sands down the outer skin layers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dermabrasion is a resurfacing technique that removes the outer skin layers to treat actinic keratoses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLEXIBLE CYSTOSCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flexible cystoscope is a type of cystoscope used for viewing and biopsy, being less invasive than a rigid cystoscope."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROWTH PLATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Growth plates are areas near which osteosarcoma starts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL LINING SORES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anal lining sores are a side effect of chemotherapy for anal cancer, causing discomfort and requiring care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2 PANCREATIC CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 2 pancreatic cancer consists of a tumor larger than 4 centimeters or has spread to 1 to 3 nearby lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TSH-STIMULATED TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TSH-stimulated testing is a diagnostic procedure performed while thyroid hormone is stopped to stimulate TSH levels, used to detect cancer recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONOCLONAL B LYMPHOCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Monoclonal B Lymphocytes are identical white blood cells that proliferate abnormally in CLL; a count of 5,000 or more per microliter is required for diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUZZING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Buzzing is a sound that may be heard during a CT scan, caused by the machine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESEARCH TEAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A research team is a group of experts managing clinical trials, responsible for reviewing the study with participants and ensuring safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"A research team is a group of experts managing clinical trials, reviewing study details, risks, and benefits with participants."&lt;SEP&gt;"A research team is a group of experts that manages clinical trials, reviews the study with participants, and provides informed consent forms detailing risks and benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"A research team is a group of experts that manages clinical trials. They review the study with participants, including its purpose, risks, and benefits, and provide informed consent forms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A research team is a group of experts who manage clinical trials, review study details with participants, and provide informed consent forms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A research team is a group of professionals who collect research data and coordinate care for patients in clinical trials, ensuring proper management and support."&lt;SEP&gt;"A research team manages clinical trials, reviewing the study purpose, risks, and benefits with participants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Research team collects research data and coordinates care for patients in clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Research team is part of the care team, collecting data and coordinating care for clinical trial participants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERFORMANCE STATUS (PS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS is a person's general level of fitness and ability to perform daily tasks, rated using scales like ECOG or KPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Performance status is a person's general level of fitness and ability to perform daily tasks, rated using scales like ECOG or KPS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TALAZOPARIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Talazoparib (Talzenna) is a PARP inhibitor used for HER2-negative breast cancer with BRCA mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Talazoparib (Talzenna) is a PARP inhibitor used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by exploiting DNA repair defects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DERMATOLOGIC SURGEON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A dermatologic surgeon is a specialist trained in skin surgery, including Mohs surgery and PDEMA procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RIGID CYSTOSCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rigid cystoscope is a more invasive type of cystoscope that can remove small tumors during cystoscopy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOINTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Joints are formed by cartilage covering bone ends."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEARABLE PUMP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A wearable pump is a device used to continuously infuse 5-FU over several days, connected to a central venous catheter."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3 PANCREATIC CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3 pancreatic cancer has grown through the pancreas to nearby major arteries or has spread to 4 or more lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL BINDER CREATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medical Binder Creation is the process of organizing medical records into a binder for easy access."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT ORGANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment Organization is categorizing records by therapy type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EASTERN COOPERATIVE ONCOLOGY GROUP (ECOG) SCORE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ECOG score is a performance status scale used to rate a person's general health and fitness for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group score is a performance status scale used to rate a person's general health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLICKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clicking is a sound that may be heard during a CT scan, caused by the machine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFORMED CONSENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Informed consent is a process in clinical trials where participants are fully informed about the trial's purpose, risks, and benefits, and sign a form agreeing to participate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Informed consent is a process in clinical trials where research teams review study details, risks, and benefits with participants, who sign a form before enrolling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Informed consent is a process in clinical trials where the research team reviews the study's purpose, risks, and benefits with participants. It is provided in an informed consent form, which participants must read carefully and sign. Participants can leave the trial at any time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Informed consent is a process where a research team explains the purpose, risks, and benefits of a clinical trial to a participant, who then signs a form confirming understanding and voluntary participation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Informed consent is a process where participants receive detailed information about a clinical trial, including risks and benefits, before signing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Informed consent is a process where participants review and sign a form detailing the trial's purpose, risks, and benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Informed consent is the process of obtaining permission for genetic testing after explaining risks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEMBROLIZUMAB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pembrolizumab (Keytruda) is an immunotherapy drug that blocks PD-1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pembrolizumab (Keytruda) is an immunotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by enhancing immune response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACTINIC KERATOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Actinic keratosis is a precancerous skin condition caused by sun exposure, characterized by rough, scaly patches that may progress to squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Actinic keratosis is a precancerous skin condition characterized by scaly or rough patches of skin caused by prolonged sun exposure. It can vary in appearance and color, and having it increases the risk of developing squamous cell skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"An area of scaly or rough skin with a higher chance of becoming squamous cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;X-RAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"X-ray is a imaging technology used in pyelogram and chest imaging to detect structural abnormalities or cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"X-ray is a type of imaging that uses radiation to create pictures of the inside of the body, used in CT scans and chest x-rays."&lt;SEP&gt;"X-ray is a type of imaging that uses radiation to take pictures of the inside of the body, used in CT scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"X-ray is a type of radiation used in small doses to make pictures of the inside of the body, also referred to as a radiograph."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adipose tissue in the breast that provides structure and is part of the breast's composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat is a component of yellow marrow and soft tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat is a type of connective tissue that can be involved in sarcomas and can be invaded by kidney cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;X-RAY GUIDANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"X-ray guidance is used during the insertion of a central venous catheter to ensure proper placement in a large vein."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 4 PANCREATIC CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 4 pancreatic cancer is metastatic cancer, having spread far from the pancreas, commonly involving the liver, lungs, or lining of the abdomen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS: ACUTE LYMPHOBLASTIC LEUKEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia is a specific publication providing care recommendations for ALL, available at NCCN.org and on the NCCN Patient Guides for Cancer app."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC FLOOR PHYSICAL THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic floor physical therapy involves exercises and techniques to strengthen pelvic floor muscles, supporting bowel and bladder control and sexual function before and after anal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KARNOFSKY PERFORMANCE STATUS (KPS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KPS is a performance status scale used to rate a person's ability to perform daily tasks, influencing treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Karnofsky Performance Status (KPS) is a scoring system used to quantify the general well-being and activities of daily living of a patient, often used in oncology to assess functional impairment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Karnofsky Performance Status (KPS) is an organization that provides a performance status scale used to rate a person's general health and ability to perform daily tasks, which is a factor in choosing a treatment plan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Karnofsky Performance Status is a performance status scale used to rate a person's general health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph Node is a small organ of the immune system that can swell due to cancer cell buildup; biopsies of lymph nodes help diagnose CLL and SLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph node is part of the lymphatic system, often biopsied to check for cancer spread, and is a common site for metastasis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph nodes are anatomical sites where cancer may spread, and their status is a key component of cancer staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph nodes are areas where cancer can spread (metastasize) and are often biopsied to confirm the presence of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph nodes are small immune organs that filter lymph fluid; they may be biopsied or removed if cancer spreads."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph nodes are small immune system structures that can be sites of cancer metastasis, often examined in imaging and biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph nodes are small, bean-shaped structures of the lymphatic system that can be sites of cancer spread. They are often examined via imaging and biopsy to detect cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Small glands that filter lymph fluid; sentinel lymph nodes are the first nodes to which cancer cells likely spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENCLOSED SPACES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enclosed spaces refer to the confined area of an MRI machine, which can cause anxiety for some patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLACEBO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A placebo is an inactive substance used in clinical trials as a control to compare the effects of an investigational treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A placebo is an inactive version of a real medicine, almost never used alone in cancer clinical trials. It may be combined with standard treatment or a new drug, and patients are informed if it is part of a trial."&lt;SEP&gt;"A placebo is an inactive version of a real medicine, almost never used alone in cancer clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"A placebo is an inactive version of a real medicine, rarely used alone in cancer clinical trials, and patients are informed if it is part of a trial."&lt;SEP&gt;"A placebo is an inactive version of a real medicine, rarely used alone in cancer clinical trials, often combined with standard treatment or a new drug."&lt;SEP&gt;"A placebo is an inactive version of a real medicine. In cancer clinical trials, placebos are almost never used alone. It is common to receive either a placebo with a standard treatment or a new drug with a standard treatment. Participants are informed if a placebo is part of a trial before enrolling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Placebo is an inactive version of a real medicine, rarely used alone in cancer clinical trials, often combined with standard treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Placebos are inactive versions of real medicines, almost never used alone in cancer clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERTUZUMAB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pertuzumab (Perjeta) is a HER2-targeted therapy used in systemic therapy to treat HER2-positive cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA (CSCC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Squamous cell carcinoma is a type of skin cancer that arises from abnormal squamous cells, often treated with surgery or topical therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell carcinoma is a type of skin cancer that can develop from various risk factors including sun exposure, environmental toxins, scars, chronic wounds, actinic keratoses, genetic syndromes, and weakened immune systems. It is characterized by abnormal growth of squamous cells in the skin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTRAST SOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contrast solution is a substance used in imaging tests like urogram to make organs easier to see."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrast solution is a substance used in imaging tests to enhance visibility of structures like the urinary tract, aiding in detecting blockages or abnormalities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENDONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tendons are part of soft tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RIGHT SIDE OF THE HEART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The right side of the heart is the anatomical location where a central venous catheter is guided to a large vein."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRUG TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Drug treatment is a common approach for most people with pancreatic cancer, used to control cancer growth and reduce symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTACT LIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contact list is a compilation of care team members' information for emergency access."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEUKEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leukemia is a cancer starting in the bone marrow, with AML being a type, and is associated with coagulopathy and clotting issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leukemia is a type of cancer that can spread outside the bloodstream to lymph nodes, liver, spleen, and skin, and rarely to the lining of the brain and spinal cord."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leukemia is a type of cancer that starts in the bone marrow, affecting blood cell production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leukemia is cancer that occurs in blood cells, with CLL being a chronic form affecting lymphocytes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SLL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SLL (Small Lymphocytic Lymphoma) is a type of cancer closely related to CLL, affecting lymph nodes; diagnosis is confirmed through lymph node biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECIAL CAMERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A special camera is used in bone scans to capture images of radioactive tracer distribution in bones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Special Camera is used in bone scans to capture images of tracer in bones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Special camera is used in PET scans to detect radioactive glucose and create images of cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Special camera is used in a bone scan to take pictures of the tracer in the bones as it moves over the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Special camera is used to visualize lymph nodes containing dye or radioactive substance during sentinel node biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPIDERMAL GROWTH FACTOR RECEPTOR (EGFR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EGFR is a protein on the surface of cells that causes them to divide; inhibiting it can prevent cancer cell growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADO-TRASTUZUMAB EMTANSINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ado-trastuzumab emtansine (T-DM1, Kadcyla) is a HER2-targeted conjugate used in systemic therapy to deliver chemotherapy to cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOPICAL THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Topical therapy is a treatment option for actinic keratoses, involving the application of medication directly to the skin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Topical therapy refers to treatments applied directly to the skin, including creams, gels, or solutions, used for actinic keratoses and some skin cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reproductive organs are located in the pelvis and may be affected by cancer spread, examined via imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPPORTIVE TISSUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Supportive tissues are part of soft tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arm is the anatomical location where a PICC line is inserted for chemotherapy administration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMOKING TOBACCO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Smoking tobacco is a lifestyle risk factor that increases the chance of developing pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARYNGEAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Laryngeal cancer is a type of cancer affecting the larynx, which should not be confused with nasopharyngeal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINE MOTOR SKILLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fine motor skills, such as handwriting or tying shoes, may be affected by nervous system damage from radiation therapy for primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fine motor skills, such as handwriting or tying shoes, may be affected by whole-brain radiation therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC ERRORS (MUTATIONS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic errors or mutations are changes in DNA that cause bladder cells to grow abnormally, leading to cancer development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RED BLOOD CELL TRANSFUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Red blood cell transfusion is a medical procedure that may be needed based on hemoglobin levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cell transfusion is a procedure to increase hemoglobin levels if needed, based on CBC results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXCISIONAL BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Excisional Biopsy is a surgical procedure that removes an entire lymph node for testing, providing a comprehensive sample for diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Excisional biopsy is a procedure where all or part of a lymph node is removed by cutting into the skin for testing. It is used when a sample is needed for diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Excisional biopsy is a type of biopsy that removes the entire abnormal area. It is not the preferred type but may be necessary if other methods are not possible or results don't match expectations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUGAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sugar is a substance produced by the body that cancer cells may use to grow, and its uptake is detected in PET scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sugar, or glucose, is used by cancer cells for growth and detected in PET scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sugar, or glucose, is used in PET scans to detect cancer cells, which use it more quickly than normal cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGRAMMED DEATH LIGAND 1 (PD-1)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PD-1 is a protein targeted by PD-1 inhibitors, which are a type of immune checkpoint inhibitor used in immunotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAM-TRASTUZUMAB DERUXTECAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fam-trastuzumab deruxtecan-nxki (Enhertu) is a HER2-targeted conjugate used in systemic therapy to treat HER2-positive cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITAMIN D&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vitamin D is a nutrient that plays a role in immune function; its analog calcipotriene is used in topical treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamin D is a nutrient that, in the form of calcipotriene, activates the skin's immune system to treat actinic keratosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vitamin D is a supplement that helps the body absorb calcium, often recommended alongside calcium to support bone health in thyroid cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINARY TRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The system of organs including the kidneys, ureters, bladder, and urethra, involved in urine production and excretion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urinary tract includes the kidneys, ureters, bladder, and urethra, which are examined for cancer and other issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urinary tract includes the kidneys, ureters, bladder, and urethra, which work together to store and eliminate urine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTEOSARCOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osteosarcomas are bone sarcomas that start in cells forming bone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEEK 5 OF RADIATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Week 5 of radiation therapy is a time point when a second 5-FU infusion may be given, along with a possible mitomycin dose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAVY ALCOHOL USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Heavy Alcohol Use is a behavior that negatively affects treatment outcomes and increases toxicity in mouth cancer patients, with a strong recommendation to seek help."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heavy alcohol use is a lifestyle risk factor that increases the chance of developing pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDULLARY THYROID CANCERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medullary thyroid cancers are a specific type of thyroid cancer that can have RET gene fusions, making them eligible for targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RED BLOOD CELL (RBC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Red blood cells are cells that carry oxygen in the blood, and their normal formation requires B12 and folic acid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells carry oxygen and are formed with the help of B12 and folic acid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INCISIONAL BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Incisional Biopsy is a surgical procedure that removes only part of a lymph node for testing, used when a full removal is not necessary."&lt;SEP&gt;"Incisional biopsy is a type of biopsy that removes a small amount of tissue through a cut in the skin or body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER TREATMENT OUTCOMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer treatment outcomes refer to the effectiveness of cancer therapy, which can be improved by managing HIV."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNE-RELATED ADVERSE EVENTS (IRAES)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immune-related adverse events are side effects specifically associated with immunotherapy, which can affect various organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAPATINIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lapatinib (Tykerb) is a HER2-targeted inhibitor used in systemic therapy to treat HER2-positive cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROTUBULE INHIBITOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microtubule inhibitors are drugs that disrupt cell division, used to kill fast-growing cells like those in actinic keratoses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE I ANAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage I anal cancer is an early stage where the tumor has not invaded nearby lymph nodes, potentially treatable with local excision for perianal cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage I anal cancer is characterized by a tumor 2 cm or smaller, with no spread to lymph nodes or distant areas, described as T1, N0, M0."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GIANT CELL TUMOR OF BONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Giant cell tumor of bone is an overgrowth of cells in the metaphysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIRST DAY OF 5-FU INFUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The first day of 5-FU infusion is when mitomycin or cisplatin is administered intravenously."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LESS HEALTHY DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A less healthy diet is a lifestyle risk factor that increases the chance of developing pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREGNANCY PREVENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pregnancy Prevention is the use of birth control to avoid pregnancy during and after cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROCEDURE ORGANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Procedure Organization is categorizing records by procedure type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BILE DUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bile ducts are tubes that carry bile from the liver to the gallbladder and small intestine, and are part of the hepatobiliary system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bile ducts are tubes that carry bile from the liver; blockage can be indicated by abnormal LFTs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bile ducts are tubes that carry bile, made up of several layers including membranes, muscle, and connective tissue, and can be affected by cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bile ducts can be blocked, affecting liver function test results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEEDLE BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A procedure to take a sample from a lymph node for testing if cancer spread is suspected."&lt;SEP&gt;"Needle Biopsy is a procedure using a needle to take a small sample from a lymph node, performed when other biopsy methods are unsafe."&lt;SEP&gt;"Needle biopsy is a procedure to remove a small sample of tissue from the breast for examination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ALL (Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia) is a type of cancer that affects blood and bone marrow, characterized by the presence of lymphoblasts. It is the focus of the first part of the text, with detailed discussions on testing, treatment, and subtypes."&lt;SEP&gt;"ALL (Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia) is a type of cancer that affects lymphoid progenitor cells, which develop into lymphocytes. It is characterized by the presence of lymphoblasts in the bone marrow, blood, and organs such as the testicles or central nervous system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIREDNESS AND MUSCLE FATIGUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tiredness and muscle fatigue are common side effects of systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARGETUXIMAB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Margetuximab-cmkb (Margenza) is a HER2-targeted antibody used in systemic therapy to treat HER2-positive cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RETINOID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Retinoids are vitamin A derivatives used topically to treat skin conditions, including hyperkeratotic actinic keratoses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE II ANAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage II anal cancer is a nonmetastatic stage where the tumor may be larger but has not spread to lymph nodes, treated with chemoradiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage II anal cancer is divided into IIA (tumor &gt;2 cm but ≤5 cm, T2, N0, M0) and IIB (tumor &gt;5 cm, T3, N0, M0), with no lymph node or distant spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TSH LEVEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TSH (thyroid-stimulating hormone) level is monitored and kept low or normal through levothyroxine therapy to reduce risk of cancer recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"TSH level is a hormone level that is kept down using levothyroxine in thyroid cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GX GRADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GX grade indicates the cancer grade cannot be determined."&lt;SEP&gt;"GX grade is an undetermined cancer grade where the grade cannot be assessed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PESTICIDES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pesticides are examples of cancer-causing chemicals that increase the risk of pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GASTROINTESTINAL (GI) TRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The GI tract includes organs through which food passes, such as the stomach, small bowel, and large bowel. Imaging tests like colonoscopy and upper endoscopy are used to examine it for potential issues related to ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The GI tract is the series of organs from the mouth to the anus through which food passes, including the esophagus, stomach, small intestine, colon, and rectum."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gastrointestinal tract is the series of organs through which food passes, including the esophagus, stomach, small intestine, colon, and rectum. It is part of the digestive system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COAGULATION FACTORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coagulation factors are proteins made by the liver that are needed for blood clotting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Coagulation factors are proteins made by the liver, needed for blood clotting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE MARROW BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A procedure where a hollow needle removes a sample of marrow from a bone (usually the hip) to test for cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone Marrow Biopsy is a procedure that removes a core sample of bone marrow to test for cancer cells, often done with an aspiration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow biopsy is a medical procedure where a wider needle is used to remove a small piece of bone and marrow for examination, often performed with an aspirate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow biopsy is a procedure that removes a core sample of bone marrow tissue from the hip bone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow biopsy is a procedure to remove a sample of bone marrow tissue for testing, used to confirm AML diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow biopsy is a procedure using a wider needle to remove a small piece of bone for testing, often done with aspirate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK (NCCN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN is a nonprofit alliance of cancer centers that provides guidelines for cancer care, including patient guides for various types of cancer such as ALL and rectal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN is an alliance of leading cancer centers in the United States that develops evidence-based cancer care recommendations, including the NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology and the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, which are used by health care providers worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) is the organization that publishes the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, providing expert recommendations for cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAUSEA/VOMITING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nausea and vomiting are common side effects of systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NERATINIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neratinib (Nerlynx) is a HER2-targeted inhibitor used in systemic therapy to treat HER2-positive cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UREA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urea is a keratolytic agent used topically to soften and break down thick skin layers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE III ANAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage III anal cancer is a nonmetastatic stage where the cancer may have spread to nearby lymph nodes but not beyond the pelvis, treated with chemoradiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage III anal cancer is divided into IIIA (tumor ≤5 cm with lymph node involvement), IIIB (tumor invades nearby organs without lymph node involvement), and IIIC (tumor &gt;5 cm or invades organs with lymph node involvement)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IODINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iodine is a chemical element used in RAI therapy and imaging, as thyroid cancer cells that take up iodine can be targeted for treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Iodine is a mineral from diet used by the thyroid to produce hormones, found in certain foods and iodized salt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Iodine is a substance that some patients may be allergic to, and such allergies should be reported to doctors before using contrast material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Iodine is a substance that thyroid cancer may or may not take up, affecting treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G1 GRADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"G1 grade is a low-grade cancer, with cells that look more normal and tend to grow slowly."&lt;SEP&gt;"G1 grade is a well-differentiated (low-grade) cancer, suitable for local excision in perianal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRONIC INFLAMMATION OF THE PANCREAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chronic inflammation of the pancreas is a health condition that increases the risk of developing pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MYCHART ACCOUNT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MyChart account is a digital health record system for tracking appointments and communicating with care providers."&lt;SEP&gt;"MyChart account is an online portal for patients to access health records and communicate with providers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISSEMINATED INTRAVASCULAR COAGULATION (DIC) PANEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DIC panel is a group of tests for clotting problems, often used in leukemia patients to detect coagulopathy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Disseminated intravascular coagulation panel is another name for the coagulation panel, used to screen for clotting problems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE MARROW ASPIRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone Marrow Aspiration is a procedure that removes liquid and cells from bone marrow, usually performed alongside a biopsy to assess disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-ALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-ALL (B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia) is a subtype of ALL that affects B-cell lymphocytes, and is treated differently from mature B-cell ALL (Burkitt leukemia)."&lt;SEP&gt;"B-ALL is a subtype of ALL that arises from B-cell lymphocytes. It includes BCR::ABL1-negative, BCR::ABL1-like, and BCR::ABL1-positive forms, each with specific treatment approaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"B-ALL is a subtype of acute lymphoblastic leukemia that starts in B-cell lymphocytes, more common than T-ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"B-ALL is a type of ALL that starts in B-cell lymphocytes. It includes subtypes like BCR::ABL1-negative, BCR::ABL1-like, and BCR::ABL1-positive B-ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"B-ALL or B-cell ALL is a type of acute lymphoblastic leukemia that starts in B lymphocytes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOSS OF APPETITE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Loss of appetite is a common side effect of chemotherapy, affecting patient nutrition and well-being."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of appetite is a common side effect of chemotherapy, resulting from damage to fast-growing cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of appetite is a common side effect of systemic therapy, including chemotherapy and targeted therapy. It can lead to weight loss and malnutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of appetite is a common side effect of systemic therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of appetite is a possible side effect of chemotherapy and radiation therapy, which can be managed with medications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of appetite is a side effect of immunotherapy, affecting nutrition and overall health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of appetite is a symptom of CLL, leading to reduced food intake."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loss of appetite is a symptom of adrenal cancer, often related to tumor burden or hormonal changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUCATINIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tucatinib (Tukysa) is a HER2-targeted inhibitor used in systemic therapy to treat HER2-positive cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lactic acid is a keratolytic agent used to soften and exfoliate thick skin in hyperkeratotic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE IV ANAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage IV anal cancer is cancer that has metastasized before diagnosis and has never been treated with radiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage IV anal cancer is metastatic, meaning it has spread to areas beyond the pelvis, such as the liver or lungs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOACTIVE IODINE (RAI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radioactive iodine (RAI) is a treatment for thyroid cancer, but may not be suitable if cancer doesn't take up iodine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G2 GRADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"G2 grade is a moderately differentiated (intermediate-grade) cancer, suitable for local excision in perianal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLOSE BLOOD RELATIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Close blood relatives with pancreatic, breast, ovarian, or colorectal cancers or melanoma are a risk factor for pancreatic cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOUTH (ORAL CAVITY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The mouth or oral cavity is a potential site for head and neck cancers, as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mouth, or oral cavity, is the first part of the digestive and respiratory systems, including the lips, cheeks, palate, teeth, and tongue, with functions in eating and speaking."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EYE IRRITATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eye irritation is a possible side effect of intraocular chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-UROTHELIAL TYPES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-urothelial types of bladder cancer are rare forms that do not originate in urothelial cells, including squamous cell carcinoma, adenocarcinoma, and small cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALLOGENEIC (DONOR) HEMATOPOIETIC CELL TRANSPLANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Allogeneic HCT is a transplant using donor cells, requiring HLA typing for compatibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplant is a type of transplant using donor cells, requiring HLA matching."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOLOGIST-ONCOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hematologist-Oncologist is a specialist in blood cancers who reviews lab results and plans treatment for patients with CLL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-ALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-ALL (T-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia) is a subtype of ALL that starts in T-cell lymphocytes, can cause an enlarged thymus, and may lead to breathing problems due to pressure on the windpipe and blood vessels."&lt;SEP&gt;"T-ALL is a subtype of ALL that starts in T-cell lymphocytes. It is less common than B-ALL and is treated with clinical trials or chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"T-ALL is a subtype of acute lymphoblastic leukemia that starts in T-cell lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"T-ALL is a type of ALL that starts in T-cell lymphocytes. It is less common than B-ALL and is treated with clinical trials or chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"T-ALL or T-cell ALL is a type of acute lymphoblastic leukemia that starts in T lymphocytes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAD AND BODY ACHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Head and body aches are common side effects of systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHESGO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phesgo is a combination therapy of trastuzumab and pertuzumab, used as a substitute in HER2-targeted systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SALICYLIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Salicylic acid is a keratolytic agent that helps remove dead skin cells and soften thick layers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICHAEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Michael is an anal cancer survivor who advises getting a mentor and paying it forward by mentoring others after recovery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTHER SYSTEMIC THERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Other systemic therapies are available and may be recommended if listed therapies aren't available or appropriate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G3 GRADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"G3 grade is a poorly differentiated (high-grade) cancer, not suitable for local excision due to aggressive behavior."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELIAC AXIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The celiac axis is a major artery near the pancreas that stage 3 pancreatic cancer may grow into."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTHER ORGANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Other organs are parts of the body beyond the lungs where cancer may metastasize."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAPILLARY THYROID CANCERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Papillary thyroid cancers are a common type of thyroid cancer that can be treated with RAI therapy if they take up iodine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DONOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Donor is a person whose proteins are compared to the patient's for HLA matching in a transplant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Donor is an individual whose HLA proteins are compared to the patient's for transplant compatibility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATHOLOGY REPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A document recording the type and features of biopsied lesions, used by the care team to plan next steps."&lt;SEP&gt;"A pathology report is a document prepared by a pathologist detailing the findings from biopsy samples, including cancer presence and aggressiveness."&lt;SEP&gt;"A pathology report is a document prepared by a pathologist that details the findings from biopsy samples, including the presence of cancer, the percentage of cancer in each core, and the extent of cancer in the prostate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathology Report is a document containing lab results from diagnostic tests, used by oncologists to plan treatment for CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathology report is a document generated by a neuropathologist detailing tumor type, grade, and biomarkers from biopsy analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pathology report is a written document by a pathologist detailing the findings from a biopsy sample, including whether cancer is present."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFANT ALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Infant ALL is a subtype of ALL that occurs in infants under 12 months of age, requiring different treatment approaches compared to other age groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infant ALL is a subtype of ALL that occurs in infants under 12 months of age. Treatment for this group is different from other age groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIARRHEA OR CONSTIPATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diarrhea or constipation are common side effects of systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SENTINEL LYMPH NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sentinel lymph nodes are the first lymph nodes where cancer cells are likely to spread, identified during biopsy to guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRICHLOROACETIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trichloroacetic acid is a chemical used in peels to remove damaged skin layers for treating actinic keratoses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-GRADE ANAL INTRAEPITHELIAL NEOPLASIA (AIN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-grade AIN is a precancerous condition of the anal canal, indicating significant cellular changes that may lead to cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECOMMENDED TARGETED THERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Recommended targeted therapies are listed in a guide for metastatic cancer that can't be treated with surgery or RAI."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G4 GRADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"G4 grade is an undifferentiated (high-grade) cancer, not suitable for local excision due to high aggressiveness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABDOMEN LINING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The lining of the abdomen is a site commonly involved when pancreatic cancer spreads to distant sites in stage 4."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD TEST PROCEDURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood Test Procedure involves drawing blood via a needle for diagnostic analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BINDER MAINTENANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Binder Maintenance is updating the binder with new records and notes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPERATIONS WITHIN THE CHEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Operations within the chest are surgical procedures performed by thoracic surgeons."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY AND REPRODUCTIVE SPECIALISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility and Reproductive Specialists are experts who help patients with fertility concerns and preservation options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility and reproductive specialists help patients sort through fertility preservation options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECTAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rectal cancer forms in the rectum and has different treatment approaches compared to colon cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rectal cancer is a disease characterized by malignant growth in the rectum, requiring staging and treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rectal cancer is a disease characterized by the growth of malignant cells in the rectum, often originating from polyps or lesions. It can be non-metastatic or metastatic, and treatment varies based on stage and extent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rectal cancer is a disease involving tumors in the rectum, with treatment options including surgery, chemoradiation, and chemotherapy based on staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rectal cancer is a type of cancer that forms in the rectum, often starting in adenomas, and is commonly an adenocarcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rectal cancer is a type of cancer that forms in the rectum, the last part of the large intestine. The most common type is adenocarcinoma, which arises from adenomatous polyps."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNG AND BREATHING PROBLEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lung and breathing problems are severe side effects of systemic therapy, including cough, shortness of breath, and chest pain."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEST WALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chest Wall is a nearby structure that can be invaded by a T4 tumor, indicating advanced local spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"The chest wall is the area of the body where radiation therapy may be directed after mastectomy to treat residual cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LASER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Laser is a resurfacing technique using focused light to remove sun-damaged skin layers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-GRADE SQUAMOUS INTRAEPITHELIAL LESIONS (HSIL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HSIL is a precancerous condition of the anal region, characterized by high-grade cellular changes that require monitoring or treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic tumors are tumors that have spread, and their growth rate affects treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARJOLIN’S ULCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of squamous cell skin cancer that forms in old wounds, burns, or scars, which can be harder to treat."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marjolin’s ulcer is a type of squamous cell carcinoma that forms in scars, chronic wounds, ulcers, or burns. It is often difficult to treat and has a higher likelihood of recurrence after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marjolin’s ulcer is a type of squamous cell skin cancer that forms in old wounds, burns, or scars, and is noted to be harder to treat."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PANCREATIC ADENOCARCINOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pancreatic adenocarcinomas are the most common type of pancreatic cancer, forming from exocrine cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCREENING PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A screening program is a structured initiative that conducts regular tests on asymptomatic individuals to detect diseases early. The text recommends enrollment in such a program for those with cirrhosis or chronic hepatitis B."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EASTERN COOPERATIVE ONCOLOGY GROUP (ECOG)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An organization that provides a performance status scale used to rate a patient's general health and ability to perform daily tasks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) is a medical organization that provides a performance status scale (ECOG score) used to rate a patient's general health, particularly in cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) is an organization that provides a performance status scale used to rate a person's general level of fitness and ability to perform daily tasks, which is a factor in choosing a treatment plan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group is an organization that developed a performance status scale."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B SYMPTOMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B Symptoms are specific symptoms of CLL, including fevers, night sweats, and unexplained weight loss, which are assessed during diagnosis and treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"B Symptoms are specific symptoms of CLL, including fevers, night sweats, and weight loss, used in diagnosis and staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"B symptoms are symptoms of FL including fever, night sweats, fatigue, and weight loss."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Growths in the colon that can be hyperplastic or inflammatory, most of which do not become cancer, but almost all colon cancers start in them; they can be removed during colonoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyps are non-cancerous growths on the colon or rectum lining. Adenomas can become invasive cancer over time, while hyperplastic and inflammatory polyps rarely do. Most colon cancers start from polyps."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyps are non-cancerous growths on the inner lining of the colon and rectum. The most common type, adenomas, can become invasive rectal cancer over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyps are overgrowths of cells on the inner lining of the rectal wall. They can be pedunculated (mushroom-shaped with a stalk) or sessile (flat without a stalk). Adenomas are the most common type, and some can become invasive cancer over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGAN DAMAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organ damage, including to the liver and kidneys, is a severe side effect of systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFRACLAVICULAR REGION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The infraclavicular region is below the collarbone, an area that may receive radiation therapy as part of cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL EXCISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgical excision is a procedure to remove a tumor and a margin of normal tissue, used for skin cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTROCAUTERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Electrocautery is a treatment method for anal precancer, performed by an HRA provider to remove abnormal tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONITORING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Monitoring is an option for metastatic tumors that are growing slowly and not causing symptoms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Monitoring is the ongoing process of checking for bladder cancer recurrence and treatment effectiveness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XERODERMA PIGMENTOSUM (XP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Xeroderma pigmentosum is a rare genetic syndrome where the body cannot repair DNA damage caused by sunlight, leading to a high risk of developing skin cancers, including squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTIDISCIPLINARY CARE TEAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A team of healthcare specialists from various fields who collaborate to treat a patient's cancer, ensuring comprehensive care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Multidisciplinary care team is a group of healthcare professionals who work together to treat bladder cancer, ensuring comprehensive and coordinated care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOBACCO USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tobacco use is a major risk factor for head and neck cancer and can affect treatment outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRIATED MUSCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Striated muscle is a type of muscle in the upper esophagus that is under voluntary control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KARNOFSKY PERFORMANCE STATUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Karnofsky Performance Status is a scale used to rate a person's general health and fitness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Body part."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colon is part of the large intestine in the digestive system, involved in water absorption and waste formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colon is part of the large intestine, often involved in surgeries like LAR where part or all of it is removed or reconnected."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colon is the large intestine where polyps and cancer develop, with walls made of multiple layers including mucosa, submucosa, muscularis propria, and serosa."&lt;SEP&gt;"Part of body where colon cancer originates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colon is a part of the digestive system, involved in the absorption of water and formation of waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colon is a pelvic organ that can be affected by ovarian cancer spread, particularly in Stage 2B."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colon is part of the large bowel, examined during colonoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colon is part of the large bowel, where polyps can form on its inner lining, and is a site for polyp development."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colon is part of the large intestine where digested food becomes stool, and it is the site where colon cancer develops."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colon is part of the large intestine where digested food becomes stool. It is the site where colon cancer develops, and together with the rectum, forms the colorectal area."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colon is part of the large intestine, absorbing water from food to form stool. It includes sections like the cecum, ascending, transverse, descending, and sigmoid colon."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colon is the large intestine that may be connected to the outside of the abdomen in a colostomy or connected to the remaining rectum or anus to retain bowel function."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colon is the main part of the large intestine, involved in water absorption and waste storage."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colon, part of the large intestine, is involved in waste processing. It is mentioned as part of the gastrointestinal tract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The part of the body where colon cancer originates and where polyps form."&lt;SEP&gt;"The part of the body where colon cancer originates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH BLOOD PRESSURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A health condition that may run in families, relevant to family health history."&lt;SEP&gt;"High blood pressure is a severe side effect of systemic therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"High blood pressure is a side effect more often seen with targeted therapy. It requires monitoring and may need medication to manage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPRACLAVICULAR AREA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The supraclavicular area is above the collarbone, an area that may receive radiation therapy as part of cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL ANESTHESIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local anesthesia numbs a specific area, used in procedures like C&amp;E and standard excision."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HRA PROVIDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An HRA (High-Resolution Anoscopy) provider is a healthcare professional who performs electrocautery or other treatments for anal precancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPERT RECOMMENDATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Expert recommendations are based on latest research and practices at leading cancer centers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECESSIVE DYSTROPHIC EPIDERMOLYSIS BULLOSA (RDEB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Recessive dystrophic epidermolysis bullosa is a rare inherited skin disorder that makes the skin extremely fragile, causing painful blisters from minor trauma. It increases the risk of developing squamous cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INNER LAYER OF THE BLADDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The inner layer of the bladder is the tissue where abnormal cells grow out of control, leading to bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSCLE FLAP RECONSTRUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muscle Flap Reconstruction is a surgical technique to rebuild tissue after APR, using muscle from another part of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Muscle flap reconstruction is a surgical technique using tissue from another body area, such as the rectus abdominis muscle, to improve healing of the perineum after APR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"APR (Abdominoperineal Resection) is a surgical procedure for removing the anus, rectum, and part of the colon, often used in anal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AML (ACUTE MYELOID LEUKEMIA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AML is a type of leukemia diagnosed through bone marrow tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHOID PROGENITOR CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymphoid progenitor cells are a type of progenitor cell that form into lymphoblasts that mature into lymphocytes. ALL is thought to arise in these cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoid progenitor cells are a type of progenitor cell that form into lymphoblasts, which mature into lymphocytes. ALL affects these cells, leading to an overproduction of immature lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoid progenitor cells are blood stem cell derivatives that can increase in blast phase CML, influencing treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoid progenitor cells are early blood cells that form into lymphoblasts, which mature into lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoid progenitor cells are progenitor cells that form into lymphoblasts, which mature into lymphocytes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoid progenitor cells are stem cell-derived cells that develop into lymphocytes, a type of white blood cell. ALL arises from these cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoid progenitor cells form into lymphoblasts that mature into lymphocytes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABNORMAL BLEEDING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal bleeding is a severe side effect of systemic therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Abnormal bleeding is a side effect more often seen with targeted therapy. It can be serious and requires immediate medical attention."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KANJINTI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kanjinti is a biosimilar of trastuzumab, used as a HER2-targeted therapy in systemic treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCALPEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A scalpel is a surgical blade used to cut tissue during procedures like Mohs surgery and excision."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL REMOVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgical removal is a treatment option for anal precancer, involving the excision of abnormal lesions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEADING CANCER CENTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leading cancer centers are institutions where current research and practices are based, informing the NCCN Guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leading cancer centers are institutions where practices are based on latest research."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL GENETICIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical geneticist is a specialist who diagnoses and manages genetic conditions, including those that increase the risk of skin cancer, and provides expert guidance on genetic syndromes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD IN THE URINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood in the urine is a side effect of intravesical therapy, requiring evaluation by the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood in the urine is the most common symptom of bladder cancer, indicating potential abnormalities in the bladder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR THYROID CANCERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follicular thyroid cancers are a type of thyroid cancer that can be treated with RAI therapy if they take up iodine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLETE BLOOD COUNT (CBC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A CBC is a blood test measuring red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets. Abnormal results may indicate health problems, including cancer or other conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A blood test measuring white blood cells, red blood cells, and platelets, used to detect health problems that may signal colon cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A common blood test that measures the number of red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets in a blood sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"A complete blood count (CBC) is a blood test measuring white blood cells, red blood cells, and platelets to assess general health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complete Blood Count (CBC) is a blood test measuring counts of white blood cells, red blood cells, and platelets, used to detect abnormalities in CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complete Blood Count (CBC) measures red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets to assess oxygen transport, infection fighting, and bleeding control."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complete blood count (CBC) is a blood test measuring red and white blood cells and platelets, used to assess overall health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complete blood count (CBC) is a blood test that measures levels of red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets, providing a picture of overall health and detecting abnormalities like low counts or high blasts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complete blood count is a blood test measuring red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets, used to assess overall health in bladder cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complete blood count is a blood test that measures red and white blood cells and platelets, used to assess overall health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complete blood count measures red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets in a blood sample to assess oxygen transport, infection fighting, and bleeding control."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Complete Blood Count (CBC) is a key blood test that measures levels of red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets, providing an overall picture of health and detecting abnormalities in AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAIR LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hair loss is a common side effect of chemotherapy regimens discussed in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hair loss is a common side effect of chemotherapy, resulting from damage to fast-growing hair follicle cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hair loss is a common side effect of chemotherapy, resulting from the death of fast-growing hair cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hair loss is a common side effect of high-dose chemotherapy, resulting from damage to rapidly dividing hair follicle cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hair loss is a common side effect of systemic therapy, particularly chemotherapy. It can be temporary and hair may regrow after treatment ends."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hair loss is a possible side effect of chemotherapy, which can be managed or addressed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hair loss is a side effect of certain chemotherapy drugs, often temporary."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hair loss is a side effect of cisplatin chemotherapy, leading to partial or complete loss of hair."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hair loss is a side effect of systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERITONEAL WASHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peritoneal washing is a procedure where a special liquid is used to rinse the abdominal cavity to collect samples for cancer cell testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OGIVRI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ogivri is a biosimilar of trastuzumab, used as a HER2-targeted therapy in systemic treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A microscope is used by pathologists to examine biopsy samples and identify cancer cells, confirming a diagnosis of squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"A microscope is used by surgeons and pathologists to examine tissue samples for cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microscope is an instrument used by pathologists to view tissue samples and identify cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microscope is used to study cells after IHC staining."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIQUID NITROGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A substance used in sperm banking to freeze semen for preservation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liquid nitrogen is used to freeze semen or eggs in fertility preservation methods like sperm banking and egg freezing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LATEST RESEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Latest research informs expert recommendations for cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOCRINOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An endocrinologist is a medical doctor specializing in hormone-related conditions, who may be involved in managing genetic syndromes that increase skin cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"An endocrinologist is a medical specialist who may be part of a thyroid cancer treatment team, focusing on hormone-related conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"An endocrinologist is a medical specialist who treats hormone-related disorders, including thyroid conditions and cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-INVASIVE BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-invasive bladder cancer is an early stage where cancer is confined to the inner layer of the bladder and is usually curable."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE SCAN PROCEDURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone Scan Procedure uses a radiotracer and special camera to detect cancer in bones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAMMOGRAM, MRI, AND ULTRASOUND TECHNOLOGISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mammogram, MRI, and ultrasound technologists operate the mammogram unit, MRI, or ultrasound machine for diagnostic imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD UPDATING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Record Updating is adding new test results and reports to the binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENTIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A differential is a blood test that counts the number of each type of white blood cell and checks if the counts are in balance with each other."&lt;SEP&gt;"A differential is a blood test that counts the number of each type of white blood cell and checks if they are in balance, helping detect blasts in the blood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Differential is a blood test component that counts the most common types of white blood cells and checks their balance, aiding in CLL diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Differential is a blood test that counts the number of each type of white blood cell, checking if counts are balanced and detecting high numbers of blasts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Differential is a type of blood test that counts the most common types of white blood cells and checks if the cell counts are in balance, often used in diagnosing CLL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD STEM CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood (hematopoietic) stem cells are early cells in bone marrow that give rise to all types of blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood stem cells (hematopoietic stem cells) are early blood-forming cells in bone marrow that develop into red blood cells, white blood cells, or platelets through a process called differentiation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood stem cells (hematopoietic stem cells) are early blood-forming cells in bone marrow that multiply and differentiate into red blood cells, white blood cells, or platelets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood stem cells (hematopoietic stem cells) are early cells in bone marrow that develop into all types of blood cells. They mature through stages to become red blood cells, white blood cells, or platelets. ALL is thought to arise from stem cells that make an increased amount of lymphoid progenitor cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood stem cells (hematopoietic stem cells) are early cells in bone marrow that multiply and differentiate into red blood cells, white blood cells, or platelets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood stem cells are early blood-forming cells in bone marrow that give rise to all types of blood cells, including red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood stem cells are found in red marrow and can become red blood cells, white blood cells, or platelets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood stem cells are found in red marrow and can differentiate into various blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood stem cells are immature cells found in bone marrow that can develop into red blood cells, white blood cells, or platelets. They can copy themselves or 'self-renew' and are rare. Their role is to make cells that will become red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood stem cells are the origin of CML, as they produce increased myeloid progenitor cells leading to the disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood stem cells are the origin of CML, producing increased amounts of myeloid progenitor cells, leading to the disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blood stem cells are the origin of all blood cells, including red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets. They mature through stages to become specific cell types."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOUTH SORES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mouth sores are a common side effect of chemotherapy, affecting the oral mucosa and requiring symptomatic treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth sores are a common side effect of chemotherapy, caused by damage to fast-growing cells in the mouth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth sores are a common side effect of chemotherapy, causing discomfort and affecting eating."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth sores are a common side effect of systemic therapy, including chemotherapy and targeted therapy. They can cause pain and difficulty eating."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth sores are a possible side effect of chemotherapy, which can be managed with medications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth sores are a side effect of cisplatin chemotherapy, causing discomfort in the oral cavity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth sores are a side effect of systemic therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth sores are painful ulcers in the mouth, a side effect of high-dose chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREMATURE MENOPAUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Premature menopause is caused when ovaries are included in the radiation field, leading to early cessation of menstrual cycles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Premature menopause is the onset of menopause caused by surgical removal of both ovaries, leading to a sudden drop in estrogen and associated symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HERZUMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Herzuma is a biosimilar of trastuzumab, used as a HER2-targeted therapy in systemic treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ULTRASOUND OF THE TESTICLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An imaging test that may be used after diagnosis if the PET/CT scan did not find cancer, specifically for testicular examination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OOCYTE CRYOPRESERVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oocyte cryopreservation is the medical term for egg freezing, a fertility preservation method."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENT OUTCOMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patient outcomes are improved by following expert recommendations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONCOLOGY NURSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nurse providing hands-on care, including administering therapy, managing care, answering questions, and helping with side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"An oncology nurse is a healthcare professional who provides care and support to cancer patients, including those with genetic syndromes and skin cancer, throughout their treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVERALL HEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Overall health refers to a patient's general physical condition, influencing treatment choices for bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARE TEAM CONTACT LIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A care team contact list is a compilation of contact information for all healthcare providers involved in a patient's care. The text advises keeping this list accessible for emergencies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood test measuring chemicals, proteins, and other substances to assess health, particularly kidney and liver function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comprehensive Metabolic Panel is a screening test measuring up to 14 blood chemicals, used to assess organ function, including kidneys and liver, in CLL patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comprehensive metabolic panel (CMP) is a blood test measuring various chemicals, used in AML testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comprehensive metabolic panel (CMP) is a blood test that measures substances in the blood, providing information about kidney and liver function and detecting hypercalcemia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Comprehensive metabolic panel is a screening test for many diseases, including tests for up to 14 chemicals in the blood, and abnormal levels may indicate kidney or liver issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL NERVOUS SYSTEM (CNS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Central nervous system (CNS) includes the brain and spinal cord; it can be affected by leukemia, requiring imaging or lumbar puncture."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central nervous system (CNS) is a site where ALL can be found, and it is tested for involvement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central nervous system (CNS) is made up of the brain and spinal cord, receives signals from senses, processes information, and controls body responses. It includes the brain, eyes, and spinal cord."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central nervous system includes the brain and spinal cord. ALL can be found in the CNS, and tests like lumbar puncture are used to check for involvement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central nervous system includes the brain and spinal cord. AML can spread to the CNS, requiring specific tests like lumbar puncture or imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"The central nervous system includes the brain and spinal cord. Primary CNS lymphoma affects this system, leading to various neurological symptoms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The part of the body (brain and spinal cord) where primary CNS lymphoma develops."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RASHES AND OTHER SKIN PROBLEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rashes and other skin problems are side effects of systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONE REPLACEMENT THERAPY (HRT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormone replacement therapy (HRT) is a treatment option to manage symptoms of surgical menopause by supplementing hormones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONTRUZANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ontruzant is a biosimilar of trastuzumab, used as a HER2-targeted therapy in systemic treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN IMMUNODEFICIENCY VIRUS (HIV) BLOOD TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood test required for everyone with primary CNS lymphoma to detect HIV, which requires specialized care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEMEN CRYOPRESERVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Semen cryopreservation is the medical term for sperm banking, a fertility preservation method."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DECISIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Decisions about cancer care can be stressful and complex."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIV/AIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HIV/AIDS is a condition that weakens the immune system, making individuals more susceptible to infections and increasing the risk of developing squamous cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERSONAL PREFERENCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Personal preferences are individual patient choices regarding treatment, considering lifestyle and values."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEXUAL HEALTH THERAPIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A sexual health therapist is a healthcare professional specializing in helping cancer survivors manage sexual side effects of treatment, offering support and strategies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEIGHT AND WEIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Height and weight are body measurements taken during physical exam to assess nutritional status."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTICLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reproductive organs that can be damaged by cancer treatment, affecting sperm production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testicles are male reproductive organs that can be damaged by cancer treatment, affecting sperm and fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testicles are male reproductive organs that can be damaged by radiation therapy, affecting fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testicles are male reproductive organs where ALL can be found in some cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testicles are organs that may be imaged via ultrasound to check for lymphoma spread, though not always needed if whole-body scans are clear."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testicles are organs that produce sperm and are part of the male reproductive system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testicles are organs where ALL can be found in certain cases, requiring specific diagnostic and treatment considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testicles are part of the male reproductive system and produce sperm, which is a component of semen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testicles are part of the male reproductive system, producing sperm and hormones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Testicles are reproductive organs that can be damaged by cancer treatment, affecting sperm production."&lt;SEP&gt;"The testicles are organs where ALL can be found, and they are checked for involvement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW BLOOD CELL COUNTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low blood cell counts are a common side effect of chemotherapy, potentially leading to infections due to low white blood cell counts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low blood cell counts are a common side effect of systemic therapy, including chemotherapy. This can lead to increased risk of infection, anemia, and bleeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low blood cell counts are a possible side effect of chemotherapy, which can lead to increased risk of infection or bleeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low blood cell counts are a side effect of systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEEP VEIN THROMBOSIS (DVT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Deep vein thrombosis (DVT) is a risk of blood clots after surgery, often prevented with blood thinners."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRAZIMERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trazimera is a biosimilar of trastuzumab, used as a HER2-targeted therapy in systemic treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPATITIS B TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood test necessary before immunotherapy treatment if the patient has had hepatitis B or is at risk, as immunotherapy can reactivate the virus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADOLESCENTS AND YOUNG ADULTS WITH CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adolescents and Young Adults with Cancer is a patient guideline topic from NCCN, addressing fertility and other issues in this population."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRESSURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pressure is a factor in making tough decisions about cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUN EXPOSURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prolonged time in the sun over many years, a leading cause of squamous cell skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sun exposure is a major risk factor for skin damage and the development of actinic keratoses and squamous cell carcinoma, as it causes DNA damage in skin cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer therapy encompasses all treatments for bladder cancer, including surgery, chemotherapy, immunotherapy, radiation, and targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGITAL RECTAL EXAM (DRE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Digital rectal exam is a clinical procedure to check the rectum and anus for abnormalities, recommended after treatment for lymph node recurrence to monitor for further recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC RADIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic Radiation is radiation therapy directed at the pelvic area, used in treating anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pelvic Radiation is radiation therapy directed at the pelvic area, used in treating cancers like anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSCULARIS MUCOSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muscularis mucosa is a very thin layer of muscle under the lamina propria in the esophagus mucosa."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPLEEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spleen is an organ that can be enlarged in FL and where DLBCL tumors may be found."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spleen is an organ that can swell due to cancer cell buildup in CLL; its size is assessed during physical examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spleen is an organ where leukemia can spread, detected by imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen is an organ in the lymphatic system that filters blood and helps fight infection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen is an organ in the lymphatic system that helps fight infection and can be involved in lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen is an organ near the esophagus that can be invaded by esophageal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen is an organ near the liver involved in immune function and blood filtration."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen is an organ near the liver involved in immune function."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen is an organ that can be affected by ovarian cancer spread, particularly in Stage 3C or Stage 4B."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen is an organ where leukemia can spread, and imaging tests may be used to detect such involvement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen is part of the lymph system and can be swollen due to accumulation of CLL or SLL cells. It plays a role in fighting infections."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen is part of the lymph system, involved in immune function and containing B cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spleen is the largest organ of the lymphatic system, producing lymphocytes and playing a role in blood filtration and storage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARGE INTESTINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Large intestine is a part of the digestive system, a portion of which is used to create a pouch in the continent cutaneous pouch procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Large intestine is part of the digestive system that prepares unused food to be moved out of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"The large intestine includes the colon and rectum, where digested food becomes stool and is held before elimination."&lt;SEP&gt;"The large intestine includes the colon and rectum, where water is absorbed and stool is formed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The large intestine is part of the digestive tract that prepares unused food for removal from the body. It is mentioned in the context of the digestive system's function."&lt;SEP&gt;"The large intestine is the final part of the digestive tract, absorbing water and forming waste. It prepares unused food for elimination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFERTILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Infertility is a longer-term side effect of systemic therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infertility is a potential long-term side effect of chemotherapy, referring to the inability to have children. It is a concern for patients who want to have children after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infertility is the inability to produce children, a potential side effect of cancer treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infertility is the inability to produce children, a potential side effect of radiation and chemotherapy for anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERVAL CYTOREDUCTIVE SURGERY (ICS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Interval cytoreductive surgery (ICS) is surgery performed after chemotherapy to remove as much cancer as possible."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KADCYLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kadcyla is the brand name for ado-trastuzumab emtansine, a HER2-targeted conjugate used in systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EYE EXAMINATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A thorough examination of the eyes to look for lymphoma in the eyes, recommended for everyone diagnosed with primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade describes how abnormal tumor cells look under a microscope (histology), with higher grades indicating faster growth and spread, and grades ranging from GX (cannot be determined) to G1 (low), G2 (intermediate), and G3 (high)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grade describes how abnormal tumor cells look under a microscope, with higher grades indicating faster growth and spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grade describes how abnormal tumor cells look under a microscope, with higher grades indicating faster growth and spread; categories include GX, G1, G2, and G3."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grade describes how much cancer cells differ from normal cells, indicating how quickly the cancer is likely to grow."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grade indicates how fast cancer cells are growing and how abnormal they appear, helping predict disease course and treatment response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grade is a classification system for tumors from 1 to 4, indicating growth rate and abnormality, used for prognosis and treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLEX CHOICES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Complex choices are part of cancer care decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN CANCER SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skin cancer screening involves regular examination of the skin by a doctor or dermatologist to detect precancerous lesions or early-stage skin cancer, especially for high-risk individuals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW TREATMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"New treatments for bladder cancer are emerging from clinical trials, improving outcomes and reducing side effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLETE SKIN EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A complete skin exam is a thorough examination of the skin to check for any abnormalities, lesions, or signs of skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONCOCYTIC THYROID CANCERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oncocytic thyroid cancers are a type of thyroid cancer that can be treated with RAI therapy if they take up iodine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPERTHERMIC INTRAPERITONEAL CHEMOTHERAPY (HIPEC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hyperthermic intraperitoneal chemotherapy (HIPEC) is a technique where warmed chemotherapy is circulated in the abdomen during surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLON CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer that starts in the colon, often originating from polyps, and is the focus of the text's discussion on diagnosis, treatment, and screening."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of cancer that starts in the colon, often originating from polyps."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colon cancer is a common and treatable cancer that starts in the colon, often from polyps. Early detection improves cure rates. Treatment differs from rectal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colon cancer is a disease characterized by the abnormal growth of cells in the colon, which can spread to other parts of the body. It is staged using the AJCC TNM system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colon cancer is a disease characterized by the growth of malignant cells in the colon, often originating from polyps, and is the main focus of the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colon cancer is a type of cancer affecting the colon, with stages 1, 2, and 3 mentioned in the text. Surveillance and follow-up testing are recommended based on the stage and risk of recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colon cancer is a type of cancer that forms in the colon, similar to rectal cancer but with different treatment approaches. It is covered in separate NCCN guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colon cancer is a type of cancer that, when present in family history, increases the risk of prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colon cancer is a type of cancer that, when present in family history, may increase prostate cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Type of cancer starting in the colon."&lt;SEP&gt;"Type of cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eligibility criteria are rules for joining a clinical trial, including age, cancer type and stage, treatment history, and general health, ensuring participant similarity for comparison."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility criteria are rules for joining a clinical trial, including age, cancer type and stage, treatment history, and general health, ensuring participants are similar for comparison."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility criteria are rules for joining a clinical trial, including age, cancer type and stage, treatment history, or general health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility criteria are rules for joining a clinical trial, which may include age, cancer type and stage, treatment history, or general health. These requirements ensure participants are alike in specific ways and that the trial is as safe as possible."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility criteria are rules for joining clinical trials, including age, cancer type and stage, treatment history, or general health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility criteria are the rules for joining a clinical trial, including age, cancer type, stage, treatment history, and general health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENHERTU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enhertu is the brand name for fam-trastuzumab deruxtecan-nxki, a HER2-targeted conjugate used in systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD SUGAR&quot;">
