      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatment methods are approaches used to manage bladder cancer, evolving with medical advancements."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD RELATIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood relative is a family member related by birth, such as parents, siblings, or children. The text advises asking blood relatives about their health history for family history assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MENOPAUSAL SYMPTOM TEAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The menopausal symptom team is a group of specialists who discuss and recommend treatments like HRT for surgical menopause."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymphoma is a cancer of lymphocytes, a type of white blood cell, with various subtypes including non-Hodgkin lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoma is a cancer of the lymph nodes that can weaken the immune system, increasing the risk of developing squamous cell skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoma is a type of blood cancer that increases the risk of anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoma is a type of cancer that affects the lymphatic system, including SLL, which is closely related to CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoma is a type of cancer that begins in the lymphatic system, with primary CNS lymphoma affecting the central nervous system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoma is an abnormal overgrowth (cancer) of lymphocytes. Primary CNS lymphoma is a specific type that affects the central nervous system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoma is cancer that forms from lymphocytes, which are white blood cells that fight infections. It is an abnormal overgrowth of lymphocytes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BCR::ABL PROTEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BCR::ABL protein is produced by the BCR::ABL1 gene and drives cancer growth in BCR::ABL1-positive B-ALL. Targeted therapies inhibit this protein."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVESTIGATIONAL DRUG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An investigational drug is a new medication being tested in clinical trials for safety and effectiveness."&lt;SEP&gt;"An investigational drug is a new treatment being studied in clinical trials, with phases assessing dose, safety, efficacy, and long-term effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"An investigational drug is a new treatment being tested in clinical trials for safety and effectiveness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARGENZA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Margenza is the brand name for margetuximab-cmkb, a HER2-targeted antibody used in systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNOTHERAPY TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer treatment that can reactivate hepatitis B virus, requiring prior testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"G3 is the highest grade for breast cancers, indicating a high-grade tumor with a higher risk of recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"G3 refers to poorly differentiated cancer cells that look very different from normal cells, indicating a high grade."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY IMPACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility impact is a concern addressed in Chapter 2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN SHAVE BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A skin shave biopsy is a procedure that removes the top layer of skin and part of the dermis using a razor-like tool, useful for flat lesions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRESCRIPTION MEDICATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prescription medications are drugs a patient takes, listed in medical history for bladder cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prescription medications are drugs prescribed by doctors that patients must disclose for safe cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MENTAL HEALTH AND WELLNESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mental health and wellness encompasses the psychological and emotional well-being of anal cancer survivors, addressing issues like anxiety, depression, and coping difficulties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNGS AND HEART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lungs and heart are organs listened to during physical exam to detect abnormalities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROUTINE BLOOD TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Routine blood tests can show abnormalities that may lead to the detection of SCLC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOT FLASHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A symptom of surgical menopause characterized by sudden feelings of heat."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hot flashes are a side effect of hormone therapy or menopause induced by treatment, causing sudden warmth and sweating."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hot flashes are a symptom of menopause, including surgical menopause, characterized by sudden warmth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proteins are components of bone tissue, including collagen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are gene products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are molecular features in tumors that may be tested to identify targeted therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are molecules in cancer cells that can be measured or targeted, such as PDL1 and p16, to guide treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are molecules made by cells based on genetic instructions, and certain proteins are named like FLT3 and targeted in AML treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are molecules made with B12 and folic acid, essential for blood cell formation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are molecules on cell surfaces that can be detected by flow cytometry to identify immunophenotypes in CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are molecules produced by genes, and their presence or absence is tested in biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are molecules produced by genes, some of which are tested in biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are molecules that can be altered in cancer and are tested as biomarkers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are molecules that can be tested as biomarkers in tumor biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are products of genes that can be tested in biomarker testing to identify mutations and guide treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Proteins are products of genes that may be tested in biomarker testing to guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEROIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of treatment option for primary CNS lymphoma, often used to reduce inflammation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Steroids are a treatment for ALL, given to everyone with the disease, as mentioned in Chapter 3."&lt;SEP&gt;"Steroids are a type of medication used in the treatment of ALL, often as part of multiagent chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Steroids are medications used in ALL treatment to reduce inflammation and kill leukemia cells, often part of multiagent chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Steroids, specifically corticosteroids, are used to shrink lymphomas and reduce brain swelling in primary CNS lymphoma patients. They are given short-term to avoid side effects and are not started until after a biopsy to ensure accurate diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN.ORG/PATIENTGUIDELINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is a resource providing information on metastatic breast cancer and patient guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is a resource providing patient information on metastatic breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is a web resource for accessing patient guidelines on cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is a website offering patient guidelines from the National Comprehensive Cancer Network, including resources on distress management."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is a website providing more information on side effects of immune checkpoint inhibitors and managing nausea."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is a website providing patient guidelines for cancer care, including a two-part book series on NSCLC."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is a website providing patient guidelines for cancer care, including information on invasive breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is a website providing patient guidelines for cancer care, including information on metastatic breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is a website providing patient guidelines, including fertility information."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is a website providing patient guidelines, including information on fertility preservation and cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is a website where fertility preservation information can be found."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is the specific web address where the NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia can be accessed."&lt;SEP&gt;"NCCN.org/patientguidelines is the web address where NCCN Guidelines for Patients are available."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NERLYNX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nerlynx is the brand name for neratinib, a HER2-targeted inhibitor used in systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPATITIS B VIRUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A virus that can be reactivated by immunotherapy, causing illness that interferes with treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GX indicates that the cancer grade cannot be determined."&lt;SEP&gt;"GX is a grade category indicating the grade can’t be determined."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROLE OF BIOMARKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Role of biomarker is discussed in Chapter 2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXCISION BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical procedure where all or part of a lesion is removed, performed in a doctor's office or hospital, with various options for closing the incision."&lt;SEP&gt;"An excision biopsy is a procedure that removes all or part of a lesion, often used for deeper or larger lesions, and may require stitches."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER STORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer story refers to an individual's unique experience with cancer, emphasizing that statistics don't define outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOPLATIN AND PACLITAXEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carboplatin and paclitaxel is a chemotherapy regimen used for anal cancer that returns to lymph nodes or for metastatic anal cancer, considered a standard option."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CASE MANAGER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Case Manager is a professional who coordinates care, including scheduling tests and follow-up appointments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SLEEPING PROBLEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A symptom of surgical menopause that can affect quality of life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sleeping problems are a symptom of menopause, including surgical menopause, affecting rest."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cells are the basic structural units of living organisms, which can be affected by cancer and treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cells are the basic structural units of living organisms; abnormal cells in blood or marrow are key indicators of CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cells are the basic units of life, and their function is controlled by hormones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cells are the basic units of life; cancer cells grow abnormally, and testosterone can fuel their growth in prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cells are the basic units that can form tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECOG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ECOG (Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group) is an organization that developed a performance status scale used to rate a person's general level of fitness and ability to perform daily tasks in cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUKYSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tukysa is the brand name for tucatinib, a HER2-targeted inhibitor used in systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARROW&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The spongy center of bones where new blood cells are made; sampled in a bone marrow biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIVER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liver cancer is a disease where malignant cells form in the tissues of the liver. It includes primary liver cancer, which starts in the liver, and secondary liver cancer, which spreads from other parts of the body. The most common type in adults is hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liver cancer refers to cancer that starts in the liver (primary) or spreads to the liver from other sites (secondary), with types including hepatocellular carcinoma and intrahepatic cholangiocarcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROLE OF TUMOR MUTATION TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Role of tumor mutation testing is discussed in Chapter 2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DERMATOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A dermatologist is a medical specialist focused on skin health, who examines and treats skin conditions such as actinic keratosis and skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STATISTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Statistics are data about cancer outcomes, which should not be used to predict an individual's prognosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLADDER CANCER BOOK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bladder cancer book is a resource that helps patients understand their diagnosis and treatment options, reducing fear and worry."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTHY DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Healthy diet refers to eating plant-based foods such as veggies, fruits, and whole grains, recommended for cancer survivors to maintain health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT GAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A symptom of surgical menopause that can occur due to hormonal changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight gain is a symptom of adrenal cancer, often caused by excess hormone production from the tumor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight gain is a symptom of menopause, including surgical menopause, involving an increase in body weight."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Disease refers to a pathological condition; CLL is a chronic disease affecting B lymphocytes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AJCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AJCC (American Joint Committee on Cancer) is an organization that created a staging system to determine the extent of cancer in the body, including anatomic and prognostic staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOTONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-energy x-rays used to treat deeper, more invasive tumors in external beam radiation therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Photons are particles of light used in radiation therapy to deliver high-energy radiation to cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A facility where marrow samples are sent for testing after a biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"A lab is a facility where biopsy samples are processed and examined under a microscope by pathologists to diagnose cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lab is a facility where biopsy samples are sent for testing and analysis by a pathologist."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lab is where biopsy tissue samples are sent for testing to determine if cancer is present."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPATOCELLULAR CARCINOMA (HCC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) is a type of liver cancer and the focus of the text. It is a disease characterized by the uncontrolled growth of cells in the liver, and the text discusses risk factors, screening, diagnosis, and treatment planning related to it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) is the most common type of primary liver cancer in adults, arising from liver cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABNORMAL GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abnormal growth of cells within a bone is a bone tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGAN TRANSPLANTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organ transplantation is a medical procedure where an organ from a donor is placed into a recipient, requiring immunosuppressant drugs that increase skin cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phases are broad categories of bladder cancer progression, further divided into stages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECOND OPINION CONSULTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Second Opinion Consultation is a medical appointment with another doctor to review diagnosis and treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Opinion Consultation is seeking another doctor's review of diagnosis and treatment plans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OBSTETRICIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Obstetrician specializes in pregnancy and childbirth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY PRESERVATION REFERRAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility Preservation Referral is being sent to a specialist for preservation options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHANGES IN MOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A symptom of surgical menopause that can affect emotional well-being."&lt;SEP&gt;"Changes in mood are a symptom of menopause, including surgical menopause, affecting emotional state."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diagnosis is the determination of the presence and type of adrenal tumor based on test results, which guides treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnosis is the identification of a disease or condition, such as basal cell skin cancer, based on test results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnosis is the identification of a disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnosis is the identification of an illness based on tests, naming the specific disease a person has."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnosis is the identification of an illness based on tests, naming the specific disease the patient has."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnosis is the identification of cancer, which influences treatment and fertility decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnosis is the process of confirming bladder cancer through tests and procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnosis is the process of identifying a disease through tests and examinations, such as those used for CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnosis is the process of identifying a disease, such as ALL, based on symptoms and test results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnosis is the process of identifying bladder cancer through medical tests and evaluations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnosis is the process of identifying breast cancer through tests like biopsy and imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnosis is the process of identifying primary CNS lymphoma through tests such as neurological exams, imaging, and biopsies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHARMACOGENOMIC TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pharmacogenomic testing examines how a patient's genetic makeup affects their response to drugs, helping to personalize chemotherapy dosing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pharmacogenomic testing is a type of test that examines how a patient's genes affect their response to drugs, used in ALL care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISTRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A broad term for psychological suffering experienced by cancer patients and caregivers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distress is a psychological state of suffering that can arise from cancer diagnosis and treatment, addressed in NCCN guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distress is an emotional state that may affect cancer survivors, addressed in survivorship care resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distress is an unpleasant experience of a mental, physical, social, or spiritual nature that can affect how a person feels, thinks, and acts, often associated with cancer diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distress is emotional or psychological suffering that may be experienced by cancer patients, screened as part of care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Charged particles used as a type of radiation beam to kill cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protons are a type of particle used in radiation therapy to target cancer cells with precision."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protons are particles used in radiation therapy to deliver targeted high-energy radiation to cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY BRAIN TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A broader category of brain tumors that includes primary CNS lymphoma; patients with these tumors often experience psychological distress."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIBROLAMELLAR HEPATOCELLULAR CARCINOMA (FLHC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fibrolamellar hepatocellular carcinoma (FLHC) is a rare subtype of HCC that typically occurs in younger individuals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCEROUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancerous refers to malignant tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNA DAMAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DNA damage in skin cells, often caused by sunlight, can lead to mutations and the development of skin cancers such as squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stages are specific classifications of bladder cancer extent, guiding treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMPORARY HOLDING CHAMBER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A temporary holding chamber refers to the stomach's role in storing food before releasing it to the small intestine. This is mentioned in the context of stomach function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAGINAL ATROPHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition where the lining of the vagina becomes thin, dry, and inflamed, often due to lack of estrogen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vaginal atrophy is thinning, drying, and irritation of the vaginal lining, a symptom of menopause."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEDATIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of medicine offered to patients who feel nervous in tight spaces during imaging scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sedative is a medication used to relax patients during procedures like bone marrow biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sedative is a medicine given to help patients relax during MRI scans, especially for those nervous in small spaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sedative is a medicine given to help patients relax during MRI scans, especially for those who feel nervous in small spaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sedative is a type of medicine given to help patients relax during enclosed imaging procedures like MRI."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sedative is a type of medicine given to help patients relax, especially if they feel nervous in enclosed spaces during medical procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUMBAR PUNCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A lumbar puncture (LP), also called a spinal tap, is a procedure that removes spinal fluid by inserting a needle into the middle of the lower back. It is used to test for leukemia cells in the spinal fluid, which can occur if leukemia travels to the fluid surrounding the spine or brain, causing symptoms like headaches, neck pain, and sensitivity to light."&lt;SEP&gt;"A procedure that removes a small amount of cerebrospinal fluid to test for cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lumbar puncture (LP or spinal tap) is a procedure to collect spinal fluid for detecting leukemia cells, involving needle insertion in the lower back."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lumbar puncture is a procedure to collect cerebrospinal fluid to check for ALL cells in the CNS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lumbar puncture is a procedure to collect cerebrospinal fluid to check for leukemia cells in the central nervous system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lumbar puncture is a procedure to collect cerebrospinal fluid, used in AML testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lumbar puncture is a procedure to collect cerebrospinal fluid, used to check for leukemia cells in the central nervous system, which is part of AML testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lumbar puncture, also known as a spinal tap, is a procedure that removes cerebrospinal fluid for testing to confirm CNS lymphoma diagnosis and assess spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEREDITARY GENETIC TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hereditary genetic testing is a medical procedure to identify inherited genetic mutations that may increase the risk of breast cancer, often recommended based on family history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hereditary genetic testing looks for inherited mutations using blood or saliva to assess cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE AREA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The lymph node area includes regions like the underarm (axilla) where lymph nodes are located, often targeted in surgery and radiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRESCRIPTION DRUGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medications prescribed by a doctor that must be listed for the treatment team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAHEPATIC CHOLANGIOCARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intrahepatic cholangiocarcinoma is the second most common type of primary liver cancer in adults, originating in the bile ducts within the liver."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NONCANCEROUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Noncancerous refers to benign tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN LESION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A skin lesion is an abnormal area of skin that may be benign or cancerous, requiring examination and biopsy to determine if it is squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER BLADDER CANCER TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter Bladder Cancer Treatment is a section of the document explaining treatment options for bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEER-TO-PEER SUPPORT PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Peer-To-Peer Support Program is an initiative by the Anal Cancer Foundation that connects anal cancer patients and caregivers with trained peer volunteers for support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEVOXYL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Levoxyl is a brand name for levothyroxine, a thyroid hormone replacement therapy used to treat thyroid conditions, including thyroid cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSATELLITE INSTABILITY (MSI) TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of biomarker testing recommended for all colon cancer patients to identify features like MSI-H or dMMR, which help guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A long-term risk of not having enough estrogen after surgical menopause."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cardiovascular disease is a long-term risk associated with insufficient estrogen levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cardiovascular disease is a long-term risk of not having enough estrogen, involving heart or blood vessel problems."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN BLOCKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pain Blocker is an injected medication used to numb an area during procedures like bone marrow biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEART TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Heart or cardiac tests assess heart function, monitor treatment side effects, and may include electrocardiogram and echocardiogram."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart tests are cardiac procedures used to evaluate heart function, monitor treatment side effects, or measure function before treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart tests are diagnostic procedures that may be part of cancer testing to assess overall health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart tests are diagnostic procedures to assess heart function, which may be affected by ALL treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart tests are general health tests that may be part of FL evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart tests are general health tests to assess cardiac function, which may be part of the AML workup."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart tests are medical examinations to assess heart function, potentially part of cancer treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart tests are procedures to assess heart function, which may be needed before certain AML treatments to ensure the heart can handle the therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart tests are procedures to assess heart function, which may be needed before or during ALL treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart tests assess cardiac function before and during treatment, as some cancer therapies can affect the heart."&lt;SEP&gt;"Heart tests assess cardiac function, part of AML testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure to remove and examine sentinel lymph nodes for cancer cells, used for staging and treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sentinel lymph node biopsy (SLNB or SNB) is a surgical procedure to remove the first lymph node(s) that cancer cells are most likely to spread to from a primary tumor, often done during mastectomy or lumpectomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sentinel lymph node biopsy is a procedure involving injection of dye or radioactive substance to identify and remove sentinel nodes for cancer testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sentinel lymph node biopsy is a procedure to identify and remove the first lymph nodes where cancer cells are likely to spread, often performed before mastectomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sentinel lymph node biopsy is a procedure to remove and examine the first lymph node(s) that cancer cells are likely to spread to, helping determine if cancer has spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sentinel lymph node biopsy is a surgery to remove and examine the first lymph node(s) to which cancer cells likely spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sentinel lymph node biopsy is a surgical procedure to examine the first lymph nodes that cancer cells are most likely to spread to, used to determine if cancer has spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AXILLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Axilla is the anatomical region commonly known as the armpit, where lymph nodes are located and biopsied in axillary lymph node procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Axilla is the anatomical term for the armpit area, where lymph nodes under the arm are located and where breast cancer can spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Axilla is the armpit area where lymph nodes are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"The armpit area where axillary lymph nodes are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"The axilla is the underarm area where sentinel lymph nodes are removed during modified radical mastectomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The axilla, or armpit, is the area where axillary lymph nodes are located. It is a common site for breast cancer metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of over-the-counter medicine that can interfere with cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXED-TYPE TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A mixed-type tumor is a rare liver cancer composed of both hepatocellular carcinoma and cholangiocarcinoma cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAPIDLY GROWING AREAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rapidly growing areas of bone, like the metaphysis, are where tumors often occur."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STITCHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stitches are used to close skin openings after punch or excision biopsies, aiding in wound healing and minimizing scarring."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sutures used to close the opening in the skin after a skin punch biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER TESTS FOR BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter Tests for Bladder Cancer is a section of the document explaining diagnostic tests for bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;5-FU AND CISPLATIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"5-FU and cisplatin is a chemotherapy regimen used for anal cancer that returns to lymph nodes or for metastatic anal cancer, considered a standard option."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICAL TRIAL SPONSOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical Trial Sponsor is an entity, often a pharmaceutical company or research institution, that funds and oversees clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTEOPOROSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone loss condition that is a long-term risk of not having enough estrogen after surgical menopause."&lt;SEP&gt;"Osteoporosis is a condition of bone loss, listed as a long-term risk of not having enough estrogen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Osteoporosis is a long-term risk of not having enough estrogen, involving bone loss."&lt;SEP&gt;"Osteoporosis is bone thinning that can result from hormone therapy or early menopause, increasing fracture risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIP BONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hip Bone is the location where bone marrow biopsy and aspiration are typically performed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hip bone is the anatomical location from which bone marrow samples are typically taken."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bone at the back of the hip where a bone marrow biopsy needle is usually inserted."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE MARROW TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone marrow tests are diagnostic procedures that include aspirate and biopsy to examine bone marrow for abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow tests are diagnostic procedures used to evaluate CML and determine the extent of disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow tests are diagnostic procedures used to examine bone marrow for cancer cells, part of CML and ALL testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow tests are procedures not often needed to diagnose CLL but may be done to find out what’s causing low blood cell counts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow tests are procedures to collect and examine bone marrow samples for ALL diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow tests are procedures to examine bone marrow for the presence of lymphoblasts, essential for diagnosing ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow tests involve aspirate and biopsy procedures to diagnose AML, with samples reviewed by a pathologist."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow tests involve removing and testing samples of bone marrow to diagnose leukemia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone marrow tests involve sampling bone marrow to confirm ALL diagnosis and assess the extent of disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAGNOSTIC MAMMOGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A breast x-ray used for those with symptoms like a lump or pain, or to examine an abnormal area found in a screening mammogram; evaluated immediately."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnostic mammogram is a breast imaging test using x-rays to examine specific areas of the breast, often used when symptoms are present or to follow up on abnormal screening results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnostic mammogram is a detailed imaging test of both breasts used to investigate abnormalities, different from a screening mammogram."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diagnostic mammogram is an imaging test used to examine the breast in detail when cancer is suspected."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DELAYED RECONSTRUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Delayed reconstruction is breast reconstruction performed after finishing cancer treatment, often in stages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASPIRIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of over-the-counter medicine that can interfere with cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspirin is a medication discussed with doctors for daily use to prevent future cancers in patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspirin is a medication that may be taken daily to prevent future cancers, as discussed with a doctor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BILE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bile is a fluid produced by the liver that helps in digestion and breaking down fats. It is part of the hepatobiliary system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bile is a yellow or green fluid produced by liver cells, composed of cholesterol, bilirubin, salts, and water, aiding in fat digestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VESSELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vessels include blood and lymph vessels, part of soft tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A scar is tissue that forms after skin injury or biopsy, and can be a site for squamous cell carcinoma development, especially in chronic wounds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER BLADDER CANCER TREATMENT WHAT’S THE BEST TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is a section of the document discussing the best treatment options for bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONFIDENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Confidence refers to the assurance patients gain from understanding their diagnosis and treatment options, enabling well-informed decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXERCISE REGIMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Exercise regimen involves physical activity of 150 minutes per week, recommended for patients after discussion with their doctor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD THINNERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood thinners are medications (oral or injections) used to prevent blood clots after surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENT PORTAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A patient portal is an online platform where patients can access their test results, visit notes, and communicate with their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"A patient portal is an online system where imaging reports may be sent directly to patients for discussion with their HCP."&lt;SEP&gt;"A patient portal is an online system where patients can access their medical reports and results."&lt;SEP&gt;"A patient portal is an online system where patients can access their test reports, but results should be discussed with the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient Portal is an online system where patients can view test results and medical records."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient Portal is an online system where patients can view their pathology reports and medical information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portal is a system where imaging reports may be available to patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portal is a system where test reports might be available, but patients are advised to wait to discuss results with their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portal is an online system for accessing medical records and test results, facilitating patient access to health information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient portal is an online system that helps patients track appointments, access records, and communicate with their care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADENOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adenoma is a benign tumor that can produce hormones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adenoma is a type of polyp that can become invasive rectal cancer over time, leading to adenocarcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adenoma is the most common type of colon polyp that can become invasive colon cancer over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adenoma is the most common type of colon polyp, which can become invasive colon cancer over many years."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adenoma is the most common type of polyp that can become invasive colon cancer over many years. Cancer forming in an adenoma is called adenocarcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adenoma is the most common type of polyp, a non-cancerous growth on the inner lining of the colon and rectum, which can become invasive rectal cancer over many years."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adenoma, also known as adrenocortical adenoma, is the most common type of adrenal gland tumor. It is noncancerous and can be functioning or nonfunctioning. Small adenomas that do not produce excessive hormones may not require treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"An adenoma is a type of benign adrenal tumor that can produce hormones, such as aldosterone or cortisol."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH CARE PROVIDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A health care provider is a medical professional who discusses test results and guides the patient through treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A health care provider is a professional who examines the oropharynx and other areas, using tools like mirrors or scopes, and interprets test results."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical professional who performs physical exams, palpates oral cavities, and guides patients through cancer care procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical professional who provides information and guidance to patients about next steps in breast cancer diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health Care Provider is a medical professional who discusses imaging results and guides treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health Care Provider is a medical professional who discusses test results and provides care, including informing patients about their overall health and treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care provider is a general term for professionals and organizations that deliver medical care, including those involved in breast cancer screening and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care provider is a medical professional or facility that provides care, including discussing family history, ordering tests, and guiding treatment decisions for cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care provider is a medical professional who guides patients through diagnosis, treatment, and genetic testing referrals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care provider is a professional or facility that tests and diagnoses conditions like bladder cancer, including doctors and clinics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care provider is a professional such as a doctor or nurse who conducts exams, interprets tests, and provides treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care provider is a professional who conducts physical exams and guides patients through testing and treatment for prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care provider is a professional who conducts physical exams and provides medical care, including checking vital signs and examining organs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care provider is a professional who delivers medical care and discusses test results with the patient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care provider is a professional who discusses results and answers patient questions about procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care provider is a professional who discusses test results and guides treatment decisions with the patient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care provider is a professional who recommends biomarker testing, refers for genetic testing, and guides treatment based on results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care providers are medical professionals who discuss test results and guide patients through treatment plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care providers are professionals who discuss test results and guide treatment decisions based on the patient's overall health and cancer characteristics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local therapy focuses on the breast, chest wall, and lymph node area, including mastectomy and radiation therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local therapy treats cancer at its source, such as surgery or radiation, without affecting the whole body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
