      <data key="d1">"A specific type of hormone receptor that binds progesterone, providing survival and proliferation signals, and suggesting estrogen dependence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Progesterone Receptor (PR) is a biomarker status that indicates whether the cancer cells have receptors for progesterone, which is important for prognosis and treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Progesterone receptor (PR) is a protein on cancer cells that influences treatment decisions, with endocrine therapy targeting PR-positive cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Progesterone receptor is a protein found on some cancer cells that, when present, indicates the cancer may respond to hormone therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
