    <node id="&quot;INFECTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Infections are a more severe side effect of intraperitoneal chemotherapy, requiring medical attention."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infections are a risk during cancer treatment, especially when blood cell counts are low, such as after high-dose chemotherapy in stem cell rescue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infections are a symptom of CLL and can recur despite treatment due to weakened immune function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infections are health conditions that can cause lung nodules, among other causes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infections are health risks that can occur when the immune system is weakened, potentially complicating skin cancer treatment and increasing risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER TESTS FOR BLADDER CANCER BLOOD AND URINE TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is a section of the document explaining blood and urine tests for bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MITOMYCIN AND CAPECITABINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mitomycin and capecitabine is a chemotherapy regimen used in addition to radiation for anal cancer that returns to lymph nodes when no prior radiation was given."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPPORT GROUP FACILITATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Support Group Facilitator is a person who leads survivor support groups, providing guidance and a safe space for sharing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITAL SIGNS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vital Signs are measurements of basic body functions, including blood pressure, heart rate, breathing rate, and temperature, checked during physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vital signs include blood pressure, heart rate, breathing rate, and body temperature, checked during a physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vital signs include temperature, blood pressure, pulse, and breathing rate, measured during physical exam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALL SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ALL specialist is a healthcare professional with expertise in treating acute lymphoblastic leukemia, often consulted for optimal care."&lt;SEP&gt;"An ALL specialist is a medical professional with expertise in treating ALL, whose opinion is recommended for optimal care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONE RECEPTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A protein found inside or on the surface of a cell that hormones bind to, causing changes within the cell. In breast cancer, hormone receptors can stimulate cancer growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hormone receptor refers to proteins like estrogen receptor (ER) and progesterone receptor (PR) that, when present, can influence cancer growth and treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-HORMONAL MEDICINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-hormonal medicine is an option to manage symptoms of surgical menopause."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINANCIAL STRESSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Financial stresses are economic burdens related to cancer care, which social workers help patients navigate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAIN TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The tissue where primary CNS lymphoma usually develops deep within, making surgery risky."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFERIOR VENA CAVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The inferior vena cava is a large vein that returns blood to the heart."&lt;SEP&gt;"The inferior vena cava is a large vein that returns deoxygenated blood from the lower body to the heart."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMICAL STORAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical storage is a function of bones, storing chemicals the body needs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIRUSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Viruses are pathogens that the body fights off with a healthy immune system; a weakened immune system increases susceptibility to viral infections."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER TESTS FOR BLADDER CANCER CYSTOSCOPY AND BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is a section of the document explaining cystoscopy and biopsy for bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fear is an emotional response that can be part of distress in cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fear is an emotional response to a cancer diagnosis that can be reduced through education and support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN CANCER (MELANOMA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skin cancer (melanoma) is a type of cancer that can be related to germline mutations in genes like BRCA1 and BRCA2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOARD-CERTIFIED EXPERTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Board-certified experts are healthcare professionals with specialized certification in their fields, part of the care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLEMENTARY AND ALTERNATIVE THERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Complementary and alternative therapies include practices like acupuncture, meditation, yoga, and herbal products that may help with side effects during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARMPIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Armpit is a body area where lymph nodes may be palpated during physical exam for CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Armpit is a common location for swollen lymph nodes in FL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Armpit is an area examined during breast palpation for lymph node assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Armpit is the common term for the axilla, where lymph nodes are located and biopsied in axillary lymph node procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENT ADVOCACY GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Patient advocacy groups are organizations that provide support and resources for patients and families, mentioned in the 'Other resources' chapter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient advocacy groups are organizations that provide support and resources for patients, as mentioned in Chapter 7."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient advocacy groups provide support and resources for patients with AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient advocacy groups provide support, resources, and information to patients and families affected by cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANATOMIC STAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anatomic Staging is based on tumor size, lymph node status, and distant metastasis, without considering treatment assumptions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anatomic staging is a method of staging based on tumor size (T), lymph node status (N), and distant metastasis (M)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anatomic staging is based on the extent of cancer as defined by tumor size (T), lymph node status (N), and distant metastasis (M)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEG SWELLING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leg swelling is a common side effect of ovarian cancer surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSURANCE STRESSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insurance stresses are difficulties with health insurance coverage, which social workers help patients manage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure to remove part or all of the colon, often performed to treat colon cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colectomy is a surgery to remove the part of the colon with cancer, involving removal of lymph nodes and reconnection of healthy ends."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colectomy is a surgical procedure to remove part or all of the colon, often used to treat colon cancer. It involves preparation, surgery, recovery, and potential side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgery to remove part or all of the colon, used for non-metastatic colon cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMON HEPATIC DUCT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The common hepatic duct is formed by the joining of left and right hepatic ducts, carrying bile from the liver."&lt;SEP&gt;"The common hepatic duct is formed by the joining of left and right hepatic ducts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONE PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormone production is a function of bones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacteria are pathogens that the body fights off with a healthy immune system; a weakened immune system increases susceptibility to bacterial infections."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER TESTS FOR BLADDER CANCER IMAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is a section of the document explaining imaging tests for bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY SPECIALIST REFERRAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility Specialist Referral is the process of being sent to a specialist for fertility preservation advice."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA (IDC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Invasive ductal carcinoma (IDC) is a type of breast cancer that starts in the cells lining the milk ducts and spreads into surrounding tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPRODUCTIVE SPECIALIST CONSULTATION&quot;">
