    <node id="&quot;LYMPHOBLASTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymphoblasts (or blasts) are immature lymphocytes produced in excess in the bone marrow in Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL). They crowd out normal bone marrow cells, leading to reduced production of normal blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoblasts are immature cells that are present in the bone marrow, blood, and organs in ALL. A diagnosis of ALL requires 20% or more lymphoblasts in the bone marrow."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoblasts are immature cells that mature into lymphocytes, a type of white blood cell."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoblasts are immature lymphocytes produced in excess in ALL, crowding out normal bone marrow cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoblasts are immature lymphocytes that are overproduced in ALL, crowding out normal bone marrow."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoblasts are immature lymphocytes that are overproduced in bone marrow in ALL, making it hard for bone marrow or blood to work."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoblasts are immature lymphocytes that are produced in excess in the bone marrow in Acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL). They can crowd out other blood cells, causing blood to not work as it should."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoblasts are immature lymphocytes that can be overproduced in certain leukemias."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoblasts are immature lymphocytes that crowd out normal bone marrow in ALL, leading to reduced blood production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoblasts are immature lymphoid cells that may be increased in blast phase CML, affecting treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoblasts are immature white blood cells that mature into lymphocytes, and in ALL, there are too many abnormal lymphoblasts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphoblasts are immature white blood cells. In ALL, a diagnosis is made when 20% or more lymphoblasts are present in the bone marrow."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCREENING MAMMOGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A routine breast x-ray done when there are no signs or symptoms of breast cancer, to detect abnormalities early."&lt;SEP&gt;"Screening mammogram is a routine breast imaging test performed when there are no signs or symptoms of breast cancer, using low-dose x-rays."&lt;SEP&gt;"Screening mammogram is a routine imaging test for early detection of breast cancer in asymptomatic women, different from diagnostic mammogram."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REMISSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Remission is a state where AML cells disappear, and blood and saliva can be used for testing leukemia predisposition syndromes during this time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Remission is a state where cancer is no longer detectable, after which maintenance therapy may follow."&lt;SEP&gt;"Remission is a state where signs of cancer are reduced or absent, monitored using PCR."&lt;SEP&gt;"Remission is the goal of AML treatment, indicating the absence of detectable cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Remission is the goal of AML treatment, referring to the absence of signs and symptoms of cancer, achieved through treatments like chemotherapy and targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Remission means there are no symptoms or signs of cancer. It may last for months or years, but primary CNS lymphoma often relapses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
