    <node id="&quot;HERNIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hernia is a possible complication of colectomy, where organs push through tissues or muscles weakened by surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hernia is a potential side effect of colectomy where organs push through weakened tissues or muscles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIVER CANCER SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liver cancer screening involves tests to detect liver cancer early in at-risk individuals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liver cancer screening is a process of regular tests to detect liver cancer early in individuals at risk, before symptoms occur. It involves an ultrasound and an alpha-fetoprotein (AFP) blood test every 6 months for those at risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liver cancer screening is a process of regular tests to detect liver cancer in individuals without symptoms, particularly those with cirrhosis or chronic hepatitis B. The goal is to find cancer early when it is more likely to be cured."&lt;SEP&gt;"Liver cancer screening refers to tests and procedures used to detect liver cancer early in at-risk individuals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
