    <node id="&quot;STANDARD-OF-CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Standard-of-care refers to the accepted, evidence-based treatment approaches that are assumed in prognostic staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A primary tumor is the initial mass of cancer cells that forms in the breast or prostate, from which cancer can spread to other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary tumor is the initial mass of cancer cells that forms in the breast tissue over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary tumor is the initial tumor formed by cancer cells in the area of the oropharynx."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary tumor is the initial tumor formed by cancer cells in the nasopharynx for NPC, which can grow into nearby tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Tumor is the original site of cancer, shown in imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary tumor is the original mass of cancer cells that forms in the breast before spreading."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary tumor is the original site of cancer growth in the kidney, from which cancer can spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary tumor is the original site of cancer, identified through imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary tumor is the original site where cancer started, as revealed by imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary tumor is the original tumor at the site of origin, measured in centimeters for staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary tumor is the original tumor from which cancer originates, and it is the first site biopsied in cancer diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary tumor refers to the original site of cancer in the prostate, identified through imaging or biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary tumor is the first (original) tumor, whose extent is part of cancer staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary tumor is the original site of cancer, from which cancer cells may spread to sentinel lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary tumor is where cancer started, identified through imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary tumor is where cancer started, shown by imaging tests to assess spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC SURGEON CONSULTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic surgeon consultation is a meeting with a plastic surgeon to discuss breast reconstruction options after mastectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOWEL OBSTRUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bowel obstruction is a potential complication after colectomy caused by scar tissue blocking the bowel."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC LIVER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic liver cancer is cancer that has spread to the liver from another primary site, such as the colon."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic liver cancer is cancer that has spread to the liver from another primary site."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic liver cancer is liver cancer that has spread to distant parts of the body, such as the lung or bone, from the primary tumor in the liver."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORIGIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Origin is where cancer begins, such as in bone or cartilage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FULL HEALTH HISTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A comprehensive review of a patient's medical background, part of testing for CSCC."&lt;SEP&gt;"A full health history is a comprehensive review of a patient's medical background, used to identify risk factors for skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER TESTS FOR BLADDER CANCER PHYSICAL EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is a section of the document explaining physical exams for bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer screening involves tests to detect other cancers early, recommended for anal cancer survivors to prevent recurrence or new cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELIMINATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Elimination is the removal of undigested waste from the body, facilitated by the large intestine and rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTHY HABITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Healthy habits include cancer screenings, exercise, diet, and lifestyle changes to prevent other health issues and improve quality of life after anal cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lifestyle practices recommended for survivors to maintain health after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL THERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treatments like surgery or ablation used for liver and lung tumors in metastatic colon cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Treatments used to address liver and lung tumors in metastatic colon cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIFESTYLE CHOICES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lifestyle Choices include diet, activity level, smoking, and alcohol consumption, which are reviewed in medical history for CLL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BCR::ABL1-NEGATIVE B-ALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BCR::ABL1-negative B-ALL is a subtype of B-ALL that does not have the BCR::ABL1 gene fusion, and clinical trials are preferred for treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"BCR::ABL1-negative B-ALL is a subtype of B-ALL that does not have the BCR::ABL1 gene fusion. It is the most common type of B-ALL, and treatment often involves clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTIDISCIPLINARY TEAM (MDT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A multidisciplinary team (MDT) is a team of health care and psychosocial care professionals from different professional backgrounds who have knowledge and experience in treating AML. They work together to plan and implement treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Multidisciplinary team (MDT) is a group of health care and psychosocial professionals with expertise in cancer, united in treatment planning and implementation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Multidisciplinary Team (MDT) is a team of health care and psychosocial care professionals from different backgrounds with expertise in AML, united in planning and implementing treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUBSTAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Substages are smaller groups within cancer stages, providing more detail on cancer extent."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNDERARM (AXILLA) SENTINEL LYMPH NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Underarm (axilla) sentinel lymph nodes are lymph nodes in the armpit area that are removed during modified radical mastectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHECKPOINT INHIBITORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Checkpoint inhibitors are a type of immunotherapy that block natural braking mechanisms in the body to allow the immune system to better fight cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Checkpoint inhibitors are immunotherapy drugs that enhance the immune system's ability to destroy cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC COLON CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metastatic colon cancer is cancer that originates in the colon and spreads to the liver, as an example of secondary liver cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic colon cancer is cancer that originates in the colon and spreads to the liver."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TYPES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Types refer to different categories of cancer, such as primary or secondary."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLOSE EXAMINATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Close examination is a detailed visual inspection of skin lesions by a doctor to assess characteristics suggestive of cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER TESTS FOR BLADDER CANCER COMPLETE BLOOD COUNT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is a section of the document explaining complete blood count for bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IODINE-131&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iodine-131 is a radioactive isotope of iodine used in RAI therapy to target and kill thyroid cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KEGEL EXERCISES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kegel exercises are at-home exercises to tighten and release vaginal and anal muscles, part of pelvic floor therapy for anal cancer survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRESCRIPTION MEDICINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prescription Medicines are medications prescribed by a doctor, which are reviewed in medical history for CLL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BCR::ABL1-LIKE B-ALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BCR::ABL1-like B-ALL is a subtype of B-ALL that has a gene expression profile similar to BCR::ABL1-positive B-ALL but lacks the BCR::ABL1 fusion, and clinical trials are preferred."&lt;SEP&gt;"BCR::ABL1-like B-ALL is a subtype of B-ALL that has a gene expression profile similar to BCR::ABL1-positive B-ALL but lacks the BCR::ABL1 fusion. It is treated similarly to BCR::ABL1-negative B-ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hematologist or hematologic oncologist is a medical expert in blood diseases and blood cancers, such as AML, and treats these conditions. They are a key member of the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hematologist or hematologic oncologist is a medical expert in blood diseases and blood cancers, treating conditions like AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUNICA ADVENTITIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tunica adventitia is the outermost layer of the esophagus, made of connective tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEST WALL MUSCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chest wall muscle may be partially removed during modified radical mastectomy to ensure complete cancer removal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PMMR/MSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"pMMR/MSS refers to a type of colon cancer with proficient mismatch repair, typically treated with chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPATIC DUCT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hepatic ducts are thin tubes that drain bile from the liver, with left and right hepatic ducts joining to form the common hepatic duct."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Group refers to a collection of cancers, such as sarcomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL APPEARANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell appearance refers to the visual characteristics of cells under a microscope, which pathologists note to diagnose cancer type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER TESTS FOR BLADDER CANCER COMPREHENSIVE METABOLIC PANEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is a section of the document explaining comprehensive metabolic panel for bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survivor is an individual who has completed anal cancer treatment and is in the survivorship phase, focusing on follow-up care and late effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glands in some parts of the esophagus secrete mucus, aiding in lubrication and protection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WELL-INFORMED DECISIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Well-informed decisions are choices made by patients based on comprehensive understanding of their diagnosis and treatment options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVER-THE-COUNTER MEDICINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medicines available without a prescription, such as antacids, aspirin, or NSAIDs, that must be disclosed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Over-the-Counter Medicines are medications available without a prescription, which are reviewed in medical history for CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Over-the-counter medicines are non-prescription drugs a patient takes, listed in medical history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Over-the-counter medicines are non-prescription drugs that patients may take, which can interact with prescribed treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Over-the-counter medicines are non-prescription drugs that patients must list for care teams to avoid interactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BCR::ABL1-POSITIVE B-ALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BCR::ABL1-positive B-ALL is a subtype of B-ALL characterized by the presence of the BCR::ABL1 gene, which produces the BCR::ABL protein. Treatment aims to stop the activity of this protein."&lt;SEP&gt;"BCR::ABL1-positive B-ALL is a subtype of B-ALL that has the BCR::ABL1 gene fusion, and treatment aims to stop the activity of the BCR::ABL protein."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYTARABINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cytarabine (Ara-C) is an anthracycline used in many AML treatment regimens, with different doses like standard, high (HiDAC), intermediate, and low (LDAC)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytarabine (also called Ara-C) is a chemotherapy drug used in many AML treatment regimens, either alone or in combination. It can be given at various doses (standard, high, intermediate, low) and is also used intrathecally for AML in the spinal fluid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytarabine is a chemotherapy drug used in combination with other agents to treat AML with core binding factor abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytarabine is a chemotherapy drug used in high doses as an alternative induction option for primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UPPER ESOPHAGUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The upper part of the esophagus is made of striated muscle, which is under voluntary control."&lt;SEP&gt;"Upper esophagus is the part of the esophagus made of striated muscle, under voluntary control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIATION THERAPY (RT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiation therapy (RT) uses high-energy radiation from x-rays, photons, protons, and other sources to kill cancer cells and shrink tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DMMR/MSI-H&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"dMMR/MSI-H refers to a type of colon cancer with deficient mismatch repair, often treated with immunotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEFT HEPATIC DUCT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The left hepatic duct drains bile from the left lobe of the liver."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rare describes sarcomas as a rare group of cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL SIZE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell size is a characteristic noted by pathologists when examining biopsy samples, helping to identify cancerous cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIGO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FIGO (International Federation of Gynecology and Obstetrics) is the organization that defines the staging system for ovarian cancer, as referenced in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTHY WEIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maintaining a healthy weight is a lifestyle factor that may decrease the aggressiveness of prostate cancer and improve outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHARED DECISION-MAKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shared decision-making is a process where patients and doctors share information, discuss options, and agree on a treatment plan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MENSTRUATION CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Menstruation Changes refer to the stopping or return of periods during and after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST CANCER SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breast cancer screening is a process to find cancer early before symptoms start, using tests like mammograms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPPLEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Over-the-counter products like vitamins or herbs that can interact with prescribed medicines and affect treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Products like vitamins or herbs that can raise or lower chemotherapy drug levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplements are additional nutritional products a patient takes, listed in medical history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplements are dietary products taken to enhance health, which are reviewed in medical history for CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplements are dietary products that can affect treatment efficacy and safety."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplements are products like vitamins or herbals that can interact with prescribed medicines and should be reported to the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplements are products like vitamins or herbs that may interact with prescribed medicines and affect treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplements are products like vitamins or minerals that patients should list, as some can interact with treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplements are products taken to add nutrients to the diet, such as vitamins or minerals. The text notes that some supplements may affect the efficacy of prescribed medicines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplements are vitamins or minerals a patient takes, which may interact with medicines, listed in medical history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplements are vitamins or minerals taken by patients, which can affect the efficacy of prescribed medicines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplements are vitamins or minerals taken to support health, but some can interact with prescribed medicines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplements are vitamins, minerals, or other dietary products that patients take, which may affect the efficacy of cancer medications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supplements taken by the patient may interact with chemotherapy, requiring disclosure to the care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYSTEMIC THERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Systemic therapies are treatments that can affect both cancer cells and normal cells, given intravenously or orally, and include chemotherapy, targeted therapy, and immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Systemic therapies are treatments that travel through the bloodstream to reach cancer cells throughout the body, including chemotherapy and targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Systemic therapies are treatments that travel through the bloodstream to reach cells throughout the body, including chemotherapy, targeted therapy, and immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Systemic therapies are treatments that work throughout the body, including chemotherapy, targeted therapy, and immunotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPOMETHYLATING AGENTS (HMAS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hypomethylating agents block methyl groups from binding to DNA, turning silenced genes back on, allowing leukemic blasts to mature into normal cells, with example Azacitidine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIDDLE ESOPHAGUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Middle esophagus is the part of the esophagus with a mixture of striated and smooth muscle."&lt;SEP&gt;"The middle part of the esophagus is a mixture of striated and smooth muscle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-ENERGY RADIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-energy radiation is used in radiation therapy to kill cancer cells and shrink tumors, sourced from x-rays, photons, or protons."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLON WALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colon wall is the structure of the colon composed of layers of tissue, through which cancer can grow if untreated."&lt;SEP&gt;"The colon wall has multiple layers, and the depth of tumor invasion into these layers determines the T stage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RIGHT HEPATIC DUCT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The right hepatic duct drains bile from the right lobe of the liver."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Common describes soft tissue sarcomas as more common than bone sarcomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL SHAPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell shape is a characteristic noted by pathologists when examining biopsy samples, helping to identify cancerous cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APP USAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"App Usage is using the NCCN Patient Guides app for information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLFCIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FOLFCIS is a chemotherapy regimen combining 5-FU, leucovorin, and cisplatin, used as first-line therapy for metastatic anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer that has spread to distant organs such as the liver, lungs, or bones, which is not the case for locally advanced cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colon cancer that has spread to other organs, such as the liver or lungs, requiring expanded biomarker testing and systemic therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cancer is cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, for which targeted therapy and immunotherapy may be options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cancer is cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, such as the lung and distant lymph nodes, and is often referred to as very advanced disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cancer is cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, with stage 4 being metastatic at diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cancer refers to cancer that has spread from its original site to other parts of the body, such as bone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cancer refers to cancer that has spread from the original site to other parts of the body, with stage 4 pancreatic cancer being an example."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cancer refers to cancer that has spread to distant parts of the body, requiring aggressive treatments like EBRT or targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cancer refers to cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, such as bone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cancer refers to cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, such as stage IV anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cancer refers to cervical cancer that has spread to distant parts of the body, often treated with systemic therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cancer refers to cervical cancer that has spread to distant parts of the body, requiring systemic therapy and imaging to assess response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cancer refers to thyroid cancer that has spread to areas far from the neck, such as the lungs, liver, muscles, bones, brain, and spinal cord."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic cervical cancer is cancer that has spread to distant organs or lymph nodes beyond the pelvis. It is typically treated with systemic therapies, though the text focuses on earlier stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metastatic esophageal cancer has spread to distant parts of the body, such as the liver, distant lymph nodes, lung, bone, or brain."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD TRANSFUSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood Transfusions are procedures where blood is given to a patient, which are reviewed in medical history for CLL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUTATION TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mutation testing identifies specific genetic changes in tumors to guide targeted therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutation testing is a type of genetic testing that looks for specific mutations in cancer cells to determine treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mutation testing is another name for biomarker testing, identifying specific genetic changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATHETER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A catheter is a thin tube used for intraperitoneal chemotherapy, connected to a port placed inside the abdomen during surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"A catheter is a thin, long tube often placed in the upper arm to deliver systemic therapy, fluids, and blood products into the body. It stays in place until treatment is complete."&lt;SEP&gt;"A catheter is a thin, long tube placed in the upper arm to deliver systemic therapy, fluids, and blood products into the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"A catheter is a tube inserted into a continent urinary diversion reservoir several times a day to drain urine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Catheter is a flexible tube used to deliver medicine into the bladder or drain urine from a pouch in urinary diversion procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Catheter is a flexible tube used to drain urine from the Indiana pouch or deliver intravesical therapy into the bladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Catheter is a tube inserted through the urethra or stoma to help empty the neobladder or continent cutaneous pouch."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOWER ESOPHAGUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lower esophagus is the part of the esophagus consisting only of smooth muscle, not under voluntary control."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lower part of the esophagus consists only of smooth muscle, which is involuntary."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHORT TREATMENT SESSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Short treatment sessions are daily radiation therapy sessions given over a few days to weeks to treat cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORLDWIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Worldwide refers to the global scope of clinical trial databases like clinicaltrials.gov, accessible internationally."&lt;SEP&gt;"Worldwide refers to the global scope of clinical trial databases, such as clinicaltrials.gov, accessible internationally."&lt;SEP&gt;"Worldwide refers to the global scope of clinical trial information available through the U.S. National Library of Medicine's clinicaltrials.gov database."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD CLOTTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood clotting is a process supported by the liver, which produces factors necessary for coagulation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORAL CAVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The mouth area that is examined and palpated during head and neck exams to detect abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oral cavity is another name for the mouth, and it is a location where head and neck cancers can occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oral cavity is the anatomical area comprising the mouth, including the lips, buccal mucosa, tongue, gums, floor of the mouth, hard palate, and retromolar trigone, where mouth cancer can develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oral cavity, also known as the mouth or buccal cavity, is the first part of the digestive and respiratory systems. It includes the lips, cheeks, palate, teeth, and tongue, and functions in eating and speaking."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oral cavity, also known as the mouth, is a location where head and neck cancers can occur."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL TYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell type refers to the classification of cells based on their origin and appearance, which pathologists use to diagnose squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATROPHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Atrophy is a condition where the lining of the vagina becomes thin, dry, and inflamed, often due to lack of estrogen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIATION TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiation treatment is a therapy for anal cancer that can weaken pelvic bones and cause side effects like vaginal stenosis, requiring monitoring and management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiation treatment to the pelvis is a cancer therapy that can weaken pelvic bones, increasing fracture risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emergency room, where a patient was diagnosed with colon cancer at age 44, as mentioned in a personal story."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency room, where a patient was diagnosed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Emergency room."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 4 CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 4 cancer is the most advanced numbered stage, but not all stage 4 cancers are metastatic, as noted in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stage 4 ovarian cancer is a specific stage where maintenance therapy is an option after successful initial treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEVERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fevers are elevated body temperatures that occur when not sick, a B symptom of CLL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RISK GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Risk groups are classifications of prostate cancer from very low to very high risk, based on clinical characteristics like PSA level, biopsy results, and tumor stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk groups categorize prostate cancer patients based on factors like PSA, Gleason score, and stage to guide treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk groups classify patients based on factors like genetic changes and response to treatment, helping to determine the intensity of therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A port is a small disc placed under the skin in the upper chest to receive intravenous chemotherapy, inserted during minor surgery and removed after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A port is a small, round disc placed in the chest to deliver systemic therapy, fluids, and blood products into the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"A port is a small, round disc placed under the skin to receive intravenous chemotherapy, as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"A port is a small, round disc usually placed in the chest to deliver systemic therapy, fluids, and blood products into the body. The type and location are tailored to the patient's needs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESOPHAGOGASTRIC JUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The esophagogastric junction (EGJ), also called gastroesophageal junction (GEJ), is where the esophagus meets the stomach, just beneath the diaphragm, separating esophageal contents from stomach acid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPPORTIVE CARE RADIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Supportive care radiation is radiation therapy used to ease pain or discomfort caused by cancer, not for curative purposes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PET-CT SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PET-CT scan is a combined imaging technique that merges PET and CT to provide detailed anatomical and functional information. It can be performed with one or two machines depending on the cancer center."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHOLESTEROL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cholesterol is a component of bile, produced by the liver."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARANASAL SINUSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The paranasal sinuses are part of the nasal cavity area and a potential site for head and neck cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The paranasal sinuses are spaces near the nasal cavity, and they are a location where head and neck cancers can occur."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL SCAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A small scar is a potential outcome of any skin biopsy, resulting from the healing process after tissue removal."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROIDECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thyroidectomy is a surgical procedure to remove all or part of the thyroid gland, often performed as part of thyroid cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUMBERED STAGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Numbered stages are classifications (e.g., stage I-IV) that summarize cancer extent based on TNM scores."&lt;SEP&gt;"Numbered stages range from stage 0 to stage 4, based on TNM scores, and are used to describe the extent of cancer progression."&lt;SEP&gt;"Numbered stages range from stage 0 to stage 4, with stage 0 being noninvasive, stages 1-3 invasive, and stage 4 metastatic, based on TNM scores and receptor status."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIGHT SWEATS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A symptom of surgical menopause involving excessive sweating during sleep."&lt;SEP&gt;"Night Sweats are excessive sweating during sleep that drenches sheets, a B symptom of CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Night sweats are a symptom of CLL, involving excessive sweating during sleep."&lt;SEP&gt;"Night sweats are a symptom of menopause, including surgical menopause, involving excessive sweating during sleep."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-ALL RISK GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-ALL risk groups are classifications based on genetic and clinical features that help determine treatment intensity."&lt;SEP&gt;"B-ALL risk groups categorize patients with B-ALL based on genetic and clinical features to guide treatment intensity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLADRIBINE (MAVENCLAD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cladribine (Mavenclad) is an antimetabolite chemotherapy drug used to treat AML by preventing DNA building blocks from being used."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESOPHAGEAL SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Esophageal squamous cell carcinoma (ESCC) starts in thin, flat cells in the inner lining of the esophagus, often found in the upper and middle esophagus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYSTEMIC THERAPY EXAMPLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Systemic therapy examples include chemotherapy, HER2-targeted therapy, inhibitors, immunotherapy, and endocrine therapy, used based on receptor expression."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SODIUM FLUORIDE PET-CT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sodium fluoride PET-CT is a specific type of PET-CT scan that may be used instead of a bone scan to detect bone abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sodium fluoride PET-CT is a specific type of PET-CT scan that uses a radiotracer made of sodium fluoride, often used as an alternative to a bone scan to detect bone abnormalities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BILIRUBIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A substance produced by the liver, measured in liver function tests to evaluate liver function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bilirubin is a component of bile, produced from the breakdown of red blood cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HARD PALATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The hard palate is the bone forming the roof of the mouth, above which the nasal cavity lies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hard palate is the bony roof of the mouth, where mouth cancer can occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hard palate is the hard, bony part of the roof of the mouth, covered by keratinized squamous epithelium, and is a site where mouth cancer can develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hard palate is the hard, front part of the roof of the mouth behind the teeth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENT TYPES OF SCARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Different types of scars can result from various biopsy methods, and patients should discuss scarring risks with their doctor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECOND OPINION DOCTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Second Opinion Doctor is a medical professional consulted by the patient to confirm diagnosis or treatment plan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLADDER MUSCLE LAYER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bladder muscle layer is the muscular wall of the bladder that cancer cells may invade as the disease progresses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESECTABLE TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Resectable tumor refers to a tumor that can be completely removed with surgery, as defined in the context of cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weight Loss is unintended loss of body weight, a B symptom of CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight loss is a sign of inadequate nutrition that treatment teams monitor during and after cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUESTIONS TO ASK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Questions to Ask is a section at the end of each chapter in the book, providing suggested questions for patients to ask their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Questions to ask are a list of patient queries about cancer type, prognosis, tests, insurance, and next steps."&lt;SEP&gt;"Questions to ask are suggested queries provided in each chapter of the NCCN Guidelines to help patients get more information about their care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Questions to ask are suggested questions provided at the end of each chapter in the NCCN patient guide to help patients and families get more information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Questions to ask is a section at the end of each chapter in the ALL book, providing suggested questions for patients and families to ask the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Questions to ask is a section in each chapter of the NCCN Guidelines for Patients that provides suggested questions for patients to ask their care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"Questions to ask is a section in the patient guide that provides suggested questions for patients to ask their care team about their CLL management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLOFARABINE (CLOLAR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clofarabine (Clolar) is an antimetabolite chemotherapy drug used to treat AML by preventing DNA building blocks from being used."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESOPHAGEAL ADENOCARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Esophageal adenocarcinoma (EAC) starts in mucus-making cells of the inner lining of the esophagus, often found in the lower esophagus, and is common in North America and Western Europe."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMOTHERAPY EXAMPLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemotherapy examples include drugs like capecitabine, carboplatin, and paclitaxel, used to kill cancer cells throughout the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FDG PET-CT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FDG PET-CT is a type of PET-CT scan using the radiotracer F-18 fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG), made of fluoride and glucose. It requires fasting for at least 4 hours before the scan and is useful when other imaging results are unclear, helping to find cancer in lymph nodes and distant sites."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POTASSIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Potassium is a salt component found in bile."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TONGUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The tongue includes several muscles that extend from the hyoid bone to the floor of the mouth. The base of the tongue is part of the oropharynx."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tongue is a muscular organ in the mouth that aids in chewing, speaking, and breathing. The front two-thirds of the tongue is a site for mouth cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tongue, specifically the front two-thirds, is a common site for mouth cancer development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACCURATE DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Accurate diagnosis is the goal of biopsy, requiring removal of as much of the suspected area as possible for reliable testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLADDER REMOVAL SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bladder removal surgery is a treatment for bladder cancer that can cause side effects such as bleeding, blood clots, kidney problems, infection, sexual dysfunction, and incontinence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER SURVIVORSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer survivorship encompasses care for healthy living and late/long-term effects, with resources available from NCCN."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPERM DAMAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sperm Damage is a potential effect of cancer treatment on male fertility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERTIFIED NURSE MIDWIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Certified nurse midwife is an advanced practice provider who can help prevent, evaluate, examine, and diagnose diseases including breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNRESECTABLE TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unresectable tumor is a tumor that cannot be completely removed with surgery due to involvement of major vessels or critical structures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIBLINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Siblings are first-degree relatives whose health history is relevant to CLL risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Siblings are immediate blood relatives whose health history is key for risk assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVOCACY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Advocacy involves actively supporting a patient's care by asking questions and making shared decisions with the care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUDARABINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fludarabine is an antimetabolite chemotherapy drug used to treat AML by interfering with DNA synthesis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fludarabine is an antimetabolite chemotherapy drug used to treat AML by preventing DNA building blocks from being used."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BARRETT ESOPHAGUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Barrett esophagus (BE) is a condition where squamous cells in the lower esophagus are replaced by abnormal cells due to chronic reflux, increasing risk of adenocarcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INHIBITOR EXAMPLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inhibitor examples include CDK4/6, mTOR, and PARP inhibitors like abemaciclib and olaparib, used to block cancer growth pathways."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FES PET-CT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FES PET-CT is a type of PET-CT scan that uses a radioactive form of the hormone estrogen, used instead of FDG PET-CT when cancer is estrogen receptor-positive."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SODIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sodium is a salt component found in bile."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUCUS MEMBRANES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mucus membranes are thin, flat cells that line the mouth, nose, and throat, where squamous cell carcinoma forms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL PRICK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A small prick is the sensation felt when a needle injects numbing medicine into the skin before a biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONLINE RESOURCE ACCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Online Resource Access is visiting NCCN.org for guidelines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MODIFIED DCF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Modified DCF is a chemotherapy regimen combining docetaxel, cisplatin, and fluorouracil, used as first-line therapy for metastatic anal cancer, after which chemoradiation is generally not considered."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOUTH CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mouth Cancer is a type of cancer affecting the mouth, with staging based on tumor size, lymph node spread, and metastasis, and is the focus of the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth cancer is a type of cancer mentioned in the text, though not detailed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth cancer refers to squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) of the mouth, including mucosa of the lip, with specific TNM staging information provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth cancer, also known as oral cancer or oral cavity cancer, is a type of cancer that affects the lips, front two-thirds of the tongue, gums, lining inside the cheeks and lips, floor of the mouth, hard palate, alveolar ridge, and retromolar trigone. It is a type of head and neck cancer and typically starts in squamous cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth cancer, also known as oral cancer, is a type of cancer that develops in the oral cavity, including the lips, buccal mucosa, tongue, gums, floor of the mouth, hard palate, and retromolar trigone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Parents are first-degree relatives whose health history is relevant to CLL risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Parents are immediate blood relatives whose health history is key for risk assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHARED DECISIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shared decisions are collaborative choices made between patients, families, and the care team regarding treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shared decisions refer to the collaborative process between patients and their care team in making treatment choices."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DAUNORUBICIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Daunorubicin is a chemotherapy drug used in combination with other agents to treat AML with core binding factor abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daunorubicin is an anthracycline chemotherapy drug used to treat AML by damaging DNA and causing cell death."&lt;SEP&gt;"Daunorubicin is an anthracycline chemotherapy drug used to treat AML, often in combination with other drugs like cytarabine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIEWERT TYPES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Siewert types are used in cancer staging to describe the location of a tumor relative to the esophagus and stomach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNOTHERAPY EXAMPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immunotherapy example includes pembrolizumab, used to enhance the immune system's ability to fight cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORE BIOPSY (CB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Core biopsy (CB) is a type of biopsy that uses a larger needle to remove a sample of tissue, often guided by imaging such as ultrasound or mammography."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Water is a component of bile, making up a significant portion of its composition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-VOLUME CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A high-volume center is a hospital or treatment facility with experience in treating a specific type of cancer, recommended for head and neck cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"A high-volume center is a hospital with experience in treating head and neck cancers, recommended for treatment when possible."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPERFICIAL SHAVE BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A superficial shave biopsy is a type of skin biopsy that removes the top layer of skin, useful for very flat lesions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic nodes are the closest lymph nodes to the cervix, where cervical cancer generally spreads first."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSOLUBLE FIBER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insoluble fiber is a type of dietary fiber that helps manage bowel movements, often recommended for anal cancer survivors to address fecal incontinence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insoluble fiber, found in certain foods, can help manage bowel problems like frequency and urgency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGE 44&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Age of diagnosis for a patient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Age."&lt;SEP&gt;"The age at which a patient was diagnosed with colon cancer in the ER, as described in a personal narrative."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA (SCC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) is the most common type of nasopharyngeal cancer, forming in the thin, flat cells of the mucus membranes of the nasopharynx. It is the focus of the book."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) is the most common type of nasopharyngeal cancer, forming in the thin, flat squamous cells that line the nasopharynx. It is the focus of the text regarding nasopharyngeal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell carcinoma is a type of cancer that starts in the squamous cells lining the inside of the mouth, as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell carcinoma is the most common type of mouth cancer, forming in the thin, flat cells of the mucous membranes of the mouth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell carcinoma is the most common type of mouth cancer, starting in the squamous cells that form the surface lining of the mouth. It is the focus of the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRANDPARENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grandparents are blood relatives whose health history can inform cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grandparents are second-degree relatives whose health history is relevant to CLL risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Care refers to the medical treatment and support provided to patients, which can be improved through active patient involvement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Care refers to the overall management of a patient's health, including cancer treatment and supportive measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Care refers to the overall management of a patient's health, including treatment, supportive care, and follow-up."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IDARUBICIN (IDAMYCIN PFS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Idarubicin (Idamycin PFS) is an anthracycline chemotherapy drug used to treat AML by damaging DNA and causing cell death."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORTH AMERICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"North America is a geographic region where esophageal adenocarcinoma is more common."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2-TARGETED THERAPY EXAMPLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HER2-targeted therapy examples include antibodies, inhibitors, and conjugates like trastuzumab and pertuzumab, used for HER2-positive cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VACUUM-ASSISTED CORE BIOPSY (VACB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vacuum-assisted core biopsy (VACB) is a type of biopsy that uses suction to remove a tissue sample with a special vacuum device."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROPATHOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A neuropathologist is a specialist who tests tissue samples for biomarkers to diagnose and characterize gliomas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neuropathologist is a specialist who examines tissue samples under a microscope to classify tumors, determine malignancy, and perform molecular testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCCHN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SCCHN (Squamous Cell Carcinoma of the Head and Neck) is the most common type of head and neck cancer, forming in the mucus membranes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAT SKIN LESIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flat skin lesions are lesions that do not protrude significantly from the skin surface, suitable for superficial shave biopsies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thyrogen (thyrotropin alfa) is a hormone injection used to increase TSH levels in patients undergoing RAI therapy, allowing continuation of thyroid hormone replacement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMICALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemicals are substances in the blood measured by tests like comprehensive metabolic panel, which can indicate organ function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemicals are substances measured in LFTs to assess liver function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chemicals in the body, such as electrolytes, are balanced by the kidneys through filtration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MITOXANTRONE (NOVANTRONE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mitoxantrone (Novantrone) is an anthracycline chemotherapy drug used to treat AML by damaging DNA and causing cell death."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WESTERN EUROPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Western Europe is a geographic region where esophageal adenocarcinoma is more common."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOSIMILARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biosimilars are similar versions of biologic drugs like trastuzumab, used as substitutes in HER2-targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY (CNB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Core needle biopsy (CNB) is a biopsy procedure using a larger needle to remove a core of tissue for cancer diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Core needle biopsy (CNB) is a biopsy technique using a larger needle to remove a core of tissue from a tumor or lymph node for pathological examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Core needle biopsy (CNB) is a biopsy technique using a larger needle to remove a core sample of tissue from a tumor or lymph node."&lt;SEP&gt;"Core needle biopsy (CNB) is a type of biopsy that removes more than one tissue sample through the same area on the breast, using a needle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASTROCYTOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Astrocytoma is a type of glioma that resembles astrocytes, often classified by biomarkers and grade, such as IDH-mutant grade 2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HNSCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HNSCC (Head and Neck Squamous Cell Carcinoma) is another term for SCCHN, the most common type of head and neck cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAZOR-LIKE TOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A razor-like tool is used in shave biopsies to remove the top layer of skin and part of the dermis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC RADIATION SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic Radiation Specialist is a radiation oncologist with expertise in treating pelvic cancers, including anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOWER ABDOMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lower abdomen is the region of the body where the bladder and pelvis are situated."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEPTH OF INVASION (DOI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Depth of invasion is a measure of how deep a tumor has grown into tissue layers, increasing the risk of lymph node metastases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depth of invasion is a measure of how deep a tumor has grown through the layers of the oral mucosa, important for staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIDNEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kidney is a part of the body where cancer can originate and spread to bone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kidney is an organ whose function is assessed through blood tests, which may be affected by CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kidneys are organs on which adrenal glands are located, and they play a role in the body's endocrine system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kidneys are organs that filter waste from the blood. They may appear bright on PET scans and their function is considered when using contrast material."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHILD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A child is a young patient, particularly relevant in ALL treatment, as the guide focuses on pediatric leukemia."&lt;SEP&gt;"A child is an individual who may inherit leukemia predisposition syndromes from biological parents, affecting risk and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CPX-351 (VYXEOS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CPX-351 (Vyxeos) is a dual-drug liposome formulation containing cytarabine and daunorubicin, used to treat AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EASTERN EUROPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eastern Europe is a geographic region where squamous cell carcinoma is more common."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMBINATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Combination therapy involves using multiple treatments together, such as trastuzumab with pertuzumab, to enhance efficacy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEREOTACTIC NEEDLE BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stereotactic needle biopsy is a type of biopsy guided by mammography, used to sample breast tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLIGODENDROGLIOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oligodendroglioma is a type of glioma that resembles oligodendrocytes, identified through histologic analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SCC (Squamous Cell Carcinoma) is the most common type of throat cancer and is the focus of the book."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAND-HELD TOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hand-held tool is used in punch biopsies to remove a small piece of skin and connective tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEXUAL DYSFUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sexual dysfunction is a potential long-term effect of cancer treatment, addressed in survivorship care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sexual dysfunction is a side effect of bladder cancer treatment or the cancer itself, including decreased desire or ability to have sex."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGAN FUNCTION ASSESSMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organ Function Assessment is the evaluation of kidney and liver health through blood tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERSONS ASSIGNED FEMALE AT BIRTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Persons assigned female at birth are individuals who are more frequently affected by breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tis is a TNM staging category for carcinoma in situ, where cancerous cells are found only in the squamous cell layer of the nasopharynx."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tis refers to carcinoma in situ, an early stage of cancer where abnormal cells are present but have not spread, specifically an intraductal tumor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tis refers to carcinoma in situ, where cancerous cells are found only in the squamous cell layer, as a stage of mouth cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLAPARIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Olaparib (Lynparza) is a PARP inhibitor used for breast cancer with BRCA1/BRCA2 mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Olaparib (Lynparza) is a PARP inhibitor used in systemic therapy to treat cancer by exploiting DNA repair defects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Olaparib is a PARP inhibitor used in maintenance therapy for ovarian cancer, typically continued for up to 2 years total."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A parent is a caregiver who advocates for their child's care and makes shared decisions with the care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AZACITIDINE (VIDAZA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Azacitidine (Vidaza) is a hypomethylating agent used to treat AML by blocking methyl groups from binding to DNA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Asia is a geographic region where NPC most often occurs, indicating a higher prevalence in certain populations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Asia is a geographic region where nasopharyngeal cancer most often occurs, as noted in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Asia is a geographic region where squamous cell carcinoma is more common."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRASTUZUMAB SUBSTITUTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trastuzumab substitutes are biosimilars like Kanjinti, Ogivri, Herzuma, Ontruzant, and Trazimera, used in HER2-targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AXILLARY LYMPH NODE NEEDLE BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Axillary lymph node needle biopsy is a procedure to biopsy a lymph node near the armpit to determine if abnormal lymph nodes contain cancer cells. It may use ultrasound-guided fine-needle aspiration or core biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT IMAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CT (Computed Tomography) imaging is a medical imaging technology used with navigation systems to target tumor samples during biopsies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY (ALL GENDERS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility (all genders) is a health consideration addressed during treatment planning for throat cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPENING IN THE SKIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An opening in the skin is created during punch or excision biopsies and is often closed with stitches."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY INFORMATION SEEKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility Information Seeking is looking up resources on fertility preservation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECTUS ABDOMINIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The rectus abdominis is a muscle in the lower abdomen, along with skin, fat, and blood vessels, often used for muscle flap reconstruction after APR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T1 is a TNM staging category indicating the tumor is confined to the nasopharynx or has grown into the oropharynx and/or nasal cavity, but not into the parapharyngeal space."&lt;SEP&gt;"T1 is a tumor size category in the TNM system, indicating the tumor is 2 cm or less in greatest dimension."&lt;SEP&gt;"T1 is a tumor stage where the tumor is 2 cm or less with DOI of 5 mm or less, as per TNM staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIRAPARIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Niraparib is a PARP inhibitor used alone as maintenance therapy for ovarian cancer, typically given for up to 3 years."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NURSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nurse is a healthcare professional who provides direct patient care and supports the care team."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nurse is a healthcare professional who provides direct patient care, including administering treatments and monitoring side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nurse is a healthcare professional who, in this context, was unaware that breast cancer could occur without a lump, highlighting a knowledge gap."&lt;SEP&gt;"A nurse provides care and support to breast cancer patients, including administering treatments and educating patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nurse is a health care professional who assists in patient care, communication, and monitoring during treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nurse is a healthcare professional who assists in patient care, including managing side effects and providing support during treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nurse is a healthcare professional who may assist during exams and provide support in patient care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRATHECAL CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intrathecal chemotherapy involves injecting drugs like cytarabine or methotrexate into the spinal fluid to treat AML in the brain or spine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intrathecal chemotherapy is a method of administering chemotherapy drugs directly into the spinal fluid, used in the treatment of certain cancers like leukemia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intrathecal chemotherapy is a method of delivering chemotherapy directly into the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) when cancer cells are found there or in the spine, as an alternative to systemic IV administration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intrathecal chemotherapy is a type of chemotherapy where drugs are infused directly into the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) to treat cancer cells found there, used in select cases or as part of treatment for primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AFRICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Africa is a geographic region where squamous cell carcinoma is more common."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHESGO SUBSTITUTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phesgo is a substitute for combination therapy of trastuzumab with pertuzumab, used in HER2-targeted systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A breast specialist is a medical professional with expertise in breast conditions, including inflammatory breast cancer, and can provide referrals for difficult diagnoses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Breast specialist is an expert in breast health and disease, providing specialized care and diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Breast specialist is an expert in breast health and disease, providing specialized care and guidance in diagnosis and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRANIOTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Craniotomy is a surgical procedure involving the removal of a piece of skull bone to access the brain, used in open biopsies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREVENTING PREGNANCY DURING TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Preventing pregnancy during treatment is a health consideration for patients undergoing cancer therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Preventing pregnancy during treatment is important to avoid harm to a developing baby, using birth control methods like IUDs or barrier methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Use of birth control methods, such as hormonal contraceptives, IUDs, or barrier methods, to avoid pregnancy during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PART OF THE LESION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Part of the lesion may be removed during excision biopsy, depending on the size and depth of the suspicious area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARA-AORTIC NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Para-aortic nodes are lymph nodes in the abdomen that may be removed and tested if cancer has spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOLUBLE FIBER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soluble fiber is a type of dietary fiber that can help with bowel regulation, but is less emphasized than insoluble fiber for anal cancer survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEDDING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A personal event mentioned in the text, occurring 58 days before the patient's diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"A personal event mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Event."&lt;SEP&gt;"Personal event mentioned in text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T2 is a TNM staging category indicating the tumor has grown into the parapharyngeal space and/or nearby soft tissue such as the medial pterygoid, lateral pterygoid, and prevertebral muscles."&lt;SEP&gt;"T2 is a tumor size category in the TNM system, indicating the tumor is more than 2 cm but not more than 5 cm."&lt;SEP&gt;"T2 is a tumor stage where the tumor is 2 cm or less with DOI more than 5 mm, or between 2 cm and 4 cm with DOI of or less."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUCAPARIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rucaparib is a PARP inhibitor used alone as maintenance therapy for ovarian cancer, typically given for up to 2 years."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specialist is a healthcare professional with expertise in a specific area, such as an ALL specialist or oncologist."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTI-AGENT CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Multi-agent chemotherapy, or a multi-agent regimen, combines multiple chemotherapy drugs to treat AML, each working differently."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutritional assessment is a test to evaluate a patient's nutritional health during cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"American Cancer Society is a national organization providing resources and information on anal cancer, including a website for patient guidance."&lt;SEP&gt;"American Cancer Society is a national organization providing resources and information on cancer, including anal cancer, through its website cancer.org."&lt;SEP&gt;"American Cancer Society is an organization that educates about cancer and testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The American Cancer Society is an organization that provides resources, support, and research funding for cancer, including breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The American Cancer Society provides education, support, and research funding for cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUMPECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure to remove a tumor from the breast, during which a sentinel lymph node biopsy may be done."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lumpectomy is a surgical procedure to remove a tumor from the breast, often performed to treat breast cancer, and may be accompanied by sentinel lymph node biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lumpectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the tumor and a small margin of surrounding tissue, preserving the breast."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASTROCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Astrocytes are glial cells in the brain that resemble astrocytoma tumor cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Astrocytes are star-shaped glial cells that maintain the chemical environment for communication between nerve cells, and they are the origin of astrocytomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAD AND NECK EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specific physical exam focusing on the head and neck, including palpation of the oral cavity and use of mirrors or fiberoptic scopes to view hard-to-see areas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALL OF THE LESION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"All of the lesion may be removed during excision biopsy to ensure complete removal of potentially cancerous tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROTROPIN ALFA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thyrotropin alfa is a synthetic form of TSH used to stimulate iodine uptake in thyroid cells for RAI therapy or imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVORSHIP CARE FOR HEALTHY LIVING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survivorship Care for Healthy Living is a resource from NCCN addressing lifestyle and wellness topics for cancer survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREFERRED THERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Preferred therapies are treatment options with the most evidence that they work better and may be safer than other therapies for AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T3 is a tumor size category in the TNM system, indicating the tumor is more than 5 cm."&lt;SEP&gt;"T3 is a tumor stage where the tumor is between 2 cm and 4 cm with DOI more than or larger than 4 cm with DOI of or less."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARP INHIBITOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PARP inhibitors are a class of drugs used in maintenance therapy for ovarian cancer, including olaparib, niraparib, and rucaparib, to delay cancer growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEDIATRIC ONCOLOGIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pediatric oncologist is a doctor who specializes in treating cancer in children, such as ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESOPHAGEAL WALL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The esophageal wall is composed of four main layers: mucosa, submucosa, muscularis propria, and tunica adventitia, which are involved in cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL CANCER FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anal Cancer Foundation is an organization dedicated to supporting individuals affected by anal cancer, offering resources and advocacy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anal Cancer Foundation is an organization dedicated to supporting patients with anal cancer and providing educational resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Anal Cancer Foundation is an organization that offers peer-to-peer support programs, matching patients and caregivers with trained volunteers for emotional and practical support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;F-18 FLUORODEOXYGLUCOSE (FDG)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"F-18 fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG) is a radiotracer used in FDG PET-CT scans, made of fluoride and glucose, which helps detect cancer by highlighting areas of high metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"F-18 fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG) is a radiotracer used in FDG-PET/CT scans, made of fluoride and glucose, to detect cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLIGODENDROCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oligodendrocytes are glial cells in the brain that resemble oligodendroglioma tumor cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oligodendrocytes are glial cells that protect electrical signaling in nerve cells, and they are the origin of oligodendrogliomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOCRINE TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood tests to assess thyroid and pituitary gland function, which may be affected by radiation therapy to the head and neck."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endocrine tests are blood tests to assess hormone levels, particularly thyroid and pituitary, before and after radiation therapy to the head and neck."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL BINDER OR NOTEBOOK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical binder or notebook is a tool for organizing medical information, test results, and treatment plans, helping patients manage their care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV Specialist is a healthcare provider focused on HPV-related conditions, including anal cancer prevention and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Orange is used as a size comparison for the bladder when empty, approximately the size of an orange."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTHER RECOMMENDED THERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Other recommended therapies may not work as well as preferred therapies but can still help treat AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Other recommended therapies may not work quite as well as preferred therapies but can still help treat AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T4A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T4a is moderately advanced local disease, where the tumor is more than 4 cm with DOI more than or invades nearby structures like cortical bone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECTAL TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A rectal tumor is a growth of cancer cells in the rectum, which can invade surrounding tissues and spread to other organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUCUS-MAKING CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mucus-making cells are cells in the inner lining of the esophagus where adenocarcinoma starts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mucus-making cells line the alveoli and are the origin of adenocarcinoma, a common subtype of NSCLC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER HOPE NETWORK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Hope Network is a non-profit organization that provides free, one-on-one support to cancer patients and their families."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer Hope Network offers support services and resources for cancer patients, including those with anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SODIUM FLUORIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sodium fluoride is a radiotracer used in sodium fluoride PET-CT scans, which is particularly effective for imaging bone abnormalities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IDH GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IDH gene is a genetic mutation that serves as a biomarker for certain gliomas, such as astrocytoma IDH-mutant."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPEECH AND SWALLOWING ASSESSMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An evaluation by a speech or swallowing therapist to test abilities before and after treatment for head and neck cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Speech and swallowing assessment tests a patient's ability to speak and swallow before and after treatment, conducted by a therapist."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEST X-RAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chest X-ray is a fast, painless imaging test using small amounts of radiation to check if cancer has spread to the lungs, used in diagnosis and treatment monitoring."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINARY INCONTINENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urinary incontinence is the inability to hold urine, a possible side effect of radiation therapy for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urinary incontinence is the involuntary leakage of urine, a common side effect after bladder cancer surgery, manageable with pelvic floor exercises."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urinary incontinence is the involuntary leakage of urine, a condition that can be managed with pelvic floor exercises and other interventions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urinary incontinence is the involuntary leakage of urine, a potential side effect of neobladder construction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER SPREAD DETECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Spread Detection is the process of identifying metastasis through tests like ALP and bone scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERSONS ASSIGNED MALE AT BIRTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Persons assigned male at birth can also develop breast cancer, including inflammatory breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERAPIES USED IN CERTAIN CASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Therapies used in certain cases work best for people with specific cancer features or health circumstances in AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T4B&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T4b is very advanced local disease, where the tumor has invaded the masticator space, pterygoid plates, or skull base and/or encases the internal carotid artery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2 OVARIAN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 2 ovarian cancer is a specific stage of ovarian cancer where cancer has spread beyond the ovaries but is still within the pelvis, with limited research on maintenance therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLORECTAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A broader term for cancer of the colon or rectum, with screening and treatment discussed in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"A broader term for cancer of the colon or rectum."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of cancer associated with inherited mutations in genes like MSH2, MSH6, MLH1, and PMS2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Broader term for cancer of colon or rectum."&lt;SEP&gt;"Broader term."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colorectal cancer is a broader term for cancers of the colon and rectum, often starting in polyps."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colorectal cancer is a term for cancers in the colon or rectum, with different treatments for each."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colorectal cancer is a term used to describe cancers that form in either the colon or rectum, with similar but distinct treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colorectal cancer is a type of cancer that anal cancer survivors are at risk for and should be screened."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colorectal cancer is a type of cancer that can be associated with BRCA mutations, increasing risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colorectal cancer is a type of cancer that can be related to germline mutations in genes like MSH2, MSH6, MLH1, and PMS2, and is mentioned as a family history factor for germline testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colorectal cancer is a type of cancer that starts in the colon or rectum, often in glandular cells, and is distinct from anal squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colorectal cancer is a type of cancer that, when present in close blood relatives, increases the risk of pancreatic cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colorectal cancer is a type of cancer; a personal or family history may be relevant to thyroid cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRONIC REFLUX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chronic reflux is a condition that can lead to Barrett esophagus by causing changes in the esophageal lining."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER.NET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer.Net is a resource from the American Society of Clinical Oncology providing information on various cancer types, including anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer.Net is a resource provided by the American Society of Clinical Oncology, offering information on various cancer types, including anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUCOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glucose is a simple sugar that forms part of FDG, used to detect cancer metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a simple sugar that is a component of FDG, used in PET scans to track metabolic activity in tissues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a simple sugar used in the production of FDG and is taken up by cancer cells, as detected in PET scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a simple sugar used in the production of FDG, a radiotracer for PET scans, and is metabolized by cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade 1 is a follicular lymphoma grade with fewer centroblasts, treated as classic FL according to ICC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grade 1 is a low-grade tumor classification indicating slow growth and usually benign nature, common in children."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHANGES IN FERTILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Changes in fertility refer to temporary or permanent impairment of reproductive ability due to cancer treatment, influenced by age, treatment type, dose, and length."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary or permanent impairment of fertility due to cancer treatment, influenced by age, treatment type, dose, and length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAGNOSTIC LAPAROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diagnostic laparoscopy is a minimally invasive procedure involving a tiny cut in the abdomen and a laparoscope to view the lining and organs, used to assess cancer extent and guide treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER TREATMENT EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Treatment Education is learning about therapies and side effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIRST-LINE THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"First-line therapy is the initial treatment for metastatic anal cancer, which is platinum-based chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STANDARD OF CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Standard of care includes biomarker testing for certain cancers like breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Standard of care is the best-known way to treat AML based on past clinical trials, with possibly more than one regimen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Standard of care refers to the best known treatment for a particular disease based on past clinical trials, and there may be multiple standard treatment regimens."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGIONAL LYMPH NODE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Regional lymph nodes are lymph nodes found near the tumor, and cancer found in them is a lymph node metastasis, distinct from distant metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVEILLANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surveillance involves follow-up testing after treatment to detect new cancer growth early, including colonoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surveillance involves regular check-ups, including flexible sigmoidoscopy, imaging, and colonoscopy, to monitor for recurrence of rectal cancer after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surveillance involves regular monitoring after treatment to detect any recurrence of colon cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surveillance involves regular monitoring after treatment to detect recurrence of ovarian cancer, including imaging and blood tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surveillance involves regular monitoring, including imaging and exams, after recurrence treatment to detect any further cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surveillance is a monitoring approach for cervical cancer after treatment, to check for recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surveillance is the ongoing monitoring process for cancer recurrence, involving regular physical exams, blood tests, and imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surveillance refers to follow-up testing started when there are no signs of cancer after treatment, aimed at finding new cancer growth early."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surveillance refers to regular follow-up appointments with an oncologist after treatment to monitor for signs of cancer recurrence, including physical and pelvic exams and possible blood tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surveillance refers to the ongoing monitoring of patients after treatment to detect any recurrence or progression of cervical cancer. It is a standard part of post-treatment care."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of monitoring for cancer recurrence after treatment, sometimes using biomarker tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of regular follow-up testing and physical exams after cervical cancer treatment to detect early signs of recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARGE BOWEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Large bowel is the lower part of the digestive tract, including the colon and rectum, ending at the anus."&lt;SEP&gt;"The large bowel includes the colon and rectum, where polyps and cancers can develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"The large bowel includes the rectum and colon, examined via colonoscopy for GI health."&lt;SEP&gt;"The large bowel is another term for the large intestine, which includes the colon and rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCOREGIONAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Locoregional or locally advanced esophageal cancer has invaded the esophagus wall and/or spread to nearby lymph nodes or organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCERCARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CancerCare is a national organization providing free, professional support services to anyone affected by cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"CancerCare is an organization providing support, resources, and information for cancer patients and their families."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CT (Computed Tomography) is an imaging procedure used to detect cancer recurrence or metastasis in the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"CT (Computed Tomography) is an imaging technique used to guide placement of brachytherapy applicators and design treatment plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"CT (Computed Tomography) is an imaging test that uses X-rays to create cross-sectional images, useful for assessing cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"CT (computed tomography) is a type of scan that uses x-rays and computer technology to take detailed pictures of the inside of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"CT (computed tomography) is an imaging technique that is combined with PET to create PET/CT scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"CT (computed tomography) is an imaging technique that provides detailed cross-sectional images of the body, often combined with PET for PET-CT scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"CT (computed tomography) is an imaging technology used in urogram and chest imaging to create detailed cross-sectional images for cancer detection and staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"CT (computed tomography) is an imaging test that uses contrast material to produce detailed pictures of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"CT is a type of imaging test."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE 2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade 2 is a follicular lymphoma grade with a mixture of centrocytes and centroblasts, treated as classic FL according to ICC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Grade 2 is a low-grade tumor classification indicating somewhat abnormal cells that grow slowly and can invade normal tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIETITIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A dietitian is a healthcare professional specializing in nutrition, particularly for cancer survivors, helping manage dietary needs and bowel changes after anal cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A dietitian provides nutritional guidance to support breast cancer patients during treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A professional who provides dietary recommendations to support patients during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dietitians provide nutrition advice to help manage bowel changes after anal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATIC MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somatic mutations are genetic changes in tumor tissue, not inherited, and are tested in biomarker analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Somatic mutations are tumor-specific mutations in BRCA and related genes, tested separately from germline mutations to inform treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRE-TREATMENT SURGICAL STAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pre-treatment surgical staging involves removing and testing pelvic and/or para-aortic lymph nodes before treatment to guide decisions for advanced cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIBER SUPPLEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fiber supplements are products used to increase dietary fiber intake, aiding in stool management for those with bowel changes after anal cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fiber supplements, such as psyllium-based products, help slow and thicken stool to manage bowel changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGE 50&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Age by which cancer often develops in classic FAP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Age."&lt;SEP&gt;"The age by which cancer often develops in people with classic FAP."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREMENOPAUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Premenopause is a stage in a woman's life when the ovaries are the main source of estrogen and progesterone, and menstrual periods may stop during treatment (amenorrhea) and for up to 2 years after, but often return in those 35 years of age and under."&lt;SEP&gt;"Premenopause refers to the phase when ovaries are the main source of estrogen and progesterone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH NODE METASTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph node metastasis is cancer that has spread to regional lymph nodes, as opposed to distant metastasis outside the neck."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph node metastasis is the spread of breast cancer to lymph nodes, often in the axilla or distant sites."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stool is the waste product of digestion that is held in the rectum and exits through the anus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stool is the waste product that passes through the colon and exits the body, affected by blockages and colostomies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARTERIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arteries are blood vessels that can be invaded by esophageal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER SUPPORT COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Support Community is an organization offering support groups, education, and resources for cancer patients and survivors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer Support Community offers emotional and social support services for cancer patients and survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAMMOGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A mammogram is an X-ray of the breast used for screening and diagnosis of breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mammogram is a type of imaging test using low dose x-rays to examine the breast, available in 2D digital or 3D tomosynthesis forms, used for breast cancer screening and diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mammogram is an imaging technique using low-dose x-rays to examine the breast, sometimes used to guide biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mammogram is an imaging test used to detect breast cancer by taking X-ray pictures of the breast."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE 3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade 3 is a high-grade tumor classification indicating more abnormal cells and faster growth, mentioned in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWALLOWING THERAPIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A professional who evaluates and treats swallowing difficulties related to head and neck cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPUTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Computer is a machine that combines images from CT scans to create 3-D pictures for detailed analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUCLEAR MEDICINE SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nuclear medicine specialist is a medical professional who uses radioactive substances for diagnostic imaging and therapeutic purposes, such as RAI therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVORSHIP CARE FOR CANCER-RELATED LATE AND LONG-TERM EFFECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survivorship Care for Cancer-Related Late and Long-Term Effects is a resource from NCCN addressing long-term health issues after cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRANODAL EXTENSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Extranodal extension is another term for extracapsular extension, where cancer grows through the protective outer layer of lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extranodal extension refers to cancer that has grown through and spread outside of the lymph node, also called extranodal extension-positive."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATINUM-RESISTANT CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Platinum-resistant cancer is ovarian cancer that does not improve or worsens during platinum-based chemotherapy or returns within 6 months, requiring non-platinum chemotherapy or targeted therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGESTED FOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Digested food is the material that moves through the colon and becomes stool in the rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer that affects the central nervous system, specifically the brain and spinal cord, and is the focus of the diagnostic and treatment discussions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary CNS lymphoma is a rare and aggressive cancer that most often affects the brain, but can also occur in the spinal cord, cerebrospinal fluid, and/or the eyes. It is an abnormal overgrowth of lymphocytes and can cause neurological symptoms such as weakness, coordination problems, personality changes, memory issues, and seizures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary CNS lymphoma is a rare and aggressive cancer that starts in the central nervous system, specifically in lymphocytes in the brain and spinal cord, and can spread to the eyes and cerebrospinal fluid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary CNS lymphoma is a rare type of non-Hodgkin lymphoma that affects the brain, spinal cord, and eyes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary CNS lymphoma is a type of cancer affecting the central nervous system, for which various treatments including chemotherapy, radiation, and stem cell rescue are used."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary CNS lymphoma is a type of cancer mentioned in the text, though not detailed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary CNS lymphoma is a type of cancer that affects the central nervous system, including the brain and spinal cord. It is characterized by the presence of lymphoma cells in the CNS and requires specific diagnostic procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary CNS lymphoma is a type of cancer that affects the central nervous system, including the brain and spinal cord. Treatment involves a two-step process of induction and consolidation phases, with options including high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy, immunotherapy, and clinical trials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary CNS lymphoma is a type of cancer that affects the central nervous system, including the brain, spinal cord, and eyes. It is the main disease being discussed in the text, with various treatment options and side effects described."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary CNS lymphoma is a type of cancer that develops deep within the brain tissue, affecting the central nervous system. It is treated with chemotherapy, steroids, and potentially stem cell rescue, but surgery is typically not an option due to risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary CNS lymphoma is a type of cancer that occurs in the central nervous system, including the brain, spinal cord, and eyes, and is treated with chemotherapy, radiation therapy, and other methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary CNS lymphoma is a type of cancer that occurs in the central nervous system, including the brain, spinal cord, and sometimes the eyes. It is diagnosed through imaging and biopsy procedures and requires comprehensive testing to determine its extent."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Veins are blood vessels that can be invaded by esophageal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLORECTAL CANCER ALLIANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colorectal Cancer Alliance is an organization focused on colorectal and anal cancer awareness, support, and research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colorectal Cancer Alliance is an organization focused on supporting patients and families affected by colorectal cancers, including anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSDUCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A transducer is a wand-like probe used in ultrasound imaging that emits high-energy sound waves to create pictures of internal body structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transducer is a wand-like probe used in ultrasound imaging, held and moved on the skin to produce images of internal structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transducer is a wand-like probe used in ultrasound to emit and receive sound waves for imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE 4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade 4 is a high-grade tumor classification indicating highly abnormal cells and rapid growth, implied in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PITUITARY GLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An endocrine gland in the brain that may be affected by head and neck radiation, requiring monitoring."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pituitary gland is an endocrine gland in the head that can be affected by radiation therapy, requiring blood tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pituitary gland is located near the base of the brain and produces TSH, which regulates thyroid hormone levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAPAROSCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Laparoscope is a thin tube with a light and camera used in diagnostic laparoscopy to view the abdomen's lining and organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER GENETICIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Geneticist is a specialist who assesses genetic risk factors for cancer, potentially relevant for anal cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRAPEFRUIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grapefruit is used as a size comparison for the bladder when full, approximately the size of a grapefruit."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACUTE MYELOID LEUKEMIA (AML)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AML is a type of leukemia diagnosed through bone marrow tests, with subtypes like BPDCN, and requires expert pathology review."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) is a type of blood cancer characterized by abnormal changes that stop immature white blood cells, called myeloid blasts or myeloblasts, from maturing, leading to a buildup of blasts in the bone marrow and blood. Diagnosis typically requires 20% or more myeloblasts in the bone marrow or blood, though certain genetic mutations or abnormal chromosomes can allow diagnosis with any number of blasts. Treatment involves phases aimed at remission, including systemic therapy, chemotherapy, targeted therapy, and supportive care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) is a type of blood cancer that requires a multidisciplinary treatment approach, involving various therapies and care team members."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) is a type of blood cancer that starts in the stem cells of bone marrow, characterized by abnormal changes that stop immature white blood cells (myeloid blasts) from maturing, leading to a buildup of blasts and a shortage of healthy blood cells. It is fatal if left untreated and has many subtypes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute myeloid leukemia (AML) is a type of blood cancer that starts in the stem cells of bone marrow, with many subtypes in adults."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute myeloid leukemia is a fast-growing disease with too many immature white blood cells, a rare but serious side effect that can develop from MDS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute myeloid leukemia is a type of blood cancer that starts in the stem cells of bone marrow, with abnormal changes stopping immature white blood cells from maturing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATINUM-SENSITIVE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Platinum-sensitive cancer is ovarian cancer that returns more than 6 months after successful platinum-based chemotherapy, and is typically treated again with platinum-based drugs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A clear fluid that carries infection-fighting white blood cells, through which cancer cells can travel."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a clear fluid carried by the lymphatic system that gives cells water and food and contains white blood cells to fight germs. It is produced by the liver."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a clear fluid circulated by the lymphatic system, which can carry cancer cells to other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a clear fluid containing cells that help fight infections, which drains through lymphatic vessels into lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a clear fluid that carries infection-fighting white blood cells (lymphocytes) throughout the body, also called lymphatic fluid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a clear fluid that carries infection-fighting white blood cells, through which cancer cells can travel."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a clear fluid that gives cells water and food and helps fight germs, draining from breast tissue into lymph vessels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a clear fluid that gives cells water and food and helps fight germs, flowing through lymph vessels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a clear fluid that provides cells with water and food and helps fight germs. It drains from breast tissue into lymph vessels and nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a fluid in lymph vessels, part of soft tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a fluid produced by the liver that provides cells with water and food and contains white blood cells to fight germs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a fluid that circulates through the lymphatic system, and cancer cells can spread through it to lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a fluid that circulates through the lymphatic system, carrying immune cells and potentially cancer cells that spread from tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph is a fluid that travels through the lymphatic system, through which cancer cells can spread in metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECONDARY CNS LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Secondary CNS lymphoma is a different kind of lymphoma that starts in another part of the body but then spreads to the brain or spinal cord."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METRIC SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The metric system is used by care teams to measure aspects of cancer treatment, such as tumor size in centimeters."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIGHT COLORECTAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fight Colorectal Cancer is an advocacy and support organization for colorectal and anal cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fight Colorectal Cancer is an advocacy organization dedicated to research, education, and support for colorectal cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clip is a small, painless metal marker placed near a breast tumor during a biopsy to mark the site for future treatment and imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALIGNANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Malignant refers to cancerous tumors that can grow and spread, as determined by biopsy analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Malignant refers to cancerous tumors that can spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIBEROPTIC SCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical instrument used to view hard-to-see areas of the mouth and throat during head and neck exams."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINE-NEEDLE ASPIRATION (FNA) BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fine-needle aspiration biopsy is a procedure using a very thin needle to remove a small tissue sample from a tumor for testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC FLOOR EXERCISES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic floor exercises are physical activities designed to strengthen the muscles that support the bladder and control urine flow, helping to manage urinary incontinence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pelvic floor exercises are physical activities that help regain control of urine function after bladder cancer surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOLOGIST REPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiologist Report is the interpretation of imaging tests sent to the doctor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PECTORAL (CHEST) MUSCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pectoral (chest) muscle is located behind the breast and helps support it."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MYELOID BLASTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Myeloid blasts are immature white blood cells found in the bone marrow or blood. Their presence at 20% or more is a key criterion for AML diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid blasts are immature white blood cells that accumulate in AML, preventing normal blood cell maturation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid blasts are immature white blood cells that accumulate in the bone marrow and blood due to AML, leading to health issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid blasts are immature white blood cells that normally mature into granulocytes (neutrophils). In AML, abnormal myeloblasts accumulate in the bone marrow or blood, crowding out healthy cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid blasts, also called myeloblasts, are immature white blood cells that fail to mature in acute myeloid leukemia (AML), leading to a buildup in the bone marrow and blood, which impairs normal blood function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEVACIZUMAB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bevacizumab (Avastin) is a drug that stops the growth of new blood vessels feeding tumors, sometimes added to chemotherapy for ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bevacizumab (Avastin) is a targeted therapy used in ovarian cancer treatment, often added to chemotherapy or used as maintenance therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bevacizumab is a chemotherapy drug used in regimens for ovarian cancer, sometimes with maintenance therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVASIVE RECTAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Invasive rectal cancer is cancer that has grown beyond the inner lining of the rectum into deeper layers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brain is a common site for breast cancer metastasis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain is a common site for distant metastasis of breast cancer, where cancer cells can form secondary tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain is a common site for metastatic esophageal cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain is a common site for metastatic thyroid cancer spread, requiring monitoring and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain is a site where leukemia can rarely spread to the lining, detected by MRI."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain is an organ that can be a less frequent site for distant metastasis of kidney cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain is an organ that may be bright on PET scans normally."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain is an organ that may be imaged with MRI to detect metastasis, and it normally appears bright on PET scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain is an organ that normally appears bright on PET scans due to high metabolic activity, and is not necessarily indicative of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain is an organ that normally appears bright on PET scans due to high metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain is an organ that normally appears bright on PET scans, not necessarily indicating cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain is an organ that requires electrolytes and is imaged in brain CT or MRI for CNS issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brain is the organ where gliomas develop, and its functions are affected by tumors, leading to various symptoms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The brain is a part of the central nervous system where primary CNS lymphoma most often occurs. A lymphoma here can cause specific nerve changes and neurological symptoms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The brain is an organ of the central nervous system where primary CNS lymphoma can occur, and it is the site for stereotactic biopsy procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The brain is an organ that may appear bright on PET scans due to normal metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The brain is an organ where leukemia can spread to the lining (meninges), detected through MRI scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The brain is part of the central nervous system, and primary CNS lymphoma often appears as tumors in the brain, detected through imaging and biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The brain is part of the central nervous system, controls functions such as feeling, moving, thinking, and learning, and is a primary location for primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"The brain is part of the central nervous system, where primary CNS lymphoma often occurs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTIMETERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Centimeters are a unit of measurement in the metric system used to describe tumor size."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV CANCERS ALLIANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV Cancers Alliance is an organization dedicated to raising awareness and supporting research on HPV-related cancers, including anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV Cancers Alliance is an organization that raises awareness and provides resources for cancers caused by HPV, including anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPH FLUID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymph fluid is a bodily fluid through which cancer cells can travel to form tumors in other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph fluid is a clear fluid that drains from the breast and nearby areas through lymph nodes, which can carry cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymph fluid is a liquid that carries water and food to cells and transports white blood cells, passing through lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROID-STIMULATING HORMONE (TSH) TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A blood test that measures the level of thyroid-stimulating hormone to assess thyroid function, with high levels indicating low thyroid hormone and low levels indicating high thyroid hormone (hyperthyroidism)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIRROR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A tool used by health care providers to view areas of the oral cavity during head and neck exams."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mirror is a small tool used in indirect laryngoscopy to view the throat area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORE BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Core biopsy is a procedure using a hollow needle to remove tissue samples from a tumor for pathological testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
