      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility Impact Education is understanding how treatment affects fertility."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The lips surround the opening of the mouth and hold food in place. The mucosal lip is a site for mouth cancer, but cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma of the vermilion lip is excluded."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACUTE PROMYELOCYTIC LEUKEMIA (APL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia (APL) is a rare subtype of AML, characterized by the abnormal fusion gene PML::RARA, and is discussed in Chapter 5 of the book."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute promyelocytic leukemia is a specific subtype of AML, included in the book."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acute promyelocytic leukemia is a subtype of AML mentioned in the text as a related condition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIRVETUXIMAB SORAVTANSINE-GYNX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mirvetuximab soravtansine-gynx (Elahere) is a targeted therapy, an antibody drug conjugate, used for recurrent ovarian cancer with folate receptor alpha biomarker."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-CANCEROUS GROWTHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-cancerous growths are benign tumors, such as polyps, that do not spread but can sometimes become cancerous."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPINAL CORD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spinal cord is a common site for metastatic thyroid cancer spread, requiring monitoring and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spinal cord is a site where leukemia can rarely spread to the lining, detected by MRI."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spinal cord is part of the central nervous system, where gliomas can sometimes start, though rarely spread to other body areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spinal cord is part of the central nervous system where leukemia can rarely spread, requiring imaging assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spinal cord is part of the central nervous system where primary CNS lymphoma can also occur, leading to movement and coordination issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spinal cord is part of the central nervous system where primary CNS lymphoma can occur, and it is involved in lumbar puncture procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spinal cord is part of the central nervous system, and primary CNS lymphoma can affect it, requiring imaging and biopsy for diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spinal cord is part of the central nervous system, transmits messages between the brain and the body, and can be affected by primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"The spinal cord is part of the central nervous system, which can be affected by primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MILLIMETERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Millimeters are a unit of measurement in the metric system used in cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOVE YOUR BUNS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Love Your Buns is an organization focused on anal cancer awareness and patient support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Love Your Buns is an organization focused on raising awareness and providing support for anal cancer patients and survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NODE POSITIVE (NODE+)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Node positive (node+) is a term used when cancer cells are found in lymph nodes, indicating cancer has spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAPILLARY CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The most common type of thyroid cancer, a differentiated cancer that usually grows and spreads slowly."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An endocrine gland in the neck that may be affected by radiation therapy, monitored through blood tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"The thyroid is a butterfly-shaped gland in the front of the neck, producing hormones that regulate body functions such as metabolism, heart rate, and blood pressure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The thyroid is a gland in the neck that produces hormones, and is the site where tumors and cancers such as follicular and oncocytic carcinoma develop, requiring surgical intervention."&lt;SEP&gt;"The thyroid is a gland in the neck that produces hormones; it is the site of thyroid cancer and the focus of surgical treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARACENTESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paracentesis is a procedure where a long, thin needle is inserted through the skin of the belly to remove a fluid sample for testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LAPAROSCOPIC SURGICAL STAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
