    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOWEL CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bowel changes refer to alterations in bowel habits, such as incontinence or diarrhea, that occur as side effects of anal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATTENUATED FAP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A milder form of FAP causing fewer polyps and later onset of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Form."&lt;SEP&gt;"Milder form of FAP causing fewer polyps and later onset."&lt;SEP&gt;"Milder form of FAP."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLASTIC PLASMACYTOID DENDRITIC CELL NEOPLASM (BPDCN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BPDCN is a subtype of AML that may require lymph node or skin lesion biopsies for diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blastic Plasmacytoid Dendritic Cell Neoplasm (BPDCN) is an aggressive subtype of AML that can be found in blood, bone marrow, lymph nodes, and/or skin, and is discussed in Chapter 6 of the book."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blastic plasmacytoid dendritic cell neoplasm is a specific subtype of AML, included in the book."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blastic plasmacytoid dendritic cell neoplasm is a subtype of AML mentioned in the text as a related condition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOPLATIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A platinum chemotherapy drug used to treat squamous cell skin cancer and other cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboplatin is a chemotherapy drug used in preferred regimens for ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboplatin is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to treat various cancers, including inflammatory breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboplatin is a chemotherapy drug used in the carboplatin and paclitaxel regimen for recurrent or metastatic anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboplatin is a platinum chemotherapy drug used to treat squamous cell skin cancer and other cancers, often in combination with other drugs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug commonly used in the treatment of ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in cancer treatment, with potential kidney-related side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in ovarian cancer treatment, with risk of hypersensitivity reactions on repeat use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug, an alternative to cisplatin, used in combination regimens for metastatic cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboplatin is an alternative platinum drug used when cisplatin is too harsh or cannot be given, for cervical cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS: COLON CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Colon Cancer is a patient guide that provides information on colon cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEREBROSPINAL FLUID (CSF)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) is the fluid surrounding the brain and spinal cord, where cancer cells may be found, leading to the use of intrathecal chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cerebrospinal fluid is a fluid that surrounds the brain and spinal cord. Primary CNS lymphoma can occur in this fluid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cerebrospinal fluid is a liquid that surrounds the brain and spinal cord, and can be involved in primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cerebrospinal fluid is the fluid surrounding the brain and spinal cord, where cancer cells may be found in primary CNS lymphoma, leading to intrathecal chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;P16 (HPV) TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"p16 (HPV) testing is a biomarker test used to detect HPV infection in throat cancer, aiding in staging and treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"p16 (HPV) testing is a diagnostic procedure used to detect the presence of HPV-related markers in throat cancer, helping to guide treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"p16 (HPV) testing is a diagnostic test used to detect HPV-related changes in throat cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL COALITION FOR CANCER SURVIVORSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"National Coalition for Cancer Survivorship is an organization advocating for cancer survivors and providing resources."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marker is a device placed in a lymph node or breast tissue to identify its location for future treatment or imaging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of differentiated thyroid cancer, second most common, that usually grows and spreads slowly."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PITUITARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An endocrine gland in the brain that may be affected by head and neck radiation, monitored through blood tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIOR SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prior surgery refers to a previous surgical procedure that may have found ovarian cancer, requiring review of results by the treatment team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHOLE-BODY RAI SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A whole-body RAI scan is an imaging procedure performed after RAI therapy to detect remaining thyroid tissue or cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COGNITIVE DYSFUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cognitive dysfunction refers to issues with thinking or memory that may occur after cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAGINAL DILATOR THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vaginal dilator therapy uses devices to gradually stretch or widen the vagina, helping manage vaginal stenosis caused by radiation therapy for anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CISPLATIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemotherapy drug used in combination with 5-FU for perianal cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A platinum chemotherapy drug used to treat squamous cell skin cancer and other cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin (Platinol) is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy to kill cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin is a chemotherapy drug containing the metal platinum, effective against bladder cancer but potentially damaging to kidneys."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin is a chemotherapy drug given intravenously on the first day of 5-FU infusions, used in combination with 5-FU for anal cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin is a chemotherapy drug used in combination with 5-FU for anal cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin is a chemotherapy drug used in regimens like 5-FU and cisplatin, FOLFCIS, and modified DCF for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin is a chemotherapy drug used in systemic therapy for cervical cancer, associated with side effects such as mouth sores, hair loss, fatigue, increased risk of infection, bleeding or bruising easily, nerve damage, kidney damage, and hearing problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin is a platinum chemotherapy drug used to treat squamous cell skin cancer and other cancers, often in combination with other drugs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug generally preferred for cervical cancer treatment, given weekly during chemoradiation or every 3 weeks for recurrent/metastatic cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug that can cause kidney damage and hearing problems with extended use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in combination regimens for treating metastatic cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in ovarian cancer treatment, with risk of hypersensitivity reactions on repeat use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in ovarian cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cisplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in the treatment of cervical cancer, which may be less effective on its own if previously used, often combined with other medicines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY PRESERVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Actions taken to keep options open for having children in the future, involving fertility specialists and discussions before starting cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility Preservation is the act of taking steps to protect ability to have children before cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility Preservation is the process of taking action to protect ability to have children before treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility preservation includes methods like sperm banking, egg freezing, ovarian tissue banking, and ovarian transposition to help patients have children after cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility preservation involves actions taken before cancer treatment to keep options open for having children in the future."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility preservation involves keeping options open for having children, with specialists helping patients sort through best approaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility preservation involves methods like egg or embryo freezing to protect fertility before cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility preservation involves methods to protect a patient's ability to have children before cancer treatment that may affect fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility preservation is a process to keep options open for having children before cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility preservation is about keeping options open for having children, possibly before cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility preservation is the process of collecting and freezing sperm or eggs to allow having a baby during or after cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility preservation refers to methods like sperm banking, egg freezing, ovarian tissue banking, and ovarian transposition to maintain the ability to have children after cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MENINGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Meninges are membranes that cover the brain and spinal cord, providing protection to the CNS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCOPING PROCEDURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scoping procedures are diagnostic techniques that use a scope to examine the throat and pharynx."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scoping procedures involve the use of thin, tube-shaped tools called scopes, such as endoscopes, inserted into the body to examine areas like the oropharynx, take pictures, and guide biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scoping procedures, including mirror and fiberoptic exams, are used to visually inspect the oropharynx and other throat areas for abnormalities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAN FOUNDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PAN Foundation is a nonprofit organization providing financial assistance to cancer patients for treatment-related costs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENIGN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Benign refers to a non-cancerous condition, and if a biopsied area is benign, a clip may remain to mark the site for future imaging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Benign refers to non-cancerous tumors that do not spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Benign refers to non-cancerous tumors that grow slowly and are less aggressive, as determined by biopsy analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Benign refers to noncancerous tumors that do not spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONCOCYTIC CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of differentiated thyroid cancer, less common, that usually grows and spreads slowly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oncocytic carcinoma, formerly known as Hürthle cell carcinoma, is an uncommon thyroid cancer more likely to spread to lymph nodes, and is diagnosed through pathologic examination of removed tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOODS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutritional items recommended by nutritionists to ensure adequate intake before treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEREDITARY OVARIAN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hereditary ovarian cancer is caused by inherited gene mutations, such as in BRCA1, BRCA2, or Lynch syndrome, often occurring at younger ages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN MANAGEMENT SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pain Management Specialist is a healthcare provider who helps manage pain associated with cancer and its treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URETER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ureter is a tube that carries urine from the kidneys to the bladder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RED BLOOD CELLS (RBCS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Red Blood Cells (RBCs) carry oxygen throughout the body and are measured in a CBC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells (RBCs or erythrocytes) are a type of blood cell that carry oxygen throughout the body. They are produced from blood stem cells and are often reduced in ALL due to crowding by lymphoblasts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells (RBCs) are blood cells that carry oxygen throughout the body, measured in a complete blood count."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells (RBCs) are blood cells that carry oxygen throughout the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells (RBCs) are cells that carry oxygen through the blood; their levels are measured in a CBC to assess overall health and detect anemia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells (erythrocytes) are a type of blood cell that carry oxygen throughout the body. They are produced in the bone marrow from blood stem cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells (erythrocytes) are a type of blood cell that carry oxygen throughout the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells are cells that carry oxygen throughout the body. Their levels are measured in a CBC to assess overall health and detect anemia, which is common in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Red blood cells, or erythrocytes, are a type of blood cell that carry oxygen, as described in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPERSENSITIVITY REACTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hypersensitivity reactions are allergic reactions that can occur with repeat use of carboplatin or cisplatin, potentially life-threatening, requiring management by treatment teams."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMAGING STUDIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diagnostic tests used to determine treatment plans for cancer, with results important for patients to understand and keep copies of."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging studies are diagnostic techniques such as CT scans, MRIs, or ultrasounds that create visual images of internal organs to detect tumors or abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging studies are diagnostic tests used to detect swollen lymph nodes and assess FL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging studies are diagnostic tests used to determine treatment plans for cancer, and results are important for patients to understand and keep copies of."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging studies are diagnostic tools used to guide AML treatment planning by visualizing internal structures and potential disease spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging studies are tests like CT or MRI scans used to visualize internal organs and detect cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging studies are tests like CT or MRI scans used to visualize internal structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging studies are tests like X-rays or scans used to assess organs and detect abnormalities in ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging studies include MRI, PET, and CT scans used to guide AML treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging studies take pictures of the inside of the body to help determine the extent of cancer and guide treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imaging studies, such as CT, MRI, and PET scans, are used to visualize tumors and assess cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPSTEIN-BARR VIRUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) is a common virus that causes infectious mononucleosis and can lead to EBV-related cancers, particularly nasopharyngeal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epstein-Barr virus is a common virus that causes mononucleosis and other illnesses, and carrying it is a risk factor for primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epstein-Barr virus is a virus that can be detected in neck lymph nodes in cases of nasopharyngeal carcinoma, even when no primary tumor is found (T0 stage)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOBACCO AND ALCOHOL USE HISTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tobacco and alcohol use history is a record of a patient's consumption habits, which are known risk factors for head and neck cancer and can affect treatment outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tobacco and alcohol use history is a record of a patient's use of these substances, which are known risk factors for head and neck cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tobacco and alcohol use history is a record of a patient's use of these substances, which are risk factors for head and neck cancer and can affect treatment outcomes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE ANCHOR STUDY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Anchor Study is a research initiative focused on anal cancer, likely involving clinical trials and patient data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFLAMMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inflammation can show up as a bright spot on PET scans, potentially mimicking cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammation is a bodily response that can appear as a bright spot on PET scans, potentially mimicking cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammation is a bodily response that can appear as bright spots on PET scans, potentially mimicking cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammation is a bodily response to infection or injury that can appear as a bright spot on PET scans, potentially mimicking cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammation is a condition that can show up as bright spots on PET scans, potentially mimicking cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammation is a possible side effect of intraocular chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammation is an immune stressor that causes germinal centers to form, and unregulated growth can lead to follicular lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDULLARY THYROID CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medullary thyroid cancer is a type of thyroid cancer that does not respond to RAI therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The third most common type of thyroid cancer, which can be inherited and runs in families."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DAILY SELF-CARE TASKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Activities of daily living assessed in performance status to determine fitness for treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST CANCER GENE 1 (BRCA1)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breast cancer gene 1 is a gene that repairs damaged cells; mutations increase risk of ovarian, breast, and other cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUTOIMMUNE REACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An autoimmune reaction is a side effect of immunotherapy where the immune system attacks healthy cells, causing various symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CIRCULATING TUMOR DNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Circulating tumor DNA is DNA from cancer cells found in the blood, used to monitor treatment response and detect recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOCTOR DISCUSSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Doctor Discussion is the conversation between doctor and patient about test results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN THICKENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skin thickening is a possible sign of inflammatory breast cancer, giving an orange-peel texture."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMARKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker is a biological molecule found in blood or tissues that indicates a disease, such as BCR::ABL1 in CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"A targetable feature of cancer, such as dMMR or MSI-H, that helps guide treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarker is a molecular characteristic, such as a genetic mutation, used to identify specific types of gliomas, like IDH-mutant astrocytoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarker refers to biological indicators like BCR::ABL1 that are tested to diagnose and monitor CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarker refers to genetic or protein markers tested in FL diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarkers are biological indicators such as BRCA1/2 mutations, HRD status, HER2 expression, and others, used to guide treatment for recurrent ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarkers are proteins or genetic changes found on or inside white blood cells that are targeted in AML treatment and used to determine subtype, prognosis, and treatment response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarkers are proteins or genetic changes on or in cells that are targeted in AML treatment and used to identify disease subtypes and guide therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomarkers are targetable changes of a cancer that can help guide treatment, such as dMMR or MSI-H in rectal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEART FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Heart function refers to the ability of the heart to pump blood, which may be affected by certain cancer treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUTOIMMUNE DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Autoimmune disease, such as lupus, is a condition where the immune system overreacts and attacks healthy tissues, increasing the risk of primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLETE HEAD AND NECK EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A complete head and neck exam is a specialized physical examination focusing on the head and neck area to detect signs of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A complete head and neck exam is a specialized physical examination using mirrors or fiberoptic scopes to inspect the oropharynx and surrounding areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complete head and neck exam is a detailed examination of the head and neck area, often using mirrors or fiberoptic scopes to view hard-to-see areas like the oropharynx."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;U.S. NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE (NLM) CLINICAL TRIALS DATABASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM) Clinical Trials Database is a government resource listing clinical trials for various conditions, including anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An organ and gland on the chest made of milk ducts, fat, nerves, lymph and blood vessels, ligaments, and connective tissue; contains lobules that produce milk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Breast is a part of the body where cancer can originate and spread to bone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Breast is the anatomical region where breast cancer develops, and is the focus of imaging and biopsy procedures described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Breast is the body part imaged in mammograms and breast MRIs, where tumors or abnormalities may be detected."&lt;SEP&gt;"Breast is the organ examined during palpation for cancer detection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The breast is a glandular organ on the chest made of milk ducts, lobules, fat, nerves, lymph and blood vessels, ligaments, and connective tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"The breast is a glandular organ on the chest, made of milk ducts, lobules, fat, nerves, lymph and blood vessels, ligaments, and connective tissue, and is the site where breast cancer develops."&lt;SEP&gt;"The breast is an organ and gland on the chest, made of milk ducts, fat, nerves, lymph and blood vessels, ligaments, and connective tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"The breast is the organ containing ducts and lobules that produce and carry milk, and is the site where breast cancer, including inflammatory breast cancer, originates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAPLASTIC THYROID CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anaplastic thyroid cancer is an aggressive type of thyroid cancer that is almost always treated with radiation therapy and does not respond to RAI."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaplastic thyroid cancer is the least common and most aggressive type of thyroid cancer. It is often treated with chemotherapy in combination with radiation therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The most aggressive and rare type of thyroid cancer, most often affecting older adults."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER REPORTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Documents detailing specific cancer type and characteristics, included in a medical binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BREAST CANCER GENE 2 (BRCA2)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Breast cancer gene 2 is a gene that repairs damaged cells; mutations increase risk of ovarian, breast, and other cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIRTH CONTROL EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Birth Control Education is learning about contraceptive options."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALVEOLAR RIDGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The alveolar ridge is the bony, raised area of the upper and lower jaw that holds the sockets of the teeth, a site for mouth cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATELETS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell fragments in the blood that help with clotting; their count is measured in a CBC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cells that help wounds heal by forming blood clots, measured in a CBC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets (PLTs or thrombocytes) are a type of blood cell that help control bleeding. They are produced from blood stem cells and can be reduced in ALL due to crowding by lymphoblasts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets (PLTs or thrombocytes) are a type of blood cell that help control bleeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets (PLTs or thrombocytes) help control bleeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets (thrombocytes) are a type of blood cell that help control bleeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets are a component of blood that help prevent bleeding, as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets are a type of blood cell that helps with blood clotting, formed from blood stem cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets are a type of blood cell that may be low in CLL patients, as mentioned in the context of blood counts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets are blood cells that may be low in CLL; their counts are measured in blood tests to assess disease impact."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets are blood components that help control bleeding, measured in a complete blood count."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets are blood components that help prevent bleeding, and their numbers are reduced in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets are blood-clotting cells that help prevent bleeding. Targeted therapy can reduce platelet counts, increasing the risk of bruising and bleeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets are produced from blood stem cells in red marrow."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets control bleeding, measured in complete blood count for bladder cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets help control bleeding and are measured in a CBC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platelets help wounds heal by forming blood clots, measured in a CBC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRCA1 MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BRCA1 mutation is a genetic biomarker associated with ovarian cancer, influencing treatment decisions such as PARP inhibitor use."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEREBROSPINAL FLUID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cerebrospinal fluid is a liquid that flows in and around the brain and spinal cord, protecting and nourishing the central nervous system, and is tested via lumbar puncture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cerebrospinal fluid is the fluid surrounding the brain and spinal cord, collected during a lumbar puncture to check for leukemia cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cerebrospinal fluid is the fluid that surrounds the brain and spinal cord, which can be blocked by tumors, causing additional symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLDER ADULT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Older adults, particularly those in their 60s or 70s, are at higher risk for primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISTRESS SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A process to evaluate the emotional and psychological well-being of cancer patients, including feelings of sadness, fear, anxiety, and depression, with support services available."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distress screening is a process to assess emotional and psychological distress in cancer patients, part of comprehensive care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distress screening is a process to evaluate a patient's emotional and psychological well-being, as cancer diagnosis can cause significant stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distress screening is a process to evaluate emotional and psychological distress in cancer patients, helping to address mental health needs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distress screening is a process to evaluate emotional and psychological distress in cancer patients, part of standard cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distress screening is a process to identify emotional or psychological distress in cancer patients, as strong feelings are common after diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABDOMINOPERINEAL RESECTION (APR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A radical surgery to remove the anus, recommended for recurrent or locally progressive anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"APR is a radical surgical procedure for anal cancer that returns to the anal area, involving removal of the anus, rectum, surrounding tissue, and creation of a permanent colostomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Abdominoperineal resection (APR) is a surgical procedure for anal cancer that removes the anus, rectum, and nearby tissues, requiring a permanent colostomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Abdominoperineal resection (APR) is a type of transabdominal surgery for lower rectal tumors, involving removal of the anus and rectum and requiring a permanent colostomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AIRPORT SECURITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Airport security is a checkpoint where metal clips placed during biopsies do not cause issues, as they are safe for such screening."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOBECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure that removes the lobe of the thyroid containing the cancerous nodule, along with the isthmus, often used for small low-risk differentiated thyroid cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lobectomy is a surgical procedure to remove one lobe of the thyroid gland, used as a treatment for thyroid cancer. It requires specific follow-up care including physical exams and TSH blood tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lobectomy is a surgical procedure to remove part of the thyroid gland, used for small, low-risk thyroid cancers, potentially avoiding the need for hormone replacement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lobectomy is a surgical procedure to remove part of the thyroid, considered as a treatment option for less invasive cancers, with follow-up monitoring or additional surgery depending on pathologic findings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAP TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pap tests, also known as cervical or vaginal cytology, are annual screening tests after treatment to detect abnormal or precancerous cells, though less effective for recurrent cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMERCIAL GENETIC TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Commercial genetic tests are over-the-counter tests that look for common gene mutations but are not comprehensive for all hereditary syndromes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEREOTACTIC BODY RADIATION THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stereotactic body radiation therapy (SBRT) is a specialized EBRT used to treat metastatic cervical cancer with high doses in few sessions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUCLEAR MEDICINE DOCTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A nuclear medicine doctor is a specialist who uses radioactive substances for diagnostic and therapeutic purposes, such as in RAI therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONCOLOGY NUTRITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oncology nutrition is a field of dietetics focused on the nutritional needs of cancer patients, including those with anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oncology nutrition is a specialized field focusing on dietary management for cancer patients and survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLASSIC FAP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Form."&lt;SEP&gt;"Severe form of FAP causing many polyps and early cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Severe form of FAP."&lt;SEP&gt;"The severe form of FAP causing hundreds to thousands of polyps and early cancer development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plasma is a clear, yellowish fluid made up of mostly water that makes up part of blood. It carries blood cells and nutrients throughout the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plasma is a clear, yellowish fluid made up of mostly water, in which blood cells float."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plasma is a clear, yellowish fluid made up of mostly water, which is a main component of blood and carries blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plasma is a clear, yellowish fluid made up of mostly water. More than half of the blood is plasma, and blood cells float in it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plasma is the clear, yellowish fluid component of blood, mostly water, in which blood cells float."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plasma is the clear, yellowish fluid component of blood, mostly water, that carries blood cells and other substances throughout the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plasma is the fluid component of blood, making up a large part of its volume."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plasma is the liquid part of blood used in CMP tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRCA2 MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BRCA2 mutation is a genetic biomarker associated with ovarian cancer, influencing treatment decisions such as PARP inhibitor use."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE MARROW CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone marrow cells are cells found in the bone marrow, including blood stem cells and lymphoblasts in ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC ABNORMALITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic abnormality (mutation) in lymphocytes is a cause of lymphoma, leading to uncontrolled growth of these cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DENTAL EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A dental checkup recommended for patients with head and neck cancer to monitor jaw, teeth, and gum health, often before starting certain treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A dental exam is a checkup procedure recommended for head and neck cancer patients to monitor jaw, teeth, and gum health, often before treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A dental exam, including x-rays like Panorex, is recommended to assess oral health, as head and neck cancer treatment can affect the jaw, teeth, and gums."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dental exam is a check-up to monitor oral health, important for head and neck cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dental exam is important for head and neck cancer patients to monitor jaw, teeth, and gum health, as treatment can affect these areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dental exam with x-ray (Panorex) or CT is used to assess oral health and detect cancer spread to the jaw."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAL SPHINCTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anal sphincter is a ring-shaped muscle around the anus that controls opening and closing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADENOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adenomas are a type of polyp that can become cancerous over time. Cancer that forms in an adenoma is called adenocarcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOTAL THYROIDECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure that removes the entire thyroid gland, and possibly nearby lymph nodes, often requiring overnight hospital stay and lifelong thyroid hormone replacement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total thyroidectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the entire thyroid gland, commonly used for thyroid cancer, especially when cancer has spread or is high-risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total thyroidectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the entire thyroid gland, used as a treatment for thyroid cancer. It requires specific follow-up care including blood tests and neck ultrasound."&lt;SEP&gt;"Total thyroidectomy is a surgical procedure to remove the entire thyroid, recommended for suspected follicular or oncocytic tumors that have grown beyond the thyroid or are larger than 4 cm, and may be followed by RAI therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVORSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A phase of care focusing on long-term side effects and maintaining healthy habits after colon cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A section of the guide addressing long-term side effects and healthy habits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survivorship encompasses the range of care for cancer survivors beyond surveillance, including monitoring for symptoms of recurrence and managing long-term health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survivorship focuses on the physical, emotional, and financial issues unique to cancer survivors, including managing long-term side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survivorship refers to the phase after cancer treatment, focusing on long-term health, follow-up care, and quality of life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survivorship refers to the phase of care after cancer treatment, focusing on long-term health, monitoring, and quality of life for cancer survivors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survivorship refers to the phase of life after cancer treatment, focusing on follow-up care, late effects, and quality of life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFICULTY EATING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Difficulty eating is a symptom of ovarian cancer, leading to potential malnutrition and need for dietary support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Difficulty eating is a symptom of ovarian cancer, leading to reduced food intake and potential nutritional deficiencies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROTOXICOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thyrotoxicosis is a condition of having too much thyroid hormone in the body, which can result from excessive levothyroxine dosage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUMBAR VERTEBRAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lumbar vertebrae are the 5 bones in the lower back region of the spine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SLEEP DISORDERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sleep disorders are common issues for cancer survivors, addressed in survivorship care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOMOLOGOUS RECOMBINATION DEFICIENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Homologous recombination deficiency (HRD) is a biomarker indicating impaired DNA repair, relevant for PARP inhibitor therapy in ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MYELOID PROGENITOR CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Myeloid progenitor cells are a stage in blood cell development that develop into red blood cells, granulocytes (a type of white blood cell), and platelets. AML affects these cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid progenitor cells are a type of progenitor cell that form into myeloblasts and other non-lymphoid blood cells. They are not directly affected in ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid progenitor cells are a type of progenitor cell that form into myeloblasts and other non-lymphoid blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid progenitor cells are blood stem cell derivatives that form into myeloblasts and other non-lymphoid blood cells. In CML, they are produced in increased amounts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid progenitor cells are blood stem cell derivatives that form myeloblasts and other non-lymphoid blood cells, often increased in CML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid progenitor cells are cells that develop into red blood cells, granulocytes, and platelets, and are affected by AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid progenitor cells are early blood cells that form into myeloblasts and other non-lymphoid blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid progenitor cells are progenitor cells that form into myeloblasts and other non-lymphoid blood cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid progenitor cells are stem cell-derived cells that develop into red blood cells, platelets, and some white blood cells, not directly affected in ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Myeloid progenitor cells form into myeloblasts and other non-lymphoid blood cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RISK FACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A risk factor is a characteristic that increases the likelihood of developing prostate cancer, with age being the most significant one."&lt;SEP&gt;"A risk factor is anything that increases a person's chance of developing lung cancer. Key risk factors include tobacco smoke, exposure to radon, asbestos, and other carcinogens."&lt;SEP&gt;"A risk factor is anything that increases the chance of developing a disease, such as liver cancer. The text identifies cirrhosis and chronic hepatitis B as specific risk factors for HCC."&lt;SEP&gt;"A risk factor is anything that increases the chance of developing a disease, such as smoking or genetic traits for lung cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A risk factor is something that increases the chance of developing a disease. Having an impaired immune system is a risk factor for primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk factor is anything that increases the chance of getting cancer; for prostate cancer, risk factors include age and family history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk factors are conditions or behaviors that increase the chance of developing a disease, such as having a reduced immune system for primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY COUNSELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility counseling addresses reproductive concerns before and during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility counseling is a service offered to address fertility concerns and preventing pregnancy during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility counseling is a service offered to patients to discuss options for preserving fertility before starting cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLOSTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colostomy is a procedure that connects the remaining upper part of the colon to an opening on the abdomen (stoma) to divert stool flow, often temporary."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colostomy is a surgery creating an opening in the abdomen for stool collection after anus removal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colostomy is a surgical procedure creating an opening (stoma) on the abdomen for stool to exit, which may be temporary or permanent depending on the surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colostomy is a surgical procedure creating an opening (stoma) on the abdomen to allow stool to exit the body, necessary after APR when the anus is removed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colostomy is a surgical procedure creating an opening for stool to leave the body, often required after APR surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colostomy is a surgical procedure creating an opening in the abdomen for waste elimination, sometimes needed after APR."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colostomy is a surgical procedure that connects the remaining colon to the outside of the abdomen, allowing stool to exit through a stoma into a bag, often permanent if the anus is removed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEDUNCULATED POLYPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pedunculated polyps are mushroom-shaped polyps that stick out from the colon wall, having a stalk and a round top."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pedunculated polyps are mushroom-shaped polyps with a stalk and round top that protrude from the colon wall."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROID HORMONE REPLACEMENT THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A treatment using medicine like levothyroxine to replace hormones no longer produced by the thyroid, needed lifelong after total thyroidectomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thyroid hormone replacement therapy involves administering synthetic thyroid hormones like levothyroxine to maintain normal hormone levels, often after thyroid removal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thyroid hormone replacement therapy with levothyroxine is a lifelong treatment after total thyroidectomy, and sometimes after lobectomy, to maintain normal hormone levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PD-L1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PD-L1 is a protein biomarker whose expression level determines if a tumor is PD-L1-positive, influencing the use of targeted therapies or immunotherapies for recurrent cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEELING FULL QUICKLY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Feeling full quickly is a symptom of ovarian cancer, affecting meal consumption and nutritional status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Feeling full quickly is a symptom of ovarian cancer, causing early satiety and affecting dietary habits."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINANCIAL COUNSELOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Financial Counselor is a professional who assists patients with insurance coverage, treatment costs, and financial aid programs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOFTER BOWEL MOVEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Softer bowel movements are a side effect of brachytherapy, affecting digestive function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUSCLES IN BLADDER WALLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muscles in bladder walls contract during urination to force urine out of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2 EXPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HER2 expression is a biomarker test that measures the presence of HER2 protein on tumor cells, potentially influencing treatment options for ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"HER2 expression is a biomarker that may be tested in ovarian cancer to guide targeted therapy options."&lt;SEP&gt;"HER2 expression refers to the presence of HER2 protein on cancer cells, which determines the use of HER2-targeted therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"HER2 is a protein that may be overexpressed in some cancers; testing guides targeted therapy in recurrent ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-cells are a type of lymphocyte that produces antibodies, and they are the origin of B-ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"B-cells are a type of white blood cell that can become cancerous in lymphoma; rituximab targets them."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMENORRHEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amenorrhea is the absence of menstrual periods, which may occur during treatment for premenopause and for up to 2 years after, but often returns in those 35 years of age and under."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amenorrhea is the cessation of menstrual periods during or after endocrine therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPATITIS B SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hepatitis B screening is a test to check for hepatitis B infection, which may be relevant before certain treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hepatitis B screening tests for the virus, which may affect treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTENSITY-MODULATED RADIATION THERAPY (IMRT)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IMRT is an advanced radiation technique preferred for treating anal cancer, delivering precise radiation doses to tumors while sparing healthy tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intensity-modulated radiation therapy (IMRT) is a type of external radiation therapy using multiple beams of varying intensities, recommended for anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SESSILE POLYPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sessile polyps are flatter polyps that do not have a stalk. They are more likely to return after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sessile polyps are flatter polyps that lie against the colon wall without a stalk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEVOTHYROXINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Levothyroxine is a medication taken to keep TSH levels down in thyroid cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Levothyroxine is a synthetic thyroid hormone used as replacement therapy, taken orally once daily on an empty stomach, and is central to managing thyroid hormone levels in patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Levothyroxine is a synthetic thyroid hormone used in replacement therapy to maintain normal hormone levels after thyroid surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Levothyroxine is a thyroid hormone replacement medication taken by patients to keep TSH levels down and manage thyroid function after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Levothyroxine is a thyroid hormone replacement therapy used to keep TSH levels low or normal, prescribed on a case-by-case basis after surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"The most commonly used thyroid hormone replacement therapy, with brand names like Levoxyl and Synthroid, used to manage TSH levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RET GENE FUSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RET gene fusion is a genetic alteration that can be targeted by specific therapies, tested in cervical cancer cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"RET gene fusion is a specific biomarker found in some medullary thyroid cancers, making them eligible for targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOWEN’S DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bowen’s disease is the earliest form of squamous cell skin cancer, treated with superficial treatments like photodynamic therapy, cryotherapy, or topical therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIDNEY PROBLEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kidney problems are a side effect of bladder removal surgery, affecting renal function and requiring care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BINDER ORGANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Binder Organization is the act of categorizing and arranging medical records in a binder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSATELLITE INSTABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker (MSI-H) indicating high instability in DNA, tested in colon cancer tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellite instability (MSI) is a biomarker indicating DNA mismatch repair deficiency, potentially guiding immunotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T-CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-cells are a type of lymphocyte that helps coordinate the immune response, and they are the origin of T-ALL."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ESTROGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hormone produced by the ovaries, whose sudden drop causes surgical menopause symptoms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A hormone that plays a role in breast development and can stimulate the growth of breast cancer cells when bound to estrogen receptors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Estrogen is a hormone made mainly by ovaries and fat tissue that can promote breast cancer growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Estrogen is a hormone produced by the ovaries, which is a main source during premenopause."&lt;SEP&gt;"Estrogen is a hormone that, in its radioactive form (FES), is used in FES PET-CT scans to detect estrogen receptor-positive cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Estrogen is a hormone whose deficiency can lead to long-term risks such as cardiovascular disease and bone loss (osteoporosis)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Estrogen is a hormone whose sudden drop after ovary removal causes surgical menopause symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOFT PALATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The soft palate is part of the roof of the mouth and is included in the oropharynx, connecting to the nasopharynx."&lt;SEP&gt;"The soft palate is the back part of the roof of the mouth, included in the oropharynx, and is a site where throat cancer can develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"The soft palate is the non-bony part of the roof of the mouth, covered by nonkeratinized squamous epithelium."&lt;SEP&gt;"The soft palate is the soft, back part of the roof of the mouth and is part of the oropharynx."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIBIDO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Libido is sexual desire, which may be affected by cancer treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALIGNANT POLYP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A malignant polyp is a polyp in which cancer has just started to grow, indicating early-stage cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A malignant polyp is a polyp in which cancer has just started to grow."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOACTIVE IODINE (RAI) UPTAKE TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A test that measures how much radioactive iodine is taken up by the thyroid, used to assess thyroid function and detect hyperthyroidism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radioactive iodine uptake test is a diagnostic procedure used to assess thyroid function and nodule activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 1 CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 1 cervical cancer is an early stage where cancer is confined to the cervix, with specific follow-up imaging recommendations based on treatment type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOPICAL THERAPIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Topical therapies are treatments applied to the skin, including 5-fluorouracil, imiquimod, and calcipotriene, used for early CSCC and actinic keratoses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEST PURPOSE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Test Purpose Education is learning why blood and imaging tests are done."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T4 PELVIC TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T4 pelvic tumor spans 3 pelvic segments or crosses the sacroiliac joint, with subcategories T4a (involves SIJ and extends into spine) and T4b (grows into major blood vessels)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUMS (GINGIVA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gums (gingiva) surround the base of the teeth and help keep them in place, and are a site for mouth cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An internal organ that can be a site of prostate cancer metastasis, mentioned in tumor testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung is a body part that may be a site of metastasis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung is a common site for bone cancer metastasis, classified as M1a."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung is a common site for distant metastasis in breast cancer, as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung is a common site for metastasis and may be biopsied to confirm cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung is a part of the body where metastatic cancer can spread, as noted in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung is an area of the body where cancer can metastasize, and biopsies may be performed to confirm cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung is an organ in the body where NSCLC develops, containing airways such as bronchi, bronchioli, and alveoli where oxygen exchange occurs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung is an organ where cancer may metastasize, and biopsy of lung metastases may be needed to confirm cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lung is a common site for metastasis from various cancers, including liver cancer, and is mentioned in the context of M1b staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lung is an organ in the body where liver cancer can metastasize, or spread, forming distant metastases. It is one of the most common sites for metastatic liver cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The lung is an organ that can be affected by esophageal cancer spread, either locally or as a distant metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR MUTATIONAL BURDEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor mutational burden (TMB) is a biomarker measuring the number of mutations in a tumor, potentially indicating response to immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutational burden (TMB) is a measure of mutations per million base pairs of tumor DNA; TMB-H predicts response to immune checkpoint inhibitors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutational burden refers to the number of mutations in tumor DNA, with high levels (TMB-H) indicating potential benefit from immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutational burden refers to the number of mutations per million base pairs of tumor DNA; high burden (TMB-H) is defined as 10 or more mutations and may be treated with pembrolizumab, nivolumab, or ipilimumab."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutational burden-high (TMB-H) is when there are 10 or more mutations per million base pairs of tumor DNA, often treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CSCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CSCC (cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma) is a type of skin cancer discussed in the text, with various risk levels and treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"CSCC (cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma) is a type of skin cancer that can be local, regional, or metastatic, with treatment options varying based on risk level and spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma, a type of skin cancer that can be treated with surgery, radiation, or systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGESTERONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hormone that plays a role in the menstrual cycle and pregnancy, and can stimulate the growth of breast cancer cells when bound to progesterone receptors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Progesterone is a hormone made mainly by ovaries that can promote breast cancer growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Progesterone is a hormone produced by the ovaries, which is a main source during premenopause."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TONSILS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The tonsils are part of the oropharynx and are a common site for throat cancer, often associated with HPV infection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tonsils are part of the oropharynx and are included in the area where throat cancer can form."&lt;SEP&gt;"The tonsils are part of the oropharynx, included in the side and back walls of the throat."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonsils are part of the lymph system, containing B cells and involved in immune function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonsils are part of the lymphatic system, helping to fight infection in the throat area."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonsils are part of the lymphatic system, involved in immune response and can be affected by lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonsils are part of the throat where HPV-related cancers can develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tonsils are small masses of lymph tissue at the back of the throat that help trap disease-causing germs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAGINAL STENOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vaginal stenosis is a condition where the vagina becomes shorter and narrower due to radiation therapy, causing discomfort or pain during sex or examinations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vaginal stenosis is a condition where the vagina narrows and shortens, often caused by radiation therapy, leading to pain during sex and exams."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOSCOPIC ULTRASOUND (EUS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endoscopic ultrasound is an imaging technique used to evaluate polyps and rectal cancer, helping guide surgical decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NECK DISSECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure to remove lymph nodes near the thyroid that are known or suspected to have cancer, often performed during total thyroidectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3 CERVICAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3 cervical cancer involves spread to the lower vagina or pelvic wall, with imaging recommended post-treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;5-FLUOROURACIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"5-fluorouracil (5-FU) is a chemotherapy cream applied directly to the skin, used to treat early CSCC and actinic keratoses, often combined with calcipotriene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PET-CT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PET-CT is a combined positron emission tomography and computed tomography scan used to detect cancer spread throughout the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MENOPAUSAL HORMONE THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Menopausal hormone therapy (MHT), formerly HRT, is used to lessen side effects of radiation-induced menopause."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGESTIVE SYSTEM CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Digestive system cancer includes cancers of the digestive tract, such as anal cancer, which may require specialized nutritional support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLORECTAL CANCER SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The process of detecting polyps or cancer early, as discussed in the NCCN guidelines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EYES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eyes are connected directly to the brain and are part of the central nervous system, and primary CNS lymphoma can spread to them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eyes are examined during a physical exam to check for abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eyes are examined during physical exam to check for signs of disease or treatment effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organs examined during a physical exam to assess vision and overall health."&lt;SEP&gt;"The eyes are connected to the brain via optic nerves and can be affected by primary CNS lymphoma, leading to vitreoretinal lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"The eyes can be affected by primary CNS lymphoma, leading to changes in eyesight such as blurry or double vision."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAF V600E MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BRAF V600E is a specific gene mutation tested as a biomarker in recurrent ovarian cancer for targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRAF V600E mutation is a genetic biomarker that may be tested in ovarian cancer to guide targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRAF V600E mutation is a specific genetic alteration in the BRAF gene, tested as a biomarker to guide targeted therapy in ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SQUAMOUS CELL SKIN CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Squamous cell skin cancer (CSCC) is a type of skin cancer that can form in old wounds, burns, or scars, and may be harder to treat in such cases. It is diagnosed through health history, lesion examination, skin biopsy, and imaging scans if spread is suspected."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell skin cancer (CSCC) is a type of skin cancer that is the primary target of the systemic therapies, targeted therapies, and immunotherapies described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell skin cancer is a type of cancer that arises from squamous cells, with subtypes that may have different risks of recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell skin cancer is a type of skin cancer that arises from squamous cells in the epidermis. It is mentioned in the text as a separate condition from basal cell skin cancer, with information available in NCCN Guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell skin cancer is a type of skin cancer that can be local or regional, requiring different follow-up schedules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell skin cancer is a type of skin cancer that can be treated with various surgical and topical therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell skin cancer is a type of skin cancer that can spread to lymph nodes and other parts of the body. It is the main subject of the text, with treatment options and monitoring discussed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Squamous cell skin cancer, also known as cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma (CSCC), is the second most common type of skin cancer, highly treatable and often curable, originating in squamous cells of the epidermis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASE OF TONGUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The base of the tongue is located in the throat and is part of the oropharynx, a potential site for throat cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic exam is a medical examination of the female reproductive organs, which may be painful in cases of vaginal stenosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pelvic exam is a physical examination of the female reproductive organs, including the ovaries, cervix, and uterus, often using a speculum and possibly including a Pap test or endometrial biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC MRI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic MRI is an imaging technique used to stage rectal cancer, showing the extent of cancer in the rectum and nearby lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPOPARATHYROIDISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A long-term side effect of thyroid removal, characterized by low levels of calcium in the blood."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXPLORATORY SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Exploratory surgery is a procedure to look inside the body to determine the extent of cancer recurrence, guiding treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CALCIPOTRIENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Calcipotriene is a form of vitamin D cream used with 5-fluorouracil to treat actinic keratosis, activating the skin’s immune system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TROUBLE SLEEPING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trouble sleeping is a common side effect of an incorrect levothyroxine dose, impacting rest and recovery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTHY LIFESTYLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Healthy lifestyles refer to habits like diet and exercise that are recommended for cancer survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKULL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skull is a bone that shields the brain, providing protection to the central nervous system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skull is the bone structure where a small opening is made to insert a needle during a stereotactic biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NECK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Area of the body examined for lymph nodes and other abnormalities during a physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck is a body area where lymph nodes are felt for enlargement during a physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck is a body area where lymph nodes are palpated to detect potential cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck is a body area where lymph nodes may be palpated during physical exam for CLL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck is a body part that may be scanned in CT or MRI to detect cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck is a body part where lymph nodes are felt for enlargement during a physical exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck is a common location for swollen lymph nodes in FL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck is a location where lymph nodes are checked for enlargement and where NPC may spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck is a part of the body where lymph nodes can be felt for enlargement, as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck is a region of the body containing lymph nodes, where head and neck cancers sometimes spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck is an area where ultrasound probes are moved to examine lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck is the area examined for enlarged lymph nodes during head and neck exam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The neck is a common area where basal cell skin cancer develops due to sun exposure, and it is often the site of skin lesions associated with the disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"The neck is a part of the body where high numbers of lymph nodes are found."&lt;SEP&gt;"The neck is the anatomical region where the thyroid gland is located."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLATE RECEPTOR ALPHA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Folate receptor alpha (FRα) is a biomarker expressed on some ovarian cancer cells, targeted by mirvetuximab soravtansine-gynx."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR GRADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of how abnormal cancer cells look under a microscope, used to guide treatment decisions for cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor grade is a measure of how abnormal cancer cells look under a microscope, indicating how quickly the cancer is likely to grow and spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor grade is a rating of how fast cancer is expected to grow and spread, based on how different tumor cells look from normal cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor grade is a rating of how fast doctors expect the cancer to grow and spread, influencing risk level."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor grade is how abnormal cancer cells look, used in staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor grade refers to how abnormal cancer cells look under a microscope, used in staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIDE AND BACK WALLS OF THROAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The side and back walls of the throat are part of the oropharynx and can be affected by throat cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCEROUS LYMPH NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancerous lymph nodes are lymph nodes that contain cancer cells, often removed during APR surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT OF THE CHEST AND ABDOMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CT of the chest and abdomen is an imaging test used to determine if rectal cancer has spread to the liver, lungs, or other organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROID NODULE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A growth or lump in the thyroid gland that may be benign or cancerous, evaluated through TSH tests, ultrasound, and biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BUN (blood urea nitrogen) is a blood test measuring kidney function, ordered if recurrence is suspected."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DERMATOLOGISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dermatologists are doctors who diagnose and treat skin conditions, including skin cancer, perform skin exams, and teach patients self-exams."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINICAL TRIAL COORDINATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinical Trial Coordinator is a professional who manages the logistics of clinical trials, including patient enrollment and data collection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TISSUE TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tissue tests are diagnostic procedures that examine tissue samples, often from biopsies, to identify cancer cells and their characteristics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL DEATH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell death is a natural process that cancer cells avoid, allowing them to accumulate and form tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VERTEBRAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vertebrae are bones that surround the spinal cord, providing protection to the central nervous system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RET MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RET mutations are genetic alterations that may be tested in ovarian cancer to guide targeted therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"RET mutations are genetic changes in the RET gene, tested as biomarkers to identify potential targeted therapies for ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"RET mutations are genetic changes tested as biomarkers in recurrent ovarian cancer for potential targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR TYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor type refers to the specific classification of cancer based on tissue analysis, including rare subtypes that may be more aggressive."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT SCAN WITH CONTRAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A CT scan with contrast is an imaging test used to visualize the main tumor and neck area to determine the extent of throat cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TISSUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tissues are biological materials imaged in dental x-rays and relevant to cancer diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissues are groups of cells that can be affected by cancer, and imaging tests evaluate them for spread or abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissues are groups of cells that make up organs, including those in the endocrine system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissues are groups of cells with similar structure and function, which may be removed during cancer surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissues are structures in the mouth and surrounding areas imaged in panoramic dental x-rays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EARLY RECTAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Early rectal cancer refers to cancer that has not spread far from the rectum, often treated with surgery or minimally invasive procedures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROID GLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An endocrine gland in the neck that may be affected by radiation therapy, requiring blood tests to monitor function."&lt;SEP&gt;"An endocrine gland in the neck that produces hormones regulating metabolism, often affected by nodules and cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The thyroid gland is an endocrine gland in the neck that can be affected by radiation therapy, requiring blood tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"The thyroid gland is the anatomical structure in the neck that produces hormones, also referred to as the thyroid."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CYTOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cervical cytology is another name for Pap testing, used to detect abnormal cells in the cervix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOHS SURGEONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mohs surgeons are doctors, usually dermatologists, with advanced training in Mohs surgery and reconstruction, removing tumors and ensuring no cancer remains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFLAMMATION OF THE BLADDER LINING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inflammation of the bladder lining is a side effect of intravesical therapy, causing swelling and discomfort."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMAGING TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Imaging Test is a diagnostic procedure, such as CT or MRI, to assess cancer status."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNODEFICIENCY DISORDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immunodeficiency disorder is an illness that weakens the immune system's ability to fight infections and diseases, increasing the risk of primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Head is a body part that may be scanned in CT or MRI to detect cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head is a region of the body containing lymph nodes, where head and neck cancers sometimes spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"The head is a common area where basal cell skin cancer develops due to sun exposure, and it is often the site of skin lesions associated with the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NTRK GENE FUSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NTRK gene fusions are genetic alterations that may be tested in ovarian cancer to guide targeted therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONNECTIVE TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A layer of tissue in the bladder wall that stage 1 cancer has invaded, but not the muscle layer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Connective tissue in a tumor is a sign of high-risk or very high-risk cancer, indicating potential for aggressive behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"Connective tissue is a type of tissue in the kidney where renal sarcoma can originate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Connective tissue is part of the breast structure, providing support and shape."&lt;SEP&gt;"Connective tissue is part of the submucosa layer, providing support and containing mucus glands, blood and lymph vessels, and nerves."&lt;SEP&gt;"Connective tissue is removed during punch biopsies and provides structural support to the skin, potentially involved in cancer invasion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Connective tissue is supportive tissue in the breast that holds structures together, including ligaments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Connective tissue is the material that makes up the lamina propria layer of the oral mucosa."&lt;SEP&gt;"Connective tissue supports and holds breast structures together, including ligaments and other tissues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissue in the breast that supports and connects structures like ducts and lobules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissue that holds the cervix in place, which may be partially removed during modified radical or radical hysterectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRI WITH OR WITHOUT CONTRAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An MRI with or without contrast is an imaging test used to provide detailed images of the throat and neck to assess tumor spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISPOSABLE BAG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Disposable bag is an external collection device used after colostomy to collect stool."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T1 TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A T1 tumor is a rectal cancer that has not grown beyond the second (muscle) layer of the rectal wall."&lt;SEP&gt;"T1 tumor is a primary tumor 8 cm or smaller in appendicular skeleton, torso, skull, or face."&lt;SEP&gt;"T1 tumor is a smaller tumor that may be treated with transabdominal surgery if certain conditions are met."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROID HORMONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormones produced by the thyroid gland that regulate metabolism, with levels assessed through TSH tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thyroid hormone refers to the collective term for T4 and T3, produced by the thyroid to regulate body functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAGINAL CYTOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vaginal cytology is another term for Pap testing, focusing on vaginal cells after hysterectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL ONCOLOGISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgical oncologists are doctors trained to diagnose and surgically treat and remove cancerous tumors, including those that have spread beyond the skin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGAN FUNCTION EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organ Function Education is understanding how tests assess kidney and liver health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORAL MUCOSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The oral mucosa is the mucous membrane lining the inside of the mouth and lips, composed of epithelium and lamina propria. Tumors can grow through its layers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOUTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mouth is a body part associated with mouth cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth is a body part through which scopes are passed in some procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth is a body part."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth is an anatomical site where a scope may be inserted for throat examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth is an entry point for scopes in endoscopy and laryngoscopy procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth is examined during panendoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth is the entry point of the digestive system where food and drink enter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mouth is the location where squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) can develop, as described in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mouth is a site where HPV can infect and cause cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mouth is the entry point of the digestive system where food and drink enter."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHOVASCULAR INVASION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymphovascular invasion is the presence of cancer cells in blood or lymph vessels, increasing the risk of spread to lymph nodes and other parts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphovascular invasion is the presence of cancer cells in blood or lymph vessels, indicating a higher risk of spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONONUCLEOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mononucleosis (mono) is an illness caused by the Epstein-Barr virus, which is a risk factor for primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEST CT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chest CT is an imaging test used to check for cancer spread to the lungs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chest CT is a computed tomography scan of the chest, used to check for cancer spread to lungs or lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chest CT is an imaging test used to check for cancer spread to the lungs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WARTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Warts are abnormal skin growths caused by HPV infection that can form on the anus or genitals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warts are abnormal tissue growths caused by HPV infection, which can occur in various body areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warts are abnormal tissue growths caused by HPV infection, which can sometimes lead to cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warts are abnormal tissue growths caused by HPV infection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warts are skin growths that can resemble actinic keratoses, which are precancerous lesions that may develop into squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOSCOPIC SUBMUCOSAL DISSECTION (ESD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ESD is a minimally invasive procedure that removes small rectal cancers in one piece, often curing them. It is recommended for T1 tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPERTHYROIDISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition of overactive thyroid where hormone levels are high, often indicated by low TSH levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hyperthyroidism is a condition of overactive thyroid with high hormone levels, indicated by low TSH levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR GENE TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor gene testing focuses on specific genes in cancer cells to identify actionable mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor gene testing is another name for biomarker testing, focusing on gene mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL ONCOLOGISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medical oncologists are doctors who specialize in prescribing cancer-treatment drugs like chemotherapy, which can be taken orally, injected, or given intravenously."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR AND ONCOCYTIC CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follicular and oncocytic carcinoma are types of differentiated thyroid cancer, typically slow-growing, treated with surgery and possibly other therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC FLOOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The pelvic floor is a group of muscles supporting pelvic organs, crucial for bowel, bladder, and sexual function, often affected by anal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAGNOSTIC COLONOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A colonoscopy performed to thoroughly examine the colon and look for other possible areas of cancer after initial detection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUPUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A connective tissue disease that may make radiation therapy inappropriate for some patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lupus is an autoimmune disease in which the immune system overreacts and attacks healthy tissues and organs, increasing the risk of primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lip is a part of the mouth where mucosa can be affected by squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECONDARY CYTOREDUCTIVE SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Secondary cytoreductive surgery is a procedure to remove visible cancer before recurrence treatment, considered in certain circumstances for platinum-sensitive cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEAKENED IMMUNE SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition that increases the likelihood of developing squamous cell skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A weakened immune system increases the risk of developing CSCC and having it return after treatment, often due to conditions like HIV or organ transplant."&lt;SEP&gt;"A weakened immune system, which can result from organ transplantation, lymphoma, chronic lymphocytic leukemia, HIV/AIDS, or other conditions, reduces the body's ability to fight infections and diseases, increasing the risk of squamous cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOSCOPY WITH EXAMINATION UNDER ANESTHESIA (EUA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endoscopy with EUA is a procedure to examine the throat and oropharynx under anesthesia for a thorough assessment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCAR TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scar tissue can form after surgery and potentially block the bowel, a possible complication of colectomy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scar tissue is a health condition that can cause lung nodules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Scar tissue is fibrous tissue that forms after injury or radiation, potentially causing narrowing in vaginal stenosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOSCOPIC MUCOSAL RESECTION (EMR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EMR is another name for endoscopic submucosal dissection, a procedure to remove small rectal cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPOTHYROIDISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition of underactive thyroid where hormone levels are low, often indicated by high TSH levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPREHENSIVE GENOMIC PROFILING (CGP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Comprehensive genomic profiling (CGP) is an extensive analysis of tumor DNA to identify all potential therapeutic targets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATHOLOGISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pathologists are doctors trained to study tissue and cells removed during a biopsy under a microscope to determine the stage of a cancerous tumor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RACING HEART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Racing heart, with or without an abnormal heartbeat, is a common side effect of an incorrect levothyroxine dose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMPLOYMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Employment concerns relate to work-related issues faced by cancer survivors during and after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANDIBLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mandible is a bone in the jaw that can be invaded by tumor in T4a stage of mouth cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW-RISK CSCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low-risk CSCC is a classification of squamous cell carcinoma with lower risk of spread, typically treated with surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEREDITARY MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene change inherited from parents, present in every cell of the body, also called germline mutation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hereditary mutation is a genetic abnormality passed down in families, but gliomas are not typically caused by such mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hereditary mutation is a genetic abnormality passed down in families, but primary CNS lymphoma is not typically caused by this type of mutation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRE-ANESTHESIA EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pre-anesthesia exam is a medical evaluation to ensure the patient is fit for anesthesia before procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pre-anesthesia exam is an assessment by an anesthesiologist to evaluate a patient's suitability for anesthesia before surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEREDITARY GENE TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of genetic test that looks for inherited germline mutations in genes like BRCA1, BRCA2, ATM, and others, using blood, urine, or saliva samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSANAL LOCAL EXCISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transanal local excision is a surgical procedure to remove T1 tumors located at the end of the rectum through the anus, cutting through all layers of the rectal wall."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tests that analyze genetic or molecular markers in biopsy samples to help determine if a nodule is cancerous and whether surgery is necessary."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BILE DUCT CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bile duct cancer is a disease characterized by abnormal cell growth in the bile duct, with stages defined by tumor size and spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bile duct cancer is a type of cancer that affects the bile ducts, with stages described based on tumor size and layers involved."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC SURGEONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic surgeons are doctors who can remove cancer and reconstruct, restore, and repair body parts, often working with pathologists during surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESEARCH NURSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Research Nurse is a nurse who supports patients in clinical trials, monitoring side effects and ensuring protocol compliance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADVANCED STAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Advanced stage refers to bladder cancer that has progressed, potentially spreading beyond the bladder to other organs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NERVOUS SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nervous system is the system that includes the CNS and other parts, and primary CNS lymphoma can spread to other areas within it."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nervous system includes the brain and spinal cord. Primary CNS lymphoma affects this system, leading to various neurological symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAXILLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maxilla is a bone in the upper jaw that can be invaded by tumor in T4a stage of mouth cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOCRINE THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A treatment that blocks estrogen receptor signaling in hormone receptor-positive breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endocrine therapy blocks or reduces hormones like estrogen and progesterone to treat hormone receptor-positive breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endocrine therapy is a drug treatment that blocks or lowers hormones to treat hormone receptor-positive breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endocrine therapy is a systemic treatment that targets hormone receptors to slow or stop cancer growth, often used based on ER and PR expression."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endocrine therapy is a treatment option for recurrent ovarian cancer, using hormones to slow cancer growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endocrine therapy is a treatment option that blocks hormones to slow or stop cancer growth, mentioned in treatment overview."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endocrine therapy is a treatment that blocks hormones to slow cancer growth, part of treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endocrine therapy is a treatment that may be used during premenopause, affecting hormone levels and potentially causing amenorrhea."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-RISK CSCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-risk CSCC is a classification of squamous cell carcinoma with higher risk of recurrence or spread, requiring more aggressive treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-risk CSCC is a squamous cell skin cancer with an increased risk of local recurrence, determined by factors like location, size, tumor shape, and recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITION, SPEECH, AND SWALLOWING EVALUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutrition, speech, and swallowing evaluation is an assessment to address potential side effects of NPC treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"This evaluation assesses the patient's ability to eat, speak, and swallow, which may be affected by throat cancer and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of genetic test that analyzes tumor tissue or blood for molecular markers to predict cancer spread and guide targeted therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSANAL ENDOSCOPIC MICROSURGERY (TEM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TEM is an advanced technique for removing tumors higher in the rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of thyroid lesion where fine-needle biopsy can identify cell nature but cannot determine cancer, often requiring surgery for diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAHEPATIC BILE DUCT CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intrahepatic bile duct cancer is a type of bile duct cancer occurring within the liver, with staging based on tumor characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intrahepatic bile duct cancer is a type of bile duct cancer with specific staging guidelines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAD AND NECK SURGEONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Head and neck surgeons are doctors trained to treat conditions of the deeper parts of the head and neck, including ears, nose, and throat."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN OR BURNING FEELING WHEN URINATING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pain or burning when urinating is a side effect of intravesical therapy, indicating bladder irritation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER SPREAD EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Spread Education is learning how tests detect metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VERY HIGH-RISK CSCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Very high-risk CSCC is a classification of squamous cell carcinoma with the highest risk of recurrence or spread, often treated with Mohs surgery or PDEMA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Very high-risk CSCC is a squamous cell skin cancer with an increased risk of local recurrence and metastasis, based on factors like size and nerve invasion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROLOGICAL SYMPTOMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neurological symptoms are difficulties caused by pressure on the central nervous system from a lymphoma tumor, including headaches, nausea, vomiting, or seizures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neurological symptoms are difficulties such as headaches, nausea, vomiting, or seizures, caused by pressure from a lymphoma tumor on the CNS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEARING TEST (AUDIOGRAM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hearing test (audiogram) is used to assess hearing function, which may be affected by certain treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hearing test (audiogram) is an evaluation to check hearing, which may be affected by NPC treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR STAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A system (TNM) used to describe tumor size, lymph node involvement, and metastasis based on imaging, biopsies, and blood tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor staging is a system used to describe the extent of cancer in the body, including tumor size, lymph node involvement, and metastasis, based on imaging, biopsies, and blood tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSANAL MINIMALLY INVASIVE SURGERY (TAMIS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TAMIS is an advanced technique for removing tumors higher in the rectum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONCOCYTIC TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of thyroid lesion where fine-needle biopsy can identify cell nature but cannot determine cancer, often requiring surgery for diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follicular lymphoma (FL) is a slow-growing, indolent non-Hodgkin lymphoma that develops from abnormal B lymphocytes forming follicles in lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIATION ONCOLOGISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiation oncologists are doctors trained to use different types of radiation therapy for cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TSH BLOOD TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TSH blood test is a diagnostic test measuring thyroid-stimulating hormone levels to assess thyroid function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEEKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The cheeks are part of the mouth that hold food in place and help form and sound words."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THROAT CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Throat cancer is a specific cancer type."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat cancer is a type of cancer that occurs in the throat, with staging based on p16 status and TNM scores, ranging from stage 0 to stage 4."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat cancer is a type of cancer that starts in the oropharynx, which includes the soft palate, tonsils, side and back walls of the throat, and base of the tongue. It is a focus of the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat cancer is a type of head and neck cancer often related to HPV, and may be tested in nasopharyngeal cancer cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat cancer is a type of head and neck cancer that can form in the pharynx, including the oropharynx, and is mentioned as a separate topic in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat cancer is the specific cancer type for which p16 (HPV) testing is recommended."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat cancer refers to cancer that develops in the oropharynx or related throat areas. The text provides guidance on testing, treatment planning, and management for this condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat cancer, including oropharyngeal cancer, is the disease being discussed, with staging and biomarker testing guiding treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Throat cancer, particularly squamous cell carcinoma of the oropharynx, is discussed in relation to HPV and p16 testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CURETTAGE AND ELECTRODESICCATION (C&amp;E)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Curettage and electrodesiccation (C&amp;E) is a recommended surgical treatment for local, low-risk CSCC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Curettage and electrodesiccation (C&amp;E) is a surgical treatment option for low-risk CSCC, involving scraping and burning the tumor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Curettage and electrodesiccation is a two-step procedure involving scraping off the tumor and burning the base with an electric needle to kill remaining cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERSONALITY CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Personality changes are a symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, affecting behavior and mental state."&lt;SEP&gt;"Personality changes are symptoms of primary CNS lymphoma, including changes in behavior, depression, confusion, or memory problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Personality changes or mood alterations are symptoms of gliomas, affecting behavior and emotional state."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HELP TO QUIT SMOKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Help to quit smoking is a support service offered to patients to reduce risk factors and improve treatment outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Help to quit smoking is a support service offered to patients to reduce tobacco use, a risk factor for throat cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FANCA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene involved in DNA repair; mutations are associated with increased cancer risk, including prostate cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLEXIBLE SIGMOIDOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flexible sigmoidoscopy is a procedure used to examine the lower part of the colon and rectum, often used in surveillance after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENTIATED THYROID CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A group of thyroid cancers including papillary, follicular, and oncocytic types that usually grow and spread slowly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Differentiated thyroid cancer includes papillary and follicular types, which often take up iodine and respond to RAI therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T LYMPHOCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T lymphocytes (T cells) are a type of lymphocyte that help fight infections, kill tumor cells, and control immune responses."&lt;SEP&gt;"T lymphocytes, or T cells, are a type of lymphocyte that help fight infections, cancer, and control immune responses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHARMACISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pharmacists are medical professionals trained to prepare and give out medicine, explain proper use and side effects, with some specializing in cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOACTIVE IODINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radioactive iodine is a substance used in uptake tests and treatment for thyroid conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC FLOOR SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pelvic floor specialist is a healthcare professional trained in therapies to strengthen pelvic floor muscles, often consulted by anal cancer survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONG-TERM SIDE EFFECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Effects of cancer treatment that persist, addressed in survivorship care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWEATING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sweating is a common side effect of an incorrect levothyroxine dose, indicating metabolic overactivity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Disability concerns relate to physical or mental limitations that may affect cancer survivors' daily life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHARYNX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The pharynx is a hollow, muscular tube inside the neck that starts behind the nose and opens into the larynx and esophagus. It has three parts: nasopharynx, oropharynx, and hypopharynx."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pharynx is part of the throat, and cancer spread to it is considered in advanced disease staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pharynx is part of the throat, located in the back of the mouth and neck, where throat cancer can develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pharynx is the anatomical region that includes the nasopharynx, oropharynx, and hypopharynx, and is relevant to throat cancer staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pharynx is the throat, which includes the nasopharynx, oropharynx, and laryngopharynx. The parapharyngeal space is located near the pharynx."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHAVE EXCISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shave excision is a surgical treatment option for low-risk CSCC, involving cutting off the tumor at skin level."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COORDINATION PROBLEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coordination problems are symptoms of primary CNS lymphoma, including leg or arm weakness or difficulty with movement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIRROR EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A mirror exam is a procedure using a special mirror to view parts of the oropharynx that are not easily visible."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mirror exam is a procedure using a mirror to view the oropharynx and nasopharynx, part of head and neck examination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASHKENAZI JEWISH ANCESTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ethnic background associated with a higher prevalence of certain inherited mutations, such as BRCA1 and BRCA2, increasing cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry is a demographic factor that increases the risk of having germline mutations in genes like BRCA1 and BRCA2, making germline testing recommended."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSABDOMINAL SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transabdominal surgery is a preferred next treatment when more treatment is needed after local excision, such as when high-risk features are found or the tumor is larger than expected."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transabdominal surgery is a surgical method involving cutting into the abdomen to remove rectal tumors, surrounding tissue, and lymph nodes, used for tumors invading the muscle layer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYROID CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A disease where malignant cells form in the thyroid gland, with several types including papillary, follicular, medullary, and anaplastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thyroid cancer encompasses various types including papillary, follicular, and oncocytic carcinoma, with treatment approaches varying based on type, invasiveness, and spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thyroid cancer is a disease characterized by abnormal cell growth in the thyroid gland, with differentiated types (papillary, follicular) being more common and responsive to certain treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thyroid cancer is a disease characterized by abnormal cell growth in the thyroid gland. It includes subtypes such as papillary, follicular, and oncocytic carcinoma, and treatment varies based on type and stage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thyroid cancer is a type of cancer that affects the thyroid gland. It can be treated with radiation therapy, systemic therapy, targeted therapy, or chemotherapy. Targeted therapies are used for thyroid cancers that cannot be treated with surgery or RAI therapy, have returned, or have metastasized. Anaplastic thyroid cancer is the least common and most aggressive type, often treated with chemotherapy combined with radiation therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thyroid cancer is a type of cancer that arises from thyroid cells, often presenting as nodules, and is most common in adults aged 18-33."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thyroid cancer is a type of cancer that may not take up iodine, leading to consideration of targeted therapy, monitoring, or other treatments. It is a condition that can be managed with levothyroxine to suppress TSH levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATURAL KILLER CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Natural killer (NK) cells are a type of lymphocyte that can kill tumor cells or virus-infected cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETICISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Geneticists are doctors who study how traits are passed down through genes, diagnose and treat genetic disorders, and counsel families at risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VISIBLE LUMP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A visible lump in the neck is a symptom of a larger thyroid nodule."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOTE TAKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Note Taking is writing down questions and information during appointments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DATA MANAGER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Data Manager is a professional who handles data collection and analysis in clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OROPHARYNX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oropharynx is a body part examined in panendoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oropharynx is a body part."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oropharynx is a part of the body examined during scoping procedures, such as endoscopy, to assess tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oropharynx is part of the throat examined during panendoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oropharynx includes the back of the roof of the mouth (soft palate), the tonsils, the side and back walls of the throat, and the base of the tongue found in the throat. It is one of the three parts of the pharynx."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oropharynx is a part of the throat including the back of the roof of the mouth, where cancer can form."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oropharynx is a part of the throat near the nasopharynx where nasopharyngeal cancer can spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oropharynx is a part of the throat that includes the back of the roof of the mouth (soft palate), tonsils, side and back walls of the throat, and base of the tongue. It is referred to as the throat in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oropharynx is a part of the throat, located inside, with areas not easily visible without special tools like a mirror or fiberoptic scope."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oropharynx is part of the throat behind the mouth, and tumor growth into this area is considered in T1 staging of nasopharyngeal carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oropharynx is part of the throat, located behind the mouth, and is examined during head and neck exams for cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oropharynx is the anatomical region in the throat that includes the soft palate, tonsils, side and back walls of the throat, and the base of the tongue. It is the focus of the text, which discusses testing and treatment for throat cancer in this area."&lt;SEP&gt;"The oropharynx is the middle part of the throat near the mouth, a site for head and neck cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STANDARD SURGICAL EXCISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Standard surgical excision is a procedure to remove a tumor along with a margin of normal tissue, with edges examined by a pathologist."&lt;SEP&gt;"Standard surgical excision is a recommended treatment option for high-risk or very high-risk local CSCC, involving removal of a wider margin of normal tissue around the lesion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Standard surgical excision is a surgical treatment option for CSCC, involving removal of the tumor with a margin of normal tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Standard surgical excision is a type of surgery for squamous cell skin cancer, involving removal of the tumor and a margin of healthy tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLURRY VISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blurry vision is a symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, affecting eyesight."&lt;SEP&gt;"Blurry vision is a symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, related to changes in eyesight."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIBEROPTIC EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A fiberoptic exam uses a flexible scope passed through the mouth or nose to inspect the oropharynx and throat."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARP INHIBITORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Targeted therapies used against cancers with specific molecular tumor markers, such as mutations in DNA repair genes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. GOOGLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Google is a colloquial term referring to using internet search engines for medical advice, which is discouraged in favor of reputable sources."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-GRADE SEROUS CARCINOMA (HGSC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-grade serous carcinoma (HGSC) is one of the most common forms of epithelial ovarian cancer, characterized by high-grade cancer cells that grow and spread quickly."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GERMINAL CENTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Germinal centers are temporary structures in lymph nodes that form in response to infection or inflammation, where B cells can grow out of control leading to follicular lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONCOLOGY NURSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oncology nurses provide hands-on care, including administering systemic therapy, managing care, and helping with side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oncology nurses provide hands-on care, including giving systemic therapy, managing care, answering questions, and helping patients cope with side effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NECK PAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neck pain is a symptom that can occur with larger thyroid nodules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neck pain or swelling in glands near the jaw is a possible side effect of RAI therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGULAR FOLLOW-UP TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Regular follow-up tests are scheduled examinations conducted over many years to monitor for bladder cancer recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TINGLING OR NUMBNESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tingling or numbness is a side effect of chemotherapy, affecting nerves and sensation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAD AND NECK CANCERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Head and neck cancers are a group of cancers that arise in the head or neck area, and NPC is one of them. They are associated with risk factors like tobacco and alcohol use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and neck cancers are a group of cancers that arise in the head or neck area, including the mouth, oropharynx, nasal cavity, nasopharynx, larynx, and hypopharynx. Squamous cell carcinoma is the most common type."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and neck cancers are a group of cancers that include throat cancer, affecting areas like the pharynx and oropharynx."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOHS SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mohs surgery is a precise surgical technique for removing skin cancer layer by layer, often used for high-risk or very high-risk CSCC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mohs surgery is a precise surgical technique that removes skin cancer layer by layer, examining each layer for cancer cells until none remain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mohs surgery is a recommended surgical technique for local CSCC, particularly for high-risk or very high-risk cases, and is a form of PDEMA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mohs surgery is a specialized surgical technique used to remove skin cancer tumors layer by layer, ensuring complete removal while preserving healthy tissue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-SMALL CELL LUNG CANCER (NSCLC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-small cell lung cancer is a common type of lung cancer that includes subtypes such as adenocarcinoma, squamous cell carcinoma, large cell carcinoma, and others. It accounts for a majority of lung cancer cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-small cell lung cancer is a group of cancers that are the most common type of lung cancer. Subtypes include adenocarcinoma, squamous cell carcinoma, and large cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRIEND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A friend is a supportive individual who may drive the patient to appointments or provide emotional support during treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A friend is someone who can provide support, such as driving to appointments or offering meals, during diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Friend is a person who can provide emotional support and practical help during diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Friend is a type of support person who can help a patient during stressful medical times."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SALIVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bodily fluid used for genetic testing for inherited cancer syndromes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bodily fluid used for genetic testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bodily fluid used for hereditary gene testing to collect DNA samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bodily fluid used for genetic testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fluid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saliva is a biological sample that can be used for genetic testing when AML cells are in remission, to assess predisposition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saliva is a bodily fluid that can be sampled for genetic testing to identify inherited mutations related to cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saliva is a bodily fluid used in genetic testing, collected by spitting into a cup or cheek swab."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saliva is a sample type used for genetic testing, collected via spitting or cheek swab."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSATELLITE STABLE (MSS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker indicating no microsatellite instability, meaning the cancer is mismatch repair proficient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellite stable (MSS) is a molecular characteristic of tumors indicating they do not have high levels of genetic mutations in microsatellite regions, which can affect treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellite stable is a biomarker status in rectal tumors indicating no high instability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LESS COMMON OVARIAN CANCERS (LCOCS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LCOCs are rare ovarian cancer types where tumor markers like inhibin, β-hCG, AFP, LDH, CEA, CA 19-9, and HE4 may be elevated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Less common ovarian cancers (LCOCs), also known as less common ovarian histologies (LCOHs), are rare types of ovarian cancer that can start in the epithelium, supporting tissues, or reproductive cells of the ovary. They include low-grade serous carcinoma, low-grade endometrioid carcinoma, carcinosarcoma, clear cell carcinoma, mucinous carcinoma, and borderline epithelial tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTROCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Centrocytes are small B cells in the light zone of germinal centers, less numerous and dividing less than centroblasts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECONSTRUCTIVE SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reconstructive surgery is a procedure performed by Mohs surgeons or plastic surgeons to restore the appearance and function of areas affected by cancer removal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reconstructive surgery is a procedure to rebuild the breast after mastectomy or lumpectomy, improving appearance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOICE CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Voice changes are a symptom that can occur with larger thyroid nodules."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOLOGIST ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiologist Role Education is understanding the radiologist's part in diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PDEMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PDEMA (peripheral deep excision with margin assessment) is a category of surgical techniques, including Mohs surgery, used for treating CSCC."&lt;SEP&gt;"PDEMA (peripheral deep excision with margin assessment) is a surgical technique similar to Mohs surgery, used for high-risk CSCC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peripheral and deep en face margin assessment (PDEMA) is a surgical technique that allows complete testing of removed tissue edges, often used for head, face, and other sensitive areas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL CELL LUNG CANCER (SCLC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Small cell lung cancer is a fast-dividing cancer of neuroendocrine cells, with cells that look small and oval- or oat-shaped under a microscope."&lt;SEP&gt;"Small cell lung cancer is a fast-dividing cancer of the neuroendocrine cells, appearing small and oval- or oat-shaped under a microscope. It is the second most common type of lung cancer and is strongly associated with smoking."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAMILY MEMBER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A family member is a relative who may provide support, such as meals or emotional assistance, during diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A family member is someone who can provide support, such as driving to appointments or offering meals, during diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Family Member is an individual who provides emotional and practical support to the patient during treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Family member is a relative who can offer support and accompany the patient to appointments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bodily fluid where blood may appear after a prostate biopsy, usually resolving within weeks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Semen is a fluid made up of liquids from the prostate and seminal vesicles as well as sperm from the testicles, released during ejaculation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Semen is the fluid containing sperm that is stored during sperm banking for fertility preservation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Semen is the fluid containing sperm, which is stored via sperm banking for fertility preservation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Semen is the fluid that transports sperm, where PSA is primarily found, with small amounts entering the bloodstream."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-METASTATIC CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer that has not spread to distant areas, treated with surgery, chemotherapy, and surveillance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colon cancer that has not spread to distant organs, with treatment options including polypectomy, colectomy, and chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-metastatic cancer refers to cancer that has not spread to distant organs, focusing treatment on the primary site."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY PERITONEAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Primary peritoneal cancer forms in the tissue that lines the abdominal wall and covers abdominal organs. Treatment information for ovarian cancer also applies to this type of cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTROBLASTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Centroblasts are large B cells in the dark zone of germinal centers that reproduce more, and their presence influences lymphoma grade."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NURSE NAVIGATORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nurse navigators are oncology nurses who guide patients through the healthcare system, managing care and answering questions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TROUBLE BREATHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trouble breathing is a symptom that can occur with larger thyroid nodules."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NASAL CAVITY AND PARANASAL SINUSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The nasal cavity and paranasal sinuses are spaces behind the nose where head and neck cancer can occur."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVARIAN CANCER SURVIVOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An ovarian cancer survivor is an individual who has experienced ovarian cancer and provides a quote about life-changing experiences, indicating personal perspective."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARGE CELL CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Large cell carcinoma is a subtype of NSCLC that starts in large cells that can grow anywhere in the lungs. It accounts for 5 out of 10 NSCLCs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Large cell carcinoma is a subtype of non-small cell lung cancer that starts in large cells that can grow anywhere in the lungs. It accounts for about 5 out of 10 NSCLCs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Large cell carcinoma is a type of NSCLC that forms from large cells found throughout the airways."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A peer is a person in a similar situation who can offer support and understanding during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A peer is someone who can provide support, such as driving to appointments or offering meals, during diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peer is a person in a similar situation who can provide support and understanding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GERMLINE MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A hereditary gene change present in every cell, passed down from parents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Germline mutation is an inherited genetic change from birth parents that can increase cancer risk and be passed to offspring."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOSCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An endoscope is a flexible tube with a camera used to visualize and operate inside the rectum."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endoscope is a general term for instruments used in procedures like esophagoscopy and bronchoscopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endoscope is a type of scope used in imaging tests, guided into the body through the mouth or nose to examine areas and guide biopsies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW-GRADE SEROUS CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low-grade serous carcinoma is a less common epithelial ovarian cancer characterized by low-grade cancer cells that grow and spread more slowly than high-grade cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The World Health Organization (WHO) is an international organization that classifies follicular lymphoma grades, with the 2022 classification (WHO5) defining grades 1, 2, and 3A as classic FL."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization works globally to prevent and control cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"World Health Organization is a global health organization that addresses cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARAC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carac is a brand name for 5-fluorouracil, a topical chemotherapy cream used to treat early CSCC and actinic keratoses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEMS SWALLOWING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Problems swallowing are a common side effect of radiation therapy to the neck area, affecting eating."&lt;SEP&gt;"Problems swallowing are a symptom that can occur with larger thyroid nodules."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REDUCED SEX DRIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reduced sex drive, or low libido, is a common sexual side effect experienced by anal cancer survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STANDARD CANCER CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Standard cancer care refers to conventional treatments for cancer that continue during a clinical trial, billed to insurance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESOURCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Additional information or support available for patients, as mentioned in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEAKENED BONES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weakened bones are a potential health problem from too much levothyroxine, increasing fracture risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACUPUNCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acupuncture is a complementary therapy involving needle insertion to relieve symptoms and improve well-being."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSY (SLNB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sentinel lymph node biopsy (SLNB) is a procedure to identify and remove the first lymph nodes where cancer cells are likely to spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sentinel lymph node biopsy (SLNB) is a procedure to identify and test the first lymph nodes where cancer might have spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUNG CANCER SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lung cancer screening is a medical procedure aimed at detecting lung cancer at an early stage, before symptoms appear, to improve treatment success and prevent death. It is recommended for individuals at high risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lung cancer screening is a process for people at high risk for lung cancer, using imaging tests to detect the disease at its earliest, most treatable stages."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIND AND BODY THERAPISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mind and body therapists are professionals who help cancer patients manage stress and distress through psychological and physical techniques."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mind and body therapists are professionals who provide counseling and support to help patients cope with cancer-related distress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mind and body therapists are professionals who provide support and counseling to help patients cope with the emotional and psychological aspects of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Therapists who offer support and counseling to help patients cope with the mental and physical aspects of cancer diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The basic structural unit of living organisms, containing DNA and performing vital functions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUID INJECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fluid injection is a technique used during ESD to lift and separate the tumor from the muscle layer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW-GRADE ENDOMETRIOID CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low-grade endometrioid carcinoma is a less common epithelial ovarian cancer with low-grade cancer cells that grow and spread more slowly."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL CONSENSUS CLASSIFICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The International Consensus Classification (ICC) is an organization that groups follicular lymphoma grades 1 and 2 as classic FL, and is followed in this text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EFUDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Efudex is a brand name for 5-fluorouracil, a topical chemotherapy cream used to treat early CSCC and actinic keratoses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYSTEMIC CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Systemic chemotherapy is a whole-body therapy that uses drugs to kill cancer cells throughout the body, often given intravenously, and may cause side effects by harming some healthy cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPOINTMENT ATTENDANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Appointment Attendance is bringing the medical binder to scheduled visits."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CA-125 LEVEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CA-125 is a tumor marker that may be checked regularly after treatment to monitor for ovarian cancer recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMOKING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Smoking is a behavior that negatively affects treatment outcomes and increases toxicity in mouth cancer patients, with a strong recommendation to stop."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a behavioral risk factor that significantly increases the likelihood of developing bladder cancer and other diseases, and quitting can reduce risk and improve treatment outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a habit involving inhaling tobacco smoke, which increases cancer risk and can impair treatment effectiveness and healing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a habit that can limit cancer treatment effectiveness and increase risks of lung problems and other cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a habit that increases cancer risk and can limit treatment effectiveness, wound healing, and increase side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a habit that increases cancer risk, and quitting is recommended with doctor-provided counseling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a habit that increases the risk of head and neck, lung, and other cancers, and can limit treatment effectiveness and wound healing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a lifestyle factor that increases the risk of developing and dying from prostate cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a lifestyle-related risk factor that increases the risk of anal cancer by weakening the immune system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a major risk factor for SCLC, involving the inhalation of tobacco smoke, which increases the likelihood of developing lung cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a major risk factor for lung cancer, particularly SCLC. It involves inhaling tobacco smoke, which contains carcinogens that damage lung cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a risk factor for anal cancer, contributing to cellular damage and increased cancer susceptibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a risk factor for cancer and other health issues, and quitting is recommended for anal cancer survivors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a risk factor for cervical cancer, potentially increasing exposure to HPV or weakening the immune system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is a risk factor that can limit cancer treatment effectiveness and increase side effects, with quitting recommended."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is the act of inhaling tobacco smoke, which delivers nicotine and carcinogens, leading to addiction and increased cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is the greatest risk factor for bladder cancer, accounting for about half of all cases, and secondhand smoke also increases risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking is the greatest risk factor for bladder cancer, contributing to genetic mutations that lead to the disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Smoking or vaping nicotine increases the risk of developing head and neck, lung, and other cancers. It can limit cancer treatment effectiveness, prevent wound healing, and increase surgical side effects. Quitting is essential for maximizing cure chances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECONDHAND SMOKE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Secondhand smoke is smoke inhaled by non-smokers from others' tobacco use, increasing their risk of bladder cancer and other diseases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Secondhand smoke is the smoke exhaled by another person or from combustible tobacco products, which also increases the risk of lung cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Secondhand smoke is the smoke exhaled by another person or from combustible tobacco products. Exposure to it increases the risk of developing lung cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Secondhand smoke is the smoke exhaled by another person or from the burning end of tobacco products, and exposure to it increases the risk of lung cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPPORT AND COUNSELING SERVICES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Support and counseling services are available to help patients deal with emotional and psychological challenges of cancer diagnosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UTERINE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer associated with inherited mutations in genes like MSH2, MSH6, MLH1, and PMS2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Uterine cancer is a type of cancer that can be related to germline mutations in genes like MSH2, MSH6, MLH1, and PMS2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Uterine cancer is a type of cancer that occurs in the uterus, distinct from cervical cancer in diagnosis and treatment. It includes endometrial cancer and uterine sarcomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH RISK FEATURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High risk features in removed tissue indicate a higher chance of cancer recurrence, necessitating additional treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"High risk features in removed tissues indicate the need for more treatment after local excision."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARCINOSARCOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carcinosarcoma, also called malignant mixed Mullerian tumors, is a less common epithelial ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLASSIC FL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Classic FL (cFL) is a term for follicular lymphoma grades 1, 2, and 3A according to WHO5, or grades 1 and 2 according to ICC, treated as a slow-growing lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLUOROPLEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fluoroplex is a brand name for 5-fluorouracil, a topical chemotherapy cream used to treat early CSCC and actinic keratoses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOSE-DENSE CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dose-dense chemotherapy is a method of speeding up chemotherapy by shortening the time between treatment doses, often used for bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SYMPTOMS OF BLADDER CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Symptoms of bladder cancer are signs that prompt medical investigation, such as blood in urine or changes in urination."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMOOTH MUSCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Smooth muscle is a type of muscle in the lower esophagus that is not under voluntary control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIRITUAL SUPPORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spiritual support is a component of supportive care, addressing existential and religious needs of cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR MARKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor markers are substances in blood or tissue that may indicate the presence of cancer, used to monitor treatment response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor markers are substances in body tissue or fluid that may indicate cancer. They help diagnose ovarian cancer and monitor treatment response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor markers are substances in the blood that may indicate cancer presence, such as CA-125, used in surveillance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NICOTINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nicotine is a chemical in tobacco that causes addiction to smoking and vaping, making quitting challenging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nicotine is a chemical in tobacco that causes addiction, making quitting smoking challenging and impacting cancer treatment effectiveness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nicotine is a substance in smoking and vaping that increases cancer risk and impairs healing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nicotine is the addictive chemical in tobacco that leads to continued smoking or vaping. Nicotine withdrawal is challenging, especially under cancer-related stress. Counseling and medicines can help with quitting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nicotine is the addictive chemical in tobacco that makes quitting challenging, especially under cancer-related stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nicotine is the addictive chemical in tobacco that makes quitting smoking challenging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nicotine is the chemical in tobacco that causes addiction and makes quitting smoking challenging, especially for cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nicotine is the chemical in tobacco that causes addiction, and withdrawal is challenging, especially under the stress of cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH CARE PROVIDER (HCP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A health care provider (HCP) is a medical professional who receives imaging reports and discusses results with patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health Care Provider (HCP) is a medical professional responsible for discussing imaging results and guiding cancer treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care providers are medical professionals who assess risk factors, recommend screenings, and guide patients in lung cancer prevention and treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Health care providers are medical professionals who evaluate test results, conduct physical exams, and guide patients through diagnosis and treatment of NPC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DENTIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A dental professional who conducts dental exams and checkups for head and neck cancer patients to maintain oral health."&lt;SEP&gt;"A dentist is a health professional who performs dental cleanings and checkups, and may recommend dental work before cancer treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A dentist is a healthcare professional who performs panoramic dental x-rays and may use them to plan treatment for dental conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A dentist is a healthcare professional who provides dental care and checkups, important for patients with head and neck cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dentist is a dental professional who is advised to be informed about head and neck cancer to manage oral health, including jaw, teeth, and gums, during treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dentist is a dental professional who monitors oral health in head and neck cancer patients, as treatment can affect the jaw and teeth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dentist is a dental professional who performs panoramic x-rays and plans treatments for oral health issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dentist is a healthcare professional who commonly performs panoramic dental x-rays and may use them for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dentist is a healthcare professional who should be informed about head and neck cancer to manage oral health during treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dentists are healthcare professionals who should be informed about a patient's head and neck cancer to manage oral health during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer mentioned in family history criteria for recommending inherited gene testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal cancer is mentioned as a type of cancer in family history that may indicate a need for germline testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T2 TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A T2 tumor is a rectal cancer that has invaded the muscle layer of the rectal wall, requiring more extensive surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"T2 tumor is a classification indicating the tumor has invaded the muscle layer of the rectal wall, requiring transabdominal surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"T2 tumor is a primary tumor larger than 8 cm in appendicular skeleton, torso, skull, or face."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLEAR CELL CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clear cell carcinoma is a less common epithelial ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFUSE LARGE B-CELL LYMPHOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) is a more aggressive type of non-Hodgkin lymphoma, which may be considered in treatment for grade 3A follicular lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALDARA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aldara is a brand name for imiquimod, a prescription cream used to treat early CSCC and actinic keratoses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DDMVAC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ddMVAC is a combination of medicines (dose-dense methotrexate, vinblastine, doxorubicin, and cisplatin) used as systemic chemotherapy for bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COCCYX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coccyx, or tailbone, is the final part of the spine, attached to the sacrum."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOCTOR ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Doctor Role Education is understanding the doctor's role in discussing results."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATINUM-BASED CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Platinum-based chemotherapy includes drugs like carboplatin, cisplatin, and oxaliplatin, which can damage kidneys and cause other side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platinum-based chemotherapy is a recommended systemic therapy option for CSCC when used with radiation therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platinum-based chemotherapy is a specific type of chemotherapy drug, such as cisplatin or carboplatin, preferred for use with radiation in certain cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platinum-based chemotherapy is a type of initial treatment for ovarian cancer, and response to it determines maintenance therapy eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platinum-based chemotherapy is a type of systemic therapy commonly used to treat metastatic cervical cancer, often given in combination with other medicines if prior cisplatin treatment was used."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platinum-based chemotherapy is a type of systemic therapy used with radiation for high-risk CSCC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platinum-based chemotherapy is a type of systemic therapy using drugs like cisplatin or carboplatin, often used as first-line treatment for metastatic cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platinum-based chemotherapy is a type of treatment using drugs like carboplatin or cisplatin, used for ovarian cancer, with sensitivity determining recurrence treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platinum-based chemotherapy is the most common systemic therapy for cervical cancer, including drugs like cisplatin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Platinum-based chemotherapy is the most common systemic therapy for cervical cancer, stopping cancer cell growth by killing or preventing division."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AIDS is a condition caused by HIV that severely weakens the immune system, raising cervical cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"AIDS is a condition resulting from HIV that severely weakens the immune system, increasing risk of CSCC."&lt;SEP&gt;"AIDS is a disease caused by HIV, the immunodeficiency virus, and is frequently linked to primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"AIDS is the advanced stage of HIV infection, severely weakening the immune system and increasing the risk of skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRONCHUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The bronchus is a major airway in the lungs that branches into smaller passages. It is one of the sites where lung cancer can start."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEAD AND NECK CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer affecting the head and neck region, requiring specific exams, tests, and treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and Neck Cancer is a broader category that includes mouth cancer, affecting oral health and treatment considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and neck cancer includes cancers of the mouth, throat, and nasopharynx, and its treatment can affect jaw, teeth, and gums health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and neck cancer is a broader category of cancer that includes throat cancer and can affect the jaw, teeth, and gums."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and neck cancer is a disease affecting the head and neck region, with treatments that can impact oral health, endocrine glands, hearing, and fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and neck cancer is a group of cancers that arise in the head or neck area, including the mouth (oral cavity), oropharynx, nasal cavity, nasopharynx, larynx, and hypopharynx. Treatment is based on tumor location."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and neck cancer is a group of cancers that arise in the head or neck area, with mouth cancer being a subtype."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and neck cancer is a specific type of cancer that affects the head and neck region, with unique considerations for treatment, hearing, and smoking cessation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and neck cancer is a type of cancer associated with smoking and vaping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and neck cancer is a type of cancer mentioned in the text, though not detailed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and neck cancer is a type of cancer that can affect the jaw, teeth, and gums, and its treatment can impact overall health, fertility, and requires dental care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Head and neck cancers are a group of cancers that arise in the head or neck area, including the mouth, oropharynx, nasal cavity, nasopharynx, larynx, and hypopharynx. Treatment is based on tumor location."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR TUMOR MARKERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Specific molecules or gene abnormalities in tumors that guide treatment decisions and predict cancer behavior."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPOMETHYLATING AGENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hypomethylating agents (HMAs) are drugs that block methyl groups from binding to DNA, turning silenced genes back on and allowing leukemic blasts to mature into normal cells. Examples include azacitidine and decitabine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hypomethylating agents (HMAs) are drugs that block methyl groups from binding to DNA, turning silenced genes back on and allowing leukemic blasts to mature. Examples include Azacitidine and Decitabine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUCINOUS CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mucinous carcinoma is a less common epithelial ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BILE DUCT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bile duct is a tube that carries bile, made up of several layers including inner and outer membranes, with muscle and connective tissue in between."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SORILUX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sorilux is a brand name for calcipotriene, a vitamin D cream used with 5-fluorouracil to treat actinic keratosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KEYTRUDA (PEMBROLIZUMAB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Keytruda is a checkpoint inhibitor immunotherapy used to treat bladder cancer, often combined with targeted therapy for metastatic cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VERMILION LIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The vermilion lip is the area where the skin and lip meet on the outside of the mouth, excluded from this book's focus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-platinum chemotherapy is a treatment option for platinum-resistant ovarian cancer, given as an alternative to platinum-based drugs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-platinum chemotherapy is an alternative treatment for bladder cancer patients with kidney conditions or other health issues who cannot receive platinum-based drugs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGAN TRANSPLANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organ transplant is a medical procedure that requires immunosuppressive drugs, weakening the immune system and increasing CSCC risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organ transplant is a medical procedure that requires immunosuppressive medications, leading to a higher risk of infections and primary CNS lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organ transplant is a medical procedure that requires taking immunosuppressants, which increases the risk of anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRONCHIOLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bronchioles are small tubes inside the lungs that branch from the bronchi and lead to the alveoli."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bronchioles are smaller airways in the lungs that branch from the bronchus. They are lined with cells that can give rise to lung cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPATITIS B&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hepatitis B (HBV) is a liver disease caused by a virus, which can be reactivated by some cancer treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hepatitis B is a viral infection that may be screened for before certain cancer treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNA REPAIR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cellular processes that fix damaged DNA, involving genes like BRCA1, BRCA2, ATM, PALB2, and FANCA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEMTUZUMAB OZOGAMICIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gemtuzumab ozogamicin (GO) is a targeted therapy linked to a chemotherapy drug that attaches to CD33, enters the cell, and releases chemotherapy. It may delay blood count recovery and cause liver issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gemtuzumab ozogamicin (GO) is a targeted therapy linked to a chemotherapy drug, attaching to CD33 proteins on leukemic blasts and releasing chemotherapy inside the cell. It may delay blood count recovery and cause liver issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BORDERLINE EPITHELIAL TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Borderline epithelial tumor, also called low malignant potential tumors, is a less common epithelial ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THYMUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The thymus is a small organ in front of the windpipe that can become enlarged in T-ALL, causing breathing problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"The thymus is a small organ in front of the windpipe. In T-ALL, it can become enlarged, leading to breathing problems due to pressure on the windpipe and blood vessels."&lt;SEP&gt;"The thymus is a small organ in the upper chest where lymphocytes develop into T lymphocytes (T cells)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The thymus is an organ in the lymphatic system that plays a role in immune function and can be affected by lymphoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"The thymus is an organ in the lymphatic system where T cells mature and develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"The thymus is part of the lymph system, involved in immune function and containing B cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thymus is a small organ in front of the windpipe that can be enlarged in T-ALL, potentially causing breathing problems due to pressure on the windpipe and blood vessels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOVONEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dovonex is a brand name for calcipotriene, a vitamin D cream used with 5-fluorouracil to treat actinic keratosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPDIVO (NIVOLUMAB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Opdivo is a checkpoint inhibitor immunotherapy used to treat bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAGINAL DRYNESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vaginal dryness is a sexual side effect of anal cancer treatment, causing discomfort during intercourse."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTING AND TREATMENT PLANNING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chapter in the guide covering MMR testing, family history, blood tests, and other care needed for treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEART RHYTHM PROBLEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Heart rhythm problems are a potential health issue from excessive levothyroxine, affecting cardiovascular function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIETARY SUPPLEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dietary supplements are products like vitamins or minerals used as complementary therapy during cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBODY DRUG CONJUGATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibody drug conjugate (ADC) is a type of targeted therapy, such as mirvetuximab soravtansine-gynx, that delivers drugs to cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORTICOSTEROID USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Long-term corticosteroid use is a condition that weakens the immune system, increasing CSCC risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALVEOLI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alveoli are sacs at the end of bronchioli where oxygen is transferred from air into the blood, and can be affected by lung cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alveoli are small air sacs at the end of bronchioles where oxygen is transferred into the blood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alveoli are small sacs at the end of bronchioli where oxygen is transferred from air into the blood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alveoli are tiny air sacs at the end of bronchioli where oxygen is transferred from air into the blood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alveoli are tiny air sacs in the lungs where gas exchange occurs. They are part of the airway system where lung cancer can originate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A common psychological condition in cancer patients, characterized by persistent sadness and loss of interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depression is a common psychological condition in cancer patients, which can be managed with support groups, therapy, or medication."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depression is a mental health condition that can occur as part of distress in cancer patients, affecting mood and daily functioning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depression is a mental health condition that may be screened for in cancer patients as part of distress screening."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depression is a mental health condition that may occur as part of distress in cancer patients, characterized by persistent sadness and loss of interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depression is a mental health condition that may occur in anal cancer survivors, requiring support and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depression is a psychological condition that may affect cancer survivors, addressed in survivorship care resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depression is a symptom that can occur in patients with primary CNS lymphoma, affecting mental health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABDOMINAL EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abdominal exam is a physical examination where a provider feels the belly to check organ size, consistency, and pain, and to detect fluid buildup (ascites)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORE BINDING FACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Core binding factor (CBF) is a genetic abnormality in AML that creates a shortage of mature blood cells. GO may be used in combination with daunorubicin and cytarabine to treat AML with CBF."&lt;SEP&gt;"Core binding factor (CBF) is a genetic abnormality that creates a shortage of all types of mature blood cells, and is treated with combinations of drugs like gemtuzumab ozogamicin, daunorubicin, and cytarabine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALIGNANT SEX-CORD STROMAL TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Malignant sex-cord stromal tumors are less common non-epithelial ovarian cancers that start in tissues that support the ovaries."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYMPHATIC VESSELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lymphatic Vessels are channels through which lymph fluid drains into lymph nodes, playing a role in cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphatic vessels are a network of thin tubes that carry lymphatic fluid and white blood cells throughout the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphatic vessels are ducts that transport lymph throughout the body, similar to how blood vessels transport blood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphatic vessels are part of the submucosa in the esophagus, involved in immune function and fluid balance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lymphatic vessels are thin tubes that carry lymphatic fluid and white blood cells throughout the body, part of the lymphatic system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 2: TESTING FOR AML&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 2: Testing for AML provides an overview of tests a patient might receive, and the role of genetic and biomarker mutation testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAVENCIO (AVELUMAB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bavencio is a checkpoint inhibitor immunotherapy used to treat bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY IMPACT ASSESSMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility Impact Assessment is evaluating how treatment may affect ability to have children."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAINTENANCE THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maintenance therapy is a follow-up treatment after initial chemotherapy to prevent cancer recurrence, mentioned as a possible next step."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maintenance therapy is a treatment given after initial therapy to prolong remission, potentially used for advanced ovarian cancer if initial treatment is effective."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maintenance therapy is ongoing treatment after initial chemotherapy to delay cancer growth, using drugs like PARP inhibitors or bevacizumab."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maintenance therapy is systemic treatment after initial ovarian cancer treatment to reduce recurrence risk or extend time until progression, used for stage 2-4 cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maintenance therapy is treatment given after remission to prevent cancer recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maintenance therapy refers to ongoing intravesical BCG or chemotherapy treatments given periodically to prevent bladder cancer recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMOKEFREE.GOV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SmokeFree.gov is a website offering online support and resources to help individuals quit smoking."&lt;SEP&gt;"SmokeFree.gov is a website providing online support and resources to help individuals quit smoking or vaping."&lt;SEP&gt;"SmokeFree.gov is a website providing online support for quitting smoking."&lt;SEP&gt;"SmokeFree.gov is an online resource providing support and information to help individuals quit smoking or vaping. It is recommended for cancer patients seeking to stop tobacco use."&lt;SEP&gt;"SmokeFree.gov is an online resource providing support and information to help individuals quit smoking, reducing cancer risk and improving health outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"SmokeFree.gov is an online resource providing support for quitting smoking."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genes are parts of cells that carry instructions for cell behavior, and mutations in them can lead to bladder cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are segments of DNA that can undergo mutations, which are tested as biomarkers in cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are segments of DNA that code for proteins and can be silenced or activated by methylation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are segments of DNA that code for proteins and may contain mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are sets of instructions that determine cell behavior and development. Inherited genetic traits can influence an individual's risk of developing lung cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are sets of instructions that tell new cells what to become and what to do, such as making hormones or absorbing nutrients. They can carry traits that increase risk for diseases like liver cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are the hereditary units in cells that can undergo mutations, contributing to bladder cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are the units of heredity that can carry mutations increasing the risk of pancreatic cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes are units of DNA that may carry mutations affecting leukemia risk and treatment response, analyzed through various testing methods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genes code for proteins."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATIC MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A gene change acquired later in life due to chance or environmental factors, also called acquired mutation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A somatic mutation occurs only in tumor cells and is not inherited."&lt;SEP&gt;"Somatic mutation is a genetic change that occurs during cell division, not inherited, and can lead to cancer development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Somatic mutation or somatic change refers to DNA alterations that occur in non-reproductive cells, not inherited from parents, and can lead to cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOMETRIAL BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endometrial biopsy is a procedure to sample the uterine lining to rule out uterine cancer, sometimes performed during a pelvic exam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLT3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FLT3 is a gene that can be mutated in AML cells, and its protein product is a target for specific therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"FLT3 is a gene that can have mutations (such as FLT3-ITD and FLT3-TKD) in AML. Targeted therapies like Gilteritinib, quizartinib, midostaurin, or sorafenib are used to treat AML with these mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"FLT3 is a gene that can have mutations in AML cells, and its testing is important for targeted treatment and prognosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"FLT3 is a gene that can have mutations such as FLT3-ITD and FLT3-TKD, which are treated with specific targeted therapies like gilteritinib, quizartinib, midostaurin, or sorafenib."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALIGNANT GERM CELL TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Malignant germ cell tumors are less common non-epithelial ovarian cancers that start in the reproductive (egg) cells of the ovary."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBODY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An antibody is a protein made by B lymphocytes that helps fight infections."&lt;SEP&gt;"An antibody is a protein produced by B lymphocytes that targets infections or cancer cells and recruits other immune system parts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibody is a protein made by B lymphocytes to help fight infection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 3: TYPES OF TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 3 is a section of the NCCN Guidelines for Patients that discusses various types of cancer treatment options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chapter 3: Types of treatment gives a general overview of AML treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TECENTRIQ (ATEZOLIZUMAB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tecentriq is a checkpoint inhibitor immunotherapy used to treat bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGULATORY AGENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Regulatory Agency is a government body, such as the FDA, that oversees clinical trials and drug approvals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physician is a medical doctor who diagnoses and treats diseases, including bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINANCIAL AID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Financial aid is a component of supportive care, helping patients manage costs related to cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLETION THYROIDECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Completion thyroidectomy is a second surgery to remove the remaining thyroid tissue after a lobectomy if high-risk features are found."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARCINOMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carcinomas are a subtype of lung cancer that starts in the cells lining the airways of the lungs, including the bronchus, bronchioles, and alveoli."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carcinomas are a type of cancer that starts in the cells lining the airways of the lungs. Most lung cancers are carcinomas, including subtypes like adenocarcinoma and squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carcinomas are cancers that start in cells lining inner or outer surfaces of the body, including most breast cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carcinomas are cancers that start in cells lining inner or outer surfaces, including most breast cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carcinomas are cancers that start in cells lining the inner or outer surfaces of the body, including most kidney cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carcinomas are cancers that start in cells lining the inner or outer surfaces of the body. Almost all breast cancers are carcinomas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECURRENCE TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Recurrence treatment is therapy given when ovarian cancer returns, with options depending on platinum sensitivity and biomarkers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BETOBACCOFREE.GOV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BeTobaccoFree.gov is a government website offering resources and guidance for tobacco cessation, supporting efforts to quit smoking and vaping."&lt;SEP&gt;"BeTobaccoFree.gov is a website offering online support and resources for quitting tobacco use, including smoking and vaping."&lt;SEP&gt;"BeTobaccoFree.gov is a website offering online support for tobacco cessation."&lt;SEP&gt;"BeTobaccoFree.gov is a website providing online support and resources for tobacco cessation."&lt;SEP&gt;"BeTobaccoFree.gov is a website providing online support for quitting tobacco use."&lt;SEP&gt;"BeTobaccoFree.gov is an online resource offering support and information for quitting tobacco use. It is suggested for patients who smoke or vape."&lt;SEP&gt;"BeTobaccoFree.gov is an online resource providing support for quitting tobacco use."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MSI-H/dMMR mutation refers to microsatellite instability or deficient mismatch repair in cancer cells, indicating a specific genetic abnormality."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSI-H/dMMR mutation refers to microsatellite instability-high or deficient mismatch repair, a condition where DNA repair mechanisms fail, leading to errors in microsatellites, often treated with pembrolizumab."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSI-H/dMMR mutation refers to microsatellite instability-high or deficient mismatch repair, where DNA errors are not fixed, leading to cancer cell growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSI-H/dMMR mutation refers to microsatellite instability-high or deficient mismatch repair, where DNA repair errors are not fixed, leading to cancer cell proliferation."&lt;SEP&gt;"MSI-H/dMMR mutation refers to microsatellite instability-high or deficient mismatch repair, which are DNA repair defects in some cancers that may influence treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECTOVAGINAL EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rectovaginal exam is a physical examination of the space between the rectum and vagina to check for cancer spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CD33&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CD33 is a cell surface protein found on many leukemic blasts but not on mature blood cells, making it a target for certain therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"CD33 is a cell surface protein found on many leukemic blasts but not on mature blood cells. It is the target for Gemtuzumab ozogamicin therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER GRADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer grade describes how abnormal cancer cells look under a microscope, influencing treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer grade indicates how abnormal cancer cells look, helping predict growth rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer grade is a rating (GX, G1-G4) indicating how abnormal cancer cells look and how fast the cancer is expected to grow, influencing treatment decisions like local excision."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer grade is a rating of how abnormal cancer cells look under a microscope. High-grade cancers grow and spread more quickly than low-grade cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRANODAL DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Extranodal disease refers to cancer that has spread outside the lymph nodes, more common in non-mediastinal gray zone lymphomas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extranodal disease refers to cancer that occurs outside the lymph nodes, which is a characteristic of MGZL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extranodal disease refers to follicular lymphoma forming tumors outside lymph nodes, such as in the bone marrow."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 4: AML&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 4: AML discusses treatment for AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PADCEV (ENFORTUMAB VEDOTIN-EJFV)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Padcev is a targeted therapy, an antibody-drug conjugate that targets the Nectin-4 protein on bladder cancer cells, often combined with immunotherapy for metastatic bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NX NODE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NX node indicates cancer in nearby lymph nodes cannot be measured."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NURSE ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nurse Role Education is understanding the nurse's role in exams."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLETE REMISSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A state where no signs of cancer are present in the body after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Complete remission is the absence of cancer signs after treatment, a prerequisite for considering platinum-sensitive recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CDC.GOV/TOBACCO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CDC.gov/tobacco is a Centers for Disease Control and Prevention resource that provides evidence-based information and tools for tobacco cessation and prevention."&lt;SEP&gt;"CDC.gov/tobacco is a section of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention website dedicated to tobacco-related information and support."&lt;SEP&gt;"CDC.gov/tobacco is a website from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention offering tobacco cessation resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"CDC.gov/tobacco is a website from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention offering tobacco-related resources and quit support."&lt;SEP&gt;"CDC.gov/tobacco is a website from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention providing information and support for tobacco cessation."&lt;SEP&gt;"CDC.gov/tobacco is a website from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention providing resources and information on tobacco cessation. It is recommended for patients seeking help to quit smoking or vaping."&lt;SEP&gt;"CDC.gov/tobacco is a website from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention providing tobacco cessation resources."&lt;SEP&gt;"CDC.gov/tobacco is an online resource from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention offering tobacco cessation support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADENOSQUAMOUS CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adenosquamous carcinoma is a less common cervical cancer containing both squamous and adenocarcinoma cells, sometimes called mixed tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adenosquamous carcinoma is a mixed type of cervical cancer containing both squamous and glandular components. It is one of the main types addressed in the treatment guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adenosquamous carcinoma is a rare subtype of non-small cell lung cancer that contains both adenocarcinoma and squamous cell carcinoma components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adenosquamous carcinoma is a type of cervical cancer, treated based on cancer stage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSATELLITES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microsatellites are short repeated DNA sequences that can become unstable when mismatch repair is deficient, leading to MSI-H."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellites are short repeated DNA sequences; errors in them can lead to MSI-H/dMMR."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellites are short, repeated DNA sequences that can become unstable when mismatch repair is deficient, leading to MSI-H."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellites are short, repeated DNA strings; when errors occur and are not fixed, they lead to MSI-H or dMMR."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellites are short, repeated strings of DNA; errors in them can lead to microsatellite instability (MSI) in cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSABDOMINAL ULTRASOUND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transabdominal ultrasound is a type of ultrasound where a probe is moved over the abdomen and pelvis to visualize the ovaries and surrounding tissues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLADRIBINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cladribine (Mavenclad) is an antimetabolite chemotherapy drug used to treat AML by preventing the building blocks of DNA from being used."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC COUNSELORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic counselors are healthcare professionals who provide guidance on genetic testing and hereditary cancer risks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE 3A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade 3A is a follicular lymphoma grade with more centroblasts, potentially treated as classic FL or DLBCL depending on the cancer center."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 5: APL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 5: APL discusses treatment of a rare subtype of AML, APL, which involves the abnormal fusion gene PML::RARA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BALVERSA (ERDAFITINIB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Balversa is a targeted therapy used for bladder cancer caused by specific mutations in the FGFR3 gene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUTANEOUS SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma of the vermilion lip is a type of skin cancer, not covered in this book but in NCCN guidelines for squamous cell skin cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROBLASTOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neuroblastoma is a rare cancer affecting children, originating in adrenal tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neuroblastoma is a rare, cancerous adrenal tumor that primarily affects children aged 5 and under, often found in infants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neuroblastoma is a rare, cancerous adrenal tumor that primarily affects children ages 5 and under, especially infants. It can spread to other parts of the body, including bones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER GROWS OR SPREADS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer grows or spreads is a condition that leads to stopping maintenance therapy, indicating disease progression."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGEON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical professional who performs surgical procedures such as mastectomy, lumpectomy, and sentinel lymph node biopsy, and uses dye and radioactive material to locate sentinel nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical professional who performs surgical procedures such as sentinel lymph node biopsy, skin grafts, and wound closures."&lt;SEP&gt;"A surgeon is a doctor who performs operations to remove tumors or breasts in breast cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A surgeon is a medical professional who diagnosed the patient with inflammatory breast cancer after multiple office visits."&lt;SEP&gt;"A surgeon is a medical professional who performs operations like mastectomy, with expertise in specific cancer surgeries, and is consulted for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"A surgeon is a medical professional who performs operations like thyroidectomy or lobectomy for thyroid cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A surgeon is a medical professional who performs operations, such as thyroidectomy, to remove cancerous tissue."&lt;SEP&gt;"A surgeon is a medical professional who performs surgical procedures, including biopsies and removal of skin lesions, and may be involved in treating squamous cell carcinoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"A surgeon is a specialist who performs surgical procedures, including Mohs surgery and lymph node dissection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgeon is a medical professional who performs colectomy and other surgical procedures, removing lymph nodes that look abnormal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgeon is a medical professional who performs surgical biopsies and is recommended to be experienced in the procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgeon is a medical professional who performs surgical procedures for CSCC treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgeon is a medical professional who performs surgical procedures like APR for anal cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SARCOMATOID CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sarcomatoid carcinoma is a rare and aggressive subtype of non-small cell lung cancer that has features of both carcinoma and sarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISMATCH REPAIR (MMR) PROTEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mismatch repair (MMR) proteins fix DNA errors; defects in them lead to deficient mismatch repair (dMMR) and cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mismatch repair (MMR) proteins fix DNA errors; defects in these proteins lead to microsatellite instability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mismatch repair (MMR) proteins fix DNA errors; defects lead to dMMR and MSI-H."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mismatch repair proteins are responsible for fixing DNA errors, and defects in these can lead to microsatellite instability and cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mismatch repair proteins are responsible for fixing DNA errors; defects in these proteins lead to dMMR and MSI."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROVIDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Provider is a healthcare professional who administers tests, recommends treatments, and monitors thyroid cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Provider is a healthcare professional who offers medical advice and treatment options for bladder cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Provider is a healthcare professional who performs physical exams and orders diagnostic tests to evaluate suspected ovarian cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Provider refers to a healthcare professional or medical team responsible for conducting physical exams, including breast palpation, and guiding patients through cancer care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLOFARABINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clofarabine (Clolar) is an antimetabolite chemotherapy drug used to treat AML by preventing DNA synthesis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEXUAL HEALTH EXPERTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sexual health experts are healthcare professionals who address sexual health concerns related to cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRADE 3B&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grade 3B is a follicular lymphoma grade containing only centroblasts, indicating a higher grade and different treatment approach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 6: BPDCN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 6: BPDCN discusses treatment of an aggressive subtype of AML, BPDCN, which can be found in blood, bone marrow, lymph nodes, and/or skin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRODELVY (SACITUZUMAB GOVITECAN-HZIY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trodelvy is a targeted therapy that targets the Trop-2 protein found on cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NARROWING AND SHORTENING OF THE VAGINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Narrowing and shortening of the vagina is a physical change caused by radiation therapy, leading to discomfort and sexual difficulties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-METASTATIC CANCER TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A section of the guide covering treatment for polyps with cancer, colectomy, and chemotherapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRY MOUTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dry mouth is a possible side effect of RAI therapy, affecting salivary glands."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EASTERN MEDICINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eastern medicine includes traditional practices from Asia, such as herbal remedies, used as complementary therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BURNING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Burning is a specific type of pain symptom that may indicate nerve invasion by cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMALL CELL CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Small cell carcinoma is a rare non-urothelial type of bladder cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Small cell carcinoma is a rare, non-urothelial type of bladder cancer that is aggressive and less common."&lt;SEP&gt;"Small cell carcinoma is a subtype of small cell lung cancer, characterized by small, oval- or oat-shaped cells under a microscope."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIVOLUMAB (OPDIVO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nivolumab (Opdivo) is a checkpoint inhibitor used in immunotherapy for dMMR/MSI-H colon cancers, sometimes combined with ipilimumab."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nivolumab is an immune checkpoint inhibitor used to treat metastatic anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nivolumab, also known as Opdivo, is an immunotherapy drug used for TMB-H tumors in some cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOATING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bloating is a common symptom of ovarian cancer, characterized by a feeling of fullness or swelling in the abdomen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bloating is a symptom of ovarian cancer, causing abdominal discomfort and potentially affecting dietary habits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bloating is a symptom of ovarian cancer, causing abdominal discomfort and potentially affecting eating habits."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IDARUBICIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Idarubicin (Idamycin PFS) is an anthracycline chemotherapy drug used to treat AML, causing DNA damage and cell death."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REGISTERED NURSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Registered nurses are healthcare professionals who provide direct patient care and support during cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NPC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NPC (Nasopharyngeal Carcinoma) is a type of cancer that affects the nasopharynx, the area connecting the back of the nose to the back of the mouth. It is the focus of the text, with squamous cell carcinoma being the most common type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 7: OTHER RESOURCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 7: Other resources provides information on patient advocacy groups and where to get help."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRIMODAL THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trimodal therapy combines TURBT, radiation, and chemotherapy to treat bladder cancer, serving as a bladder-preserving alternative to radical cystectomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIRTH CONTROL CONSULTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Birth Control Consultation is discussing contraceptive options with a doctor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STINGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stinging is a brief sensation felt during the injection of numbing medicine before a biopsy, but no pain should occur during the procedure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stinging is a specific type of pain symptom that may indicate nerve invasion by cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMBINED (SMALL AND NON-SMALL) CELL LUNG CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Combined cell lung carcinoma is a type of lung tumor that contains both small cell and non-small cell lung cancer cells, typically treated like SCLC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IPILIMUMAB (YERVOY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ipilimumab (Yervoy) is a checkpoint inhibitor used in combination with nivolumab for dMMR/MSI-H colon cancers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ipilimumab, also known as Yervoy, is an immunotherapy drug used for TMB-H tumors in some cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEARTBURN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Heartburn is a symptom that can occur with ovarian cancer, involving a burning sensation in the chest or throat."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MITOXANTRONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mitoxantrone (Novantrone) is an anthracycline chemotherapy drug used to treat AML, with potential heart issues and lifetime dose limits."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CARE PROVIDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A primary care provider is a doctor who manages overall health and can help manage other health conditions affected by cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary care provider is a healthcare professional who may first suspect lung cancer and refer patients to specialists."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTING FOR NPC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Testing for NPC includes general health tests, imaging tests, biopsy, and biomarker testing, which are used to determine the treatment plan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IBRANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ibrance (palbociclib) is a CDK4/6 inhibitor used in endocrine therapy for hormone receptor-positive breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FDA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FDA (U.S. Food and Drug Administration) is the regulatory agency that approves drugs and treatments after successful clinical trials, ensuring their safety and efficacy."&lt;SEP&gt;"The FDA is the regulatory body that approves new drugs, devices, or treatment approaches after they are found safe and effective in clinical trials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER RESEARCH CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer Research Center is an institution dedicated to advancing cancer research and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATHOLOGY DEPARTMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pathology department is a medical unit that examines tissue samples under a microscope to diagnose cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAMILY COUNSELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Family counseling is a component of supportive care, assisting families in dealing with the impact of cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONITORING AND FOLLOW-UP CARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Monitoring and follow-up care involve regular check-ups and tests after thyroid cancer treatment to detect recurrence or manage side effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROENDOCRINE CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neuroendocrine cells are specialized cells that release hormones in response to signals. SCLC originates from these cells in the lungs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neuroendocrine cells are the origin of small cell lung cancer (SCLC), which is a fast-dividing cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOSS OF FEELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Loss of feeling is a symptom that may indicate nerve invasion by cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR MUTATION TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor mutation testing analyzes tumor DNA for specific mutations like PIK3CA to identify targeted therapies, distinct from inherited genetic testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutation testing analyzes tumor samples for specific DNA mutations to guide targeted therapies, distinct from inherited genetic testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutation testing is a type of testing mentioned in Chapter 2, related to biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutation testing is a type of testing mentioned in Chapter 2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutation testing uses a sample of tumor or blood to identify specific DNA mutations in cancer cells, which may be targeted with specific therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutation testing, or genomic aberration testing, examines a tumor sample for specific DNA mutations that may be targeted with specific therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutation testing, or tumor genomic aberration testing, uses a tumor or blood sample to identify specific DNA mutations in cancer cells, distinct from inherited genetic testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INDIGESTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Indigestion is a symptom that may be associated with ovarian cancer, causing discomfort or pain in the upper abdomen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CPX-351&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CPX-351 (Vyxeos) is a dual-drug liposome of cytarabine and daunorubicin, combining an antimetabolite and an anthracycline for AML treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ABDOMINAL AND PELVIC EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abdominal and pelvic exams are physical examinations used to detect abnormalities in the abdomen and pelvic area, potentially indicating ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIVE AMERICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Native America is a geographic region where NPC most often occurs, indicating a higher prevalence in certain populations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Native America is a geographic region where nasopharyngeal cancer most often occurs, as noted in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KISQALI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kisqali (ribociclib) is a CDK4/6 inhibitor used in combination with endocrine therapy for breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADICAL CYSTECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radical cystectomy is a major surgery for muscle-invasive bladder cancer that involves removing the bladder, nearby lymph nodes, and other pelvic organs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radical cystectomy is bladder removal surgery, which trimodal therapy can replace in certain bladder cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radical cystectomy is the most widely used surgery for muscle-invasive bladder cancer, involving removal of the entire bladder, nearby lymph nodes, and sometimes other organs, requiring a hospital stay and a recovery period of 2-3 months."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLOSTOMY REVERSAL SURGERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colostomy Reversal Surgery is a procedure to reconnect the bowel after a temporary colostomy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC EXAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic exams are physical examinations performed by an oncologist during surveillance to check for signs of cancer recurrence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOVEMENT LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Movement loss is a symptom that may indicate nerve invasion by cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESPIRATORY SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The respiratory system includes the airways and lungs that facilitate breathing, moving air from the throat through the trachea, bronchi, bronchioles, and alveoli."&lt;SEP&gt;"The respiratory system includes the lungs and airways, responsible for gas exchange. Lung cancer affects this system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IDH1 MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IDH1 mutation is a specific gene mutation that can be targeted with therapies like ivosidenib, particularly in chondrosarcoma patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC PAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pelvic pain is a symptom of ovarian cancer, located in the pelvis or abdomen, impacting patient comfort and nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pelvic pain is a symptom of ovarian cancer, often leading to reduced food intake and nutritional challenges."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pelvic pain is a symptom of ovarian cancer, referring to discomfort or pressure in the pelvic region."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AZACITIDINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Azacitidine (Vidaza) is a hypomethylating agent used to treat AML by blocking methyl groups from binding to DNA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Azacitidine (Vidaza) is a hypomethylating agent used to treat leukemia by blocking methyl groups from binding to DNA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAMILY HISTORY AND GENETIC TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Family history and genetic testing are used to assess hereditary risk for ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORTH AFRICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"North Africa is a geographic region where NPC most often occurs, indicating a higher prevalence in certain populations."&lt;SEP&gt;"North Africa is a geographic region where nasopharyngeal cancer most often occurs, as noted in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AFINITOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Afinitor is the brand name for everolimus, an mTOR inhibitor used in breast cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NECTIN-4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nectin-4 is a specific protein found on the surface of bladder cancer cells, targeted by Padcev."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRATIFIED SQUAMOUS CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stratified squamous cells are thin, flat cells that form the epithelium of the oral mucosa and are the origin of squamous cell carcinoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHICS COMMITTEE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ethics Committee is a group that reviews clinical trial protocols to ensure patient safety and ethical standards."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL EXAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physical exams are routine check-ups by an oncologist during surveillance to monitor for cancer recurrence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Physical exams are routine follow-up visits conducted by an oncologist to monitor for recurrence, with recommended frequencies varying by time since treatment and individual risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Routine medical examinations performed by an oncologist during surveillance to monitor for cancer recurrence and overall health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOUBLE VISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Double vision is a symptom of primary CNS lymphoma, affecting eyesight."&lt;SEP&gt;"Double vision is a symptom that may indicate nerve invasion by cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXYGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxygen is a gas breathed in by the lungs and transferred into the blood at the alveoli, essential for cellular function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a gas delivered to the blood by the lungs during respiration. Lung cancer can impair this function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a gas used by the body during breathing, measured in lung function tests to assess lung efficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a molecule transported by red blood cells throughout the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is transferred from air into blood in the alveoli, a process that can be impaired by lung cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IVOSIDENIB (TIBSOVO)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ivosidenib, also known as Tibsovo, is a targeted therapy for IDH1 mutations, used in chondrosarcoma."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BELLY PAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Belly pain is a symptom of ovarian cancer, involving discomfort in the abdominal area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DECITABINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Decitabine (Dacogen) is a hypomethylating agent used to treat AML by turning silenced genes back on."&lt;SEP&gt;"Decitabine (Dacogen) is a hypomethylating agent used to treat leukemia by blocking methyl groups from binding to DNA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITIONAL AND DIGESTIVE TRACT HEALTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutritional and digestive tract health assessments are part of testing for ovarian cancer, as symptoms may affect eating and digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutritional and digestive tract health refers to the impact of diet and eating habits on overall health, relevant as ovarian cancer symptoms can affect nutrition."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPREHENSIVE CANCER CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A comprehensive cancer center is a specialized facility with experts in evaluating and treating NPC, recommended for optimal care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PARP is a cell protein that repairs damaged cancer cells; blocking it can cause cancer cell death."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FGFR3 GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FGFR3 gene mutations can cause bladder cancer, and Balversa targets these specific mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAGINAL DILATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A vaginal dilator is a medical device used to gradually stretch the vagina, helping manage stenosis after radiation therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METASTATIC CANCER TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A section of the guide covering expanded biomarker testing, local therapies, and systemic therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRY EYES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dry eyes are a possible side effect of RAI therapy, affecting tear production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLURRED VISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blurred vision is a symptom that may indicate nerve invasion by cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON DIOXIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon dioxide is a gas produced by cells and exhaled from the body through the lungs, removed during respiration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a gas produced by the body during breathing, measured in lung function tests to assess lung efficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a gas removed from the blood by the lungs during respiration. Lung cancer can disrupt this process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEXT-GENERATION SEQUENCING (NGS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NGS is a method to determine a portion of a person's DNA sequence, showing if a gene has mutations that might affect AML treatment and prognosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"NGS is a method used in biomarker testing to analyze multiple genes simultaneously."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing (NGS) is a high-throughput method for analyzing multiple genes simultaneously in biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing (NGS) is a method that tests for many biomarkers at one time to guide treatment decisions for thyroid cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing is a method to determine DNA sequences in detail, identifying mutations that affect gene function, often used in tumor testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Next-generation sequencing is a method to determine a portion of a person's DNA sequence, identifying mutations that affect gene function in a detailed manner."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TROUBLE EATING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trouble eating is a symptom of ovarian cancer, characterized by difficulty consuming food or feeling full quickly."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GILTERITINIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gilteritinib is a targeted therapy used to treat AML with certain FLT3 mutations, such as FLT3-ITD and FLT3-TKD."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gilteritinib is a targeted therapy used to treat AML with certain FLT3 mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKALINE PHOSPHATASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alkaline phosphatase (ALP) is an enzyme found in the blood; high levels can indicate bone tumors, liver disorders, or pregnancy, and may lead to a bone scan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alkaline phosphatase is an enzyme measured in blood tests, elevated levels may indicate bone or liver involvement in cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"An enzyme produced by the liver, measured in liver function tests to assess liver health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEPRESSION SCREENING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Depression screening assesses mental health during cancer diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depression screening is part of the testing process to assess mental health during NPC diagnosis and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LYNPARZA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lynparza is the brand name for olaparib, a PARP inhibitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TROP-2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trop-2 is a protein found in large numbers on cancer cells, targeted by Trodelvy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hormonal Birth Control Use is the application of hormonal methods, which may or may not be recommended."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELAPSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Relapse is another term for recurrence, referring to the return of cancer after treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Relapse refers to the return of lymphoma after earlier treatment. Stem cell rescue is used in cases of relapse or when other treatments have not been effective."&lt;SEP&gt;"Relapse refers to the return of primary CNS lymphoma in the brain, spinal cord, or eye after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A procedure to remove a sample of inflamed skin on the breast to diagnose inflammatory breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"A procedure to remove a skin sample for testing for cancer, including types like punch and excision biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"A skin biopsy is a medical procedure where a sample of suspicious skin lesion is removed and examined under a microscope to diagnose skin cancer. Types include shave biopsy, punch biopsy, and excision biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin biopsy is a diagnostic procedure where a small tissue sample is removed for testing to diagnose squamous cell skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin biopsy is a procedure to remove a sample of skin for testing to diagnose squamous cell skin cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Skin biopsy is a type of biopsy that takes a small sample of inflamed skin on the breast."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESPIRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Respiration is the process of gas exchange in the body, involving oxygen intake and carbon dioxide removal, performed by the lungs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PCR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PCR (Polymerase chain reaction) is a technique that amplifies DNA or RNA to detect rare abnormal cells, used for monitoring treatment response and identifying gene rearrangements like PML::RARA."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR (polymerase chain reaction) is a lab process that amplifies DNA to detect rare abnormal cells, often used for NGS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is a technique that amplifies DNA or RNA, capable of detecting one abnormal cell among over 100,000 normal cells, and is used for treatment response and remission testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is a technique that amplifies DNA or RNA, highly sensitive, detecting rare abnormal cells, and can be used for NGS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEELING FULL FAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Feeling full fast is a symptom of ovarian cancer, where a person feels satiated after eating only a small amount."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUIZARTINIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Quizartinib is a targeted therapy used to treat AML with FLT3-ITD mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTATE DEHYDROGENASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lactate dehydrogenase (LDH) is an enzyme found in most cells; dying cells and fast-growing cells like tumor cells release LDH into the blood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactate dehydrogenase (LDH) is an enzyme measured in blood tests, relevant in AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPSTEIN-BARR VIRUS (EBV) DNA TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) DNA testing is a biomarker test used as needed in NPC diagnosis and management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TALZENNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Talzenna is the brand name for talazoparib, a PARP inhibitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VINBLASTINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vinblastine is a chemotherapy drug included in the ddMVAC combination for bladder cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASBESTOS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Asbestos is a cancer-causing agent linked to lung cancer, particularly in individuals who smoke. It is a mineral fiber used in construction and other industries."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMUNITY HEALTH CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Community Health Center is a local facility providing accessible cancer care and support services."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community health center is a local facility that provides accessible health care services."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONCOLOGY DEPARTMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oncology department is a specialized unit that provides cancer treatment and management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AXILLARY LYMPH NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Axillary lymph nodes are lymph nodes located in the armpit area. They are often checked for cancer spread in breast cancer cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLLICULAR VARIANT OF PAPILLARY THYROID CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Follicular variant of papillary thyroid cancer is a subtype of papillary thyroid cancer that may grow and spread more quickly than classic type."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRCA MUTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BRCA mutation is a genetic alteration in BRCA1 or BRCA2 genes, making PARP inhibitor maintenance therapy an option after recurrence treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRCA mutation is a genetic alteration in cancers that makes them responsive to PARP inhibitors and affects maintenance therapy choices."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TISSUE SAMPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tissue sample is a piece of tissue, such as from a biopsy, used for immunohistochemistry or genetic testing in AML."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissue sample is a small piece of tissue taken during a biopsy for examination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissue sample is the material removed during a biopsy and analyzed by a pathologist to determine cancer type."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tissue samples are taken from tumors and tested for biomarkers to provide diagnostic and treatment information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cell growth is the process by which cells divide and multiply. Cancer cells exhibit uncontrolled cell growth, leading to tumor formation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer includes primary bone cancers that start in bone or cartilage, and secondary bone malignancies that metastasize from other parts of the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone cancer is a rare type of cancer that originates in the bone, with various subtypes including chondrosarcoma, chordoma, Ewing sarcoma, giant cell tumor of bone, and osteosarcoma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone cancer is a type of cancer that can spread to lungs, other bones, or other parts, staged using TNM and grade."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone cancer is a type of cancer that forms in bone tissue, with diagnosis confirmed via biopsy, and staging using TNM system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINATING OFTEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urinating often is a symptom of ovarian cancer, involving frequent need to urinate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIDOSTAURIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Midostaurin is a targeted therapy used to treat AML with certain FLT3 mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPERCALCEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hypercalcemia is a condition of higher than normal calcium levels in the blood, which can be caused by bone damage from cancer releasing calcium into the bloodstream."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EYE AND ENDOCRINE EVALUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eye and endocrine evaluation is an assessment to monitor for potential effects of NPC treatment on vision and hormonal function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2-&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HER2- refers to breast cancer that does not overexpress the HER2 protein, a condition for PARP inhibitor use."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIDNEY CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kidney conditions are health issues that may prevent patients from receiving certain chemotherapy drugs like cisplatin, leading to alternative non-platinum treatments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOLATE RECEPTOR ALPHA BIOMARKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Folate receptor alpha biomarker is a specific marker on tumors, targeted by mirvetuximab soravtansine-gynx for recurrence treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAIN TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Main tumor is the primary cancer mass, and cancer cells outside it in vessels indicate higher risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An organ is a structure made of tissues that performs a specific function. The lungs are organs that can be harmed by cancer cell overgrowth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organ refers to body parts like bones that provide structure and support."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSSIFICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ossification is the process of new bone formation, starting in the womb and ending in adolescence, involving osteoblasts and osteoclasts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URGENT URINATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urgent urination is a symptom of ovarian cancer, characterized by a sudden, strong need to urinate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SORAFENIB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sorafenib is a targeted therapy used to treat AML with FLT3-ITD mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOTRACER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiotracer is a radioactive substance used in PET scans to visualize cancer cells and metabolic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiotracer is a radioactive substance used in PET scans, such as FDG, to highlight areas of interest in the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiotracer is a substance that releases small amounts of radiation, used in bone scans and PET scans to detect areas of abnormal activity such as bone damage or cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiotracer is a substance that releases small amounts of radiation, used in bone scans and PET scans to detect cancer or bone damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Radiotracer is a substance used in bone scans that releases small amounts of radiation to highlight bone abnormalities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRI WITH CONTRAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MRI with contrast is an imaging test used to visualize the skull base and neck, helping to stage NPC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PIQRAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Piqray is the brand name for alpelisib, a PIK3CA inhibitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREATMENT CYCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A treatment cycle is a sequence of chemotherapy treatments followed by a rest period, repeated several times over months."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARE TEAM ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Care Team Role Education is understanding the roles of all healthcare providers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NONKERATINIZED SQUAMOUS EPITHELIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nonkeratinized squamous epithelium covers the soft palate, inner lips, inner cheeks, floor of the mouth, and area under the tongue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNE CHECKPOINT INHIBITORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immune checkpoint inhibitors are a type of immunotherapy that can have side effects, as discussed in the guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune checkpoint inhibitors are a type of immunotherapy that may be used for ovarian cancer with certain biomarkers, with side effects managed per NCCN guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune checkpoint inhibitors are therapies that target PD-1/PD-L1 to activate the immune system against cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEARBY LYMPH NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nearby lymph nodes are lymph nodes close to the cervix that may be affected by cancer spread. They are more likely to be removed if LVSI is present."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nearby lymph nodes are the first sites where cancer may spread, and their involvement is a risk factor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SMOKING CIGARETTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Smoking cigarettes is the main cause of SCLC, involving inhaling tobacco smoke that damages lung cells and increases cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REMODELING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Remodeling is the continuous process of bone breakdown and rebuilding, maintaining calcium levels, involving osteoclasts and osteoblasts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN DURING SEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pain during sex is a sexual side effect of anal cancer treatment, often due to vaginal stenosis or dryness."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pain during sex is a symptom of ovarian cancer, involving discomfort during sexual intercourse."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLT3-ITD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FLT3-ITD is a specific mutation in the FLT3 gene associated with AML, targeted by drugs like gilteritinib and quizartinib."&lt;SEP&gt;"FLT3-ITD is a specific mutation in the FLT3 gene that is targeted by drugs like quizartinib and sorafenib."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE TUMORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone tumors are abnormal growths in bone that can cause high ALP levels and bone damage, detected through imaging tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone tumors are abnormal growths of cells within a bone, which may be malignant or benign."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CT OF SKULL BASE AND NECK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CT of skull base and neck is an imaging test used to assess the extent of NPC and guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PD-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PD-1 is an immune 'off switch' that tumors exploit; blocking it can enhance immune response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBODY-DRUG CONJUGATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An antibody-drug conjugate is a type of targeted therapy, like Padcev, that combines an antibody with a drug to target specific proteins on cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DILATOR KITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dilator kits contain multiple sizes of vaginal dilators, allowing gradual increase in size as the vagina widens."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BENIGN GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A non-cancerous polyp that can become invasive over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-cancerous polyp that can become invasive."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-cancerous polyp."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATERY EYES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Watery eyes are a possible side effect of RAI therapy, often due to gland irritation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DISTANT SITES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Distant sites are areas of the body beyond the primary tumor where cancer may metastasize."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant sites are areas where cancer has spread beyond nearby lymph nodes, part of staging."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant sites are locations where cancer has spread from the primary site, detectable via FDG-PET/CT."&lt;SEP&gt;"Distant sites are parts of the body far from the primary tumor where cancer may spread, indicating advanced disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Locations in the body beyond the bladder where stage 4 cancer has spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMBUSTIBLE TOBACCO PRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Combustible tobacco products are items like cigarettes and cigars that produce smoke when burned, contributing to secondhand smoke exposure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTEOCYTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osteocytes are bone cells that maintain bone tissue, part of the living bone structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASCITES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ascites is a condition of fluid buildup in the belly area, which can be a sign of ovarian cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ascites is the accumulation of fluid in the abdominal cavity, which is checked for cancer cells in ovarian cancer staging."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLT3-TKD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FLT3-TKD is a specific mutation in the FLT3 gene associated with AML, targeted by drugs like gilteritinib."&lt;SEP&gt;"FLT3-TKD is a specific mutation in the FLT3 gene that is targeted by drugs like gilteritinib."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIVER DISORDERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liver disorders are conditions affecting the liver that can cause high ALP levels, detected through blood tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEST CT WITH CONTRAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chest CT with contrast is an imaging test used to check for lung metastases in NPC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CTLA-4&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CTLA-4 is an immune 'off switch' that tumors exploit; blocking it can enhance immune response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL RESEARCH STUDY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A medical research study is a clinical trial that assesses new treatment methods, including drugs, devices, or approaches."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-hormonal Birth Control Use is the application of barrier methods or IUDs, preferred after breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAPTER 5: SURVIVORSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chapter 5: Survivorship is a section of a document providing information on care for cancer survivors, referenced for additional support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chapter 5: Survivorship is a section of a guide that provides information on other care important for cancer survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL CSCC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local CSCC is squamous cell carcinoma confined to the original site, with treatment options varying by risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local CSCC refers to squamous cell skin cancer that has not spread to nearby lymph nodes, and is most often treated with surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"Local CSCC refers to squamous cell skin cancer that has not spread to nearby lymph nodes, requiring regular skin exams and possibly imaging tests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAMILY HEALTH HISTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Family health history is information about diseases and health conditions in a family, reflecting patterns of certain diseases among family members."&lt;SEP&gt;"Family health history is information about diseases in blood relatives, used to assess hereditary cancer risk and guide screening."&lt;SEP&gt;"Family health history is information about inherited cancer risks, used to assess the likelihood of Lynch syndrome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Family health history refers to the collection of information about inherited syndromes like Lynch syndrome and familial adenomatous polyposis, relevant for colon cancer risk assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Family health history refers to the health conditions of biological relatives, which can influence an individual's risk for lung cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Family health history refers to the medical history of a patient's family, which is important for assessing risk of rectal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Information about biological relatives' health, used to assess colon cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Information about health conditions of biological relatives, used to assess risk of colorectal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Information about health issues of blood relatives, such as heart disease, cancer, and diabetes, and the ages at which they were diagnosed, used to assess risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTEOBLASTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osteoblasts are bone-forming cells that create bone from calcium in the bloodstream."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECULUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A speculum is a medical tool used to examine the vagina and cervix, allowing visualization of the ectocervix."&lt;SEP&gt;"Speculum is a widening instrument used during a pelvic exam to view the vagina and cervix."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER CARE PLAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A cancer care plan is a personalized treatment strategy developed by doctors for cervical cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer care plan is a personalized treatment plan developed by the care team for patients with ovarian cancer or AML."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE DAMAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone damage can be caused by cancer, cancer treatment, previous injuries, or arthritis, and is detected through bone scans."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALCOHOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alcohol consumption can increase cancer risk, so anal cancer survivors are advised to drink little to none."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alcohol is a substance that can increase cancer risk, and patients are advised to drink little to no alcohol."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alcohol is a substance whose use is a risk factor for head and neck cancer, and patients are advised to limit it during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KEYTRUDA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Keytruda is the brand name for pembrolizumab, an immunotherapy drug."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTRAPERITONEAL (IP) CHEMOTHERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intraperitoneal chemotherapy is a method where medicine is injected into the abdomen through a catheter, delivering higher doses to cancer cells in the belly area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TELEHEALTH PROVIDER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Telehealth Provider is a service that offers remote medical consultations, useful for follow-up care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSPORTATION SERVICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transportation service is a provider that helps patients travel to medical appointments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEALTH RECORD ACCOUNT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A health record account is an online system that stores a patient's medical information and allows access to test results and appointments."&lt;SEP&gt;"A health record account is an online system, such as MyChart, that stores a patient's medical records and facilitates communication with healthcare providers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TALL-CELL/COLUMNAR CELL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tall-cell/columnar cell is a subtype of papillary thyroid cancer associated with more aggressive growth and spread."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RISK ASSESSMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Risk assessment is a process used to evaluate the likelihood of prostate cancer spreading or recurring, using tools like risk groups, life expectancy, nomograms, and molecular biomarker tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk assessment is the process of determining whether a CSCC is low-, high-, or very high-risk based on key features of the cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk assessment is the process of evaluating an individual's likelihood of developing lung cancer based on risk factors, guiding screening decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Risk assessment is the process of evaluating cancer risk based on family history and genetic testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MISMATCH REPAIR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mismatch repair (MMR) is a DNA repair mechanism, and its deficiency is a biomarker for immunotherapy in ovarian cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARGIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Margin is the area of normal tissue around a tumor removed during surgery, with wider margins for high-risk CSCC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSTEOCLASTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osteoclasts are cells that break down bone to release calcium into the bloodstream."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORAL CONTRAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oral contrast is a liquid substance ingested before a CT scan to enhance imaging of the abdomen and pelvis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oral contrast is a type of contrast material taken by mouth, not absorbed by intestines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SENTINEL LYMPH NODE (SLN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The sentinel lymph node is the first lymph node that cancer cells are most likely to spread to from a primary tumor. It is a key concept in cancer staging and surgical planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARTHRITIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arthritis is a health condition that can cause bone damage, which may be detected in a bone scan."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLLARBONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Collarbone is an anatomical landmark used in imaging to define the lower boundary of the head and neck region."&lt;SEP&gt;"Collarbone is an anatomical location where a central venous catheter is inserted into a vein in the upper chest."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LHRH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Luteinizing hormone-releasing hormone (LHRH) is made by the hypothalamus and stimulates ovaries/testicles to produce hormones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CA-125&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CA-125 is a tumor marker tested before each chemotherapy cycle to monitor treatment effectiveness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STOMACH CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stomach cancer is a disease characterized by the abnormal growth of cells in the stomach lining, developing slowly over years, with types including early-stage, locoregional, and metastatic, and is often preceded by precancerous changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stomach cancer is a disease where malignant cells form in the lining of the stomach, often starting as adenocarcinomas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stomach cancer is a type of cancer that can spread to the lungs but remains stomach cancer, not lung cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stomach cancer is a type of cancer that develops in the stomach. The text provides an overview of stomach anatomy and how stomach cancer spreads, though the main focus is on liver cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LESION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A lesion is an abnormal area on the skin that may indicate basal cell skin cancer and requires testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A lesion is an area of abnormal tissue, which can be dysplasia or cancer, as referred to in cervical cancer terminology."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lesion is the abnormal area of skin affected by CSCC, which is removed during surgery."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHECKUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Checkups are regular medical examinations recommended by health care providers to monitor health and screen for cancers, including lung cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Checkups are regular medical or dental visits to monitor health, especially important for cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EPIPHYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Epiphysis is the area of bone that widens to form a joint, where GCTB can extend."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epiphysis is the area of bone that widens to form a joint."&lt;SEP&gt;"Epiphysis is the end of a bone, covered with cartilage to form joints."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IRI is a term used in medical regimens, indicating the presence of the drug irinotecan, which is associated with side effects such as abdominal cramping, nausea, diarrhea, and hair loss."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSY (SLNB OR SNB)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure to remove sentinel lymph nodes during surgery, such as mastectomy or lumpectomy, to determine if cancer cells have spread to the lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREVIOUS INJURIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Previous injuries can cause bone damage, which may be detected in a bone scan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Previous injuries refer to past physical trauma that can cause bone damage, which may be identified on bone scans or x-rays."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROENDOCRINE CARCINOMA OF THE CERVIX (NECC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NECC is a rare and aggressive type of cervical cancer, including small cell NECC, with distinct treatment focus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GNRH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH) is another name for LHRH, involved in hormone production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARP INHIBITORS (PARPI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PARP inhibitors are oral targeted therapies for maintenance therapy, effective in HRD-positive cancers including BRCA-mutated ones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY SPECIALIST ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility Specialist Role Education is understanding the specialist's role in fertility preservation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KERATINIZED SQUAMOUS EPITHELIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Keratinized squamous epithelium is present on rough surfaces like the gums, hard palate, and top of the tongue."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORMAL CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Healthy cells that are compared to cancer cells by a pathologist to determine the grade of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal cells are healthy cells that behave in a regulated manner, unlike cancer cells which grow and spread abnormally."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal cells are healthy cells that behave in a regulated manner, unlike cancer cells which grow uncontrollably and can spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal cells are healthy cells that behave properly, unlike cancer cells which grow out of control and crowd them out."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal cells are healthy cells that can be affected by systemic therapies, leading to side effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal cells are healthy cells that follow growth and death rules. Cancer cells crowd out and overwhelm normal cells, causing organ dysfunction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal cells are healthy cells that function properly and are crowded out or overwhelmed by cancer cells as the disease progresses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal cells are healthy cells used as a baseline in PCR sensitivity detection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal cells are healthy cells used as a comparison to tumor cells to determine grade and risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal cells are healthy cells; PCR can detect 1 abnormal cell among 100,000 normal cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal cells are healthy cells; the difference between tumor cells and normal cells under a microscope determines tumor grade."&lt;SEP&gt;"Normal cells follow the body's rules, increasing only when needed and dying when old or damaged, unlike cancer cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER SCREENINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer screenings are medical tests to detect cancer early, including screenings for skin, breast, prostate, and lung cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METAPHYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metaphysis is the area of bone that grows rapidly, where bone tumors often occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metaphysis is the area of bone that grows rapidly, where tumors often occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metaphysis is the region of bone between the growth plate (physis) and diaphysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRINOTECAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Irinotecan is a chemotherapy drug that tends to cause abdominal cramping, nausea, diarrhea, and hair loss."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONE RECEPTOR-POSITIVE BREAST CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of breast cancer where estrogen and/or progesterone receptors are found, often treated with endocrine therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOGRAPH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radiograph is another term for an x-ray, a type of radiation used to make pictures of the inside of the body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH PARITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High parity, or having given birth more than once, is a risk factor for cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANDROGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Androgen is a hormone made by adrenal glands, testicles, and ovaries that can convert to estrogen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLAPARIB (LYNPARZA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Olaparib is a PARP inhibitor used for maintenance therapy, given alone for up to 2 years or with bevacizumab for up to 15 months."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANCER TREATMENT CENTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer treatment centers are medical facilities that provide comprehensive care, including programs focused on sexual health after anal cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INVASIVE COLON CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cancer that has spread beyond the polyp into the colon wall."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer that has spread beyond the polyp."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer that has spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUCOSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mucosa is the inner membrane of the esophagus wall that contacts food, consisting of epithelium, lamina propria, and muscularis mucosa."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mucosa is the innermost layer of the colon wall that comes in contact with food, where cancer starts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mucosa is the innermost layer of the esophagus where cancer typically starts, and where precancerous changes often occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mucosa is the innermost layer of the stomach wall where stomach cancer typically begins, and it is the site of precancerous changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mucosa is the inner membrane of the stomach wall, in contact with food, consisting of surface epithelium, lamina propria, and muscularis mucosae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR CELLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor cells are abnormal cells that can be killed by T cells or natural killer cells as part of the immune response."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor cells are abnormal cells that differ from normal cells, with more difference indicating higher risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor cells are cancer cells that form a tumor. Their presence in blood or lymph vessels (LVSI) indicates a higher risk of spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor cells are fast-growing cells that release LDH, detected in blood tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor cells are the abnormal cells in cancer; their appearance under a microscope determines tumor grade and risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EARLY STAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Early stage refers to cancer that has not spread extensively, when treatment is most successful, as targeted by lung cancer screening."&lt;SEP&gt;"Early stage refers to the initial phase of bladder cancer when it is highly treatable and often found through symptoms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIAPHYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diaphysis is the middle region of a bone, a structural part of the skeletal system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diaphysis is the middle region of a bone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diaphysis is the shaft of long bones where Ewing sarcoma commonly occurs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diaphysis is the shaft of long bones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KIDNEY CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kidney cancer is a broad term for cancers arising in the kidney, with renal cell carcinoma being the most common type, and can spread through local invasion or metastasis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kidney cancer is a disease affecting the kidneys, with subtypes and spread patterns discussed in the text, though details are limited."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kidney cancer is a disease that starts in the tissues of the kidneys, with renal cell carcinoma (RCC) being the most common type."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kidney cancer is a type of cancer that can be associated with certain hereditary conditions that also increase the risk of adrenal tumors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HORMONE RECEPTOR-NEGATIVE BREAST CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of breast cancer where neither estrogen nor progesterone receptors are present, often growing faster than hormone receptor-positive cancers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CAT (computed axial tomography) is another term for a CT scan, using x-rays and computer technology."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORAL CONTRACEPTIVE USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oral contraceptive (birth control) use is a risk factor for cervical cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BILATERAL OOPHORECTOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bilateral oophorectomy is a surgical procedure to remove both ovaries, a form of endocrine therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIRAPARIB (ZEJULA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Niraparib is a PARP inhibitor used for maintenance therapy, given alone for up to 3 years."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BARRIER METHOD USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Barrier Method Use is employing condoms, diaphragms, cervical caps, or sponges to prevent pregnancy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CABOZANTINIB (CABOMETYX)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cabozantinib (Cabometyx) is a targeted therapy drug recommended for treating thyroid cancer that worsens after treatment with lenvatinib or sorafenib."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUBMUCOSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Submucosa is a layer of connective tissue below the mucosa in the esophagus, containing blood vessels, nerves, and lymphatic vessels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Submucosa is a layer of the esophagus wall, part of the four main layers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Submucosa is the second layer of the colon wall, made of connective tissue containing mucus glands, blood and lymph vessels, and nerves."&lt;SEP&gt;"Submucosa is the second layer of the stomach wall, which cancer invades in locoregional or locally advanced stomach cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The submucosa is a layer of connective tissue, blood vessels, and nerve cells in the stomach wall."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUBTYPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Subtype is a specific classification of squamous cell skin cancer, with rare subtypes having higher recurrence risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEATH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Death is a potential outcome of lung cancer, which early detection aims to prevent by finding cancer before it becomes advanced."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physis is the growth plate made of cartilage, which leaves a scar after skeletal maturity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Physis is the growth plate of a bone, made of cartilage, which leaves a physeal scar or line after skeletal maturity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RENAL CAPSULE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The renal capsule is a thin layer of tissue covering the kidney, similar to the skin of an apple."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2-POSITIVE BREAST CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of breast cancer with too many HER2 genes or receptors, leading to rapid cell growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"HER2-positive breast cancer is a subtype that overexpresses HER2 receptors, often treated with targeted therapies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PET (Positron Emission Tomography) is an imaging test that uses radioactive tracers to detect metabolic activity of cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET (positron emission tomography) is a type of scan that uses a radioactive drug called a tracer to see where cancer cells are located."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEXUALLY TRANSMITTED INFECTION (STI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"STIs, including HPV, are risk factors for cervical cancer, with a history of STIs increasing risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OVARIAN SUPPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ovarian suppression uses drugs to temporarily stop ovaries from making hormones."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUCAPARIB (RUBRACA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rucaparib is a PARP inhibitor used for maintenance therapy, given alone for up to 2 years."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOME CARE AGENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Home Care Agency is an organization that provides in-home nursing and support services after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEAL DELIVERY SERVICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Meal delivery service is a provider that supplies meals to patients during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCOREGIONAL DISEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Locoregional Disease refers to a tumor that has spread to nearby tissue, organs, or lymph nodes near the mouth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Locoregional disease is cancer that has spread to nearby tissues or lymph nodes, also known as local metastasis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOBNAIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hobnail is a subtype of papillary thyroid cancer with a distinct cell appearance, often linked to more aggressive behavior."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UROTHELIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urothelium is the inner layer of the urinary tract, including the kidneys, ureters, and urethra, where cancer can start instead of the bladder."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urothelium is the inner lining of the bladder and urinary tract, where most bladder cancers originate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERITONEUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peritoneum is the abdominal lining, which is a common site for distant metastasis in metastatic stomach cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPREAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spread is the movement of cancer from one part to another."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spread is the movement of cancer to other parts of the body, with risk factors including depth and vessel invasion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spread refers to the movement of cancer cells to other areas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY SPECIALIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A fertility specialist is a professional who helps patients understand and preserve fertility options before cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A medical expert who discusses fertility preservation options and helps patients plan for future children before treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility Specialist is a medical expert who helps patients understand and preserve their fertility before and during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility specialist is a doctor who helps patients preserve fertility before cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility specialist is a healthcare professional who helps patients preserve fertility before cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility specialist is a healthcare provider who helps patients preserve fertility before cancer treatment, as some treatments can affect fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility specialist is a medical professional who helps cancer patients preserve fertility before treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fertility specialist is an expert in helping people have babies, who can explain options for having a baby during or after treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADRENAL GLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adrenal gland is a singular term for the adrenal glands, which are located on top of each kidney and produce hormones."&lt;SEP&gt;"An adrenal gland sits on top of each kidney and is surrounded by a layer of fat."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY (IHC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A special staining process used to find estrogen, progesterone, and HER2 receptors in breast cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immunohistochemistry (IHC) is a special staining process that uses chemical markers to study cells under a microscope, looking for immunophenotypes in biopsy or tissue samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immunohistochemistry is a special staining process that involves adding a chemical marker to cells and studying them under a microscope to look for the immunophenotype of cells from a biopsy or tissue sample."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PYELOGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pyelogram is an imaging test that uses x-rays and contrast solution to detect blockages such as tumors, kidney stones, or blood clots in the ureters or kidneys, typically performed during a cystoscopy under anesthesia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMAN IMMUNODEFICIENCY VIRUS (HIV)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HIV is a virus that weakens the immune system, increasing the risk of cervical cancer due to reduced ability to clear HPV."&lt;SEP&gt;"Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a virus that attacks the immune system, leading to AIDS and increased cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LHRH AGONISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LHRH agonists are drugs that stop LHRH production, thereby suppressing ovarian hormone production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MYELODYSPLASTIC SYNDROME (MDS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Myelodysplastic syndrome is a cancer where bone marrow doesn't produce enough healthy blood cells, a rare but serious side effect of treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CURETTAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Curettage is a procedure involving scraping away skin with a spoon-shaped tool, often used for actinic keratoses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Curettage is a surgical technique involving scraping the tumor, often combined with electrodesiccation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMATURIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hematuria is the presence of blood in urine, the most common symptom of bladder cancer, which can be visible or detected microscopically."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SARCOMA CANCER CENTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sarcoma cancer center is a specialized facility that treats bone cancer, recommended for biopsy and treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEROTA'S FASCIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gerota's fascia is a layer of connective tissue surrounding the kidney, which kidney cancer can invade in locally advanced disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gerota's fascia is an outer layer of fibrous tissue covering the fat around the kidney and adrenal gland; its involvement indicates advanced kidney cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (ISH)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A test that counts the number of copies of the HER2 gene, used when IHC results are unclear."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEST IMAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chest imaging uses CT or x-ray to determine if cancer has spread to the lungs, serving as a diagnostic tool in cancer staging and treatment planning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FERTILITY AND PREGNANCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fertility and pregnancy considerations are part of testing and care for cervical cancer patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOSERELIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Goserelin (Zoladex) is an LHRH agonist used for ovarian suppression."&lt;SEP&gt;"Goserelin is a specific LHRH agonist used in androgen deprivation therapy for prostate cancer, administered as an injection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOMOLOGOUS RECOMBINATION DEFICIENCY (HRD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HRD is a condition where cells cannot repair DNA damage effectively, often due to BRCA mutations. HRD status guides maintenance therapy decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homologous recombination deficiency is a condition in cancers, including BRCA-mutated ones, where PARP inhibitors work best."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NCCN ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NCCN Role Education is understanding NCCN's role in providing guidelines."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINARY DIVERSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urinary diversion is a surgical procedure performed alongside radical cystectomy to create a new pathway for urine to exit the body."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urinary diversion is an additional surgical procedure needed when the bladder is removed, providing a new way for urine to exit the body, with three main types: ileal conduit, neobladder, and continent cutaneous pouch."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone is a biological tissue that is light, strong, and capable of regrowing, and is the focus of the document's discussion on bone cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a common site for breast cancer metastasis, including the spine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a common site for breast cancer metastasis, particularly the spine. It is one of the distant sites where breast cancer can spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a common site for distant metastasis from cancers such as liver cancer, and is referenced in the M1b staging category."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a common site for distant metastasis in breast cancer, as mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a common site for metastatic esophageal cancer spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a distant tissue that can be a site of metastasis in stage 4B cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a living tissue made of specialized cells, collagen, blood vessels, nerves, proteins, vitamins, and minerals, providing structure and support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a part of the body that can be affected by cancer spread, detected via bone scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a part of the body where cancer may be detected via FDG-PET/CT, potentially eliminating the need for bone scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a possible site for metastasis in stomach cancer, though less common than other sites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a tissue in the body where liver cancer can metastasize, or spread, forming distant metastases. It is one of the most common sites for metastatic liver cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a tissue in the body where metastatic cervical cancer can spread, and local therapies may be used to treat tumors in this location."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a tissue to which cervical cancer may spread, resulting in metastatic disease, and can be treated with SBRT or ablative therapies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a tissue where cancer can spread, detected via bone scans or FDG-PET/CT."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bone is a tissue where metastatic cervical cancer can spread, and SBRT can target tumors there."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bones are anatomical structures that can be sites of prostate cancer metastasis, detected via bone scans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bones are parts of the body that can be affected by prostate cancer metastasis. Bone damage, which can be caused by cancer or treatment, is detected through imaging that shows areas absorbing more tracer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTRODESICCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Electrodesiccation is a surgical technique using heat to destroy cancer cells, often combined with curettage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINARY TRACT INFECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urinary tract infection is a common cause of blood in the urine, distinct from bladder cancer, and requires medical testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urinary tract infection is a condition that can elevate PSA levels, affecting test interpretation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BONE CANCER STAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bone cancer staging is a process to describe tumor size, location, spread, and grade, used to plan treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RENAL ARTERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Renal artery is the blood vessel that carries blood into the kidney for filtration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Renal artery is the blood vessel that carries blood into the kidney, part of the kidney's filtration system."&lt;SEP&gt;"The renal artery carries blood with waste into the kidney."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR MARKERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proteins found in blood or biopsy tissue that may indicate the presence or progression of cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor markers are proteins in blood or tissue, such as CEA, CA 15-3, and CA, that may indicate cancer progression but are not reliable alone for detection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor markers, including CA-125, are tested before each chemotherapy cycle to monitor treatment response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CDKN2A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CDKN2A is a gene in which germline mutations are commonly found in bladder cancer, indicating inherited risk and potential need for specialized treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLPOSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colposcopy is a procedure to closely examine the cervix, vagina, and vulva for abnormalities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZOLADEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zoladex is the brand name for goserelin, an LHRH agonist."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PELVIC AND RECTOVAGINAL EXAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A pelvic and rectovaginal exam may be done during physical exams to check for cancer spread or treatment effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DYSPNEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dyspnea, or trouble breathing, is a general side effect reported by some anal cancer survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLON CANCER DIAGNOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Process of identifying colon cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Process of identifying."&lt;SEP&gt;"Process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of identifying colon cancer, often through colonoscopy and testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGESTIVE SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Digestive system is a body system that transports and breaks down food, absorbs nutrients, and removes waste, including the esophagus and stomach."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive system is a biological system that takes in and breaks down food, absorbs nutrients, and removes waste from the body. It includes organs such as the liver, gallbladder, stomach, pancreas, and intestines."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive system is a group of organs that take in food, break it down, absorb nutrients, and remove waste. It includes the stomach, liver, pancreas, and intestines, and is central to the text's discussion of stomach cancer basics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive system is affected by chemotherapy, leading to side effects like nausea and diarrhea."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive system is the body system that processes food, and the pancreas is part of it."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive system is the body system that takes in and breaks down food, absorbs nutrients, and removes waste, and it includes the stomach."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive system takes in food, breaks it down, absorbs nutrients, and removes waste, and includes the hepatobiliary system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXCISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Excision is a surgical procedure to remove cancer tissue, with standard or shave variations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Excision is the surgical removal of cancerous lesions and nearby lymph nodes, used in treating regional CSCC."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEMICAL EXPOSURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chemical exposure to substances in dyes, rubber, leather, printing materials, textiles, and paint products is linked to increased bladder cancer risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATIC CHANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somatic change is another term for somatic mutation, referring to DNA alterations in non-germline cells that are not inherited."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RENAL TUBULES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Renal tubules are tiny filtering tubes in the kidney that remove waste and excess water from the blood to make urine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Renal tubules are tiny tubes in the kidneys that remove waste from blood and make urine, where renal cell carcinoma originates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Renal tubules are tiny tubes in the kidneys that remove waste from blood and make urine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPEN BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A surgical procedure to remove (excise) a tumor to confirm histology, as recommended when further tissue analysis is needed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Open biopsy is a surgical procedure involving a craniotomy, where a piece of skull bone is removed to access and remove tumor tissue for diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Open biopsy is a type of standard biopsy for gliomas, though not detailed in the text, it is mentioned as an alternative to stereotactic biopsy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FGFR3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FGFR3 is a gene in which germline mutations are associated with bladder cancer, serving as a marker for inherited risk and influencing treatment strategies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Conization is a surgical procedure to remove a cone-shaped piece of tissue from the cervix for diagnosis or treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEUPROLIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leuprolide (Lupron Depot) is an LHRH agonist used for ovarian suppression."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leuprolide, also known as Lupron, is a commonly used LHRH agonist for prostate cancer treatment, given as an injection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PAIN IN THE BELLY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pain in the belly is a more severe side effect of intraperitoneal chemotherapy, causing discomfort."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHANGE IN SMELL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Change in smell is a possible side effect of RAI therapy, affecting olfactory senses."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IUD INSERTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"IUD Insertion is the placement of an intrauterine device for birth control."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;H. PYLORI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"H. pylori is a type of bacteria that can infect the stomach and is a risk factor for stomach cancer, with a history of infection being relevant in medical history."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Resection is a surgical procedure that attempts to remove the entire tumor or as much as safely possible, serving as both a biopsy and a treatment to relieve symptoms and potentially extend life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Resection is a surgical procedure to remove a larger piece of the colon when polypectomy is insufficient, depending on polyp characteristics and test results."&lt;SEP&gt;"Resection is a surgical procedure to remove a larger piece of the rectum, sometimes needed after polypectomy depending on polyp characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Resection is a surgical procedure to remove a new cancer growth, often used when the cancer is localized and can be surgically removed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Resection is a surgical procedure to remove cancer, often with PDEMA for high-risk cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical removal of a tumor or cancer, often followed by radiation therapy as adjuvant treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URINALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urinalysis is a test that studies urine to help diagnose bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEFICIENT MISMATCH REPAIR (DMMR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Deficient mismatch repair (dMMR) is a condition where MMR proteins are defective, causing MSI."&lt;SEP&gt;"Deficient mismatch repair is a condition where MMR proteins fail to fix DNA errors, leading to microsatellite instability."&lt;SEP&gt;"dMMR is a DNA repair defect."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RENAL VEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Renal vein is the blood vessel that carries blood out of the kidney, which tumors can grow into."&lt;SEP&gt;"Renal vein is the blood vessel that carries filtered blood out of the kidney."&lt;SEP&gt;"The renal vein carries clean, filtered blood out of the kidney."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ER-LOW-POSITIVE INVASIVE BREAST CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A subtype of breast cancer where estrogen receptors are found in 1 to 10 out of every 100 cancer cells, and endocrine therapy may not be recommended."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PIK3CA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PIK3CA is a gene frequently mutated in breast cancer, leading to increased growth and treatment resistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"PIK3CA is a gene in which germline mutations are linked to bladder cancer, contributing to inherited cancer risk and guiding clinical decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"PIK3CA is a gene mutation that can be targeted with specific therapies in tumor mutation testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LASER THERAPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Laser therapy uses a focused beam of light to destroy abnormal cervical cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUPRON DEPOT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lupron Depot is the brand name for leuprolide, an LHRH agonist."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medications taken by the patient may interact with chemotherapy, requiring disclosure to the care team."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHARMACY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pharmacy is a facility that dispenses medications, including those for pain and side effect management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pharmacy is a place where patients obtain prescribed medications and over-the-counter products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TELEHEALTH PLATFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Telehealth platform is a technology service that enables remote medical consultations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCALLY ADVANCED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Locally advanced refers to cancer that has spread extensively in the local area, such as to nearby lymph nodes or tissues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYTOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cytology is a test that studies urine samples to detect cancer cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytology is the examination of cells under a microscope by a pathologist to confirm cancer presence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytology is the study of cells under a microscope to confirm cancer presence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytology is the study of cells under a microscope, used by pathologists to examine biopsy samples and confirm cancer presence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytology is the study of cells under a microscope."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SENTINEL NODES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sentinel nodes are the first lymph nodes where cancer might spread, identified and tested via SLNB."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSATELLITE INSTABILITY-HIGH (MSI-H)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biomarker indicating high instability in microsatellite regions, similar to dMMR, used for treatment planning."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellite instability-high (MSI-H) is a biomarker indicating high levels of genetic mutations, making the cancer eligible for immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microsatellite instability-high is a specific classification where cancer cells have more microsatellites than normal, often due to dMMR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VENA CAVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The vena cava is a larger vein that takes clean blood from the renal vein back to the heart."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vena cava is a large vein that returns blood to the heart, which kidney tumors can grow into."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2 GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gene that codes for the HER2 protein; when overexpressed or amplified, it leads to HER2-positive breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERBB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ERBB is a gene family in which mutations may be found in bladder cancer, indicating potential inherited risk and affecting treatment approaches."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CERVICAL CANCER SURVIVOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A cervical cancer survivor is an individual who has completed treatment and is living with or beyond the disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AROMATASE INHIBITORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aromatase inhibitors (AIs) block androgen conversion to estrogen by interfering with aromatase enzyme."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 2 CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 2 ovarian cancer is a specific stage where maintenance therapy may be an option, including observation for BRCA-mutated cases."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENETIC RISK TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genetic risk testing assesses inherited genetic mutations that increase risk of developing kidney cancer, such as those related to sickle cell trait."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic risk testing involves analyzing genes to identify inherited risks or mutations related to ALL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic risk testing is a diagnostic approach to assess hereditary risk for esophageal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic risk testing is a test that assesses inherited genetic mutations that may increase the risk of developing stomach cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genetic risk testing looks for inherited germline mutations using blood or saliva to assess cancer risk and guide treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DYE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A substance injected along with radioactive material to travel through lymphatics and help identify sentinel lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dye is a harmless substance used in SLNB to identify sentinel lymph nodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dye is a substance injected into the cervix during sentinel lymph node biopsy to identify sentinel nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESECTION AND BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Resection and biopsy involve analyzing a sample of surgically removed bladder tissue to diagnose bladder cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR MUTATIONAL BURDEN-HIGH (TMB-H)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor mutational burden-high (TMB-H) is a biomarker indicating a high number of mutations in the cancer cells, making it eligible for immunotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor mutational burden-high is defined as having 10 or more mutations per million base pairs of tumor DNA, indicating high immunogenicity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RENAL PELVIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The renal pelvis is a hollow space in the middle of the kidney where urine collects before leaving through the ureter."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2 OVEREXPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A condition where there are too many HER2 receptors on cancer cells, leading to rapid growth and division."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR TISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor tissue is a sample of cancer tissue used in biomarker testing to identify genetic mutations or features."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor tissue is a sample taken from a cancer site, used in biopsies and genetic testing to determine cancer characteristics and guide treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor tissue is the sample used for NGS if enough remains after other testing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PATIENT NAVIGATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A patient navigator helps guide cervical cancer patients through diagnosis and treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A patient navigator is a healthcare professional who helps guide patients through the healthcare system, providing support and education."&lt;SEP&gt;"Patient Navigator is a professional who guides patients through the healthcare system, helping with appointments and resources."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANASTROZOLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anastrozole (Arimidex) is a non-steroidal aromatase inhibitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAGE 3 CANCER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stage 3 ovarian cancer is a specific stage where maintenance therapy is an option after successful initial treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDICAL BINDER ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medical Binder Role Education is understanding how a binder helps organize care."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE ANUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The anus is the opening through which stool exits the body, located at the end of the large intestine, and is the site where anal cancer develops."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOCRINE SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The endocrine system is a network of glands and organs that produce hormones to regulate bodily functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The endocrine system is made up of tissues and organs that produce hormones, which are carried through the bloodstream to control how organs or cells work."&lt;SEP&gt;"The endocrine system is made up of tissues and organs that produce hormones, which are chemical substances carried through the bloodstream to control how organs or cells work."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDOSCOPY PROCEDURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endoscopy procedures are diagnostic methods to visualize the esophagus and obtain biopsies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endoscopy procedures are medical tests that use a flexible tube with a camera to examine the inside of the stomach and take biopsies."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RADIOACTIVE SOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Radioactive solution is a low-level substance used in SLNB to identify sentinel lymph nodes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URETERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tubes that carry urine from the kidneys to the bladder, examined in imaging tests if cancer is suspected."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ureters are tubes connecting the kidneys to the bladder, examined during ureteroscopy or urogram for abnormalities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ureters are tubes that carry urine from the kidneys to the bladder, and are examined in imaging tests to identify blockages or other issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ureters are tubes that carry urine from the kidneys to the bladder, connected to the tube or pouch in urinary diversions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ureters are tubes that carry urine from the kidneys to the bladder, part of the urinary tract's inner layer where urothelial cancer can occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ureters are tubes that carry urine from the kidneys to the bladder."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR GENOMIC ABERRATION TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tumor genomic aberration testing is another name for tumor mutation testing, analyzing tumor DNA for specific mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RENAL CELL CARCINOMA (RCC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Renal cell carcinoma (RCC) is the most common type of kidney cancer, starting in the cells lining the renal tubules, and is the focus of the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HER2 AMPLIFICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An increase in the number of copies of the HER2 gene, leading to overexpression of HER2 receptors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INHERITED CANCER RISK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inherited cancer risk is the likelihood of developing cancer due to genetic factors from family history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inherited cancer risk refers to the increased likelihood of developing cancer due to genetic mutations passed from parents, prompting genetic testing and counseling."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPPORT GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A support group is a gathering of breast cancer patients and survivors who share experiences and provide mutual support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support Group is a gathering of individuals facing similar challenges, such as cancer, to share experiences and provide emotional support."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support group is a collection of individuals who share experiences and provide emotional support to cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support group is a collective of individuals offering emotional and social support to cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support group provides emotional help for cancer patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Support groups offer emotional and informational support to cervical cancer patients and survivors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARIMIDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arimidex is the brand name for anastrozole, an aromatase inhibitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OBSERVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Observation is an option for some stage 2 cancers with BRCA mutation or after complete response to chemotherapy, meaning no signs of cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLON CANCER TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Therapy for colon cancer, including surgery, chemotherapy, and other approaches."&lt;SEP&gt;"Therapy for colon cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Therapy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITION ASSESSMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A consultation with a nutritionist or dietitian to ensure adequate nutrition before starting cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutrition assessment involves meeting with a nutritionist or dietician to ensure adequate food and fluid intake before cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutrition assessment is a meeting with a nutrition expert to ensure adequate nutrition before and during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutrition assessment is an evaluation of a patient's dietary status and needs, important for managing stomach cancer treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRITICAL HEALTHY ORGANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Critical healthy organs are vital structures that may be damaged by radiation, influencing treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FREQUENT URINATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Frequent or painful urination is a common side effect during EBRT."&lt;SEP&gt;"Frequent urination is a short-term side effect of radiation therapy for anal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Frequent urination is a side effect of intravesical therapy, impacting daily activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Frequent urination is a symptom of bladder cancer, characterized by needing to urinate more often than usual."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHONDROSARCOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chondrosarcoma is a bone sarcoma that starts in cartilage-forming cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chondrosarcoma is a type of bone cancer that is prone to IDH1 mutations and can be treated with ivosidenib."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chondrosarcoma is a type of bone cancer that is typically treated with surgery to remove the tumor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chondrosarcoma starts in cells that form cartilage, a tough, flexible tissue covering bone ends and providing structure to parts like the nose and ears."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UROTHELIAL CARCINOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urothelial carcinoma starts in the cells lining the renal pelvis and ureter, sharing features with bladder cancer, and is not considered kidney cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN LEVELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The amount of specific proteins in tumor cells, measured through biomarker testing to inform treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GERMLINE MUTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Germline mutations are inherited gene changes from biological parents that increase cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Germline mutations are inherited gene changes present in all cells, tested via blood, saliva, or cheek swab to assess hereditary cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Germline mutations are inherited genetic changes present in every cell, increasing cancer risk and influencing treatment decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL CANCER INSTITUTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"National Cancer Institute is a research organization that provides guidelines on biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Cancer Institute conducts and funds research on cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The National Cancer Institute is a U.S. government agency that conducts and supports cancer research, including breast cancer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LETROZOLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Letrozole (Femara) is a non-steroidal aromatase inhibitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPLETE RESPONSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Complete response means no signs of cancer in the body after chemotherapy, making observation an option."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIN RASH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skin rash or redness is a common side effect of radiation therapy to the neck area."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONDOM USE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Condom Use is the application of condoms as a barrier method."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENERAL HEALTH TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A set of tests including physical exams, imaging, and biopsies used to assess overall health and diagnose conditions like breast cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests are assessments conducted as part of diagnosing esophageal cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests are assessments of a patient's overall health status, used to plan treatment and monitor health during and after prostate cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests are assessments of overall health, including blood tests and physical exams, part of the testing process."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests are assessments of overall health, part of the testing process for cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests are basic assessments of overall health, including physical exams and medical history, used in bladder cancer care."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests are part of the testing process for CBCL, assessing overall health status before treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests are part of the testing process for adrenal tumors, assessing overall health and organ function."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests are part of the testing process for diagnosing basal cell skin cancer, assessing overall health."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests are routine assessments conducted as part of the testing process for throat cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests are routine assessments of overall health, including medical history, physical exam, and basic measurements. They are used to evaluate a patient's condition before cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests are routine assessments to evaluate overall health before and during ALL treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests are routine medical assessments to evaluate overall health status, often performed before or during cancer diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests include medical history and physical exams that help assess a patient's overall health before cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests include medical history, blood tests, imaging tests, and other assessments to evaluate overall health before cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests include medical history, physical exams, and other baseline assessments to determine overall health before cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"General health tests include various procedures like medical history, physical exam, and blood tests to evaluate overall health."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMMUNE CHECKPOINT INHIBITOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of drug used in immunotherapy for anal cancer, potentially reducing the need for surgery."&lt;SEP&gt;"An immune checkpoint inhibitor is a type of immunotherapy drug that helps the immune system attack cancer cells, preferred for eligible patients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune checkpoint inhibitor is a therapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune checkpoint inhibitor is a type of immunotherapy drug that helps the immune system fight cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune checkpoint inhibitor is a type of immunotherapy that blocks proteins that prevent the immune system from attacking cancer cells, such as pembrolizumab."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune checkpoint inhibitor is a type of therapy that activates the immune system against cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune checkpoint inhibitors are a class of immunotherapy drugs that block proteins like PD-1 to enhance the immune system's ability to fight cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune checkpoint inhibitors are a type of immunotherapy used for metastatic anal cancer that does not respond to chemotherapy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune checkpoint inhibitors are a type of immunotherapy used to treat CSCC, recommended for eligible patients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URGENCY TO URINATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urgency to urinate is a symptom of bladder cancer, involving a sudden, strong need to urinate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RNA is genetic information that can be amplified by PCR for analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"RNA is genetic information that can be copied by PCR for analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"RNA is genetic material that can be amplified by PCR to detect gene rearrangements like PML::RARA in leukemia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILMS TUMOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wilms tumor (nephroblastoma) is a type of kidney cancer that usually occurs in young children."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR TESTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Another term for biomarker testing, which looks at DNA mutations, protein levels, or other molecular features of a tumor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular testing is a laboratory procedure that analyzes genetic characteristics of tumor samples to identify biomarkers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular testing is an alternative name for biomarker testing, analyzing genetic changes in tumors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular testing is another name for biomarker testing, analyzing genes and proteins to guide cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular testing is another name for biomarker testing, analyzing tumor DNA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular testing is another name for genetic testing that looks for changes in leukemia cells, including gene expression profiling and genomic testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular testing is another term for biomarker testing, analyzing genes or proteins for treatment guidance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular testing is another term for biomarker testing, analyzing genes or proteins to guide cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular testing is another term for biomarker testing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular testing is another term for genetic testing that looks for changes in leukemia cells, guiding treatment and prognosis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
    </node>
