    <node id="&quot;PRIMARY CARE PHYSICIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A healthcare provider who is kept informed of changes to the patient's care team contact list and is involved in the patient's overall care."&lt;SEP&gt;"A healthcare provider who should be kept informed of changes to the patient's care team and contact list."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary care physician (PCP) is a health care professional that people with anal cancer symptoms often first reach out to for evaluation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary care physician is a doctor who provides general healthcare and should be kept informed of changes in the patient's care team and medical status."&lt;SEP&gt;"A primary care physician may perform initial screenings and refer patients to specialists for cervical cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary care physician (PCP) is a doctor who provides general healthcare and is kept informed of a patient's cancer care, acting as a partner in treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary care physician (PCP) is a healthcare provider who coordinates overall patient care and should be updated on cancer treatment details."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary care physician is a healthcare provider who coordinates overall patient care, monitors health changes, and is kept informed of updates in the patient's medical team and condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"The primary care physician is a health care provider who should be kept informed of changes to the patient's care team and contact list."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOBACCO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tobacco is a plant product containing nicotine, which is addictive and a primary cause of smoking-related health issues, including cancer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tobacco is a substance containing nicotine, which is addictive and used in smoking."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tobacco is a substance that contains nicotine and is harmful to health, especially during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tobacco is a substance whose use is a risk factor for head and neck cancer, and patients are advised to avoid it during treatment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
    </node>
