    <node id="&quot;GLIOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glioma is a type of brain tumor that can cause various symptoms such as vision problems, sensory disturbances, and is linked to blood clots; it is identified through imaging and diagnosed via biopsy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glioma is a type of brain tumor that develops from glial cells, often treated with surgery, radiation, and chemotherapy, and can be fatal but is subject to ongoing research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glioma is a type of brain tumor that originates from glial cells, classified by histology, grade, and biomarkers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glioma is a type of brain tumor, mentioned in the text as a separate topic, with questions about its causes, diagnosis, and curability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glioma is a type of tumor that grows in the brain, developing from glial cells, and is the most common malignant brain tumor in adults. It can be challenging to treat due to its invasive nature."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;E-CIGARETTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"E-cigarettes are electronic devices that deliver nicotine and are harmful during cancer treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"E-cigarettes are vaping devices that deliver nicotine, and their use can limit cancer treatment effectiveness and increase side effects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACK PAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Back pain is a symptom of adrenal cancer, often caused by tumor growth pressing on nearby structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Back pain is a symptom that can occur in bladder cancer, often indicating more advanced disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Core needle biopsy is a biopsy technique using a larger needle to remove a small cylinder of tissue for analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Core needle biopsy is a procedure to obtain a tumor sample for diagnosis, recommended to be performed at experienced centers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Core needle biopsy is a type of biopsy used to test lymph nodes for CSCC spread."&lt;SEP&gt;"Core needle biopsy is a type of biopsy using a hollow needle to extract tissue samples, often performed under light sedation by an interventional radiologist."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLEAR CELL RCC (CCRCC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clear cell RCC is the most common subtype of RCC, occurring in about 7 out of 10 people with RCC, and appears pale or clear under a microscope."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUMOR SEQUENCING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of biomarker testing that determines the order of DNA bases in tumor genes to identify mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor sequencing is a method of biomarker testing that analyzes DNA sequences in tumors to find mutations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tumor sequencing is a method of biomarker testing that determines the order of DNA bases in tumor genes to find mutations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UPPER URINARY TRACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Upper urinary tract includes the kidneys and ureters, and cancer in this area may prompt germline testing due to higher inherited risk."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HPV VACCINATION PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HPV Vaccination Program is a public health initiative to prevent HPV infection, reducing anal cancer risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPV vaccination programs aim to reduce cervical cancer by immunizing populations against HPV."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ER MODULATORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Estrogen receptor (ER) modulators prevent estrogen from binding to receptors, including SERMs and SERDs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EJACULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ejaculation is the process during which semen is released from the body through the urethra and out through the penis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOD TEST ROLE EDUCATION&quot;">
