      <data key="d5">"treatment planning, patient assessment"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA&quot;" target="&quot;IMAGING&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Imaging tests, such as MRI and CT scans, are used to identify the location and size of primary CNS lymphoma."</data>
      <data key="d5">"diagnostic imaging, tumor detection"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA&quot;" target="&quot;MRI&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"An MRI of the spine is used to detect cancer in primary CNS lymphoma, which may influence treatment decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"MRI is the most useful imaging technique for identifying primary CNS lymphoma, providing detailed images of the brain and spine."</data>
      <data key="d5">"diagnosis, treatment planning"&lt;SEP&gt;"diagnostic imaging, tumor detection"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA&quot;" target="&quot;CT SCAN&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"A CT scan is used as an alternative to MRI for identifying primary CNS lymphoma when MRI is unavailable."</data>
      <data key="d5">"diagnostic imaging, alternative method"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PRIMARY CNS LYMPHOMA&quot;" target="&quot;BIOPSY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">27.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"A biopsy is key to confirming the diagnosis of primary CNS lymphoma by taking a sample of tissue or fluid."&lt;SEP&gt;"A biopsy is necessary to diagnose primary CNS lymphoma, and steroid therapy should not start until after biopsy to ensure accurate diagnosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"A biopsy is the only way to confirm a diagnosis of primary CNS lymphoma, as it involves testing a tissue sample."</data>
      <data key="d5">"diagnosis, confirmation"&lt;SEP&gt;"diagnosis, treatment sequencing"&lt;SEP&gt;"diagnostic confirmation, tissue analysis"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23</data>
    </edge>
